f_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8213b6a-7e03-582d-beeb-059db64aab77', 'word_count': 1054, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8213b6a-7e03-582d-beeb-059db64aab77'}, {'abstract': 'Readers weigh in on the etiquette of handing over money to newborns and their families in lieu of blankets or rattles.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/08/31/why-college-money-is-the-best-baby-gift/', 'snippet': 'Readers weigh in on the etiquette of handing over money to newborns and their families in lieu of blankets or rattles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week’s Your Money column about the ins and outs of giving money as a gift to someone’s 529 college savings account wasn’t meant to be an etiquette lesson. But I do think giving money is totally defensible, even if it means pushing the parents to open a 529 or other savings account to use the gift. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why College Money Is the Best Baby Gift', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs, Etiquette and Manners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gifts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-01T01:10:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Lieber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lieber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/faec1d39-e5e3-5fcc-bc86-64ad1071dd6b', 'word_count': 124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/faec1d39-e5e3-5fcc-bc86-64ad1071dd6b'}, {'abstract': 'The unrest at South African mines has placed the spotlight on the country’s business leaders and politicians, who once led protests and are now wealthy members of the establishment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/01/world/africa/south-africa-leaders-on-other-side-of-rich-poor-divide.html', 'snippet': 'The unrest at South African mines has placed the spotlight on the country’s business leaders and politicians, who once led protests and are now wealthy members of the establishment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JOHANNESBURG — When 360,000 gold and coal miners walked off the job in South Africa in 1987, protesting the poor pay and grim working conditions of apartheid-era mines, a charismatic young man named Cyril Ramaphosa, the firebrand leader of the National Union of Mineworkers, led the charge. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/01/world/jp-safrica1/jp-safrica1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/01/world/jp-safrica1/jp-safrica1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/01/world/jp-safrica1/jp-safrica1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/01/world/jp-safrica1/jp-safrica1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/01/world/jp-safrica1/jp-safrica1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/01/world/jp-safrica1/jp-safrica1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank'