y night on Clarkson Avenue in Prospect-Lefferts Gardens, an area where violence has been rampant all summer, residents said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The morning after his mother was killed in Brooklyn, Chinnarie Gordon, 5, took his grandmother’s hand and walked to Parkside Playground. As his cousins played in the fountains, Chinnarie climbed up to a checkers table and began drawing a picture of his mother in blue chalk, giving her long blue hair and a mermaid’s tail.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/01/nyregion/SHOOT3/SHOOT3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 425, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/01/nyregion/SHOOT3/SHOOT3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 425, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/01/nyregion/SHOOT3/SHOOT3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/01/nyregion/SHOOT3/SHOOT3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/01/nyregion/SHOOT3/SHOOT3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Killing on a Brooklyn Block Known for Its Violence', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Killing on a Brooklyn Block Known for Its Violence', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gordon, Fatima', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Prospect Lefferts Gardens (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-01T01:48:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Maag', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Maag', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/61d8e1c7-7419-5c12-93bb-98a8b8dc9683', 'word_count': 754, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61d8e1c7-7419-5c12-93bb-98a8b8dc9683'}, {'abstract': 'A study released on Friday said the New York City Department of Education had done a good job of preparing for significant special education reforms that will begin in earnest next week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/01/nyregion/schools-planned-well-for-special-education-changes-but-may-need-more-funds-study-finds.html', 'snippet': 'A study released on Friday said the New York City Department of Education had done a good job of preparing for significant special education reforms that will begin in earnest next week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A study released on Friday said that the New York City Department of Education had done a good job of preparing for significant special education reforms that will begin in earnest next week, but it expressed concerns about whether schools had enough money and teachers had enough training to carry out the changes.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mainstreaming Efforts Praised in Schools Study', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mainstreaming Efforts Praised in Schools Study', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'v