al': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8343b2b6-4827-5b76-938c-9fefb99c251d', 'word_count': 929, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8343b2b6-4827-5b76-938c-9fefb99c251d'}, {'abstract': 'The Orioles, who jumped out to an early lead on Yankees starter Hiroki Kuroda, have made up four games in less than two weeks in the American League East.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/01/sports/baseball/orioles-beat-yankees-to-trim-lead-to-2-games.html', 'snippet': 'The Orioles, who jumped out to an early lead on Yankees starter Hiroki Kuroda, have made up four games in less than two weeks in the American League East.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few starts ago, Hiroki Kuroda threw a seven-inning shutout in a rain-shortened victory over the Toronto Blue Jays. The win, on July 18, increased the Yankees’ lead in the American League East to a whopping 10 games. The margin has been slashed to two, in part, by a rash of injuries and inconsistent performances. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/01/sports/jp-yankees/jp-yankees-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/01/sports/jp-yankees/jp-yankees-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1638, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/01/sports/jp-yankees/jp-yankees-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/01/sports/jp-yankees/jp-yankees-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Giving the Yankees Reason for Pause', 'kicker': 'Orioles 6, Yankees 1', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Giving the Yankees Reason for Pause', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baltimore Orioles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-01T02:27:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zach Schonbrun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zach', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schonbrun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c49b771b-c4db-513f-9b28-3e30348e7ecf', 'word_count': 833, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c49b771b-c4db-513f-9b28-3e30348e7ecf'}, {'abstract': 'Mark Edward, in coming clean about tricks used for duping people, tries to enter a class of magicians and mediums who perform their crafts and also debunk them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/01/us/in-book-mark-edward-tells-tricks-used-as-a-medium.html', 'snippet': 'Mark Edward, in coming clean about tricks used for duping people, tries to enter a class of magicians and mediums who perform their crafts and also debunk them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Don’t mistake Mark Edward for John Edward. The two men, who are not related, are both professional mediums, men who charge money for their supposed skill at transmitting messages from the dead. But whereas John Edward had a nationally syndicated television show and still plays to large crowds in Las Vegas and across the country, Mark Edward’s biggest gigs were a baby shower at Eddie Murphy’s house and Buddy Hackett’s 70th birthday party.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 't