'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dickey, R A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-01T02:40:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Snyder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Snyder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/655b2952-ed7b-5190-8d66-e67426eda61c', 'word_count': 578, 'uri': 'nyt://article/655b2952-ed7b-5190-8d66-e67426eda61c'}, {'abstract': 'At Upstate, a restaurant in the East Village, two longtime friends met up for a light dinner after work: beer and oysters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/02/nyregion/at-upstate-childhood-friends-reconnect.html', 'snippet': 'At Upstate, a restaurant in the East Village, two longtime friends met up for a light dinner after work: beer and oysters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the wife-and-husband team of Jennifer and Shane Covey opened their 28-seat East Village restaurant, Upstate, last July, the concept was monkishly minimal: beer and oysters. “We’re relatively uncomplicated people,” Ms. Covey said, though she also said her husband used three types of beer glasses at home. Not that more complicated people have found a better way to salute a late summer sunset. The Coveys have since added a few cooked dishes, some wine and free slices of Ms. Covey’s whiskey cake, but it is still the original pairing that brings the customers in — some calling it a light dinner, others pre-dinner ballast, an evening equivalent of elevenses. The décor is spare, and the menu would almost fit in a Twitter post. From 5 to 7 p.m., you get a beer and six oysters for $12. One evening at the end of August, a crowd waited on the sidewalk for seats to open up. Inside, the early birds slurped and slugged. Were oyster happy hours everywhere this summer? Yes, they were. What took them so long?', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/nyregion/02TABLE_SPAN/02TABLE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 351, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/02/nyregion/02TABLE_SPAN/02TABLE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 351}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/nyregion/02TABLE_SPAN/02TABLE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/nyregion/02TABLE_SPAN/02TABLE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/nyregion/02TABLE_SPAN/02TABLE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/02/nyregion/02TABLE_SPAN/02TABLE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/nyregion/02TABLE_SPAN/02TABLE_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Old Friends and Oysters', 'kicker': 'At the Table | Upstate', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Old Friends And Oysters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Upstate (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Village (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-01T02:41:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Leland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3539292c-a69b-55db-8166-1e874d2e95bb', 'word_count': 525, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3539292c-a69b-55db-8166-1e874d2e95bb'}, {'abstract': 'Few other issues present a starker difference between the two tickets, with President Obama seeking a big expansion and the Republicans pushing big cuts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/01/us/politics/campaigns-have-sharply-different-visions-for-medicaid.html', 'snippet': 'Few other issues present a starker difference between the two tickets, with President Obama seeking a big expansion and the Republicans pushing big cuts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The way Mitt Romney and Representative Paul D. Ryan frame it, the debate over social programs that has become a dominant theme of the presidential race is all about the future of Medicare, the government health insurance program for retirees.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/01/us/MEDICAID/MEDICAID-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 878, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/01/us/MEDICAID/MEDICAID-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1755, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/01/us/MEDICAID/MEDICAID-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/01/us/MEDICAID/MEDICAID-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/01/us/MEDICAID/MEDICAID-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '2 Campaigns Differ Sharply on Medicaid, Seeking Vast Growth or Vast Cuts', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '2 Campaigns Differ Sharply on Medicaid, Seeking Vast Growth or Vast Cuts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicaid', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-01T02:49:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abby Goodnough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goodnough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1a9158c-5097-53da-91a2-8efde5ee3eb5', 'word_count': 829, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1a9158c-5097-53da-91a2-8efde5ee3eb5'}, {'abstract': 'The Energy Department’s inspector general said that managers knew about broken equipment and other lapses at the Y-12 plant where there was a break-in this summer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/01/science/earth/audit-finds-security-lapses-at-y-12-uranium-storage-plant.html', 'snippet': 'The Energy Department’s inspector general said that managers knew about broken equipment and other lapses at the Y-12 plant where there was a break-in this summer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The contractors in charge of guarding the national stockpile of bomb-grade uranium in Tennessee knew well before an 82-year-old nun and two other pacifists broke through three barriers this summer that a lot of the security equipment was broken, and government managers knew it too, according to an internal audit of Energy Department operations at the weapons facility. The inspector general’s investigation found “troubling displays of ineptitude.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Weapons Plant Security Issues Are Described in U.S. Audit', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Weapons Plant Security Issues Are Described In U.S. Audit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Energy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Energy Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Security and Warning Systems', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Uranium', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oak Ridge (Tenn)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank'