ame', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-01T03:06:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By GEOFF MACDONALD', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Geoff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MACDONALD', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ca94eb8-aae8-5142-b6ea-10f3f2069dac', 'word_count': 426, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ca94eb8-aae8-5142-b6ea-10f3f2069dac'}, {'abstract': 'Federal health officials confirmed the death of a 61-year-old Ohio woman and said 14 other victims had been hospitalized by the new strain.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/01/health/first-death-is-reported-from-new-pig-flu-strain.html', 'snippet': 'Federal health officials confirmed the death of a 61-year-old Ohio woman and said 14 other victims had been hospitalized by the new strain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first human death from a new strain of pig flu was reported Friday by state health officials in Ohio.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'First Death Is Reported From New Pig Flu Strain', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'First Death Is Reported From New Pig Flu Strain', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Swine Influenza', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epidemics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-01T03:09:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Donald G. McNeil Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Donald', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'McNeil', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62d3da93-80b4-5c7c-bf72-a73da193e1dd', 'word_count': 338, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62d3da93-80b4-5c7c-bf72-a73da193e1dd'}, {'abstract': 'Republicans, even House challengers, are distancing themselves from the proposed Medicare cuts in Paul D. Ryan’s budget plan, even as he and Mitt Romney urge them to embrace it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/01/us/politics/republican-troops-keeping-ryans-budget-plan-at-arms-length.html', 'snippet': 'Republicans, even House challengers, are distancing themselves from the proposed Medicare cuts in Paul D. Ryan’s budget plan, even as he and Mitt Romney urge them to embrace it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAMPA, Fla. — Even as Mitt Romney and Representative Paul D. Ryan exhort Republicans to embrace their proposed Medicare changes and spending cuts, the party’s rank and file is growing less enthusiastic about the fight than the top of the ticket.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/01/us/ECON1/ECON1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 853, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/01/us/ECON1/ECON1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1706, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/01/us/ECON1/ECON1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/01/us/ECON1/ECON1-thumbStandard.jpg