 'persons', 'value': 'Benedict XVI', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-01T08:35:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Morris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/88ee0fdf-9386-5ce0-b132-ae481ed9a927', 'word_count': 565, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88ee0fdf-9386-5ce0-b132-ae481ed9a927'}, {'abstract': 'The outcome of American elections affect the entire world — yet most people outside the United States (and many inside) don’t understand American politics. I anchored our livestreaming coverage from the Republican convention and will do the same at the Democrats. Send me your questions about American politics, the political parties and Barack Obama and Mitt Romney.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/01/what-i-saw-at-the-republican-convention/', 'snippet': 'The outcome of American elections affect the entire world — yet most people outside the United States (and many inside) don’t understand American politics. I anchored our livestreaming coverage from the Republican convention and will do the same a...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The outcome of American elections affect the entire world — yet most people outside the United States (and many inside) don’t understand American politics. In an effort to bring greater understanding to the process, the politics, the personalities and the policies, The New York Times, for the first time, livestreamed coverage from the Republican National Convention. I was one of the anchors of that coverage. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What I Saw at the Republican Convention', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Republican National Convention', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-01T09:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marcus Mabry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marcus', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mabry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d3a9795-57be-536c-a89c-06902da6baea', 'word_count': 233, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d3a9795-57be-536c-a89c-06902da6baea'}, {'abstract': 'A round-up of news from across India.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/01/newswallah-bharat-edition-54/', 'snippet': 'A round-up of news from across India.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jammu and Kashmir: Recent amendments to the Right to Information Act of 2010 have weakened the State Information Commission, a watchdog agency tasked with safeguarding the law’s provisions, Hindustan Times reported. Civic groups and opposition politicians criticized the changes; the chief information commissioner, G.R. Sufi, accused the state government of trying to make the commission a “toothless body.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Newswallah: Bharat Edition', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-01T09:17:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/826ca845-0559-591e-b7d9-a0f0eaa1bc8b', 'word_count': 414, 'uri': 'nyt://article/826ca845-0559-591e-b7d9-a0f0eaa1bc8b'}, {'abstract': 'Political news from today’s Times and around the Web, plus a look at the weekly addresses and the latest happenings in Washington.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/01/the-weekend-word-political-theater/', 'snippet': 'Political news from today’s Times and around the Web, plus a look at the weekly addresses and the latest happenings in Washington.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Today’s Times', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Weekend Word: Political Theater', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-01T10:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jada F. Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jada', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3556a341-5ef0-565e-a986-044a2831e88c', 'word_count': 745, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3556a341-5ef0-565e-a986-044a2831e88c'}, {'abstract': 'The culture of tax evasion in Greece is widespread and “will take some time” to change.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/01/how-greek-taxpayers-hide-11-billion-euros-a-year/', 'snippet': 'The culture of tax evasion in Greece is widespread and “will take some time” to change.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After a brief summer holiday, the euro crisis is back. Adam Davidson’s latest column\xa0previews seven dramas coming to the Euro zone this fall. As usual, things begin with Greece, which has to cut its budget by an additional 11.5 billion euros in order to secure the next round of debt relief. In a surprising twist, that may be the exact amount of money that Greece loses from tax evaders each year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Greek Taxpayers Hide 11 Billion Euros a Year', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Evasion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davidson, Adam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hydra (Greece)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-01T11:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Kedmey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kedmey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9328d46-e905-5d21-88b4-adf76d0a8f16', 'word_count': 421, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9328d46-e905-5d21-88b4-adf76d0a8f16'}, {'abstract': 'Vietnam’s political mandarins are struggling to reconcile their party’s message of social justice and equality with the realities of an elite awash in wealth and privilege.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/02/world/asia/in-vietnam-message-of-equality-challenged-by-wealth-gap.html', 'snippet': 'Vietnam’s political mandarins are struggling to reconcile their party’s message of social justice and equality with the realities of an elite awash in wealth and privilege.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HANOI, Vietnam — She wore a pink outfit and matching high heels as she toured the dusty construction site. Soon after To Linh Huong’s visit in April, photos that captured the moment went viral on the Internet, but not because of Ms. Huong’s sense of style.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/world/VIETNAM/VIETNAM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 937, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/world/VIETNAM/VIETNAM-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1873, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/world/VIETNAM/VIETNAM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/02/world/VIETNAM/VIETNAM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/world/VIETNAM/VIETNAM-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Vietnam, Message of Equality Is Challenged by Widening Wealth Gap', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Widening Wealth Gap in Vietnam Is Challenging Leaders’ Message of Equality', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vietnam', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nepotism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dung, Nguyen Tan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-01T11:41:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Fuller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fuller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c237eca3-ca77-5902-86a5-c9b5d56fcc24', 'word_count': 1070, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c237eca3-ca77-5902-86a5-c9b5d56fcc24'}, {'abstract': 'Marathon truthers, vindicated.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/01/three-hours-four-hours-whatever/', 'snippet': 'Marathon truthers, vindicated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ahem. (Via Mark Thoma, who has more).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Three Hours, Four Hours, Whatever', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-01T11:44:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/49ecddbf-8f03-5bb6-98c0-c87f155eb124', 'word_count': 200, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49ecddbf-8f03-5bb6-98c0-c87f155eb124'}, {'abstract': 'Highlight matches at the United States Open include Sloane Stephens vs. Ana Ivanovic and Jack Sock vs. Nicolas Almagro.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/01/what-to-watch-on-saturday-at-the-us-ope/', 'snippet': 'Highlight matches at the United States Open include Sloane Stephens vs. Ana Ivanovic and Jack Sock vs. Nicolas Almagro.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Down a set and trailing 3-2 in her second round match Thursday, nothing seemed to work for Sloane Stephens. Her first serve was off, her forehand shaky. Tatjana Malek’s route to victory seemed easy enough: Keep balls in play and wait for the inevitable miss.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What to Watch on Saturday', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-01T12:09:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By ARON PILHOFER', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Aron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'PILHOFER', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fbb08ba5-5f99-52aa-8344-b4398009ec24', 'word_count': 1089, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fbb08ba5-5f99-52aa-8344-b4398009ec24'}, {'abstract': 'The Fed offers the wrong kind of forward guidance.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/01/woodford-on-monetary-policy-sort-of-wonkish/', 'snippet': 'The Fed offers the wrong kind of forward guidance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m not in Jackson Hole — actually, I appear to have been blackballed for a long time, probably because I had the temerity to criticize the great Greenspan before it was fashionable. No matter. I can still read the papers — and the most important one was by Mike Woodford (pdf).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Woodford on Monetary Policy (Sort of Wonkish)', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-01T12:13:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db567bba-8b4a-547b-8993-50f5a2ba3b45', 'word_count': 527, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db567bba-8b4a-547b-8993-50f5a2ba3b45'}, {'abstract': 'The New York Times is providing live analysis of college football on the first Saturday of the season.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/01/live-updates-first-saturday/', 'snippet': 'The New York Times is providing live analysis of college football on the first Saturday of the season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The stars have aligned for the first Saturday of the college football season. Paul Myerberg is in Manhattan. Tim Rohan is in Happy Valley to watch Penn State host Ohio. Later tonight, Tom Spousta will be in Arlington, Tex., to provide feedback on Alabama’s date with Michigan. Keep close tabs throughout the day for updates and analysis.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Live Updates: First Saturday', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-01T15:01:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Myerberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Myerberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/806f13c5-51f2-5485-ba97-d7db392db146', 'word_count': 7346, 'uri': 'nyt://article/806f13c5-51f2-5485-ba97-d7db392db146'}, {'abstract': 'Keeping track of stuff that happened, for like a zillion years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/02/opinion/sunday/a-brief-history-of-timelines.html', 'snippet': 'Keeping track of stuff that happened, for like a zillion years.', 'lead_paragraph': '385 million B.C. During the Middle Devonian Period of the Paleozoic Era, a prehistoric fern adds a new growth ring to its trunk, creating the world’s first timeline. A trilobite third-grade teacher immediately assigns it to her class as busywork.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Brief History of Timelines', 'kicker': 'Loose Ends', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Brief History Of Timelines', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'History (Academic Subject)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-01T15:12:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Frank Lesser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Frank', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lesser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/50429c4f-ad84-5798-8ba9-6a99d3c2a52e', 'word_count': 593, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50429c4f-ad84-5798-8ba9-6a99d3c2a52e'}, {'abstract': 'What Alice Waters is reading, watching, following, wearing and, of course, eating.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/02/opinion/sunday/catching-up-with-alice-waters.html', 'snippet': 'What Alice Waters is reading, watching, following, wearing and, of course, eating.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A pioneer in the organic, locally grown and slow-food movements, Alice Waters is a chef, cookbook author and owner of Chez Panisse in Berkeley, Calif.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/sunday-review/0902Download/0902Download-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 316, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/s