 nearly three-quarters of the votes cast on Friday after 60 percent of the ballots had been counted, electoral officials said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LUANDA, Angola — Angola’s governing party was poised on Saturday to sweep parliamentary elections, winning a landslide victory that would ensure President José Eduardo dos Santos a five-year extension to his 33 years at the country’s helm. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Angola’s Governing Party and Its President Are Poised to Win Election', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Angola’s Governing Party and Its President Are Poised to Win Election', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ANGOLA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Union for the Total Independence of Angola', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Popular Movement for the Liberation of Angola', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dos Santos, Jose Eduardo', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-01T15:26:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lydia Polgreen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lydia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Polgreen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2bb4740b-8d0e-5d35-a09e-8ca3d7768f0b', 'word_count': 387, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2bb4740b-8d0e-5d35-a09e-8ca3d7768f0b'}, {'abstract': 'The Saints remain the most talented team in the division, and they made the smart decision to replace the interim head coach with the offensive line coach, Aaron Kromer, and keep the coordinators with their units.', 'web_url': 'htt