fact, couldn’t it be the key to your book’s selling or not? Ah, yes, the title.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is This Title O.K.?', 'kicker': 'Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-01T18:16:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c95c8e1-bcd7-5b46-8194-09ecfd4a3a08', 'word_count': 1138, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c95c8e1-bcd7-5b46-8194-09ecfd4a3a08'}, {'abstract': 'Mets Manager Terry Collins endured 10 seasons in the Pittsburgh Pirates and Los Angeles Dodgers organizations, but he never made it to the big leagues as a player.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/02/sports/baseball/terry-collins-overlooked-as-player-but-at-ease-at-the-top.html', 'snippet': 'Mets Manager Terry Collins endured 10 seasons in the Pittsburgh Pirates and Los Angeles Dodgers organizations, but he never made it to the big leagues as a player.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before a game during the Mets’ last homestand, Terry Collins emerged from the dugout, picked up a baseball and began warming up his arm as he walked toward second base to watch batting practice. Three decades earlier, Collins, 63, would have performed a similar routine, when he was a utility player in the minor leagues.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/sports/dog-collins/dog-collins-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 660, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 