s not until Saturday that their relatives in New York City were finally able to gather to mourn their loss and bury their loved ones.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/nyregion/FUNERAL-sub/FUNERAL-sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/02/nyregion/FUNERAL-sub/FUNERAL-sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/nyregion/FUNERAL-sub/FUNERAL-sub-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/nyregion/FUNERAL-sub/FUNERAL-sub-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Americans Are Buried a Year After a Train Crash in China', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Two Americans Are Buried Year After China Train Crash', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cao, Leo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Railroad Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Funerals and Memorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-01T19:30:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marc Santora and Jeffrey E. Singer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jeffrey', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Singer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5f4a483-2129-5abe-9f2b-66d0198c11d0', 'word_count': 752, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5f4a483-2129-5abe-9f2b-66d0198c11d0'}, {'abstract': 'John Cage’s 1944 piece “Four Walls” translated the innermost rooms of my obsessive-compulsive mind into sound.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/01/music-of-the-unquiet-mind/', 'snippet': 'John Cage’s 1944 piece “Four Walls” translated the innermost rooms of my obsessive-compulsive mind into sound.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Music of the Unquiet Mind', 'kicker': 'Anxiety', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Anxiety and Stress', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buddhism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Obsessive-Compulsive Disorder', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cage, John', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-01T19:30:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Leng Tan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': 'Leng', 'lastname': 'Tan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a256e51-8de9-53b8-8066-145af98f6aa7', 'word_count': 1270, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a256e51-8de9-53b8-8066-145af98f6aa7'}, {'abstract': 'Readers weigh in on my column about the GOP and reproductive health', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/01/mitt-romney-and-abortion-politics/', 'snippet': 'Readers weigh in on my column about the GOP and reproductive health', 'lead_paragraph': 'My Sunday column looks at the GOP and reproductive health, from abortion to sex education. As you can see from the column, I think it’s a pathetic sight — but in fairness, one point I wish I had had space for in the column is to note that if the Republican platform is baffling in its message to centrist voters, it’s also arguably a rare example of political courage. Republicans are looking at the same polls I am, and presumably they realize that their reluctance to back exceptions in abortion bans for rape or the health of the mother risk losing voters. It’s not often that politicians risk losing votes for something that they believe in, and I give them credit for that — even though I think their positions are utter nonsense. Your thoughts?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mitt Romney and Abortion Politics', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-01T19:33:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec5a677d-bffe-571a-9d4e-16bec1d86fe5', 'word_count': 135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec5a677d-bffe-571a-9d4e-16bec1d86fe5'}, {'abstract': 'If state and local governments had not cut back so much, the broader economy would be stronger today. So why did they do what they did?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/02/your-money/framing-prevents-needed-stimulus-economic-view.html', 'snippet': 'If state and local governments had not cut back so much, the broader economy would be stronger today. So why did they do what they did?', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHY have so many teachers, police officers, firefighters and other public workers been laid off since the financial crisis hit — and why are so few being offered new jobs now?', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/business/02-VIEW/02-VIEW-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 590, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/business/02-VIEW/02-VIEW-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1180, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/business/02-VIEW/02-VIEW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/02/business/02-VIEW/02-VIEW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/business/02-VIEW/02-VIEW-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Framing’ Prevents Needed Stimulus', 'kicker': 'Economic View', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Framing’ Prevents Needed Stimulus', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Employees', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-01T19:52:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert J. Shiller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Shiller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/16ce4267-2d8d-5acc-904a-b889dbfa74e1', 'word_count': 1014, 'uri': 'nyt://article/16ce4267-2d8d-5acc-904a-b889dbfa74e1'}, {'abstract': 'With his party’s nominating convention approaching, President Obama started a four-day campaign swing in Iowa on Saturday, returning to the state where he opened his unlikely quest for the presidency five years ago.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/01/obama-returns-to-iowa-on-eve-of-his-convention/', 'snippet': 'With his party’s nominating convention approaching, President Obama started a four-day campaign swing in Iowa on Saturday, returning to the state where he opened his unlikely quest for the presidency five years ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'URBANDALE, Iowa — With his party’s nominating convention approaching next week, President Obama\xa0started a four-day, four-state campaign trip on Saturday in Iowa, the state where he opened his quest for the presidency five years ago.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Visits Swing States Before Convention', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-01T20:03:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jackie Calmes', 'person': [{'fir