. But he is a big civic booster, and he believes that the Indy-car race on the streets around the Inner Harbor can become like the Preakness — only with more horsepower.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/sports/dog-andretti/dog-andretti-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 813, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/sports/dog-andretti/dog-andretti-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1625, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/sports/dog-andretti/dog-andretti-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/02/sports/dog-andretti/dog-andretti-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/sports/dog-andretti/dog-andretti-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Trying to Win Race He Helped Save', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trying to Win Race He Helped Save', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANDRETTI, MICHAEL', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Racing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-01T20:15:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Auto Racing', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Caldwell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caldwell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/20b2d0ee-60a1-5b56-9bdc-658ada8d856f', 'word_count': 984, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20b2d0ee-60a1-5b56-9bdc-658ada8d856f'}, {'abstract': 'Fredy Montero, 25, a native of Colombia, has played for the Seattle Sounders since 2009. He hopes to play in Europe someday.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/01/30-seconds-with-fredy-montero/', 'snippet': 'Fredy Montero, 25, a native of Colombia, has played for the Seattle Sounders since 2009. He hopes to play in Europe someday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After coming off the bench in four of the previous six games, Fredy Montero returned to the Seattle Sounders’ starting lineup last weekend against Chivas USA and scored his first hat trick in his 100th game in Major League Soccer. That increased his season total to 11 goals, giving him four consecutive seasons with 10 or more for the Sounders.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '30 Seconds With Fredy Montero', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '30 Seconds With Fredy Montero: A Hot Scorer Tries to Stay Cool', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Montero, Fredy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Seattle Sounders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Seattle (Wash)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-01T20:19:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Bell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1352b107-bbdf-51c6-803d-594e08020c39', 'word_count': 738, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1352b107-bbdf-51c6-803d-594e08020c39'}, {'abstract': 'Dan Duquette is nearing the end of his first season as the Baltimore Orioles’ executive vice president for baseball operations, and his first team has been better than any rational person could have expected.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/01/duquette-and-orioles-back-in-the-game/', 'snippet': 'Dan Duquette is nearing the end of his first season as the Baltimore Orioles’ executive vice president for baseball operations, and his first team has been better than any rational person could have expected.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than most, Dan Duquette understands the need to share credit for a team’s success. As the general manager of the Boston Red Sox from 1994 to 2001, Duquette acquired many of the players who would win the team’s first championship in 86 years, in 2004. While his successor, Theo Epstein, got the glory, Duquette spent nearly a decade without a job in the majors.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Duquette and Orioles Back in the Game', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Extra Bases: Duquette and Orioles Back in the Game', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duquette, Dan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baltimore Orioles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-01T20:20:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9f5ab57-5515-545a-a5b8-3e1541ce9de6', 'word_count': 600, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9f5ab57-5515-545a-a5b8-3e1541ce9de6'}, {'abstract': 'Defenders and critics in France agree that the actual impact of a law banning full-face veils in public places has been far less dramatic than the politicized prologue to it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/02/world/europe/tolerance-eases-impact-of-french-ban-on-full-face-veils.html', 'snippet': 'Defenders and critics in France agree that the actual impact of a law banning full-face veils in public places has been far less dramatic than the politicized prologue to it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — During a recent protest in Marseille, seven people were suddenly surrounded by the police, bundled into a van and brought in for questioning. Their offense was not the demonstration itself but the balaclavas they were wearing, a violation of the French law banning full-face veils in public places, passed in April 2011.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/world/02france/FRANCE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 684, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/world/02france/FRANCE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1369, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/world/02france/02france-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/02/world/02france/02france-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbna