usic and cultures — living in Nigeria, France and Chicago, playing blues, reggae and Afrobeat — but kept returning to Philadelphia, his hometown, died on Aug. 23 at a hospice in Wyndmoor, Pa. He was 70.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/arts/dog-LANCASTER-obit/dog-LANCASTER-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 614, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/arts/dog-LANCASTER-obit/dog-LANCASTER-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1229, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/arts/dog-LANCASTER-obit/dog-LANCASTER-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/02/arts/dog-LANCASTER-obit/dog-LANCASTER-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/arts/dog-LANCASTER-obit/dog-LANCASTER-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Byard Lancaster, Jazz Alto Saxophonist, Dies at 70', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Byard Lancaster, 70, Jazz Alto Saxophonist', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lancaster, Byard', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-01T22:58:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Ratliff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ratliff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/47d2f345-88a0-55dc-906e-e1e1bcd43ae0', 'word_count': 645, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47d2f345-88a0-55dc-906e-e1e1bcd43ae0'}, {'abstract': 'Forty years ago, the N.H.L. stars of Team Canada played the Soviet national team in the Summit Series. Vladimir Petrov, who played for the Soviets, recalls the memorable first game.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/01/the-summit-series-of-1972-talking-with-vladimir-petrov/', 'snippet': 'Forty years ago, the N.H.L. stars of Team Canada played the Soviet national team in the Summit Series. Vladimir Petrov, who played for the Soviets, recalls the memorable first game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Forty years ago Sunday, on Sept. 2, 1972, in Montreal, one of the most stunning upsets in the history of sports took place. Team Canada — an N.H.L. all-star team led by Phil Esposito, Brad Park, Yvan Cournoyer, Frank and Peter Mahovlich, Bobby Clarke,Ken Dryden and the Rangers’ GAG Line of Jean Ratelle, Rod Gilbert and Vic Hadfield — met the Soviet national team, the world and Olympic champion but a group that had never played a game against professional opponents.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Summit Series of 1972: Talking With Vladimir Petrov', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clarke, Bobby', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dryden, Ken', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Esposito, Phil', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Petrov, Vladimir', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Rangers', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-01T23:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8469368-a8cf-5c1b-9ecc-992a2ce91365', 'word_count': 656, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8469368-a8cf-5c1b-9ecc-992a2ce91365'}, {'abstract': 'Nicolas Almagro of Spain will advance to the fourth round of the Open for the first time after fighting off a spirited challenge from the up-and-coming American teenager Jack Sock.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/01/almagro-ends-socks-run-in-four-sets/', 'snippet': 'Nicolas Almagro of Spain will advance to the fourth round of the Open for the first time after fighting off a spirited challenge from the up-and-coming American teenager Jack Sock.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nicolas Almagro of Spain will advance to the fourth round of the United States Open for the first time after fighting off a spirited challenge from the up-and-coming American teenager Jack Sock on Saturday afternoon. Almagro, seeded 11th, pulled out a 7-6 (3), 6-7 (4), 7-6 (2), 6-1 victory in the sultry afternoon heat of the half-sunbaked, half-shaded Grandstand Stadium.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Almagro Ends Sock’s Run in Four Sets', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-01T23:00:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By THOMAS LIN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'LIN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b98ac9e5-d8ea-5daf-83bd-228411ed28e1', 'word_count': 415, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b98ac9e5-d8ea-5daf-83bd-228411ed28e1'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Shelton and his longtime design partner, Lee Mindel, were known for interior designs that blended clean lines with references to classical periods to create opulent settings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/02/arts/design/peter-shelton-architect-who-made-luxury-minimal-dies-at-67.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Shelton and his longtime design partner, Lee Mindel, were known for interior designs that blended clean lines with references to classical periods to create opulent settings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Peter Shelton, an award-winning architect whose sleek yet luxurious interior designs won his firm commissions for the homes of wealthy people and for corporate showcases like the headquarters of Polo Ralph Lauren, died on Aug. 26 at his home in Manhattan. He was 67.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/nyregion/dog-SHELTON1-obit/dog-SHELTON1-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 709, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/nyregion/dog-SHELTON1-obit/dog-SHELTON1-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1418, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/nyregion/dog-SHELTON1-obit/dog-SHELTON1-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/02/nyregion/dog-SHELTON1-obit/dog-SHELTON1-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/nyregion/dog-SHELTON1-obit/dog-SHELTON1-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Peter Shelton, Architect Who Made Luxury Minimal, Dies at 67', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Peter Shelton, 67, Architect Who Made Luxury Minimal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shelton, Peter', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-01T23:07:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Leslie Kaufman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Leslie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaufman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/013b15fd-72fd-5987-9a53-123dc746e940', 'word_count': 714, 'uri': 'nyt://article/013b15fd-72fd-5987-9a53-123dc746e940'}, {'abstract': 'Marin Cilic of Croatia, seeded 12th and able to force errors, won, 6-3, 6-4, 6-7 (3), 6-3.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/01/in-battle-for-round-of-16-cilic-prevails-over-nishikori/', 'snippet': 'Marin Cilic of Croatia, seeded 12th and able to force errors, won, 6-3, 6-4, 6-7 (3), 6-3.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Early in the third set, into a sky bright with a blistering sun, Kei Nishikori of Japan tossed the ball high and aced Marin Cilic of Croatia to take a 4-3 lead. For nearly 2,800 spectators, there was hope that the contest might extend beyond three sets. \xa0They got their wish.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Battle for Round of 16, Cilic Prevails Over Nishikori', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-01T23:21:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By JOHN MARTIN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MARTIN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2e39fa1-1fe2-5f3e-ad6d-dd64d739551d', 'word_count': 362, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2e39fa1-1fe2-5f3e-ad6d-dd64d739551d'}, {'abstract': 'Canada’s hockey pride nearly proved costly against a mysterious Soviet team in the 1972 Summit Series.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/02/sports/hockey/after-canada-stopped-laughing-at-soviets-hockey-summit-series-got-serious.html', 'snippet': 'Canada’s hockey pride nearly proved costly against a mysterious Soviet team in the 1972 Summit Series.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a September afternoon in Montreal in 1972, I stood next to the Rangers’ Brad Park at the Forum as we watched the Soviet Union’s best hockey players go through their bizarre practice rituals. In one routine, they swarmed at center ice like mad bees.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/sports/hockey/02eskenazi/02eskenazi-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/02/sports/hockey/02eskenazi/02eskenazi-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/sports/hockey/02eskenazi/02eskenazi-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 655, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/sports/hockey/02eskenazi/02eskenazi-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1279, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Once They Stopped Laughing, Things Got Serious Fast', 'kicker': 'Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Once They Stopped Laughing, Things Got Serious Fast', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Summit Series', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dryden, Ken', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Esposito, Phil', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Henderson, Paul', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-01T23:33:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gerald Eskenazi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gerald', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eskenazi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/667491bc-b66d-54bc-98db-94c72e12ef7a', 'word_count': 1356, 'uri': 'nyt://article/667491bc-b66d-54bc-98db-94c72e12ef7a'}, {'abstract': 'The polling data so far suggests that the Republican convention may produce only a modest bounce in the polls for Mitt Romney.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/01/sept-1-romneys-convention-bounce-appears-middling-so-far/', 'snippet': 'The polling data so far suggests that the Republican convention may produce only a modest bounce in the polls for Mitt Romney.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Republican National Convention in Tampa, Fla. received mediocre television ratings — and the polling data so far suggests that it may produce only a modest bounce in the polls for Mitt Romney.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sept. 1: Romney’s Convention Bounce Appears Middling So Far', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-01T23:47:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a264758-8e10-5229-a717-f53676914a10', 'word_count': 637, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a264758-8e10-5229-a717-f53676914a10'}, {'abstract': 'Something like a maximum-security prison for adults, Texas’ Phoenix Program plucks out the most serious offenders in the juvenile-justice system to undergo intensive counseling.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/02/us/phoenix-program-gives-texas-juveniles-intensive-counseling.html', 'snippet': 'Something like a maximum-security prison for adults, Texas’ Phoenix Program plucks out the most serious offenders in the juvenile-justice system to undergo intensive counseling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MART — The green-black lines of prison life are scrawled on 16-year-old Luis’s face: a cross on his left cheek, three dots arranged in a triangle under his left eye and “cholo” written vertically on his right cheek.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/03/us/03TTPhoenix/03TTPhoenix-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 846, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/03/us/03TTPhoenix/03TTPhoenix-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1692, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Giving Juveniles Intensive Counseling', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Giving Juveniles Intensive Counseling', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Juvenile Delinquency', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-02T00:32:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brandi Grissom', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brandi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grissom', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f78f