hrinking. The minimalist movement is most obviously exemplified by the casual, street-style shoes some professionals have begun wearing in competition.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Golf Shoes for on the Course and on the Town', 'kicker': 'On Par', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Shoes for on the Course And on the Town', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-02T16:46:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Pennington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pennington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03b88b00-dc17-5d22-b037-46c59f2b9320', 'word_count': 366, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03b88b00-dc17-5d22-b037-46c59f2b9320'}, {'abstract': 'Norman’s name comes up an awful lot even though he has played in only three PGA Tour events in the last five years.', 'web_url': 'https://onpar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/02/greg-norman-still-an-inspiration/', 'snippet': 'Norman’s name comes up an awful lot even though he has played in only three PGA Tour events in the last five years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Greg Norman’s name still comes up an awful lot even though he has played in only three PGA Tour events in the last five years.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Greg Norman Fan Club Is a Mutual Admiration Society', 'kicker': 'On Par', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Greg Norman Fan Club: Mostly Mutual Admiration', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Norman, Greg', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-02T16:55:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Pennington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pennington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e67d5edf-32bb-5b58-9e68-f34ff27eed32', 'word_count': 499, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e67d5edf-32bb-5b58-9e68-f34ff27eed32'}, {'abstract': 'A theory: Those bad bounces and strange snags of summer turn favorable when days shorten and the air cools down.', 'web_url': 'https://onpar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/02/autumn-brings-out-the-best-in-golf-gods/', 'snippet': 'A theory: Those bad bounces and strange snags of summer turn favorable when days shorten and the air cools down.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I have a theory that the golf gods go on vacation in the fall. In the summer, they are much too busy to take time off. They have the major championships to keep an eye on, all the amateur tournaments and thousands of club championships.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shorter Days and a Chill in the Air Can Warm Fate’s Heart', 'kicker': 'On Par', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Shorter Days and a Chill in the Air Can Warm Fate’s Heart', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-02T16:58:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Pennington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pennington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'typ