stname': 'Carr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a444f13-9ed7-5425-b443-c1765348743b', 'word_count': 1058, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a444f13-9ed7-5425-b443-c1765348743b'}, {'abstract': 'We humans are deeply divided on fundamental moral, religious and philosophical questions. But that can be a good thing.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/02/in-praise-of-the-clash-of-cultures/', 'snippet': 'We humans are deeply divided on fundamental moral, religious and philosophical questions. But that can be a good thing.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Praise of the Clash of Cultures', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christians and Christianity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-02T21:00:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carlos Fraenkel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carlos', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fraenkel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e2239c5-786b-5405-b8ba-9ef861ab8c3c', 'word_count': 1966, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e2239c5-786b-5405-b8ba-9ef861ab8c3c'}, {'abstract': 'Following the Republican National Convention, President Obama added a new element to his usual stump speech, describing Mitt Romney and Congressional Republicans as backward-looking.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/03/us/politics/obama-see-republicans-as-stuck-in-past.html', 'snippet': 'Following the Republican National Convention, President Obama added a new element to his usual stump speech, describing Mitt Romney and Congressional Republicans as backward-looking.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOULDER, Colo. — As President Obama heads into the Democratic National Convention this week, he is seizing on the just-concluded Republican convention to ramp up his argument that Mitt Romney and his party are stuck in the policies of the past and are afraid to spell out the details of their plans.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/03/us/03obama-2/03obama-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 364, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/03/us/03obama-2/03obama-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 364}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/03/us/03obama-2/03obama-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/03/us/03obama-2/03obama-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/03/us/03obama-2/03obama-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/03/us/03obama-2/03obama-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit'