'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/03/arts/dance/20120903-competition-slide-434Q/20120903-competition-slide-434Q-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/03/arts/dance/20120903-competition-slide-434Q/20120903-competition-slide-434Q-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Chance to Dance', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Dance Alliance', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-02T22:15:14+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Arts', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/6612f9eb-4657-51b4-96ac-544898d23a0a', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/6612f9eb-4657-51b4-96ac-544898d23a0a'}, {'abstract': 'The National Geographic Channel said that Melissa Bachman, an animal hunter who writes for a blog called “Hardcore Huntress,” will no longer be a participant in the coming reality series “Ultimate Survivor Alaska.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/03/arts/television/national-geographic-takes-hunter-off-tv-show.html', 'snippet': 'The National Geographic Channel said that Melissa Bachman, an animal hunter who writes for a blog called “Hardcore Huntress,” will no longer be a participant in the coming reality series “Ultimate Survivor Alaska.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The National Geographic Channel said on Friday that Melissa Bachman, an animal hunter who writes for a blog called “Hardcore Huntress,” will no longer be a participant in the coming reality series “Ultimate Survivor Alaska,” after an online petition protesting her involvement received more than 13,000 signatures in less than 24 hours. According to the Hollywood Reporter’s Web site the petition posted on Change.org by Tim Martell, a Florida resident, called for a boycott of National Geographic and stated that the cable channel had abandoned its “traditional stance of conservation and protection” by working with Ms. Bachman, who also has her own Web site that contains hunting videos, tips and a photographic trophy room. “The National Geographic Channel has carefully considered the public discussion of our series on surviving the wilds of Alaska currently in production and premiering sometime next year,” the cable channel said in a statement. “Upon further reflection we plan to eliminate one of the survivalists from the ensemble cast, Melissa Bachman. Hunting is not the focus of the show, and we regret the misinformation that has clouded what we hope will be an exciting adventure series set in the incredible Alaskan landscape.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'National Geographic Takes Hunter Off TV Show', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'National Geographic Takes Hunter Off TV Show', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Geographic Channel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hunting and Trapping', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bachman, Melissa', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-02T22:16:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ef6bd84-c81c-51c5-af1f-4311dd13bb60', 'word_count': 200, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ef6bd84-c81c-51c5-af1f-4311dd13bb60'}, {'abstract': 'The Spanish filmmaker David Victori was the grand prize winner of the first Your Film Festival.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/02/spanish-filmmaker-wins-prize-at-online-festival/', 'snippet': 'The Spanish filmmaker David Victori was the grand prize winner of the first Your Film Festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Spanish filmmaker David Victori was the grand prize winner of the first Your Film Festival, an online competition sponsored by YouTube, Scott Free Productions and Emirates airlines, for his short film “The Guilt,” about a man out for revenge after his wife’s murder. The announcement was made at the Venice Film Festival on Sunday after his film was selected from a pool of 10 finalists by a jury that included the director Ridley Scott and the actor Michael Fassbender.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spanish Filmmaker Wins Prize at Online Festival', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spanish Filmmaker Wins Prize at Online Festival', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Contests and Prizes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venice International Film Festival', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fassbender, Michael', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Emirates Airlines', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Scott Free Productions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'YouTube.com', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-02T22:23:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4110847-60fe-56bf-a03f-010a548fbcc1', 'word_count': 134, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4110847-60fe-56bf-a03f-010a548fbcc1'}, {'abstract': 'The festival will host the latest installment the series — in which popular movie scripts are performed by contemporary actors — with a reading of Alan Ball’s screenplay for the 1999 film “American Beauty.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/03/movies/live-read-series-at-toronto-festival.html', 'snippet': 'The festival will host the latest installment the series — in which popular movie scripts are performed by contemporary actors — with a reading of Alan Ball’s screenplay for the 1999 film “American Beauty.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Toronto International Film Festival will host the latest installment of the director Jason Reitman’s “Live Read” series — in which popular movie scripts are performed by contemporary actors — with an unrehearsed reading of Alan Ball’s screenplay for the 1999 film “American Beauty.” The performance will take place on Thursday at the Ryerson Theater in Toronto; Mr. Reitman, above, will announce the cast for the reading on his Twitter account, @jasonreitman, in the days before the event. Tickets can be purchased at tiff.net/festival. Mr. Reitman created the series last year in collaboration with Elvis Mitchell, a former film critic for The New York Times, for the film society at the Los Angeles County Museum of Art. Previous entries included presentations of “The Apartment” with Paul Rudd and Emma Stone at the TimesCenter in Manhattan, and “The Big Lebowski” featuring Seth Rogen in Los Angeles, among 