 say it is doubtful a deal can be completed in time to use regular officials for Week 1.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/03/sports/football/nfl-football-roundup.html', 'snippet': 'People on both sides of the negotiations say it is doubtful a deal can be completed in time to use regular officials for Week 1.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The N.F.L. sent a memo to its teams Sunday indicating that it thought Friday that it was close to a deal to end the lockout of officials but that negotiations broke off the next day after a brief meeting in which officials made clear that retirement benefits remained the key sticking point. Now, people on both sides say it is doubtful a deal can be completed in time to use regular officials for Week 1, which starts Wednesday when the Giants host the Cowboys.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'N.F.L. and Officials Still at Odds', 'kicker': 'Roundup', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'N.F.L. and Officials Still at Odds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Officiating (Sports)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lockouts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-02T23:35:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judy Battista', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Battista', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e1ea197-b38b-5cc0-b49d-6d53d1a31492', 'word_count': 522, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e1ea197-b38b-5cc0-b49d-6d53d1a31492'}, {'abstract': 'The Romney campaign clearly hasn’t thought about how eating only the tops of muffins will play to a crucial voting bloc: Asian immigrants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/03/opinion/my-asian-dad-and-mitt-romneys-muffin-tops.html', 'snippet': 'The Romney campaign clearly hasn’t thought about how eating only the tops of muffins will play to a crucial voting bloc: Asian immigrants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SOME supporters of Mitt Romney, in an effort to make him seem more human (or at least humanoid), have been disseminating a story, first told by a biographer, about how their candidate has a charmingly eccentric habit: he eats only the tops of muffins. His theory is that during the baking process, the butter sinks to the bottom. This story conveys so many things: our guy is an everyday Joe — he eats muffins, not crumpets. And look, even his breakfast is an opportunity to make disciplined decisions — just think how he’ll do with the budget. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Muffins Say About Mitt Romney', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What Muffins Say About Mitt Romney', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muffins', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Asian-Americans', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-02T23:37:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marie Myung-Ok Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marie', 'middlename': 'Myung-ok', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_