asia/', 'snippet': 'A delegation representing members of the American Association of Independent Music will visit Hong Kong; Seoul, South Korea; and Shanghai to meet with business contacts and study foreign markets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To compete in the global marketplace, the major record companies have branches and subsidiaries all over the world. Most small labels do not have that advantage, so for help they are turning to federal and state government agencies.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Small Music Labels to Court Asia', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Small Music Labels to Court Asia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Assn of Independent Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ANTIBALAS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hong Kong', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Seoul (South Korea)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Shanghai (China)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-02T23:51:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ac8b008-b93d-5767-a216-32848aeaa11a', 'word_count': 338, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ac8b008-b93d-5767-a216-32848aeaa11a'}, {'abstract': 'Rebels set off two bombs amid military buildings in the Syrian capital Sunday, as the new United Nations envoy to the country refused to call for President Bashar al-Assad to step down.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/03/world/middleeast/rebels-bomb-heavily-guarded-neighborhood-in-damascus.html', 'snippet': 'Rebels set off two bombs amid military buildings in the Syrian capital Sunday, as the new United Nations envoy to the country refused to call for President Bashar al-Assad to step down.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — Rebels set off two bombs among a cluster of military headquarters buildings in the Syrian capital, Damascus, on Sunday, as the new United Nations envoy for Syria pointedly refused to call for President Bashar al-Assad to give up power.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/03/world/middleeast/03syria_cnd/03syria_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/03/world/middleeast/03syria_cnd/03syria_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/03/world/middleeast/03syria_cnd/03syria_cnd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 651, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/03/world/middleeast/03syria_cnd/03syria_cnd-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1302, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/03/world/middleeast/03syria_cnd/03syria_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/03/world/middleeast/03syria_cnd/03syria_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rebels Bomb Heavily Guarded Damascus Neighborhood', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rebels Bomb Heavily Guarded Damascus Neighborhood', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War and Guerrilla Warfare', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brahimi, Lakhdar', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-02T23:54:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By David D. Kirkpatrick and Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7fa46fe-5411-520d-bbea-1e108d04f60a', 'word_count': 1181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7fa46fe-5411-520d-bbea-1e108d04f60a'}, {'abstract': 'Labor Day is the last stop before we go careening into fall, a holiday in school-bus yellow.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/03/opinion/rounding-the-seasonal-mark.html', 'snippet': 'Labor Day is the last stop before we go careening into fall, a holiday in school-bus yellow.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Other holidays are celebrated for the day and the season itself — Thanksgiving, Christmas, the Fourth of July. But Labor Day, as most of us know it, is a holiday about what comes next. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rounding the Seasonal Mark', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rounding the Seasonal Mark', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor Day', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seasons and Months', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-02T23:57:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7ff18d1-a723-5acd-85b3-b2493df9d22e', 'word_count': 290, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7ff18d1-a723-5acd-85b3-b2493df9d22e'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Kriegsman, whose long career at The Washington Post coincided with a period of growth and diversification in American dance, was the first dance critic to win a Pulitzer Prize.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/03/arts/dance/alan-m-kriegsman-dance-critic-dies-at-84.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Kriegsman, whose long career at The Washington Post coincided with a period of growth and diversification in American dance, was the first dance critic to win a Pulitzer Prize.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alan M. Kriegsman, a longtime dance critic for The Washington Post and the first dance critic to win a Pulitzer Prize, died on Friday at his home in Washington. He was 84.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/03/arts/kriegsman-obit/kriegsman-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1008, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/03/arts/kriegsman-obit/kriegsma