 'The mysterious crash of a Ferrari in Beijing last March is now having repercussions at the highest levels of the Chinese Communist Party. President Hu Jintao’s chief aide has been effectively sidelined — his son died in the crash — amid allegation...', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — When the chief of staff to President Hu Jintao was moved to a lesser position last week, it sounded like so much inside baseball, a ho-hum reshuffling of personnel as the Chinese Communist Party prepares for a leadership change this autumn.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In China, a Ferrari Crashes and the Party Is Dented', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Luxury Goods', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hu Jintao', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ferrari SpA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-03T04:54:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark McDonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McDonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09adba73-a096-5a48-9611-f7f6549f42fe', 'word_count': 672, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09adba73-a096-5a48-9611-f7f6549f42fe'}, {'abstract': 'Indian students battling homesickness in Wyoming head for the cricket pitch.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/03/pitch-on-the-pasture-cricket-in-the-cowboy-state/', 'snippet': 'Indian students battling homesickness in Wyoming head for the cricket pitch.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The heart of the University of Wyoming’s campus in Laramie is Prexy’s Pasture, a big, grassy area surrounded by blue spruce and mountain pine. According to university lore, the pasture was where students grazed their horses in the late 19th century; a standing university rule dictates that the president, or “prexy,” has sole rights to the area for livestock grazing. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pitch on the Pasture: Cricket in the Cowboy State', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cricket (Game)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Wyoming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wyoming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-03T04:59:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nina Swamidoss McConigley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nina', 'middlename': 'Swamidoss', 'lastname': 'McConigley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5059dfce-f547-52d9-81aa-3e1aa9faf190', 'word_count': 264, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5059dfce-f547-52d9-81aa-3e1aa9faf190'}, {'abstract': 'Students all around the world have been preparing for the start of the school year this month, and what a start it has been, with protests and scandals in Hong Kong, in London, in the Ivy League.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/03/hey-teacher-leave-those-kids-alone/', 'snippet': 'Students all around the world have been preparing for the start of the school year this month, and what a start it has been, with protests and scandals in Hong Kong, in London, in the Ivy League.', 'lead_p