9/03/chess-gets-the-artistic-treatment-in-new-saatchi-show/', 'snippet': 'Sixteen chess sets designed by contemporary artists are the focus of a new exhibition at the Saatchi Gallery in London.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since the new Islamic art galleries opened at the Metropolitan Museum of Art last fall, one of the most popular objects on display has been a chess set dating from 12th-century Iran, one that looks surprisingly modern because the pieces are highly abstracted. The Shah (king), for example, is represented by a large throne.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chess Gets the Artistic Treatment in a New Saatchi Show', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cattelan, Maurizio', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hirst, Damien', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCarthy, Paul', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Noble, Tim', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Whiteread, Rachel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Saatchi Gallery', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Somerset House', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-03T15:30:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Vogel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vogel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/94edb807-6cce-50d3-9d90-2c31e0c467b5', 'word_count': 205, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94edb807-6cce-50d3-9d90-2c31e0c467b5'}, {'abstract': 'The answer to who got one of the biggest scoops of the early 20th century — the interview with the surviving telegraph operator from the Titanic — is murky.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/03/100-years-after-the-titanic-still-wondering-who-got-the-story/', 'snippet': 'The answer to who got one of the biggest scoops of the early 20th century — the interview with the surviving telegraph operator from the Titanic — is murky.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If newspaper articles had routinely carried reporters’ bylines 100 years ago, there would be no question now about who got one of the biggest scoops of the early 20th century, the April 18, 1912, interview with the surviving telegraph operator from the Titanic.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '100 Years After the Titanic, Still Wondering Who Got the Story', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mystery of Who Got Big Titanic Interview', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maritime Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ships and Shipping', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shipwrecks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Titanic (Ship)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berger, Meyer', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marconi, Guglielmo', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roosevelt, Theodore', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-03T15:39:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Barron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aaebad6c-1665-5a6f-9b4b-f3dfdf07d725', 'word_count': 1106, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aaebad6c-1665-5a6f-9b4b-f3dfdf07d725'}, {'abstract': 'A clerk of the Supreme Court provided a rare inside look at how the justices are prepared to rule on matters of life and death in capital cases.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/us/in-capital-punishment-cases-weeks-go-into-deciding-last-minute-reprieves-sidebar.html', 'snippet': 'A clerk of the Supreme Court provided a rare inside look at how the justices are prepared to rule on matters of life and death in capital cases.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — John Balentine was an hour away from being put to death in Texas last month when the Supreme Court granted him a stay of execution.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'To Beat the Execution Clock, the Justices Prepare Early', 'kicker': 'Sidebar', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Beat the Execution Clock, the Justices Prepare Early', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scalia, Antonin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Balentine, John', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-03T15:48:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Liptak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liptak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/22f60dda-b398-5bb0-909e-3ff631fcac32', 'word_count': 862, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22f60dda-b398-5bb0-909e-3ff631fcac32'}, {'abstract': 'Russian public and private schools seem to exist in two different countries, with public schools still firmly rooted in the Soviet Union.', 'web_url': 'https://lati