n Richmond, Ky.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/03/the-stonewall-of-the-west/', 'snippet': 'Patrick Cleburne, an Irish immigrant turned Confederate major general, led the rebels to a decisive victory in Richmond, Ky.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Generals Robert E. Lee and Thomas J. “Stonewall” Jackson were winning their smashing victory at the Second Battle of Bull Run in Virginia, another Confederate army triumphed even more decisively at the little known battle of Richmond, Ky., led in part by the man destined to be known as the “Stonewall of the West”: Gen. Patrick Cleburne. Richmond was potentially even more decisive than Bull Run — it opened Kentucky to Confederate invasion, giving the rebels a possible route to the aorta of the Union war effort, the Ohio River.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Stonewall of the West', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tennessee', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-03T16:30:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phil Leigh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leigh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5b856e2-a98a-5ad2-9292-cffb0f2c68a6', 'word_count': 1519, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5b856e2-a98a-5ad2-9292-cffb0f2c68a6'}, {'abstract': 'Up to 15 percent of strokes affect people no older than 45 — and the sooner the correct diagnosis is made, the less likely the result will be lifelong impairment.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/03/too-young-to-have-a-stroke-think-again/', 'snippet': 'Up to 15 percent of strokes affect people no older than 45 — and the sooner the correct diagnosis is made, the less likely the result will be lifelong impairment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Six years ago, Todd McGee was a lean, athletic 34-year-old working in construction and living with his wife and toddler daughter on Martha’s Vineyard, where he spent summer weekends surfing. A stroke changed his life forever.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/04/science/04BROD_SPAN/04BROD-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/04/science/04BROD_SPAN/04BROD-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/04/science/04BROD_SPAN/04BROD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 564, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/04/science/04BROD_SPAN/04BROD-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1127, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/04/science/04BROD_SPAN/04BROD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/04/science/04BROD_SPAN/04BROD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/04/science/04BROD_SPAN/04BROD-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Too Young to Have a S