Stark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Rebecca', 'middlename': 'Lee', 'lastname': 'Douglas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/6430f173-aadf-5610-9b85-7579303feb47', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/6430f173-aadf-5610-9b85-7579303feb47'}, {'abstract': 'This year’s lineup at the Telluride Film Festival featured movies that, while clearly fictional, have that bracing feeling of reality.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/movies/four-days-of-films-at-telluride.html', 'snippet': 'This year’s lineup at the Telluride Film Festival featured movies that, while clearly fictional, have that bracing feeling of reality.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TELLURIDE, Colo. — A film festival held almost 9,000 feet above sea level on a holiday weekend may not be the likeliest setting for philosophical speculation, but for the past four days the Telluride Film Festival has offered something like a seminar on the nature of truth. In an age of reality television, journalistic fakery and political mendacity everyone knows that words and images can distort and mislead. And film is a particularly unstable medium, alluring us with a promise of honesty while it feeds us ever more elaborate fantasies.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/04/arts/0904TELLURIDE1/0904TELLURIDE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 389, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/04/arts/0904TELLURIDE1/0904TELLURIDE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 389}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/04/arts/0904TELLURIDE1/0904TELLURIDE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 697, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/04/arts/0904TELLURIDE1/0904TELLURIDE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1394, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/04/arts/0904TELLURIDE1/0904TELLURIDE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/04/arts/0904TELLURIDE1/0904TELLURIDE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/04/arts/0904TELLURIDE1/0904TELLURIDE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Film Festival With Truths to Tell', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Film Festival With Truths to Tell', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Audiard, Jacques', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telluride Film Festival', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murray, Bill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Haneke, Michael', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baumbach, Noah', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Telluride (Colo)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-03T22:16:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4506302d-6272-5ea4-8ebe-12013fee12ac', 'word_count': 1240, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4506302d-6272-5ea4-8ebe-12013fee12ac'}, {'abstract': 'The writer uses statistics to show that John Isner should put more emphasis on his net game over his baseline game to produce the best results.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/03/staying-back-is-a-losing-strategy-for-isner/', 'snippet': 'The writer uses statistics to show that John Isner should put more emphasis on his net game over his baseline game to produce the best results.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Staying Back Is a Losing Strategy for Isner', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-03T22:27:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': "By CRAIG O'SHANNESSY", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Craig', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'SHANNESSY", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db3a5078-bb19-5581-b53f-8c2cbb53a9e9', 'word_count': 839, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db3a5078-bb19-5581-b53f-8c2cbb53a9e9'}, {'abstract': 'On Tuesday, BuzzFeed will take over the science museum in Charlotte, N.C., and allow conventioneers to mix with other party animals.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/03/social-media-site-creates-buzz-with-convention-parties/', 'snippet': 'On Tuesday, BuzzFeed will take over the science museum in Charlotte, N.C., and allow conventioneers to mix with other party animals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the Republican convention last week, the big bash sponsored by BuzzFeed at the Florida Aquarium in Tampa was among the most exotic and most talked about, featuring mermaids (undulating in full fin alongside fish in glass tanks) and penguins (sitting adorably in little wagons, with a helpful handler reminding revelers that, yes, even cute penguins do bite).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Social Media Site Creates Buzz With Convention Parties', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-03T22:32:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Barbaro and Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barbaro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b5e638f-a76b-53c9-81ef-ec163b4d804b', 'word_count': 158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b5e638f-a76b-53c9-81ef-ec163b4d804b'}, {'abstract': 'Kelly Shoppach and Daniel Murphy hit two-run shots in a Mets rally, but the Cardinals hung on.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/sports/baseball/mets-late-rally-not-enough-to-beat-cardinals.html', 'snippet': 'Kelly Shoppach and Daniel Murphy hit two-run shots in a Mets rally, but the Cardinals hung on.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ST. LOUIS — As reporters filed into the visiting manager’s office at Busch Stadium on Monday morning, one mentioned to Terry Collins that the Mets were roughly the same number of games outside a playoff spot that the St. Louis Cardinals were one year ago during their exhilarating World Series-winning run.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source'