 thinks the Fed should do, if anything, to stimulate the weak economy. What is known is that, without more help, the economy is likely to remain weak, or grow weaker, through the rest of this year. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mr. Bernanke’s Next Task', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mr. Bernanke’s Next Task', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bernanke, Ben S', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T02:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a5617ed-eefe-5d03-8f3a-a3d1d53bbc1b', 'word_count': 545, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a5617ed-eefe-5d03-8f3a-a3d1d53bbc1b'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on September 4, 2012.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/pageoneplus/corrections-september-4-2012.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on September 4, 2012.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRONT PAGE', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: September 4, 2012', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T02:00:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/2bdc3dcb-cd02-5bce-b8fc-444ca1fd68af', 'word_count': 325, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2bdc3dcb-cd02-5bce-b8fc-444ca1fd68af'}, {'abstract': 'The police used rubber bullets to disperse a crowd of striking gold miners on Monday at the Gold Fields mine, just east of Johannesburg, injuring four of them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/world/africa/striking-south-african-miners-hurt-in-clash-with-police.html', 'snippet': 'The police used rubber bullets to disperse a crowd of striking gold miners on Monday at the Gold Fields mine, just east of Johannesburg, injuring four of them.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The police used rubber bullets to disperse a crowd of striking gold miners on Monday at the Gold Fields mine, right, just east of Johannesburg, injuring four of them. Four people were arrested. The miners have been on strike since June. The clash came days after Julius S. Malema, a former leader of the Youth League of the African National Congress who has called for South Africa’s mines to be nationalized, visited the miners. It also followed an episode on Aug. 16, when the police opened fire on workers engaged in a strike at a platinum mine in Marikana, northwest of Johannesburg, killing 34 of them, a response that reminded many of apartheid-era police violence against demonstrators. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/04/world/BRIEFS-SOUTH-AFRICA/BRIEFS-SOUTH-AFRICA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 385, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/04/world/BRIEFS-SOUTH-AFRICA/BRIEFS-SOUTH-AFRICA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 385}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'i