ous composer Leonard Bernstein.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Vandals lately have been marauding through Green-Wood Cemetery, the historic gem atop the heights of Brooklyn, toppling and shattering dozens of gravestones, befouling mausoleums and beheading a marble angel at the grave of a 5-year-old boy. But, just a few days earlier, a visitor to the cemetery had found the truer spirit of Green-Wood displayed at the simple grave of Leonard Bernstein, the prodigious composer and conductor who died in 1990. Someone had left a small garland of blossoms and an empty bottle of Jack Daniel’s sour mash whiskey to honor the maestro at rest.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bernstein at Green-Wood', 'kicker': 'Editorial | The City Life', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bernstein at Green-Wood', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Green-Wood Cemetery (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vandalism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cemeteries', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bernstein, Leonard', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T02:20:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Francis X. Clines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Francis', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Clines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab71df9b-d241-5f41-8194-5f203eb5692e', 'word_count': 321, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab71df9b-d241-5f41-8194-5f203eb5692e'}, {'abstract': 'Most of the illegal ivory seized in large-scale shipments in the past thre