liar-face-this-time-on-the-opposite-side-of-the-court/', 'snippet': 'Doubles partners Sara Errani and Roberta Vinci will meet in a singles quarterfinal on Wednesday, the first all-Italian quarterfinal in a Grand Slam event in the Open era.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the new doubles rankings are released after the United States Open, the Italian pair of Sara Errani and Roberta Vinci will occupy the top two spots, with Errani at No. 1 and Vinci at No. 2. The pair, who won the French Open and reached the Australian Open final this year, play their women’s doubles quarterfinal Tuesday morning in the first match on the Grandstand Court. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Familiar Face, This Time on the Opposite Side of the Court', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T02:58:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By BEN ROTHENBERG', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'ROTHENBERG', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/30c16d22-a19e-533d-bd14-ef3f990b96e7', 'word_count': 430, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30c16d22-a19e-533d-bd14-ef3f990b96e7'}, {'abstract': 'Remember the days when the political conventions actually mattered?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/opinion/political-conventions-are-not-what-they-used-to-be.html', 'snippet': 'Remember the days when the political conventions actually mattered?', 'lead_paragraph': 'What did I miss while I was away? Ah, yes, the Republican National Convention. I hear the Republicans nominated Mitt Romney and Paul Ryan for president and vice president. Imagine that.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York