2012/09/04/how-should-india-deal-with-changing-monsoons/', 'snippet': 'Rainwater harvesting, new crops and river management could help, experts say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In many parts of India, including in New Delhi and Mumbai, monsoon rains have picked up in recent weeks, bringing much-needed relief. But much of north, west and south India still have gotten only a fraction of the rain they normally receive, as I reported recently.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Should India Deal With Changing Monsoons?', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drought', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T05:08:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vikas Bajaj', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vikas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bajaj', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/934c77fb-ddd7-50cd-93a6-323b16dbd8f2', 'word_count': 863, 'uri': 'nyt://article/934c77fb-ddd7-50cd-93a6-323b16dbd8f2'}, {'abstract': 'Carl Richards makes the case for considering cost-per-use and buying things that last (and last).', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/striving-to-lead-more-of-an-heirloom-life/', 'snippet': 'Carl Richards makes the case for considering cost-per-use and buying things that last (and last).', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carl Richards is a certified financial planner in Park City, Utah, and is the director of investor education at BAM Advisor Services. His book, “The Behavior Gap