, a reminder that strokes aren’t just for older people, coping at the airport without a wallet and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and on our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tuesday Reading: A Study Questions the Advantages of Organic Food', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T12:34:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b4e924a-6122-5599-afcc-11ade90fe8c4', 'word_count': 126, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b4e924a-6122-5599-afcc-11ade90fe8c4'}, {'abstract': 'When an icon becomes a punchline.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/whom-the-gods-would-destroy-they-first-make-bipartisan/', 'snippet': 'When an icon becomes a punchline.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Brad DeLong points us to a truly weird column by Clive Crook, which apparently was supposed to be a satirical take on Paul Ryan’s critics but falls completely flat. This follows on an almost equally weird piece by Ben Smith berating all those people who had the temerity to judge Ryan the great Truthteller on whether he actually, you know, told the truth.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Whom The Gods Would Destroy, They First Make Bipartisan', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywor