 accordion to his harmonica. Quite the duo!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Edible Selby | Kirk Lombard', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T13:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c36624b5-0727-509a-98c3-4a40e38e09d8', 'word_count': 56, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c36624b5-0727-509a-98c3-4a40e38e09d8'}, {'abstract': 'Dick Clark Productions, the company that produces the Golden Globe Awards show and the New Year’s Eve broadcast hosted for nearly 40 years by its late founder, was sold to Guggenheim Partners and a pair of multimedia investors on Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/dick-clark-productions-sold-to-guggenheim-partners/', 'snippet': 'Dick Clark Productions, the company that produces the Golden Globe Awards show and the New Year’s Eve broadcast hosted for nearly 40 years by its late founder, was sold to Guggenheim Partners and a pair of multimedia investors on Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dick Clark Productions, the company that produces the Golden Globe Awards show and the New Year’s Eve broadcast hosted for nearly 40 years by its late founder, was sold to Guggenheim Partners and a group of investors on Tuesday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dick Clark Productions Sold to Guggenheim Partners', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organiz