ishing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Censorship', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cultural Revolution', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T13:11:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clarissa Sebag-Montefiore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clarissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sebag-Montefiore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/782feb6f-cc07-5e8d-806e-3d0a2db28b2b', 'word_count': 821, 'uri': 'nyt://article/782feb6f-cc07-5e8d-806e-3d0a2db28b2b'}, {'abstract': 'The music-themed cable channel is creating “Fuse News,” a daily live news show that will be anchored by Ashanti, Elaine Moran, Alexa Chung and Jack Osbourne.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/fuse-introduces-fuse-news-with-some-recognizable-hosts/', 'snippet': 'The music-themed cable channel is creating “Fuse News,” a daily live news show that will be anchored by Ashanti, Elaine Moran, Alexa Chung and Jack Osbourne.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fuse, the music-themed cable channel that mixes videos and documentaries with offbeat fare like the comedy game show “Funny or Die’s Billy on the Street,” is increasing its commitment to music journalism. On Tuesday it said that it was creating a dedicated news division and introducing a daily news show whose hosts may be familiar to viewers of its sometime rival MTV. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fuse Introduces ‘Fuse News,’ With Some Recognizable Hosts', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fuse Channel Creating A News Division', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ashanti (1980- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chung, Alexa', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Osbourne, Jack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Osbourne, Sharon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T13:13:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/24c52467-a320-57bc-8c0d-2a413824e8e5', 'word_count': 299, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24c52467-a320-57bc-8c0d-2a413824e8e5'}, {'abstract': 'The Day: The post-Labor Day workweek begins with leading figures in Albany facing investigations into the actions they took — or should have taken, but didn’t — in Assemblyman Vito Lopez’s sexual harassment scandal.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/looming-over-states-delegation-the-shadow-of-a-harassment-case/', 'snippet': 'The Day: The post-Labor Day workweek begins with leading figures in Albany facing investigations into the actions they took — or should have taken, but didn’t — in Assemblyman Vito Lopez’s sexual harassment scandal.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The Yankees once had a player whose fielding lapses inspired a New York Post label that stuck to him like flypaper: Hector (What a Pair of Hands) Lopez. That was 50 years ago. But retro is fashionable. Thanks to the New York State Assembly and its shenanigans, there is reason to revive the sobriquet. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Looming Over State’s Delegation, the Shadow of a Harassment Case', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Democratic National Convention', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sexual Harassment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lopez, Vito J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Silver, Sheldon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T13:15:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clyde Haberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clyde', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72914325-7f1c-5528-89b8-e377630a2874', 'word_count': 805, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72914325-7f1c-5528-89b8-e377630a2874'}, {'abstract': 'Even the Cardinals themselves don’t sound too optimistic about 2012, but their defense gives them reason for hope.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/arizona-cardinals-2012-n-f-l-season-preview/', 'snippet': 'Even the Cardinals themselves don’t sound too optimistic about 2012, but their defense gives them reason for hope.', 'lead_paragraph': 'These days, there’s about as much optimism in Arizona as there is rain. Even the Cardinals themselves don’t sound too amped about their chances in 2012. They seem to understand that it’s never good when your quarterback competition carries on through the entire preseason. Coach Ken Whisenhunt reluctantly made a final decision after the fourth meaningless contest, naming John Skelton the starter. This comes a year after Whisenhunt and General Manager Rod Graves traded cornerback Dominique Rodgers-Cromartie and a second-round pick, and forked over $12 million guaranteed (which has since become $20 million) to acquire Kevin Kolb.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Arizona Cardinals, 2012 N.F.L. Season Preview', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARIZONA CARDINALS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T13:15:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Benoit', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Benoit', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2297f815-d0f5-5caa-9cfc-4a51b91ee331', 'word_count': 2826, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2297f815-d0f5-5caa-9cfc-4a51b91ee331'}, {'abstract': 'Egypt’s Muslim Brotherhood is committed to upholding patriarchal and traditional values around a woman’s place in society, and many Egyptian women need no convincing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/05/world/middleeast/05iht-letter05.html', 'snippet': 'Egypt’s Muslim Brotherhood is committed to upholding patriarchal and traditional values around a woman’s place in society, and many Egyptian women need no convincing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — Women are erratic and emotional, and they make good wives and mothers — but never leaders or rulers. That, at least, is what Osama Abou Salama, a professor of botany at Cairo University and a member of the Muslim Brotherhood, told young men and women during a recent premarital counseling class.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/world/jp-cairo/jp-cairo-articleLarge.jpg', 'he