 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mona El-Naggar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mona', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'El-Naggar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d730196d-7ee2-5770-baff-8e01ae0115a6', 'word_count': 1013, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d730196d-7ee2-5770-baff-8e01ae0115a6'}, {'abstract': 'The Democratic super PAC backing President Obama raised $10 million in August, a record increase in contributions that may be a demonstration of growing concern among some elite Democratic donors that Republican outside groups will swamp Mr. Obama’s re-election effort', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/priorities-usa-action-reports-record-monthly-donations/', 'snippet': 'The Democratic super PAC backing President Obama raised $10 million in August, a record increase in contributions that may be a demonstration of growing concern among some elite Democratic donors that Republican outside groups will swamp Mr. Obama...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Democratic “super PAC” backing President Obama raised $10 million in August, as donors gave a record amount to the group amid growing concern among some elite Democratic contributors that Republican outside groups will swamp Mr. Obama’s re-election effort.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Priorities USA Action Reports Record Monthly Donations', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Action Committees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burton, Bill', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Priorities USA Action', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T13:39:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Confessore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Confessore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00ff7279-af17-5d92-abe8-265e7b60733d', 'word_count': 260, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00ff7279-af17-5d92-abe8-265e7b60733d'}, {'abstract': 'The $2.6 billion acquisition of Medicis Pharmaceutical is the 11th deal this year for the Montreal-based Valeant, which merged with Biovail of Canada in 2010.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/valeant-continues-its-string-of-acquisitions/', 'snippet': 'The $2.6 billion acquisition of Medicis Pharmaceutical is the 11th deal this year for the Montreal-based Valeant, which merged with Biovail of Canada in 2010.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Valeant Pharmaceuticals International has not been afraid to spend its cash.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Valeant Sticks to Torrid Pace of Deal-Making', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Medicis Pharmaceutical Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Valeant Pharmaceuticals International Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T13:51:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/775e06d3-da9e-54fa-8c17-607e9f2dd751', 'word_count': 458, 'uri': 'nyt://article/775e06d3-da9e-54fa-8c17-607e9f2dd751'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/what-were-reading-513/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York Times: Though they are undoubtedly more expensive, organic fruits, vegetables and meat aren’t more nutritious than their conventional counterparts, according to scientists at Stanford University. — Emily Weinstein', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T13:53:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2cc56394-7937-5f07-9399-dbddc8a2f7c7', 'word_count': 525, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2cc56394-7937-5f07-9399-dbddc8a2f7c7'}, {'abstract': 'With Mitt Romney keeping a low profile this week, Paul D. Ryan is the face of the Republican ticket, and on Tuesday he blitzed all three morning network television shows, pressing the attack against President Obama days before he is renominated at the Democratic National Convention.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/in-interview-blitz-ryan-plays-defense-and-offense/', 'snippet': 'With Mitt Romney keeping a low profile this week, Paul D. Ryan is the face of the Republican ticket, and on Tuesday he blitzed all three morning network television shows, pressing the attack against President Obama days before he is renominated at...', 'lead_paragraph': 'GREENVILLE, N.C. — With Mitt Romney keeping a low profile this week, Representative Paul D. Ryan is the face of the Republican ticket, and on Tuesday he blitzed all three morning network television shows, pressing the attack against President Obama days before he is renominated at the Democratic National Convention. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Interview Blitz, Ryan Plays Defense and Offense', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Carolina', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T13:55:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Trip Gabriel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Trip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37f1439a-e31a-5d29-bc91-b720de857299', 'word_count': 643, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37f1439a-e31a-5d29-bc91-b720de857299'}, {'abstract': 'The economic crisis in Europe has failed to deter migrants from fleeing poverty and unrest at home by attempting the sometimes perilous journey to the Continent. As the latest would-be immigrants were turned back by Spanish authorities, human rights groups have been expressing concern about measures being taken to protect Fortess Europe.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/on-the-fringes-of-europe-a-crackdown-on-migrants/', 'snippet': 'The economic crisis in Europe has failed to deter migrants from fleeing poverty and unrest at home by attempting the sometimes perilous journey to the Continent. As the latest would-be immigrants were turned back by Spanish authorities, human righ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — In the early hours of Tuesday, units of Spain’s paramilitary Civil Guard rounded up a group of would-be African immigrants on an otherwise uninhabited Spanish rock off the North African coast and shipped them back to the Moroccan shore just a few dozen yards away.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/04/blogs/rdv-migrants/rdv-migrants-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 664, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/04/blogs/rdv-migrants/rdv-migrants-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1328, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'On the Fringes of Europe, a Crackdown on Migrants', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigrants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T13:57:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Morris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7bd6d628-6019-5e8a-8e87-2045e79f143b', 'word_count': 595, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7bd6d628-6019-5e8a-8e87-2045e79f143b'}, {'abstract': 'Our culture tells our children that lying and cheating are acceptable ways to get ahead in life.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/how-we-teach-students-to-cheat/', 'snippet': 'Our culture tells our children that lying and cheating are acceptable ways to get ahead in life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I was in high school, I saw a dear friend unroll a slip of paper and copy answers onto an exam we were taking. I was floored. After a lot of time trying to decide if it was better to feel like an accomplice or a prig, I opted for prig.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/style/motherlode-school-bus/motherlode-school-bus-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/style/motherlode-school-bus/motherlode-school-bus-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/27/style/motherlode-school-bus/motherlode-school-bus-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/27/style/motherlode-school-bus/motherlode-school-bus-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75