enegildo Zegna. The fate of Mr. Pilati, as you will recall, was the subject of much speculation, well before he was out the door at YSL. And all that talk had a clear effect on his work and his psyche, so much so that it was a wonder when everyone stood up to give him an ovation at his last show.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stefano Pilati Returns to Italian Fashion', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pilati, Stefano', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zegna, Ermenegildo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yves Saint Laurent', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T13:59:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/634dabad-9018-5ff2-b38f-4413e1079ff2', 'word_count': 181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/634dabad-9018-5ff2-b38f-4413e1079ff2'}, {'abstract': 'Instead of hiding behind her notepad, a reporter opens up to her subjects to better understand the context behind a Muslim Brotherhood premarital counseling workshop.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/love-and-marriage-in-a-traditional-climate/', 'snippet': 'Instead of hiding behind her notepad, a reporter opens up to her subjects to better understand the context behind a Muslim Brotherhood premarital counseling workshop.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — When raising issues related to culture and women, I often remember that the very realities that perplex us are the ones truly worth understanding. And in order to fully understand, we must consider context. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Love and Marriage in a Traditional Climate', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T14:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mona el Naggar', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/060a418d-4cf5-5e40-8516-7dcf3f04aaa9', 'word_count': 456, 'uri': 'nyt://article/060a418d-4cf5-5e40-8516-7dcf3f04aaa9'}, {'abstract': 'In his regular post-match question-and-answer session, Andy Murray talked with The TImes’ Greg Bishop about which players he like to borrow shots from.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/conversations-with-andy-murray-building-the-perfect-player/', 'snippet': 'In his regular post-match question-and-answer session, Andy Murray talked with The TImes’ Greg Bishop about which players he like to borrow shots from.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After Andy Murray played a nearly perfect 6-4, 6-4, 6-2 trouncing of Milos Raonic, Murray sat down with Straight Sets for his regular post-match question-and-answer session. From the perfect match, he attempted to build the perfect player.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Conversations With Andy Murray: Building the Perfect Player', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murray, Andy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T14:09:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Greg Bishop', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Greg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bishop', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7fa51911-d093-58aa-a2e5-7b0c10509d5b', 'word_count': 957, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7fa51911-d093-58aa-a2e5-7b0c10509d5b'}, {'abstract': 'Also, advertisers and marketing firms try to promote more diversity in their industry, and a Pirate Bay co-founder facing charges of copyright violations is arrested in Cambodia.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/the-breakfast-meeting-boom-bust-summer-of-movies-and-hugo-awards-cut-short/', 'snippet': 'Also, advertisers and marketing firms try to promote more diversity in their industry, and a Pirate Bay co-founder facing charges of copyright violations is arrested in Cambodia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As summer vacations were ending, the movie industry took stock of the season just past and found reasons for concern, Brooks Barnes writes. Ticket sales at North American cinemas in the summer declined an estimated 3 percent, to $4.28 billion, the first decline in seven years; total attendance was the lowest since at least 1993, when independent records first were kept. There were specific reasons that could, perhaps, explain the decline — the Olympics; the shootings in Aurora, Colo. — but still the results were sobering.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: Boom-Bust Summer of Movies, and Hugo Awards Cut Short', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': 