al cupboard has a 77-day supply, only half the amount of a good year. Food supply, as he has warned, also serves as a kind of barometer for social unrest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — When Lester Brown finally gets to say, “I told you so,” we are all in very deep trouble. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/blogs/grain-rdv/grain-rdv-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 629, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/02/blogs/grain-rdv/grain-rdv-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1257, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Going Against the Grain of Complacency', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T16:00:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mort Rosenblum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mort', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenblum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d1f765e-2e1a-5170-b7a0-a7b153d307f6', 'word_count': 502, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d1f765e-2e1a-5170-b7a0-a7b153d307f6'}, {'abstract': 'Apple issued invitations for an event next week where it is expected to introduce its next iPhone. The invitation’s vague teaser says, “It’s almost here.”', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/apple-confirms-sept-12-event/', 'snippet': 'Apple issued invitations for an event next week where it is expected to introduce its next iPhone. The invitation’s vague teaser says, “It’s almost here.”', 'lead_paragraph': ' Apple on Tuesday sent invitations to news organizations for an event next week where it is expected to introduce the sixth model of the iPhone.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/04/technology/04bits-invite/04bits-invite-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 625, 'width': 700, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/04/technology/04bits-invite/04bits-invite-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 625, 'width': 700, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Apple Confirms Sept. 12 Event', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T16:19:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian X. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ee8fb90-c202-55ab-a8a2-8c36e231fe4d', 'word_count': 121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ee8fb90-c202-55ab-a8a2-8c36e231fe4d'}, {'abstract': 'Every few years, we revisit the question of what to do about the “problem” of Pennsylvania Station. But, the author asks, is there no one who would miss it if it were gone?', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/celebrating-a-transit-hub-in-all-its-blandness/', 'snippet': 'Every few years, we revisit the question of what to do about the “problem” of Pennsylvania Station. But, the author asks, is there no one who would miss it if it were gone?', 'lead_paragraph': 'I remember the first time I swept through Penn Station. My oldest sister, Clare, had agreed to take us four “little kids” into the city to see the new movie “Sounder” at Radio City Music Hall. I held fast to her hand as we raced through the crowded station to make the show — it was hot and noisy and confusing, but oddly thrilling when we finally pushed through the mass of dark coats and reached the bracing night air on Seventh Avenue. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Celebrating a Transit Hub, in All Its Blandness', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pennsylvania Station (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Low, William', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T16:23:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Theresa Burns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Theresa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cfd70c90-014e-57ef-a2a0-7dd89d8f1380', 'word_count': 845, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cfd70c90-014e-57ef-a2a0-7dd89d8f1380'}, {'abstract': 'In North Carolina, where the Democratic faithful have descended to hold their convention, 47 percent of likely voters are supporting the Republican candidate, Mitt Romney, and 43 percent are supporting President Obama.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/in-north-carolina-romney-and-obama-are-in-a-tight-race/', 'snippet': 'In North Carolina, where the Democratic faithful have descended to hold their convention, 47 percent of likely voters are supporting the Republican candidate, Mitt Romney, and 43 percent are supporting President Obama.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In North Carolina, where the Democratic faithful have descended to hold their convention, a new poll shows that Mitt Romney and President Obama are running closely in the state.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In North Carolina, Romney and Obama Are in a Tight Race', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Elon University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Carolina', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T16:25:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allison Kopicki', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allison', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kopicki', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4392161f-645f-5613-88c0-a4bf5bc2cb07', 'word_count': 236, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4392161f-645f-5613-88c0-a4bf5bc2cb07'}, {'abstract': 'You don’t have long to wait for a new seafood shack, a burger joint and a restaurant 39 floors up.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/05/dining/restaurants-opening-in-early-september.html', 'snippet': 'You don’t have long to wait for a new seafood shack, a burger joint and a restaurant 39 floors up.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BAIT & HOOK This easygoing but citified seafood shack will serve traditional clam chowders, lobster rolls and crab cakes, in addition to inventions like crab, chorizo and corn pizza. Some non-seafood items, like regular mac and cheese, will also be available. (Monday): 231 Second Avenue (14th Street), (212) 260-8015.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/05/dining/05PREVIEW1_SPAN/05PREVIEW1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/05/dining/05PREVIEW1_SPAN/05PREVIEW1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/05/dining/05PREVIEW1_SPAN/05PREVIEW1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 875, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/05/dining/05PREVIEW1_SPAN/05PREVIEW1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1750, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/05/dining/05PREVIEW1_SPAN/05PREVIEW1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/05/dining/05PREVIEW1_SPAN/05PREVIEW1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/05/dining/05PREVIEW1_SPAN/05PREVIEW1_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Restaurants Opening in Early September', 'kicker': 'Fall Restaurant Preview', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Opening in the Next Week', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chefs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T16:27:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/166cd0ef-77fb-5c8e-b138-ecb4e28edb59', 'word_count': 728, 'uri': 'nyt://article/166cd0ef-77fb-5c8e-b138-ecb4e28edb59'}, {'abstract': 'Catering to an immigration-sensitive electorate, the Australian government is making it harder for Afghan refugees to make a new home on a land they’ve risked death to reach.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/new-australian-immigration-policy-hurts-afghan-refugees/', 'snippet': 'Catering to an immigration-sensitive electorate, the Australian government is making it harder for Afghan refugees to make a new home on a land they’ve risked death to reach.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MELBOURNE — A takeaway kebab shop in a leafy Australian suburb seems a far cry from the troubles of Afghanistan. But even here the anguish of war and centuries-old prejudices bite.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Coming to Australia', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Asylum, Right of', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hazaras (Ethnic Group)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigrants', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Australia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T16:30:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Luke Hunt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Luke', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hunt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/54c9894a-21d0-5c53-bfb9-09010161cb1a', 'word_count': 763, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54c9894a-21d0-5c53-bfb9-09010161cb1a'}, {'abstract': 'How a miscalculation near Mobile Bay led to a political firefight in Civil War Washington.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/commander-prebles-very-bad-day/', 'snippet': 'How a miscalculation near Mobile Bay led to a political firefight in Civil War Washington.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Imagine it’s the summer of 1862, and you have just one job: guarding a few miles of the Gulf Coast to keep enemy ships from crossing the Union naval blockade. But you’ve been on the job less than a week, with a creaky ship and little time to train your crews or establish an effective strategy. Your engineers took down one of the two boilers on your vessel for repairs, and you are just now coming back to about half strength. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Commander Preble’s Very Bad Day', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Navy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Southern States (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T16:30:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jed Morrison', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jed', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morrison', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ab6ed68-e8fd-5002-8156-31e153f66e01', 'word_count': 1915, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ab6ed68-e8fd-5002-8156-31e153f66e01'}, {'abstract': 'In decades to come, global warming is likely to result in heavier bursts of rain and longer dry spells.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/q-and-a-climate-change-and-the-monsoon/', 'snippet': 'In decades to come, global warming is likely to result in heavier bursts of rain and longer dry spells.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As I report today in The Times, the South Asian monsoon is critical to sustaining plants, animals and 1.6 billion people on the subcontinent. When it brings too little rain between June and October, shortages of food and drinking water can develop. When its bounty is too great, floods can displace millions and cause hundreds of deaths.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q. and A.: Climate Change and the Monsoon', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drought', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monsoons', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rain', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nature Climate Change (Journal)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T16:35:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vikas Bajaj', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vikas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bajaj', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d19f92d9-e126-5607-a904-3efc908959e4', 'word_count': 980, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d19f92d9-e126-5607-a904-3efc908959e4'}, {'abstract': 'Andy Roddick, who will play Tuesday night at the United States Open, participated in some of the most memorable matches of our time.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/roddicks-legacy-work-ethic-and-willpower/', 'snippet': 'Andy Roddick, who will play Tuesday night at the United States Open, participated in some of the most memorable matches of our time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Andy Roddick’s stirring first-week run, coming after he announced that this would be his last tournament, has prompted many accolades, along with the belated acknowledgment that in addition to being his era’s best American player he has also been its least understood. As Karen Crouse pointed out Monday in her fine appreciation, Roddick’s story has been consistently, and mistakenly, represented as a narrative of failed promise — in part because his one major championship came so early (at the 2003 Open, when he was 21).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Roddick’s Legacy: Work Ethic and Willpower', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'AGASSI, ANDRE', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Connors, Jimmy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Federer, Roger', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ferrero, Juan Carlos', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roddick, Andy', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sampras, Pete', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T16:37:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Tanenhaus', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tanenhaus', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/24e7f9d6-f3d1-5f03-8220-f0d1f3620821', 'word_count': 804, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24e7f9d6-f3d1-5f03-8220-f0d1f3620821'}, {'abstract': 'Tickets are now available for our Sept. 12 event, Sockets and Streams.', 'web_url': 'https://open.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/sockets-streams-tickets-now-available/', 'snippet': 'Tickets are now available for our Sept. 12 event, Sockets and Streams.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We’ve just opened up registration for our Sept. 12 event, Sockets and Streams. Get your ticket today via EventBrite.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sockets & Streams: Tickets Now Available', 'kicker': 'Open', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T16:37:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marci Windsheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marci', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Windsheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4bc3de9c-6b91-531e-a4bc-0210d4dc2c6e', 'word_count': 51, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4bc3de9c-6b91-531e-a4bc-0210d4dc2c6e'}, {'abstract': 'The Democratic Party platform approved Tuesday offered a stark contrast to the Republican one adopted last week, especially on abortion rights, gay marriage and the future of Medicare and Social Security.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/05/us/politics/how-the-party-platforms-differ.html', 'snippet': 'The Democratic Party platform approved Tuesday offered a stark contrast to the Republican one adopted last week, especially on abortion rights, gay marriage and the future of Medicare and Social Security.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Voters are forever being told that they face stark choices. But the platform that Democrats approved Tuesday at their convention in Charlotte, N.C., was, in areas from social issues to entitlements, a mirror image of the platform that the Republicans adopted last week in Tampa, Fla.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/05/us/BETTER/BETTER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/05/us/BETTER/BETTER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/05/us/BETTER/BETTER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/05/us/BETTER/BETTER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/05/us/BETTER/BETTER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/05/us/BETTER/BETTER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/05/us/BETTER/BETTER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Party Platforms Are Poles Apart in Their View of the Nation', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Party Platforms Are Poles Apart In Their View of the Nation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Republican National Convention', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Democratic National Convention', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T16:41:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/95c95d54-3d0a-5756-b8de-23348287ee92', 'word_count': 1042, 'uri': 'nyt://article/95c95d54-3d0a-5756-b8de-23348287ee92'}, {'abstract': 'A look at the day’s events and the broadcast schedule for TimesCast politics.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/timescast-politics-and-democratic-convention-day-at-a-glance/', 'snippet': 'A look at the day’s events and the broadcast schedule for TimesCast politics.', 'lead_paragraph': '12:48 p.m. | Updated  CHARLOTTE, N.C. — As Democrats gather here, seeking to recapture the unity from 2008, the convention officially opens on Tuesday, and The Times’s political unit will be broadcasting live with the latest from the convention, beginning at 2 p.m. Here are a few of the highlights from the program:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'TimesCast Politics and Democratic Convention Day at a Glance', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Democratic National Convention', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speeches and Statements', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Castro, Julian', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murray, Patty', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Michelle', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T16:44:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c4b0885-b06f-58b4-86c2-5772669af121', 'word_count': 358, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c4b0885-b06f-58b4-86c2-5772669af121'}, {'abstract': 'All-Clad, known for pots and pans, has made some useful cutting tools.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/05/dining/all-clad-is-the-latest-to-make-kitchen-knives.html', 'snippet': 'All-Clad, known for pots and pans, has made some useful cutting tools.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is no shortage of well-made, useful knives on the market these days, with new models showing up regularly. All-Clad, the company that made its name in pots and pans, is the latest player in the game. Its knives offer high-carbon stainless steel blades fitted into sleek, beautifully finished rosewood handles smoothly wrapped with steel at the end. Of the 10 models, 2 are especially worthwhile: what it calls a seven-inch daily slicer and a four-inch daily parer. The well-balanced slicer has a rectangular blade, similar to a hard-to-find Japanese nakiri or vegetable knife; it’s like a chef’s knife on its way to being a cleaver. I own one of these from Japan and rely on it, though mine is a little lighter than the All-Clad. The parer has a rounded end, almost like a mini-santoku, making it useful for all kinds of fine cutting and paring jobs.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/29/dining/29STUFF_KNIVES/29STUFF2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 313, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/29/dining/29STUFF_KNIVES/29STUFF2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 626, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/29/dining/29STUFF_KNIVES/29STUFF_KNIVES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/29/dining/29STUFF_KNIVES/29STUFF_KNIVES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Kitchen Knives by a Household Name', 'kicker': 'Food Stuff ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Kitchen Knives By a Household Name', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Knives', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T16:45:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0f3da96-25a4-588c-8b10-d257195dad49', 'word_count': 180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0f3da96-25a4-588c-8b10-d257195dad49'}, {'abstract': 'Jonathan Adams joined iCrossing, New York, part of the Hearst Corporation, in a new post, senior vice president of media for North America, leading the media practice.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/business/media/accounts-and-people-of-note-in-the-advertising-industry.html', 'snippet': 'Jonathan Adams joined iCrossing, New York, part of the Hearst Corporation, in a new post, senior vice president of media for North America, leading the media practice.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jonathan Adams joined iCrossing, New York, part of the Hearst Corporation, in a new post, senior vice president of media for North America, leading the media practice. He had most recently been senior vice president and director for global media at Digitas, part of the Publicis Groupe.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Accounts and People of Note in the Advertising Industry', 'kicker': 'Webdenda', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Webdenda', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Relations and Publicity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], '