'word_count': 219, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6aa29cf-e98b-5267-9fa3-f00577f349f1'}, {'abstract': 'Hackers have released a file that they say contains more than one million identification numbers for Apple iPhones, iPads and iPod Touch devices. They claim to have obtained the file by hacking into the computer of a federal agent, though the F.B.I. denied that this had happened.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/hackers-claim-to-have-12-million-apple-device-records/', 'snippet': 'Hackers have released a file that they say contains more than one million identification numbers for Apple iPhones, iPads and iPod Touch devices. They claim to have obtained the file by hacking into the computer of a federal agent, though the F.B....', 'lead_paragraph': '8:00 p.m. | Updated Hackers released a file that they said contained a million identification numbers for Apple mobile devices, claiming that they had obtained it by hacking into the computer of an F.B.I. agent. The F.B.I. said it had no evidence that this was true.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/04/technology/04bits-apple/04bits-apple-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/04/technology/04bits-apple/04bits-apple-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/04/technology/04bits-apple/04bits-apple-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/04/technology/04bits-apple/04bits-apple-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/04/technology/04bits-apple/04bits-apple-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hackers Claim to Have 12 Million Apple Device Records', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hackers Post ID Numbers for Apple Devices, Claiming They Are From F.B.I.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberattacks and Hackers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Anonymous (Internet Group)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T16:53:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicole Perlroth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicole', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perlroth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/04e521ad-5c8a-585e-9685-5342fa325ff8', 'word_count': 761, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04e521ad-5c8a-585e-9685-5342fa325ff8'}, {'abstract': 'A capsule of travel news for the week of September 4, 2012, curated by our writers and editors.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/walkabout-94-avoiding-airport-fast-food-and-snagging-expensive-souvenirs/', 'snippet': 'A capsule of travel news for the week of September 4, 2012, curated by our writers and editors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No More Pastry Buffets A number of mobile applications and Web sites can now direct business travelers, once condemned to eating greasy meeting-room and airport fare, toward healthier options. (The New York Times)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Walkabout – 9/4: Avoiding Airport Fast Food and Snagging Expensive Souvenirs', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T17:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e19620d-27e0-58ba-847b-7fe33efaae26', 'word_count': 204, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e19620d-27e0-58ba-847b-7fe33efaae26'}, {'abstract': 'In observance of National Yoga Month in September, hotels at home and abroad are offering incentives to pose on the road.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/never-too-far-from-a-yoga-mat/', 'snippet': 'In observance of National Yoga Month in September, hotels at home and abroad are offering incentives to pose on the road.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In observance of National Yoga Month in September, hotels at home and abroad are offering incentives to pose on the road.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Never Too Far From a Yoga Mat', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'HOTELS AND MOTELS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Yoga', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T17:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elaine Glusac', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elaine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glusac', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0eaa4456-aacd-5e85-ba36-0d32d373ddd1', 'word_count': 168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0eaa4456-aacd-5e85-ba36-0d32d373ddd1'}, {'abstract': 'The Paris-based plus-size model is happily Rubenesque and out to defy the stereotype that all French women are rail-thin.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/large-format-stephanie-zwickys-blog-de-big-beauty/', 'snippet': 'The Paris-based plus-size model is happily Rubenesque and out to defy the stereotype that all French women are rail-thin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The belief that French women’s vaunted chic and their slender waistlines are inseparable — indeed, self-propagating — is so reflexive that it’s spurred its own ever-expanding self-help genre. So it may come as a surprise to learn that one of the most popular fashion bloggers in France is the Swiss-born, Paris-based plus-size model, actress and television host Stéphanie Zwicky of Le Blog de Big Beauty, who is happily and unabashedly Rubenesque. Zwicky started blogging in 2005 as a resource for other women struggling to find stylish clothes in sizes larger than 42 (an American 12) — which, she notes, is what 60 percent of French women wear. Today, she logs 230,000 readers from around the world every month, many of whom post ecstatic reviews of her colorful, body-conscious outfits (“J’aime, j’aime, et je sur-aime!” reads a typical comment.) “There are girls like me on every block, I’m just lucky to be so visible,” she says.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Large Format | Stéphanie Zwicky’s Blog de Big Beauty', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T17:01:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nancy MacDonell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nancy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacDonell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce5892aa-96f7-5d40-9d6f-20c09804c8ee', 'word_count': 700, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce5892aa-96f7-5d40-9d6f-20c09804c8ee'}, {'abstract': 'On an Android phone, an app and a widget are two different things.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/qa-telling-android-widget-from-app/', 'snippet': 'On an Android phone, an app and a widget are two different things.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q&A: Telling Android Widget From App', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Telling Widget From App in Android', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Android (Operating System)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T17:02:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By J.d. Biersdorfer', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8cb0344-ae45-595e-9fa1-8f2e6cc48c2d', 'word_count': 295, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8cb0344-ae45-595e-9fa1-8f2e6cc48c2d'}, {'abstract': 'The new economy in North Carolina has made the state more competitive, but it still leans Republican.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/in-north-carolina-obamas-2008-victory-was-ahead-of-schedule/', 'snippet': 'The new economy in North Carolina has made the state more competitive, but it still leans Republican.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We continue our Presidential Geography series, a one-by-one examination of the peculiarities that drive the politics in all 50 states and the District of Columbia. Here, a look at North Carolina, the Tar Heel State. FiveThirtyEight spoke with Eric Heberlig, an associate professor of political science at the University of North Carolina-Charlotte, and Ferrel Guillory, a longtime writer and editor for the The News & Observer in Raleigh, N.C., and an adjunct faculty member in the Department of Public Policy at the University of North Carolina-Chapel Hill.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In North Carolina, Obama’s 2008 Victory Was Ahead of Schedule', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T17:15:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Micah Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Micah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3b6f6e4-4f04-54a7-8260-1a95728e26c9', 'word_count': 1103, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3b6f6e4-4f04-54a7-8260-1a95728e26c9'}, {'abstract': 'What makes a restaurant work? For one thing, personalization, a place with a working chef, not a cookie-cutter spinoff or a circus.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/05/dining/sometimes-formica-is-better-than-white-cloth.html', 'snippet': 'What makes a restaurant work? For one thing, personalization, a place with a working chef, not a cookie-cutter spinoff or a circus.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE last time I ate in a four-star white-tablecloth restaurant, I was frustrated and unhappy. (Bear with me; I’m 