25-93fa-5128-8406-9906246001dd'}, {'abstract': 'Paul Tough’s new book highlights educators whose unsparing style actually helps children succeed.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/what-makes-a-good-teacher/', 'snippet': 'Paul Tough’s new book highlights educators whose unsparing style actually helps children succeed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York City children start school this week, and, like many parents, I hope that each of my kids will get the perfect teacher. The new book from Paul Tough, “How Children Succeed: Grit, Curiosity and the Hidden Power of Character,” has given me a new sort of perfection to hope for: someone like Elizabeth Spiegel, the chess teacher at I.S. 318 in Brooklyn. Here is Spiegel writing in a blog post after her girls’ team won a national championship in 2010:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Makes a Good Teacher?', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tough, Paul', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T17:35:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vera Titunik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vera', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Titunik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb28766c-4206-5ad3-a82b-e18f362becd9', 'word_count': 559, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb28766c-4206-5ad3-a82b-e18f362becd9'}, {'abstract': 'Of all the swing states this election, there are few more coveted by Democrats than this former capital of the Confederacy.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/on-the-road-to-north-carolina-obama-stops-to-shore-up-support-in-virginia/', 'snippet': 'Of all the swing states this election, there are few more coveted by Democrats than this former capital of the Confederacy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MECHANICSVILLE, Va. — Of all the swing states this election, there are few more coveted by Democrats than this former capital of the Confederacy, where an influx of Hispanics and population growth in Northern Virginia has turned this formerly red state, if not blue, then at least, purple.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On the Road to North Carolina, Obama Stops to Shore Up Support in Virginia', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Democratic National Convention', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T17:38:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Helene Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Helene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/583d8945-3fd7-5eb1-a2ff-68eb6ee0aa9d', 'word_count': 653, 'uri': 'nyt://article/583d8945-3fd7-5eb1-a2ff-68eb6ee0aa9d'}, {'abstract': 'Visit the Fashion and Style section of The New York Times daily for continual fashion week coverage, on and off the runways. Here’s what to expect from our reporters and editors.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/newyorkfashionweekspring-2013-shows-begin/', 'snippet': 'Visit the Fashion and Style section of The New York Times daily for continual fashion week coverage, on and off the runways. Here’s what to expect from our reporters and editors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Though the official kickoff comes on Thursday, with more than 300 designers presenting their spring 2013 collections at Lincoln Center, Milk Studios and other spaces around town, New York Fashion Week has already begun in the minds of the designers, journalists, buyers and followers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For the Fashion World, Spring 2013 Has Arrived', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T17:42:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simone S. Oliver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simone', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Oliver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/45bfcbb2-b082-55e8-bb25-6b4ae2c5bbf3', 'word_count': 236, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45bfcbb2-b082-55e8-bb25-6b4ae2c5bbf3'}, {'abstract': 'Mumbo-jumbo about interest rates.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/natural-born-recovery-killers/', 'snippet': 'Mumbo-jumbo about interest rates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hmm. Brad DeLong finds Niall Ferguson touting a paper by William White (pdf) that I read as a desperate attempt to find some reason why we should be raising interest rates despite a deeply depressed economy and an absence of obvious inflationary pressure. Why the desperation? There’s a certain kind of central banker who just hates the idea of easy money; plus the desire to raise rates is closely identified with the political right. No surprise, then, that Ferguson likes the paper.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Natural Born Recovery Killers', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T17:42:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee87a033-c78b-5358-a258-3cd6adecf78b', 'word_count': 449, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee87a033-c78b-5358-a258-3cd6adecf78b'}, {'abstract': 'A new ad warns that Americans would face delays in medical treatment because of President Obama’s health care overhaul.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/super-pac-ad-takes-aim-at-obama-health-overhaul/', 'snippet': 'A new ad warns that Americans would face delays in medical treatment because of President Obama’s health care overhaul.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Republican-leaning non-profit group Americans for Prosperity is debuting a new commercial at the start of the Democratic National Convention, suggesting that President Obama‘s health care overhaul would leave the United States with a system much like Canada’s, one in which costly delays in treatment would threaten people’s lives.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ad Takes Aim at Obama Health Overhaul', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Democratic National Convention', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'U