, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T18:51:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Firestone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Firestone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de994183-1bbf-5b5e-8f4d-541ba94bb90a', 'word_count': 454, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de994183-1bbf-5b5e-8f4d-541ba94bb90a'}, {'abstract': 'The top two men’s players, Roger Federer and Novak Djokovic, have yet to be challenged at the U.S. Open. But fans should be in for a treat when Andy Roddick plays Juan Martin Del Potro Tuesday night.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/video-competitive-tennis-anyone/', 'snippet': 'The top two men’s players, Roger Federer and Novak Djokovic, have yet to be challenged at the U.S. Open. But fans should be in for a treat when Andy Roddick plays Juan Martin Del Potro Tuesday night.', 'lead_paragraph': "(function($){var data = chameleonData;var ticker = new NYTD.NYTMM.NewsTicker($('#nytmm_embed_431'), data);})(jQuery||NYTD.jQuery);", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video: Competitive Tennis, Anyone?', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Djokovic, Novak', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Federer, Roger', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roddick, Andy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T18:54:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5860c4c2-a164-57a8-b8a9-626bc23aaa5a', 'word_count': 99, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5860c4c2-a164-57a8-b8a9-626bc23aaa5a'}, {'abstract': 'A principal was fined for trying to get her sister a job at a nonprofit that does business with her school; an elevator repairman also was fined for selling scrap metal from a city building.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/suspended-principal-is-among-5-fined-by-conflicts-board/', 'snippet': 'A principal was fined for trying to get her sister a job at a nonprofit that does business with her school; an elevator repairman also was fined for selling scrap metal from a city building.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An elevator repairman who sold scrap metal from a city building and a Bronx high school principal who was already in hot water were among five city workers fined by the city’s Conflicts of Interest Board in proceedings announced on Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Suspended Principal Among 5 Fined by Conflicts Board', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conflicts of Interest', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Principals (School)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Conflicts of Interest Board (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T18:55:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9f92ac1-bc62-5fec-b0ba-94edfc76e4c9', 'word_count': 337, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9f92ac1-bc62-5fec-b0ba-94edfc76e4c9'}, {'abstract': 'The stage adaptation of “Flashdance,” based on the 1983 movie about a female welder-turned-dancer, will begin performances on Broadway in August 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/flashdance-musical-set-for-broadway-in-august-2013/', 'snippet': 'The stage adaptation of “Flashdance,” based on the 1983 movie about a female welder-turned-dancer, will begin performances on Broadway in August 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The stage adaptation of “Flashdance,” based on the 1983 movie about a female welder-dancer, will begin performances on Broadway in Aug. 2013, the show’s producers announced on Tuesday. A theater, dates and casting are still to be announced.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Flashdance’ Musical Set for Broadway in August 2013', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Flashdance’ Now Aims for Broadway in August', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T19:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6d7c273-0e6f-5203-aa0f-675fbd49a5d0', 'word_count': 357, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6d7c273-0e6f-5203-aa0f-675fbd49a5d0'}, {'abstract': 'The San Francisco-based artist’s urban-inspired paintings and installations may pack a serious visual wallop, but his family’s cozy Colonial Revival-style house, in the city’s Mission district, is completely chill.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/profile-in-style-barry-mcgee/', 'snippet': 'The San Francisco-based artist’s urban-inspired paintings and installations may pack a serious visual wallop, but his family’s cozy Colonial Revival-style house, in the city’s Mission district, is completely chill.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The San Francisco-based artist’s urban-inspired paintings and installations may pack a serious visual wallop, but his family’s cozy Colonial Revival-style house, in the city’s Mission district, is completely chill. Artworks by friends and treasures culled from vintage stores and antique markets around the world stand in for formal décor. “Everything in the house is connected to us personally,” McGee says. As much can be said of his no-frills fashion sense. “Some of my favorite pieces are from thrift shops. When I find something I really love, I live, work and sleep in it.” Some things, however, he’d sooner let go of. Asked about his current midcareer retrospective at the Berkeley Art Museum, he says, “It’s very intense to go back to the past and revive work that I’ve already experienced and moved forward from. It’s like seeing an old girlfriend — awkward at times, nostalgic at times and downright maddening and embarrassing.” More…', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Profile in Style | Barry McGee', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGee, Barry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T19:00:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sandra Ballentine', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ballentine', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c62cbc8e-da36-50d6-bf1c-ab5772ea992d', 'word_count': 153, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c62cbc8e-da36-50d6-bf1c-ab5772ea992d'}, {'abstract': 'The Obama and Romney campaigns answer 14 questions on science, health, innovation and related policies.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/obama-and-romney-weigh-in-on-science-questions/', 'snippet': 'The Obama and Romney campaigns answer 14 questions on science, health, innovation and related policies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Science Debate initiative, launched with the 2008 presidential campaign\xa0to try to develop reasoned discussion of science-framed issues by the candidates, produced a list of 14 questions this year with advice from an array of scientists and scientific organizations and publications. The answers provided by the Obama and Romney campaigns are now posted at the following links:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama and Romney Weigh in on Science Questions', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2008', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pace University', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T19:04:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '