n advance of the settlement’s final approval before a federal judge.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'My Thoughts on E-Book Pricing? Let Me Draw You a Picture', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antitrust Laws and Competition Issues', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Books and Readers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cote, Denise', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kohn, Bob', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T19:15:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a277b9e6-f177-59ba-8c5e-556b111149df', 'word_count': 224, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a277b9e6-f177-59ba-8c5e-556b111149df'}, {'abstract': 'Technical and budgetary problems have repeatedly delayed the opening of Berlin’s new airport, which was supposed to be a symbol of the city’s dominance and a tribute to German unification.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/05/business/global/airport-delays-undermine-image-of-german-efficiency.html', 'snippet': 'Technical and budgetary problems have repeatedly delayed the opening of Berlin’s new airport, which was supposed to be a symbol of the city’s dominance and a tribute to German unification.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The ambitious Berlin airport project conceived two decades ago as a glittering symbol of German unification and the city’s importance as a global hub has hit yet another delay and may not open before late next year, officials said Tuesday. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/05/business/AIRPORT/AIRPORT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/05/business/AIRPORT/AIRPORT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/05/business/AIRPORT/AIRPORT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 602, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/05/business/AIRPORT/AIRPORT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1204, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/05/business/AIRPORT/AIRPORT-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/05/business/AIRPORT/AIRPORT-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/05/business/AIRPORT/AIRPORT-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Airport Delays Undermine Image of German Efficiency', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Berlin Airport’s Delays Taint Image of Efficiency', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Berlin-Brandenburg International Airport', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRPORTS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Berlin (Germany)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T19:18:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicola Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicola', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5cc30c4b-60c9-593f-b7f0-186fe5ea89ea', 'word_count': 1265, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5cc30c4b-60c9-593f-b7f0-186fe5ea89ea'}, {'abstract': 'Scientists may have found the answer to why oceans emit so much methane.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/solving-the-ocean-methane-paradox/', 'snippet': 'Scientists may have found the answer to why oceans emit so much methane.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Four percent of the methane found in the earth’s atmosphere comes from oceans. But for decades, researchers have been flummoxed by how that could be. The only known biological source of methane is a class of microorganisms that produce methane when they are alive but die when exposed to oxygen. How could these microorganisms, called methanogens, be so plentiful in the oxygen-rich ocean?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Solving the Ocean Methane Paradox', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Methane', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Microbiology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oceans and Seas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Metcalf, William', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Hawaii', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Illinois', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T19:18:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanna M. Foster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca19bf33-f591-5094-9fe6-cc329ab9e438', 'word_count': 468, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca19bf33-f591-5094-9fe6-cc329ab9e438'}, {'abstract': 'The Columbus, Ohio, company will present tastings in Manhattan and Brooklyn Sept. 8 to 15.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/05/dining/jenis-ice-creams-to-offer-free-samples.html', 'snippet': 'The Columbus, Ohio, company will present tastings in Manhattan and Brooklyn Sept. 8 to 15.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jeni’s Splendid Ice Creams, based in Columbus, Ohio, has earned a national reputation thanks to quality and uncommon flavors, a Web site that offers mail order, an expanding distribution network and a cookbook. Now, for a week, the company’s ice cream truck heads east to patrol the streets of New York, dispensing sample scoops of its summer flavors: sweet corn and black raspberries, roasted strawberry buttermilk and salty caramel ice creams, and lemon-blueberry frozen yogurt. The trucks will mostly be parked outside retailers that sell Jeni’s ice cream.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/05/dining/05STUFF2/05STUFF2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/