'nyt://article/b6a09274-f3b2-5b2f-a3d8-5f12cfd87b99'}, {'abstract': 'Clint Eastwood’s sketch-comedy routine with an empty chair has become a seemingly mandatory (read: worn out) joke here, dropped with as much frequency as the names Michelle or Barack.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/at-democratic-convention-eastwood-joke-is-a-recurring-one/', 'snippet': 'Clint Eastwood’s sketch-comedy routine with an empty chair has become a seemingly mandatory (read: worn out) joke here, dropped with as much frequency as the names Michelle or Barack.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHARLOTTE, N.C. — It is the punch line that won’t die.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Democratic Convention, Eastwood Joke Is a Recurring One', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T19:58:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Barbaro and Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barbaro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e7cffd4-91a6-5a32-8958-1d673b261d44', 'word_count': 175, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e7cffd4-91a6-5a32-8958-1d673b261d44'}, {'abstract': 'A report says that control of one-quarter of Liberia’s land has been granted to logging companies in just two years through permits that were illegally or fraudulently awarded.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/illegal-logging-deals-rife-in-liberia-group-reports/', 'snippet': 'A report says that control of one-quarter of Liberia’s land has been granted to logging companies in just two years through permits that were illegally or fraudulently awarded.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For years, the environmental group Global Witness has been investigating the destruction of forests in the developing world. Much of the wood illegally harvested there ends up in the hands of international companies that manufacture furniture, paper and biofuels. Global Witness has campaigned against illegal harvesting of ebony and rosewood in Madagascar, exposed illegal exports of timber from Myanmar to China and documented the killings of antilogging activists in Cambodia.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Illegal Logging Deals Rife in Liberia, Group Reports', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forests and Forestry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Logging Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson Sirleaf, Ellen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Global Witness', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Liberia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T19:58:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c425247-1762-50b4-bb1c-dde0a0246fea', 'word_count': 208, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c425247-1762-50b4-bb1c-dde0a0246fea'}, {'abstract': 'The Intersect Fund focuses on sole proprietors with one or no employees that operate in traditional, “bread-and-butter” industries — beauty salons, cleaning services and caterers.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/drilling-down-the-impact-of-a-very-small-loan/', 'snippet': 'The Intersect Fund focuses on sole proprietors with one or no employees that operate in traditional, “bread-and-butter” industries — beauty salons, cleaning services and caterers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week’s Dashboard roundup of small-business news includes a link to an article about a new program introduced by the New Jersey Department of Labor in partnership with the nonprofit Intersect Fund, a microlender. With loans as small as $500, the program will support small-business development in poor and distressed areas of the state. We decided to contact Rohan Mathew, one of the founders of the Intersect Fund, to learn more. A condensed version of the conversation follows.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Drilling Down: The Impact of a Very Small Loan', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Microfinance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T20:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gene Marks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Marks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1979f0e9-11eb-5e83-8528-92b5fce95b81', 'word_count': 824, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1979f0e9-11eb-5e83-8528-92b5fce95b81'}, {'abstract': 'The Rev. Rodney McFarland made his way to his seat inside the Time Warner Cable Arena before the first evening of the Democratic National Convention in Charlotte, N.C.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/the-caucus-click-heading-toward-the-floor/', 'snippet': 'The Rev. Rodney McFarland made his way to his seat inside the Time Warner Cable Arena before the first evening of the Democratic National Convention in Charlotte, N.C.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Caucus Click: Heading Toward the Floor', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Democratic National Convention', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Charlotte (NC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T20:10:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Doug Mills', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Doug', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mills', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/40a2bfdf-90b6-5ed1-a3d1-c2b5436e4965', 'word_count': 1, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40a2bfdf-90b6-5ed1-a3d1-c2b5436e4965'}, {'abstract': 'A recent trip to Africa gave Bill Clinton, his daughter, Chelsea, and a handful of donors and aides from the Clintons’ years in Arkansas and the White House a firsthand look at the philanthropic work of the Clinton Foundation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/09/04/us/politics/20120905-CLINTON.html', 'snippet': 'A recent trip to Africa gave Bill Clinton, his daughter, Chelsea, and a handful of donors and aides from the Clintons’ years in Arkansas and the White House a firsthand look at the philanthropic work of the Clinton Foundation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A recent trip to Africa gave Bill Clinton, his daughter, Chelsea, and a handful of donors and aides from the Clintons’ years in Arkansas and the White House a firsthand look at the philanthropic work of the Clinton Foundation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/04/us/politics/20120905-CLINTON-slide-ZYQY/20120905-CLINTON-slide-ZYQY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/04/us/politics/20120905-CLINTON-slide-ZYQY/20120905-CLINTON-slide-ZYQY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/04/us/politics/20120905-CLINTON-slide-ZYQY/20120905-CLINTON-slide-ZYQY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/04/us/politics/20120905-CLINTON-slide-ZYQY/20120905-CLINTON-slide-ZYQY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/04/us/politics/20120905-CLINTON-slide-ZYQY/20120905-CLINTON-slide-ZYQY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Clinton Foundation in Africa', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Bill', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Uganda', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rwanda', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T20:12:45+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/b5e99a0a-67a6-58d7-82da-2cb02b053ef0', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/b5e99a0a-67a6-58d7-82da-2cb02b053ef0'}, {'abstract': 'For Joshua George, a race at the Paralympic Games made him realize that nobody gives you a medal for a month of solid workouts.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/at-paralympic-games-a-lesson-in-a-loss/', 'snippet': 'For Joshua George, a race at the Paralympic Games made him realize that nobody gives you a medal for a month of solid workouts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The wheelchair racer Joshua George will be competing in the 2012 Paralympic Games in London and writing for the 2012 London blog.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Paralympic Games, a Lesson in a Loss', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paralympic Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Track and Field', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T20:15:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joshua George', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joshua', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'George', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec03403f-064d-5e0e-8003-83ca881e240d', 'word_count': 1177, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec03403f-064d-5e0e-8003-83ca881e240d'}, {'abstract': 'Andy Murray went old-school to disarm Milos Raonic’s power game in their United States Open match on Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/the-chip-return-the-drop-shot-and-andy-murray/', 'snippet': 'Andy Murray went old-school to disarm Milos Raonic’s power game in their United States Open match on Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Andy Murray used the chip return to get into the point against Milos Raonic’s huge first serve, then played shrewd neutralizing groundstrokes, taking away his two chief weapons: the booming serve and the first strike forehand. It was a clinic in how to disarm the power game, as Murray massaged the ball in the tricky, gusty conditions on Arthur Ashe Stadium on Monday, using chips, counterpunching backhands and, on several occasions, soft drop shots to destroy Raonic’s rhythm.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Chip Return, the Drop Shot and Andy Murray', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Federer, Roger', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lendl, Ivan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McEnroe, John', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murray, Andy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Raonic, Milos', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roddick, Andy', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T20:18:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Geoff Macdonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Geoff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macdonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d89c601-02a1-55ca-9133-2da23591da60', 'word_count': 591, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d89c601-02a1-55ca-9133-2da23591da60'}, {'abstract': 'The state, with the power to set its own emissions policy, was at the negotiating table throughout the creation of the next round of federal fuel economy standards.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/californias-quiet-but-crucial-role-in-shaping-fuel-economy-standards/', 'snippet': 'The state, with the power to set its own emissions policy, was at the negotiating table throughout the creation of the next round of federal fuel economy standards.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the Obama administration completed the Corporate Average Fuel Economy, or CAFE, standards for 2017 to 2025 last month, it was a milestone in a long and frequently contentious process, but not the last word.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California’s Quiet but Crucial Role in Shaping Fuel Economy Standards', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ALLIANCE OF AUTOMOBILE MANUFACTURERS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T20:20:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Motavalli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Motavalli', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/622d0df8-5f4c-5dc4-9752-abf16eb106a8', 'word_count': 481, 'uri': 'nyt://article/622d0df8-5f4c-5dc4-9752-abf16eb106a8'}, {'abstract': 'At Eleven Madison Park, the chef Daniel Humm and general manager Will Guidara believe a restaurant should take risks in the quest for “endless reinvention.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/05/dining/at-eleven-madison-park-a-reinvention.html', 'snippet': 'At Eleven Madison Park, the chef Daniel Humm and general manager Will Guidara believe a restaurant should take risks in the quest for “endless reinvention.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'THERE’S something Whitmanesque about what Daniel Humm, the chef of Eleven Madison Park, and Will Guidara, the general manager, envision for their restaurant when it reveals its reinvention on Friday. Think of it as a gastronomic paean to New York City, full of dishes and gestures that make reference to the four-century saga of the metropolis.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/05/dining/05ELEVEN1_SPAN/05ELEVEN1a-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 291, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/05/dining/05ELEVEN1_SPAN/05ELEVEN1a-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 291}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/05/dining/05ELEVEN1_SPAN/05ELEVEN1a-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 497, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/05/dining/05ELEVEN1_SPAN/05ELEVEN1a-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 994, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/05/dining/05ELEVEN1_SPAN/05ELEVEN1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/05/dining/05ELEVEN1_SPAN/05ELEVEN1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Reinvention, With Card Tricks and a Drink Cart', 'kicker': 'Fall Restaurant Preview', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Reinvention, With Card Tricks And a Drink Cart', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Humm, Daniel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Eleven Madison Park (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Guidara, Will', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T20:22:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Gordinier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gordinier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad680227-303b-522c-9ed0-d7cb5377f529', 'word_count': 864, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad680227-303b-522c-9ed0-d7cb5377f529'}, {'abstract': 'The Financial Industry Regulatory Authority said its vice chairman, Stephen Luparello, was leaving to join the law firm Wilmer Hale in Washington.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/finra-executive-departs-for-wilmer-hale/', 'snippet': 'The Financial Industry Regulatory Authority said its vice chairman, Stephen Luparello, was leaving to join the law firm Wilmer Hale in Washington.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wall Street’s self-policing organization has lost one of its top cops. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Finra Executive Departs for Wilmer Hale', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals an