.–The big question heading into the Democratic Convention is just how forcefully the party will defend the Affordable Care Act, which the president fought to pass and then declined to sell. On Tuesday, an unusually vocal endorsement of the law came from an unlikely source: Anti-abortion Democrats.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Anti-Abortion, Pro-Democrat', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Democratic National Convention', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stupak, Bart', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T20:49:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Juliet Lapidos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Juliet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lapidos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4fdedc39-8d69-59e8-8c7b-0ba03a40bb97', 'word_count': 439, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4fdedc39-8d69-59e8-8c7b-0ba03a40bb97'}, {'abstract': 'Several well-known weight-loss specialists announced their support for Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg’s proposal to restrict sales of big sugary drinks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/05/nyregion/mayors-soda-plan-backed-by-weight-loss-industry.html', 'snippet': 'Several well-known weight-loss specialists announced their support for Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg’s proposal to restrict sales of big sugary drinks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The names read like a who’s who of diet tycoons.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25',