k-hosni-charged-with-corruption-in-egypt.html', 'snippet': 'Farouk Hosni, who was culture minister for more than two decades, was charged with corruption on Tuesday, joining other former officials accused of using their positions to enrich themselves.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — Farouk Hosni, who for more than two decades served as culture minister under President Hosni Mubarak, was charged with corruption on Tuesday, the state news media reported, joining a number of other former government officials and businessmen accused of using their positions and connections to enrich themselves.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt to Try Ex-Official on Charge of Corruption', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Egypt to Try Ex-Official On Charge Of Corruption', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mubarak, Hosni', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mubarak, Gamal', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mubarak, Suzanne', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hosny, Farouk', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mubarak, Alaa', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T21:04:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Sayare', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sayare', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b88ee8d9-7431-5f6a-b0e6-a6aec4feb9bb', 'word_count': 522, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b88ee8d9-7431-5f6a-b0e6-a6aec4feb9bb'}, {'abstract': 'Robert Gibbs, the former press secretary who is now an outside adviser to Mr. Obama, was mobbed when he walked through the convention hall on Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/can-we-have-your-autograph-mr-gibbs/', 'snippet': 'Robert Gibbs, the former press secretary who is now an outside adviser to Mr. Obama, was mobbed when he walked through the convention hall on Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHARLOTTE, N.C. – If you are into celebrity-spotting – and who isn’t? — trolling the halls of political conventions can be rewarding, as long as your standards are not too high. Think less George Clooney and more Andrea Mitchell or Chuck Schumer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Can We Have Your Autograph, Mr. Gibbs?', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Democratic National Convention', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gibbs, Robert L', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Charlotte (NC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T21:05:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Nagourney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nagourney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e01df78a-dc70-5a61-87e0-6e709542afc1', 'word_count': 232, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e01df78a-dc70-5a61-87e0-6e709542afc1'}, {'abstract': 'How many shades of green can you distinguish?', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/its-not-easy-seeing-green/', 'snippet': 'How many shades of green can you distinguish?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Describing color is more properly a poetic art than a scientific one, argues Merriam Webster’s Kory Stamper in a recent, charming post that I cited in my latest dispatch for The One-Page Magazine. Looking back over more than 150 years’ worth of definitions, Stamper tracks the evolution (or, depending on your perspective, devolution) in approach from more picturesque comparisons — blue with “the clear sky,” red with “blood or rubies” — to the more formulaic color chart system used in Webster’s Third New International Dictionary, which is currently undergoing revisions. “With its zeal for modernism and science and objectivity,” Stamper says, the most recent edition of the dictionary “sometimes lost sight of the forest for all the xylem and phloem.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'It’s Not Easy Seeing Green', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T21:05:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maud Newton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maud', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/790a0e6b-5076-5189-a121-a9a922d43f04', 'word_count': 492, 'uri': 'nyt://article/790a0e6b-5076-5189-a121-a9a922d43f04'}, {'abstract': 'On his first trip to the Russian city, the Frugal Traveler scores two deals from the Hermitage, finds ideal budget boxers and does a shot to get a shot.', 'web_url': 'https://frugaltraveler.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/saving-rubles-in-st-petersburg/', 'snippet': 'On his first trip to the Russian city, the Frugal Traveler scores two deals from the Hermitage, finds ideal budget boxers and does a shot to get a shot.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT is hard not to like St. Petersburg. Its canals invite unavoidable comparisons with Venice, its Baroque and neo-Classical architecture recall, Rorschach-style, whatever other European city you know best. Meanwhile, Russia is in the details: the onion-domed Church of the Savior on the Spilled Blood, the public tram fare collectors straight from babushka central casting, the Cyrillic signs, the young women for whom beauty comes naturally but a light touch with the mascara does not.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Saving Rubles in St. Petersburg', 'kicker': 'Frugal Traveler', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In St. Petersburg, Gilded Grandeur On a Few Rubles', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T21:11:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By SETH KUGEL', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'KUGEL', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7eeaa7b5-299b-58cd-806c-e72622f242e1', 'word_count': 1569, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7eeaa7b5-299b-58cd-806c-e72622f242e1'}, {'abstract': 'In the work of a 24-year-old poet, the Internet’s staccato vernacular comes alive.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/timely-the-prophet/', 'snippet': 'In the work of a 24-year-old poet, the Internet’s staccato vernacular comes alive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Prepare to love a poet, to get poems stuck in your head like they were pop songs — like it was the age of Homer or Milton or Poe, when poets were pop stars. According to the 24-year-old M.F.A. dropout Steve Roggenbuck, “We are entering a golden age of literature” that is perfect for poetry. Chunks of verse should populate the “content streams” on phones and Facebook feeds. His do.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '136', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline