g Kim’s “For Ellen.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even though its protagonist is a heavy-metal singer, “For Ellen,” So Yong Kim’s third feature, is a remarkably quiet film. This simple, closely observed story — of a musician on the verge of divorce trying to find some connection to his estranged young daughter — certainly seems wired for melodrama. But Ms. Kim and the lead actor, Paul Dano, turn down the emotional volume, betting that whispers and downcast looks will be more effective than shouting and raging.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/05/arts/0905FORELLEN/0905FORELLEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/05/arts/0905FORELLEN/0905FORELLEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/05/arts/0905FORELLEN/0905FORELLEN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/05/arts/0905FORELLEN/0905FORELLEN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1437, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/05/arts/0905FORELLEN/0905FORELLEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/05/arts/0905FORELLEN/0905FORELLEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/05/arts/0905FORELLEN/0905FORELLEN-thumb