hion week momentum and access to reel in new users.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When it’s all about splashy big-budget runway shows what’s an app maker to do? With all eyes soon to be on New York Fashion Week, digital style start-ups have been scrambling for ways to get involved. Problem is they don’t have the cash or the clout to compete with big brands for attention. Here’s how seven start-ups are nimbly getting in on the action.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Digital Style Start-Ups Get Nimble at New York Fashion Week', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T23:17:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Caroline Waxler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Caroline', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waxler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ae052f5-2028-58b7-8f47-bd5c2e38c616', 'word_count': 774, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ae052f5-2028-58b7-8f47-bd5c2e38c616'}, {'abstract': 'On a recent trip to Africa, former President Bill Clinton discussed a range of topics — from health care and the political climate in Washington to the shooting in Aurora, Colo., to Secretary of State Hillary Clinton’s plans.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/but-wait-theres-more-excerpts-from-conversations-with-president-clinton/', 'snippet': 'On a recent trip to Africa, former President Bill Clinton discussed a range of topics — from health care and the political climate in Washington to the shooting in Aurora, Colo., to Secretary of State Hillary Clinton’s plans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a recent Clinton Foundation trip to Africa, former President Bill Clinton discussed a range of topics — from health care and the political climate in Washington to the shooting at an Aurora, Colo., movie theater to Secretary of State Hillary Clinton’s future plans. Here are edited excerpts of those conversations, which took place in mid-July in South Africa, Rwanda, Uganda and Cyprus.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'But Wait, There’s More. Excerpts From Conversations With President Clinton.', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2008', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Bill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T23:21:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Chozick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chozick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8085fa9-23c4-5f75-8d40-9076af9ba522', 'word_count': 1371, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8085fa9-23c4-5f75-8d40-9076af9ba522'}, {'abstract': 'The findings challenged conventional medical thinking, which holds that prolonged resuscitation for hospital patients that go into cardiac arrest is usually futile.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/05/health/research/doctors-may-be-ending-cpr-efforts-too-soon-study-says.html', 'snippet': 'The findings challenged conventional medical thinking, which holds that prolonged resuscitation for hospital patients that go into cardiac arrest is usually futile.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When a hospital patient goes into cardiac arrest, one of the most difficult questions facing the medical team is how long to continue cardiopulmonary resuscitation. Now a new study involving hundreds of hospitals suggests that many doctors may be giving up too soon.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/05/us/jp-CARDIAC/jp-CARDIAC-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/05/us/jp-CARDIAC/jp-CARDIAC-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/05/us/jp-CARDIAC/jp-CARDIAC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/05/us/jp-CARDIAC/jp-CARDIAC-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/05/us/jp-CARDIAC/jp-CARDIAC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/05/us/jp-CARDIAC/jp-CARDIAC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/05/us/jp-CARDIAC/jp-CARDIAC-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Prolonged CPR Holds Benefits, a Study Shows', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Prolonged CPR Holds Benefits, A Study Shows', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lancet, The (Journal)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Heart', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cardiopulmonary Resuscitation (CPR)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emergency Medical Treatment', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-04T23:45:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Research', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roni Caryn Rabin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roni', 'middlename': 'Caryn', 'lastname': 'Rabin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f12a8ec-acc1-5bf2-84c0-460781d87780', 'word_count': 859, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f12a8ec-acc1-5bf2-84c0-460781d87780'}, {'abstract': 'The Dallas Cowboys will open their N.F.L. season Wednesday against the Giants, who knocked them out of the playoffs last year and have owned the series lately.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/05/sports/football/cowboys-to-face-giants-in-nfl-season-opener.html', 'snippet': 'The Dallas Cowboys will open their N.F.L. season Wednesday against the Giants, who knocked them out of the playoffs last year and have owned the series lately.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IRVING, Tex. — Eight months and three days seems like a long time for motivation to marinate. But as the Dallas Cowboys continued to stew in the buildup to Wednesday night’s N.F.L. season opener against the Giants, they sounded trapped somewhere between seeking revenge and suffering championship envy.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/05/sports/YCOWBOYS/YCOWBOYS-articleLarge.jpg', 'hei