ome criticize what they call heavy-handed tactics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few years ago, Elliot G. Sander, the executive director of the Metropolitan Transportation Authority at the time, got a call at home from Vito J. Lopez, the assemblyman and Brooklyn Democratic leader. Mr. Lopez wanted his son-in-law, a transit manager named Keith Summa, promoted. Mr. Sander was dubious, and soon after called Mr. Lopez to say it would not happen.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/05/nyregion/JP-VITO/JP-VITO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/05/nyregion/JP-VITO/JP-VITO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/05/nyregion/JP-VITO/JP-VITO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/05/nyregion/JP-VITO/JP-VITO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/05/nyregion/JP-VITO/JP-VITO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'If This Brooklyn Kingmaker Is Asking, Saying No Is Risky Option', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'If This Brooklyn Kingmaker Is Asking, Saying No Is Risky Option', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organiza