mas Kaplan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Danny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hakim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4fdd79c6-ae3f-531f-85c1-7acbeea1e3bf', 'word_count': 742, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4fdd79c6-ae3f-531f-85c1-7acbeea1e3bf'}, {'abstract': 'Mario Cárdenas Guillén, a presumed top leader of one of the country’s largest and most powerful criminal groups, was caught by the Mexican Navy on Monday as he was carrying a large gun.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/05/world/americas/major-drug-suspect-is-arrested-in-mexico.html', 'snippet': 'Mario Cárdenas Guillén, a presumed top leader of one of the country’s largest and most powerful criminal groups, was caught by the Mexican Navy on Monday as he was carrying a large gun.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A presumed top leader of the Gulf Cartel, one of the country’s largest and most powerful criminal groups, was caught by the Mexican Navy on Monday as he was carrying a large gun. The kingpin, Mario Cárdenas Guillén, was detained in Tamaulipas State, where violence has surged in the past couple of years. The navy did not detail what kind of gun he had, but said he was also in possession of cash, ammunition, fragmentation grenades and other arms. Mr. Cárdenas took over the group — reluctantly, some analysts say — when his brother was killed by Mexican forces in 2010. The Gulf Cartel has waned as a spinoff group, the Zetas, has battled for its turf. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/05/world/BRIEFS/BRIEFS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 669, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name':