late-season swoon won’t cost them a playoff spot.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/04/with-lead-all-but-gone-yankees-dwell-on-the-finish/', 'snippet': 'Starting Wednesday, the Yankees have 27 games to make sure that a late-season swoon won’t cost them a playoff spot.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ST. PETERSBURG, Fla. — For days, if not weeks, the Yankees have been holding dear to one irrefutable fact of the American League East race. As poorly as they have played, and as well as the Baltimore Orioles and Tampa Bay Rays have performed, the Yankees have still held the lead.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Lead All but Gone, Yankees Dwell on the Finish', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chavez, Eric', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Girardi, Joe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-05T02:03:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e257ebb7-add2-5301-9a15-68cd64798fa4', 'word_count': 815, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e257ebb7-add2-5301-9a15-68cd64798fa4'}, {'abstract': 'Whether the economy is doing better or worse than it was four years ago can depend on when you start counting.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2012/09/05/us/politics/better-and-worse.html', 'snippet': 'Whether the economy is doing better or worse than it was four years ago can depend on when you start counting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Whether the economy is doing better or worse than it was four years ago can depend on when you start counting.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Better and Worse', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-05T02:04:16+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/c9a02bb1-561e-5304-b68b-ec7e0ea3bf0f', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/c9a02bb1-561e-5304-b68b-ec7e0ea3bf0f'}, {'abstract': 'The pardon of Ramil Safarov by the president of Azerbaijan has caused tension with Armenia, the home country of the serviceman that Mr. Safarov killed eight years ago.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/05/world/europe/pardon-reignites-azerbaijan-armenia-tensions.html', 'snippet': 'The pardon of Ramil Safarov by the president of Azerbaijan has caused tension with Armenia, the home country of the serviceman that Mr. Safarov killed eight years ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — Ramil Safarov stepped uncertainly off the plane in his native Azerbaijan last Friday, returning home after spending eight years in a Hungarian prison for a gruesome murder. But it took only a few minutes for the celebrations to begin. There was a pardon, a new apartment, eight years of back pay, a promotion to the rank of major and the status of a national hero.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/05/global-home/5armenia-image/5armenia-image-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 648, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'su