m-for-mamata-banerjee-in-muslim-officers-book/', 'snippet': 'The West Bengal chief minister is trying to “trick” Muslims with new policies, book claims.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KOLKATA — In just over a week since its launch, Musalamander Koroniyo (What Muslims Should Do),  a book in written in Bengali by a senior police officer, has attracted national attention and raised new questions about intolerance in West Bengal, where Mamata Banerjee is chief minister.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sharp Criticism for Mamata Banerjee in Muslim Officer’s Book', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Banerjee, Mamata', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'All India Trinamool Congress', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kolkata (India)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Bengal (India)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-05T07:26:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anuradha Sharma', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anuradha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sharma', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d510de39-4f1a-5298-9c91-bf0488fdfd3e', 'word_count': 1378, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d510de39-4f1a-5298-9c91-bf0488fdfd3e'}, {'abstract': 'The convention’s primetime lineup almost seems designed to suggest that the Democratic Party has a past and a present, but not much of a future.', 'web_url': 'https://campaignstops.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/05/the-obamas-party/', 'snippet': 'The convention’s primetime lineup almost seems designed to suggest that the Democratic Party has a past and a present, but not much of a future.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After Ann Romney spoke in Tampa, Fla., last week, much of the next day’s conversation revolved around whether the convention organizers had made a big mistake by having her precede Chris Christie to the lectern. Her speech was praised to the skies, his was criticized for being self-serving and self-absorbed – and by leaving the last word to the New Jersey governor, critics argued, the convention swept the spotlight off her husband and undercut the power of her pitch.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Obamas’ Party', 'kicker': 'Campaign Stops', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Democratic National Convention', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Republican National Convention', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Michelle', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-05T07:29:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/136324b0-7318-516a-a533-07222a00dac6', 'word_count': 920, 'uri': 'nyt://article/136324b0-7318-516a-a533-07222a00dac6'}, {'abstract': 'Fishing disputes, harassed religious pilgrims and a suspended sports official signal weakening of ties.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/05/relations-between-india-and-sri-lanka-sour/', 'snippet': 'Fishing disputes, harassed religious pilgrims and a suspended sports official signal weakening of ties.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week, while traveling down the coast of Tamil Nadu for  my article about the fishing wars between India and Sri Lanka, I noticed pilgrims walking along the side of the road. They trudged along, despite the heat, as they walked kilometers on a pilgrimage to Christian shrines in the state of Tamil Nadu. What I had not realized is that some of the pilgrims visiting the state were from Sri Lanka.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Relations Between India and Sri Lanka Sour', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sinhalese (Ethnic Group)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tamils (Ethnic Group)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sri Lanka', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tamil Nadu (India)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-05T08:23:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Yardley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yardley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/954869a8-550f-58e9-842c-6745eacb500b', 'word_count': 575, 'uri': 'nyt://article/954869a8-550f-58e9-842c-6745eacb500b'}, {'abstract': 'The question is about the percentage of a home’s selling price that is paid in the buyer’s down payment in an affordable housing program.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/05/test-yourself-math-sept-5-2012/', 'snippet': 'The question is about the percentage of a home’s selling price that is paid in the buyer’s down payment in an affordable housing program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Test your math skills with this question created by Scott Matthews at Math for America from the article “In Affordable Housing Program, City Oversight of Builders Is Found Wanting.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Test Yourself | Math, Sept. 5, 2012', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-05T08:33:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5073530d-cd81-55ff-b1cd-1bace410a433', 'word_count': 57, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5073530d-cd81-55ff-b1cd-1bace410a433'}, {'abstract': 'What do you think should be done to stop elephant poaching in Garamba National Park and elsewhere in Africa?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/05/elephants-in-trouble/', 'snippet': 'What do you think should be done to stop elephant poaching in Garamba National Park and elsewhere in Africa?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Watch the video to answer the following questions:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Elephants in Trouble', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-05T08:44:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Gonchar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonchar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/02a3b92b-12ee-531e-9eb2-c38d5b6a1c45', 'word_count': 139, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02a3b92b-12ee-531e-9eb2-c38d5b6a1c45'}, {'abstract': 'Why the battle to take credit for Ohio’s ever-so-slightly above-average economy could swing the presidential election.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/09/magazine/ohio-economy.html', 'snippet': 'Why the battle to take credit for Ohio’s ever-so-slightly above-average economy could swing the presidential election.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The way John Kasich sees it, he is fulfilling a grand design, a mission for which he was chosen by God, to save Ohio. “It’s like what what’s-his-name told the hobbit,” Ohio’s Republican governor told me as we flew on the plane that ferries him around the state. “What’s that guy’s name? Gandel? Gandorf?” A pair of young aides seated across from Kasich called out helpfully over the drone of the engine. “Gandalf,” Kasich repeated. “Do you remember what he told the hobbit?”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/magazine/09ohio1/09ohio1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/09/magazine/09ohio1/09ohio1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/magazine/09ohio1/09ohio1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 769, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/magazine/09ohio1/09ohio1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1537, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/20