azine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Bai', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bai', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b122515f-2281-5ca8-8749-7a64f31712fb', 'word_count': 7113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b122515f-2281-5ca8-8749-7a64f31712fb'}, {'abstract': 'Joseph Michael Lopez’s New York street photography shows the city as a beast of chaos that New Yorkers attempt to contain, or at least live with, on a daily basis.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/05/breaking-down-the-beast/', 'snippet': 'Joseph Michael Lopez’s New York street photography shows the city as a beast of chaos that New Yorkers attempt to contain, or at least live with, on a daily basis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Joseph Michael Lopez’s photography is fundamentally about his New York. He presents street scenes, people and everyday objects without any semblance of objectivity.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Breaking Down the Beast', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lopez, Joseph Michael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-05T09:00:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Moskowitz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moskowitz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c985b0d3-7fd7-5a38-a3dd-ac0f3b754d36', 'word_count': 552, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c985b0d3-7fd7-5a38-a3dd-ac0f3b754d36'}, {'abstract': 'Would you call yourself competitive? If so, in what circumstances does your drive to win come out most?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/05/how-competitive-are-you/', 'snippet': 'Would you call yourself competitive? If so, in what circumstances does your drive to win come out most?', 'lead_paragraph': 'This question is inspired by a recent article about President Obama that reports that, whether shooting pool, reading to children or working to raise his bowling scores, he cannot contain his competitive nature. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Competitive Are You?', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-05T09:05:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ariha Setalvad and Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ariha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Setalvad', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9eefbe37-011b-5ab7-a6c9-4bc535b50456', 'word_count': 314, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9eefbe37-011b-5ab7-a6c9-4bc535b50456'}, {'abstract': 'The Dutch financial services giant ING Group plans to sell its 9 percent stake in Capital One in a deal that could be worth around $3 billion.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/09/05/ing-to-sell-stake-in-capital-one/', 'snippet': 'The Dutch financial services giant ING Group plans to sell its 9 percent stake in Capital One in a deal that could be worth around $3 billion.', 'lead_paragraph': '9:16 a.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'ING Group to Sell Stake in Capital One', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-05T09:47:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0454253-b8a8-5fdb-90e8-b14045980c8f', 'word_count': 282, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0454253-b8a8-5fdb-90e8-b14045980c8f'}, {'abstract': 'A World Economic Forum survey of 144 countries noted that a growing north-south divide was one of the factors at the heart of the continuing euro zone crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/business/global/daily-euro-zone-watch.html', 'snippet': 'A World Economic Forum survey of 144 countries noted that a growing north-south divide was one of the factors at the heart of the continuing euro zone crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — European economies are diverging in competitiveness, according to a report published Wednesday that highlighted a growing north-south divide as one of the factors at the heart of the continuing euro zone crisis.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Competitiveness Gap Widening in Europe, Study Finds', 'kicker': 'Euro Watch', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Competition Gap Grows In Europe, Study Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Economic Forum', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Monetary Union', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European