/article/50ca0959-7bee-59f3-b446-d46480829a99', 'word_count': 890, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50ca0959-7bee-59f3-b446-d46480829a99'}, {'abstract': 'Mark Bittman has had enough of white-tablecloth restaurants. Now, he writes, he wants “his” place, and has some specific thoughts on what that means. Is there a place you think of as yours? If so, are you willing to share?', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/05/eating-where-it-feels-like-home-but-you-dont-have-to-do-the-dishes/', 'snippet': 'Mark Bittman has had enough of white-tablecloth restaurants. Now, he writes, he wants “his” place, and has some specific thoughts on what that means. Is there a place you think of as yours? If so, are you willing to share?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The cookbook author and New York Times food writer Mark Bittman has had enough of white-tablecloth restaurants, he writes. He wants his own place, wherever he is in the world, and he’s got some specific requirements for it: ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Eating Where It Feels Like Home (But You Don’t Have to Do the Dishes)', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bittman, Mark', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Madrid (Spain)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-05T15:23:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By The International Herald Tribune', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The International Herald Tribune'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a06033af-9ad3-501c-bd45-ffd0e9c0dd68', 'word_count': 439, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a06033af-9ad3-501c-bd45-ffd0e9c0dd68'}, {'abstract': 'In a glancing fashion, the headliners on the first night of the Democratic National Convention nod to same-sex marriage.', 'web_url': 'https://bruni.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/05/marriage-equality-goes-prime-time/', 'snippet': 'In a glancing fashion, the headliners on the first night of the Democratic National Convention nod to same-sex marriage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHARLOTTE, N.C.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Marriage Equality Goes Prime Time', 'kicker': 'Frank Bruni', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Democratic National Convention', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Castro, Julian', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Michelle', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Patrick, Deval L', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Charlotte (NC)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-05T15:24:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Frank Bruni', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Frank', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bruni', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97f9c458-1511-5bd1-92b3-3cbdced81bc7', 'word_count': 436, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97f9c458-1511-5bd1-92b3-3cbdced81bc7'}, {'abstract': 'At times, it seemed as if every speaker on the first night of the Democratic National Convention was touting same-sex marriage.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/05/at-the-democratic-convention-an-emphasis-on-social-issues/', 'snippet': 'At times, it seemed as if every speaker on the first night of the Democratic National Convention was touting same-sex marriage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHARLOTTE, N.C. — On Monday night, Michelle Obama told the nation that her husband wants everyone to succeed no matter “who we love.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At the Democratic Convention, an Emphasis on Social Issues', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Democratic National Convention', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Michelle', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-05T15:25:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7bd97a9-8128-53c9-a5cc-e1f408b8925a', 'word_count': 716, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7bd97a9-8128-53c9-a5cc-e1f408b8925a'}, {'abstract': 'Three Siberian tiger cubs, now 4 months old, are part of an effort by the Bronx Zoo’s parent organization, the Wildlife Conservation Society, to educate people about tigers’ critically endangered status.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/05/tiger-triplets-make-their-debut-in-the-bronx/', 'snippet': 'Three Siberian tiger cubs, now 4 months old, are part of an effort by the Bronx Zoo’s parent organization, the Wildlife Conservation Society, to educate people about tigers’ critically endangered status.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is a busy time for local youngsters. Just as the city’s children prepare to go back to school, three 4-month-old Siberian tiger cubs made their debut on Wednesday at the Bronx Zoo (see video below or click here). ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tiger Triplets Make Their Debut in the Bronx', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tigers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bronx Zoo Wildlife Conservation Park', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-05T15:26:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/099e2cc1-afae-5d51-bef1-825878ced1ac', 'word_count': 224, 'uri': 'nyt://article/099e2cc1-afae-5d51-bef1-825878ced1ac'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights of this year’s festival include a premiere of the film adaptation of “Cloud Atlas,” followed by a conversation with its directors Tom Tykwer and Andy and Lana Wachowski.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/05/lineup-announced-for-2012-new-yorker-festival/', 'snippet': 'Highlights of this year’s festival include a premiere of the film adaptation of “Cloud Atlas,” followed by a conversation with its directors Tom Tykwer and Andy and Lana Wachowski.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first United States showing of the film version of “Cloud Atlas” – as well as a rare showing-up by its co-directors Andy and Lana Wachowski – will be one of the marquee events of the 2012 New Yorker Festival. On Wednesday organizers announced the lineup for the annual festival, which runs this year from Oct. 5 through 7 and features public events with various cultural luminaries and contributors to The New Yorker magazine. Among its highlights is a premiere screening of “Cloud Atlas,” adapted from the David Mitchell novel, followed by a conversation with the Wachowski siblings (“The Matrix,” “Speed Racer”) and their co-director, Tom Tykwer. (The “Cloud Atlas” team will be interviewed by Aleksandar Hemon, who wrote about them in this week’s issue of The New Yorker.)', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Yorker Festival to Include ‘Cloud Atlas’ Premiere', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Cloud Atlas’ Premiere At New Yorker Festival', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Armisen, Fred', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bechdel, Alison', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brownstein, Carrie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ehle, Jennifer', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garcia, Greg', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Cherry', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Norah', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schur, Michael', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Slattery, John', 'rank': 9, 'major': 