lue': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-05T15:38:44+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/8a2d35bf-0a75-53a7-a37a-d501d76c0a43', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/8a2d35bf-0a75-53a7-a37a-d501d76c0a43'}, {'abstract': 'On Thursday night, should he linger on his record or focus on the future?', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/05/what-should-the-president-say/', 'snippet': 'On Thursday night, should he linger on his record or focus on the future?', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHARLOTTE, N.C.–Only 38 percent of respondents in a new Gallup poll said Mitt Romney’s performance at the Republican Convention was good or excellent, the lowest approval rating for any presidential candidate’s acceptance speech since Gallup started asking the question.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Should the President Say?', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Democratic National Convention', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-05T15:39:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93bdb473-d70d-5a35-bb08-0cd24259cb8b', 'word_count': 170, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93bdb473-d70d-5a35-bb08-0cd24259cb8b'}, {'abstract': 'David Ferrer emphasized his hit-and-run tactics to defeat Richard Gasquet at the United States Open.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/05/breaking-it-down-ferrer-vs-gasquet/', 'snippet': 'David Ferrer emphasized his hit-and-run tactics to defeat Richard Gasquet at the United States Open.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Malcolm Gladwell’s 2005 best-seller, “Blink,” he focused on the subject of “thin-slicing” – the ability to understand what is important from an extremely narrow moment in time.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Breaking It Down: Ferrer vs. Gasquet', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Djokovic, Novak', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ferrer, David', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gasquet, Richard', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-05T15:43:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': "By Craig O'Shannessy", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Craig', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Shannessy", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7703c3c-77ca-5542-83ce-3d46567844ad', 'word_count': 874, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7703c3c-77ca-5542-83ce-3d46567844ad'}, {'abstract': 'Is the minimum wage one of the most important causes of the American income slowdown?', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/05/why-the-minimum-wage-doesnt-explain-stagnant-wages/', 'snippet': 'Is the minimum wage one of the most important causes of the American income slowdown?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Until the mid-1980s, only a single state – and one of the smallest in population, Alaska – had set a minimum wage higher than the federal minimum. But with the federal minimum remaining unchanged at $3.35 an hour for most of the 1980s, more states began to set higher floors for wages.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why the Minimum Wage Doesn’t Explain Stagnant Wages', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minimum Wage', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Autor, David', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Card, David', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, David S', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Economic Policy Institute', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-05T15:44:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5fe55d13-9af1-558c-b96e-7f489da74f7a', 'word_count': 988, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5fe55d13-9af1-558c-b96e-7f489da74f7a'}, {'abstract': 'Poppin, an e-commerce start-up that opened to the public on Tuesday, thinks it has a solution to the problems suffered by office supply companies like Staples: an uncluttered Web site, colorful staplers and pens and designing, manufacturing and selling products itself. But will penny-pinching office managers order $14 magenta staplers?', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/05/a-start-up-offers-a-new-way-to-shop-for-office-supplies/', 'snippet': 'Poppin, an e-commerce start-up that opened to the public on Tuesday, thinks it has a solution to the problems suffered by office supply companies like Staples: an uncluttered Web site, colorful staplers and pens and designing, manufacturing and se...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The renaissance of e-commerce has brought us new ways to shop for pants, diapers and eyeglasses. Next up: office supplies.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/31/technology/31bits-poppin/31bits-poppin-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 180, 'width': 592, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/31/technology/31bits-poppin/31bits-poppin-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 180, 'width': 592, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Start-Up Offers a New Way to Shop for Office Supplies', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-05T15:49:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claire Cain Miller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claire', 'middlename': 'Cain', 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6258850-8acb-51c7-96c0-927ade387867', 'word_count': 544, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6258850-8acb-51c7-96c0-927ade387867'}, {'abstract': 'The erosion of a big lead, the growing sense of panic in the fan base — that’s something that just hasn’t happened in the current Yankees era of success.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/05/yankees-borrow-a-page-from-the-mets/', 'snippet': 'The erosion of a big lead, the growing sense of panic in the fan base — that’s something that just hasn’t happened in the current Yankees era of success.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In New York, it’s the Mets who normally have a copyright on collapses. They fell apart after the All-Star break this season, going 11-29; they blew an easy shot at the postseason in 2008 with some unbelievable bullpen mayhem in the final weeks of September; and they made history by blowing a seven-game division lead with 17 games to go in 2007.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yankees Borrow a Page From the Mets', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Showalter, Buck', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Torre, Joe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-05T15:56:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jay Schreiber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schreiber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/819e8344-933a-5899-8ca7-96a09166cb55', 'word_count': 575, 'uri': 'nyt://article/819e8344-933a-5899-8ca7-96a09166cb55'}, {'abstract': 'Former President Bill Clinton tried to rebut Republican arguments against the re-election of President Obama in a major speech at the Democratic National Convention Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/us/politics/obama-to-speak-indoors-because-of-weather-threat.html', 'snippet': 'Former President Bill Clinton tried to rebut Republican arguments against the re-election of President Obama in a major speech at the Democratic National Convention Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHARLOTTE, N.C. — Former President Bill Clinton tried to rebut Republican arguments against the re-election of President Obama in a major speech at the Democratic National Convention Wednesday night, saying Mr. Obama has taken steps to turn around an economy left in shambles by Republicans.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/06/us/06convention_span/06convention_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/06/us/06convention_span/06convention_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/06/us/06convention_span/06convention_span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/06/us/06convention_span/06convention_span-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Counts on Clinton to Help Sway Independents', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama Counting on Clinton to Help Sway Independent Voters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Democratic National Convention', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stadiums and Arenas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-05T16:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Hulse and Jeff Zeleny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hulse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zeleny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93fe3eb8-0f1d-517e-b724-f1c2940f41a9', 'word_count': 1377, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93fe3eb8-0f1d-517e-b724-f1c2940f41a9'}, {'abstract': 'The Securities and Exchange Commission has proposed rules to lift advertising restrictions for hedge funds, but the way this looks on paper and the way it will play out in the real world are a tad different.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/09/05/pruning-hedge-fund-regulation-without-cultivating-better-rules/', 'snippet': 'The Securities and Exchange Commission has proposed rules to lift advertising restrictions for hedge funds, but the way this looks on paper and the way it will play out in the real world are a tad different.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fresh from having declined to constrain money market funds, the Securities and Exchange Commission has moved to loosen marketing constraints on hedge funds.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pruning Hedge Fund Regulation Without Cultivating Better Rules', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pruning Regulation Without Cultivating Better Rules', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'},