ue': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marois, Pauline', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Parti Quebecois (Canada)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Montreal (Quebec)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Quebec Province (Canada)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-05T16:10:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e198225f-21a0-5b3d-8ba0-1ee8a2f546a1', 'word_count': 449, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e198225f-21a0-5b3d-8ba0-1ee8a2f546a1'}, {'abstract': 'Shares of Safeway climbed after the supermarket chain announced plans to sell a minority stake in its fast-growing Blackhawk Network gift card business.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/09/05/safeway-plans-i-p-o-of-gift-card-unit/', 'snippet': 'Shares of Safeway climbed after the supermarket chain announced plans to sell a minority stake in its fast-growing Blackhawk Network gift card business.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Safeway, the supermarket chain based in California, said on Wednesday that it planned to file for an initial public offering of a minority stake in its fast-growing gift card unit, Blackhawk Network Holdings. Shares of Safeway were up 5 percent by midday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Safeway Plans I.P.O. of Gift Card Unit', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gift Cards and Certificates', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Supermarkets and Grocery Stores', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Safeway Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-05T16:11:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd46dab0-8d8c-5520-95a4-6edded066fa2', 'word_count': 202, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd46dab0-8d8c-5520-95a4-6edded066fa2'}, {'abstract': 'The new collection was inspired by a discovery in the brand’s Place Vendôme maison.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/05/the-get-van-cleef-arpels-touch-wood-vintage-alhambra-pendant/', 'snippet': 'The new collection was inspired by a discovery in the brand’s Place Vendôme maison.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After discovering a trove of letter wood in the attic of the brand’s Place Vendôme maison, Van Cleef & Arpels’s North America president and CEO Nicolas Bos and team decided to honor the find and use it to create the touch wood Vintage Alhambra collection. Each necklace, bracelet and earring in the collection is limited and numbered and set in rose gold — a first for the brand’s signature, four-leaf clover-shaped Alhambras. “It’s a warm color and the modern alternative to yellow gold,” Bos says of the choice to use rose gold. “With the wood it was an interesting feeling — more of a vintage feeling that still felt like a very new combination.” Charmed, for sure!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Get | Van Cleef & Arpels Touch Wood Vintage Alhambra Pendant', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-05T16:16:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af667d83-488d-5266-a840-49fcf7072426', 'word_count': 131, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af667d83-488d-5266-a840-49fcf7072426'}, {'abstract': 'Several surveys conducted after the Republican National Convention show little lift for Mitt Romney.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/05/polls-little-to-no-bounce-for-romney/', 'snippet': 'Several surveys conducted after the Republican National Convention show little lift for Mitt Romney.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Several new polls show that in the immediate days after the Republican National Convention, Mitt Romney, the Republican presidential nominee, did not see much of a boost to his campaign, although slightly more Americans now see him as someone who can understand the needs of the middle class.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Polls: Little to No Bounce for Romney', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-05T16:17:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allison Kopicki', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allison', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kopicki', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5580d7be-c34e-58d2-8ddf-373af1ebe611', 'word_count': 580, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5580d7be-c34e-58d2-8ddf-373af1ebe611'}, {'abstract': 'The only surviving draft of the preliminary Emancipation Proclamation in Abraham Lincoln’s handwriting will be displayed in an exhibition that will travel to several New York state museums.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/05/lincolns-draft-of-emancipation-proclamation-coming-to-schomburg-center-in-harlem/', 'snippet': 'The only surviving draft of the preliminary Emancipation Proclamation in Abraham Lincoln’s handwriting will be displayed in an exhibition that will travel to several New York state museums.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Schomburg Center for Research in Black Culture in Harlem will be the first stop for the New York State Museum’s traveling exhibition of the only surviving draft of the preliminary Emancipation Proclamation in Abraham Lincoln’s handwriting.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lincoln’s Handwitten Draft of the Emancipation Proclamation Is Coming to Harlem', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emancipation Proclamation (1863)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Slavery', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lincoln, Abraham', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Schomburg Center for Research in Black Culture', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'HARLEM (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-05T16:21:16+0000',