nytimes.com/2012/09/05/michelle-obamas-children-come-first-should-they/', 'snippet': 'When Michelle Obama declares that her most important title is “mom in chief,” does she make things easier, or more difficult, for working mothers?', 'lead_paragraph': '“At the end of the day, my most important title is still ‘mom in chief.’ My daughters are still the heart of my heart and the center of my world.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Michelle Obama’s Children Come First. Should They?', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Democratic National Convention', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Michelle', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Slaughter, Anne-Marie', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Mary Elizabeth', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-05T17:55:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a778fb52-d7d5-5194-ad61-96d14810001b', 'word_count': 585, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a778fb52-d7d5-5194-ad61-96d14810001b'}, {'abstract': 'It can be difficult to get far-flung employees to work cohesively. The suggestions in this guide come from small-business owners who have tried.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/business/smallbusiness/running-a-business-with-employees-around-the-world.html', 'snippet': 'It can be difficult to get far-flung employees to work cohesively. The suggestions in this guide come from small-business owners who have tried.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Ralph Dandrea needed to hire a handful of employees for his rapidly growing Web design business, he figured he would have no trouble finding information technology professionals. It was 1998, and the technology boom was in full swing. But even though Mr. Dandrea, founder and chief executive of ITX Corporation, based in Pittsford, N.Y., looked all across the country, he struggled to find candidates. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/06/business/smallbusiness/06sbiz/06sbiz-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 729, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/06/business/smallbusiness/06sbiz/06sbiz-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1459, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/06/business/smallbusiness/06sbiz/06sbiz-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/06/business/smallbusiness/06sbiz/06sbiz-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/06/business/smallbusiness/06sbiz/06sbiz-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Running a Business With Staff Scattered Around the World', 'kicker': 'Small-Business Guide', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Running a Business With Staff Scattered Around the World', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-05T17:56:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bryan Borzykowski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bryan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borzykowski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/86136ad1-72d1-5235-9c31-f5e1819f9d3d', 'word_count': 1279, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86136ad1-72d1-5235-9c31-f5e1819f9d3d'}, {'abstract': 'The next installment in a series on house-hunting in Tuscany.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/05/viva-la-villa-palatial-near-pienza/', 'snippet': 'The next installment in a series on house-hunting in Tuscany.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Adventures in house-hunting: a writer chronicles her attempt to find the perfect home in Italy. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Viva la Villa | Palatial Near Pienza', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-05T18:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Danielle Pergament', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Danielle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pergament', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/492811b8-7b9e-5876-90dd-9bf328b4a979', 'word_count': 625, 'uri': 'nyt://article/492811b8-7b9e-5876-90dd-9bf328b4a979'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama is preparing to make an aggressive pitch at the Democratic convention, hoping to return to the fold voters who supported him in 2008 but now express disappointment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/us/politics/charting-voters-drift-away-from-obama.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama is preparing to make an aggressive pitch at the Democratic convention, hoping to return to the fold voters who supported him in 2008 but now express disappointment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dahlgren and Robert McElwain, retired business owners who live outside Kansas City, were in agreement in 2008. Despite their nearly lifelong support of Republican candidates, they made a bold move together and cast ballots for Barack Obama, enchanted by what they saw as his intelligence and charm.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Faces Test From Voters Who Drifted Away', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Seeing the President as Too Conciliatory, Some Have Drifted Away', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Democratic National Convention', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-05T18:02:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Saulny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saulny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/306dc1cf-2f53-5e36-b11e-81c206498f09', 'word_count': 926, 'uri': 'nyt://article/306dc1cf-2f53-5e36-b11e-81c206498f09'}, {'abstract': 'The Times’s political unit will be broadcasting live with the latest from the convention, beginning at 7 p.m. Here are a few of the highlights from the program.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/05/timescast-politics-and-democratic-convention-day-2-at-a-glance/', 'snippet': 'The Times’s political unit will be broadcasting live with the latest from the convention, beginning at 7 p.m. Here are a few of the highlights from the program.', 'lead_paragraph': '5:57 p.m. | Updated Democrats on Wednesday will try to continue to build on the energy from Tuesday night’s speeches, highlighted by an emotional address from the first lady, Michelle Obama. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'TimesCast Politics and Democratic Convention Day 2 at a Glance', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Democratic National Convention', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-05T18:02:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/92dc949f-f4dd-5f80-9a75-8ab8ae55ab97', 'word_count': 414, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92dc949f-f4dd-5f80-9a75-8ab8ae55ab97'}, {'abstract': 'What have you learned about managing remote employees?', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/05/are-your-employees-really-more-productive-working-at-home/', 'snippet': 'What have you learned about managing remote employees?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ralph Dandrea’s company, ITX Corporation, has 128 employees but only 46 of them report to the main office in Pittsford, N.Y. The rest are scattered internationally (72 in Argentina, p