Anton Goss takes cues from his clients’ home décor when designing their talk show sets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ricki Lake, who next week begins her second go-round as a daytime talk-show host with “The Ricki Lake Show,” lives in a house that’s beautiful but “not too precious,” likes the color purple and follows “a somewhat green lifestyle.” She also wanted her new set to feel less like a stage and more “like someone’s living room, where everyone’s opinion is heard.”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/06/garden/06QNA1_SPAN/06QNA1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/06/garden/06QNA1_SPAN/06QNA1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/06/garden/06QNA1_SPAN/06QNA1_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/06/garden/06QNA1_SPAN/06QNA1_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/06/garden/06QNA1_SPAN/06QNA1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/06/garden/06QNA1_SPAN/06QNA1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/06/garden/06QNA1_SPAN/06QNA1_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Designing Sets for Oprah, Ellen, Tyra and Now Ricki', 'kicker': 'Currents | Q&A', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After The Break: Designers Who Listen to Clients', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goss, Anton', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lake, Ricki', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-05T22:45:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Kurutz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kurutz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/66620380-0825-535c-89a4-d3f69df6d7a0', 'word_count': 613, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66620380-0825-535c-89a4-d3f69df6d7a0'}, {'abstract': 'Fifty plywood discs stacked together form an asymmetrical table that defies gravity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/garden/the-stack-50-table-from-restoration-hardware.html', 'snippet': 'Fifty plywood discs stacked together form an asymmetrical table that defies gravity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Marcello Pozzi, the Italian architect and designer now living in Los Angeles, has designed his first mass-produced piece for the home. Commissioned by Restoration Hardware for its fall line, the Stack 50 table consists of 50 discs of plywood. Forty-eight inches wide, it has a metal disc embedded in the tabletop that secures a metal rod to keep the discs in place, and an asymmetrical base that juts hither and yon in the spirit of a bonsai. The table costs $2,495, and much is made in the promotional materials of its design: “Stack 50 taunts gravity by shifting each disc away from the rod’s axis.”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/06/garden/06FURNITURE_SPAN/06FURNITURE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/06/garden/06FURNITURE_SPAN/06FURNITURE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/06/garden/06FURNITURE_SPAN/06CURR5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 615, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/06/garden/06FURNITURE_SPAN/06CURR5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1229, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/06/garden/06FURNITURE_SPAN/06FURNITURE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/06/garden/06FURNITURE_SPAN/06FURNITURE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/06/garden/06FURNITURE_SPAN/06FURNITURE_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Turning the Tables on Gravity', 'kicker': 'Currents | Furniture', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Turning the Tables on Gravity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tables', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Furniture', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pozzi, Marcello', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-05T22:46:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joyce Wadler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joyce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wadler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb9724f2-dbec-578a-9fb9-74a13baa400b', 'word_count': 202, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb9724f2-dbec-578a-9fb9-74a13baa400b'}, {'abstract': 'Available in October, this versatile light fixture demands to be touched.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/garden/the-kiss-lamp-from-artecnica.html', 'snippet': 'Available in October, this versatile light fixture demands to be touched.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stephen Johnson’s goal in designing Kiss for Artecnica was to create a lamp that demands to be touched. “It was important for me to give it a real physicality,” said Mr. Johnson, a London-based designer, adding that the versatile piece can be plunked on a desk as a task lamp or dangled over a table as a pendant. “It’s something you want to pick up and explore.”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/06/garden/06LIGHTING/06CURR3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 687, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/06/garden/06LIGHTING/06CURR3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1375, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail'