gher price in a proposed merger with Glencore International, which trades in raw materials.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A huge merger in the natural resources business is close to falling apart.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Qatar Imperils Big Merger of Commodity Companies', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Commodity Companies’ Big Merger Is Imperiled', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Commodities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mines and Mining', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Glencore International AG', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Xstrata', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Qatar', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T00:12:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William MacNamara', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacNamara', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/98172729-dfaa-5c93-addb-68537c95c242', 'word_count': 959, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98172729-dfaa-5c93-addb-68537c95c242'}, {'abstract': 'To create legal clarity since a court ruling in June equated circumcision with bodily injury, justice officials in Berlin laid out guidelines to allow the practice to continue in the city.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/world/europe/berlin-officials-clarify-circumcision-guidelines.html', 'snippet': 'To create legal clarity since a court ruling in June equated circumcision with bodily injury, justice officials in Berlin laid out guidelines to allow the practice to continue in the city.', 'lead_paragraph': ' In the first move to create legal clarity since a court ruling in June equated circumcision with bodily injury, justice officials in Berlin laid out guidelines on Wednesday to allow the practice to continue in the city pending nationwide legislation that is expected to back the procedure. The move comes after an outcry from doctors who feared they could be prosecuted for carrying out circumcisions after the June 26 ruling in a Cologne court. While it is not applicable in other jurisdictions, it created legal confusion across the country. The ruling also provoked strong protests from religious communities in Germany and abroad. The Berlin guidelines stipulate that both parents must confirm they wish to have their son circumcised because of religious beliefs and that the practice must be performed in a sterile environment. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Germany: Officials in Berlin Clarify Guidelines on Circumcision', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Germany: Officials in Berlin Clarify Guidelines On Circumcision to Ease Doctors’ Concerns on Ruling', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Circumcision', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Berlin (Germany)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T00:13:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Eddy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eddy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/3615bede-c931-5e5f-9d15-df30ec95c0cf', 'word_count': 133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3615bede-c931-5e5f-9d15-df30ec95c0cf'}, {'abstract': 'The pizzerias, a few feet apart on Avenue of the Americas, both raised their prices after cutting them to 75 cents a slice in March.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/nyregion/two-manhattan-pizza-parlors-end-price-war.html', 'snippet': 'The pizzerias, a few feet apart on Avenue of the Americas, both raised their prices after cutting them to 75 cents a slice in March.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The signs have been changed. The invectives have softened. The products remain, well, unlikely to win any culinary awards.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/06/nyregion/PIZZA/PIZZA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 673, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/06/nyregion/PIZZA/PIZZA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1345, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/06/nyregion/PIZZA/PIZZA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/06/nyregion/PIZZA/PIZZA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/06/nyregion/PIZZA/PIZZA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '$1 Pizza Slice Is Back After a Sidewalk Showdown Ends Two Parlors’ Price War', 'kicker': None, 'c