3+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adeshina Emmanuel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adeshina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Emmanuel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/401320d3-a6b2-52f6-9237-46ffecb8d485', 'word_count': 877, 'uri': 'nyt://article/401320d3-a6b2-52f6-9237-46ffecb8d485'}, {'abstract': 'Five people died and at least one was wounded when a police convoy came under attack on Wednesday in the volatile southern Russian republic of Ingushetia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/world/europe/police-convoy-is-attacked-in-a-russian-republic.html', 'snippet': 'Five people died and at least one was wounded when a police convoy came under attack on Wednesday in the volatile southern Russian republic of Ingushetia.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Five people died and at least one was wounded when a police convoy came under attack on Wednesday in the volatile southern Russian republic of Ingushetia. A hidden explosive device ripped through the first of the convoy’s two vehicles as it moved through the republic’s Sunzhen district, said a local official of the Investigative Committee. Unidentified fighters then opened fire from a nearby wooded area before fleeing, the Investigative Committee said. Officials have begun an investigation and are searching for the attackers. The bombing came after several weeks of increased violence in the North Caucasus region. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia: Police Convoy Is Attacked in Restive Ingushetia', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia: Police Convoy Is Attacked in Restive Ingushetia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ingushetia (Russian Republic)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Attacks on Police', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T00:21:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anna Kordunsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kordunsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/f2b964de-ebcc-54fb-ac5f-4330786045e0', 'word_count': 96, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f2b964de-ebcc-54fb-ac5f-4330786045e0'}, {'abstract': 'The G.O.P. is seeking to make Assemblyman Vito J. Lopez’s sexual harassment scandal a campaign issue against Democrats.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/nyregion/sexual-harassment-scandal-in-albany-becomes-political-fodder.html', 'snippet': 'The G.O.P. is seeking to make Assemblyman Vito J. Lopez’s sexual harassment scandal a campaign issue against Democrats.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALBANY — New York Republicans, sensing that the sexual harassment allegations against Assemblyman Vito J. Lopez could become a liability for Democrats, are moving to make the scandal a campaign issue.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/06/nyregion/Y-LOPEZ/Y-LOPEZ-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/06/nyregion/Y-LOPEZ/Y-LOPEZ-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1233, 'width': 1849, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'ran