e media.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/world/middleeast/netanyahu-cancels-security-meeting-after-leak.html', 'snippet': 'Israel’s prime minister, Benjamin Netanyahu, angrily cut short a key gathering of top security officials, accusing an unnamed participant of leaking details of the sensitive meeting to the media.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu abruptly canceled a meeting of his security cabinet on Wednesday, saying information was leaked from the highly confidential deliberations, a security failure that could undermine his efforts to project a unified front to the West about how to deal with Iran’s nuclear program.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Leak Prompts Netanyahu to Cancel Security Cabinet Meeting on Iran Issue', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Leak Prompts Netanyahu to Cancel Security Cabinet Meeting on Iran Issue', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netanyahu, Benjamin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T00:24:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Kershner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c14957ec-0155-5567-8328-efefb687be33', 'word_count': 833, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c14957ec-0155-5567-8328-efefb687be33'}, {'abstract': 'In the suit the man, Muhammad A. Salah, says, in essence, that it is impossible for him to lead a normal life without seeking approval from the government.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/us/illinois-man-sues-over-terrorist-status.html', 'snippet': 'In the suit the man, Muhammad A. Salah, says, in essence, that it is impossible for him to lead a normal life without seeking approval from the government.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A Bridgeview man has filed a lawsuit in federal court seeking to lift restrictions placed on him by the Department of Treasury when it deemed him a “specially designated terrorist” in 1995. In the suit the man, Muhammad A. Salah, says, in essence, that it is impossible for him to lead a normal life — to open a bank account, get a job or donate to his mosque — without seeking approval from the government. In 2007, Mr. Salah was convicted of lying in a civil lawsuit about ties to Hamas, the Palestinian organization, but he was acquitted of more serious charges of racketeering conspiracy after prosecutors accused him of helping to funnel aid to Hamas. A spokesman for the Treasury Department, named as a defendant in the suit, said he could not comment on pending litigation. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Illinois: Man Sues Over Terrorist Status ', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Midwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Illinois: Man Sues Over Terrorist Status', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T00:26:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Monica Davey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Monica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/a41219a1-92e6-5339-ab34-b3faf9b3baa1', 'word_count': 137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a41219a1-92e6-5339-ab34-b3faf9b3baa1'}, {'abstract': 'After earning his first PGA Tour victory in February, Kyle Stanley was surprised by how empty he felt. He has since taken on a more holistic approach.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/sports/golf/kyle-stanley-focusing-on-process-no-matter-how-hes-golfing.html', 'snippet': 'After earning his first PGA Tour victory in February, Kyle Stanley was surprised by how empty he felt. He has since taken on a more holistic approach.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CARMEL, Ind. — It started with a shy request, made last week on the eve of the Deutsche Bank Championship. Kyle Stanley found himself on the practice green alongside Steve Stricker, one of the best putters in the game, so he asked if he could look at his stroke. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/06/sports/Y-GOLF/Y-GOLF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 758, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/06/sports/Y-GOLF/Y-GOLF-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1515, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/06/sports/Y-GOLF/Y-GOLF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/06/sports/Y-GOLF/Y-GOLF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/06/sports/Y-GOLF/Y-GOLF-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Young Golfer Makes Progress in Focusing on Process', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Young Golfer Makes Progress in Focusing on Process', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stricker, Steve', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stanley, Kyle (1987- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T00:28:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a68764cb-6bc6-578d-b4b7-40a526644682', 'word_count': 979, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a68764cb-6bc6-578d-b4b7-40a526644682'}, {'abstract': 'Rahm Emanuel’s departure from the Obama campaign reflects Democrats’ worries about the fund-raising gap enjoyed by Republican-leaning outside groups.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/us/politics/emanuel-leaves-campaign-to-help-super-pacs.html', 'snippet': 'Rahm Emanuel’s departure from the Obama campaign reflects Democrats’ worries about the fund-raising gap enjoyed by Republican-leaning outside groups.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHARLOTTE, N.C. — Senior Democrats put aside any remaining qualms about jumping into the “super PAC” era, enlisting Mayor Rahm Emanuel of Chicago to focus on raising money for outside groups that are seeking to help the White House rather than keep a leadership role in President Obama’s re-election campaign.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/06/us/subDONATE/subDONATE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 648, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/06/us/subDONATE/subDONATE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1296, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Emanuel Takes On New Role as a ‘Super PAC’ Wrangler', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Emanuel Takes On New Role As a ‘Super PAC’ Wrangler', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Action Committees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Democratic National Convention', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Priorities USA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Emanuel, Rahm', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T00:30:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Confessore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Confessore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5cb5e1bc-8496-5c1e-aa81-6a0254117cb0', 'word_count': 1245, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5cb5e1bc-8496-5c1e-aa81-6a0254117cb0'}, {'abstract': 'An Israeli airstrike killed three Palestinian militants in the Gaza Strip late Wednesday and seriously wounded a fourth, according to Palestinian and Israeli officials.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/world/middleeast/israeli-airstrike-kills-three-militants-in-gaza-strip.html', 'snippet': 'An Israeli airstrike killed three Palestinian militants in the Gaza Strip late Wednesday and seriously wounded a fourth, according to Palestinian and Israeli officials.', 'lead_paragraph': ' An Israeli airstrike killed three Palestinian militants in the Gaza Strip late Wednesday and seriously wounded a fourth, according to Palestinian and Israeli officials. Israel said the militants had been preparing to launch a rocket to attack Israel. The raid came days after Palestinian militants fired about a dozen rockets into southern Israel from Gaza, the coastal enclave controlled by Hamas. Groups affiliated with Al Qaeda claimed responsibility for those attacks and criticized Hamas this week for cracking down on them. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gaza: Israeli Airstrike Kills Three Militants', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gaza: Israeli Airstrike Kills Three Militants', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gaza Strip', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T00:31:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fares Akram', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fares', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Akram', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc372407-4ca0-5954-8852-394698b820ad', 'word_count': 152, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc372407-4ca0-5954-8852-394698b820ad'}, {'abstract': 'Eli Manning, the two-time Super Bowl most valuable player, found limited opportunities against the Cowboys. He completed 21 of 32 passes for 213 yards and a touchdown.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/sports/football/for-giants-winning-the-super-bowl-may-have-been-the-easy-part.html', 'snippet': 'Eli Manning, the two-time Super Bowl most valuable player, found limited opportunities against the Cowboys. He completed 21 of 32 passes for 213 yards and a touchdown.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST RUTHERFORD, N.J. — Eli Manning got a different look when he surveyed the Dallas defense in the season opener. For the most part, he did not like what he saw in a 24-17 loss to the Cowboys on Wednesday night.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Manning Fails to Solve Cowboys’ New Look on Defense', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Manning Fails to Solve Cowboys’ New Look on Defense', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manning, Eli', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dallas Cowboys', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T00:33:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Pedulla', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pedulla', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1aba6c8a-c1eb-531e-a2aa-7f553784807e', 'word_count': 384, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1aba6c8a-c1eb-531e-a2aa-7f553784807e'}, {'abstract': 'The trial of Bishop Robert W. Finn and the Diocese of Kansas City-St. Joseph on charges of failure to report suspected child abuse avoids a lengthy public trial that was set to start Sept. 24.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/us/missouri-bishop-will-face-judge-not-jury.html', 'snippet': 'The trial of Bishop Robert W. Finn and the Diocese of Kansas City-St. Joseph on charges of failure to report suspected child abuse avoids a lengthy public trial that was set to start Sept. 24.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The trial of Bishop Robert W. Finn and the Diocese of Kansas City-St. Joseph on charges of failure to report suspected child abuse has been moved up to Thursday and will be decided by a judge, not a jury. The change was made public in a court filing on Wednesday, and avoids a lengthy public trial that was set to start Sept. 24. Bishop Finn is the first Roman Catholic prelate in the country to be indicted in the sexual abuse scandals. He and the diocese each face two misdemeanor counts of failing to report hundreds of lewd photographs of young girls on a laptop computer belonging to the Rev. Shawn Ratigan. Father Ratigan pleaded guilty to pornography charges in August. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Missouri: Bishop Will Face Judge, Not Jury ', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Midwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Missouri: Bishop Will Face Judge, Not Jury', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Priests', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Finn, Robert William', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kansas City (Mo)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T00:34:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laurie Goodstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laurie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goodstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a338dd0-6be4-5c42-b21e-0aeece966bab', 'word_count': 122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a338dd0-6be4-5c42-b21e-0aeece966bab'}, {'abstract': 'Officials said the insects had declined by 93 percent in places that received two consecutive nights of spraying.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/us/texas-mosquito-spraying-shows-results.html', 'snippet': 'Officials said the insects had declined by 93 percent in places that received two consecutive nights of spraying.', 'lead_paragraph': ' State health officials said Wednesday that the death toll from West Nile virus continues to rise, but they were encouraged by data that suggested the virus had peaked in the Dallas area. The mosquito-borne disease has sickened hundreds of people there and killed 13. A recent spraying operation in the area appeared to reduce the population of mosquitoes. Officials said the insects had declined by 93 percent in places that received two consecutive nights of spraying. Nationwide, 1,993 cases have been reported, including 87 deaths, a 25 percent increase over last week’s numbers. In Texas, there have been 1,113 cases, including 40 deaths, the most fatalities of any state. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Texas: Mosquito Spraying Shows Results ', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Southwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Texas: Mosquito Spraying Shows Results ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'West Nile Virus', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mosquitoes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T00:36:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manny Fernandez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fernandez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/326205f5-3f15-5dfd-bb1b-3c0f03d3e598', 'word_count': 111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/326205f5-3f15-5dfd-bb1b-3c0f03d3e598'}, {'abstract': 'The United States said Wednesday that Iraq had an obligation to stop and inspect Iranian planes flying through its airspace that are suspected of carrying arms to Syria.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/world/middleeast/us-presses-iraq-on-iranian-planes-thought-to-carry-arms-to-syria.html', 'snippet': 'The United States said Wednesday that Iraq had an obligation to stop and inspect Iranian planes flying through its airspace that are suspected of carrying arms to Syria.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The State Department said Wednesday that Iraq has an obligation under United Nations Security Council resolutions to insist that Iranian planes that are suspected of flying arms to Syria over Iraqi airspace land so the cargo can be inspected. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Presses Iraq on Iranian Planes Thought to Carry Arms to Syria', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Presses Iraq on Iran Flights Thought to Carry Arms to Syria', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'valu