between the United States and China on a daunting range of issues. “Our two nations,” she said, “are trying to do something that has never been done in history, which is to write a new answer to the question of what happens when an established power and a rising power meet.” As the secretary’s fifth trip to China demonstrated, that is proving to be a complicated process.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Touchy Relationship', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Touchy Relationship', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Far East, South and Southeast Asia and Pacific Areas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South China Sea', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T01:32:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf08f4dc-0dcc-57b5-a8c5-00a913fb0074', 'word_count': 378, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf08f4dc-0dcc-57b5-a8c5-00a913fb0074'}, {'abstract': 'The Constitution does not let someone go into a public place with a legal handgun and terrify the public.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/opinion/an-ak-47-in-a-tennessee-park.html', 'snippet': 'The Constitution does not let someone go into a public place with a legal handgun and terrify the public.', 