e, 'lastname': 'Sussman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/8d451d3d-c788-5343-ba2b-b83ca404d62f', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/8d451d3d-c788-5343-ba2b-b83ca404d62f'}, {'abstract': 'The area that was among the hardest hit by the BP spill that state wildlife officials announced the emergency closing of some coastal waters to commercial fishing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/us/louisiana-hurricane-isaac-churns-up-oil-off-coast.html', 'snippet': 'The area that was among the hardest hit by the BP spill that state wildlife officials announced the emergency closing of some coastal waters to commercial fishing.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Hurricane Isaac churned up enough oil in a part of south Louisiana that was among the hardest hit by the BP spill that state wildlife officials announced the emergency closing of some coastal waters to commercial fishing. Six heavy tar mats were found just offshore of a 13-mile stretch of sandy and marshy coastline, and tar balls were found on the beach as well. Tests are being performed to determine whether the oil belongs to the well drilled by the Deepwater Horizon, and results are expected within days. “It possibly could be our oil, but we don’t know,” said Ray Melick, a spokesman for BP, adding that crews were engaged in cleanup activities in the area only days before the storm. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Louisiana: Storm Churns Up Oil Off Coast ', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Louisiana: Storm Churns Up Oil Off Coast', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fishing, Commercial', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Louisiana', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wa