y entrepreneurs Mayor Michael Bloomberg announced the winners of Project Pop-UP N.Y.C., a competition that the mayor’s office and the Economic Development Corporation. Would-be winners had four weeks to get their applications in starting from the end of June. The nine application questions solicited thetype of information that one would put on a business plan: Who is your competition, and how are you different or better? Who is on your management team? What market does it address, and how big is thismarket?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mayor Bloomberg Announces Winners of Project Pop-Up N.Y.C.', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T03:09:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Caroline Waxler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Caroline', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waxler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6fc6852-337b-5bdc-a42d-f13afb9e2bb7', 'word_count': 243, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6fc6852-337b-5bdc-a42d-f13afb9e2bb7'}, {'abstract': 'At the time of his retirement, Andy Roddick was the most decorated active American male tennis player. He remains the last American to win a Grand Slam final.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/09/04/sports/tennis/SPTSRODDICK0904.html', 'snippet': 'At the time of his retirement, Andy Roddick was the most decorated active American male tennis player. He remains the last American to win a Grand Slam final.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the time of his retirement, Andy Roddick was the most decorated active American male tennis player. He remains the last American to win a Grand Slam final.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'captio