s', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T10:00:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Benoit', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Benoit', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ea75199-cb3f-52b6-9fc9-8711bee7beca', 'word_count': 2678, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ea75199-cb3f-52b6-9fc9-8711bee7beca'}, {'abstract': 'A new interactive tool from ProPublica allows you to search and compare nursing home inspection reports.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/shopping-for-a-nursing-home-theres-a-tool-for-that/', 'snippet': 'A new interactive tool from ProPublica allows you to search and compare nursing home inspection reports.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shopping for a Nursing Home? There’s a Tool for That', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nursing Homes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T10:33:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paula Span', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paula', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Span', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f703bfe-8db3-5e86-b059-f1418adb1464', 'word_count': 720, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f703bfe-8db3-5e86-b059-f1418adb1464'}, {'abstract': 'Too eager to evacuate Migron without a clash, Israel’s leaders have failed to question the wisdom of moving the settlers just a couple of miles away.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/n-evacuating-migron-israels-leaders-were-motivated-by-politics/', 'snippet': 'Too eager to evacuate Migron without a clash, Israel’s leaders have failed to question the wisdom of moving the settlers just a couple of miles away.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — Sunday was an eventless day. Yes, Migron, the most famous of illegal Jewish outposts in the West Bank, was evacuated. But nothing happened, really. The move was peaceful, with only minor protests. The settlers’ warnings that they’d resist proved hollow, and the government’s fear that they might, baseless.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Migron Settlement Myth', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Israeli Settlements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T10:36:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shmuel Rosner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shmuel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/148c7106-c6ce-5919-b153-0a028af7b983', 'word_count': 599, 'uri': 'nyt://article/148c7106-c6ce-5919-b153-0a028af7b983'}, {'abstract': 'Measuring the bounce the incumbent party gets out of its convention is trickier than doing so for the challenger, but a golf analogy can help us to understand the possibilities.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/sept-5-looking-ahead-after-charlotte/', 'snippet': 'Measuring the bounce the incumbent party gets out of its convention is trickier than doing so for the challenger, but a golf analogy can help us to understand the possibilities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was almost nothing worth talking about in the polls that were out on Wednesday. So let’s take a quick look forward instead — to about a week from now, by which point we will have plenty of data on what effect the Democratic National Convention had on the polls.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sept. 5: Looking Ahead After Charlotte', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Democratic National Convention', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T10:38:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c57aadab-ab05-5232-9851-462bb984d6b4', 'word_count': 697, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c57aadab-ab05-5232-9851-462bb984d6b4'}, {'abstract': 'The former N.F.L. director of officials gave the officials a passing grade in the Dallas-Giants game on Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/pereira-compliments-replacement-officials/', 'snippet': 'The former N.F.L. director of officials gave the officials a passing grade in the Dallas-Giants game on Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The former N.F.L. director of officials Mike Pereira, who has supported his former colleagues in their labor dispute with the N.F.L., gave the replacement officials a passing grade in the Dallas-Giants game on Wednesday. Pereira, now a Fox analyst, wrote on FoxSports.com:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pereira Compliments Replacement Officials', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pereira, Mike', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T10:55:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de2d7cf0-ad45-56c3-aaa1-d23c54a2343a', 'word_count': 211, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de2d7cf0-ad45-56c3-aaa1-d23c54a2343a'}, {'abstract': 'Chocolaty, citrusy, sugary or savory.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2012/09/09/magazine/shortbread-cookie-recipes.html', 'snippet': 'Chocolaty, citrusy, sugary or savory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chocolaty, citrusy, sugary or savory.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Shortbread Variations', 'kicker': 'Eat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cookies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T10:58:00+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_n