'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment Insurance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Central Bank', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T15:01:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nathaniel Popper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nathaniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Popper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/12739b97-30c5-537b-bbe6-1ddf91f93901', 'word_count': 963, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12739b97-30c5-537b-bbe6-1ddf91f93901'}, {'abstract': 'Forthcoming musical performances at the Metropolitan Museum include compositions by Tan Dun and David Lang as well as 16 Beethoven string quartets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/09/arts/music/efterklang-and-tan-dun-at-the-metropolitan-museum.html', 'snippet': 'Forthcoming musical performances at the Metropolitan Museum include compositions by Tan Dun and David Lang as well as 16 Beethoven string quartets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THINK of the new concert season at the Metropolitan Museum of Art as the Met Remixed. Limor Tomer, who was appointed in 2011 to run the museum’s concerts and lectures department, has already staged several concerts at the museum, most notably a 10th-anniversary commemoration of the Sept. 11 terrorist attacks and a celebration in April of the composer Philip Glass and the violinist Timothy Fain in the Temple of Dendur. But the season about to open is the first she planned fully. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '33', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/arts/09TOMER1_SPAN/09TOMER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/09/arts/09TOMER1_SPAN/09TOMER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/arts/09TOMER1_SPAN/09TOMER1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/arts/09TOMER1_SPAN/09TOMER1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/arts/09TOMER1_SPAN/09TOMER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/09/arts/09TOMER1_SPAN/09TOMER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Danish Art-Rock, and Beethoven, Too', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Danish Art-Rock, and Beethoven, Too', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Museum of Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tomer, Limor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T15:10:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e0914af-0e59-5433-88c0-3669ff80ddee', 'word_count': 838, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e0914af-0e59-5433-88c0-3669ff80ddee'}, {'abstract': 'Nestled along the country’s western coast, Galway is often called Ireland’s most Irish city. And while you can still get a Guinness served with Gaelic, a global flavor is emerging.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/09/travel/36-hours-in-galway-ireland.html', 'snippet': 'Nestled along the country’s western coast, Galway is often called Ireland’s most Irish city. And while you can still get a Guinness served with Gaelic, a global flavor is emerging.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FREQUENTLY called Ireland’s most Irish city, this coastal metropolis is a place where Celtic culture and literature have long thrived, often in the traditional Gaelic language. But these days you’re just as likely to hear Spanish, Polish or Japanese along Galway’s crowded streets in this increasingly international college town (the National University of Ireland, Galway, is here). While the fall is less crowded than the tourist-clogged summer, Galway’s festival culture keeps going strong, with the 10,000-person Galway International Oyster and Seafood Festival in late September and the Galway Theater Festival in early October, to name just two events. Of course, the city’s notoriously lively pubs can provide a few pints and plenty of craic (Irish slang for “a good time”) any night of the year.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/travel/09HOURS1_SPAN/09HOURS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 492, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xl