e.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Obama Should Say', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T15:45:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6211a17c-b4d0-57bc-a390-80ef414efb8e', 'word_count': 1506, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6211a17c-b4d0-57bc-a390-80ef414efb8e'}, {'abstract': 'Many people with cancer define themselves as cancer survivors. But some of us cringe at adopting such an identity.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/not-a-cancer-survivor/', 'snippet': 'Many people with cancer define themselves as cancer survivors. But some of us cringe at adopting such an identity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I am not a cancer survivor, and neither are the women in my cancer support group. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/06/health/06well_cancer/06well_cancer-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 681, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/06/health/06well_cancer/06well_cancer-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1362, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/06/health/06well_cancer/06well_cancer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/06/health/06well_cancer/06well_cancer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/06/health/06well_cancer/06well_cancer-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Not a Cancer Survivor', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T15:45:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Gubar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gubar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c82cb96-228d-5d68-820b-ecd4b4b3112a', 'word_count': 867, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c82cb96-228d-5d68-820b-ecd4b4b3112a'}, {'abstract': 'Jay-Z has a piece of the Nets, a glamorous wife and a baby girl who melts his heart. Brooklyn, meet your once and future king.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/09/t-magazine/the-house-that-hova-built.html', 'snippet': 'Jay-Z has a piece of the Nets, a glamorous wife and a baby girl who melts his heart. Brooklyn, meet your once and future king.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s difficult to know what to ask a rapper. It’s not unlike the difficulty (I imagine) of being a rapper. Whatever you say must be considered from at least three angles, and it’s an awkward triangulation. In one corner you have your hard-core hip-hop heads; the type for whom the true Jay-Z will forever be that gifted 25-year-old with rapid-fire flow, trading verses with the visionary teenager Big L — “I’m so ahead of my time, my parents haven’t met yet!” — on a “rare” (easily dug up on YouTube) seven-minute freestyle from 1995. Meanwhile, over here stands the pop-rap fan. She loves the Jiggaman with his passion for the Empire State Building and bold claims to “Run This Town.” Finally, in the crowded third corner, stand the many people who feel rap is not music at all but rather a form of social problem. They have only one question to ask a rapper, and it concerns his choice of vocabulary. (Years pass. The question never changes.) How to speak to these audiences simultaneously? Anyway: I’m at a little table in a homey Italian restaurant on Mulberry Street waiting for Mr. Shawn Carter, who has perfected the art of triangulation. It’s where he likes to eat his chicken parms.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '109', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/t-magazine/09well-jayz/09well-jayz-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 819, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/t-magazine/09well-jayz/09well-jayz-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1638, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/t-magazine/09well-jayz/09well-jayz-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/09/t-magazine/09well-jayz/09well-jayz-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/t-magazine/09well-jayz/09well-jayz-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The House That Hova Built', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jay Z', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rap and Hip-Hop', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jay-Z', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'West, Kanye', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T15:48:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zadie Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zadie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d31a98a1-16b5-5a55-96fb-850e9cca59d0', 'word_count': 3146, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d31a98a1-16b5-5a55-96fb-850e9cca59d0'}, {'abstract': 'Five months after the deal was first announced, the Federal Trade Commission cleared Facebook to complete its acquisition of Instagram, the popular mobile photo-sharing application.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/its-official-facebook-closes-its-acquisition-of-instagram/', 'snippet': 'Five months after the deal was first announced, the Federal Trade Commission cleared Facebook to complete its acquisition of Instagram, the popular mobile photo-sharing application.', 'lead_paragraph': ' 11:50 a.m. | Updated  Adding details.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'It’s Official: Facebook Closes Its Acquisition of Instagram', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Instagram Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T15:50:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenna Wortham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wortham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9681dd8-617d-5f6a-a585-92a523df8cba', 'word_count': 284, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9681dd8-617d-5f6a-a585-92a523df8cba'}, {'abstract': 'Even with two young daughters, the Beutlers of Traverse City, Mich., eschewed iPads, laptops and portable DVD players on a road trip in a 1971 Oldsmobile Vista Cruiser.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/the-family-barge-minus-a-flotilla-of-personal-technology/', 'snippet': 'Even with two young daughters, the Beutlers of Traverse City, Mich., eschewed iPads, laptops and portable DVD players on a road trip in a 1971 Oldsmobile Vista Cruiser.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DEARBORN, Mich. — It’s one thing to take a 41-year-old station wagon for a Sunday drive, quite another to put it on the road for a six-day, 1,400-mile family vacation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Family Barge, Minus a Flotilla of Personal Technology', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Road Trips', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ford, Henry, Museum', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Traverse City (Mich)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T15:55:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mary M. Chapman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'quali