.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/doctor-is-charged-in-death-of-slipknot-bassist/', 'snippet': 'The doctor also reportedly faces manslaughter charges in the deaths of seven other patients.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An Iowa doctor who helped run a pain clinic has been charged with involuntary manslaughter in connection with the death of Paul Gray, the Slipknot bassist and co-founder who died of an overdose of narcotics in May 2010, The Des Moines Register reported.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Doctor Is Charged in Death of Slipknot Bassist', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Doctor Is Charged In Death of Bassist', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Malpractice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gray, Paul', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Slipknot', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T16:58:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3a4a44a-a9d8-571f-a3fd-7b36c6da8c60', 'word_count': 243, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3a4a44a-a9d8-571f-a3fd-7b36c6da8c60'}, {'abstract': 'The idea of the “submerged state” — largely unrecognized government benefits — is treated with greater suspicion in the United States than in Canada or Europe. The original architects of the submerged state were Republicans and conservative Democrats, although Bill Clinton and Barack Obama have energetically built on that legacy.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/why-such-suspicion-of-the-submerged-state/', 'snippet': 'The idea of the “submerged state” — largely unrecognized government benefits — is treated with greater suspicion in the United States than in Canada or Europe. The original architects of the submerged state were Republicans and conservative Democr...', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW YORK — In my column this week I write about Suzanne Mettler’s idea of the “submerged state” — the government benefits that Americans receive, like tax credits, or support channeled through nonprofits, which is paid for by the state but which are either invisible or feel as if they’ve come from some other source.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Such Suspicion of the ‘Submerged State’?', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T16:59:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chrystia Freeland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chrystia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Freeland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e176c4e1-7d76-5e3d-a413-01ac77a92583', 'word_count': 193, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e176c4e1-7d76-5e3d-a413-01ac77a92583'}, {'abstract': 'A pair of mesmerizing, monochromatic earrings that put old world glamour back in the moment.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/the-get-stephen-russell-earrings/', 'snippet': 'A pair of mesmerizing, monochromatic earrings that put old world glamour back in the moment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Known for exceptional estate gems, the fine jeweler Stephen Russell has created a pair of mesmerizing monochromatic earrings that put Old World glamour back in the moment. Modeled after an 18th-century pendeloque shape, they’re made of almost 200 sapphires, their setting upstaged by all that brilliant blue. And about that setting: Russell chose 18-karat blackened gold to augment the vintagelike quality.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Get | Stephen Russell Earrings', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Metals and Minerals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T16:59:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d4b2e46-1078-5936-9b46-2aabcb458e3c', 'word_count': 72, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d4b2e46-1078-5936-9b46-2aabcb458e3c'}, {'abstract': 'Several long-planned architectural projects, including Barclays Center in Brooklyn and 4 World Trade Center, are making their ways, at varied speeds, to completion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/09/arts/design/barclays-center-and-other-projects-in-process.html', 'snippet': 'Several long-planned architectural projects, including Barclays Center in Brooklyn and 4 World Trade Center, are making their ways, at varied speeds, to completion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ARCHITECTURE is slow. So slow it sometimes appears not to be moving forward at all. Projects get bogged down — more now than ever, it seems — by financial shortfalls, public opposition, disputes over labor or design. All on top of the mundane difficulties of putting together, piece by piece, the stuff that makes a building.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '70', 