words': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Democratic National Convention', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Axelrod, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Bill', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T17:09:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Damon Winter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Damon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Winter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ae841d2-b73a-5986-90e4-f78e90c2dae1', 'word_count': 1, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ae841d2-b73a-5986-90e4-f78e90c2dae1'}, {'abstract': 'Sampling comics’ tweets in response to Bill Clinton’s speech at the Democratic National Convention.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/the-peanut-gallery-takes-on-the-democrats/', 'snippet': 'Sampling comics’ tweets in response to Bill Clinton’s speech at the Democratic National Convention.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Let the historians decide who was the greatest president in American history; I would argue that the best modern commander in chief for comedians is pretty clear. Sure, Nixon is a solid contender, but Bill Clinton, a man with big appetites and a distinctive accent, has given joke tellers a wealth of material. So it’s no surprise that his return to the spotlight at the Democratic National Convention on Wednesday night in Charlotte, N.C., inspired an avalanche of jokes on Twitter. (Just as the Republicans’ gathering did last week). Here are a few highlights:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Peanut Gallery Takes On the Democrats', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Democratic National Convention', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Republican National Convention', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Bill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nixon, Richard Milhous', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Charlotte (NC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T17:15:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Zinoman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinoman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cef2c7d2-c26b-5255-9a47-40d6cd1c6f64', 'word_count': 184, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cef2c7d2-c26b-5255-9a47-40d6cd1c6f64'}, {'abstract': 'A senior French diplomat said the government was providing funds to five revolutionary councils in rebel-held parts of Syria to help them restore water supplies, sanitation, health services and bakeries.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/world/europe/france-sends-funds-to-5-syrian-civic-groups.html', 'snippet': 'A senior French diplomat said the government was providing funds to five revolutionary councils in rebel-held parts of Syria to help them restore water supplies, sanitation, health services and bakeries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — The French government is providing funds to five revolutionary councils in rebel-held parts of Syria to help them restore water supplies, sanitation, health services and bakeries, a senior French diplomat, Éric Chevallier, said Thursday.', 'print_sec