': '2012-09-06T17:23:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jessica Silver-Greenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jessica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver-Greenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd392a1e-6de0-5dab-a5b4-0fc23a168c03', 'word_count': 560, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd392a1e-6de0-5dab-a5b4-0fc23a168c03'}, {'abstract': 'At the Young Scholars’ Academy for Discovery and Exploration in Brooklyn, the pencils and Popsicle sticks came out.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/in-one-class-time-to-draw-and-in-another-a-return-to-the-olympics/', 'snippet': 'At the Young Scholars’ Academy for Discovery and Exploration in Brooklyn, the pencils and Popsicle sticks came out.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first graders at Young Scholars’ Academy for Discovery and Exploration in Bedford-Stuyvesant, Brooklyn, know how to write their first names, though not necessarily their last names, as they demonstrated for reporters on their first day back to school. A group of them sat around a tiny table Thursday morning, frowning with concentration as they tried to decide how to draw themselves.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/06/nyregion/06school5-cityroom/06school5-cityroom-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 702, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/06/nyregion/06school5-cityroom/06school5-cityroom-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1151, 'width': 1680, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': '