et, a $45 Vince V-Neck Tee and a $15,675 BMW R1200R Classic.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'BMW Motorrad and Bloomingdale’s, Riding Tandem', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Motorcycles, Motor Bikes and Motorscooters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bayerische Motorenwerke AG', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Bloomingdale's", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Midtown Area (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T17:27:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roy Furchgott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Furchgott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/501e8adc-3d19-51bd-b334-7ee80f016a91', 'word_count': 437, 'uri': 'nyt://article/501e8adc-3d19-51bd-b334-7ee80f016a91'}, {'abstract': 'At the Department of Health and Human Services, new efforts are under way to understand what effects a changing climate could have on infectious diseases, allergies, air pollution and so on.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/the-baffling-nexus-of-climate-change-and-health/', 'snippet': 'At the Department of Health and Human Services, new efforts are under way to understand what effects a changing climate could have on infectious diseases, allergies, air pollution and so on.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2004, a rare tropical fungus caused a string of respiratory failures and neural disorders along the Pacific Northwest coast, baffling the health community. That same year, Alaskan cruise ship passengers dining on local oysters fell sick with a gastric virus typically found in warm water estuaries. Now Texas, after an unusually wet spring and dry summer, is battling what may become the country’s worst recorded outbreak of West Nile virus.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Baffling Nexus of Climate Change and Health', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mosquitoes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'West Nile Virus', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Public Health Assn', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Centers for Disease Control and Prevention', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Institute of Environmental Health Sciences', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Institutes of Health', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T17:28:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dylan Walsh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dylan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Walsh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d15ee0f6-705f-5479-bf4b-5e906ec87e79', 'word_count': 778, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d15ee0f6-705f-5479-bf4b-5e906ec87e79'}, {'abstract': 'In a loss to Tomas Berdych at the United States Open, Roger Federer’s forehand disintegrated.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/breaking-it-down-berdych-vs-federer/', 'snippet': 'In a loss to Tomas Berdych at the United States Open, Roger Federer’s forehand disintegrated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Roger Federer more than doubled his forehand errors from any of his previous three United States Open matches to lose in four sets to sixth-seeded Tomas Berdych, 7-6 (1), 6-4, 3-6, 6-3, Wednesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Breaking It Down: Berdych vs. Federer', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berdych, Tomas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Federer, Roger', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T17:30:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': "By Craig O'Shannessy", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Craig', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Shannessy", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c019a9f-7459-51bb-b705-036cc61bd313', 'word_count': 835, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c019a9f-7459-51bb-b705-036cc61bd313'}, {'abstract': 'By turns stirring and scathing, Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo sounded unmistakably like a man with ambitions well beyond Albany even as he tried to stay out of the spotlight.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/in-charlotte-cuomo-denounces-gop-policy-praises-new-yorks-accomplishments/', 'snippet': 'By turns stirring and scathing, Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo sounded unmistakably like a man with ambitions well beyond Albany even as he tried to stay out of the spotlight.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHARLOTTE, N.C. — Giant clusters of red, white and blue balloons hung overhead and an imposing black rope line stretched across the room. Campaign-style bunting festooned the podium and Bon Jovi’s “Working for the Working Man” blared through loudspeakers. A seasoned political spouse leapt to her feet at applause lines, and the candidate shouted to be heard over an adoring crowd.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cuomo, in Convention City, Gives Spirited Speech From Small Stage', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cuomo, in Brief Visit to Convention City, Gives a Spirited Speech From a Small Stage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Democratic National Convention', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Sandra', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T17:30:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Barbaro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barbaro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4805b59e-8322-5d6a-a61c-e913d7713eae', 'word_count': 789, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4805b59e-8322-5d6a-a61c-e913d7713eae'}, {'abstract': 'Perhaps only Bill Clinton could deliver one of the most brutal partisan poundings of the other party in recent memory and come out of it with people talking about how bipartisan he is.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/clinton-was-a-bipartisan-president-except-when-he-wasnt/', 'snippet': 'Perhaps only Bill Clinton could deliver one of the most brutal partisan poundings of the other party in recent memory and come out of it with people talking about how bipartisan he is.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHARLOTTE, N.C. – Perhaps only Bill Clinton could deliver one of the most brutal partisan poundings of the other party in recent memory and come out of it with people talking about how bipartisan he is.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Clinton Was a Bipartisan President, Except When He Wasn’t', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Bill', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Charlotte (NC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T17:31:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/96c41a09-1546-58ce-8563-fb7399338695', 'word_count': 1087, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96c41a09-1546-58ce-8563-fb7399338695'}, {'abstract': 'Prime Minister Lee Hsien Loong pointedly addressed the question of America’s world standing, a subject that Chinese academics and writers in the state-run media have written caustically about in recent months.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/world/asia/singapores-prime-minister-warns-china-on-view-of-us.html', 'snippet': 'Prime Minister Lee Hsien Loong pointedly addressed the question of America’s world standing, a subject that Chinese academics and writers in the state-run media have written caustically about in recent months.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — In an unusual public airing of strategic problems surrounding China’s rise, the prime minister of Singapore, Lee Hsien Loong, warned China on Thursday that it should view the United States not as a declining power, but as a nation with the ability to innovate and bounce back. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Singaporean Tells China U.S. Is Not in Decline', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Singaporean Tells China U.S. Is Not in Decline', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee Hsien Loong', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Singapore', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T17:37:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane Perlez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perlez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}