85, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1603a931-5bac-522d-b994-00e008a0f3f4'}, {'abstract': 'So-called safety-net hospitals have long been considered the ugly stepchild of the American health care system, but as a new study reports, you can’t judge the quality of a hospital’s care by its decor.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/the-fraying-hospital-safety-net/', 'snippet': 'So-called safety-net hospitals have long been considered the ugly stepchild of the American health care system, but as a new study reports, you can’t judge the quality of a hospital’s care by its decor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Slender and in his 60s, the patient had been short of breath for several days, a result of untreated heart failure causing fluid to build up in his lungs. Despite his wife’s entreaties, he had refused to go to the hospital, one of the biggest in the city, and waited at home, gasping, until his appointment at our clinic. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/06/health/06Chen/06Chen-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/06/health/06Chen/06Chen-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/06/health/06Chen/06Chen-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/06/health/06Chen/06Chen-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/06/health/06Chen/06Chen-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Fraying Hospital Safety Net', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T19:32:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pauline W. Chen, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pauline', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8524e5fa-a7fa-5eac-aa83-ac036756d746', 'word_count': 769, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8524e5fa-a7fa-5eac-aa83-ac036756d746'}, {'abstract': 'The president makes a strong case for a vision of government that serves the middle class.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/opinion/mr-obamas-second-chance.html', 'snippet': 'The president makes a strong case for a vision of government that serves the middle class.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama’s dilemma has always been that he has been far more successful a president than his opponents claim, but far less successful than he needs to be at making voters see that. Powerful speeches by former President Bill Clinton, Vice President Joe Biden and others did a lot to fix that impression during the convention. But it was up to Mr. Obama to make the case for another term, with a speech that was every bit as fraught with uncertainty and risk as his 2008 convention address.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'President Obama’s Second Chance', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'President Obama&#8217;s Second Chance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Democratic National Convention', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T19:35:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a222c9b3-451e-5104-824d-a7b26e4c5257', 'word_count': 809, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a222c9b3-451e-5104-824d-a7b26e4c5257'}, {'abstract': 'Dennis M. Walcott may be the leader of the city’s school system, but he was no match for a basketball-shooting robot built by students at one Staten Island school.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/before-school-lets-out-a-basketball-playing-robot-takes-the-court/', 'snippet': 'Dennis M. Walcott may be the leader of the city’s school system, but he was no match for a basketball-shooting robot built by students at one Staten Island school.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first day of school was coming to an end at Staten Island Technical High School, but the members of the school’s robotics team, Team 375: The Robotic Plague, still had one hurdle to clear. They couldn’t wait to demonstrate their champion basketball-launching robot to Schools Chancellor Dennis M. Walcott and other dignitaries who had dropped by.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/nyregion/06cityroom-school9/06cityroom-school9-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 762, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/nyregion/06cityroom-school9/06cityroom-school9-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1524, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/nyregion/06cityroom-school9/06cityroom-school9-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/07/nyregion/06cityroom-school9/06cityroom-school9-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/nyregion/06cityroom-school9/06cityroom-school9-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Before School Lets Out, a Basketball-Playing Robot Takes the Court', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robots and Robotics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walcott, Dennis M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Staten Island (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T19:44:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivian Yee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/01b88867-255c-5a1f-b8b5-621e730a9785', 'word_count': 328, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01b88867-255c-5a1f-b8b5-621e730a9785'}, {'abstract': 'The Post 9/11 G.I. Bill has helped tens of thousands of veterans attend college, but the potentially lucrative source of guaranteed student tuition needs to be safeguarded from less the scrupulous actors in the higher education market.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/making-the-g-i-bill-work-for-veterans/', 'snippet': 'The Post 9/11 G.I. Bill has helped tens of thousands of veterans attend college, but the potentially lucrative source of guaranteed student tuition needs to be safeguarded from less the scrupulous actors in the higher education market.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Today’s veterans have faced incredible challenges, but have also received extraordinary opportunities – like the Post 9/11 G.I. Bill. Each year, it helps tens of thousands of veterans attend college by helping pay for tuition and living expenses. Through this program, many veterans have been able to transition successfully from combat back to civilian life. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Making the G.I. Bill Work for Veterans', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': '