 for Lamé and Condemned Men', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Thing for Lamé And Condemned Men', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Daniels, Lee', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Paperboy (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kidman, Nicole', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T20:10:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Leah Rozen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Leah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rozen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff053efa-801f-5528-8115-ffcf3f86eac4', 'word_count': 1485, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff053efa-801f-5528-8115-ffcf3f86eac4'}, {'abstract': 'Musical-theater composer David Yazbek describes why an improv comedy duo has excited him more than most scripted theater he’s seen recently.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/theater-talkback-finding-inspiration-in-improvisation/', 'snippet': 'Musical-theater composer David Yazbek describes why an improv comedy duo has excited him more than most scripted theater he’s seen recently.', 'lead_paragraph': 'During the summer, ArtsBeat invited members of the theater world to contribute to the weekly Theater Talkback column, alternating with the critics Ben Brantley and Charles Isherwood. Trav S. D., a historian of vaudeville, talked about the long bare-knuckles history shared between the boxing ring and the stage; Alexis Soloski, a critic and theater professor, highlighted unforgettable stage entrances; and the playwright Sarah Ruhl explained why critics were not invited to review her “Melancholy Play.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Theater Talkback: Finding Inspiration in Improvisation', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Creativity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'C K, Louis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yazbek, David', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T20:13:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Yazbek', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yazbek', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee6a52ab-fcb2-52e0-8bb3-d0c957f841ea', 'word_count': 703, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee6a52ab-fcb2-52e0-8bb3-d0c957f841ea'}, {'abstract': 'President Vladimir V. Putin is hoping to strengthen ties with the Pacific Rim and pursuing ambitious development in Russia itself.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/world/europe/at-asia-pacific-meeting-putin-focuses-on-the-far-east.html', 'snippet': 'President Vladimir V. Putin is hoping to strengthen ties with the Pacific Rim and pursuing ambitious development in Russia itself.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VLADIVOSTOK, Russia — President Vladimir V. Putin of Russia is seizing on the Asia-Pacific economic summit conference being held here this weekend to turn assertively to the Far East, hoping to strengthen ties with the Pacific Rim and pursuing ambitious development in Russia itself, starting with this formerly secret naval fortress turned shipping hub on the Sea of Japan.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/world/russia1/russia1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/07/world/russia1/russia1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/world/russia1/russia1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/world/russia1/russia1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Putin’s Ambitions Turn to the Far East', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Putin’s Ambitions Turn to the Far East', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vladivostok (Russia)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infrastructure (Public Works)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Far East, South and Southeast Asia and Pacific Areas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T20:14:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By David M. Herszenhorn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4bd9480f-2621-5474-911f-86cb7e62b435', 'word_count': 1074, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4bd9480f-2621-5474-911f-86cb7e62b435'}, {'abstract': 'I love the industry of the second-grade classroom. And I also love the unassailable logic of keeping the tissues in the country-music corner.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/first-day-of-school-brooklyn/', 'snippet': 'I love the industry of the second-grade classroom. And I also love the unassailable logic of keeping the tissues in the country-music corner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'So today is the first day of public school in New York City. My three kids are all old hands at this by now, so the drop-off was easy. They’re going into second, fifth and eighth grades. For some reason, the eighth grader doesn’t begin school until tomorrow, so he got to go back to his elementary school to see off his younger brother and sister. He was fawned over by his old teachers, who seemed truly amazed that he is now a very tall 13-year-old. I could tell he was enjoying the attention until it happened that the director of his middle school has a second grader he was dropping off; my 13-year-old quickly vanished. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'First Day of School, Brooklyn', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T20:14:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Wm. Ferguson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Wm', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ef4ae36-9242-5a6c-8b8d-657fb603142a', 'word_count': 263, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ef4ae36-9242-5a6c-8b8d-657fb603142a'}, {'abstract': 'The former slave and memoirist goes to Washington as a correspondent. What she finds among the city’s black refugees shocks a nation.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/harriet-jacobss-first-assignment/', 'snippet': 'The former slave and memoirist goes to Washington as a correspondent. What she finds among the city’s black refugees shocks a nation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Harriet Jacobs arrived in Washington in June 1862, she later reported, “without molestation.” Lots of people traveled in and out of the capital at the time, but for Jacobs it was quite a feat. By then a correspondent on assignment for William Lloyd Garrison’s newspaper The Liberator, Jacobs was a former slave and author of the book “Incidents in the Life of a Slave Girl,” which she wrote under the assumed name Linda Brent. Traveling through Maryland, where slavery was still legal, and Pennsylvania, where anti-black animus still ran high, would have made for tough going for most free blacks. Even fewer could have taken in the squalor that Jacobs found among the thousands of refugees from the South now huddled in the capital. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Harriet Jacobs’s First Assignment', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Slavery', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garrison, William Lloyd', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T20:18:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Korb', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Korb', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4260bc95-55d2-512b-98bc-e00eabb835ac', 'word_count': 1875, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4260bc95-55d2-512b-98bc-e00eabb835ac'}, {'abstract': 'The president will outline his plan for cutting “what we don’t need” tonight, which should worry anyone concerned about the future of Medicare and Medicaid.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/the-dangerous-center/', 'snippet': 'The president will outline his plan for cutting “what we don’t need” tonight, which should worry anyone concerned about the future of Medicare and Medicaid.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many of the Democrats who thrilled to Bill Clinton’s defense of an active government last night have conveniently forgotten how angry they were every time he tacked to the center, most notably by drastically reducing welfare benefits in 1996. President Obama shares some of those instincts toward ideological concessions, creating a bit of suspense regarding the nature of the second-term agenda he intends to unveil tonight.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Dangerous Center', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicaid', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cutter, Stephanie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T20:19:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Firestone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Firestone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1820ddca-30b5-5296-9b71-6a1626bc5ea9', 'word_count': 471, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1820ddca-30b5-5296-9b71-6a1626bc5ea9'}, {'abstract': 'Former executives at Sotheby’s and Christie’s join forces as part of a new partnership of superdealers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/arts/design/connery-pissarro-seydoux-dealers-in-a-new-partnership.html', 'snippet': 'Former executives at Sotheby’s and Christie’s join forces as part of a new partnership of superdealers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When was the last time an expert from a top auction house dispensed with longtime allegiances and joined forces with someone from the enemy camp? In the fiercely competitive world of Sotheby’s and Christie’s, such an occurrence is rarer than a prized Vermeer. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/arts/07VOGEL/VOGEL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 852, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/arts/07VOGEL/VOGEL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1704, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/arts/07VOGEL/07VOGEL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/07/arts/07VOGEL/07VOGEL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/arts/07VOGEL/07VOGEL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {