/article/ebf67868-1196-5cdd-be3d-f2909dd9a768'}, {'abstract': 'Hermès hosted a Fashion Week cocktail party and dinner in a deconsecrated Park Avenue church, a fine place in which to gather a group of prosperous New Yorkers to show reverence for the efforts that go into making a Kelly bag.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/herms-and-craftsmanship/', 'snippet': 'Hermès hosted a Fashion Week cocktail party and dinner in a deconsecrated Park Avenue church, a fine place in which to gather a group of prosperous New Yorkers to show reverence for the efforts that go into making a Kelly bag.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The question was surely rhetorical. “Do you know the right way to eat caviar?’’ said John Martinez, a cater-waiter.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hermès and Craftsmanship', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Fashion Week', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hermes International SA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T21:37:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Guy Trebay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Guy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Trebay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7373507-aefc-52a9-8372-604afcc777e0', 'word_count': 665, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7373507-aefc-52a9-8372-604afcc777e0'}, {'abstract': 'The new Consumer Financial Protection Bureau says that just over half the mortgage complaints over the last year centered on problems borrowers encountered when they fell behind in payments.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/09/realestate/mortgages-complaints-against-lenders.html', 'snippet': 'The new Consumer Financial Protection Bureau says that just over half the mortgage complaints over the last year centered on problems borrowers encountered when they fell behind in payments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE new Consumer Financial Protection Bureau received 23,500 complaints about mortgage lenders from last December through this past June, according to a recently released semiannual report. And, not surprisingly, just over half the complaints centered on the problems borrowers encountered when they were unable to make payments.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/realestate/09mort-graphic/09mort-graphic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 304, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/09/realestate/09mort-graphic/09mort-graphic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 304}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/realestate/09mort-graphic/09mort-graphic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 577, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/realestate/09mort-graphic/09mort-graphic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1154, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/realestate/09mort-graphic/09mort-graphic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/09/realestate/09mort-graphic/09mort-graphic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/realestate/09mort-graphic/09mort-graphic-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Complaints Against Lenders', 'kicker': 'Mortgages', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Complaints Against Lenders', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Financial Protection Bureau', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T21:38:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vickie Elmer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vickie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elmer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d92cbe9-3eb4-5fc9-8516-aa92ca54b8cb', 'word_count': 610, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d92cbe9-3eb4-5fc9-8516-aa92ca54b8cb'}, {'abstract': 'A show at Artists Space gathers together the prolific output of this influential and intentionally enigmatic quasi-corporation.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/all-of-their-business-bernadette-corporation-at-artists-space/', 'snippet': 'A show at Artists Space gathers together the prolific output of this influential and intentionally enigmatic quasi-corporation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since the mid-1990s, Bernadette Van-Huy, John Kelsey and Antek Walczak, operating as the collective Bernadette Corporation, have run a critically acclaimed underground fashion label; published a magazine, Made in USA, as well as a novel, “Reena Spaulings”; and produced a handful of films, including “Get Rid of Yourself” (2003), which revolves around the riots at the 2001 G8 Summit and features an awkward star turn by the actress Chloë Sevigny.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'All of Their Business | Bernadette Corporation at Artists Space', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T21:39:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alix Browne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alix', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Browne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed62596e-1a1a-5f9a-8516-d5522f4c1390', 'word_count': 188, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed62596e-1a1a-5f9a-8516-d5522f4c1390'}, {'abstract': 'The Times will be providing updates and analysis from Charlotte on our live dashboard. You can also follow along on Twitter @thecaucus, or follow our list of Times journalists covering the convention.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/live-updates-from-the-democratic-convention/', 'snippet': 'The Times will be providing updates and analysis from Charlotte on our live dashboard. You can also follow along on Twitter @thecaucus, or follow our list of Times journalists covering the convention.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Times will be providing updates and analysis from Charlotte on our live dashboard. You can also follow along on Twitter @thecaucus, or follow our list of Times journalists covering the convention.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Live Updates From the Democratic Convention', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Democratic National Convention', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T21:39:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/98487ffc-5acb-5d20-b4f6-0d38c3cf8385', 'word_count': 5317, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98487ffc-5acb-5d20-b4f6-0d38c3cf8385'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney will appear on “Meet the Press” on Sunday.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/romneys-next-test/', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney will appear on “Meet the Press” on Sunday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To put the question bluntly: How will Mitt Romney perform on “Meet the Press”?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney’s Next Test', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T21:39:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jodi Kantor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jodi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kantor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6194e9b0-0902-5947-a3fd-5e4deee03f15', 'word_count': 261, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6194e9b0-0902-5947-a3fd-5e4deee03f15'}, {'abstract': 'Marin Mazzie, in her show at 54 Below, uses cabaret as a time machine to revisit her musical past.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/arts/music/marin-mazzies-cabaret-show-at-54-below.html', 'snippet': 'Marin Mazzie, in her show at 54 Below, uses cabaret as a time machine to revisit her musical past.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What sweet, silly dreams we have as naïve adolescents soaking up popular culture and mooning over the teen idols of the moment. When the Broadway singer Marin Mazzie (“Kiss Me, Kate,” “Passion”) was growing up in Rockford, Ill., she recalled on Wednesday evening at 54 Below, she was in the thrall of the Monkees’ Davy Jones and of David Cassidy and fantasized about being “the long-lost Partridge” on “The Partridge Family.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/arts/07MAZZIE/07MAZZIE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 906, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/arts/07MAZZIE/07MAZZIE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1813, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/arts/07MAZZIE/07MAZZIE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/07/arts/07MAZZIE/07MAZZIE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/arts/07MAZZIE/07MAZZIE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Songs of Innocence, à la the Monkees', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Songs of Innocence, à la the Monkees', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mazzie, Marin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': '54 Below (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MONKEES, THE', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T21:40:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/03c20fca-ccf3-58a1-b196-7477f1a7e41c', 'word_count': 376, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03c20fca-ccf3-58a1-b196-7477f1a7e41c'}, {'abstract': '“Toxic Beauty: The Art of Frank Moore,” a retrospective in two galleries at New York University, reflects an intellectually fervent maverick commenting on contemporary issues.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/arts/design/toxic-beauty-the-art-of-frank-moore-at-nyu.html', 'snippet': '“Toxic Beauty: The Art of Frank Moore,” a retrospective in two galleries at New York University, reflects an intellectually fervent maverick commenting on contemporary issues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Frank Moore had a busy, productive career in and around painting until it was cut short by AIDS in 2002. He was 48, one among many artists felled by the disease. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/arts/07TOXIC_SPAN/07TOXIC_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 449, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'ar