ead_paragraph': 'There’s one advantage that President Obama has that Mitt Romney probably doesn’t. If he can get a good turnout from his base, he’ll be the heavy favorite to win in November — even if Mr. Romney gets a strong turnout as well.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Would Be Big Favorite With ‘Fired Up’ Base', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T21:40:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37c7319e-7890-530a-bd7f-1e1807c6d10f', 'word_count': 594, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37c7319e-7890-530a-bd7f-1e1807c6d10f'}, {'abstract': 'Discarded plastic provides ideas for new porcelain containers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/garden/global-table-sells-bottles-collection-by-van-duin.html', 'snippet': 'Discarded plastic provides ideas for new porcelain containers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Foekje Fleur van Duin was an art student in the Netherlands, she read about the masses of discarded containers that float in the ocean. She went to the Maas River near Rotterdam in search of her own “plastic soup.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/garden/07GOODS_SPAN/07GOODS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 314, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/07/garden/07GOODS_SPAN/07GOODS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 314}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None