': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/arts/spare-times-for-sept-7-13.html', 'snippet': 'A listing of noteworthy cultural events in the New York area.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Around Town', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spare Times for Sept. 7-13', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spare Times', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parks and Other Recreation Areas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T21:56:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anne Mancuso', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mancuso', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/055ed5d9-dac1-5ff0-8fd1-cea39b9025db', 'word_count': 2983, 'uri': 'nyt://article/055ed5d9-dac1-5ff0-8fd1-cea39b9025db'}, {'abstract': '“Keep the Lights On,” by Ira Sachs, follows two men as their relationship grows, falters and endures over more than a decade.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/movies/keep-the-lights-on-directed-by-ira-sachs.html', 'snippet': '“Keep the Lights On,” by Ira Sachs, follows two men as their relationship grows, falters and endures over more than a decade.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When we first meet Erik (Thure Lindhardt), a Danish filmmaker living in New York in 1997, he is on the telephone looking for a casual sexual hookup. He seems fickle and impatient, hanging up on potential partners at the first hint that the chemistry might be wrong, but eventually he finds more or less what he is looking for. Quite a bit more, actually, in the person of Paul (Zachary Booth), even though Paul says he has a steady girlfriend, and Erik is not interested in commitment.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/arts/07KEEP_SPAN/07KEEP_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/07/arts/07KEEP_SPAN/07KEEP_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/arts/07KEEP_SPAN/JPKEEP-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/arts/07KEEP_SPAN/JPKEEP-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/arts/07KEEP_SPAN/07KEEP_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/07/arts/07KEEP_SPAN/07KEEP_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/arts/07KEEP_SPAN/07KEEP_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Enduring Erotic Life Cycle of an Unpromising Relationship', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Enduring Erotic Life Cycle of an Unpromising Relationship', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sachs, Ira', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Booth, Zachary', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Keep the Lights On (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lindhardt, Thure', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T21:58:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/34273b25-c04a-52d0-bbed-7e95076e295f', 'word_count': 820, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34273b25-c04a-52d0-bbed-7e95076e295f'}, {'abstract': 'The emerging jazz duo of Peter Brötzmann and Jason Adasiewicz, now on tour, offered a set of improvisation at Le Poisson Rouge.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/arts/music/peter-brotzmann-and-jason-adasiewicz-at-le-poisson-rouge.html', 'snippet': 'The emerging jazz duo of Peter Brötzmann and Jason Adasiewicz, now on tour, offered a set of improvisation at Le Poisson Rouge.', 'lead_paragraph': '“You take when a high note comes through, lifting and going and then stopping because there’s no place else for it to go,” the saxophonist Sidney Bechet explained some time in the 1950s. “That’s stepping music — it’s got to rush itself right off your voice or your horn because it’s so excited.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/arts/2NDSUBLPR/2NDSUBLPR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 984, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/arts/2NDSUBLPR/2NDSUBLPR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2034, 'width': 1955, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Generations United for Improvisation, Refined but Violent', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Generations United For Improvisation, Refined but Violent', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brotzmann, Peter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adasiewicz, Jason', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T21:59:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Ratliff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ratliff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/073e93ed-fe6f-5e77-aab5-c79686ec91cf', 'word_count': 597, 'uri': 'nyt://article/073e93ed-fe6f-5e77-aab5-c79686ec91cf'}, {'abstract': 'John Cage’s centennial was commemorated this week by programs at the Stone, in the East Village, and Symphony Space, on the Upper West Side.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/arts/music/john-cage-centennials-at-symphony-space-and-the-stone.html', 'snippet': 'John Cage’s centennial was commemorated this week by programs at the Stone, in the East Village, and Symphony Space, on the Upper West Side.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a composer who was a true rebel, a pioneering American maverick, John Cage was frequently celebrated in programs and festivals at the world’s most prestigious concert halls. But he surely would have been delighted to see the centennial of his birth commemorated in New York at “Cage100,” a three-day festival at the Stone, the nonprofit performance space in the East Village dedicated to experimental and avant-garde music. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_pa