nal Convention gave the musical responsibilities to one man: DJ Cassidy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHARLOTTE, N.C. — As the first notes of Fleetwood Mac’s “Don’t Stop” rang through the Time Warner Cable Arena here on Wednesday night, the packed crowd whipped into a frenzy, nearly drowning out the song as they cheered for minutes for former President Bill Clinton. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dropping the Beats at the Democratic Convention', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Democratic National Convention', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T22:18:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Corasaniti', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Corasaniti', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5376e0d-279e-58e9-a98b-96e012a9997f', 'word_count': 382, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5376e0d-279e-58e9-a98b-96e012a9997f'}, {'abstract': 'Some may say that women’s tennis is boring, but the women remaining at the U.S. Open are set up for an intriguing semifinals. Lynn Zinser has the latest from Flushing.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/video-is-womens-tennis-boring-not-at-the-open/', 'snippet': 'Some may say that women’s tennis is boring, but the women remaining at the U.S. Open are set up for an intriguing semifinals. Lynn Zinser has the latest from Flushing.', 'lead_paragraph': "(function($){var data = chameleonData;var ticker = new NYTD.NYTMM.NewsTicker($('#nytmm_embed_834'), data);})(jQuery||NYTD.jQuery);", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video: Is Women’s Tennis Boring? Not at the Open', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T22:18:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/874ec3fa-aa7f-52ed-8dee-36ce65bcebbe', 'word_count': 84, 'uri': 'nyt://article/874ec3fa-aa7f-52ed-8dee-36ce65bcebbe'}, {'abstract': 'T-shirt descriptions inspired the works in “Raw/Cooked: Ulrike Müller,” at the Brooklyn Museum.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/arts/design/raw-cooked-ulrike-muller-at-the-brooklyn-museum.html', 'snippet': 'T-shirt descriptions inspired the works in “Raw/Cooked: Ulrike Müller,” at the Brooklyn Museum.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Collaboration is one of the hallmarks of feminist art and scholarship. The art system doesn’t really accommodate this, however. Instead, criticism, art history and institutions are set up to canonize (historically male) individual artists. And for curators, it’s considerably easier to work with one artist than a hundred. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/arts/07ULRIKE/SUBULRIKE-1346949251964-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 753, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/arts/07ULRIKE/SUBULRIKE-1346949251964-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1505, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail'