e, started toward a drop shot and stopped, the promise of pain too great. Moments later, his partner, Marcel Granollers, looked Lopez in the eye. Lopez nodded.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Men’s Doubles Final Has a Familiar Feel', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bryan, Mike', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paes, Leander', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stepanek, Radek', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T22:52:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cba9d169-493d-5acb-b97b-0fe9815c2c18', 'word_count': 522, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cba9d169-493d-5acb-b97b-0fe9815c2c18'}, {'abstract': 'A guide to movies playing in and outside the New York area as well as noteworthy film series.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/movies/movie-listings-for-sept-7-13.html', 'snippet': 'A guide to movies playing in and outside the New York area as well as noteworthy film series.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Movies', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Movie Listings for Sept. 7-13', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Listings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T22:53:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/a463cf94-eccf-5394-a220-2e6802cb1a3a', 'word_count': 3035, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a463cf94-eccf-5394-a220-2e6802cb1a3a'}, {'abstract': 'A federal program that grants so-called EB-5 visas to foreigners who invest at least $500,000 in an American business has become a popular source of cheap financing for hotel companies.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/visas-for-dollars-program-a-boon-to-hotel-developers/', 'snippet': 'A federal program that grants so-called EB-5 visas to foreigners who invest at least $500,000 in an American business has become a popular source of cheap financing for hotel companies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Marriott International wanted to open a new hotel in downtown Seattle, the company’s developers didn’t sell bonds, take out a mortgage or tap other traditional forms of financing for the $88 million project. Instead, it raised the bulk of the money from wealthy immigrants who wanted a green card.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Visas-for-Dollars Program a Boon to Hotel Developers', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Visas-for-Dollars Program a Boon to Hotel Developers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Investments', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'HOTELS AND MOTELS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citizenship and Immigration Services (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Marriott International Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T22:54:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Janet Morrissey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Janet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morrissey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/52bca2b7-a7f5-5798-a7a9-8e59126eed60', 'word_count': 1125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52bca2b7-a7f5-5798-a7a9-8e59126eed60'}, {'abstract': 'The teenage characters of a popular British TV sitcom take their antics to the big screen in “The Inbetweeners.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/movies/the-inbetweeners-directed-by-ben-palmer.html', 'snippet': 'The teenage characters of a popular British TV sitcom take their antics to the big screen in “The Inbetweeners.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In “Among the Thugs,” Bill Buford’s horrifying nonfiction book about the brutal excesses of British soccer hooliganism, he writes about gangs of fans who travel to European cities like Turin ostensibly to support their teams. In one unforgettable scene Mr. Buford watches as hordes of Manchester United followers swarm out of a Turin stadium and into the streets in a frenzy of violence, savagely beating anyone, children included. In the middle of the mayhem, in between the stomping and punching, he overhears one of the rampaging goons say, “The city is ours” and repeat the word ours, ours, ours. There’s a sense that the rioting is a kind of postcolonial invasion for at least this one thug, an idea that’s cemented when later he says, “We took the city.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/arts/07INBETWEENERS_SPAN/07INBETWEENERS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 349, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/07/arts/07INBETWEENERS_SPAN/07INBETWEENERS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 349}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/arts/07INBETWEENERS_SPAN/INBETWEENERS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/arts/07INBETWEENERS_SPAN/INBETWEENERS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/arts/07INBETWEENERS_SPAN/07INBETWEENERS_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/07/arts/07INBETWEENERS_SPAN/07INBETWEENERS_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/arts/07INBETWEENERS_SPAN/07INBETWEENERS_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Unhappy Hooligans, Dripping With Lust', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Unhappy Hooligans, Dripping With Lust', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Palmer, Ben', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-06T22:55:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'org