thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/07/arts/07RDP_ACACIAS_SPAN/07RDP_ACACIAS_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/arts/07RDP_ACACIAS_SPAN/07RDP_ACACIAS_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Softening a Trucker’s Rough Edges', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Las Acacias', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Las acacias (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T00:02:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeannette Catsoulis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeannette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Catsoulis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1541863-eb43-5706-a05c-685e5e5cdda4', 'word_count': 251, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1541863-eb43-5706-a05c-685e5e5cdda4'}, {'abstract': 'The police summoned a lawyer for the punk band Pussy Riot for questioning in a criminal case that the authorities say is unrelated to the Pussy Riot case.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/world/europe/russia-pussy-riot-lawyer-questioned.html', 'snippet': 'The police summoned a lawyer for the punk band Pussy Riot for questioning in a criminal case that the authorities say is unrelated to the Pussy Riot case.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The police summoned a lawyer for the punk band Pussy Riot for questioning in a criminal case that the authorities say is unrelated to the Pussy Riot case. They plan to question the lawyer, Mark Feygin, about disturbances during a large street protest last spring in Moscow. The wide-ranging investigation has led to the arrests of many opposition figures. Mr. Feygin was one of the speakers at the protest, but he said that he never scuffled with the police and that he thought the summons was indeed related to his work as a defense lawyer for the band members, three of whom were recently convicted of hooliganism for a protest in a Moscow cathedral. “I link this with the Pussy Riot case, there are no doubts about it,” he said in an interview. “I think this is simply an attempt to pressure us.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia: Pussy Riot Lawyer Questioned', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia: Pussy Riot Lawyer Questioned', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pussy Riot', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T00:02:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ilya Mouzykantskii', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ilya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mouzykantskii', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/713f0d7a-0e0e-5357-a74a-c98f0339ee51', 'word_count': 145, 'uri': 'nyt://article/713f0d7a-0e0e-5357-a74a-c98f0339ee51'}, {'abstract': 'A New York advertising firm has chosen two ideas from a crowdsourcing competition, including one that will give employees 4,500 square feet of office space for personal projects.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/business/media/advertising-agency-crowdsources-its-own-morale.html', 'snippet': 'A New York advertising firm has chosen two ideas from a crowdsourcing competition, including one that will give employees 4,500 square feet of office space for personal projects.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AN advertising agency that has been crowdsourcing ideas from its employees is at it again, adopting additional suggestions from staff members on how to improve operations and, by extension, morale.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/business/Adco/Adco-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 689, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/business/Adco/Adco-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1379, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Ad Agency Crowdsources Its Own Employees’ Morale', 'kicker': 'Advertising', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Ad Agency Crowdsources Its Own Employees’ Morale', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Workplace Environment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kirshenbaum Bond Senecal & Partners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crowdsourcing (Internet)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T00:02:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4cdc1c78-5c3d-539c-96fc-b2b46ea7e120', 'word_count': 759, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4cdc1c78-5c3d-539c-96fc-b2b46ea7e120'}, {'abstract': 'A Russian Air Force MiG-29 fighter jet crashed Thursday afternoon near Chita, a city in Eastern Siberia, slamming into a hill close to a local airport and killing the pilot.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/world/europe/russia-fighter-jet-crashes-killing-pilot.html', 'snippet': 'A Russian Air Force MiG-29 fighter jet crashed Thursday afternoon near Chita, a city in Eastern Siberia, slamming into a hill close to a local airport and killing the pilot.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Russian Air Force MiG-29 fighter jet crashed Thursday afternoon near Chita, a city in Eastern Siberia, slamming into a hill close to a local airport and killing the pilot. Flights of MiG-29 fighters have been grounded pending further investigation, a Defense Ministry spokesman, Igor Konashenkov, told the RIA Novosti news agency. The pilot’s body was found by a search party, and there were no weapons on board, Mr. Konashenkov said. The Interfax news service reported that a second fighter plane crashed Thursday near the Siberian city of Novosibirsk, this one a Sukhoi Su-27. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia: Fighter Jet Crashes, Killing Pilot', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia: Fighter Jet Crashes, Killing Pilot', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aviation Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Military Aircraft', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T00:03:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anna Kordunsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anna', 'middlename': None, 'last