 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/f76d9fa1-c795-5baf-9e21-7aec028aa83c', 'word_count': 845, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f76d9fa1-c795-5baf-9e21-7aec028aa83c'}, {'abstract': 'Rory McIlroy, currently ranked No. 1 in the world, shot an opening-round 64 Thursday to share the lead with three other golfers at the BMW Championship. Tiger Woods shot a 65, good for fifth place.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/sports/golf/bmw-championship-anything-tiger-woods-can-do-rory-mcilroy-can-do-better.html', 'snippet': 'Rory McIlroy, currently ranked No. 1 in the world, shot an opening-round 64 Thursday to share the lead with three other golfers at the BMW Championship. Tiger Woods shot a 65, good for fifth place.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CARMEL, Ind. — Tiger Woods produced a deft display of scoring, if not shotmaking, with a seven-under-par 65 at Crooked Stick Golf Club on Thursday in the first round of the BMW Championship. With a little bit of magic, including a holed bump and run shot for a birdie on his final hole, Woods managed to escape mediocrity but not the shadow of his playing partner, Rory McIlroy. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/sports/golf/golf-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/07/sports/golf/golf-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/sports/golf/golf-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 704, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/sports/golf/golf-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1409, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/sports/golf/golf-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/07/sports/golf/golf-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/sports/golf/golf-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Anything Woods Can Do, McIlroy Does Better', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Anything Woods Can Do, McIlroy Does Better', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McIlroy, Rory', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woods, Tiger', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T00:59:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ff7f079-9058-5785-8500-513b4fbd0b6b', 'word_count': 845, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ff7f079-9058-5785-8500-513b4fbd0b6b'}, {'abstract': 'If we are serious about uprooting corruption in Albany, the next step is to make service as a legislator a full-time job and ban outside sources of employment and income for our public officials.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/opinion/new-yorks-moonlighting-lawmakers.html', 'snippet': 'If we are serious about uprooting corruption in Albany, the next step is to make service as a legislator a full-time job and ban outside sources of employment and income for our public officials.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TO read the news, one might think that the “perp walk” was a necessary rite in the career of a New York State legislator. Eighteen Albany lawmakers have left office as a result of criminal charges or ethical misconduct since 1999, according to the government-reform organization Citizens Union — a run that the organization appropriately terms a “crime wave.” There are many reasons to account for this dismal record, but one in particular concerns a practice that, at first glance, may seem endearingly quaint: the legislators are part-timers.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York’s Moonlighting Lawmakers', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New York’s Moonlighting Lawmakers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T01:01:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric R. Dinallo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Dinallo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/b34ed521-2aa4-5513-a9dc-ff2c0d252a25', 'word_count': 512, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b34ed521-2aa4-5513-a9dc-ff2c0d252a25'}, {'abstract': 'The softball team of Dewey & LeBoeuf, the behemoth firm that went bankrupt this year, is 10-1 and is defending its league championship from last season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/nyregion/dewey-leboeuf-keeps-its-troubles-off-the-softball-field.html', 'snippet': 'The softball team of Dewey & LeBoeuf, the behemoth firm that went bankrupt this year, is 10-1 and is defending its league championship from last season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a field of bright green turf, a group of men and women trotted about on Wednesday evening, catching and throwing, hitting, spitting and sliding. They were ballplayers, but in a sense, they were also ghosts, casualties of an immense corporate collapse, with the name of their defunct former employer emblazoned on their torsos: Dewey. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/nyregion/DEWEY/DEWEY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/nyregion/DEWEY/DEWEY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/nyregion/DEWEY/DEWEY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/07/nyregion/DEWEY/DEWEY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/nyregion/DEWEY/DEWEY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Defunct Law Firm Keeps Its Troubles Off the Softball Field', 'kicker':