l', 'snippet': 'One day after a company unveiled an app allowing yellow-taxi drivers and passengers to find one another, the city said it had not authorized the use of smartphone apps for taxi-hailing or payment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One day after a start-up company unveiled an app allowing yellow-taxi drivers and passengers to find one another, New York City issued this gentle reminder: Smartphone apps may be the future of hailing a taxicab, but at least for now, their time will have to wait.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Now, Taxi Office Says, Cab-Hailing Apps Aren’t Allowed', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Now, Taxi Office Says, Cab-Hailing Apps Aren’t Allowed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxicabs and Taxicab Drivers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taxi and Limousine Commission', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Uber Technologies Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T01:50:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Flegenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flegenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bfe41f58-d403-5a99-97fa-cf43ffaff015', 'word_count': 439, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bfe41f58-d403-5a99-97fa-cf43ffaff015'}, {'abstract': 'A look at December’s movie releases.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/09/movies/december-release-schedule.