atus of people who they suspect are in the country illegally.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/us/key-element-of-arizona-immigration-law-survives-ruling.html', 'snippet': 'The authorities will be required to verify the status of people who they suspect are in the country illegally.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TUCSON — A decision by a federal judge on Wednesday paved the way for the most controversial section of Arizona’s sweeping immigration legislation, requiring the authorities to verify the status of people who they suspect are in the country illegally, to finally take effect. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/us/ARIZONA/ARIZONA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 665, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/us/ARIZONA/ARIZONA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1329, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Arizona Immigration Law Survives Ruling', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Arizona Immigration Law Survives Ruling', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Arizona Immigration Law (SB 1070)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigrants', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T02:03:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fernanda Santos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fernanda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5ac9efb-4c68-5501-859c-d3f69ec5c115', 'word_count': 701, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5ac9efb-4c68-5501-859c-d3f69ec5c115'}, {'abstract': 'The United States takes on Jamaica in a World Cup qualifier without Landon Donovan or Michael Bradley and with Clint Dempsey rejoining the team days after a Premier League transfer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/sports/soccer/us-soccer-team-faces-challenge-in-qualifier-vs-jamaica.html', 'snippet': 'The United States takes on Jamaica in a World Cup qualifier without Landon Donovan or Michael Bradley and with Clint Dempsey rejoining the team days after a Premier League transfer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As storm clouds tumbled toward their Miami training base earlier this week, the United States national soccer team players piled into the gym at Florida International University for a mini-basketball tournament. As Coach Jurgen Klinsmann looked on, he had to hope that his players would take that same bounce to Kingston for Friday night’s World Cup qualifying match against Jamaica.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Faces Challenge in Qualifier vs. Jamaica', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Faces Challenge in Qualifier vs. Jamaica', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dempsey, Clint', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klinsmann, Jurgen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T02:04:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Bell', 'person': [{'firstn