cratic-national-convention.html', 'snippet': 'The following is the full text of President Obama’s speech Thursday from the Democratic National Convention.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The following is the full text of President Obama’s speech Thursday from the Democratic National Convention.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'President Obama’s Full Remarks From the Democratic National Convention', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Democratic National Convention', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speeches and Statements', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T03:35:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Text', '_id': 'nyt://article/51d096c4-adf9-5c40-af87-0595f5ce4335', 'word_count': 5016, 'uri': 'nyt://article/51d096c4-adf9-5c40-af87-0595f5ce4335'}, {'abstract': 'The Democratic National Convention was without Mr. Gore, one of the party’s biggest stars, who was instead doling out commentary for his network, Current TV.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/al-gore-takes-a-pass-on-charlotte/', 'snippet': 'The Democratic National Convention was without Mr. Gore, one of the party’s biggest stars, who was instead doling out commentary for his network, Current TV.', 'lead_paragraph': 'He came ever so close to capturing the presidency in 2000, and even spoke at the 2008 convention, but this time around, Al Gore was nowhere to be seen as Democrats gathered in Charlotte, N.C., this week.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Al Gore Takes a Pass on Charlotte', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Gore, a Spectacle He’s Seen From Both Sides', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Democratic National Convention', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speeches and Statements', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Bill', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gore, Al', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kerry, John', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Current TV', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Charlotte (NC)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T03:39:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Will Storey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Will', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Storey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eefd41bd-6840-578e-bf3b-6148cbb2a486', 'word_count': 203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eefd41bd-6840-578e-bf3b-6148cbb2a486'}, {'abstract': 'The Democratic convention concludes with a workmanlike nomination speech.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/06/the-president-plays-it-safe/', 'snippet': 'The Democratic convention concludes with a workmanlike nomination speech.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The strongest impression left by Mitt Romney’s convention speech last week was that the Republican nominee’s campaign sees itself on pace for a narrow victory in November, with no risks or course corrections needed. The impression left by President Obama’s convention speech tonight was that incumbent’s campaign feels exactly the same way. This was a pure stay-the-course speech, workmanlike and occasionally somewhat distant, with a few inspired and moving passages standing out amid a litany of rhetorical moves that the president has made many times before. There was only the most general sketch of a second term agenda, only a relatively cursory defense of the president’s economic stewardship, and mostly assertions, rather than sustained arguments, to back up his claim that the country is headed (slowly) in the right direction. The strongest and most detailed portions of his remarks came on foreign policy (where his record is more popular and easier to defend)\xa0and in his late-in-the-speech attacks on the Republican ticket, which did effectively exploit some of the vulnerabilities that Romney’s rather content-free address created. And yes, maybe if Bill Clinton hadn’t covered so much of that territory so effectively last night, these strengths would have been enough to make the speech feel successful as a whole. But in the shadow of Clinton’s performance, the president often felt flat, rote, and unconvincing\xa0— almost as though he wasn’t quite convinced by his own arguments and promises, and felt a little awkward selling them to us.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The President Plays It Safe', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T03:51:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/abe170cb-596f-5308-9878-a03b18878354', 'word_count': 291, 'uri': 'nyt://article/abe170cb-596f-5308-9878-a03b18878354'}, {'abstract': 'Second-ranked Novak Djokovic won his quarterfinal against Juan Martín del Potro, 6-2, 7-6 (3), 6-4, in front of a packed Arthur Ashe Stadium.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/sports/tennis/djokovic-pushes-his-way-back-into-spotlight.html', 'snippet': 'Second-ranked Novak Djokovic won his quarterfinal against Juan Martín del Potro, 6-2, 7-6 (3), 6-4, in front of a packed Arthur Ashe Stadium.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After Rafael Nadal withdrew and Andy Roddick retired and Roger Federer stumbled earlier than expected, the United States Open spotlight again settled on Novak Djokovic, at once the world’s second-ranked player and, for most of this tournament, an afterthought.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/sports/djokovic/djokovic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 723, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/sports/djokovic/djokovic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1446, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/sports/djokovic/djokovic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/07/sports/djokovic/djokovic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/sports/djokovic/djokovic-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Defending Champion (Remember Him?) Reaches Semifinals', 'kicker': 'On Tennis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Defending Champion (Remember Him?) Reaches Semifinals', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Djokovic, Novak', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'del Potro, Juan Martin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T03:51:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Greg Bishop', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Greg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bishop', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/12c05cb2-97c8-5d33-86cf-fbdde8678e5e', 'word_count': 943, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12c05cb2-97c8-5d33-86cf-fbdde8678e5e'}, {'abstract': 'Adam Nagourney with Mayor Antonio Villaraigosa of Los Angeles, the Democratic Convention Chairman.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/us/politics/100000001765885/interview-with-antonio-villaraigosa.html', 'snippet': 'Adam Nagourney with Mayor Antonio Villaraigosa of Los Angeles, the Democratic Convention Chairman.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Adam Nagourney with Mayor Antonio Villaraigosa of Los Angeles, the Democratic Convention Chairman.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/06/us/politics/video-dnc-day3-7pm-villaraigos/video-dnc-day3-7pm-villaraigos-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge'