 do a better job the next four years? A good campaign must be prepared to argue its case under both paradigms.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The two competing models for understanding presidential elections are the referendum paradigm and the choice paradigm. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sept. 6: A Referendum or a Choice?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Democratic National Convention', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Republican National Convention', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T12:10:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/419ee834-0903-5971-a5df-5c584619b6c7', 'word_count': 1044, 'uri': 'nyt://article/419ee834-0903-5971-a5df-5c584619b6c7'}, {'abstract': 'Trulia, the real estate search site, said it planned to price its offering of six million shares at $14 to $16 a share.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/trulia-plans-to-raise-up-to-100-million-in-i-p-o/', 'snippet': 'Trulia, the real estate search site, said it planned to price its offering of six million shares at $14 to $16 a share.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Trulia, the real estate search site, said it could raise nearly $100 million in an initial public offering. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trulia Plans to Raise Up to $100 Million in I.P.O.', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Company News: Trulia Says Its I.P.O. Could Raise $96 Million', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Trulia.com', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T12:19:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84af359a-575f-5e9f-ba87-fd21bf2428a6', 'word_count': 249, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84af359a-575f-5e9f-ba87-fd21bf2428a6'}, {'abstract': 'Relatives of Reynaldo Cuevas, the man killed by the police outside a Bronx bodega, said he was a nephew of the owner and had been working at the store for about three months.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/police-fatally-shoot-a-man-at-bronx-bodega/', 'snippet': 'Relatives of Reynaldo Cuevas, the man killed by the police outside a Bronx bodega, said he was a nephew of the owner and had been working at the store for about three months.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 3:57 p.m. | A 20-year-old man was shot and killed by the police early on Friday as he fled from a group of robbers inside a bodega in the Bronx and collided with a police officer, the authorities said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Police Fatally Shoot a Man Outside a Bronx Bodega', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T12:29:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Colin Moynihan and Nate Schweber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Colin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moynihan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6012105e-eae6-5249-a1af-f95e203b81b5', 'word_count': 906, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6012105e-eae6-5249-a1af-f95e203b81b5'}, {'abstract': 'The unexplained murders of three members of a British family and a Frenchman in an isolated corner of rural France have dominated headlines in both countries. The two governments have pledged to co-operate to find the perpetratators of what looks like a professional assassination.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/murder-mystery-stuns-france-and-britain/', 'snippet': 'The unexplained murders of three members of a British family and a Frenchman in an isolated corner of rural France have dominated headlines in both countries. The two governments have pledged to co-operate to find the perpetratators of what looks ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — In news terms, murders are often local affairs, taking a straight line from the police blotter to the city pages and remaining there only as long as it takes for public interest to fade.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/blogs/rdv-murder/rdv-murder-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype':