t the Toronto International Film Festival as it opened here on Thursday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Problems, More Than Solutions, On Screen in Toronto', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Toronto International Film Festival', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rabin, Yitzhak', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shin Bet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T12:37:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cieply', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cieply', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c147cc8-3744-5f95-884f-47cedea28e15', 'word_count': 303, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c147cc8-3744-5f95-884f-47cedea28e15'}, {'abstract': 'The economy added 96,000 jobs in August, well below expectations, raising the pressure on the White House and strengthening the argument for action by the Federal Reserve.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/08/business/economy/us-added-96000-jobs-in-august-rate-fell-to-8-1.html', 'snippet': 'The economy added 96,000 jobs in August, well below expectations, raising the pressure on the White House and strengthening the argument for action by the Federal Reserve.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The nation’s employers eased up on hiring in August, making it clear that the economy was stuck in low gear. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/08/business/Jobs/Jobs-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/08/business/Jobs/Jobs-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/08/business/Jobs/Jobs-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/08/business/Jobs/Jobs-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/08/business/Jobs/Jobs-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/08/business/Jobs/Jobs-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/08/business/Jobs/Jobs-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hiring Slows in U.S., Putting Pressure on Obama and Fed', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Job Gains Slow, Posing Problem For Obama’s Bid', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T12:41:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nelson D. Schwartz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nelson', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c99043e6-17da-5cd2-b213-ab2fd5e2f2ea', 'word_count': 1156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c99043e6-17da-5cd2-b213-ab2fd5e2f2ea'}, {'abstract': 'Obama’s very good case.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/if-only-this-goes-on/', 'snippet': 'Obama’s very good case.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A while back I mentioned, in a quite different context, an essay by Isaac Asimov (?) on Soviet science fiction, in which he argued that the two main themes of Western sci-fi — “what if” and “if only” — were ruled out; instead, writers wrote on the theme “if only this goes on”.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'If Only This Goes On', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T12:51:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e001dcc6-5ebc-5a00-8d33-a9a3c96babc9', 'word_count': 225, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e001dcc6-5ebc-5a00-8d33-a9a3c96babc9'}, {'abstract': 'The Carlyle Group said Friday that it had bought Cogentrix Energy’s North American power plants from Goldman Sachs, as the private equity firm seeks to build up a presence in the energy business.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/carlyle-buys-power-plants-from-goldman/', 'snippet': 'The Carlyle Group said Friday that it had bought Cogentrix Energy’s North American power plants from Goldman Sachs, as the private equity firm seeks to build up a presence in the energy business.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Carlyle Group said Friday that it had bought Cogentrix Energy’s North American power plants from Goldman Sachs, as the private equity firm seeks to build up a presence in the energy business. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Carlyle Buys Power Plants From Goldman Sachs', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Energy and Power', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carlyle Group LP', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T12:52:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c5900e32-2b27-5f9d-80ce-bce0dde933d5', 'word_count': 276, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c5900e32-2b27-5f9d-80ce-bce0dde933d5'}, {'abstract': 'Jobs growing with population, same as it’s been.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/no-news-on-jobs/', 'snippet': 'Jobs growing with population, same as it’s been.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The headline number came in a bit below expectations, but that’s probably just the noisiness in the data. The best hypothesis about the US economy this past year and more is that it has been steadily adding jobs at a pace roughly fast enough to keep up with but not get ahead of population growth. Today’s report was consistent with a continuation of that story. Nothing to see here. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No News On Jobs', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T12:55:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8b3774f-aa8c-5a5a-aa56-ce8dc98e4787', 'word_count': 70, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8b3774f-aa8c-5a5a-aa56-ce8dc98e4787'}, {'abstract': 'The publisher contends that the new edition of “Remembrance of Things Past” will be the longest audiobook in existence.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/audiobook-publisher-issues-120-disc-version-of-proust/', 'snippet': 'The publisher contends that the new edition of “Remembrance of Things Past” will be the longest audiobook in existence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lovers of Proust, get out your headphones: Naxos AudioBooks, a British division of the classical music label, has recorded all seven volumes of “Remembrance of Things Past” on CD — 120 discs, which will take 153 hours to get through. The last one comes out on Oct. 29.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Audiobook Publisher Issues 120-Disc Version of Proust', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Proust Lovers, 153 Hours Of ‘Remembrance,’ Spoken', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Audiobooks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Proust, Marcel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T13:00:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles McGrath', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGrath', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c4e87516-e13e-5369-b7f9-76688d0386c9', 'word_count': 303, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4e87516-e13e-5369-b7f9-76688d0386c9'}, {'abstract': 'Steps from the red carpet in Cannes, the festival’s brightest lights show off their season’s premier essential: a non-red-carpet coat.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/stars-aligned/', 'snippet': 'Steps from the red carpet in Cannes, the festival’s brightest lights show off their season’s premier essential: a non-red-carpet coat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Steps from the red carpet in Cannes, the festival’s brightest lights show off their season’s premier essential: a non-red-carpet coat.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Men’s Fashion Issue | Stars Aligned at Cannes', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cannes International Film Festival', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Festivals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cannes (France)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T13:00:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By PETER LINDBERGH and Jacob Brown', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'LINDBERGH', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jacob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brown', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt