disparaged by Republicans as another month of sluggish economic underperformance.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Steady Progress or More of Same? Politicians React', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T13:56:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By John H. Cushman Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'H.', 'lastname': 'Cushman', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/08a20eef-ef0d-5077-9a82-fec623c5d07f', 'word_count': 697, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08a20eef-ef0d-5077-9a82-fec623c5d07f'}, {'abstract': 'Jessica Chastain, soon coming to Broadway in “The Heiress,” paid a visit to her alma mater, the Juilliard School.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/09/theater/jessica-chastain-in-the-heiress-and-at-juilliard.html', 'snippet': 'Jessica Chastain, soon coming to Broadway in “The Heiress,” paid a visit to her alma mater, the Juilliard School.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JESSICA CHASTAIN has turned up lately in so many movies all at once that audiences may be forgiven for imagining that with her ethereal manner (in “The Tree of Life,” anyway) and Botticelli looks — the alabaster skin, huge green eyes and cascade of auburn hair — she wafted into Hollywood on a seashell. In fact Ms. Chastain, who makes her Broadway debut in “The Heiress” on Nov. 1, is a trained stage actress who spent four transformative years at Juilliard, from which she graduated in 2003.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/arts/09MCGRATH1_SPAN/09MCGRATH1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/09/arts/09MCGRATH1_SPAN/09MCGRATH1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/arts/09MCGRATH1_SPAN/09SUBMCGRATH1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/arts/09MCGRATH1_SPAN/09SUBMCGRATH1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/arts/09MCGRATH1_SPAN/09MCGRATH1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/09/arts/09MCGRATH1_SPAN/09MCGRATH1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/arts/09MCGRATH1_SPAN/09MCGRATH1_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Off to Broadway and Back to School', 'kicker': 'The New Season', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Off to Broadway and Back to School', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chastain, Jessica', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Juilliard School', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T14:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles McGrath', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGrath', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bbfc6116-025c-520d-9227-30d233e65062', 'word_count': 1325, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bbfc6116-025c-520d-9227-30d233e65062'}, {'abstract': 'A 12-year-old’s brush with the Indian prison system is a stark reminder that, even if it now attracts tourists, Kashmir remains a police state.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/a-boys-brush-with-prison-in-kashmir/', 'snippet': 'A 12-year-old’s brush with the Indian prison system is a stark reminder that, even if it now attracts tourists, Kashmir remains a police state.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SRINAGAR, Kashmir — On the morning of Aug. 21, during the foremost Muslim festival of Eid al-Fitr, I drove through Srinagar, the summer capital of the disputed Indian-controlled region of Kashmir.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lawless in Srinagar', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Attacks on Police', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kashmir and Jammu (India)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T14:19:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Basharat Peer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Basharat', 'middlename': Non