, 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T15:17:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jesse McKinley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jesse', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3cfc7ae-13cc-5189-83da-68a9da5aedd4', 'word_count': 270, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3cfc7ae-13cc-5189-83da-68a9da5aedd4'}, {'abstract': 'No, it’s not science fiction: for those who have run out of places to go, companies are competing to take amateur astronauts into the heights, and beyond.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/09/travel/space-tourism-is-here-wealthy-adventurers-wanted.html', 'snippet': 'No, it’s not science fiction: for those who have run out of places to go, companies are competing to take amateur astronauts into the heights, and beyond.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WEDGED between a strip-mall chiropractor and a cluster of optometrists in Rochester, N.Y., the offices of the DePrez Group of Travel Companies hardly seems like the kind of place where someone would begin a journey to the stars. ', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/travel/09SPACE4/09JPSPACE5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 791, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/travel/09SPACE4/09JPSPACE5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1582, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/travel/09SPACE4/09SPACE4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/09/travel/09SPACE4/09SPACE4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/travel/09SPACE4/09SPACE4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Space Tourism Is Here! Wealthy Adventurers Wanted', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Out of This World!', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Blue Origin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Spaceflight', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Virgin Galactic', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'XCOR Aerospace', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Space Adventures', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T15:17:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jesse McKinley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jesse', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f3765e1-8c0a-5aad-bf11-13ee8d3954e1', 'word_count': 2367, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f3765e1-8c0a-5aad-bf11-13ee8d3954e1'}, {'abstract': 'Volunteers building a straw bale house in Utah have found mud and straw to be a forgiving medium.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/at-one-with-the-earth-and-the-clients/', 'snippet': 'Volunteers building a straw bale house in Utah have found mud and straw to be a forgiving medium.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The skeleton of the straw bale house has risen with remarkable speed. In little more than a week, we framed out the walls and almost finished the roof. Now there is no doubt that a house is coming into being, although at this point it is not obvious that it will be anything out of the ordinary. The trained eye will notice the lack of the evenly spaced studs that are normally needed to hang drywall, as well as the presence of a second set of wooden sill plates to support the inside edge of the 18-inch-thick straw bales.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At One With the Earth, and the Clients', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Affordable Housing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Moab (Utah)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T15:22:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71465369-f30e-5c77-a1ca-f1bfea4acaa7', 'word_count': 1455, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71465369-f30e-5c77-a1ca-f1bfea4acaa7'}, {'abstract': 'For years, the artist painted some of his most majestic works along this rocky knuckle of coastline. Later this month, his studio will open to the public for the first time.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/09/travel/in-maine-walking-where-waves-moved-winslow-homers-brush.html', 'snippet': 'For years, the artist painted some of his most majestic works along this rocky knuckle of coastline. Later this month, his studio will open to the public for the first time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN the summer, when the sun played on the juniper bushes, and in the fall, when the air was clear enough to see to the white lighthouse on Wood Island, and in the winter, when the sea battered the granite rocks, Winslow Homer thrived at Prouts Neck, a spit of land off the Southern coast of Maine.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/travel/09JOURNEYS1_SPAN/09JOURNEYS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/09/travel/09JOURNEYS1_SPAN/09JOURNEYS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/travel/09JOURNEYS1_SPAN/09JOURNEYS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/travel/09JOURNEYS1_SPAN/09JOURNEYS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1365, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/travel/09JOURNEYS1_SPAN/09JOURNEYS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/09/travel/09JOURNEYS1_SPAN/09JOURNEYS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Maine, Walking Where Waves Moved Winslow Homer’s Brush', 'kicker': 'Journeys', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Winslow Homer’s Maine And Its Changing Seas', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maine', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Portland Museum of Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Homer, Winslow', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T15:31:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Geraldine Fabrikant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Geraldine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabrikant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d6230ff-af93-5065-b547-375f377b805f', 'word_count': 1219, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d6230ff-af93-5065-b547-375f377b805f'}, {'abstract': 'In a place that offers both muted luxury and abundant marine life, the author discovers the “singular feeling of, at last, having escaped.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/09/travel/sharing-paradise-with-the-barracuda.html', 'snippet': 'In a place that offers both muted luxury and abundant marine life, the author discovers the “singular feeling of, at last, having escaped.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN, after two days of flying, one reaches the island of Bali only to realize that more days of travel lie ahead — from Denpasar to Makassar, then to Sorong in West Papua on one dodgy Indonesian airline after another, and finally a five-hour boat trip — a traveler begins to wonder whether a stay at an eco-resort on a remote Pacific Island will make all the jet lag, chaotic airports and carbon dioxide emissions seem worth it.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type