es.com/2012/09/07/police-seeking-man-who-abused-dog-in-elevator/', 'snippet': 'A man was caught on video kicking a small dog in an elevator at the Wagner Houses in East Harlem last month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For at least the fifth time in less than three years, the police are seeking the public’s help in tracking down someone caught on video beating a dog in a housing-project elevator. The latest incident happened Aug. 26 at the Wagner Houses in East Harlem, site of a similar episode in 2011.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Police Seeking Man Who Abused Dog in Elevator', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cruelty to Animals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Harlem (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T15:39:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f654ffcb-0b5d-52da-b15a-df7b2fe1fa76', 'word_count': 102, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f654ffcb-0b5d-52da-b15a-df7b2fe1fa76'}, {'abstract': 'States are turning to managed care in an effort to reduce Medicaid costs, and the elderly may bear the brunt of the changes.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/medicaid-changes-loom-for-the-elderly/', 'snippet': 'States are turning to managed care in an effort to reduce Medicaid costs, and the elderly may bear the brunt of the changes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Times reports this morning on states’ efforts to rein in Medicaid costs with managed care programs and how these may affect the elderly in nursing homes.', 'source': 'The New York Times',