_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/048bb9c1-c0e5-5434-9d44-98a3f6ceb7ee', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/048bb9c1-c0e5-5434-9d44-98a3f6ceb7ee'}, {'abstract': 'Jennifer Egan discusses Mr. Chabon’s new novel.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/book-review-podcast-michael-chabons-telegraph-avenue/', 'snippet': 'Jennifer Egan discusses Mr. Chabon’s new novel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week in the New York Times Book Review, one Pulitzer Prize winner reviews another as Jennifer Egan considers Michael Chabon’s “Telegraph Avenue.” The novel is set in and around a used-record store on the boulevard where Oakland aligns with Berkeley. Ms. Egan writes:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Book Review Podcast: Michael Chabon’s ‘Telegraph Avenue’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Podcasts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chabon, Michael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cowles, Gregory', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Egan, Jennifer', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Daniel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tanenhaus, Sam', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T16:41:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/22dc74ef-bc6f-5715-9f0d-6c71d3ef00e8', 'word_count': 225, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22dc74ef-bc6f-5715-9f0d-6c71d3ef00e8'}, {'abstract': 'The first few notes of “Close to You” by the Carpenters played at the beginning of the Peter Som show Friday morning. That was enough to suggest a romantic nostalgia.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/at-peter-soms-show-birds-suddenly-appear/', 'snippet': 'The first few notes of “Close to You” by the Carpenters played at the beginning of the Peter Som show Friday morning. That was enough to suggest a romantic nostalgia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first few notes of “Close to You” by the Carpenters played at the beginning of the Peter Som show Friday morning. That was enough to suggest a little bit of romantic nostalgia, the kind that usually describes Mr. Som’s dreamy floral prints. For spring, he made jeans in a pink print that looked like bubble gum, part of a collaboration between Mr. Som and Earnest Sewn, the jeans company, and a series of multicolored pieces, like a T-shirt, a coat and a skirt, each made of a patchwork of snakeskin in an oversize herringbone pattern. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Peter Som’s Show, Birds Suddenly Appear', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Som, Peter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T16:43:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/454d61a2-45b8-5333-b48d-1837d8bd67ad', 'word_count': 97, 'uri': 'nyt://article/454d61a2-45b8-5333-b48d-1837d8bd67ad'}, {'abstract': 'The C.E.O. of the Council of Fashion Designers of America agrees to explain why he has