tell me himself.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/what-my-fathers-dementia-told-me/', 'snippet': 'My father’s dementia told me things about him that he never could or never would tell me himself.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was the copy editor assigned to work on Alex Witchel’s memoir about her mother’s dementia. I was fortunate because her writing is compelling and didn’t need any help from me, and also because it forced me to focus on the quality of my father’s dementia, maybe for the first time.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What My Father’s Dementia Told Me', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dementia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T17:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Dickson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dickson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/897336b0-a9fd-5c50-b356-b37b65b1a7f8', 'word_count': 1202, 'uri': 'nyt://article/897336b0-a9fd-5c50-b356-b37b65b1a7f8'}, {'abstract': 'To sum up his case against Mitt Romney, President Obama offered a new theme: citizenship.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/what-citizenship-means/', 'snippet': 'To sum up his case against Mitt Romney, President Obama offered a new theme: citizenship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHARLOTTE, N.C. – He didn’t deliver a clear second-term agenda, or a speech that thrilled. He didn’t explain how his re-election will spell an end to Washington’s policy stalemate. But President Obama did offer a sort of consolation prize in his convention speech: a new theme to sum up his case against Mitt Romney.', 'source': 'The New 