 much action these past three years.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/the-employment-situation/', 'snippet': 'Not much action these past three years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My current favorite gauge of the jobs picture is the employment-population ratio for prime-age adults (25-54). EP ratio instead of unemployment rate, because U may be distorted by workers dropping out. Prime-age not because the old and young don’t matter, but to take demographic change out of the picture.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Employment Situation', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T17:12:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/263104bb-40ec-573b-b91b-81e280605cc5', 'word_count': 76, 'uri': 'nyt://article/263104bb-40ec-573b-b91b-81e280605cc5'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney questioned on Friday whether President Obama “knows what he’s doing” when it comes to fixing the economy.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/after-a-disappointing-jobs-report-romney-attacks-obama/', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney questioned on Friday whether President Obama “knows what he’s doing” when it comes to fixing the economy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SIOUX CITY, Iowa – Seizing on a disappointing jobs report, Mitt Romney questioned on Friday whether President Obama “knows what he’s doing” when it came to fixing the economy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After a Disappointing Jobs Report, Romney Attacks Obama', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T17:13:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy W. Peters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/979fa257-8966-5255-aca5-ed68b8b11cb6', 'word_count': 319, 'uri': 'nyt://article/979fa257-8966-5255-aca5-ed68b8b11cb6'}, {'abstract': 'Readers solve the case of a 17-year-old girl whose skin mysteriously turns blue.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/think-like-a-doctor-the-blue-girl-solved/', 'snippet': 'Readers solve the case of a 17-year-old girl whose skin mysteriously turns blue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Thursday, we challenged Well readers to solve the mystery of a 17-year-old girl who was turning blue. We received more than 400 colorful responses that ran from Smurfitis and the occasional reference to Willy Wonka to the very serious suggestion of methemoglobinemia, a disorder in which patients turn blue intermittently because of abnormal red blood cells that cannot hold on to oxygen. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/health/07tlad/07tlad-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/health/07tlad/07tlad-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1050, 'width': 1680, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/health/07tlad/07tlad-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/07/health/07tlad/07tlad-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/07/health/07tlad/07tlad-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Think Like a Doctor: The Blue Girl Solved!', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bacteria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sweating', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T17:14:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Sanders, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sanders', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c254130b-cfed-5aaa-a481-7288a285aaae', 'word_count': 1076, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c254130b-cfed-5aaa-a481-7288a285aaae'}, {'abstract': '“Coexist” is the second album by the British band the xx.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/09/arts/music/the-xxs-album-coexist.html', 'snippet': '“Coexist” is the second album by the British band the xx.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE day that “Coexist,” the second album by the miserabilist British band the xx, was mastered, the group’s three members — Romy Madley Croft, Oliver Sim, Jamie Smith — went out for McDonald’s. Each day during the months of recording the album, on the way to the studio with black velvet-covered walls they were hunkered down in, they’d walk past McDonald’s and sigh, tempted by the smell but not giving in.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '65', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/arts/09THEXX_SPAN/09JPTHEXX1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/09/arts/09THEXX_SPAN/09JPTHEXX1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/arts/09THEXX_SPAN/09JPTHEXX1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/arts/09THEXX_SPAN/09JPTHEXX1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/arts/09THEXX_SPAN/09JPTHEXX1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/09/arts/09THEXX_SPAN/09JPTHEXX1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lowercase Minimalists', 'kicker': 'The New Season | Pop', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lowercase Minimalists', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'xx', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T17:26:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e038c11b-c3b4-5809-9f93-54f18aba691b', 'word_count': 1499, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e038c11b-c3b4-5809-9f93-54f18aba691b'}, {'abstract': 'If you’re braising brisket for a holiday meal, you can save time by cooking ahead and freezing the results.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/freezing-brisket/', 'snippet': 'If you’re braising brisket for a holiday meal, you can save time by cooking ahead and freezing the results.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week’s column is about braising brisket for a holiday meal. For years, my mother often cooked her brisket ahead and froze it. This was extremely convenient and the results were good. She would transfer the cooked and cooled meat to a plastic Ziploc, spoon in the sauce and then close the bag, squeezing out the air. Squeezing out the air is the key step. Sometimes she created a faux vacuum by inserting a straw into the bag, inhaling the air and quickly closing it. Of course a vacuum sealer works even better if you have one.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Freezing Brisket', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Meat', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clark, Melissa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T17:26:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4eff758-2a49-5425-82b3-b78cf8dd6b80', 'word_count': 157, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4eff758-2a49-5425-82b3-b78cf8dd6b80'}, {'abstract': 'Had things worked out differently, Mario Ancic would have spent the past two weeks grinding it out at the United States Open. Instead, he has been holed up in the Columbia law library, poring over his contracts casebook.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/former-tennis-star-makes-a-mark-at-columbia-law-school/', 'snippet': 'Had things worked out differently, Mario Ancic would have spent the past two weeks grinding it out at the United States Open. Instead, he has been holed up in the Columbia law library, poring over his contracts casebook.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every fall, Columbia Law School admits a couple hundred students to its prestigious master’s program. This year’s crop includes a civil rights activist from Armenia, a terrorism-finance expert from Bangladesh and a Croatian lawyer with a win over Roger Federer. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Former Tennis Star Makes a Mark at Columbia Law School', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Athlete-Turned-Student Leaves Tennis Courts Behind for the Courtrooms', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Columbia University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T17:32:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/98a6922d-c131-5da3-b578-d1aa44cd1b31', 'word_count': 835, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98a6922d-c131-5da3-b578-d1aa44cd1b31'}, {'abstract': 'Rocco Scuiletti was charged with leaving the scene of an accident after Ms. Kennedy swerved into his truck in July.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/08/nyregion/truck-driver-in-kerry-kennedy-crash-pleads-not-guilty.html', 'snippet': 'Rocco Scuiletti was charged with leaving the scene of an accident after Ms. Kennedy swerved into his truck in July.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ARMONK, N.Y. -- The driver of a tractor-trailer who was involved in an accident with a car driven by Kerry Kennedy two months ago pleaded not guilty on Friday to leaving the scene of an accident and vowed to fight the charge.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/08/nyregion/08kennedy-web/08kennedy-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/08/nyregion/08kennedy-web/08kennedy-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'im