url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/in-midtown-pedestrians-secret-shortcut-is-now-official/', 'snippet': 'From 51st to 57th Streets, along a stretch of pedestrian arcades connected by crosswalks, New Yorkers can find themselves on “Sixth-and-a-Half Avenue.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'For years, it was an open secret — a midblock portal that kept the savviest travelers away from the pedestrian gridlock of Midtown avenues, even if they had to jaywalk a bit to execute the shortcut.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Midtown, Pedestrians’ Secret Shortcut Is Now Official', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transportation Department (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Midtown Area (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T17:53:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Flegenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flegenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/33c3dcf3-d079-5367-addb-6810b3b47bd7', 'word_count': 286, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33c3dcf3-d079-5367-addb-6810b3b47bd7'}, {'abstract': 'When you own a classic house by Philip Johnson, what more could you want? How about a barn for your art?', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/out-of-the-box-2/', 'snippet': 'When you own a classic house by Philip Johnson, what more could you want? How about a barn for your art?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Among the houses that Philip Johnson designed in New Canaan, Conn., the suburban enclave that became a laboratory for postwar Modernist design, the Robert C. Wiley house, completed in 1953, remains one of his most elegant. It is a strikingly simple composition of two rectangular boxes: one, a glass and wood pavilion with a single, 15-foot-tall living, dining and kitchen space, is cantilevered over the other, a stone and concrete base that contains, among other things, four small bedrooms, bathrooms and a sitting room. The 3,000-square-foot house typifies Modernism’s insistence on efficient use of space, but by the advent of the McMansion era, despite its architectural pedigree, it merely seemed quaintly, and unsalably, tiny.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '118', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Out of the Box', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Out of The Box', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T17:58:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pilar Viladas and NIKOLAS KOENIG', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pilar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Viladas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Nikolas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'KOENIG', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/02dcb547-6dc6-5706-a2c9-0de81900bd0b', 'word_count': 606, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02dcb547-6dc6-5706-a2c9-0de81900bd0b'}, {'abstract': 'T plucks the best shoes right off the runway. Today’s pick: a Jason Wu heel with pearls and a contrasting animal print strap.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/the-daily-shoe-jason-wu-3/', 'snippet': 'T plucks the best shoes right off the runway. Today’s pick: a Jason Wu heel with pearls and a contrasting animal print strap.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jason Wu showed a very pretty and semiformal collection full of sex-pot signatures (leather harnesses, lace and leopard, lots of transparency) that, under Wu’s command, took a turn toward boudoir dressing without falling into bed. Some of the stilettos had nail-sharp heels studded with rhinestones. Others featured black netting bejeweled with circles and stars. These with tiny pearls dotting the contrasting ankle strap were the ones that T editors would, if they could, take home tonight.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Daily Shoe | Jason Wu', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T18:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane Herman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Herman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/011d3d15-57ee-5053-b383-4712defbe8bc', 'word_count': 86, 'uri': 'nyt://article/011d3d15-57ee-5053-b383-4712defbe8bc'}, {'abstract': 'Workers on ropes cleaned the exterior of the Guggenheim Museum on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/so-thats-how-they-do-it/', 'snippet': 'Workers on ropes cleaned the exterior of the Guggenheim Museum on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Workers cleaning the exterior of the Guggenheim Museum on Friday morning, the first such work since the museum’s restoration was completed in 2008. View a larger version.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'So That’s How They Do It', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Guggenheim, Solomon R, Museum', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T18:00:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'or