the entire run of the Vertigo series from DC Comics created by Grant Morrison and originally serialized in the 1990s, lands at No. 1 on our hardcover graphic books best-seller list this week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Graphic Books Best Sellers: ‘The Invisibles’ at the Top', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comic Books and Strips', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Graphic Novels', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morrison, Grant', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'DC Comics', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T20:12:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc6486cb-bd1a-5c52-8da0-197e45cb8a79', 'word_count': 185, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc6486cb-bd1a-5c52-8da0-197e45cb8a79'}, {'abstract': 'With the importance of jobs to Americans, many of whom have long been out of work, it’s no wonder the monthly jobs report gets so much weight. But some experts, and some readers, think it gets too much emphasis, or the wrong kind.', 'web_url': 'https://publiceditor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/the-trouble-with-numbers-complaints-on-a-much-anticipated-jobs-report/', 'snippet': 'With the importance of jobs to Americans, many of whom have long been out of work, it’s no wonder the monthly jobs report gets so much weight. But some experts, and some readers, think it gets too much emphasis, or the wrong kind.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s a drumroll beforehand and a great crashing of cymbals as it happens. It’s the federal government’s monthly report on the nation’s employment – a matter that’s given huge political weight in the current presidential campaign, as Jim Rutenberg’s news analysis on today’s front page makes clear. The Wall Street Journal and many other news organizations also gave it front-page treatment, before the fact.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Trouble With Numbers: Complaints on a Much Anticipated Jobs Report', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stevenson, Betsey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T20:18:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2047a33b-3d2e-59cd-96e8-412d8d37f193', 'word_count': 806, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2047a33b-3d2e-59cd-96e8-412d8d37f193'}, {'abstract': 'Security forces again fired tear gas and arrested demonstrators in Bahrain’s capital on Friday, as protesters renewed their calls for reform and the release of political prisoners.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/bahraini-activists-document-crackdown-on-protest/', 'snippet': 'Security forces again fired tear gas and arrested demonstrators in Bahrain’s capital on Friday, as protesters renewed their calls for reform and the release of political prisoners.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Security forces again fired tear gas and arrested demonstrators in Bahrain’s capital on Friday, as protesters renewed their calls for reform and the release of political prisoners in the island kingdom that is home to the United States Navy’s Fifth Fleet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bahraini Activists Document Crackdown on Protest', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Military Tribunals', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khawaja, Abdulhadi al-', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rajab, Nabeel', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Navy', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wefaq National Islamic Society, Al-', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bahrain', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manama (Bahrain)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Saudi Arabia', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T20:18:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Hauser and Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'last