 McGrath’s play “Checkers” this fall at Off Broadway’s Vineyard Theater, executives there announced on Friday. The play, set during the 1952 presidential election, is a character study of Nixon (then the Republican nominee for vice president) as well as a rendering of the Nixon marriage in a moment of crisis, as he delivered his so-called Checkers speech addressing allegations of financial improprieties.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Meet the Nixons: Anthony LaPaglia, Kathryn Erbe Will Star in ‘Checkers’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'u2018Checkersu2019 Play Finds Its Nixons', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Erbe, Kathryn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kinney, Terry (1954- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'LaPaglia, Anthony', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGrath, Douglas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vineyard Theater', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T20:31:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/210ab2cb-d3d3-5429-8058-63ca1ce393c5', 'word_count': 272, 'uri': 'nyt://article/210ab2cb-d3d3-5429-8058-63ca1ce393c5'}, {'abstract': 'David Ferrer’s quarterfinal victory over Janko Tipsarevic was everything the writer wanted in a tennis match and then some.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/breaking-it-down-ferrer-vs-tipsarevic/', 'snippet': 'David Ferrer’s quarterfinal victory over Janko Tipsarevic was everything the writer wanted in a tennis match and then some.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thank you, Janko. Thank you, David.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Breaking It Down: Ferrer vs. Tipsarevic', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ferrer, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T20:33:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': "By Craig O'Shannessy", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Craig', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Shannessy", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99e7fc09-bf1a-505e-9b25-30b10a63bcfe', 'word_count': 993, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99e7fc09-bf1a-505e-9b25-30b10a63bcfe'}, {'abstract': 'I expected to send my son off to kindergarten this year, but after looking at all the options, I’ve decided to teach him at home.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/why-my-kindergartner-will-stay-home-for-school/', 'snippet': 'I expected to send my son off to kindergarten this year, but after looking at all the options, I’ve decided to teach him at home.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When my son was 2 and a half and our daughter was born, I fantasized about the day I would take him to kindergarten. But by the time he turned 4, he had evolved from a demanding toddler who seemed to wake his sister from every nap to a delightful little boy. We enjoyed each other’s company and I could tell that he was benefiting from our extended time together. Surrendering him to another person’s influence for more than 40 hours a week didn’t hold the same appeal as it once had, and suddenly, I wasn’t sure what to do about school. What seemed like an easy default decision — sign your kid up for kindergarten, and off he goes — felt more complicated when I looked at my son.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why My Kindergartner Will Stay Home for School', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Home Schooling', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T20:38:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicole Russell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicole', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Russell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df8ca1d6-197d-5256-8cc8-f260eaaf1850', 'word_count': 818, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df8ca1d6-197d-5256-8cc8-f260eaaf1850'}, {'abstract': 'Federal prosecutors say that Rajiv Goel, whose testimony helped convict the hedge fund billionaire Raj Rajaratnam of insider trading crimes, deserves a lenient sentence because of his cooperation with the government.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/a-key-witness-in-rajaratnam-trial-is-set-to-be-sentenced/', 'snippet': 'Federal prosecutors say that Rajiv Goel, whose testimony helped convict the hedge fund billionaire Raj Rajaratnam of insider trading crimes, deserves a lenient sentence because of his cooperation with the government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A disgraced former Intel executive whose testimony helped convic