3-329a63f54882'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Roth says the online encyclopedia’s entry for his novel “The Human Stain” contains gossip, not truth.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/philip-roth-goes-public-with-fact-check-of-wikipedia/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Roth says the online encyclopedia’s entry for his novel “The Human Stain” contains gossip, not truth.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Philip Roth has written an open letter to Wikipedia that goes on for nearly as long as some of the celebrated author’s recent short novels. The letter appeared on Page-Turner, the books blog of The New Yorker magazine, and in it Mr. Roth adamantly denies that his novel “The Human Stain” was based on the life of Anatole Broyard, a longtime cultural critic for The Times.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Philip Roth Goes Public With Fact Check of Wikipedia', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Human Stain (Book)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Broyard, Anatole', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roth, Philip', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wikipedia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T21:38:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6faade00-5658-52a5-8b3b-545d175d3d96', 'word_count': 502, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6faade00-5658-52a5-8b3b-545d175d3d96'}, {'abstract': 'A slide show of photographs of cultural events from this week.', 'web_url