 city’s second-most-prominent 9/11 memorial — Fritz Koenig’s “Sphere for Plaza Fountain” sculpture from the original World Trade Center — a guerrilla cleaning crew took matters into its own gloved hands on Thursday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As 9/11 Anniversary Nears, Guerrilla Cleaners Scrub the ‘Sphere’ Memorial', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sculpture From World Trade Center Gets a Bath but Needs a Home', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sculpture', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burke, Michael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National September 11 Memorial and Museum', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Port Authority of New York and New Jersey', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'BATTERY PARK (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T22:04:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Dunlap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Dunlap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/45269750-b744-5e07-a602-763fd5d25c81', 'word_count': 464, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45269750-b744-5e07-a602-763fd5d25c81'}, {'abstract': 'Top-ranked Victoria Azarenka needed almost three hours to outlast Maria Sharapova, 3-6, 6-2, 6-4, but Serena Williams took only 64 minutes to eliminate Sara Errani in the semifinals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/08/sports/tennis/us-open-women-azarenka-sharapova-williams-errani.html', 'snippet': 'Top-ranked Victoria Azarenka needed almost three hours to outlast Maria Sharapova, 3-6, 6-2, 6-4, but Serena Williams took only 64 minutes to eliminate Sara Errani in the semifinals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The women’s final at the United States Open is going to be a test of which is the better way to advance through a draw at a major championship: rolling over everyone in your path, or having to dig for every point in grueling victories. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/08/sports/08open_span_337/08open_span_337-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/08/sports/08open_span_337/08open_span_337-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/08/sports/08open_span_337/08open_span_337-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/08/sports/08open_span_337/08open_span_337-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/08/sports/08open_span_337/08open_span_337-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/08/sports/08open_span_337/08open_span_337-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/08/sports/08open_span_337/08open_span_337-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 132, 'width': 132, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', '