merican Dance Guild.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The performance festival of the American Dance Guild usually honors two dance luminaries a year, one living, one dead. This year, however, both of the honorees — the choreographers Elaine Summers and Dianne McIntyre — are very much alive. And if the performances at the Ailey Citigroup Theater on Thursday weren’t the strongest arguments for the enduring merit of their art, the spirit of happy vitality was just right. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/08/arts/ADG1/ADG1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 384, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/08/arts/ADG1/ADG1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 384}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/08/arts/ADG1/ADG1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 676, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/08/arts/ADG1/ADG1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1351, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/08/arts/ADG1/ADG1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/08/arts/ADG1/ADG1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/08/arts/ADG1/ADG1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '2 Leading Lights, Very Much Alive', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '2 Leading Lights, Very Much Alive', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McIntyre, Dianne', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Dance Guild', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Summers, Elaine', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T22:30:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Seibert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seibert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc8e472b-d297-550a-8c22-9ef0e16c5a29', 'word_count': 583, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc8e472b-d297-550a-8c22-9ef0e16c5a29'}, {'abstract': 'Designers are trying to make fashion more responsive to the way men actually aspire to dress, i.e. to look on-trend but with offhand elegance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/09/t-magazine/editors-letter.html', 'snippet': 'Designers are trying to make fashion more responsive to the way men actually aspire to dress, i.e. to look on-trend but with offhand elegance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This issue is about the fall men’s collections, so perhaps it is best to start with the news: this season, you’ll want a new coat, because there haven’t been so many terrific options in years, but you’ll come to wear it counterintuitively. An impeccably tailored number in the finest cashmere? Pair it for day with knits and slouchy trousers, as the artist Jeremy Everett does under the chic guidance of Bruce Pask. An oversize parka in waterproof nylon? Make like the director Michael Haneke and toss it over your red-carpet suit. If it all sounds a bit mad, consider it thus: in reversing the normal codes of dressing well (evening coat with evening look, casual jacket with casual wear), designers are trying to make fashion more responsive to the way men actually aspire to dress, i.e. to look on-trend but with offhand elegance.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '42', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/t-magazine/09edletter/09edletter-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 825, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/t-magazine/09edletter/09edletter-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1080, 'width': 1341, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/t-magazine/09edletter/09edletter-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/09/t-magazine/09edletter/09edletter-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Editor’s Letter', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Editor’s Letter', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-07T22:30:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sally Singer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sally', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Singer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/732a25f0-cc5d-5206-a378-dac84dc8cb07', 'word_count': 364, 'uri': 'nyt://article/732a25f0-cc5d-5206-a378-dac84dc8cb07'}, {'abstract': 'All the fashion news of the week that’s fit