leen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jacobson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f40dfa34-99ca-5836-8e8e-1d9331a9253a', 'word_count': 1157, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f40dfa34-99ca-5836-8e8e-1d9331a9253a'}, {'abstract': 'Drumming workouts like Pound and Drums Alive are winning converts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/09/fashion/drumming-workouts-win-converts.html', 'snippet': 'Drumming workouts like Pound and Drums Alive are winning converts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CRISTINA PEERENBOOM wasn’t looking to pound away pounds. All she wanted in the summer of 2010 was to escape some romantic drama by disappearing into her drum playing. But the petite Ms. Peerenboom had broken her drum stool standing on it to reach a book, so she spent an hour squatting as she practiced her favorite Rage Against the Machine songs.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/fashion/09DRUMMING1/09DRUMMING1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/09/fashion/09DRUMMING1/09DRUMMING1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/fashion/09DRUMMING1/09DRUMMING1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 597, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/fashion/09DRUMMING1/09DRUMMING1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1194, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/fashion/09DRUMMING1/09DRUMMING1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/09/fashion/09DRUMMING1/09DRUMMING1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/fashion/09DRUMMING1/09DRUMMING1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'They’re Not With the Band', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'They’re Not With the Band', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Clubs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-08T00:55:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Courtney Rubin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Courtney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rubin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/52add400-844f-58d4-853a-0fedd60d60b7', 'word_count': 1479, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52add400-844f-58d4-853a-0fedd60d60b7'}, {'abstract': 'Lincoln and the Civil War, as seen through the eyes of a centenarian veteran of the Revolution.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/father-waldos-america/', 'snippet': 'Lincoln and the Civil War, as seen through the eyes of a centenarian veteran of the Revolution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sleep eluded the clergyman Daniel Waldo during the eve of his 100th birthday on Sept. 10, 1862. The former chaplain of the House of Representatives tossed and turned in bed at his home in Syracuse, lost in thought. What kept him awake were not reflections on his past, but concerns about the future of the Republic. Waldo had lived long enough to know firsthand that the leaders of the Southern rebellion were in deadly earnest, for he himself was once a rebel.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Father Waldo’s America', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chaplains', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Longevity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lincoln, Abraham', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syracuse (NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-08T00:55:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ronald S. Coddington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ronald', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Coddington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a6713a4-dad4-58df-9477-6565fb62ebeb', 'word_count': 1219, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a6713a4-dad4-58df-9477-6565fb62ebeb'}, {'abstract': 'There are no women on the European Central Bank’s executive board, a point that is delaying a hearing to consider the candidacy of Yves Mersch, governor of the Luxembourg central bank.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/08/business/global/european-central-bank-candidacy-delayed-over-lack-of-women.html', 'snippet': 'There are no women on the European Central Bank’s executive board, a point that is delaying a hearing to consider the candidacy of Yves Mersch, governor of the Luxembourg central bank.', 'lead_paragrap