s.com/2012/09/08/opinion/jobs-and-politics.html', 'snippet': 'Republicans have the wrong answers for fixing the weak job market.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Coming two months before Election Day, the employment report for August is a problem for President Obama. The economy added 96,000 jobs last month, a slow pace that lowered the monthly average this year to 139,000, versus 153,000 in 2011. Even the decline in the jobless rate, to 8.1 percent from 8.3 percent in July, was a disappointment, because it indicated a shrinking labor force as people gave up looking for work. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jobs and Politics', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jobs and Politics', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bernanke, Ben S', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-08T01:35:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd4686b5-58cf-594a-8dc7-94565880a9d6', 'word_count': 458, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd4686b5-58cf-594a-8dc7-94565880a9d6'}, {'abstract': 'In a scalding opinion, a Federal District Court judge rejected new rules that limit access to counsel for prisoners at Guantánamo Bay.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/08/opinion/a-court-denounces-executive-fiat.html', 'snippet': 'In a scalding opinion, a Federal District Court judge rejected new rules that limit access to counsel for prisoners at Guantánamo Bay.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a scalding opinion issued on Thursday, Judge Royce Lamberth of Federal District Court rejected new rules imposed by the Obama administration last spring that limit access to counsel for prisoners at Guantánamo Bay, Cuba, who are not actively challenging their detention.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Court Denounces ‘Executive Fiat’', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Court Denounces ‘Executive Fiat’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guantanamo Bay Naval Base (Cuba)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lamberth, Royce C', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classified Information and State Secrets', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-08T01:38:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/90887f61-e581-50ed-99d1-f25f76b29a26', 'word_count': 326, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90887f61-e581-50ed-99d1-f25f76b29a26'}, {'abstract': 'For President Obama, the Democratic National Convention captured his tricky balancing act: a four-year struggle to show that pro-worker does not mean antibusiness.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/08/us/politics/democrats-juggle-a-mixed-message-on-economy.html', 'snippet': 'For President Obama, the Democratic National Convention captured his tricky balancing act: a four-year struggle to show that pro-worker does not mean antibusiness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHARLOTTE, N.C. — With both parties’ conventions now concluded, what is clear is that each played to type — Republicans as the party of business, Democrats of the worker. For President Obama, however, the week here captured his tricky balancing act: a four-year struggle to show that pro-worker does not mean antibusiness.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/08/us/MESSAGE-REPUBS/MESSAGE-REPUBS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/08/us/MESSAGE-REPUBS/MESSAGE-REPUBS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/08/us/MESSAGE-REPUBS/MESSAGE-REPUBS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/08/us/MESSAGE-REPUBS/MESSAGE-REPUBS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/08/us/MESSAGE-REPUBS/MESSAGE-REPUBS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Democrats Face a Juggling Act Over Economy Message', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Democrats Face a Juggling Act Over Jobs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': 