e state primary on June 26, the primary for Congressional seats. The only consolation is that every single vote could make a difference.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York’s Thursday Primary', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New York’s Thursday Primary', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endorsements', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Linares, Guillermo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Espaillat, Adriano', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rozic, Nily', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alabi, Olanike', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Guerrier, Martine', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Iannece, Jerry M', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hoylman, Brad M', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greco, Thomas M', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mosley, Walter T', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-08T01:46:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e866392-915f-5cee-8048-b59a5208f6ac', 'word_count': 458, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e866392-915f-5cee-8048-b59a5208f6ac'}, {'abstract': 'Character matters as much as schoolwork, or maybe even more. And new initiatives are showing how it can be taught.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/08/opinion/nocera-a-ray-of-hope-in-education.html', 'snippet': 'Character matters as much as schoolwork, or maybe even more. And new initiatives are showing how it can be taught.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Early in his acceptance speech Thursday night, President Obama gave a nod to his administration’s backing of education reform. “Some of the worst schools in the country have made real gains in math and reading,” he said, calling on the country to add 100,000 math and science teachers in the next decade. Then he moved on to other topics, like foreign policy and Medicare, that he clearly views as more vital to the campaign as it enters the home stretch.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbLarge-v4.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Reading, Math and Grit', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Reading, Math And Grit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tough, Paul', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'How Children Succeed: Grit, Curiosity, and the Hidden Power of Character (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-08T01:47:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Nocera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nocera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/13a41f2d-6e47-5c25-9504-d83d0924c1ea', 'word_count': 828, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13a41f2d-6e47-5c25-9504-d83d0924c1ea'}, {'abstract': 'Three weeks after making headlines with a game of strip billiards in a Las Vegas hotel suite, Prince Harry, third in line to the British throne, has begun a four-month deployment to Afghanistan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/08/world/europe/britain-prince-harry-begins-new-afghan-deployment.html', 'snippet': 'Three weeks after making headlines with a game of strip billiards in a Las Vegas hotel suite, Prince Harry, third in line to the British throne, has begun a four-month deployment to Afghanistan.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Three weeks after making headlines with a game of strip billiards with a group of women in a Las Vegas hotel suite, Prince Harry, third in line to the British throne, has begun a four-month deployment to Afghanistan as the co-pilot and weapons officer of an Apache attack helicopter. The 27-year-old prince joined his unit of the Army Air Corps at Camp Bastion in Helmand Province, where he will fly combat missions against the Taliban. His previous service in Afghanistan was in 2007 and 2008, when he served 10 weeks as a forward air traffic controller, helping direct strikes on the Taliban. The Apache deployment was one he had lobbied strongly for with British defense chiefs. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Britain: Prince Harry Begins New Afghan Deployment', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Britain: Prince Harry Begins New Afghan Deployment', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Prince Henry of Wales', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-08T01:54:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By John F. Burns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Burns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c058b56-d6a4-5547-8983-286c6ec5fc69', 'word_count': 119, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c058b56-d6a4-5547-8983-286c6ec5fc69'}, {'abstract': 'How I approach a Byron Walden puzzle (Hint: It involves furniture.)', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/lumps/', 'snippet': 'How I approach a Byron Walden puzzle (Hint: It involves furniture.)', 'lead_paragraph': 'SATURDAY’S PUZZLE — Byron Walden puzzles don’t come up in The New York Times that often anymore (he’s a busy dad and a professor of mathematics), but when they do, I treat them as they deserve to be treated: with fear and respect, much as one would approach a wild lion that had suddenly materialized in one’s living room.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Take One’s Lumps', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-08T02:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41808b8f-c329-51f7-8b17-50a199b93143', 'word_count': 424, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41808b8f-c329-51f7-8b17-50a199b93143'}, {'abstract': 'For 13 years, the photographer Anne Deniau had a rare view into the backstage world of Alexander McQueen’s runway shows.Her images are compiled in the new book, “Love Looks Not with the Eyes: Thirteen Years with Lee Alexander McQueen.” Here, a Q. and A. with the photographer.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/07/backstage-mcqueen-q-and-a-with-anne-deniau/', 'snippet': 'For 13 years, the photographer Anne Deniau had a rare view into the backstage world of Alexander McQueen’s runway shows.Her images are compiled in the new book, “Love Looks Not with the Eyes: Thirteen Years with Lee Alexander McQueen.” Here, a Q. ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'For 13 years, the photographer Anne Deniau had a rare view into the backstage world of Alexander McQueen’s runway shows. Hired by the designer to create images that captured the spirit of his collections, she found a perspective on his work that audiences in the front rows never had 