e Empire State.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WATCH out when an academic press approaches a popular subject. Chances are that whatever merriment might have been mined from it will be buried again in footnotes or suffocated by scholarly jargon. In “Queen of Vaudeville: The Story of Eva Tanguay” (Cornell University Press, $29.95), Andrew L. Erdman defies that unfortunate stereotype in resurrecting an early-20th-century celebrity who was suggestively famous as the “I Don’t Care Girl” because she popularized the song “I Don’t Care” and made it her mantra.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/nyregion/09BOOK2/09BOOK2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 711, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/nyregion/09BOOK2/09BOOK2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1042, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/nyregion/09BOOK2/09BOOK2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/09/nyregion/09BOOK2/09BOOK2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/nyregion/09BOOK2/09BOOK2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Queen, a Poem and a Handbook, All Big', 'kicker': 'Bookshelf', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Queen, a Poem and a Handbook, All Big', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'val