'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Visas', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-08T16:48:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Salman Masood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Salman', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Masood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7b3a461-e5ef-589b-825d-546288541b78', 'word_count': 581, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7b3a461-e5ef-589b-825d-546288541b78'}, {'abstract': 'Two months before the election, President Obama and Mitt Romney agree on at least one thing: the collection of states where the race will be decided.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/09/us/politics/obama-romney-battle-plans-set-for-final-charge.html', 'snippet': 'Two months before the election, President Obama and Mitt Romney agree on at least one thing: the collection of states where the race will be decided.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Two months before the election, President Obama and Mitt Romney agree on one thing: the collection of states where the race will be decided.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/us/politics/09campaign_337/09campaign_337-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 716, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/us/politics/09campaign_337/09campaign_337-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1432, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/us/politics/09campaign_337/09campaign_337-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/09/us/politics/09campaign_337/09campaign_337-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Five Crucial Factors to Watch, Just 58 Days From the Election', 'kicker': 'Political Memo', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Five Crucial Factors to Watch, Just 58 Days From the Election', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-08T16:57:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Zeleny and Jim Rutenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zeleny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rutenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6cf8d0aa-cf74-5e0a-ba47-082f255a2ed7', 'word_count': 1902, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6cf8d0aa-cf74-5e0a-ba47-082f255a2ed7'}, {'abstract': 'A mathematical examination of the social networks in three mythological narratives reveals a degree of historical reality for each tale.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/09/opinion/sunday/the-social-networks-of-myths.html', 'snippet': 'A mathematical examination of the social networks in three mythological narratives reveals a degree of historical reality for each tale.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN we pick up a mythological text like “The Iliad” or “Beowulf,” we like to imagine that the societies they describe existed. Even if the stories are fiction, we believe that they tell us something about ancient Greece or the Anglo-Saxons, and that some of the characters and events were based on reality. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/sunday-review/09GRAY/09GRAY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 734, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/sunday-review/09GRAY/09GRAY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1468, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/sunday-review/09GRAY/09GRAY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/09/sunday-review/09GRAY/09GRAY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/sunday-review/09GRAY/09GRAY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'If Achilles Used Facebook...', 'kicker': 'Gray Matter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'If Achilles Used Facebook...', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Iliad (Book)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Myths', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Beowulf (Book)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'EPL (Journal)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Tain Bo Cuailnge (Book)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-08T16:58:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Padraig Mac Carron and Ralph Kenna', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Padraig', 'middlename': 'Mac', 'lastname': 'Carron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ralph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kenna', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/f442975c-2351-5362-8479-48619965ed77', 'word_count': 796, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f442975c-2351-5362-8479-48619965ed77'}, {'abstract': 'Modern biology is making it clearer by the day that a man’s health and well-being have a measurable impact on his future children’s health and happiness.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/09/opinion/sunday/why-fathers-really-matter.html', 'snippet': 'Modern biology is making it clearer by the day that a man’s health and well-being have a measurable impact on his future children’s health and happiness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOTHERHOOD begins as a tempestuously physical experience but quickly becomes a political one. Once a woman’s pregnancy goes public, the storm moves outside. Don’t pile on the pounds! Your child will be obese. Don’t eat too little, or your baby will be born too small. For heaven’s sake, don’t drink alcohol. Oh, please: you can sip some wine now and again. And no matter how many contradictory things the experts say, don’t panic. Stress hormones wreak havoc on a baby’s budding nervous system. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '1', 'source':