show/b5003bb5-d613-5c4d-8095-3c91dfe29d87'}, {'abstract': 'Muhammad Wilkerson and Quinton Coples, defensive linemen who played together in military school, were the Jets’ top draft picks in consecutive years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/09/sports/football/side-by-side-inside-2-young-linemen-energize-the-jets.html', 'snippet': 'Muhammad Wilkerson and Quinton Coples, defensive linemen who played together in military school, were the Jets’ top draft picks in consecutive years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FLORHAM PARK, N.J. — That Muhammad Wilkerson’s teammates and coaches on the Jets rave about his modesty does not seem to surprise Robert Prunty, who remembers his reaction the day players at Hargrave Military Academy were given three ham sandwiches as part of their lunch to eat during a six-hour trip to Annapolis, Md. As a practicing Muslim, Wilkerson cannot have pork. So he ate his apple and his cookies, and he drank his milk, and he did not complain. He did not even tell his coach.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/sports/dogYJETS/dogYJETS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/09/sports/dogYJETS/dogYJETS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/sports/dogYJETS/dogYJETS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 630, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/sports/dogYJETS/dogYJETS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1260, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/sports/dogYJETS/dogYJETS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/09/sports/dogYJETS/dogYJETS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/sports/dogYJETS/dogYJETS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '2 Jets Defensive Linemen Hope Reunion Continues at the Quarterback', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '2 Jets Defensive Linemen Hope Reunion Continues at the Quarterback', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coples, Quinton (1990- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Rex', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilkerson, Muhammad', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-08T18:54:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/164dabf2-97c0-5db5-b005-6a50fbed8e3a', 'word_count': 1043, 'uri': 'nyt://article/164dabf2-97c0-5db5-b005-6a50fbed8e3a'}, {'abstract': 'For most of us, work is a means to something else: it makes a living, but it doesn’t make a life. So shouldn’t leisure be our goal?', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/08/work-good-or-bad/', 'snippet': 'For most of us, work is a means to something else: it makes a living, but it doesn’t make a life. So shouldn’t leisure be our goal?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Is work good or bad?\xa0 A fatuous question, it may seem, with unemployment such a pressing national concern.\xa0 (Apart from the names of the two candidates, “jobs” was the politically relevant word most used by speakers at the Republican and Democratic conventions.)\xa0Even apart from current worries, the goodness of work is deep in our culture. We applaud people for their work ethic, judge our economy by its productivity and even honor work with a national holiday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Work Is Really For', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capitalism (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Productivity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Russell, Bertrand', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-08T19:00:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gary Gutting', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gutting', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a0818c8c-db24-5246-aef5-586500cabb3a', 'word_count': 1265, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a0818c8c-db24-5246-aef5-586500cabb3a'}, {'abstract': 'Before an audience that included a first daughter, Barbara Bush, and the already reigning young actresses of this runway season (Allison Williams, Hailee Steinfeld and Kate Bosworth), Prabal Gurung showed a spring collection that seemed to be trying to straddle the fence between uptown and downtown.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/08/prabal-gurung-calm-before-the-storm/', 'snippet': 'Before an audience that included a first daughter, Barbara Bush, and the already reigning young actresses of this runway season (Allison Williams, Hailee Steinfeld and Kate Bosworth), Prabal Gurung showed a spring collection that seemed to be tryi...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before an audience that included a first daughter, Barbara Bush, as well as a few socialites and the already reigning young actresses of this runway season (Allison Williams, Hailee Steinfeld and Kate Bosworth), Prabal Gurung showed a spring collection that seemed to be trying to straddle the fence between uptown and downtown. It started with street-tough outfits of layered trousers, sheer undershirts with an ominous bird-wing print, artfully folded skirts and an asymmetrical jacket or two — all in black and white — which had me thinking I was at the wrong show. Did I end up at Alexander Wang by mistake?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Prabal Gurung: Calm Before the Storm', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gurung, Prabal', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-08T19:01:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ff6342d-98ec-5e30-b4ef-b427cd4e7558', 'word_count': 239, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ff6342d-98ec-5e30-b4ef-b427cd4e7558'}, {'abstract': 'So far, eight people out of the thousands who visited the park this summer have been infected with the mouse-borne virus, which has no known cure.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/09/us/third-hantavirus-death-prompts-wider-warning.html', 'snippet': 'So far, eight people out of the thousands who visited the park this summer have been infected with the mouse-borne virus, which has no known cure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After the death last week of a third person exposed to the deadly mouse-borne hantavirus, public health officials were expanding their warning to include more than 22,000 visitors to Yosemite National Park.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wider Warning After 3rd Yosemite Hantavirus Death', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wider Warning After 3rd Yosemite Hantavirus Death', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hantavirus', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yosemite National Park', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-08T19:03:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marc Santora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06d2e127-5f8f-5ff6-9dcf-c7e57329847a', 'word_count': 737, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06d2e127-5f8f-5ff6-9dcf-c7e57329847a'}, {'abstract': 'After years in baseball’s doldrums the Orioles are in contention in the American League East, taking their veteran TV broadcaster Gary Thorne along for the wild ride.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/09/sports