ddlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cieply', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0053a5eb-3078-58f1-9307-c770ebc1c016', 'word_count': 299, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0053a5eb-3078-58f1-9307-c770ebc1c016'}, {'abstract': 'This Sunday, Representative Paul D. Ryan will hunker down for his first full day of debate preparation before facing off against Vice President Joseph R. Biden Jr.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/08/ryan-to-spend-sunday-preparing-for-debate-with-biden/', 'snippet': 'This Sunday, Representative Paul D. Ryan will hunker down for his first full day of debate preparation before facing off against Vice President Joseph R. Biden Jr.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Each day the briefing books have grown fatter. At home in Wisconsin last Sunday, he watched a tape of Sarah Palin’s 2008 debate. And this Sunday, Representative Paul D. Ryan will hunker down for his first full day of debate prep before he faces off against Vice President Joseph R. Biden Jr. next month.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ryan to Spend Sunday Preparing for Debate With Biden', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vice Presidents and Vice Presidency (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-08T19:27:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Trip Gabriel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Trip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f87abdd-3313-55eb-a111-51e954fd04dd', 'word_count': 401, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f87abdd-3313-55eb-a111-51e954fd04dd'}, {'abstract': 'Readers comment on my column about agriculture, and a dairy farm that keeps cows happy and milk healthy.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/08/when-happy-cows-produce-happy-milk/', 'snippet': 'Readers comment on my column about agriculture, and a dairy farm that keeps cows happy and milk healthy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My Sunday column takes a break from politics and looks at something even more basic: food. Regular readers know that I’m distressed by what’s happening in rural America and the way we’re drifting to vast corporate food factories that produce food that tastes plastic and raises public health concerns. Yet the defenders of industrial farming point out, correctly, that their system does produce food that is very cheap at the grocery store. They argue that family farms just can’t compete and are an anachronism in the 21st century.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Happy Cows Produce Happy Milk', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-08T19:32:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1dbf38c3-80af-51b9-9f0e-acb2291943ad', 'word_count': 197, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1dbf38c3-80af-51b9-9f0e-acb2291943ad'}, {'abstract': 'T plucks the best shoes right off the runway. Today’s shoe: a blue snakeskin, half-wedge slash heel.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/08/the-daily-shoe-helmut-lang/', 'snippet': 'T plucks the best shoes right off the runway. Today’s shoe: a blue snakeskin, half-wedge slash heel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'T plucks the best shoes right off the runway.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Daily Shoe | Helmut Lang', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shoes and Boots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lang, Helmut', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-08T19:33:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane Herman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Herman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb6c0466-0ab9-54ff-8d6e-6c55cd7a40a0', 'word_count': 95, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb6c0466-0ab9-54ff-8d6e-6c55cd7a40a0'}, {'abstract': 'Federal officials will determine whether comments suggesting that there would be budget cuts if Republicans keep control of Congress constituted political pressure to vote for Democrats.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/09/us/politics/faa-officer-in-inquiry-over-remark-seen-as-partisan.html', 'snippet': 'Federal officials will determine whether comments suggesting that there would be budget cuts if Republicans keep control of Congress constituted political pressure to vote for Democrats.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — A senior Federal Aviation Administration official told subordinates there would be budget cuts that could lead to furloughs if Republicans held control of Congress, and federal investigators are determining whether the remarks constituted political pressure to vote for Democrats, a person with knowledge of the inquiry said on Saturday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Inquiry Starts at F.A.A. Over Remark on Budget', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Inquiry Starts At F.A.A. Over Remark On Budget', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Aviation Administration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Mail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hickey, John', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hatch Act (1939)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Office of Special Counsel', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-08T19:33:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sheryl Gay Stolberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sheryl', 'middlename': 'Gay', 'lastname': 'Stolberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5574ee71-1b00-5a15-9ae4-88b961d81f88', 'word_count': 400, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5574ee71-1b00-5a15-9ae4-88b961d81f88'}, {'abstract': 'The Singer Bowl, which was built for the 1964-65 World’s Fair, then divided and incorporated into the National Tennis Center, had an eclectic history before the United States Open.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/09/sports/tennis/armstrong-back-when-it-wasnt-tennis-rocking-the-house.html', 'snippet': 'The Singer Bowl, which was built for the 1964-65 World’s Fair, then divided and incorporated into the National Tennis Center, had an eclectic history before the United States Open.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is fair to say that nearly every top-ranked tennis player during the last three decades has played at least one match at Louis Armstrong Memorial Stadium, the second-largest venue at the National Tennis Center in Flushing. Thousands more have faced off at the Grandstand, a smaller locale attached to Armstrong.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/sports/dog-sub-stadium-1/dog-sub-stadium-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 672, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/sports/dog-sub-stadium-1/dog-sub-stadium-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1345, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Armstrong, Back When It Wasn’t Tennis Rocking the House', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Armstrong, Back When It Wasn&#8217;t Tennis Rocking the House', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stadiums and Arenas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Tennis Center', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Tennis Assn', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-08T19:35:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifie