soners to be organ donors could make transplants available to many Texans on the waiting lists, but the prospect is fraught with moral, ethical and medical challenges.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/09/us/considering-the-ethics-of-organ-donations-from-death-row.html', 'snippet': 'Allowing executed prisoners to be organ donors could make transplants available to many Texans on the waiting lists, but the prospect is fraught with moral, ethical and medical challenges.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before Gov. John Kitzhaber of Oregon established a moratorium on his state’s death penalty last year, Christian Longo, a death row inmate, started a campaign to allow the condemned to donate their organs.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Considering Death Row for Organs', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Considering Death Row For Organs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organ Donation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transplants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-08T22:47:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brandi Grissom', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brandi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grissom', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/018cf0fe-849f-59b5-9c23-8c8640c730f9', 'word_count': 521, 'uri': 'nyt://article/018cf0fe-849f-59b5-9c23-8c8640c730f9'}, {'abstract': 'Afghanistan’s estimated $1 trillion in untapped mineral resources seems i