ress conference here on Saturday afternoon.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Toronto, Moviegoers Waiting to See ‘The Master’ Ask What It’s About', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Toronto International Film Festival', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANDERSON, PAUL THOMAS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hoffman, Philip Seymour', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Phoenix, Joaquin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Church of Scientology', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Toronto (Ontario)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venice (Italy)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-09T04:30:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cieply', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cieply', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6ebb4d6-c28e-5c40-9f49-5cd99e61d132', 'word_count': 303, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6ebb4d6-c28e-5c40-9f49-5cd99e61d132'}, {'abstract': 'When the United States last week declared the Haqqani network in Afghanistan to be a terrorist organization, the Taliban’s reaction was angry, swift and deadly. Noting the close ties between the Haqqanis and Pakistan’s main spy agency, some analysts saw a possibility that Pakistan itself might some day be declared a state sponsor of terrorism.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/09/taliban-rages-over-u-s-decision-on-terrorist-group/', 'snippet': 'When the United States last week declared the Haqqani network in Afghanistan to be a terrorist organization, the Taliban’s reaction was angry, swift and deadly. Noting the close ties between the Haqqanis and Pakistan’s main spy agency, some analys...', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — Washington has formally branded the Haqqani network a foreign terrorist organization for its attacks against American and NATO forces and for its role in the Taliban superstructure in Afghanistan. The Taliban’s response? Angry, swift and deadly.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/blogs/haq-rdv/haq-rdv-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 817, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/09/blogs/haq-rdv/haq-rdv-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1582, 'width': 1982, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Taliban Rages Over U.S. Decision on Terrorist Group', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Haqqani Network', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'No Easy Day: The Firsthand Account of the Mission That Killed Osama bin Laden (Book)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-09T05:29:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark McDonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McDonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/911a4bec-977c-5052-86f9-c883f1002bf5', 'word_count': 1105, 'uri': 'nyt://article/911a4bec-977c-5052-86f9-c883f1002bf5'}, {'abstract': 'Lewis Hamilton and Jenson Button were the fastest drivers during qualifying on Saturday for the Italian Grand Prix. The relatively flat course at Monza, unlike the wet, hilly and sometimes scary track at Spa last week, is the fastest of the season.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/09/the-control-freaks-behind-the-wheel/', 'snippet': 'Lewis Hamilton and Jenson Button were the fastest drivers during qualifying on Saturday for the Italian Grand Prix. The relatively flat course at Monza, unlike the wet, hilly and sometimes scary track at Spa last week, is the fastest of the season...', 'lead_paragraph': 'MONZA, Italy — For the third time this season the two McLaren Mercedes drivers qualified first and second on the grid — Lewis Hamilton edging out his teammate, Jenson Button, for pole position at the Italian Grand Prix. The two drivers are certainly on a roll, as Hamilton won the Hungarian Grand Prix at the end of July before the summer break, and Button won the Belgian Grand Prix last weekend, the first event after racing resumed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The ‘Control Freaks’ Behind the Wheel', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fear (Emotion)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Button, Jenson', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Formula One', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name