-9fbd98504bb4', 'word_count': 908, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5704b17b-70d7-5746-b5d1-9fbd98504bb4'}, {'abstract': 'The ATP Player Council, with Roger Federer as its president, is pushing for more prize money at Grand Slam tournaments in an attempt to address an earning gap in a top-heavy sport.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/10/sports/tennis/10iht-arena10.html', 'snippet': 'The ATP Player Council, with Roger Federer as its president, is pushing for more prize money at Grand Slam tournaments in an attempt to address an earning gap in a top-heavy sport.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There were rain delays and lost sessions at the United States Open, pushed again to a Monday men’s final. There was a tornado warning and a chair blown onto the court in the midst of the men’s semifinal between Tomas Berdych and Andy Murray, the eventual champion.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/12/sports/YCLAREY/YCLAREY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 702, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/12/sports/YCLAREY/YCLAREY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1404, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/12/sports/YCLAREY/YCLAREY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/12/sports/YCLAREY/YCLAREY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/12/sports/YCLAREY/YCLAREY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Off Court, Tennis Stars Are Putting Pressure on the Grand Slams', 'kicker': 'On Tennis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Off Court, Stars Are Pressuring Grand Slams', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sampras, Pete', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Australian Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Federer, Roger', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-09T12:47:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Clarey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clarey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d2c26ae-215f-5959-ac9b-9a9cfe68805f', 'word_count': 1493, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d2c26ae-215f-5959-ac9b-9a9cfe68805f'}, {'abstract': 'If the school hasn’t imposed a limit on bra tops or T-shirts with dubious slogans, should parents?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/09/should-parents-impose-a-dress-code/', 'snippet': 'If the school hasn’t imposed a limit on bra tops or T-shirts with dubious slogans, should parents?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2009-10, about 57 percent of public school principals reported that their schools enforced a dress code. The codes themselves vary; some rules are intended to promote modesty (skirts and shorts must extend beyond fingertips; there can be no spaghetti straps) and others to encourage a respectful learning environment (no jeans; no screen prints or text on shirts).', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Should Parents Impose a Dress Code?', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'You’re Not Wearing That to School', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-09T13:00:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34ee7725-9ee0-5df7-b64d-63ae8a6a8ba4', 'word_count': 401, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34ee7725-9ee0-5df7-b64d-63ae8a6a8ba4'}, {'abstract': 'The design and the execution of this particular dress, created with peplumed linens, blue silk, Swarovski crystals and sunburst embroideries, proved to be very complex.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/09/dress-code-joseph-altuzarra/', 'snippet': 'The design and the execution of this particular dress, created with peplumed linens, blue silk, Swarovski crystals and sunburst embroideries, proved to be very complex.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dress Code | Altuzarra', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Fashion Week', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Altuzarra, Joseph', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-09T13:00:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e601d29d-fe23-58c2-ae66-6370a6b2c784', 'word_count': 309, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e601d29d-fe23-58c2-ae66-6370a6b2c784'}, {'abstract': 'Top magazine and long-form articles this week.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/09/newswallah-long-reads-edition-41/', 'snippet': 'Top magazine and long-form articles this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Politics and political leaders dominated the magazine covers this week. Prime Minister Manmohan Singh found himself at the center of many stories that highlighted his government’s predicament and his own loss of credibility. Outlook’s cover carried the words “King is Singed,” a play on the title of a popular Indian movie. “Manmohan Singh’s integrity was the Congress’s USP in 2009,” it read. “By making the P.M. the target of the coal scam, the BJP has turned the middle-class mascot into an electoral liability ahead of 2014,” when the country will hold its next national elections. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Newswallah: Long Reads Edition', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-09T13:41:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Niharika Mandhana', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Niharika', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mandhana', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/870d823c-3dd0-5ebf-a2bf-37a2f9152a72', 'word_count': 577, 'uri': 'nyt://article/870d823c-3dd0-5ebf-a2bf-37a2f9152a72'}, {'abstract': 'Born in Alabama and raised in Iceland, Aron Johannsson’s string start in Denmark’s Superliga may attract the attention of two national teams.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/09/americans-abroad-aron-johannsson-starts-strong/', 'snippet': 'Born in Alabama and raised in Iceland, Aron Johannsson’s string start in Denmark’s Superliga may attract the attention of two national teams.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While most of the top leagues in Europe are taking an early break for the FIFA international window, the first eight games of the Danish Superliga season already has some great stories. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Americans Abroad: Aron Johannsson Starts Strong', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "United States Men's National Soccer Team", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-09T14:00:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Sciaretta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sciaretta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a787e87-3c3c-5ec2-927a-c5fa4dd71c3e', 'word_count': 787, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a787e87-3c3c-5ec2-927a-c5fa4dd71c3e'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney says there are parts of President Obama’s health care reform that he likes.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/09/romney-would-keep-some-of-obamas-health-care-reform/', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney says there are parts of President Obama’s health care reform that he likes.', 'lead_paragraph': '3:09 p.m. | Updated Mitt Romney said Sunday that he would retain elements of President Obama’s health care overhaul, blamed Republicans as much as Democrats for the “mistake” of agreeing to automatic cuts in military spending to avoid a fiscal crisis and acknowledged that Mr. Obama’s national security strategy has made America in “some ways safer.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney Has Conciliatory Remarks on Obama and Health Overhaul', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Democratic National Convention', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Republican National Convention', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speeches and Statements', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gregory, David', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Ann', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN LEGION', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 18, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Weekly Standard', 'rank': 19, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 20, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tampa (Fla)', 'rank': 21, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-09T14:12:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Barbaro and Jim Rutenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barbaro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rutenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fee6efa-d607-51a8-9512-d89d9dfde693', 'word_count': 1016, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fee6efa-d607-51a8-9512-d89d9dfde693'}, {'abstract': 'A clean, matte complexion and ponytail with a taped center-part complemented the minimalist nature of Alexander Wang’s Spring 2013 collection.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/09/backstage-beauty-report-alexander-wang-2/', 'snippet': 'A clean, matte complexion and ponytail with a taped center-part complemented the minimalist nature of Alexander Wang’s Spring 2013 collection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Look: Modern MinimalismThe Makeup: The makeup artist Diane Kendal opted for a clean, matte complexion to complement the minimalist nature of Alexander Wang’s Spring 2013 collection. Skin was first primed with NarsSkin Optimal Brightening Concentrate, then coated with the brand’s Pure Radiant Tinted Moisturizer SPF 30/PA+++. Next, using a contoured blush brush (in place of the classic, dome-shaped powder brush), Kendal applied two shades of Nars Sheer Glow Powder Foundation — a lighter one on the outside of the face and a darker one across the cheeks — to perfect. (At press time, Kendal was not at liberty to disclose why, but a selection of models were given a more futuristic finish using Nars Light Reflecting Loose Setting Powder and Albatross Highlighting Blush on the high points of their cheeks, with some also sporting bleached or whited-out brows.) Eyes were contoured using Cayenne eyeshadow, while the same product in Blondie (light) or Bali (dark) were used to fill in the brows. Lashes were left bare.The Hair: “Ponytails are always very prevalent in New York,” says the stylist Guido Palau. “Half my career has been based on trying to reinvent it.” For Wang’s presentation, Palau used a variation on a look he’d originally conceived in the early ’90s: the taped center-part. To modernize the look, the stylist opted for dual texture — a sleek top with movement in the back — and low positioning. To achieve this, the top of the head (to behind the ears) was first dampened, then parted and treated with Redken Satinwear 02 Ultimate Blow-Dry Lotion before being blown straight. Once secured into a ponytail, the ends were sectioned and curled.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Backstage Beauty Report | Alexander Wang', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-09T14:30:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lily Nima', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nima', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b933dc81-cd7f-5681-b58a-51f694dea728', 'word_count': 383, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b933dc81-cd7f-5681-b58a-51f694dea728'}, {'abstract': 'Way down.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/09/government-employment/', 'snippet': 'Way down.', 'lead_paragraph': 'During today’s round table on ABC, Rand Paul seemed shocked at my claim that government employment is down under Obama. Of course, it is. But maybe he’s thinking of the fact that since govt employment rose under Bush, we’re still at higher absolute levels than we were a decade ago.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Government Employment', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-09T14:40:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc4d8add-0768-5f80-b7d9-6463be57c38f', 'word_count': 99, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc4d8add-0768-5f80-b7d9-6463be57c38f'}, {'abstract': 'Gretchen Reynolds, the Phys Ed columnist, talks about the latest research and a promising exercise to combat the pain of tennis elbow.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/health/100000001768943/a-fix-for-tennis-elbow.html', 'snippet': 'Gretchen Reynolds, the Phys Ed columnist, talks about the latest research and a promising exercise to combat the pain of tennis elbow.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gretchen Reynolds, the Phys Ed columnist, talks about the latest research and a promising exercise to combat the pain of tennis elbow.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/science/video-phys-ed-ten