M.A.C. Archie’s Collection Spoiled Rich palette in Ron Ron Ron (using the #266 brush),then finished with a line of Technakohl Liner in Auto-de-Blu — drawn to the curve of the lid, with no extension — and a swipe of Haute & Naughty Lash mascara.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Backstage Beauty Report | Altuzarra', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-09T19:30:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lily Nima', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nima', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fdf61bb6-cd8d-52a9-a5f9-189a172a2e04', 'word_count': 295, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fdf61bb6-cd8d-52a9-a5f9-189a172a2e04'}, {'abstract': 'Lawmakers, fresh off their parties’ conventions, appear to favor action this fall on bills that emphasize their political agendas over actual lawmaking.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/10/us/politics/congress-to-face-angry-farmers.html', 'snippet': 'Lawmakers, fresh off their parties’ conventions, appear to favor action this fall on bills that emphasize their political agendas over actual lawmaking.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — When Congress returns to business this week, it will be met not by the Code Pink antiwar protesters or the Tea Party supporters who often gathered near the Capitol last year. Instead, farmers will be out in force, rallying for a bill that lawmakers failed to pass before they recessed five weeks ago. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Congress Comes Back to a Face-Off With Angry Farmers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Congress 