program, “Men, Maids and Mischief: Bawdy English Songs,” included drinking songs and tales by Purcell, Weelkes, Eccles and others.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/10/arts/music/musica-nuova-at-jimmys-no-43.html', 'snippet': 'Musica Nuova’s fast-paced program, “Men, Maids and Mischief: Bawdy English Songs,” included drinking songs and tales by Purcell, Weelkes, Eccles and others.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The classical-music club scene in New York grows ever livelier. Though “grows” may seem an odd word applied to the tiny performance space at Jimmy’s No. 43, a basement bar and restaurant in the East Village. Musica Nuova, a spunky Boston-born early-music ensemble, opened its second New York season at Jimmy’s on Thursday evening with a fast-paced, 50-minute program, “Men, Maids and Mischief: Bawdy English Songs,” and delivered the goods (bads?) handsomely. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/10/arts/sub-musica/sub-musica-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 356, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/10/arts/sub-musica/sub-musica-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 356}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/10/arts/sub-musica/sub-musica-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 666, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/10/arts/sub-musica/sub-musica-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1332, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/10/arts/sub-musica/sub-musica-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width'