, 'lead_paragraph': 'The Treasury Department said on Sunday that it was planning its biggest sale of shares in the American International Group to date, making the federal government a minority shareholder in the bailed-out insurer for the first time since it took control of the company four years ago.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Treasury to Cut A.I.G. Stake Below 50%', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Treasury To Reduce A.I.G. Stake Below 50%', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN INTERNATIONAL GROUP INC', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Treasury Department', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-09T21:55:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/10882e06-abd1-57d5-b573-f75ffce5b323', 'word_count': 741, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10882e06-abd1-57d5-b573-f75ffce5b323'}, {'abstract': 'Soul artists like Jessie Ware and AlunaGeorge manage to have an R&B sound that is British.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/10/arts/music/british-soul-offshoots-evolve-fitfully.html', 'snippet': 'Soul artists like Jessie Ware and AlunaGeorge manage to have an R&B sound that is British.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The desperate center of Jessie Ware’s debut album, “Devotion,” is “Taking In Water,” a languorous and arresting tragedy about punishing oneself so that someone less worthy might live. Over gaseous, melancholy synths Ms. Ware unfurls her tale heavily.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 