ne, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-10T01:14:01+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Fashion & Style', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': "Women's Runway", 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/242003b5-2926-5963-bbfd-124629175c4c', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/242003b5-2926-5963-bbfd-124629175c4c'}, {'abstract': 'The ensemble of crickets on late summer nights sounds like the end of a season, and like the start of one, too.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/10/opinion/the-roar-of-the-night.html', 'snippet': 'The ensemble of crickets on late summer nights sounds like the end of a season, and like the start of one, too.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1899, Dr. Robert Thaxter Edes, a Harvard graduate and Civil War veteran, noted that “the tree cricket does not say much in the daytime.” Dr. Edes was trying to calibrate the change in the pitch of a tree cricket’s note as the temperature changes. He offered a graph but not the actual pitches. F. H. Hall, writing in 1912, was more specific. The song is “a clear mellow whistle resembling the words treat, treat, treat, pitched about in C, two octaves above middle C, on a warm evening rising to D.” One species sings a half pitch higher and another “about F# on an average summer evening.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Roar of the Night', 'kicker': 'The Rural Life', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Roar of the Night', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seasons and Months', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crickets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Summer (Season)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-10T01:14:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Verlyn Klinkenborg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Verlyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Klinkenborg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/f748d285-c704-58d8-8b6b-d4de0107bec2', 'word_count': 350, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f748d285-c704-58d8-8b6b-d4de0107bec2'}, {'abstract': 'Interactive One, a digital media company best known for creating content for African-Americans, is set to announce on Monday that it has started Zona De Sabor, a Web site aimed at urban Latinos.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/09/interactive-ones-site-for-latinos/', 'snippet': 'Interactive One, a digital media company best known for creating content for African-Americans, is set to announce on Monday that it has started Zona De Sabor, a Web site aimed at urban Latinos.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Interactive One, a digital media company best known for creating content for African-Americans, is set to announce on Monday that it has started a Web site aimed at urban Latinos.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Interactive One’s Site for Latinos', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Interactive One’s Site for Latinos', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TV One', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-10T01:16:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tanzina Vega', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tanzina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vega', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ab4a910-92f7-52b2-902a-29c3d34f6300', 'word_count': 327, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ab4a910-92f7-52b2-902a-29c3d34f6300'}, {'abstract': 'The recent election was more about ousting the tired and corruption-tainted Liberal Party than about independence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/10/opinion/separatist-victory-in-quebec-but-not-separation.html', 'snippet': 'The recent election was more about ousting the tired and corruption-tainted Liberal Party than about independence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the past four decades, proponents of an independent Quebec have fought a political battle with the federalist Liberals without achieving, or putting to rest, the separatists’ dream of an independent French-speaking state. Last Tuesday, Quebecers again voted into office the Parti Québécois, whose purpose since its formation in 1968 has been separatism. This time separatism is not a serious prospect. Nor was it the main issue in the election. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Separatist Victory, but Not Separation', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Separatist Victory, but Not Separation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Quebec Province (Canada)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Parti Quebecois (Canada)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marois, Pauline', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Liberal Party (Canada)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Charest, Jean', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-10T01:17:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/e793d4db-e454-5c11-baef-d9a38964b2fa', 'word_count': 362, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e793d4db-e454-5c11-baef-d9a38964b2fa'}, {'abstract': 'Voters turned out in big numbers after a controversy over a government plan to introduce mandatory pro-Beijing patriotic education in Hong Kong schools.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/10/world/asia/hong-kong-voting-for-legislature-is-heavy.html', 'snippet': 'Voters turned out in big numbers after a controversy over a government plan to introduce mandatory pro-Beijing patriotic education in Hong Kong schools.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — Pro-democracy candidates won strong voter support in legislative elections here on Sunday, but came away with fewer seats than expected because pro-Beijing political parties with greater financial resources proved more skillful in navigating Hong Kong’s complex electoral system.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/10/world/sub-hong-kong/sub-hong-kong-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/10/world/sub-hong-kong/sub-hong-kong-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/10/world/sub-hong-kong/sub-hong-kong-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0,