ood of unlimited independent spending in political campaigns. It has also inspired a wave of lawsuits seeking to overturn the reasonable campaign finance restrictions that remain on the books in various states. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corporate Contributions and Disclosure', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corporate Contributions and Disclosure', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizens United v Federal Election Commission (Supreme Court Decision)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Minnesota', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-10T01:24:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f83dc66-9fe5-5188-b01d-778ee1402795', 'word_count': 368, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f83dc66-9fe5-5188-b01d-778ee1402795'}, {'abstract': 'Account assignments, executive appointments and miscellaneous news from advertising agencies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/10/business/media/news-from-the-advertising-industry.html', 'snippet': 'Account assignments, executive appointments and miscellaneous news from advertising agencies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Accounts', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News From the Advertising Industry', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'News From the Advertising Industry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'maj