lfiger’s men’s collection, his women’s wear had a lot of rope stripes – red ones, blue ones, white ones – running up and down suits and flowing trapeze dresses in multiple fabrics.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/09/textured-sportswear-at-tommy-hilfiger/', 'snippet': 'Like Mr. Hilfiger’s men’s collection, his women’s wear had a lot of rope stripes – red ones, blue ones, white ones – running up and down suits and flowing trapeze dresses in multiple fabrics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Sunday night, Tommy Hilfiger took over a long portion of the High Line north of West 14th Street, building a runway that looked like a boardwalk with hundreds of illuminated lanterns dangling from an overhang. It was a beautiful setting for a collection he called “American Voyage,” which had a nautical theme and resembled a big Hamptons-style beach wedding.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Textured Sportswear at Tommy Hilfiger', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hilfiger, Tommy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-10T01:58:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1dafa06-94ed-5abd-8f5a-5f73707a1fa3', 'word_count': 171, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1dafa06-94ed-5abd-8f5a-5f73707a1fa3'}, {'abstract': 'The winning lottery numbers for New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/10/nyregion/lottery-numbers-for-new-york-new-jersey-and-connecticut.html', 'snippet': 'The winning lottery numbers for New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sept. 9, 2012', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lottery Numbers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lottery Numbers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lotteries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-10T01:58:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/df90bb27-fae2-5ce2-a7ce-81e28faf722e', 'word_count': 180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df90bb27-fae2-5ce2-a7ce-81e28faf722e'}, {'abstract': '“The Train Driver,” written and directed by Athol Fugard, tells how a death on the tracks has left the train operator emotionally scarred.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/10/theater/reviews/athol-fugards-train-driver-from-signature-theater.html', 'snippet': '“The Train Driver,” written and directed by Athol Fugard, tells how a death on the tracks has left the train operator emotionally scarred.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A ghost haunts the graveyard setting of “The Train Driver,” the latest play by Athol Fugard, which opened Sunday night at the Pershing Square Signature Center in a production directed by the playwright. This particular specter is made of flesh and blood. Roelf Visagie (Ritchie Coster) is unquestionably a living man, and yet there is something hollowed out about his presence, as if the soul that once inhabited his body has withered away, leaving an echoing emptiness behind. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'm