jor races just over a month after his doping ban ended. Contador easily navigated the largely processional final leg, into and around Madrid, to edge out Alejandro Valverde and Joaquim Rodríguez in the 21-stage race. Valverde, the 2009 winner, finished 1 minute 16 seconds behind. Rodríguez was 1:38 back. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Contador Wins Second Vuelta', 'kicker': 'Sports Briefing | Cycling', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Contador Wins Second Vuelta', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Contador, Alberto', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vuelta a Espana (Bicycle Race)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doping (Sports)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cycling, Road', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bicycles and Bicycling', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-10T04:56:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Cycling', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/f615113a-cbfc-589c-98b0-fa79691668d0', 'word_count': 124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f615113a-cbfc-589c-98b0-fa79691668d0'}, {'abstract': 'Lars Petter Nordhaug of Norway held off the field to win the Grand Prix Cycliste de Montreal, one of the final events in cycling’s elite World Tour series.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/10/sports/cycling/norwegian-takes-montreal-race.html', 'snippet': 'Lars Petter Nordhaug of Norway held off the field to win the Grand Prix Cycliste de Montreal, one of the final events in cycling’s elite World Tour series.', 'lead_