raph': 'Here’s Gabby Douglas illustrating Mitt Romney’s position on coverage of Americans with pre-existing conditions:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Health Care Gymnastics', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-10T13:08:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bdcc638f-bb3b-55bc-b824-56f2d4189981', 'word_count': 56, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bdcc638f-bb3b-55bc-b824-56f2d4189981'}, {'abstract': 'The Day: Before the Sept. 11 anniversary, taking a glimpse of the summer’s gun violence in New York City.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/10/remembering-victims-of-a-summer-of-terror/', 'snippet': 'The Day: Before the Sept. 11 anniversary, taking a glimpse of the summer’s gun violence in New York City.', 'lead_paragraph': ' This is the season for reciting, and remembering, the names of terror’s victims in New York. There is no need, though, to wait for a ceremony like the one planned for Tuesday to call the roll. Dispensing with alphabetical order, the tragic roster can begin like this: ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Remembering Victims of a Summer of Terror', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-10T13:09:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clyde Haberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clyde', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d1c8b08-13d1-5c2c-82d9-59da071bafcf', 'word_count': 799, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d1c8b08-13d1-5c2c-82d9-59da071bafcf'}, {'abstract': 'The strike left 350,000 children without classes, and placed both the powerful teachers’ union and Mayor Rahm Emanuel in a risky standoff.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/11/education/teacher-strike-begins-in-chicago-amid-signs-that-deal-isnt-close.html', 'snippet': 'The strike left 350,000 children without classes, and placed both the powerful teachers’ union and Mayor Rahm Emanuel in a risky standoff.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — This city found itself engulfed on Monday by a sudden public school strike that left 350,000 children without classes, turned a spotlight on rising tensions nationally over teachers’ circumstances, and placed both the powerful teachers’ union and Mayor Rahm Emanuel in a risky, politically fraught standoff with no clear end in sight. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/11/us/jp-STRIKE-1/jp-STRIKE-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/11/us/jp-STRIKE-1/jp-STRIKE-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/11/us/jp-STRIKE-1/jp-STRIKE-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 694, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/11/us/jp-STRIKE-1/jp-STRIKE-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1389, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/11/us/jp-STRIKE-1/jp-STRIKE-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/11/us/jp-STRIKE-1/jp-STRIKE-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Teachers’ Strike in Chicago Tests Mayor and Union', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Teachers’ Strike In Chicago Tests Mayor and Union', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Teachers Union', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Strikes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Emanuel, Rahm', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-10T13:31:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Monica Davey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Monica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0005ddbf-8669-52c3-a0b3-9057df0d299d', 'word_count': 1221, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0005ddbf-8669-52c3-a0b3-9057df0d299d'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/10/what-were-reading-517/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Design Sponge: Desserts that maximize and magnify the last of the season’s berries. — Jeff Gordinier ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-10T13:37:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e85514d9-3959-516e-9911-956e3fcaba27', 'word_count': 388, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e85514d9-3959-516e-9911-956e3fcaba27'}, {'abstract': 'In Georgia, a university’s journalism department injects life and resources into local coverage, and a chronicler of police misconduct in Harlem says he has been punished for his work.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/10/the-breakfast-meeting-journalisms-big-tent-and-google-vs-amazon-on-search/', 'snippet': 'In Georgia, a university’s journalism department injects life and resources into local coverage, and a chronicler of police misconduct in Harlem says he has been punished for his work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An experiment in journalism education at Mercer University in Macon, Ga., will also inject life and resources into the professional journalism in the city, Christine Haughney writes. Backed by a $4.6 million grant from the John S. and James L. Knight Foundation, Mercer’s Center for Collaborative Journalism will be home to reporters and editors of the city’s 186-year-old paper, The Telegraph, and the local public radio station. Students will do reporting legwork, with guidance from professors and working journalists, in what the university’s president compares to the way medical schools use hospitals to train their students.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: Journalism’s Big Tent, and Google vs. Amazon on Search', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-10T13:40:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By NOAM COHEN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'COHEN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/525e9572-03db-5300-908d-056957883b10', 'word_count': 525, 'uri': 'nyt://article/525e9572-03db-5300-908d-056957883b10'}, {'abstract': 'Our director of photography received the award for Outstanding Service to Photography at a ceremony last week in London.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/10/kathy-ryan-honored-by-royal-photographic-society/', 'snippet': 'Our director of photography received the award for Outstanding Service to Photography at a ceremony last week in London.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At a ceremony last week in London, the magazine’s photo director, Kathy Ryan, was one of several people recognized by\xa0The Royal Photographic Society\xa0for their significant contributions to photography. Kathy received the society’s annual award for Outstanding Service to Photography.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kathy Ryan Honored by Royal Photographic Society', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-10T13:58:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By The photo department', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The photo department'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6bd7bee-5c92-5ea1-a57f-2c95a2c2054d', 'word_count': 127, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6bd7bee-5c92-5ea1-a57f-2c95a2c2054d'}, {'abstract': 'The new Canon Selphy CP900, a photo printer that is the company’s first with built-in Wi-Fi, can make prints from your computer, phone or tablet, if all are connected to your Wi-Fi network.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/10/one-hour-photo-try-one-minute/', 'snippet': 'The new Canon Selphy CP900, a photo printer that is the company’s first with built-in Wi-Fi, can make prints from your computer, phone or tablet, if all are connected to your Wi-Fi network.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Although we get digital photos instantly, it generally takes a quite a bit longer – days, in fact – to send away for prints of your shots.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/05/technology/05gw-printer/05gw-printer-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 769, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/05/technology/05gw-printer/05gw-printer-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1537, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/05/technology/05gw-printer/05gw-printer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/05/technology/05gw-printer/05gw-printer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 