and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teeth and Dentistry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sugar', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-10T16:43:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By C. Claiborne Ray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'C.', 'middlename': 'Claiborne', 'lastname': 'Ray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/9cfe110d-e126-55b4-8edc-358397426a29', 'word_count': 257, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9cfe110d-e126-55b4-8edc-358397426a29'}, {'abstract': 'The Briton who pioneered interaction design is remembered by colleagues.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/10/garden/tributes-to-bill-moggridge-cooper-hewitt-director.html', 'snippet': 'The Briton who pioneered interaction design is remembered by colleagues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some considered it an inspired choice, others simply surprising, when Bill Moggridge was appointed director of the Smithsonian Cooper-Hewitt National Design Museum in 2010. The 115-year-old New York institution is a treasure house of decorative objects, from panoramic wallpapers to dessert forks. Mr. Moggridge, who died Saturday at the age of 69,  was an industrial designer who invented the first laptop computer, the Grid Compass, in 1980, and was a founder, in 1991, of the global industrial design company IDEO. A British-born resident of Silicon Valley, with the intellectual curiosity of Nikola Tesla and the affability of Father Christmas, he had investigated the modes through which people manipulate machines, and used this research to pioneer a field known as interaction design.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/10/garden/10CURRENTS_MOGGRIDGE/10CURRENTS_MOGGRIDGE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 726, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/10/garden/10CURRENTS_MOGGRIDGE/10CURRENTS_MOGGRIDGE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1128, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/10/garden/10CURRENTS_MOGGRIDGE/10CURRENTS_MOGGRIDGE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/10/garden/10CURRENTS_MOGGRIDGE/10CURRENTS_MOGGRIDGE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/10/garden/10CURRENTS_MOGGRIDGE/10CURRENTS_MOGGRIDGE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why ‘User Friendly’ Is So Friendly: A Tribute to Bill Moggridge', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Why ‘User Friendly’ Is So Friendly', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moggridge, Bill', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cooper-Hewitt National Design Museum', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-10T16:54:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Lasky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lasky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'An Appraisal', '_id': 'nyt://article/36c27ae1-91ba-5cc0-b87c-9bebf3959947', 'word_count': 1388, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36c27ae1-91ba-5cc0-b87c-9bebf3959947'}, {'abstract': 'Brian d’Arcy James, Kate Baldwin, and P.J. Griffith will play the lead roles in the musical adaptation of Edna Ferber’s novel.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/10/public-theater-announces-giant-casting/', 'snippet': 'Brian d’Arcy James, Kate Baldwin, and P.J. Griffith will play the lead roles in the musical adaptation of Edna Ferber’s novel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Public Theater executives said on Monday that their fall production of the new musical “Giant,” based on Edna Ferber’s epic novel about a powerful Texas ranching family, will star the Tony Award nominees Brian d’Arcy James (“Shrek”) and Kate Baldwin (“Finian’s Rainbow”) as the patriarch Bick Benedict and his wife, Leslie, the roles played in the 1956 movie by Rock Hudson and Elizabeth Taylor.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Public Theater Announces ‘Giant’ Casting', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Public Theater Names Stars for ‘Giant’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baldwin, Kate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ferber, Edna', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greif, Michael', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "James, Brian D'Arcy", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'LaChiusa, Michael John', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pearson, Sybille', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Steggert, Bobby', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dallas Theater Center', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Public Theater', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-10T17:00:34+000