ted stock units that Facebook had granted to employees over the years. It’s odd timing for a tax bill. Why would Facebook, not the employees, owe tax on compensation income? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Facebook Is Paying the Tax Tab on Employee Compensation', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Gains Tax', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zuckerberg, Mark E', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-10T17:24:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Victor Fleischer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Victor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fleischer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/57f2c6b4-547e-5867-887d-3fedb71fc8e3', 'word_count': 1161, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57f2c6b4-547e-5867-887d-3fedb71fc8e3'}, {'abstract': 'The butcher’s recipe for Angus beef slices as prepared at Meatopia, the festival of more than 40 chefs and 2,600 carnivores that invaded Randall’s Island on Saturday evening.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/10/how-pat-lafrieda-cooks-a-900-pound-steer/', 'snippet': 'The butcher’s recipe for Angus beef slices as prepared at Meatopia, the festival of more than 40 chefs and 2,600 carnivores that invaded Randall’s Island on Saturday evening.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A recipe for Angus beef slices from the butcher Pat LaFrieda as prepared at Meatopia, the festival of more than 40 chefs and 2,600 carnivores that staged a five-hour invasion of Randalls Island on Saturday evening, undeterred by rain. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Pat LaFrieda Cooks a 900-Pound Steer', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Meat', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-10T17:28:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Glenn Collins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Glenn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/54363dbe-7c33-5d53-97fc-09ca24b0ac45', 'word_count': 228, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54363dbe-7c33-5d53-97fc-09ca24b0ac45'}, {'abstract': 'An abundance of desirable, easy-to-wear looks was prevalent at Diane von Furstenberg.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/10/backstage-beauty-report-diane-von-furstenberg-2/', 'snippet': 'An abundance of desirable, easy-to-wear looks was prevalent at Diane von Furstenberg.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Look:  To Each Her Own', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Backstage Beauty Report | Diane Von Furstenberg', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-10T17:30:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lily Nima', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nima', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ccfc34f-e172-558a-b918-e91d2d9c68e6', 'word_count': 278, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ccfc34f-e172-558a-b918-e91d2d9c68e6'}, {'abstract': 'The 103-year-old composer will receive France’s highest honor.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/10/elliott-carter-to-join-legion-of-honor/', 'snippet': 'The 103-year-old composer will receive France’s highest honor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The composer Elliott Carter, who turns 104 in December and is still composing prolifically, has collected his share of prestigious awards over the decades, among them two Pulitzer Prizes and the National Medal of Honor in the United States, Germany’s Ernst von Siemens Music Prize and the Commander of the Order of Arts and Letters, from France.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Elliott Carter to Join Legion of Honor', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carter, Elliott', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-10T17:32:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ed38afe-c64c-50a3-810e-fb40339c28e0', 'word_count': 292, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ed38afe-c64c-50a3-810e-fb40339c28e0'}, {'abstract': 'Andy Murray defeated Novak Djokovic in a grueling United States Open men’s singles final on Monday, earning his first Grand Slam title with a 7-6 (12), 7-5, 2-6, 3-6, 6-2 victory.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/10/analysis-of-u-s-open-mens-final/', 'snippet': 'Andy Murray defeated Novak Djokovic in a grueling United States Open men’s singles final on Monday, earning his first Grand Slam title with a 7-6 (12), 7-5, 2-6, 3-6, 6-2 victory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Andy Murray won his first Grand Slam title, surviving a mid-match collapse to outlast defending champion Novak Djokovic 7-6 (10), 7-5, 2-6, 3-6, 6-2 in four hours and 54 minutes for the men’s singles championship at the 2012 United States Open. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Highlights and Analysis: Andy Murray Wins U.S. Open', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Djokovic, Novak', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Federer, Roger', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murray, Andy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nadal, Rafael', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-10T17:33:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Rothenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rothenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6546f33e-1977-5e54-b804-ce09e817745e', 'word_count': 5258, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6546f33e-1977-5e54-b804-ce09e817745e'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney didn’t use the word troops in his convention address. Then he attacked the Democrats for (initially) not using the word God in their platform.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/10/god-and-the-troops/', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney didn’t use the word troops in his convention address. Then he attacked the Democrats for (initially) not using the word God in their platform.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mitt Romney has about had it with reporters and politicians asking why he didn’t mention American troops (who are still dying in Afghanistan for a war that he thinks they should be fighting) during his speech at the Republican convention in Tampa.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'God and the Troops', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Robertson, Pat', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-10T17:34:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fed51d1a-27ed-5049-ad91-38de105eba30', 'word_count': 405, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fed51d1a-27ed-5049-ad91-38de105eba30'}, {'abstract': 'Wheels spends a holiday weekend with the diesel-burning equivalent to the GTI, which is not available for sale in the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/10/driving-the-volkswagen-golf-gtd/', 'snippet': 'Wheels spends a holiday weekend with the diesel-burning equivalent to the GTI, which is not available for sale in the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The sixth generation of the Volkswagen Golf has been on American roads for three years. That may seem like sufficient time for a vehicle not named Murciélago, Zonda or Veyron to shake off the incredulous gasps and covetous glares of passers-by. But the Golf I drove over Labor Day weekend, painted a Kermit-like shade of green, was on a tourist visa, its German license plate gleaming below its honeycomb grille. The car prompted children to squeal and fanboys to fumble for their camera phones.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Driving the Volkswagen Golf GTD', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Volkswagen AG', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-10T17:42:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Schultz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schultz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2451d25-0f07-5977-a6dc-86b92da9a5f5', 'word_count': 789, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2451d25-0f07-5977-a6dc-86b92da9a5f5'}, {'abstract': 'Taking Questions: This week, Frank A. Bolz Jr., a retired New York Police Department captain, responds to readers’ questions.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/10/ask-a-hostage-negotiator/', 'snippet': 'Taking Questions: This week, Frank A. Bolz Jr., a retired New York Police Department captain, responds to readers’ questions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated | We are no longer accepting questions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/08/nyregion/cityroom-bloz-radio/cityroom-bloz-radio-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 673, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank':