ning point in police practices for handling similar situations.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/10/a-1973-hostage-situation-revisited/', 'snippet': 'Retro City: A 47-hour-long hostage situation at a sporting goods store in Williamsburg, Brooklyn, is still one of the longest in the city’s history and a turning point in police practices for handling similar situations.', 'lead_paragraph': '“We know some of you are hurt. We want to help you,” boomed a bullhorn on top of an armored police vehicle. “Please come out with your hands on your heads and you will be treated. There is no place for you to go. The building, the block and the entire area is surrounded.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A 1973 Hostage Situation, Revisited', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Revisiting 47 Hours of Fear in 1973', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hostages', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bedford-Stuyvesant (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bushwick (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Williamsburg (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-10T17:48:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily S. Rueb', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Rueb', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/69558b8f-b268-52b3-9036-ea144fae29be', 'word_count': 748, 'uri': 'n