dline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Eggs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-10T17:54:38+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Food', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/b8c60008-ae7b-56b3-9367-2263737583bb', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/b8c60008-ae7b-56b3-9367-2263737583bb'}, {'abstract': 'The two big-budget, big-expectation tentpoles, “Cloud Atlas” and “The Master” had audiences waiting for hours and industry speculating.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/10/toronto-film-festival-partying-with-ben-affleck-and-reactions-to-the-master-cloud-atlas-and-more/', 'snippet': 'The two big-budget, big-expectation tentpoles, “Cloud Atlas” and “The Master” had audiences waiting for hours and industry speculating.', 'lead_paragraph': ' TORONTO – The front-loaded schedule at the Toronto International Film Festival  has yielded a few expected payoffs and a few unpredicted ones. Eagerly-awaited movies like Ben Affleck’s “Argo” (which earned good word-of-mouth at a sneak preview at the Telluride Film Festival last month) delivered, earning a standing ovation at its packed premiere on Friday. Reviews called the film, about the Iranian hostage crisis in the 1970s, Mr. Affleck’s coming-of-age moment as an actor-director. At the after-party last week, Mr. Affleck was jovial, ordering pizza and chatting with friends like Matt Damon, John Krasinski and Emily Blunt late into the night. He talked eagerly about shooting at CIA headquarters in Langley, Va., but admitted to some worry that the geo-political theme would make the film “challenging” to market. “I’m working harder to promote this movie,” he said. “I can furnish you with endless” material. (We will expect it.)', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Toronto Film Festival: Partying With Ben Affleck and Reactions to ‘The Master,’ ‘Cloud Atlas’ and More', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pleasures, Some Unexpected, At Toronto Film Festival', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Toronto International Film Festival', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'AFFLECK, BEN', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hawkes, John', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Russell, David O', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox Searchlight Pictures', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Weinstein Co', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-10T17:56:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/94a23dae-9600-5b95-9607-e18204c44fd3', 'word_count': 414, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94a23dae-9600-5b95-9607-e18204c44fd3'}, {'abstract': 'The Albert and Mary Lasker Foundation announced that seven scientists would be honored with the 2012 Lasker Award, one of the world’s most prestigious scientific prizes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/11/science/seven-scientists-win-2012-lasker-award.html', 'snippet': 'The Albert and Mary Lasker Foundation announced that seven scientists would be honored with the 2012 Lasker Award, one of the world’s most prestigious scientific prizes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Albert and Mary Lasker Foundation announced on Monday that seven scientists would be honored with the 2012 Lasker Award, one of the world’s most prestigious scientific prizes.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', '