iations Monday with representatives of its so-called troika of European lenders, trying to agree to an €11 billion package of budget cutting measures that would enable Greece to receive its next allotment of bailout money.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Greece Wrestles With Cuts to Unlock Bailout Funds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Greece Wrestles With Cuts to Unlock Bailout Funds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Commission', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Monetary Fund', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Central Bank', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-10T18:37:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Niki Kitsantonis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Niki', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kitsantonis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/247f0df7-ec37-575a-acb5-0343cd78933d', 'word_count': 350, 'uri': 'nyt://article/247f0df7-ec37-575a-acb5-0343cd78933d'}, {'abstract': 'Sales of sunflower seeds have financed the conversion of a 70-acre tract of state-owned land into a grassland habitat.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/10/a-crop-dividend-restored-bird-habitat-in-n-j/', 'snippet': 'Sales of sunflower seeds have financed the conversion of a 70-acre tract of state-owned land into a grassland habitat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Farmers and wildlife advocates don’t often see eye to eye; each can look at a field and see widely divergent possibilities. Yet by encouraging farmers to plant fields of flowers, an innovative program in New Jersey is helping to finance the rehabilitation of wildlife areas for endangered species of birds. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Crop Dividend: Restored Bird Habitat in New Jersey', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flowers and Plants', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Invasive Species', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Audubon Society, New Jersey', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-10T18:40:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin Granville', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Granville', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/74ae1edc-0e0c-59b4-8a4d-0c1e3a8078bf', 'word_count': 881, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74ae1edc-0e0c-59b4-8a4d-0c1e3a8078bf'}, {'abstract': 'In navigating his country’s debt crisis, Mariano Rajoy, the Spanish prime minister, must contend with angry voters, rancorous regional leaders and scrutiny from European leaders.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/11/business/global/spains-prime-minister-walks-political-minefield.html', 'snippet': 'In navigating his country’s debt crisis, 