30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72a7e068-7d60-5b9c-902c-bac832ed8ef2', 'word_count': 388, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72a7e068-7d60-5b9c-902c-bac832ed8ef2'}, {'abstract': 'Darrelle Revis’s availability for Sunday’s game in Pittsburgh was cast into doubt Monday when the Jets announced that he sustained a “mild” concussion in their season-opening victory against Buffalo.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/11/sports/jets-darrelle-revis-has-a-concussion.html', 'snippet': 'Darrelle Revis’s availability for Sunday’s game in Pittsburgh was cast into doubt Monday when the Jets announced that he sustained a “mild” concussion in their season-opening victory against Buffalo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FLORHAM PARK, N.J. — A newcomer to football whose only exposure to the sport consisted of the Jets’ victory Sunday might have come away convinced that Mark Sanchez is an elite quarterback, better than those Manning fellows; that Austin Howard resembled a young Dan Dierdorf at right tackle; and that a sculptor would be visiting team headquarters this week to survey the rookie receiver Stephen Hill’s facial features — you know, for his Hall of Fame bust. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/11/sports/football/11jets-pic/11jets-pic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 758, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/11/sports/football/11jets-pic/11jets-pic-