in-bikinis/', 'snippet': 'Announcing the winner of the Bug Beauty Contest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The voting is now closed in our Bug Beauty Contest, and the results are staggering: the three grasshoppers in the pageant took home the gold, silver and bronze medals (tiaras?). The Colorful Eupropacris Grasshopper edged out Toxic Grasshopper No. 1 with 2,289 votes to 2,143. Toxic Grasshopper No. 2 hopped into third place with 740 votes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Next Up: Grasshoppers in Bikinis', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beauty Contests', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insects', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-10T19:21:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Samantha Henig', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Samantha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Henig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0fb813d9-ee62-5291-9356-2a7d6f68cfc5', 'word_count': 163, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0fb813d9-ee62-5291-9356-2a7d6f68cfc5'}, {'abstract': 'How would you use $100 if someone gave it to you and told you to spend it doing something nice for someone else?', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/10/spending-your-money-to-make-someone-else-happy/', 'snippet': 'How would you use $100 if someone gave it to you and told you to spend it doing something nice for someone else?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carl Richards is a certified financial planner in Park City, Utah, and is the director of investor education at BAM Advisor Services. His book, “The Behavior Gap,” was published this year. His sketches are archived on the Bucks blog. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The