stinal bacteria caused our immune systems to go haywire? Moises Velasquez-Manoff lays out the hygiene hypothesis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Never fall in love. Oh, well, go ahead, if you must, but make sure you fall for a living being. A romance with anything else, be it a pair of shoes or a scientific theory, is only asking for trouble, so seldom will the inanimate beloved live up to your besotted expectations. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/11/science/11ZUGE/11ZUGE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 669, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/11/science/11ZUGE/11ZUGE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1338, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/11/science/11ZUGE/11ZUGE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/11/science/11ZUGE/11ZUGE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/11/science/11ZUGE/11ZUGE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Messy, Exuberant Case Against Being Too Clean', 'kicker': 'Books', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Messy, Exuberant Case Against Being Too Clean', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immune System', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Microbiology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Velasquez-Manoff, Moises', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTIBIOTICS', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Intestinal Tract', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-10T20:18:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abigail Zuger, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abigail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zuger', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/30be38b9-fba8-5514-a19c-17a872579ee6', 'word_count': 923, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30be38b9-fba8-5514-a19c-17a872579ee6'}, {'abstract': 'The Tigers have won two games by a combined score of 82-17, but have forced just three turnovers.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/10/miles-enjoys-l-s-u-s-victories-would-like-more-turnovers/', 'snippet': 'The Tigers have won two games by a combined score of 82-17, but have forced just three turnovers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BATON ROUGE, La. — Louisiana State’s defense dominated Washington on Saturday — scaring its quarterback, smothering its running game — but Coach Les Miles, perhaps grasping for motivation, said he wished the Tigers bullied the Huskies into more turnovers too.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Miles Enjoys L.S.U.’s Victories but Would Like More Turnovers', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mathieu, Tyrann', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Louisiana State University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-10T20:28:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'new