gs.nytimes.com/2012/09/10/politics-and-the-pizza-man/', 'snippet': 'Scott Van Duzer, the Obama campaign’s favorite Republican bench-pressing pizza-parlor owner, found that fame can be a complicated proposition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Sunday, Scott Van Duzer became the Obama campaign’s favorite Republican bench-pressing pizza-parlor owner when he lifted President Obama off the floor during a surprise hug in his Florida restaurant. The image made the front pages of newspapers around the country and immediately whizzed around the Internet.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Politics and the Pizza Man', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On The Internet: Getting A Taste of Fame', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-10T21:57:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gerry Mullany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gerry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mullany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9c8ab60-99b0-5140-a75f-ea74002d184c', 'word_count': 240, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9c8ab60-99b0-5140-a75f-ea74002d184c'}, {'abstract': 'Some of the first leading news surveys show a bit of a bump for President Obama after the Democratic convention.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/10/polls-slight-post-convention-bounce-for-obama/', 'snippet': 'Some of the first leading news surveys show a bit of a bump for President Obama after the Democratic convention.', 'lead_paragra