t this fall in a new production of the Tony Award-winning play “The Heiress.” Click on the image above to watch the event, which was moderated by Charles McGrath. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Live Streaming: TimesTalks With Jessica Chastain', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chastain, Jessica', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-10T22:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e166ed6c-7508-52f9-b44c-b8da25175c22', 'word_count': 58, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e166ed6c-7508-52f9-b44c-b8da25175c22'}, {'abstract': 'Underscoring the hazards of drilling for oil in the Arctic Ocean, Shell said that encroaching sea ice had forced it to halt drilling its first exploration well off Alaska’s coast one day after it began.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/10/shell-halts-arctic-drilling-right-after-it-began/', 'snippet': 'Underscoring the hazards of drilling for oil in the Arctic Ocean, Shell said that encroaching sea ice had forced it to halt drilling its first exploration well off Alaska’s coast one day after it began.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — A day after it began drilling its first well in the Arctic Ocean, Shell has been forced to temporarily abandon the work because of sea ice moving into the area.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shell Halts Arctic Drilling Right After It Began', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ice Forces Shell To Halt Work On Arctic Well', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drilling and Boring', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Offshore Drilling and Exploration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal Dutch Shell Plc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALASKA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-10T22:12:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By John M. Broder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/86a51f2e-f40e-5124-a4f0-d9c89d12cb96', 'word_count': 366, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86a51f2e-f40e-5124-a4f0-d9c89d12cb96'}, {'abstract': 'The 2012 U.S. Open goes away for good today, but compelling as this year’s tournament has been, it won’t challenge the 1977 edition, when I got to play.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/10/the-time-i-played-for-a-championship-at-the-1977-u-s-open/', 'snippet': 'The 2012 U.S. Open goes away for good today, but compelling as this year’s tournament has been, it won’t challenge the 1977 edition, when I got to play.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 2012 U.S. Open goes away for good today, but as compelling as this year’s tournament has been, it won’t challenge the 1977 edition — the last to be held at Forest Hills and chronicled by Michael Steinberger two weeks ago — as the craziest U.S. Open ever. It also makes this the 35th consecutive year without a mixed singles champion.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Time I Played for a Championship at the 1977 U.S. Open', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'cont