New York Public Library, I thought, that’s it, he’s finally lost his mind.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/10/thom-browne-in-his-bauhaus-period/', 'snippet': 'Walking into Thom Browne’s women’s presentation at the New York Public Library, I thought, that’s it, he’s finally lost his mind.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Walking into Thom Browne’s women’s presentation at the New York Public Library, I thought, that’s it, he’s finally lost his mind. Nine or more handsome men wearing gray seersucker suits were lined against a backdrop of funhouse mirrors, each with a bulbous silver turban propped upon his head. One was plonking away on a xylophone. Then came the women with their hair in stiff orbs, a troupe in conical dresses pirouetting on round platforms painted with black and white spirals. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thom Browne in His Bauhaus Period', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Fashion Week', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Browne, Thom', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-10T23:42:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/125474cc-1269-588d-806b-e462ed0a4c75', 'word_count': 226, 'uri': 'nyt://article/125474cc-1269-588d-806b-e462ed0a4c75'}, {'abstract': 'Barbara Carroll, still at the piano and microphone at 87, celebrates experience as well as love and optimism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/11/arts/music/barbara-carroll-at-54-below.html', 'snippet': 'Barbara Carroll, still at the piano and microphone at 87, celebrates experience as well as love and optimism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are few sights more heartening than an 87-year-old musician in complete musical command leaning back at the piano and singing, “I’m in love again” with a rapturous sigh of exultation. That performer, seen on Sunday afternoon at 54 Below, was the elegant jazz pianist and singer Barbara Carroll. Her transition from the defunct Oak Room at the Algonquin Hotel to the recently opened 54 Below along with her longtime bassist, Jay Leonhart, has been seamless. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/11/arts/carroll/carroll-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 377, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/11/arts/carroll/carroll-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 377}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/11/arts/carroll/carroll-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 643, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/11/arts/carroll/carroll-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1285, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/11/arts/carroll/carroll-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/11/arts/carroll/carroll-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/20