ons', 'value': 'Jaipur (India)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-11T02:40:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Guy Trebay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Guy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Trebay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/7527fed3-e8e0-5fb0-81d3-876ec83cfbe8', 'word_count': 789, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7527fed3-e8e0-5fb0-81d3-876ec83cfbe8'}, {'abstract': 'College-educated whites are simultaneously more racially tolerant and more likely to express the racial resentment that they do feel politically.', 'web_url': 'https://campaignstops.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/10/the-unexpected-impact-of-coded-appeals/', 'snippet': 'College-educated whites are simultaneously more racially tolerant and more likely to express the racial resentment that they do feel politically.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After signing into law the landmark Civil Rights Act of 1964, President Lyndon B. Johnson famously told an aide, “we just delivered the South to the Republican Party for a long time to come.” Indeed, the Johnson-Goldwater contest was notable in two important respects related to race: it featured the first appearance in almost a century of racial animus as a central dimension of partisan conflict in a presidential election, and it was the last time a Democrat received a majority of the white vote.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Unexpected Impact of Coded Appeals', 'kicker': 'Campaign Stops', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pew Research Center', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-11T02:41:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Federico, Howard Lavine and Christopher Johnston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Federico', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Howard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lavine', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/350d2a56-aae5-5183-9de5-7217c93303b6', 'word_count': 1459, 'uri': 'nyt://article/350d2a56-aae5-5183-9de5-7217c93303b6'}, {'abstract': 'With Monday’s loss to the Washington Nationals, the Mets have lost 20 of their past 24 games at Citi Field, where they are 30-39 over all this season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/11/sports/baseball/mets-struggles-at-home-continue-in-loss-to-nationals.html', 'snippet': 'With Monday’s loss to the Washington Nationals, the Mets have lost 20 of their past 24 games at Citi Field, where they are 30-39 over all this season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The misery of the Mets has become all-encompassing, seeping through every aisle and empty seat at Citi Field.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Home-Game Misery Persists for Mets and Fans', 'kicker': 'Nationals 5, Mets 1', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Home-Game Mi