 that if they can host a successful global event their country’s image will soar. Not true. Ask South Africa. And Brazil?', 'lead_paragraph': 'After London’s triumphant Olympic Games and Paralympics, I’m sure that most of the foreign government officials who descended on London went away fervently believing that if only they too can win the chance to host a major event, and pull it off successfully, this will catapult their nation into the realms of international celebrity. But research suggests otherwise.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/11/blogs/rdv-london-olympics-parade/rdv-london-olympics-parade-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/11/blogs/rdv-london-olympics-parade/rdv-london-olympics-parade-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Risks of Hosting a Successful Olympics', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Investments', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-11T06:10:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simon Anholt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Anholt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c66f1b6f-b6a8-552f-9cce-7b752ef065f0', 'word_count': 511, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c66f1b6f-b6a8-552f-9cce-7b752ef065f0'}, {'abstract': 'YouTube lost its prime real estate on the next version of the iPhone, where it has been on the home screen since 2007. In response, YouTube released a new app in the App Store on Tuesday. YouTube benefits because it can sell ads and introduce new features, but it has to convince iPhone users to download it.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/11/losing-its-place-on-the-iphone-youtube-introduces-a-new-iphone-app/', 'snippet': 'YouTube lost its prime real estate on the next version of the iPhone, where it has been on the home screen since 2007. In response, YouTube released a new app in the App Store on Tuesday. YouTube benefits because it can sell ads and introduce new ...', 'lead_paragraph': '11:01 a.m. | Updated  with information about why Apple is removing the YouTube app as a default on the iPhone.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/11/technology/11bits-youtube/11bits-youtube-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 577, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/11/technology/11bits-youtube/11bits-youtube-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1600, 'width': 902, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Losing Its Place on the iPhone, YouTube Introduces a New iPhone App', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Online Advertising', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'YouTube.com', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-11T07:01:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claire Cain Miller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claire', 'middlename': 'Cain', 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7698bb22-1e36-57f7-ace6-a0a23a19ec4d', 'word_count': 456, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7698bb22-1e36-57f7-ace6-a0a23a19ec4d'}, {'abstract': 'At age 39, it might be time for the world’s most famous cricket player to retire.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/11/is-it-time-for-tendulkar-to-hang-up-his-bat/', 'snippet': 'At age 39, it might be time for the world’s most famous cricket player to retire.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Until recently, it was considered sacrilegious to speak a word against Sachin Tendulkar, the world’s most famous cricketer, who enjoys a God-like status in India, where cricket is practically a religion.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is It Time for Tendulkar to Hang Up His Bat?', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cricket (Game)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dravid, Rahul', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tendulkar, Sachin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bangalore (India)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-11T07:38:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Haresh Pandya', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Haresh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pandya', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/28f0aebc-c219-5c06-b37c-56a396c5