icle/7f9e45a2-3673-5249-a75e-5328af1224d7', 'word_count': 93, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f9e45a2-3673-5249-a75e-5328af1224d7'}, {'abstract': 'It’s time to forget about the bank that almost destroyed the world.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/16/magazine/lehman-brothers-we-heard-you-were-dead.html', 'snippet': 'It’s time to forget about the bank that almost destroyed the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lehman Brothers is having a great year. The bank, which almost destroyed the global economy four years ago this week, recently emerged from bankruptcy, resolved a third of its debts and executed the largest U.S. real estate deal of the year. Today, the company appears an awful lot like a normal investment bank. Its trading floor — on one of the two floors Lehman occupies in the Time & Life Building in Midtown Manhattan — is filled with dozens of young people who stare at financial graphs on Bloomberg terminals and talk in the hallways about the deals they’re working on.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/10/01/magazine/01economy/01economy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 538, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/10/01/magazine/01economy/01economy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 538}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/10/01/magazine/01economy/01economy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 892, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/10/01/magazine/01economy/01economy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1307, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit