Zhensheng, whose images of the Chinese Cultural Revolution are getting fresh attention, turned the camera on himself using frames left on a roll.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Li Zhensheng, a newspaper photographer who was active in the 1960s in northern China, documented the country’s Cultural Revolution, in honest, cinematic images. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Extra Frames, a Chinese Photographer Looks Inward', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Barbican Center', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-11T09:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sim Chi Yin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sim', 'middlename': 'Chi', 'lastname': 'Yin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/69d38e66-ebe7-5ce0-94f1-ba7d45906dc0', 'word_count': 368, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69d38e66-ebe7-5ce0-94f1-ba7d45906dc0'}, {'abstract': 'Have you ever come from behind and surprised yourself with greatness, whether on the field, in school or in some other aspect of your life?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/11/when-have-you-ever-succeeded-when-you-thought-you-might-fail/', 'snippet': 'Have you ever come from behind and surprised yourself with greatness, whether on the field, in school or in some other aspect of your life?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Serena Williams just won the United States Open women’s singles title, after fending off a match point — not to mention 11 months of injuries and health concerns that plagued her during the last two years. Have you ever come from behind and surprised yourself with greatness, whether on the field, in school or in some other aspect of your life? When have you ever managed to perform better than you imagined?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Have You Ever Succeeded When You Thought You Might Fail?', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-11T09:09:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Gonchar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonchar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af6bc182-c686-59c2-903a-58824583465b', 'word_count': 289, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af6bc182-c686-59c2-903a-58824583465b'}, {'abstract': 'Three Afghan service personnel were killed on board the helicopter, which was parked inside Bagram Air Base.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/world/asia/taliban-claims-attack-on-helicopter-in-afghanistan.html', 'snippet': 'Three Afghan service personnel were killed on board the helicopter, which was parked inside Bagram Air Base.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — A coalition heavy-transport helicopter parked inside the sprawling Bagram Air Base was hit and destroyed by insurgent fire late Monday, killing three Afghan service members who were on board, NATO said Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'NATO Copter Destroyed by Taliban at Base', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'NATO Copter Destroyed by Taliban at Base', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bagram Air Base (Afghanistan)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'North Atlantic Treaty Organization', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-11T09:18:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Graham Bowley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Graham', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bowley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ca12d1e-2712-56f2-a40a-f3ba154a50c0', 'word_count': 401, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ca12d1e-2712-56f2-a40a-f3ba154a50c0'}, {'abstract': 'The sovereign wealth fund Qatar Holding says it has yet to decide whether to support Glencore International’s increased all-share offer for the mining giant Xstrata.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/09/11/qatar-makes-glencore-wait-on-revised-xstrata-bid/', 'snippet': 'The sovereign wealth fund Qatar Holding says it has yet to decide whether to support Glencore International’s increased all-share offer for the mining giant Xstrata.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Glencore International, the world’s biggest commodities trader, will have to wait a bit longer to see whether its increased all-share offer for the mining giant Xstrata will be backed by one of that company’s largest shareholders.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Qatar Holding Makes Glencore Wait on Revised Xstrata Bid', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Commodities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mines and Mining', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Glencore International AG', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Xstrata', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-11T09:34:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb7c0a39-0b43-5d27-a7a8-ed21a0f8a7df', 'word_count': 330, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb7c0a39-0b43-5d27-a7a8-ed21a0f8a7df'}, {'abstract': 'Maimuna Abdi Yussuf, a Somali student at African Leadership Academy in Johannesburg, South Africa, is one of eight high school seniors around the world who are blogging about their college searches.', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/11/maimuna-abdi-yussuf-1/', 'snippet': 'Maimuna Abdi Yussuf, a Somali student at African Leadership Academy in Johannesburg, South Africa, is one of eight high school seniors around the world who are blogging about their college searches.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve had my life all figured out since I was ten. The plan? Finish primary school with the best scores so that I could get into a national high school. Once there, I would work even harder to get the best grades so that I could gain admission into the University of Nairobi Law School.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/03/education/envpls13-maimuna/envpls13-maimuna-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 362, 'width': 495, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/0