 iPhones to its customers. But it is aiming to take advantage of the iPhone by introducing a marketing campaign aimed at people who want to bring older versions of the iPhone to T-Mobile’s network.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/11/t-mobile-usa-says-bring-us-your-iphones/', 'snippet': 'T-Mobile USA is the one major carrier in the United States that has not had a deal with Apple to sell iPhones to its customers. But it is aiming to take advantage of the iPhone by introducing a marketing campaign aimed at people who want to bring ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'T-Mobile USA is the one major carrier in the United States that has not had a deal with Apple to sell iPhones to its customers. That will not change when Apple introduces a new iPhone this week. But T-Mobile is still aiming to take advantage of the iPhone by introducing a new marketing campaign aimed at people who want to bring older versions of the iPhone to T-Mobile’s network. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/11/technology/11bits-tmobile/11bits-tmobile-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 677, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/11/technology/11bits-tmobile/11bits-tmobile-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1210, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'T-Mobile USA Says Bring Us Your iPhones', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'T-Mobile', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-11T13:08:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Wingfield', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wingfield', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/910797ea-c98a-5934-a7ed-7aa75601f585', 'word_count': 433, 'uri': 'nyt://article/910797ea-c98a-5934-a7ed-7aa75601f585'}, {'abstract': 'More and more university students are choosing to study abroad, according to a new league table ranking the world’s top academic institutions. Is it a positive trend and how important are the rankings in picking the right school?', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/11/university-ranking-shows-boom-in-global-student-mobility/', 'snippet': 'More and more university students are choosing to study abroad, according to a new league table ranking the world’s top academic institutions. Is it a positive trend and how important are the rankings in picking the right school?', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The compilers of a leading league table of the world’s top universities on Tuesday reported an “unstoppable rise” in the numbers of students choosing to travel abroad to study.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'University Ranking Shows Boom in Global Student Mobility', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Students (in US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cambridge University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Massachusetts Institute of Technology', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-11T13:09:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Morris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e71319cc-3715-5cf8-887f-9d022287c526', 'word_count': 557, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e71319cc-3715-5cf8-887f-9d022287c526'}, {'abstract': 'The Day: Today, politicians may speak about the strength of this country’s institutions and how no terrorist could make us afraid, but that last part will not reflect reality.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/11/as-another-anniversary-passes-still-waiting-for-justice/', 'snippet': 'The Day: Today, politicians may speak about the strength of this country’s institutions and how no terrorist could make us afraid, but that last part will not reflect reality.', 'lead_paragraph': ' On another Sept. 11 morning with skies so blue you could hurt your eyes as well as your heart looking at them, the annual remembrance of the city’s worst day echoed across the space where the twin towers once stood. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Another Anniversary Passes, Still Waiting for Justice', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mohammed, Khalid Shaikh', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-11T13:13:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clyde Haberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clyde', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/92afb04b-0973-5550-826a-7ed775736295', 'word_count': 800, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92afb04b-0973-5550-826a-7ed775736295'}, {'abstract': 'The government of Madrid hocked too much public trust to lure to the city a mega gambling project with uncertain financing.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/11/madrid-government-courts-a-mega-casino/', 'snippet': 'The government of Madrid hocked too much public trust to lure to the city a mega gambling project with uncertain financing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MADRID — On Friday, the American casino magnate Sheldon Adelson announced that he’d chosen Madrid over Barcelona to host EuroVegas, a multibillion-dollar casino and resort complex. For months the two cities, both desperate for jobs, had competed to court him and his company, Las Vegas Sands. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Casino Is Coming to Town', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Casinos', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gambling', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Las Vegas Sands Corp', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Madrid (Spain)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-11T13:20:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Blitzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Blitzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1feeef0f-74bb-5873-adb6-f1c259523a17', 'word_count': 605, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1feeef0f-74bb-5873-adb6-f1c259523a17'}, {'abstract': 'The president and the first lady paused to remember victims of the Sept. 11 attacks at the White House.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/11/remembering-911-at-the-white-house/', 'snippet': 'The president and the first lady paused to remember victims of the Sept. 11 attacks at the White House.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Washington, President Obama and his wife, Michelle, observed a moment of silence on the South Lawn of the White House at approximately 8:46 a.m., the minute American Airlines Flight 11 hit the north tower 11 years ago. They were joined by hundreds of members of the White House staff and a full Marine color guard. A Marine trumpeter signaled the end of the ceremony by playing taps. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Remembering 9/11 at the White House', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Michelle', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-11T13:22:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Goodridge', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goodridge', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0bf20484-242a-587b-b02e-6c380d9861f6', 'word_count': 70, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0bf20484-242a-587b-b02e-6c380d9861f6'}, {'abstract': 'A simple act, the reading of the names of those killed 11 years ago, continues to evoke strong emotions.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/11/a-somber-reading-of-the-names-of-the-dead/', 'snippet': 'A simple act, the reading of the names of those killed 11 years ago, continues to evoke strong emotions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Though they were not to speak, Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo of New York, Gov. Chris Christie of New Jersey, Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg and former Mayor Rudolph W. Giuliani created a small stir when they arrived shortly before the ceremony was to begin. They stopped together about 10 yards from the platform where 200 readers, reciting the names of the dead, were to stand at lecterns.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Somber Reading of the Names of the Dead', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giuliani, Rudolph W', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-11T13:38:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivan Yee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2db189f-7602-56ed-b31f-05e4c741a43a', 'word_count': 406, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2db189f-7602-56ed-b31f-05e4c741a43a'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/11/what-were-reading-518/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Economist: Tracking the explosion in the number of American craft distilleries: a decade ago there were 24, and now there are more than 200. Their vodka, gin, rum, rye and whiskey is claiming a greater share of the once-moribund spirits market – and 16 states have voted to repeal bans on Sunday alcohol sales in the last decade. – Glenn Collins', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-11T13:42:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aaf56146-09bf-5102-977c-2f1ce3499c49', 'word_count': 453, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aaf56146-09bf-5102-977c-2f1ce3499c49'}, {'abstract': 'Morgan Stanley and Citigroup agreed on Tuesday to value their brokerage joint venture, Morgan Stanley Smith Barney, at $13.5 billion, allowing Morgan Stanley to buy full control of the business at a favorable valuation.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/09/11/morgan-stanley-smith-barney-is-valued-at-13-5-billion/', 'snippet': 'Morgan Stanley and Citigroup agreed on Tuesday to value their brokerage joint venture, Morgan Stanley Smith Barney, at $13.5 billion, allowing Morgan Stanley to buy full control of the business at a favorable valuation.', 'lead_paragraph': '9:16 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morgan Stanley to Take Over Smith Barney, With Citigroup’s Blessing', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citigroup Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Morgan Stanley', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-