even just the faintest wisp, would send my body into full-fledged panic.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Protecting Children From Raw 9/11 Memories', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Trade Center (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-11T14:46:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Scelfo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scelfo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/153b315c-96fb-552b-9f2c-b4908d0d5041', 'word_count': 625, 'uri': 'nyt://article/153b315c-96fb-552b-9f2c-b4908d0d5041'}, {'abstract': 'What the teachers’ strike in Chicago means for organized labor. | Morgan Stanley’s showdown with Citigroup over a brokerage.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/09/11/business-day-live-in-standoff-latest-sign-of-unions-under-siege/', 'snippet': 'What the teachers’ strike in Chicago means for organized labor. | Morgan Stanley’s showdown with Citigroup over a brokerage.', 'lead_paragraph': ' What the teachers’ strike in Chicago means for organized labor. | Morgan Stanley’s showdown with Citigroup over a brokerage.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Business Day Live: In Standoff, Latest Sign of Unions Under Siege', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-11T14:47:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed5d8c59-c9fb-5a78-8f34-4cb2414ef313', 'word_count': 20, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed5d8c59-c9fb-5a78-8f34-4cb2414ef313'}, {'abstract': 'Several courts have lately been expanding the already broad protections that derivatives and repo contracts enjoy.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/09/11/too-much-protection-for-derivatives-in-bankruptcy/', 'snippet': 'Several courts have lately been expanding the already broad protections that derivatives and repo contracts enjoy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I have written before about my opinions regarding the “safe harbors” in the bankruptcy code. These are the provisions that exempt derivatives and repo contracts from the automatic stay, the prohibition on termination of contracts with the debtor, the prohibition on constructively fraudulent transfers and the prohibition on obtaining preferential treatment on the eve of bankruptcy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Too Much Protection for Derivatives in Bankruptcy', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Derivatives (Financial Instruments)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rakoff, Jed S', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-11T14:48:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen J. Lubben', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Lubben', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03d6ef83-4bfe-570c-a96f-e8eb10a7683e', 'word_count': 627, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03d6ef83-4bfe-570c-a96f-e8eb10a7683e'}, {'abstract': 'Andy Murray capped off Britain’s incredible sports summer by breaking through to win his first Grand Slam final.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/sports/andy-murray-britains-triumphant-summer-us-open.html', 'snippet': 'Andy Murray capped off Britain’s incredible sports summer by breaking through to win his first Grand Slam final.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sure, it came in the wee hours of the morning in Britain, and who knows how many Britons stayed awake to witness it as it happened, but Andy Murray’s victory over Novak Djokovic in a wild United States Open final made it official. Britain owned the summer of sports. Its best cyclist won the Tour de France. It played the triumphant Olympic host to a T, reveling in the spectacle as much as its own success, then moved on to stage a worthy Paralympics. But men’s tennis was an even more daunting frontier, a Grand Slam drought that stretched to 1936, and Murray, well, let’s just say Britain has long taken measure of its rumpled, brooding star and thought, “Oh, bother. ...”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/12/sports/12leading1/12leading1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/12/sports/12leading1/12leading1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/12/sports/12leading1/12leading1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/12/sports/12leading1/12leading1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1337, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/12/sports/12leading1/12leading1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/12/sports/12leading1/12leading1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/12/sports/12leading1/12leading1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Britain’s Triumphant Summer', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murray, Andy (1987- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Djokovic, Novak', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oakland Raiders', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-11T14:48:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ef29525-b307-5e27-a4a5-e48ca681366d', 'word_count': 536, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ef29525-b307-5e27-a4a5-e48ca681366d'}, {'abstract': 'Solar installations in the second quarter of this year were more than double those of a year earlier. And the solar energy generated on California’s grid topped one gigawatt for the first time in August.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/11/the-growing-might-of-solar-power/', 'snippet': 'Solar installations in the second quarter of this year were more than double those of a year earlier. And the solar energy generated on California’s grid topped one gigawatt for the first time in August.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From California to New Jersey, the summer sun was hot this year — and so was the solar industry. While the business of solar energy is still small enough and young enough to record firsts at the fearsome pace of a toddler, the milestones are getting more substantial.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Growing Might of Solar Power', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Solar Energy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Energy Information Administration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Solar Energy Industries Assn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-11T14:53:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicity Barringer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicity', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barringer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e5a733a-c520-5c80-9754-8d9d8037cf5d', 'word_count': 493, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e5a733a-c520-5c80-9754-8d9d8037cf5d'}, {'abstract': 'Andy Murray, the U.S. Open champion, caught up with Straight Sets after he walked back onto the court at Arthur Ashe Stadium for the first time since his victory. He looked back at what he had just done and looked ahead to what comes next.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/11/conversations-with-andy-murray-savoring-the-victory/', 'snippet': 'Andy Murray, the U.S. Open champion, caught up with Straight Sets after he walked back onto the court at Arthur Ashe Stadium for the first time since his victory. He looked back at what he had just done and looked ahead to what comes next.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Within hours of winning the United States Open, Andy Murray had done nearly a dozen interviews, posed for thousands of photographs with his trophy, held a news conference, and had done several additional television and radio interviews. He caught up with Straight Sets at a unique moment, after he walked back onto the court at Arthur Ashe Stadium for the first time since his victory. As he stood in the now empty stadium where he had made history, he looked back at what he had just done and looked ahead to what comes next. (All of Murray’s interviews during the tournament can be found here.) ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Conversations With Andy Murray: Savoring the Victory', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murray, Andy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-11T14:55:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Rothenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rothenberg', 'qualifier': 