ty board that will rule on a proposed ban on large sugary drinks, has had a major influence on the health habits of New Yorkers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 11 largely faceless members of the New York City Board of Health who will decide Thursday whether to ban the sale of super-size sugary soft drinks in certain establishments trace their authority to 1805, when the power to monitor the city’s health was formally vested in a city “inspector,” John Pintard, a Renaissance man who is most famous for popularizing Santa Claus. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Rulings on Rubbish and Tattoos, Safeguarding the City for Centuries', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'City’s Health Boards Have Ruled on Livestock and Tattoos. Up Next: Soda.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smoking and Tobacco', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weight', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Farley, Thomas A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Board of Health (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-11T16:50:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Roberts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roberts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/712f740f-c01e-5468-9cf3-b67fb1c6bc18', 'word_count': 736, 'uri': 'nyt://article/712f740f-c01e-5468-9cf3-b67fb1c6bc18'}, {'abstract': 'This alternative to mass-burn incineration, proponents say, disposes of garbage and toxic contaminants while minimizing emissions and providing electricity and usable byproducts.', 'we