lementary Medicine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARTHRITIS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Migraine Headaches', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Osteoarthritis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pain', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-11T16:53:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': "By Anahad O'Connor", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anahad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Connor", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/144b827a-4094-5060-b285-9d1efb31f2ce', 'word_count': 698, 'uri': 'nyt://article/144b827a-4094-5060-b285-9d1efb31f2ce'}, {'abstract': 'The G.O.P. used to dominate on likability, stick-to-it-ive-ness and military toughness. Not any more.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/11/republican-turf/', 'snippet': 'The G.O.P. used to dominate on likability, stick-to-it-ive-ness and military toughness. Not any more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For decades Republican presidential candidates have campaigned on stick-to-it-ive-ness, likability and military toughness, and in these areas have generally had the edge on their Democratic opponents.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Republican Turf', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-11T16:59:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifi