.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e878a5d-0592-5f41-b87b-9219aa070d6a', 'word_count': 426, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e878a5d-0592-5f41-b87b-9219aa070d6a'}, {'abstract': 'Responding to reader comments about how to deal with a nuclear Iran.', 'web_url': 'https://keller.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/11/nuclear-mullahs-continued/', 'snippet': 'Responding to reader comments about how to deal with a nuclear Iran.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My column on confronting the prospect of a nuclear-armed Iran seems to have caught a lot of readers by surprise. The surprise ranges from approving (“Thank heavens, at last a voice of sanity!”) to indignant (“Are you out of your [expletive] mind?!?”)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nuclear Mullahs, Continued', 'kicker': 'Bill Keller', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'AHMADINEJAD, MAHMOUD', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-11T17:34:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Keller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/814a4e8a-def4-534b-bba9-b7b7ce184e07', 'word_count': 1650, 'uri': 'nyt://article/814a4e8a-def4-534b-bba9-b7b7ce184e07'}, {'abstract': 'In this lesson, students evaluate firsthand accounts of the war in Syria and make judgments about the role President Bashar al-Assad’s government may have played in stoking long-buried sectarian divisions.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/11/the-fog-of-war-helping-students-make-sense-of-syria/', 'snippet': 'In this lesson, students evaluate firsthand accounts of the war in Syria and make judgments about the role President Bashar al-Assad’s government may have played in stoking long-buried sectarian divisions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Overview | How does a multiethnic society come undone, and who’s to blame when it happens? If the “Arab Spring” uprisings across the Middle East inspire hope for democracy, the nearly 18-month-old conflict in Syria raises a darker possibility: civil conflict. Observers say religious and sectarian differences are increasingly fueling a war that has claimed an estimated 20,000 lives, pitting members of the ruling Alawite minority against a fractious Sunni Muslim majority.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Fog of War: Helping Students Make Sense of Syria', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-11T17:37:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Marshall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Marshall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d794a9e3-6de7-5520-8f4d-d67e1f1798c7', 'word_count': 1892, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d794a9e3-6de7-5520-8f4d-d67e1f1798c7'}, {'abstract': 'My mother called last night to report that researchers have found that a few wails from a baby learning to sleep on her own don’t seem to hurt one bit. She was laughing.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/11/sleep-training-wont-hurt-might-help/', 'snippet': 'My mother called last night to report that researchers have found that a few wails from a baby learning to sleep on her own don’t seem to hurt one bit. She was laughing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My mother may still be laughing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sleep Training Won’t Hurt, Might Help', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sleep', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-11T17:42:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/67b49c9c-9c0a-5438-8e77-d756274c9872', 'word_count': 359, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67b49c9c-9c0a-5438-8e77-d756274c9872'}, {'abstract': 'Using Google seems simple enough. But the company says that most people are not taking advantage of all the features Google offers, from simple to sophisticated, to make searching more efficient. So it is offering a free online course to teach people how to do a better Google search. Registration starts Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/11/a-class-to-teach-you-how-to-use-google/', 'snippet': 'Using Google seems simple enough. But the company says that most people are not takin