', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-11T18:37:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed38942c-055f-5f86-a931-93282141bf70', 'word_count': 256, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed38942c-055f-5f86-a931-93282141bf70'}, {'abstract': 'Jerry Garrett recalls a drive in 2001 with Zanardi, the Cart champion and double amputee who last week won two gold medals at the London Paralympics, in his special-edition NSX.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/11/alex-zanardi-in-an-acura-nsx-a-memorable-monaco-tour-guide/', 'snippet': 'Jerry Garrett recalls a drive in 2001 with Zanardi, the Cart champion and double amputee who last week won two gold medals at the London Paralympics, in his special-edition NSX.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last month, while attending the collector car events and auctions around the Monterey Peninsula, Calif., I reviewed a morning-after report from a sale organized by Russo & Steele. There was a double-take when, listed among the sales, I spotted what the auctioneer called a 1999 Acura NSX Alex Zanardi Edition Coupe.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Alex Zanardi: In an Acura NSX, a Memorable Monaco Tour Guide', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monaco Grand Prix', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zanardi, Alex', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ACURA DIVISION OF HONDA MOTOR CO', 'r