, 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-11T19:40:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Simonson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Simonson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a24c9d48-da7a-59b8-93e5-a01616e92b25', 'word_count': 975, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a24c9d48-da7a-59b8-93e5-a01616e92b25'}, {'abstract': 'New York', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/09/11/fashion/runway-womens/rodarte-spring-2013-rtw.html', 'snippet': 'New York', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/11/fashion/runway-womens/rodarte_spring13app-slide-IUSH/rodarte_spring13app-slide-IUSH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/11/fashion/runway-womens/rodarte_spring13app-slide-IUSH/rodarte_spring13app-slide-IUSH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/11/fashion/runway-womens/rodarte_spring13app-slide-IUSH/rodarte_spring13app-slide-IUSH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/11/fashion/runway-womens/rodarte_spring13app-slide-IUSH/rodarte_spring13app-slide-IUSH-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1365, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rodarte: Spring 2013 RTW', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-11T19:47:25+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Fashion & Style', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': "Women's Runway", 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/fea15a6e-d604-5c76-8185-92a39b1a2df5', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/fea15a6e-d604-5c76-8185-92a39b1a2df5'}, {'abstract': 'Dorie Greenspan and Susan Berlin are each making the leap into opening a brick-and-mortar shop.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/dining/baking-their-own-way.html', 'snippet': 'Dorie Greenspan and Susan Berlin are each making the leap into opening a brick-and-mortar shop.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dorie Greenspan’s butter cookies have gone from pop-up to permanence. Ms. Greenspan, a food writer and author of several cookbooks, mostly on baking, joined forces with her son, Joshua, right, a few years ago and started selling her cookies, mostly around special occasions like Valentine’s Day. Now, with another partner, Daniel Seehoff, left, they are opening retail shops called Beurre & Sel (butter and salt) on Saturday in La Marqueta in Harlem, where they do the baking, and in a snazzy red-and-white walk-in closet of a space in the Essex Street Market on the Lower East Side. They are starting with a dozen flavors of French-style sablé cookies, mostly sweet, some savory.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/12/dining/12STUFF2_BAKERYSPAN/12STUFF2_BAKERYSPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/12/dining/12STUFF2_BAKERYSPAN/12STUFF2_BAKERYSPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credi