. The looks: baseball caps, bare midriffs, leather skirts, blue jeans, denim shorts and floral jumpers.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/11/street-style-serene-vs-extreme-3/', 'snippet': 'T tracks one statement worn two ways. The looks: baseball caps, bare midriffs, leather skirts, blue jeans, denim shorts and floral jumpers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Street Style | Serene vs. Extreme', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-11T20:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/30b19fe4-ea20-5392-986b-956e7ef63b75', 'word_count': 38, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30b19fe4-ea20-5392-986b-956e7ef63b75'}, {'abstract': 'At least 12 people were killed in a car bombing in the capital of Yemen on Tuesday, in what appeared to be an attack targeting the country’s defense minister.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/11/after-militant-is-killed-car-bomb-targets-yemen-minister/', 'snippet': 'At least 12 people were killed in a car bombing in the capital of Yemen on Tuesday, in what appeared to be an attack targeting the country’s defense minister.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At least 12 people were killed in a car bombing in the capital of Yemen on Tuesday, in what appeared to be an attack targeting the country’s defense minister. The bombing came after a top Al Qaeda leader in Yemen, and six people traveling with him, were killed in what Yemeni officials said was an airstrike by an American drone.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Militant Is Killed, Car Bomb Targets Yemen Minister', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drones (Pilotless Planes)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cowell, Alan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hadi, Abdu Rabbu Mansour', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saleh, Ali Abdullah', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Worth, Robert F', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Al Qaeda in the Arabian Peninsula', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Enterprise Institute for Public Policy Research', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sana (Yemen)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Saudi Arabia', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-11T20:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ad1ee40-de53-5c3c-870e-c5a82fe8cfa6', 'word_count': 531, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ad1ee40-de53-5c3c-870e-c5a82fe8cfa6'}, {'abstract': 'A fresh look at ways to conserve tigers despite growing pressure for land and tiger body parts.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/11/saving-space-for-tigers-on-a-crowding-planet/', 'snippet': 'A fresh look at ways to conserve tigers despite growing pressure for land and tiger body parts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tigers, the biggest of the great cats, are having a tough time finding space as the growth spurt in human numbers and appetites in Asia presses in on their last wild havens. Alan Rabinowitz, a biologist who has been studying and working to save tigers and other wild cat species for decades (see him in the field in the video above), recently helped run a Bangkok meeting of scientists, law enforcement officials and conservationists developing new tactics for boosting tigers’ prospects in the face of relentless poaching pressure driven by the booming demand for tiger skins and products in China and parts of Southeast Asia.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Saving Space for Tigers on a Crowding Planet', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poaching (Wildlife)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tigers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rabinowitz, Alan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Panthera Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wildlife Conservation Society', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bangkok (Thailand)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Far East, South and Southeast Asia and Pacific Areas', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-11T20:03:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d61a462-97b5-5711-b5b6-3767782a8a60', 'word_count': 504, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d61a462-97b5-5711-b5b6-3767782a8a60'}, {'abstract': 'Volpi Foods of St. Louis has expanded not only the distribution of its products but also the variety of its dry-cured salami.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/dining/salami-from-around-the-world.html', 'snippet': 'Volpi Foods of St. Louis has expanded not only the distribution of its products but also the variety of its dry-cured salami.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lorenza Pasetti is a member of the third generation of the family that founded Volpi Foods in St. Louis in 1902. And since she has taken the reins of the company, which specializes in cured meats, she has expanded not only the distribution of the products but also the variety of dry-cured salami the company makes. Most are Italian, but as a self-described “history nut,” she has just introduced a line called Un Mondo, an assortment of small 6-ounce varieties inspired by traditional international styles: fine-textured German landjäger and Hungarian, more rustic Catalan called fuet, Spanish chorizo, French with herbs and with cepes mushrooms, and even spicy-sweet Chinese lap cheong. Also new are some Italian versions seasoned with cheeses like aged asiago and Parmesan. They are made without sodium nitrites or nitrates and contain no fillers. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/12/dining/12STUFF3_SALAMISPAN/12STUFF3_SALAMISPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 