, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4c46798-399f-5064-baeb-6288c9b1933b', 'word_count': 201, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4c46798-399f-5064-baeb-6288c9b1933b'}, {'abstract': 'A new report calls TSA operations “costly, counterintuitive, and poorly executed.”', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/11/is-this-the-pose-of-a-free-man/', 'snippet': 'A new report calls TSA operations “costly, counterintuitive, and poorly executed.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the Sunday before the Republican convention, Senator Rand Paul ranted against his least favorite government bureaucracy: The Transportation Security Administration. Addressing a crowd at the University of South Florida, he mimicked the backscatter-machine stance (arms up in the air, legs apart) and asked “Is this the pose of a free man?”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Is This the Pose of a Free Man?’', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'So Many Screeners and So Little Shampoo, but Are Our Planes Safer?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Airport Security', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Rand', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transportation Security Administration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-11T20:09:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Juliet Lapidos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Juliet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lapidos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b78fda0f-377c-5b03-a4fa-90fe100da7c5', 'word_count': 685, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b78fda0f-377c-5b03-a4fa-90fe100da7c