ow/0f689967-0d3c-54c9-bf51-c06e7c2d9001', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/0f689967-0d3c-54c9-bf51-c06e7c2d9001'}, {'abstract': 'The Treasury Department said on Tuesday that it had sold an additional $2.7 billion worth of its holdings in A.I.G., as underwriters for the offering exercised what’s known as an overallotment option to meet higher-than-expected demand.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/09/11/treasury-sells-additional-2-7-billion-worth-of-a-i-g-shares/', 'snippet': 'The Treasury Department said on Tuesday that it had sold an additional $2.7 billion worth of its holdings in A.I.G., as underwriters for the offering exercised what’s known as an overallotment option to meet higher-than-expected demand.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Apparently, $18 billion worth of American International Group shares weren’t enough for investors.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Treasury Sells Additional $2.7 Billion Worth of A.I.G. Shares', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emergency Economic Stabilization Act (2008)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN INTERNATIONAL GROUP INC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Treasury Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-11T20:33:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/14c65c39-e2dc-537f-9c27-c28f60f98078', 'word_count': 248, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14c65c39-e2dc-537f-9c27-c28f60f98078'}, {'abstract': 'My husband and I agreed that we would terminate a fetus with genetic defects. We’re too old to parent a special-needs child.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/11/pregnant-at-49/', 'snippet': 'My husband and I agreed that we would terminate a fetus with genetic defects. We’re too old to parent a special-needs child.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was pregnant the week of the Republican convention, when they ratified their platform regarding abortion. Pregnant and considering an abortion, and not one that would fit into any of the “exceptions” identified by many Republican politicians: rape, incest or to save the life of the mother. It was a more usual condition, an unplanned pregnancy at my age. But not because I’m a young teenage girl with my life stretching out before me. It was quite the opposite: I’m 49.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pregnant at 49', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Childbirth', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests (Medical)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-11T20:39:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erin Kelly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kelly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d424327-8351-5f9b-be3f-f64db266d4c1', 'word_count': 816, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d424327-8351-5f9b-be3f-f64db266d4c1'}, {'abstract': '“Independents,” a musical held over from the New York International Fringe Festival, alternates between stoner comedy and romance, until dramatic storm clouds gather.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/theater/reviews/independents-by-marina-keegan-at-soho-playhouse.html', 'snippet': '“Independents,” a musical held over from the New York International Fringe Festival, alternates between stoner comedy and romance, until dramatic storm clouds gather.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The sunset of youth is witnessed from a crow’s nest in Marina Keegan’s “Independents,” a musical held over from the New York International Fringe Festival at the SoHo Playhouse. And like the show itself, it is a thing to savor. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/12/arts/inddepend/inddepend-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 353, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/12/arts/inddepend/inddepend-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 353}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/12/arts/inddepend/inddepend-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 652, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/12/arts/inddepend/inddepend-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1304, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/12/arts/inddepend/inddepend-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/12/arts/inddepend/inddepend-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/12/arts/inddepend/inddepend-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nothing Like Reality to Break Up a Party', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nothing Like Reality to Break Up a Party', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sonnenblick, Mark', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keegan, Marina', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feigenbaum, Stephen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Independents (Play)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Polinger, Charlie', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-11T20:40:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Webster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1662a44-faea-563d-a3d9-5b16b86e939d', 'word_count': 303, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1662a44-faea-563d-a3d9-5b16b86e939d'}, {'abstract': 'A number of bankers and financiers were at Arthur Ashe Stadium on Monday to witness tennis history as Andy Murray defeated Novak Djokovic in the men’s singles final. But as the night wore on, some turned to unconventional means to stay warm.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/09/11/wall-streets-sits-courtside-for-a-marathon-match/', 'snippet': 'A number of bankers and financiers were at Arthur Ashe Stadium on Monday to witness tennis history as Andy Murray defeated Novak Djokovic in the men’s singles final. But as the night wore on, some turned to unconventional means to stay warm.', 'lead_paragraph': 'John Paulson, the billionaire hedge fund manager, will be forever known on Wall Street as the man who made nearly billions shorting subprime mortgages. But on Monday night at the United States Open men’s singles final, DealBook witnessed Mr. Paulson do something that, while not nearly as remunerative, was almost as impressive: He turned his necktie into an ascot. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wall Street Sits Courtside for a Marathon Match', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Djokovic, Novak', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lutnick, Howard', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murray, Andy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Palm, Gregory K', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paulson, John A', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-11T20:41:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4014044f-9ab6-5057-baaa-252a1dba1ea7', 'word_count': 429, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4014044f-9ab6-5057-baaa-252a1dba1ea7'}, {'abstract': 'How uncertainty is built into the science of weather forecasting.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/11/past-forward-why-do-we-still-buy-5-umbrellas-at-the-last-minute/', 'snippet': 'How uncertainty is built into the science of weather forecasting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Oumar Diallo, a merchant with a tiny sliver of a shop, sells umbrellas at the entrance to the subway near the corner of 40th Street and Seventh Avenue. Whenever it’s raining, Diallo is the busiest person at the top of the subway stairs, taking cash, making change and opening umbrellas over his customers’ heads. I asked Diallo, who is from Guinea and has been selling umbrellas for five years, what it’s like for his income to be so dependent on the weather. “When it’s not raining, I get bored,” he said. Like many people, Diallo checks the weather forecast when he wakes up in the morning and before he goes to bed. Still, his business relies on the fact that the weather — and meteorology — is unpredictable. “I make money when people are unprepared.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Past Forward: Why Do We Still Buy $5 Umbrellas at the Last Minute?', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gleick, James', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Silver, Nate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-11T20:42:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maya Lau', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lau', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d878eb62-de07-5dbd-9d52-82192217023a', 'word_count': 563, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d878eb62-de07-5dbd-9d52-82192217023a'}, {'abstract': 'The young photographer’s short film for Hermès is sweet yet sensual, with a fairy tale-like guilelessness.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/11/scarf-tricks-olivia-bee-for-hermes/', 'snippet': 'The young photographer’s short film for Hermès is sweet yet sensual, with a fairy tale-like guilelessness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Olivia Bee, 18, started photographing her friends when she was just 11, gradually developing a dreamy, color-drenched aesthetic that is a visual metaphor for the emotional lushness and near-religious sensory intensity of adolescence. Neither are qualities normally associated with the bourgeois elegance of Hermès, but after seeing Bee’s work in Le Monde, a representative of the house contacted her about photographing for Le Monde d’Hermès, the brand’s magazine, and shooting a short film, “Il Est Pour Nous,” which stars Bee, her boyfriend Cooper Campbell and a pair of pastel bunnies, for its Web site. Sweet yet sensual, with a fairy-tale-like guilelessness, the resulting images are a whole new way of looking at the foulard, which Bee fashioned into both a giant hair bow and a curvy elf hat. “They suggested I make them into head wraps or skirts but I was thinking more stylized,” she said. Touché!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Scarf Tricks | Olivia Bee for Hermès', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hermes International SA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-11T20:48:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nancy MacDonell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nancy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacDonell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09bfab48-3838-5783-ad4d-f3da4162f12e', 'word_count': 750, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09bfab48-3838-5783-ad4d-f3da4162f12e'}, {'abstract': 'Stu Loeser, the former press secretary for Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg, has been hired by Speaker Sheldon Silver to help navigate a sexual harassment scandal engulfing the State Assembly.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/nyregion/stu-loeser-hired-to-aid-sheldon-silver-in-assembly-scandal.html', 'snippet': 'Stu Loeser, the former press secretary for Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg, has been hired by Speaker Sheldon Silver to help navigate a sexual harassment scandal engulfing the State Assembly.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALBANY — It did not take Stu Loeser long to find a high-profile client.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/12/nyregion/12vito-web/12vito-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/12/nyregion/12vito-web/12vito-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/12/nyregion/12vito-web/12vito-web-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/12/nyregion/12vito-web/12vito-web-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/12/nyregion/12vito-web/12vito-web-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ex-Mayoral Aide to Help Assembly Speaker in Harassment Case', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Former Aide To Bloomberg H