omen, but the Deal Professor asks whether that will make a difference in how companies are run.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/09/11/seeking-critical-mass-of-gender-equality-in-the-boardroom/', 'snippet': 'European Union leaders are considering a law to require that 40 percent of a company’s directors be women, but the Deal Professor asks whether that will make a difference in how companies are run.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s a remarkable lack of women in corporate boardrooms around the world. The European Union is considering a remedy that would require that 40 percent of a company’s directors be women. This may be a milestone for gender equality, but the question is, will it make any difference in how companies are run?', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Seeking Critical Mass of Gender Equality in the Boardroom', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Seeking Critical Mass of Gender Equality in the Boardroom', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boards of Directors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gender', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-11T22:18:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Davidoff Solomon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': 'Davidoff', 'lastname': 'Solomon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d383f9e-689f-5359-9d56-571cc4f5ecc1', 'word_count': 1066, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d383f9e-689f-5359-9d56-571cc4f5ecc1'}, {'abstract': 'Even as the European Commission puts the final touches on a regulatory plan for banks, some countries are seeking to modify or delay the proposed system.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/business/global/integrating-banks-spurs-last-minute-fears-in-europe.html', 'snippet': 'Even as the European Commission puts the final touches on a regulatory plan for banks, some countries are seeking to modify or delay the proposed system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRUSSELS — Even as European Union officials put the final touches on a plan for a central bank supervisor, prominent Germans and some leaders in Central and Eastern Europe were trying on Tuesday to modify or delay the proposal. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Integrating Banks Spurs Last-Minute Fears in Europe', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Europe Readies Bank Plan, Last-Minute Jitters and a Move to Pull Back', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Central Bank', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Commission', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-11T22:22:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Kanter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kanter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/01dd5318-2d55-57c0-9923-028c19e80dca', 'word_count': 930, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01dd5318-2d5