 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/e0a51516-0c42-57a8-bb17-1f0b8f99c069', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/e0a51516-0c42-57a8-bb17-1f0b8f99c069'}, {'abstract': 'Lehman Brothers has been waiting for the real estate market to improve so it can sell its properties at higher prices than it would have received during the depth of the financial crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/realestate/commercial/lehman-brothers-with-much-real-estate-to-sell-is-biding-its-time.html', 'snippet': 'Lehman Brothers has been waiting for the real estate market to improve so it can sell its properties at higher prices than it would have received during the depth of the financial crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nearly four years after Lehman Brothers touched off a worldwide financial crisis when it filed for bankruptcy protection on Sept. 15, 2008, the estate of the failed investment bank continues to control more than $10 billion of real estate assets in its $40.5 billion portfolio. And all of it eventually must be converted to cash to repay creditors. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/12/business/Lehman1/Lehman1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/12/business/Lehman1/Lehman1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/12/business/Lehman1/Lehman1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 628, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/12/business/Lehman1/Lehman1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1256, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'c