rted', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d67a777-3f67-5c9a-97c4-a0c3aa274b75', 'word_count': 887, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d67a777-3f67-5c9a-97c4-a0c3aa274b75'}, {'abstract': 'The damage caused by influence-seeking campaign money unleashed by recent Supreme Court rulings is spreading to state judicial elections.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/opinion/a-defeat-for-impartial-courts.html', 'snippet': 'The damage caused by influence-seeking campaign money unleashed by recent Supreme Court rulings is spreading to state judicial elections.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The damage caused by enormous amounts of influence-seeking campaign money unleashed by recent Supreme Court rulings is spreading beyond elections for legislative and executive posts to contests for important state court judgeships. Following on those destructive decisions, the West Virginia Supreme Court of Appeals ruled last week to deny matching funds under the state’s pilot campaign financing program for judicial races to a Republican candidate, Allen Loughry II, for a seat on that court. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/17/opinion/17EDSALL-HOUSEHOLD/17EDSALL-HOUSEHOLD-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 144, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/17/opinion/17EDSALL-HOUSEHOLD/17EDSALL-HOUSEHOLD-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 144}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/17/opinion/17EDSALL-HOUSEHOLD/17EDSALL-HOUSEHOLD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 177, 'width': 738, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/