c at the top of men’s tennis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/sports/tennis/with-grand-slam-title-murray-joins-tennis-elite.html', 'snippet': 'Andy Murray, with his victory Monday at the U.S. Open, has joined the rarefied company of Roger Federer, Rafael Nadal and Novak Djokovic at the top of men’s tennis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For years, more than seven to be exact, men’s tennis was defined by its three best players: Roger Federer, Rafael Nadal and Novak Djokovic. They divvied up almost every Grand Slam trophy, and in the process created a separation from the pack.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/sports/12tennis1/12tennis1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/sports/12tennis1/12tennis1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/sports/12tennis1/12tennis1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/13/sports/12tennis1/12tennis1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/sports/12tennis1/12tennis1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Murray Elbows His Way Into Exclusive Men’s Club', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Murray Takes His Turn at Rising Over Rivals', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murray, Andy (1987- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Federer, Roger', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nadal, Rafael', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Djokovic, Novak', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T01:03:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Greg Bishop', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Greg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bishop', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55ec09af-0251-5741-8563-6bebb4371ce8', 'word_count': 915, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55ec09af-0251-5741-8563-6bebb4371ce8'}, {'abstract': 'The U.S. Open practice courts offered a glimpse at how Andy Murray gets ready for matches.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/11/watching-murray-prepare-on-his-way-to-championship/', 'snippet': 'The U.S. Open practice courts offered a glimpse at how Andy Murray gets ready for matches.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In his news conference following his grueling five-set victory over Novak Djokovic in the United States Open final, Andy Murray said he was happy that he was “ able to do it for all the guys I work with.” There are many such guys in today’s hyper-refined game. The top earners employ small armies that include coach, trainer, “physio” and one or more on-court practice partners. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Watching Murray Prepare on His Way to Championship', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lendl, Ivan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murray, Andy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T01:05:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Tanenhaus', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tanenhaus', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed58ca44-aaf0-55f6-b92e-d92abab511f9', 'word_count': 779, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed58ca44-aaf0-55f6-b92e-d92abab511f9'}, {'abstract': 'Five more people in southeast Georgia have been charged with helping an antigovernment militia accused of killing two people.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/us/georgia-more-charges-in-militia-plot.html', 'snippet': 'Five more people in southeast Georgia have been charged with helping an antigovernment militia accused of killing two people.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Five more people in southeast Georgia have been charged with helping an antigovernment militia accused of killing two people. District Attorney Tom Durden of the\xa0Atlantic Judicial Circuit\xa0said Tuesday that five suspects had committed burglaries, thefts and car break-ins to finance a militia called FEAR, or Forever Enduring Always Ready.\xa0Three other people suspected of membership in the militia already face the death penalty for the murder of a soldier and his girlfriend in December. Prosecutors say the militia was formed by former soldiers at Fort Stewart near Savannah. The group plotted several attacks, including poisoning the apple crop in Washington State, attacking a dam and assassinating President Obama.\xa0 The five charged are Christopher Jenderseck, Adam Dearman, Timothy Joiner, Anthony Garner and Randall Blake Dearman. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Georgia: More Charges In Militia Plot ', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Georgia: More Charges In Militia Plot', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fort Stewart (Ga)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T01:06:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robbie Brown', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robbie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brown', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/02a6cc50-63d1-532f-b944-65cd04bd6516', 'word_count': 130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02a6cc50-63d1-532f-b944-65cd04bd6516'}, {'abstract': 'The filmmakers David Redmon and Ashley Sabin examine the lives of teenage girls in Siberia who audition at open casting calls for fashion models.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/opinion/100000001777605/scouted.html', 'snippet': 'The filmmakers David Redmon and Ashley Sabin examine the lives of teenage girls in Siberia who audition at open casting calls for fashion models.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The filmmakers David Redmon and Ashley Sabin examine the lives of teenage girls in Siberia who audition at open casting calls for fashion models.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/11/opinion/opdoc-girlmodel-sub/opdoc-girlmodel-sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subT