the absence of sensible gun controls. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Aurora’s Aftermath', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Aurora’s Aftermath', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aurora, Colo, Shooting (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Aurora (Colo)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T01:19:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5a4bd63-9f6c-5f89-a3f3-94650c44bb2e', 'word_count': 347, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5a4bd63-9f6c-5f89-a3f3-94650c44bb2e'}, {'abstract': 'New evidence on screening tests is disturbing. The tests provide no gain, but can lead to harmful surgeries and complications.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/opinion/false-promises-on-ovarian-cancer.html', 'snippet': 'New evidence on screening tests is disturbing. The tests provide no gain, but can lead to harmful surgeries and complications.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New evidence that women are more likely to be harmed than helped by screening tests for ovarian cancer is disturbing. The tests do nothing to prevent healthy women from dying from the usually fatal disease. Yet they often lead doctors to perform needless surgeries that cause serious complications in many patients. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'False Promises on Ovarian Cancer', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '