contribution to a system that redistributes tax revenue to poorer regions. Catalonia also has the largest debt among Spanish regions, which has forced its government to make some of the deepest budget cuts in Spain. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spain: Marchers Demand Independence for Catalonia, as Budget Cuts Bolster Separatism', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spain: Hundreds of Thousands Demand Independence For Catalonia, as Budget Cuts Bolster Separatism', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Barcelona (Spain)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Catalonia (Spain)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T01:47:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Raphael Minder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Raphael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Minder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/69601cce-c916-5ddd-bcf3-cf0bea8b674e', 'word_count': 118, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69601cce-c916-5ddd-bcf3-cf0bea8b674e'}, {'abstract': 'Rhode Island’s state primary on Tuesday gave its new voter identification law its most strenuous exercise yet, stirring dissent and praise from voters who lined up with ID cards, but few problems were reported.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/11/rhode-island-primary-tests-new-voter-id-law/', 'snippet': 'Rhode Island’s state primary on Tuesday gave its new voter identification law its most strenuous exercise yet, stirring dissent and praise from voters who lined up with ID cards, but few problems were reported.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PROVIDENCE, R.I. — Candy McSwain and Bonnie Stevenson, two poll workers in this city’s diverse Elmwood neighborhood, peered at Jeziel Jared Lopez’s passport and expired state ID card and consulted the state’s new list of acceptable forms of voter identification.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rhode Island Primary Tests New Voter ID Law', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Civil Liberties Union', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rhode Island', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T01:50:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jess Bidgood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jess', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bidgood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/813afde2-f15e-58ee-8d14-3363b2272c7d', 'word_count': 623, 'uri': 'nyt://article/813afde2-f15e-58ee-8d14-3363b2272c7d'}, {'abstract': 'Narciso Rodriguez packed so much into his show, from minimalist dresses to nearly baroque embroidery.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/11/simple-yet-effortless-mastery/', 'snippet': 'Narciso Rodriguez packed so much into his show, from minimalist dresses to nearly baroque embroidery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Narciso Rodriguez started out as a minimalist designer 15 years ago, became known as a sublime colorist over the last several years and now, after showing his spring collection tonight, can henceforth be known simply as the master. So much was packed into his show, from the minimalist dresses to the nearly baroque embroidery, and yet he made it all look so simple and effortless.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Simple Yet Effortless Mastery', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Fashion Week', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodriguez, Narciso', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T01:52:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/953dda33-3139-5155-89f9-64048449c7d1', 'word_count': 211, 'uri': 'nyt://article/953dda33-3139-5155-89f9-64048449c7d1'}, {'abstract': 'Questions on how teachers should be evaluated have been added to traditional issues of pay, benefits and working conditions as Chicago teachers walk picket lines.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/education/chicago-is-focus-of-national-debate-on-teacher-evaluation.html', 'snippet': 'Questions on how teachers should be evaluated have been added to traditional issues of pay, benefits and working conditions as Chicago teachers walk picket lines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — What started here as a traditional labor fight over pay, benefits and working conditions has exploded into a dramatic illustration of the national debate over how public school districts should rate teachers.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'ca