web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/pageoneplus/corrections-september-12-2012.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on September 12, 2012.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NATIONAL', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: September 12, 2012', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T02:00:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f2cb3cf0-2a1a-5f97-b86e-36758712cd69', 'word_count': 719, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f2cb3cf0-2a1a-5f97-b86e-36758712cd69'}, {'abstract': 'Gendarmes questioned Dominique de Villepin on Tuesday on suspicion of involvement in fraud that investigators believe was committed by a friend, the businessman Régis Bulot.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/world/europe/france-former-premier-is-questioned-in-fraud-case.html', 'snippet': 'Gendarmes questioned Dominique de Villepin on Tuesday on suspicion of involvement in fraud that investigators believe was committed by a friend, the businessman Régis Bulot.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Gendarmes questioned the former prime minister Dominique de Villepin on Tuesday on suspicion of involvement in fraud that investigators believe was committed by a friend, the businessman Régis Bulot. It was unclear whether charges might be brought against Mr. de Villepin, who was released after several hours of questioning, a police spokesman said. Investigators believe that Mr. Bulot, the former president of Relais et Châteaux, a luxury hotel and restaurant network, embezzled more than $2 billion from the company. In a recorded telephone conversation from 2010, Mr. de Villepin, who was no longer in government, appears to tell Mr. Bulot that he pressured managers at the company to keep the fraud a secret, according to French news media reports. Mr. Bulot’s lawyer told the newsmagazine Le Nouvel Observateur that his client had embezzled about $640,000, but that Mr. de Villepin had been unaware of it. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France: Former Premier Is Questioned in Fraud Case', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France: Former Premier Is Questioned in Fraud Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bulot, Regis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Villepin, Dominique Galouzeau', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embezzlement', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T02:02:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Sayare', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sayare', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/17b0767d-78f2-5f53-85e3-03e5d819826d', 'word_count': 146, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17b0767d-78f2-5f53-85e3-03e5d819826d'}, {'abstract': 'Several companies and research labs are working on wearable robots to help disabled people walk or to make the human body superhuman.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/technology/wearable-robots-that-can-help-people-walk-again.html', 'snippet': 'Several companies and research labs are working on wearable robots to help disabled people walk or to make the human body superhuman.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RICHMOND, Calif. — When Joey Abicca pokes a metal crutch into the ground with his right arm, tiny motors start whirling around his left leg, lifting it and moving it forward. When he does the same with his left arm, the motors whir to life again and his right leg takes a step. The metallic whine is like something out of the movie “RoboCop.”', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/12/business/0912BIZWALK/0912BIZWALK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/12/business/0912BIZWALK/0912BIZWALK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/12/business/0912BIZWALK/0912BIZWALK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 731, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/12/business/0912BIZWALK/0912BIZWALK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1462, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/12/business/0912BIZWALK/0912BIZWALK-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/12/business/0912BIZWALK/0912BIZWALK-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/12/business/0912BIZWALK/0912BIZWALK-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Breed of Robotics Aims to Help People Walk Again', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Robots in All Walks of Life', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disabilities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robots and Robotics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ekso Bionics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Physical Therapy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T02:02:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian X. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3efe9112-16a3-5121-81b7-0bc803b2ae22', 'word_count': 974, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3efe9112-16a3-5121-81b7-0bc803b2ae22'}, {'abstract': 'The Institute of Medicine says the American medical system loses $750 billion annually by squandering 30 cents of every dollar spent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/health/policy/waste-and-promise-seen-in-us-health-care-system.html', 'snippet': 'The Institute of Medicine says the American medical system loses $750 billion annually by squandering 30 cents of every dollar spent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The American medical system squanders 30 cents of every dollar spent on health care, according to new calculations by the respected Institute of Medicine. But in all that waste and misuse, policy experts and economists see a significant opportunity — a way to curb runaway health spending, to improve medical outcomes and even to put the economy on sounder footing. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Study of U.S. Health Care System Finds Both Waste and Opportunity to Improve', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Study of U.S. Health Care System Finds Both Waste and Opportunity to Improve', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Institute of Medicine', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T02:06:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Money & Policy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annie Lowrey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lowrey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/abdf3c7e-4247-5fe5-84f6-55e998e3e1a7', 'word_count': 813, 'uri': 'nyt://article/abdf3c7e-4247-5fe5-84f6-55e998e3e1a7'}, {'abstract': 'British schools now do a better job of lifting students up the social ladder, the Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development said in a report published Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/world/europe/britain-british-schools-offer-more-upward-mobility-for-students-than-american-ones-report-says.html', 'snippet': 'British schools now do a better job of lifting students up the social ladder, the Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development said in a report published Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'British schools now do a better job than American schools of lifting students up the social ladder, the Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development said in a report published Tuesday. In Britain, a student whose parents never graduated from high school has a 60 percent chance of attending college, while in the United States the odds are just 29 percent, one of the lowest levels among the 34 countries with advanced economies that make up the O.E.C.D., which is based in Paris. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Britain: British Schools Offer More Upward Mobility for Students Than American Ones, Report Says', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Britain: British Schools Offer More Upward Mobility For Students Than American Ones, New Report Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T02:08:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By D. D. Guttenplan', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/752f1ef8-fa2a-5de0-af15-52e4f220ebb0', 'word_count': 85, 'uri': 'nyt://article/752f1ef8-fa2a-5de0-af15-52e4f220ebb0'}, {'abstract': 'Preaching basics in his first season managing, Robin Ventura has the White Sox two games ahead of the Tigers, who are led by the grizzled and veteran Jim Leyland.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/sports/baseball/managing-in-al-race-old-school-vs-older-school.html', 'snippet': 'Preaching basics in his first season managing, Robin Ventura has the White Sox two games ahead of the Tigers, who are led by the grizzled and veteran Jim Leyland.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — One is old by a manager’s standards. At 67, he smokes Marlboro Reds before and after games, dispensing nuggets of baseball wisdom collected over a more-than-20-year managerial career as the smoke curls up past his silver mustache and around his thinning hair. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/12/sports/MANAGERS2/MANAGERS2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/12/sports/MANAGERS2/MANAGERS2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/12/sports/MANAGERS2/MANAGERS2-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/12/sports/MANAGERS2/MANAGERS2-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/12/sports/MANAGERS2/MANAGERS2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/12/sports/MANAGERS2/MANAGERS2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/12/sports/MANAGERS2/MANAGERS2-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 91, 'width': 91, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In A.L. Central Race, It’s Old School vs. Older School', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In A.L. Central Race, It’s Old School vs. Older School', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ventura, Robin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Tigers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leyland, Jim', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago White Sox', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T02:11:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Strauss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Strauss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eeb1d1d1-a94d-5678-8616-92092c2e0ac1', 'word_count': 997, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eeb1d1d1-a94d-5678-8616-92092c2e0ac1'}, {'abstract': 'Having both declined public money, President Obama and Mitt Romney are committing to ambitious fund-raising schedules that are eating into valuable campaign time.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/us/politics/romney-and-obama-juggle-campaigning-and-fund-raising.html', 'snippet': 'Having both declined public money, President Obama and Mitt Romney are committing to ambitious fund-raising schedules that are eating into valuable campaign time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the closing weeks of a closely fought presidential campaign, Mitt Romney will be mingling with wealthy Republican donors in Chicago, San Diego and San Francisco, hundreds of miles from the swing state voters who will make or break his White House bid.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/12/us/12donate/12donate-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 728, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/12/us/12donate/12donate-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1456, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Candidates Look to Balance Need for Campaigning With Need for Money', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Candidates Look to Balance Need for Campaigning With Need for Money', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T02:14:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Confessore and Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Confessore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c629e577-adf8-56a2-9dfa-e814aee20aa2', 'word_count': 1032, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c629e577-adf8-56a2-9dfa-e814aee20aa2'}, {'abstract': 'The Hamas government demolished more than a dozen makeshift homes this week in the impoverished enclave, and officials said they would soon remove the rest of the structures.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/world/middleeast/gaza-bulldozers-raze-part-of-forgotten-neighborhood.html', 'snippet': 'The Hamas government demolished more than a dozen makeshift homes this week in the impoverished enclave, and officials said they would soon remove the rest of the structures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Hamas government demolished more than a dozen makeshift homes this week in an impoverished enclave known as the Forgotten Neighborhood, and officials said they would soon remove the rest of the structures, which were built without permits on public land. Residents said that two bulldozers came to the Gaza City enclave on Monday and razed the rusted-zinc shanties that housed about 18 Bedouin families, some for more than two decades. The neighborhood was the focus of an article on Monday in The New York Times about poverty in Gaza. Amal Shamaly, a spokeswoman for the Land Authority, said that all “illegal building” on government land would be removed, and that a security compound was planned for the area. Residents said that they had been sent demolition orders several years ago, and again several months ago, but that no action was taken until this week. The families who lost their houses were staying in a tent on Tuesday, while some of the women and children moved in with relatives. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gaza: Bulldozers Raze Part of Forgotten Neighborhood', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gaza: Bulldozers Raze Part of Forgotten Neighborhood', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gaza Strip', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hamas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T02:16:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fares Akram', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fares', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Akram', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/03ae0e42-275c-5541-8fe8-2fc1554b690f', 'word_count': 171, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03ae0e42-275c-5541-8fe8-2fc1554b690f'}, {'abstract': 'Dr. Szasz wrote “The Myth of Mental Illness,” a book that questioned the legitimacy of his field and made enemies of many fellow doctors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/health/dr-thomas-szasz-psychiatrist-who-led-movement-against-his-field-dies-at-92.html', 'snippet': 'Dr. Szasz wrote “The Myth of Mental Illness,” a book that questioned the legitimacy of his field and made enemies of many fellow doctors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thomas Szasz, a psychiatrist whose 1961 book “The Myth of Mental Illness” questioned the legitimacy of his field and provided the intellectual grounding for generations of critics, patient advocates and antipsychiatry activists, making enemies of many fellow doctors, died Saturday at his home in Manlius, N.Y. He was 92.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/12/us/SZASZ-obit/SZASZ-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 721, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/12/us/SZASZ-obit/SZASZ-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1442, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/12/us/SZASZ-obit/SZASZ-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75,