phant-in-the-room/', 'snippet': 'Is the memory of George W. Bush’s presidency dragging Mitt Romney down?', 'lead_paragraph': 'If a polling lead in the first week of September were a guarantee of victory two months later, then John McCain and Al Gore would have both been sworn in as president of the United States. So no, President Obama’s convention bounce has not – repeat, has not — sealed the election for the Democrats.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Elephant in the Room', 'kicker': 'Campaign Stops', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservatism (US Politics)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T03:22:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7cf2106-9f6b-5252-b7cd-5c65a3f6715e', 'word_count': 967, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7cf2106-9f6b-5252-b7cd-5c65a3f6715e'}, {'abstract': 'The Dutch electorate will go to the polls on Wednesday with economic stagnation and euro skepticism on its mind, in a vote that may foreshadow next year’s elections in Germany.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/world/europe/dutch-voters-may-point-way-for-rest-of-europe.html', 'snippet': 'The Dutch electorate will go to the polls on Wednesday with economic stagnation and euro skepticism on its mind, in a vote that may foreshadow next year’s elections in Germany.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AMSTERDAM — The Netherlands is an unusually good European weather vane. It may be comparatively tiny, with only 16.7 million people, and comparatively rich and secure, but it forecasts where the Continent is headed.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/12/world/NETHERLANDS-1/NETHERLANDS-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/12/world/NETHERLANDS-1/NETHERLANDS-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dutch Voters May Point Way for Rest of Europe', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dutch Voters May Point Way for Rest of Europe', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rutte, Mark', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilders, Geert', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Netherlands', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T03:26:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Erlanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erlanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank