r holding a concert Monday in Tel Aviv when so many other musicians won’t play here.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/a-thank-you-note-to-the-red-hot-chili-peppers/', 'snippet': 'Thank you, the Red Hot Chili Peppers, for holding a concert Monday in Tel Aviv when so many other musicians won’t play here.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TEL AVIV — The crowd and the critics were happy, but to me, the Red Hot Chili Peppers’s concert on Monday night was a nuisance. Hayarkon Park, where the band performed in front of some 50,000 sweaty Israelis, is ten minutes away from home. And it’s where I jog in the evenings.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Play Music, Not Politics', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Red Hot Chili Peppers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tel Aviv (Israel)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T10:28:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shmuel Rosner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shmuel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3aaadd5f-0842-5ccc-b0b0-d49cdd663096', 'word_count': 380, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3aaadd5f-0842-5ccc-b0b0-d49cdd663096'}, {'abstract': 'If this is how the Patriots’ defense is going to play all season, the N.F.L. might as well save us all time and give Robert Kraft the Lombardi Trophy right now.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/week-1-film-review-in-praise-of-patriots-defense/', 'snippet': 'If this is how the Patriots’ defense is going to play all season, the N.F.L. might as well save us all time and give Robert Kraft the Lombardi Trophy right now.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A closer look at the opening week of games, with the benefit of film analysis. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Week 1 Film Review: In Praise of Patriots’ Defense', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Patriots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T10:36:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Benoit', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Benoit', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97a7d65b-290f-5474-94d0-fa6859971ba7', 'word_count': 673, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97a7d65b-290f-5474-94d0-fa6859971ba7'}, {'abstract': 'A proposal to give the European Union more control over banking has stirred up dissent from countries that have doubts about the plan’s practicality.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/business/global/13iht-banks13.html', 'snippet': 'A proposal to give the European Union more control over banking has stirred up dissent from countries that have doubts about the plan’s practicality.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRUSSELS — The European Commission president, José Manuel Barroso, described the proposal for a single supervisor for the region’s banks on Wednesday as the first step in a renewed drive for a federally unified Europe.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/business/0913BIZBANKS/0913BIZBANKS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 786, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/business/0913BIZBANKS/0913BIZBANKS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1572, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Weary of Crisis, but Wary of Change', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Weary of Crisis, but Wary of Change', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barroso, Jose Manuel Durao', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euro (Currency)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Central Bank', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T10:58:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Kanter and Stephen Castle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kanter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e57bd71-eb64-5428-965e-145ef0daf67b', 'word_count': 1117, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e57bd71-eb64-5428-965e-145ef0daf67b'}, {'abstract': 'In the unspoiled wilds of southwestern Uganda and northern Rwanda, Volcanoes Safaris has built a string of high-design lodges that have played host to image-conscious politicos like Rahm Emanuel and former Senator Bill Frist.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/jungle-nook/', 'snippet': 'In the unspoiled wilds of southwestern Uganda and northern Rwanda, Volcanoes Safaris has built a string of high-design lodges that have played host to image-conscious politicos like Rahm Emanuel and former Senator Bill Frist.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the unspoiled wilds of southwestern Uganda and northern Rwanda, Volcanoes Safaris has built a string of high-design lodges that have played host to image-conscious politicos like Rahm Emanuel and former Senator Bill Frist. What brings them here are not just the land-before-time vistas and the chance to track the elusive silverback gorilla. It’s also the company’s strenuous commitment to do-gooding — a comfort to travelers who might otherwise be reluctant to visit very poor countries rivened by past conflicts. Volcanoes’ newest outpost, Kyambura Gorge (above), sits on a once-derelict coffee plantation near Uganda’s Queen Elizabeth National Park. The eight-room eco-lodge supports a collective of coffee farmers and has cleverly used detritus from local villages in its design. Human-animal conflict is a very real problem in these parts; elephants can destroy a family’s subsistence crops in minutes. So Volcanoes has helped villagers learn beekeeping — elephants are terrified of bees — which allows them to protect crops and establish a sweet new revenue stream: honey. Four-day safaris from $510 per night; volcanoessafaris.com.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jungle Nook', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jungle Nook', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Uganda', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T11:00:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Heyman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Heyman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6d08697-e002-5942-9120-7233b1ba85d1', 'word_count': 172, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6d08697-e002-5942-9120-7233b1ba85d1'}, {'abstract': 'Two social change groups recently joined forces. The result? They are now housing homeless people faster than ever.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/whe-one-fix-leads-to-another/', 'snippet': 'Two social change groups recently joined forces. The result? They are now housing homeless people faster than ever.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week in Washington, people from Detroit, Tucson, New Orleans, San Diego, Atlanta and nine other cities gathered to celebrate doing the impossible. The participants share a tough job:\xa0 getting homeless veterans off the street and into apartments and social services. \xa0They work in cities that have large numbers of homeless vets — but most of their cities were making only modest progress toward housing them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Teaming Up to End Homelessness', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homeless Persons', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smoking and Tobacco', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Impact Bonds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T11:00:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tina Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8093a8a0-a5bd-549b-bc3f-09eadbd749a7', 'word_count': 1465, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8093a8a0-a5bd-549b-bc3f-09eadbd749a7'}, {'abstract': 'People seem happy, but the question I now ask myself is, Is it all a front?', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/is-it-a-mistake-to-pick-an-employee-of-the-month/', 'snippet': 'People seem happy, but the question I now ask myself is, Is it all a front?', 'lead_paragraph': 'I recently met a management consultant and business author who asked me if I had an “employee of the month” program. I said I did, at which point he reprimanded me for the error of my ways. His argument was that it was a waste of time and was actually counterproductive; only one person wins, and the rest are resentful. My managers and I actually considered that before we started the program, but the conversation with the consultant, Aubrey C. Daniels, got me thinking about it again. As I have gotten older, I have become more open-minded about recognizing that my way might not be the best way.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is It a Mistake to Pick an Employee of the Month?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T11:00:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jay Goltz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goltz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'ra