, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Palmer, Amanda', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN FEDERATION OF MUSICIANS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T11:53:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eba911eb-6760-5139-b980-b4df0b3ac8c3', 'word_count': 676, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eba911eb-6760-5139-b980-b4df0b3ac8c3'}, {'abstract': 'The replacement of a pipeline that ruptured in 2010 with a line that has a far bigger diameter has some Michigan residents up in arms.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/on-our-radar-a-pipeline-land-grab/', 'snippet': 'The replacement of a pipeline that ruptured in 2010 with a line that has a far bigger diameter has some Michigan residents up in arms.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The replacement of Line 6B, a 43-year-old pipeline that leaked more than one million gallons of heavy crude into the Kalamazoo River in Michigan, faces opposition from landowners who do not want more of their land taken over to accommodate the new one. [InsideClimate News]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Our Radar: A Pipeline Land Grab?', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T11:56:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5a7b5d8-d9fe-52f1-96c0-b866c19c6c8c', 'word_count': 235, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5a7b5d8-d9fe-52f1-96c0-b866c19c6c8c'}, {'abstract': 'A smartphone application that gives an updated prediction for football games after each play may be as notable for what it says about gambling as for what it reveals about football.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/the-potential-value-of-in-game-n-f-l-predictions/', 'snippet': 'A smartphone application that gives an updated prediction for football games after each play may be as notable for what it says about gambling as for what it reveals about football.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The creator of a new smartphone application that gives an updated prediction for football games after each play in real time says it can offer fans a fresh look at the game. But the app may be as notable for what it says about gambling as for what it reveals about the game.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Potential Value of In-Game N.F.L. Predictions', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gambling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T12:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joshua Brustein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joshua', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brustein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9efc3940-e17b-5839-a03b-abba0699a96a', 'word_count': 610, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9efc3940-e17b-5839-a03b-abba0699a96a'}, {'abstract': 'Answers to questions about public service loan forgiveness, options for people with private loans who are struggling with their debts and the impact of student loans on debtors’ credit score.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/answers-to-your-questions-about-student-loans-part-one/', 'snippet': 'Answers to questions about public service loan forgiveness, options for people with private loans who are struggling with their debts and the impact of student loans on debtors’ credit score.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week, two New York Times reporters and Geoffry Walsh, an expert on student debt and bankruptcy at the National Consumer Law Center, are answering questions about ways to avoid default, pay off student loans or try to expunge student loans through bankruptcy court. The first set of answers is below.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Answers to Your Questions About Student Loans, Part 1', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Scores', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Student Loans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T12:00:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Martin and Ron Lieber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lieber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/26cd752e-09ca-5d4b-88db-4afc2efef49d', 'word_count': 915, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26cd752e-09ca-5d4b-88db-4afc2efef49d'}, {'abstract': 'An attack that killed the United States ambassador to Libya on Tuesday night has brought the issue of foreign policy to the forefront of the presidential race.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/obama-condemns-attack-that-kills-ambassador-to-libya/', 'snippet': 'An attack that killed the United States ambassador to Libya on Tuesday night has brought the issue of foreign policy to the forefront of the presidential race.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An attack that killed the American ambassador to Libya on Tuesday night has brought foreign policy to the forefront of the presidential race, puncturing the solemn unity seen on the campaign trail one day earlier as both candidates observed the anniversary of the Sept. 11 terrorist attacks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Condemns Attack That Kills Ambassador to Libya', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T12:04:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Baker and Sarah Wheaton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wheaton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa3fa92e-f47d-56b0-af2b-20319819918c', 'word_count': 572, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa3fa92e-f47d-56b0-af2b-20319819918c'}, {'abstract': 'The splashy show opening next month at London’s Victoria and Albert Museum, “Hollywood Costume,” will unspool like a highlight reel of classic cinema getups.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/tinsel-gowns/', 'snippet': 'The splashy show opening next month at London’s Victoria and Albert Museum, “Hollywood Costume,” will unspool like a highlight reel of classic cinema getups.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The splashy show opening next month at London’s Victoria and Albert Museum, “Hollywood Costume,” will unspool like a highlight reel of classic cinema getups. There’s Dorothy’s pinafore and ruby slippers, Walter Plunkett’s immortal “drapery dress” for Scarlett O’Hara and Hubert de Givenchy’s sleeveless black gown from “Breakfast at Tiffany’s.” The exhibit, which runs through January, is curated by Deborah Nadoolman Landis, a costume designer who’s thrown in her own rugged creation for Indiana Jones from “Raiders of the Lost Ark.”', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tinsel Gowns', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tinsel Gowns', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T12:04:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Farran Smith Nehme', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Farran', 'middlename': 'Smith', 'lastname': 'Nehme', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06aec7a2-0539-5f80-8ede-daa4617f8a83', 'word_count': 230, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06aec7a2-0539-5f80-8ede-daa4617f8a83'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/morning-take-out-556/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOP STORIES', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Take-Out', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T12:09:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4dbb0dc4-b676-58df-8834-4260a2e44194', 'word_count': 2083, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4dbb0dc4-b676-58df-8834-4260a2e44194'}, {'abstract': 'A summary of what’s on today’s editorial page.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/opinion-report-chicago-teachers-strike/', 'snippet': 'A summary of what’s on today’s editorial page.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From the editorial page', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Opinion Report: Chicago Teachers’ Strike', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T12:12:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d48ece5d-baa7-50e0-83d6-cebac011f30b', 'word_count': 60, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d48ece5d-baa7-50e0-83d6-cebac011f30b'}, {'abstract': 'In a close election, Mitt Romney would face a daunting challenge if he failed to win Florida’s 29 electoral votes.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/sept-11-florida-a-true-must-win-for-romney/', 'snippet': 'In a close election, Mitt Romney would face a daunting challenge if he failed to win Florida’s 29 electoral votes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Florida has a well-established reputation as a swing state. But as the election season has worn on, it has come to look even more important. Florida now ranks a clear second on our list of tipping point states, those most likely to provide the decisive votes in the Electoral College, behind only Ohio.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sept. 11: Florida a True Must-Win for Romney', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electoral College', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T12:13:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41c2e56d-a13e-5f57-b91b-539f8b015c03', 'word_count': 1144, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41c2e56d-a13e-5f57-b91b-539f8b015c03'}, {'abstract': 'Chris Stevens arrived back in Tripoli in May as the U.S. ambassador. In July, he e-mailed friends to give his first impressions about the country after the fall of Muammar al-Qaddafi and his hopes for the future.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/slain-u-s-ambassadors-letter-to-friends-and-family/', 'snippet': 'Chris Stevens arrived back in Tripoli in May as the U.S. ambassador. In July, he e-mailed friends to give his first impressions about the country after the fall of Muammar al-Qaddafi and his hopes for the future.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — I last heard from Chris Stevens two months ago, just after he hosted a July 4 reception in the gardens of the U.S. embassy in Tripoli, Libya.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Letter to Friends, Slain U.S. Ambassador Expressed Hope', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transitional National Council (Libya)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T12:16:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Morris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/35d2f8e6-5888-5001-a66a-20351d5c8690', 'word_count': 719, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35d2f8e6-5888-5001-a66a-20351d5c8690'}, {'abstract': 'By building warehouses across the country, Amazon.com hopes to cut as much as a day off its two-day shipping times. But the warehouses also mean it must start collecting sales tax in many states. Amazon will begin collecting sales tax in California on Saturday.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/daily-report-amazon-will-collect-sales-tax-to-expand-boldly/', 'snippet': 'By building warehouses across the country, Amazon.com hopes to cut as much as a day off its two-day shipping times. But the warehouses also mean it must start collecting sales tax in many states. Amazon will begin collecting sales tax in Californi...', 'lead_paragraph': ' Amazon is building massive distribution centers near several major cities. This multibillion-dollar building frenzy means Amazon is about to lose perhaps its biggest competitive edge — that it does not charge sales tax on the vast majority of its customers, reports David Streitfeld of The New York Times. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-jumbo-v6.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-superJumbo-v3.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thum