ntrast to the government’s reaction to cartoon critiques today.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/under-the-british-satire-and-critical-cartooning-thrived-in-india/', 'snippet': 'A sharp contrast to the government’s reaction to cartoon critiques today.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Christmas Day in 1887, a Mumbai paper, Parsee Punch, ran a cartoon depicting India striking a gong of Congress by the ear of a slumbering John Bull. “Rousing the sentinel,” ran the caption. It was only one of thousands of politically charged illustrations that would be carried in the weekly, which first appeared in July 1854 and was still being published well into the 1930s under the name Hindi Punch.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Under the British, Satire and Critical Cartooning Thrived in India', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Archives and Records', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cartoons and Cartoonists', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bull, John', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Archives and Records Administration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mumbai (India)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T12:43:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Naresh Fernandes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Naresh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fernandes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/78ec796d-0c84-500a-b155-4bde42730d45', 