the economy, it’s the perception of trend. If the economy appears to be improving, the incumbent tends to do well even if in absolute terms it’s still pretty bad.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Economic Fundamentals and the Election', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T13:02:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c4b86b6-93f9-5b73-b8ef-f2e7de76724b', 'word_count': 331, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c4b86b6-93f9-5b73-b8ef-f2e7de76724b'}, {'abstract': 'An analysis of Apple’s patent filings offer a look at the company’s long-term ambitions for the iPhone. The report by Thomson Reuters points, for example, to a miniature fuel-cell as a power source that could keep an iPhone going for days or weeks without recharging.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/the-patent-clues-to-the-apple-iphone-beyond-5/', 'snippet': 'An analysis of Apple’s patent filings offer a look at the company’s long-term ambitions for the iPhone. The report by Thomson Reuters points, for example, to a miniature fuel-cell as a power source that could keep an iPhone going for days or weeks...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bigger screen, longer battery life, clever new features. It’s another version of the iPhone, waiting in the wings to be announced on Wednesday, as everyone expects.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Patent Clues to the Apple iPhone Beyond ‘5’', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inventions and Patents', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T13:04:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Lohr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lohr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a963e30-ac45-5f0f-8e7a-bf27b641ee2a', 'word_count': 326, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a963e30-ac45-5f0f-8e7a-bf27b641ee2a'}, {'abstract': 'The Chesapeake Energy Corporation said on Wednesday that it had agreed to a series of asset sales as part of an effort to reduce its considerable debt burden.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/chesapeake-to-sell-assets-for-6-9-billion/', 'snippet': 'The Chesapeake Energy Corporation said on Wednesday that it had agreed to a series of asset sales as part of an effort to reduce its considerable debt burden.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Chesapeake Energy Corporation said on Wednesday that it had agreed to a series of asset sales, including the majority of its holdings in the Permian Basin. The move will raise $6.9 billion as it seeks to repay some of its considerable debt burden.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chesapeake Energy to Sell Assets for $6.9 Billion', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Natural Gas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chesapeake Energy Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chevron Corpor