as simple as that.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The American International Group, of all companies, wants to avoid a rule designed to stop risky trading. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why A.I.G. May Not Be Able to Avoid the Volcker Rule', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Benmosche, Robert H', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN INTERNATIONAL GROUP INC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T13:43:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Eavis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eavis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/efb940b3-e758-5794-9b80-b2beac6cd167', 'word_count': 815, 'uri': 'nyt://article/efb940b3-e758-5794-9b80-b2beac6cd167'}, {'abstract': 'In the third “Darn Squirrels” book by Adam Rubin and Daniel Salmieri, squirrels join birds on a trip down south.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/books/the-third-darn-squirrels-book-by-adam-rubin-and-daniel-salmieri.html', 'snippet': 'In the third “Darn Squirrels” book by Adam Rubin and Daniel Salmieri, squirrels join birds on a trip down south.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just what makes a picture book great is often a mystery. A captivating story needn’t be a great adventure or have an especially happy ending. It may not include a single dragon or dinosaur, no princesses, pirates or petulant children. There may be no children at all. And yet somehow the book is still great.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/books/13childrens-img/13childrens-img-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/13/books/13childrens-img/13childrens-img-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/books/13childrens-img/13childrens-img-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/books/13childrens-img/13childrens-img-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 720, 'width': 1440, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/books/13childrens-img/13childrens-img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/13/books/13childrens-img/13childrens-img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/books/13childrens-img/13childrens-img-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Old Man and the Squirrels', 'kicker': "Children's Books", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rubin, Adam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T13:48:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pamela Paul', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pamela', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Paul', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/099dda45-0e23-55e0-b465-44a2ca07d3b2', 'word_count': 509, 'uri': 'nyt://article/099dda45-0e23-55e0-b465-44a2ca07d3b2'}, {'abstract': 'Students could be found in contingency programs at schools, in churches and in day care centers. Some slept late, stayed home alone and wandered neighborhoods.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/education/chicago-teachers-strike-enters-third-day.html', 'snippet': 'Students could be found in contingency programs at schools, in churches and in day care centers. Some slept late, stayed home alone and wandered neighborhoods.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — For hundreds of thousands of families here, ordinary life has turned upside down. As Chicago public schoolteachers on Wednesday spent a third day on picket lines, their students could be found in contingency programs at schools, in churches and in costly day care centers. Some slept late, stayed home alone, then wandered their neighborhoods as if there were one more chapter of summer. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/us/STRIKE-1/STRIKE-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/13/us/STRIKE-1/STRIKE-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/us/STRIKE-1/STRIKE-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/us/STRIKE-1/STRIKE-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/us/STRIKE-1/STRIKE-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/13/us/STRIKE-1/STRIKE-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/us/STRIKE-1/STRIKE-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'As Chicago Teachers Strike, Students Are on the Loose and at Loose Ends', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Chicago, on the Loose And at Loose Ends', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Teachers Union', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Strikes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T13:55:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Monica Davey and Steven Yaccino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Monica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yaccino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/911f8975-1ad5-5342-b7e1-a9eebeb8a9f8', 'word_count': 1042, 'uri': 'nyt://article/911f8975-1ad5-5342-b7e1-a9eebeb8a9f8'}, {'abstract': 'The most frequent reason given by men 25 to 54 for leaving the labor force over the last 15 years was illness or disability. For women, a majority left to become household caregivers.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/why-men-drop-out-of-the-labor-force/', 'snippet': 'The most frequent reason given by men 25 to 54 for leaving the labor force over the last 15 years was illness or disability. For women, a majority left to become household caregivers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As I mentioned on Friday, the share of men who are actively in the labor force is at an all-time low (a trend David Brooks also explored in his column Tuesday). Now Steve Hipple, an economist at the Labor Department, points me to a related paper from the Federal Reserve Bank of Atlanta, which helps explain why.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Men Drop Out of the Labor Force', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T14:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/69260c80-3278-5c14-b212-1074247c34bb', 'word_count': 314, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69260c80-3278-5c14-b212-1074247c34bb'}, {'abstract': 'By now, we know that it’s rude to play Angry Birds at the table, or ignore your date while you post an update to Facebook and Twitter. But what are the other rules that are starting to form concerning the dos and don’ts of digital etiquette?', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/ask-us-your-digital-etiquette-questions/', 'snippet': 'By now, we know that it’s rude to play Angry Birds at the table, or ignore your date while you post an update to Facebook and Twitter. But what are the other rules that are starting to form concerning the dos and don’ts of digital etiquette?', 'lead_paragraph': ' Most of us know that it’s rude to text at the dinner table or talk on the phone while paying for groceries at the store — even if we do it anyway.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ask Us Your Digital Etiquette Questions', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs, Etiquette and Manners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T14:00:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenna Wortham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wortham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c5d04511-9db2-5e07-83ec-1378d4b2750c', 'word_count': 327, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c5d04511-9db2-5e07-83ec-1378d4b2750c'}, {'abstract': 'PollWatchUSA, which enables reports in real time of undue delays, trouble getting or casting a ballot, or harassment or intimidation, will be tested at the primary elections on Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/new-app-to-help-voters-expose-trouble-at-the-polls/', 'snippet': 'PollWatchUSA, which enables reports in real time of undue delays, trouble getting or casting a ballot, or harassment or intimidation, will be tested at the primary elections on Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new app that lets voters flag polling-place irregularities will be tested at the primaries on Thursday and, if it works well, will be rolled out citywide for the November general election.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New App to Help Voters Expose Trouble at the Polls', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Board of Elections (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Common Cause', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Personal Democracy Forum', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T14:02:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Roberts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roberts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25f80715-c2b3-56a9-88d5-f26c076b6bfa', 'word_count': 559, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25f80715-c2b3-56a9-88d5-f26c076b6bfa'}, {'abstract': 'The start-up, called M-Go, is expected to announce agreements with five of Hollywood’s six major movie studios that will allow it to stream or rent movies as soon as they are released on DVD or Blu-ray.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/a-new-movie-streaming-service-has-commitments-from-studios/', 'snippet': 'The start-up, called M-Go, is expected to announce agreements with five of Hollywood’s six major movie studios that will allow it to stream or rent movies as soon as they are released on DVD or Blu-ray.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new digital entertainment service called M-Go is expected on Wednesday to announce agreements with five of Hollywood’s six major movie studios that will allow M-Go to stream or rent movies as soon as they are released on DVD or Blu-ray.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Movie Streaming Service Has Commitments From Studios', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T14:11:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a981bd3b-bb29-56e3-a603-32d0a8bf4cfe', 'word_count': 220, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a981bd3b-bb29-56e3-a603-32d0a8bf4cfe'}, {'abstract': 'The popular chewing tobacco and betel nut product is linked to India’s high rates of oral cancer.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/delhis-gutka-ban-hailed-even-by-users/', 'snippet': 'The popular chewing tobacco and betel nut product is linked to India’s high rates of oral cancer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Delhi state government’s ban of gutka, a popular product made from betel nut and chewing tobacco, has drawn protests from manufacturers, but found support from an unlikely group of people – those who actually buy and sell the product.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Delhi’s Gutka Ban Hailed, Even By Users', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smoking and Tobacco', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Delhi (India)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T14:15:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hari Kumar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hari', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kumar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7c3bdbf-6146-5a53-81e4-e257265e804a', 'word_count': 599, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7c3bdbf-6146-5a53-81e4-e257265e804a'}, {'abstract': 'The new play “The Two Worlds of Charlie F” casts wounded soldiers in the roles of wounded soldiers. The result is extraordinary.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/on-the-two-worlds-of-charlie-f/', 'snippet': 'The new play “The Two Worlds of Charlie F” casts wounded soldiers in the roles of wounded soldiers. The result is extraordinary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — A letter written by Corporal Stephen Shaw of the Princess of Wales Royal Regiment should have arrived at the White House by now. In it Shaw describes a play in which he has acted, “The Two Worlds of Charlie F.” And he says that he and the rest of the theater company — Bravo 22 Company — who have just finished touring Britain, would love to come to Washington to perform for President Barack Obama and help American W.I.S. (wounded, injured and sick) service personnel get involved in a similar project. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Johnny Got His Part', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T14:16:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kamila Shamsie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kamila', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shamsie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b00c34c-4a53-58be-ad2a-696aa1326b6d', 'word_count': 624, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b00c34c-4a53-58be-ad2a-696aa1326b6d'}, {'abstract': 'Cartoonist held in Mumbai wants overturn of sedition law.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/released-from-jail-cartoonist-vows-to-fight-sedition-law/', 'snippet': 'Cartoonist held in Mumbai wants overturn of sedition law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The cartoonist Aseem Trivedi was released from jail Wednesday, following the Mumbai High Court’s orders.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Released From Jail, Cartoonist Vows to Fight Sedition Law', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cartoons and Cartoonists', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hazare, Anna', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nehru, Jawaharlal', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Reporters Without Borders', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mumbai (India)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T14:24:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hari Kumar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hari', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kumar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b3e36d6-e2d2-5d61-bd6f-8baaf7c59fc2', 'word_count': 316, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b3e36d6-e2d2-5d61-bd6f-8baaf7c59fc2'}, {'abstract': 'Companies often focus too much on Web traffic and forget to work on turning that traffic into revenue.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/business/smallbusiness/three-keys-to-converting-web-visitors-into-buyers.html', 'snippet': 'Companies often focus too much on Web traffic and forget to work on turning that traffic into revenue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When potential customers search the Internet for Botox or laser hair removal in the greater New York City area, Verve Medical Cosmetics has long been easy to find. But the company’s Web site has been more successful attracting visitors than it has been converting those visitors into new customers, according to Michele Bracci, the company’s director of marketing and the wife of its founder, Dr. Stephen Bracci.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/business/smallbusiness/13sbiz-1/13sbiz-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/business/smallbusiness/13sbiz-1/13sbiz-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/business/smallbusiness/13sbiz-1/13sbiz-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/13/business/smallbusiness/13sbiz-1/13sbiz-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/business/smallbusiness/13sbiz-1/13sbiz-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Three Proven Ways to Convert Visitors Into Buyers Online', 'kicker': 'Small-Business Guide', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Three Proven Ways To Convert Visitors Into Buyers Online', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customer Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T14:29:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Reynolds Lewis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': 'Reynolds', 'lastname': 'Lewis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_materi