ection_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Monica Drake', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Monica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Drake', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a73a0243-46e2-5837-83e3-3afa7a10ca71', 'word_count': 165, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a73a0243-46e2-5837-83e3-3afa7a10ca71'}, {'abstract': 'In an interview with Rolling Stone Bob Dylan speaks out about race relations, and responds to critics.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/dylan-says-slavery-still-stains-united-states/', 'snippet': 'In an interview with Rolling Stone Bob Dylan speaks out about race relations, and responds to critics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a new interview in Rolling Stone, Bob Dylan spoke out about the continuing taint of slavery on the United States, according to The Associated Press. America was “founded on the back of slaves,” Mr. Dylan said. “If slavery had been given up in a more peaceful way, America would be far ahead today.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dylan Says Slavery Still Stains United States', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dylan Says Slavery Still Stains U.S.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dylan, Bob', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rolling Stone', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T17:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/49fd313a-a1fe-52fe-a272-3857a46520a7', 'word_count': 188, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49fd313a-a1fe-52fe-a272-3857a46520a7'}, {'abstract': 'Holmes & Yang is the fashion collection started by the actress Katie Holmes and the stylist Jeanne Yang three years ago. But, for some reason, everyone was particularly excited about seeing it this season.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/really-were-just-here-to-see-katie/', 'snippet': 'Holmes & Yang is the fashion collection started by the actress Katie Holmes and the stylist Jeanne Yang three years ago. But, for some reason, everyone was particularly excited about seeing it this season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Holmes & Yang is the fashion collection started by the actress Katie Holmes and the stylist Jeanne Yang three years ago. But, for some reason, everyone was particularly excited about seeing it this season. There were paparazzi outside Lincoln Center, or more than usual, anyway. It was as if the designers were famous for something.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Really, We’re Just Here to See Katie', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Fashion Week', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holmes, Katie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T17:02:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a99cd106-555a-52af-8457-7bf625c621e9', 'word_count': 247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a99cd106-555a-52af-8457-7bf625c621e9'}, {'abstract': 'Researchers warn that the city’s aeration process could pose risks for air quality.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/whats-bubbling-up-from-newtown-creek/', 'snippet': 'Researchers warn that the city’s aeration process could pose risks for air quality.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Reached aboard a boat in Newtown Creek the other day, John Lipscomb of the advocacy group Riverkeeper described the water by phone. “It’s this green-blue chalky color,” he said. “You’re floating around and there are dead rats, condoms, and there’s this stench of sewage – this sulphuric smell.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s Bubbling Up From Newtown Creek?', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Department of Environmental Protection (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Queens College, City University of New York', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Riverkeeper', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Newtown Creek (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T17:05:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emma Bryce', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emma', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bryce', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/07ebee1f-9a60-54b1-a274-73b27f6ba17b', 'word_count': 632, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07ebee1f-9a60-54b1-a274-73b27f6ba17b'}, {'abstract': 'The man featured in a New York Times article about student loans and bankruptcy must return to federal court on Jan. 28 to discuss his medical issues and whether he is employable.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/an-update-on-a-student-debt-case/', 'snippet': 'The man featured in a New York Times article about student loans and bankruptcy must return to federal court on Jan. 28 to discuss his medical issues and whether he is employable.', 'lead_paragraph': ' In an article about what happens to people who try to get a judge to discharge their student loans in bankruptcy court, I told the story of Doug Wallace, a blind man in Ohio in the middle of his own case. He’s trying to prove that paying his debt would cause an “undue hardship,” according to the governing legal standard. To do so, he needs to prove, among other things, that there is a “certainty of hopelessness” that he will be unable to pay his debt during the term of the loans.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Update on a Student Debt Case', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Bankruptcies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Student Loans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T17:05:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Lieber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lieber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/52042a50-32e6-5ca2-9da7-68ec9454c00a', 'word_count': 169, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52042a50-32e6-5ca2-9da7-68ec9454c00a'}, {'abstract': 'President Hamid Karzai condemning the attack on Wednesday said his office “strongly and resolutely denounces this desecrating act and declares its serious abhorrence in the face of such an insult.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/world/asia/afghan-leader-hamid-karzai-condemns-anti-islam-film.html', 'snippet': 'President Hamid Karzai condemning the attack on Wednesday said his office “strongly and resolutely denounces this desecrating act and declares its serious abhorrence in the face of such an insult.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — President Hamid Karzai condemned an anti-Islam film that has been backed by the American pastor Terry Jones, issuing a statement on Wednesday that said his office “strongly and resolutely denounces this desecrating act and declares its serious abhorrence in the face of such an insult.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Afghan Leader Condemns Anti-Islam Film', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Afghan Leader Condemns Anti-Islam Film', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karzai, Hamid', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Terry (Pastor)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T17:09:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rod Nordland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rod', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nordland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e39ed4bd-10ac-5bf5-a992-41f8a37ccbeb', 'word_count': 366, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e39ed4bd-10ac-5bf5-a992-41f8a37ccbeb'}, {'abstract': 'Scenes from the New York fashion week photo diary of Bryan Derballa.', 'web_url': 'https://