annual report on income, poverty and health insurance coverage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Census Bureau just released its sweeping annual report on income, poverty and health insurance coverage.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Behind the Decline in Incomes', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Census Bureau', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T17:24:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6526e5ea-64fe-576c-a813-27f0939979da', 'word_count': 238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6526e5ea-64fe-576c-a813-27f0939979da'}, {'abstract': 'The trailer for the video at the center of the violence in Libya and Egypt was uploaded to the Web by an individual whose identity remains in question.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/world/middleeast/origins-of-provocative-video-shrouded.html', 'snippet': 'The trailer for the video at the center of the violence in Libya and Egypt was uploaded to the Web by an individual whose identity remains in question.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — The film that set off violence across North Africa was made in obscurity somewhere in the sprawl of Southern California, and promoted by a network of right-wing Christians with a history of animosity directed toward Muslims. When a 14-minute trailer of it — all that may actually exist — was posted on YouTube in June, it was barely noticed.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/world/provoke/provoke-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 753, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/world/provoke/provoke-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1507, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Origins of Provocative Video Are Shrouded', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Video That Stoked Violence Has Murky History', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Innocence of Muslims (Movie)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klein, Steve', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bacile, Sam', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Terry (Pastor)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T17:30:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Nagourney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nagourney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6920b833-2791-5299-9d51-899c6aa24563', 'word_count': 1215, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6920b833-2791-5299-9d51-899c6aa24563'}, {'abstract': 'The company’s engagement at Lincoln Center will feature 21 dances.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/paul-taylor-dance-company-announces-spring-season/', 'snippet': 'The company’s engagement at Lincoln Center will feature 21 dances.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Paul Taylor Dance Company will be among the many arts groups celebrating the 100th anniversary of Stravinsky’s “Rite of Spring” in the coming year. The troupe will revive Mr. Taylor’s “Sacre Du Printemps (The Rehearsal)” as part of its spring season, which will run from March 5 to 24 at Lincoln Center, the company announced.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paul Taylor Dance Announces Spring Season', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Paul Taylor Announces Spring Season Lineup', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taylor, Paul', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taylor, Paul, Dance Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T17:30:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bloom', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bloom', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62f693d1-aeca-5e35-9711-5dfb4bbf8991', 'word_count': 138, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62f693d1-aeca-5e35-9711-5dfb4bbf8991'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney feels Barack Obama has been overly sensitive to the grievances of America’s enemies.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/book-suggests-roots-of-romneys-sentiments-on-crisis/', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney feels Barack Obama has been overly sensitive to the grievances of America’s enemies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To understand why Mitt Romney was so quick to condemn President Obama for “sympathizing with those who waged the attacks” in Libya, read Mr. Romney’s 325-page political manifesto, “No Apology,” whose very title encapsulates his approach to such moments.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Book Suggests Roots of Romney’s Sentiments on Crisis', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Americans Abroad', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Czech Republic', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Poland', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T17:31:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Barbaro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barbaro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bfd8ad8c-d41a-5763-ad7e-560dfe06bfd0', 'word_count': 400, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bfd8ad8c-d41a-5763-ad7e-560dfe06bfd0'}, {'abstract': 'Sixty-one percent of voters said they believed the state’s laws pertaining to gun sales should be tougher, according to a poll conducted by Quinnipiac University.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/most-new-yorkers-favor-stricter-gun-laws-poll-finds/', 'snippet': 'Sixty-one percent of voters said they believed the state’s laws pertaining to gun sales should be tougher, according to a poll conducted by Quinnipiac University.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALBANY – Following mass shootings this summer in Colorado and Wisconsin, a majority of voters in New York State favor more stringent laws restricting the purchase of guns, according to a poll released Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Most New Yorkers Favor Stricter Gun Laws, Poll Finds', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stiffer Gun Laws Popular in State, A Survey Finds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gianaris, Michael N', 'rank': 6, 'majo