://article/9496c6af-a225-5978-8b98-d7098d608cb4'}, {'abstract': 'Did Anna Wintour start a trend? Just about everyone, including CNN’s Alina Cho, Allure magazine’s Linda Wells, and Simon Collins, the dean of fashion at Parsons The New School for Design, wore dark sunglasses at the 9 a.m. Tory Burch show at Lincoln Center on Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/fashion-week-stargazing-day-6/', 'snippet': 'Did Anna Wintour start a trend? Just about everyone, including CNN’s Alina Cho, Allure magazine’s Linda Wells, and Simon Collins, the dean of fashion at Parsons The New School for Design, wore dark sunglasses at the 9 a.m. Tory Burch show at Linco...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Did Anna Wintour start a trend? Just about everyone, including CNN’s Alina Cho, Allure magazine’s Linda Wells and Simon Collins, the dean of fashion at Parsons The New School for Design, wore dark sunglasses at the 9 a.m. Tory Burch show at Lincoln Center on Tuesday. In truth, it was less a trend than functional accessory. There was the incredible sunlight, which streamed in through an entire wall of windows at Avery Fisher Hall, and, of course, the increasing lack of sleep for Fashion Week attendees.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fashion Week Stargazing: Day 6', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Celebrities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Fashion Week', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T17:47:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bee-Shyuan Chang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bee-shyuan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f26