ey’re getting the showcase of Lincoln Center,” said Rob Daniels, the company’s spokesman.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quid pro Furniture at City Ballet', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Koch, David H, Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Ballet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T18:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b27da262-4be2-5bfd-a786-c7dd616bfda6', 'word_count': 143, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b27da262-4be2-5bfd-a786-c7dd616bfda6'}, {'abstract': 'David Byrne’s new book is a jumble of thoughts from the co-founder of Talking Heads.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/books/how-music-works-by-david-byrne.html', 'snippet': 'David Byrne’s new book is a jumble of thoughts from the co-founder of Talking Heads.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The critic Clive James once began a review of a Leonid Brezhnev biography by observing that it was so dull that “if it were read in the open air, birds would fall stunned from the sky.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/arts/BOOK/BOOK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 696, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/arts/BOOK/BOOK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1392, 'subType': 