e}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Fashion Week', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Betsey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rodarte', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T18:58:28+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Fashion & Style', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By JOHN ORTVED', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'ORTVED', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/ef899457-92cc-5d9d-8b1c-236a4bab5c11', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/ef899457-92cc-5d9d-8b1c-236a4bab5c11'}, {'abstract': 'The central bank would become chief regulator of all banks in the euro zone, but many details have not been worked out about how it would handle the job.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/business/global/ecb-to-get-more-clout-even-if-it-isnt-ready.html', 'snippet': 'The central bank would become chief regulator of all banks in the euro zone, but many details have not been worked out about how it would handle the job.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRANKFURT — To the European Central Bank’s existing duties — bulwark against inflation, lender of last resort, ultimate guardian of the euro — add another task: top cop for the euro zone’s banking system.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/business/ECB/ECB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 718, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/business/ECB/ECB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1437, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'European Central Bank May Get an Enforcement Role', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'European Central Bank May Get an Enforcement Role', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Central Bank', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T18:59:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Ewing', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ewing', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e3c5f02-240e-5414-ad72-00eb0144391a', 'word_count': 1246, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e3c5f02-240e-5414-ad72-00eb0144391a'}, {'abstract': 'Meeting locals abroad while traveling can seem like a daunting proposition. A new hotel in Berlin strives to change that.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/freund-with-benefits/', 'snippet': 'Meeting locals abroad while traveling can seem like a daunting proposition. A new hotel in Berlin strives to change that.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the impatient, socially awkward, unilingual traveler — in other words, for many of us — meeting locals can sometimes seem like a daunting proposition. But what if they came bundled in your hotel price, like Wi-Fi or a fruit basket? In March, Clare Freeman, a British expat and a veteran of Design Hotels, opened Plus One Berlin, a one-room concept hotel that operates a bit like a platonic escort service. Freeman gut-renovated a studio apartment in the city’s rapidly gentrifying Kreuzkölln district and turned the space into an airy urban refuge. She has since enlisted 35 locals, many of whom are her friends, to show guests Berlin from a Berliner’s point of view. “It’s a curated network,” she says of her associates. “You know you’re not getting just anyone.” You might get a German portrait photographer, a Serbian astrophysicist or a Roman coffee aficionado for, say, a quick afternoon drink to get restaurant suggestions or a half day spent as a guide’s plus-one. Past outings include record-release parties, lessons on flea-market haggling and pop-up film screenings at Yaam, a Jamaican beach club on the Spree. Each booking includes a jaunt with a local, and guests can pick whom they’d like to meet and schedule an appointment online. From about $150 per night; plusoneberlin.com.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Freund With Benefits', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Freund With Benefits', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T19:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Heyman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Heyman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1c6fee8-0c26-52c9-b434-196d9db3a541', 'word_count': 214, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1c6fee8-0c26-52c9-b434-196d9db3a541'}, {'abstract': 'A day after Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu criticized the Obama administration over Iran, Israelis were sympathetic to Mr. Netanyahu even as they mulled the possible damage to ties with the White House.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/world/middleeast/netanyahus-comments-cause-stir-in-israel.html', 'snippet': 'A day after Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu criticized the Obama administration over Iran, Israelis were sympathetic to Mr. Netanyahu even as they mulled the possible damage to ties with the White House.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — In Israel, where arguments are rife, there are at least two issues of national consensus: that the special relationship with the United States must be preserved at all costs, and that the looming threat of a nuclear Iran must be dealt with. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/world/israel/israel-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 729, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/world/israel/israel-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1458, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Israelis Fear Fallout From Netanyahu’s Blunt Comments', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Israelis Fear Fallout From Netanyahu’s Blunt Comments', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netanyahu, Benjamin', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'