59a53f4a5'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama’s aides indicated he would have reconsidered his trip had the violence in Libya and Egypt spilled into a second day in a major way, but follow-up protests were relatively modest.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/despite-libyan-crisis-obama-campaign-plans-to-stay-on-schedule/', 'snippet': 'President Obama’s aides indicated he would have reconsidered his trip had the violence in Libya and Egypt spilled into a second day in a major way, but follow-up protests were relatively modest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAS VEGAS – President Obama may be consumed with an international crisis, but the campaign goes on as planned, at least at this point. The president is still scheduled to start a Western campaign swing Wednesday night, with a rally here in Las Vegas and another in Colorado on Thursday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Despite Libyan Crisis, Obama Campaign Plans to Stay on Schedule', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Las Vegas (Nev)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T19:44:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Rutenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rutenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca30794f-aac0-5443-ba38-be66c31a8dff', 'word_count': 396, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca30794f-aac0-5443-ba38-be66c31a8dff'}, {'abstract': 'Readers complained to the public editor over The Times’s decision to display a photograph of the unconscious ambassador in Libya.', 'web_url': 'https://publiceditor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/was-photo-of-dead-ambassador-acceptable/', 'snippet': 'Readers complained to the public editor over The Times’s decision to display a photograph of the unconscious ambassador in Libya.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Where is the line between good taste and important journalism? And did The Times cross it when it used, in a Wednesday afternoon online photo gallery, an image of an unconscious J. Christopher Stevens, the ambassador, who was killed in an attack on the American Consulate in Benghazi, Libya?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Was Photo of Dead Ambassador Acceptable?', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T19:44:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e4d858d-8e13-55e4-8bab-ee34eecf6d33', 'word_count': 603, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e4d858d-8e13-55e4-8bab-ee34eecf6d33'}, {'abstract': 'In an internal memo circulated on Wednesday, the bank said it would break its corporate and investment banking division into two units.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/jpmorgan-reshuffles-its-operations-again/', 'snippet': 'In an internal memo circulated on Wednesday, the bank said it would break its corporate and investment banking division into two units.', 'lead_paragraph': '4:05 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'JPMorgan Reshuffles Its Operations Again', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JPMorgan Chase & Company', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T19:45:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jessica Silver-Greenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jessica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver-Greenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d3d6294-9fa2-5aec-bfeb-89bb9ce7f64b', 'word_count': 266, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d3d6294-9fa2-5aec-bfeb-89bb9ce7f64b'}, {'abstract': 'In this lesson, students will define hydrofracking, identify how demand for natural gas is changing and why this method is controversial, then map how natural gas development may impact a community.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/fuel-for-debate-examining-the-natural-gas-fracking-controversy/', 'snippet': 'In this lesson, students will define hydrofracking, identify how demand for natural gas is changing and why this method is controversial, then map how natural gas development may impact a community.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Overview | What is hydraulic fracturing? Why is it so controversial? In this lesson, students will define hydrofracking, identify how the demand for natural gas is changing, then research and map how natural gas development may impact a community.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fuel for Debate: Examining the Natural Gas Fracking Controversy', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T19:45:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alison Fromme, Jennifer Cutraro and Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fromme', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cutraro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/405f9df9-9040-5afa-b790-a82ab84e114f', 'word_count': 1449, 'uri': 'nyt://article/405f9df9-9040-5afa-b790-a82ab84e114f'}, {'abstract': 'A new look at the fate of Himalayan glaciers in a changing climate, and the implications for 1.5 billion Asians, cuts through caricatures.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/academy-finds-mixed-climate-impacts-on-himalayan-glaciers-water-supplies/', 'snippet': 'A new look at the fate of Himalayan glaciers in a changing climate, and the implications for 1.5 billion Asians, cuts through caricatures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Given all the oversimplified assertions over the years about Himalayan glaciers in a warming global climate, it’s great to see a committee assembled by the National Academy of Sciences weigh in on the question with some data-based findings in a new report, “Himalayan Glaciers: Climate Change, Water Resources, and Water Security.” The bottom line — in sync with other recent analysis — is that the region is seeing a mix of changes, with glaciers growing in some places and shrinking in others and impacts on water supplies mostly inconsequential for decades to come. In most regions, monsoon patterns, population and consumption pressures and dependence on groundwater pumping will remain the dominant source of water-related risks, the report concludes. Read on for an excerpt from the news release and link to the full report, followed by related background:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Academy Finds Mixed Climate Impacts on Himalayan Glaciers, Water Supplies', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drought', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Glaciers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'HIMALAYAS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Population', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rain', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rivers', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Academy of Sciences', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ganges River', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mekong River', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T19:50:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/821fa7c8-40e9-597c-afb3-432fc5b2e0f3', 'word_count': 641, 'uri': 'nyt://article/821fa7c8-40e9-597c-afb3-432fc5b2e0f3'}, {'abstract': 'New Yorkers will be choosing candidates for the fall State Assembly and Senate contests.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/nyregion/voting-information-for-new-york-legislative-primaries.html', 'snippet': 'New Yorkers will be choosing candidates for the fall State Assembly and Senate contests.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Primary elections for the State Legislature and some local offices will be held across New York State on Thursday. The Legislature moved the primary from Tuesday so that voters would not have to go to the polls on the anniversary of the Sept. 11 terrorist attacks.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Voting Information: Legislative Primaries', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Voting Thursday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Legislature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T19:54:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/61e85cd4-912a-5f60-aa1f-2fc7eb47988d', 'word_count': 124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61e85cd4-912a-5f60-aa1f-2fc7eb47988d'}, {'abstract': 'A film shown Tuesday on the state-owned Rossiya 1 channel claimed to have found the mastermind behind the Pussy Riot controversy: Boris Berezovsky, the exiled Russian tycoon living in London.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/film-shown-on-russian-tv-ties-exiled-tycoon-to-pussy-riot/', 'snippet': 'A film shown Tuesday on the state-owned Rossiya 1 channel claimed to have found the mastermind behind the Pussy Riot controversy: Boris Berezovsky, the exiled Russian tycoon living in London.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Update | Friday, 10:00 a.m. MOSCOW — A report broadcast Tuesday on the state-owned Rossiya 1 channel claimed to have found the mastermind behind the Pussy Riot controversy: Boris A. Berezovsky, the exiled Russian tycoon living in London. The second installment of “Provocateurs,” a film by the journalist Arkady Mamontov, suggests that Mr. Berezovsky financed the punk band in order to destabilize Russian society.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russian State TV Claims Exiled Tycoon Behind Pussy Riot', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berezovsky, Boris', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pussy Riot', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T19:57:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By ANNA KORDUNSKY', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'KORDUNSKY', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e2b9772-9b27-5076-975d-f3cb6cdac08d', 'word_count': 435, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e2b9772-9b27-5076-975d-f3cb6cdac08d'}, {'abstract': 'Apple introduces the iPhone 5. | Bionic suits help paraplegics walk again. | Nostalgic apps.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/technology/100000001779724/timescast-tech-september-12-2012-.html', 'snippet': 'Apple introduces the iPhone 5. | Bionic suits help paraplegics walk again. | Nostalgic apps.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Apple introduces the iPhone 5. | Bionic suits help paraplegics walk again. | Nostalgic apps.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/12/business/video-tech-120912/video-tech-120912-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width':