 of the Bank of Credit and Commerce International scandal or the Iran-contra affair. One begins to wish for a similar explication of Mr. Lombardi and his work during Mareike Wegener’s frustratingly self-evident documentary, “Mark Lombardi: Death-Defying Acts of Art and Conspiracy.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/arts/13mark/13mark-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 580, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/arts/13mark/13mark-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1160, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Artist Who Delineated the Money', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Mark Lombardi: Death-Defying Acts'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Artist Who Delineated the Money', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum of Modern Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lombardi, Mark', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T21:43:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicolas Rapold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicolas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rapold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7930005-fb34-5e35-9ced-d7a119ed6578', 'word_count': 219, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7930005-fb34-5e35-9ced-d7a119ed6578'}, {'abstract': 'A partnership between Eugene Lang College, part of the New School, and Global Citizen Year would allow students who took a gap year to arrive on campus as newly minted sophomores.', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/lang-college-gap-year/', 'snippet': 'A partnership between Eugene Lang College, part of the New School, and Global Citizen Year would allow students who took a gap year to arrive on campus as newly minted sophomores.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sometimes, after a hectic high school experience overshadowed by a competitive — or perhaps, disappointing — college admissions process, seniors just need a break.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lang College Offers Academic Credit for Taking a Gap Year', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADMISSIONS STANDARDS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T21:45:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tanya Abrams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tanya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abrams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/122014ba-6c19-5bf1-b66a-df82031141f5', 'word_count': 1026, 'uri': 'nyt://article/122014ba-6c19-5bf1-b66a-df82031141f5'}, {'abstract': 'The United States should stay engaged with Libya despite the killing of Ambassador Stevens and three other Americans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/opinion/murder-in-benghazi.html', 'snippet': 'The United States should stay engaged with Libya despite the killing of Ambassador Stevens and three other Americans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Libya and its pro-democracy revolution had no better friend than J. Christopher Stevens, the United States ambassador who was killed a