0 copies in the United States, according to Nielsen SoundScan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Matchbox Twenty has reached No. 1 on the Billboard album chart for the first time with “North” (Atlantic), its first studio record in a decade. “North” sold 95,000 copies in the United States, according to Nielsen SoundScan, and leads a handful of high-charting new titles as the music industry begins releasing its fall albums. Imagine Dragons, an alternative-rock band from Las Vegas, is No. 2, with 83,000 sales of “Night Visions” (Interscope), its first full-length album. The Christian rapper Lecrae is No. 3, with “Gravity” (Reach), which sold 72,000 copies. Last week’s No. 1, “Eye on It” (ForeFront), by another Christian rapper, TobyMac, fell to No. 8 in its second week out, with 26,000 sales. Cat Power opened at No. 10 with 23,000 sales of “Sun” (Matador).', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Matchbox Twenty Tops Album Chart', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Matchbox Twenty Tops Album Chart', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nielsen SoundScan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T21:50:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/832a2a87-a0e3-57e5-b1d3-2c65afe9bccd', 'word_count': 127, 'uri': 'nyt://article/832a2a87-a0e3-57e5-b1d3-2c65afe9bccd'}, {'abstract': 'Bigger screen, longer battery life, more sophisticated camera, better sound. Overall, Apple seems to have put its focus on the important things you want in an app phone.', 'web_url': 'https://pogue.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/the-iphone-5-my-first-impressions/', 'snippet': 'Bigger screen, longer battery life, more sophisticated camera, better sound. Overall, Apple seems to have put its focus on the important things you want in an app phone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Apple unveiled the new iPhone 5 today in San Francisco. As it turns out, most of the individual rumors about it were true — but even so, they didn’t describe the whole package.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The iPhone 5: My First Impressions', 'kicker': 'Pogue&#039;s Posts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T21:54:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Pogue', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogue', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f489bfc-85c2-5df7-9c3d-363c7369b109', 'word_count': 714, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f489bfc-85c2-5df7-9c3d-363c7369b109'}, {'abstract': '“The Why Overhead,” by Adam Szymkowicz, depicts the consequences of workplace tedium in comic, even musical, terms.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/theater/reviews/the-why-overhead-by-adam-szymkowicz-at-access-theater.html', 'snippet': '“The Why Overhead,” by Adam Szymkowicz, depicts the consequences of workplace tedium in comic, even musical, terms.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Adam Szymkowicz’s office comedy “The Why Overhead” has some genuinely funny moments and an odd sensibility. It’s a decent play that pushes against its own boundaries with varying success. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtyp