agraph': 'Some interesting items that the tech reporters and editors of The New York Times found on the Web recently. See more here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Today’s Scuttlebot: Inside Foxconn, and Technology’s Limits', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T22:07:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cdcc1c5f-cce7-5710-a280-11a671515031', 'word_count': 233, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cdcc1c5f-cce7-5710-a280-11a671515031'}, {'abstract': 'Steve Reich’s “WTC 9/11,” performed on Tuesday at Le Poisson Rouge, was an intensely personal account of the tragedy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/arts/music/american-contemporary-music-ensemble-at-le-poisson-rouge.html', 'snippet': 'Steve Reich’s “WTC 9/11,” performed on Tuesday at Le Poisson Rouge, was an intensely personal account of the tragedy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When a composer takes up the theme of unthinkable man-made tragedy as the impetus for a new piece, what is the proper tone to adopt? Richard Strauss, responding to the World War II bombing of Munich with “Metamorphosen,” fashioned a lament not only for a city but also for a culture vanished in violence and guilt. John Adams, asked to imagine a response to the terrorist attacks of Sept. 11, 2001, produced “On the Transmigration of Souls,” a complex, contemplative work that used personal mementos as a springboard to transcendental concerns.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/arts/13reich/13reich-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 628, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/arts/13reich/13reich-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1256, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Combining Taped Voices From 9/11 and Live Strings', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Combining Taped Voices From 9/11 and Live Strings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Le Poisson Rouge', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Contemporary Music Ensemble', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T22:08:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qual