', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ROOSEVELT ISLAND (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T22:15:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Kimmelman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kimmelman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f322df18-b0a0-5135-b396-72fed417fc50', 'word_count': 1190, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f322df18-b0a0-5135-b396-72fed417fc50'}, {'abstract': 'The boogie-woogie band was on hand in SoHo on Tuesday night to introduce the limited-edition sedan.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/of-chryslers-fashion-plates-and-beards-zz-top-introduces-300c-john-varvatos-limited-edition/', 'snippet': 'The boogie-woogie band was on hand in SoHo on Tuesday night to introduce the limited-edition sedan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Whether by positioning Eminem behind the wheel of a 200, Clint Eastwood in a dank, dimly lighted tunnel or Jennifer Lopez in an imaginary Bronx, Chrysler has strove to associate itself with totems of popular culture since emerging from bankruptcy in 2009. That impulse was given full rein on Tuesday night in SoHo when the automaker organized a meeting of ZZ Top, Jack Daniels, John Varvatos and GQ magazine under one roof.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Of Chryslers, Fashion Plates and Beards: ZZ Top Introduces 300C John Varvatos Limited Edition', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Varvatos, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chrysler Group LLC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ZZ Top', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'SoHo (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T22:18:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Schultz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schultz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65f38df4-0c82-51ba-8a9d-1c30b444b5cf', 'word_count': 316, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65f38df4-0c82-51ba-8a9d-1c30b444b5cf'}, {'abstract': 'The New York Times decides not to remove the photo of the dying ambassador to Libya, J. Christopher Stevens, from NYTimes.com.', 'web_url': 'https://publiceditor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/update-the-times-denies-state-department-request-to-remove-photo-from-web-site/', 'snippet': 'The New York Times decides not to remove the photo of the dying ambassador to Libya, J. Christopher Stevens, from NYTimes.com.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The State Department asked The New York Times on Wednesday afternoon to remove a photograph of the dying ambassador to Libya from a gallery on the newspaper’s Web site. The ambassador, J. Christopher Stevens, was killed Tuesday in an attack on the American Consulate in Libya.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Update: The Times Denies State Department Request to Remove Photo From Web Site', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T22:20:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'report