d curb the influence of Wall Street regulators, a move that came as some federal officials mounted opposition to the effort.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lawmakers Delay Plans to Increase Oversight of Regulators', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T23:15:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e55b776-f063-503d-a25b-484b76c45b50', 'word_count': 328, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e55b776-f063-503d-a25b-484b76c45b50'}, {'abstract': 'The makeup was graphic and ’60s-inspired, and the hair was sleek and reminiscent of the ’90s.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/12/backstage-beauty-report-michael-kors-2/', 'snippet': 'The makeup was graphic and ’60s-inspired, and the hair was sleek and reminiscent of the ’90s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Look: Sharp Lines.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Backstage Beauty Report | Michael Kors', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T23:15:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lily Nima', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nima', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac4c1497-cf00-552f-90a2-0f31044ff600', 'word_count': 293, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac4c1497-cf00-552f-90a2-0f31044ff600'}, {'abstract': 'Fishs Eddy serves up President Obama’s birth certificate on a plate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/garden/fishs-eddy-serves-up-obamas-birth-certificate-on-a-plate.html', 'snippet': 'Fishs Eddy serves up President Obama’s birth certificate on a plate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Manners dictate that one avoids politics at mixed partisan gatherings, but if you are determined to annoy certain family members, what better gift than the Obama Birth Certificate dish, which arrives today at the Manhattan housewares store Fishs Eddy? At $19.95, it’s not excessively expensive (though admit it, you’d spend a lot more to zetz Uncle Frank), and at 8 by 7 inches, it’s not so big that when Uncle Frank slams it down on your head he’ll be able to do any real damage. And if you’re thinking that it represents a point of view of the store’s owners, you’re right.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/garden/13GOODS/13CURR1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 693, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/garden/13GOODS/13CURR1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1386, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/garden/13GOODS/13GOODS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/13/garden/13GOODS/13GOODS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/garden/13GOODS/13GOODS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Feeding Believers and Doubters Alike', 'kicker': 'Currents | Goods', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Feeding Believers and Doubters Alike', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fishs Eddy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tableware', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Certificates', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T23:16:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joyce Wadler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joyce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wadler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef204337-d0cd-5301-be2e-f773cc54394c', 'word_count': 260, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef204337-d0cd-5301-be2e-f773cc54394c'}, {'abstract': '“Trees and Stones,” a show of Andrea Branzi’s furniture, opens at the Friedman Benda gallery in Manhattan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/garden/trees-and-stones-a-show-of-andrea-branzis-furniture-opens-at-friedman-benda.html', 'snippet': '“Trees and Stones,” a show of Andrea Branzi’s furniture, opens at the Friedman Benda gallery in Manhattan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Italian designer Andrea Branzi, 73, has been integrating rocks and trees into household objects for some 30 years. His Animali Domestici collection from 1985 featured laminate chairs with backrests of raw birch. A decade later, he hollowed containers out of stones and lumps of wood.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/garden/13SHOWSA/13CURR2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 769, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/garden/13SHOWSA/13CURR2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1078, 'width': 810, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/garden/13SHOWSA/13SHOWSA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/13/garden/13SHOWSA/13SHOWSA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/garden/13SHOWSA/13SHOWSA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mixing Man’s Work With Nature’s', 'kicker': 'Currents | Shows', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mixing Man’s Work With Nature’s', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Branzi, Andrea', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Furniture', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock and Stone', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-12T23:17:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Lasky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lasky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/35ad36dd-8f83-5dc3-8a08-030258e08e15', 'word_count': 162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35ad36dd-8f83-5dc3-8a08-030258e08e15'}, {'abstract': 'Cast in papier-mâché and mounted on black or chromed steel, Harry Allen’s collection includes a table lamp, floor lamp and chandelier.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/garden/harry-allens-recast-fixtures-emit-a-ghostly-glow.html', 'snippet': 'Cast in papier-mâché and mounted on black or chromed steel, Harry Allen’s collection includes a table lamp, floor lamp and chandelier.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Harry Allen deals in twisted household archetypes. The New York-based designer’s ongoing Reality series includes a fruit bowl cast from a bunch of bananas, a coat hook shaped like a hand and a roller skate playing the role of door stop. For his latest project, Paperwork lanterns for Hive, he has transformed an old barn lantern into a ghostly light fixture. “It’s humble, like a found object,” Mr. Allen said. Cast in papier-mâché and mounted on black or chromed steel, the collection includes a table lamp, floor lamp and chandelier, all designed to hang from hooks attached to an armature. The lights are illuminated with LED bulbs. A single lantern measures 15 ½ inches high, 9 5/8 inches wide and 4 ¾ inches deep, and costs $350. Information: (888) 889-9005 or designbyhive.com.\xa0', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/garden/13LIGHTING/13CURR6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 785, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/garden/13LIGHTING/13CURR6-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1570, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/garden/13LIGHTING/13LIGHTING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {