law.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/opinion/fewer-uninsured-people.html', 'snippet': 'Wider coverage strengthens the case for retaining President Obama’s health care reform law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The number of Americans who lack health insurance declined last year, the first drop since 2007. This is, in large part, the result of the health care reform law and better coverage under public programs like Medicaid. This also shows why repealing the health care law or revamping and shrinking Medicaid, as many Republicans want to do, would be disastrous moves. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fewer Uninsured People', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fewer Uninsured People', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Census Bureau', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kaiser Family Foundation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T01:03:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/13136fd3-01d2-578f-81b6-84cac419ba50', 'word_count': 406, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13136fd3-01d2-578f-81b6-84cac419ba50'}, {'abstract': 'A reader talks about the New York City map she can’t throw away.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/opinion/my-map-of-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'A reader talks about the New York City map she can’t throw away.', 'lead_paragraph': 