09/13/us/politics/florida-agrees-to-let-citizens-mistakenly-purged-from-rolls-to-vote.html', 'snippet': 'In settling a lawsuit, Florida agreed that residents who were removed from voting rolls after mistakenly being classified as noncitizens will be allowed to vote in November.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MIAMI — In a partial victory for voter rights and immigrant groups, Florida residents who were mistakenly removed from the voter rolls this year because the state classified them as noncitizens will be returned to the rolls and allowed to vote in November.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/us/VOTE/VOTE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 695, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/us/VOTE/VOTE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1389, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/us/VOTE/VOTE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/13/us/VOTE/VOTE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/us/VOTE/VOTE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After Mistakenly Purging Citizens, Florida Agrees to Let Them Vote', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Mistakenly Purging Citizens, Florida Agrees to Let Them Vote', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizenship and Naturalization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T03:30:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lizette Alvarez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lizette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alvarez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0d2d417-0564-55d0-8434-eec106ba1165', 'word_count': 436, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0d2d417-0564-55d0-8434-eec106ba1165'}, {'abstract': 'Some analysts see the protests as less about Muslim intolerance than about extremists’ exploiting popular anger to draw attention to political goals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/world/middleeast/ideological-struggle-seen-in-middle-east-attacks.html', 'snippet': 'Some analysts see the protests as less about Muslim intolerance than about extremists’ exploiting popular anger to draw attention to political goals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DOHA, Qatar — The Arab uprisings have appeared to offer a new bridge in the anguished relationship between the United States and the Muslim world, perhaps most of all in Libya, where American firepower helped oust Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi and earned the United States deep popular gratitude.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Struggle for Ideological Upper Hand in Muslim World Seen as Factor in Attacks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Struggle for Ideological Upper Hand in Muslim World Seen as Factor in Attacks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'ke