': [{'firstname': 'Anastasia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Economides', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c5ec28d-dbb0-5a15-bc08-e7c43f723e8c', 'word_count': 22, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c5ec28d-dbb0-5a15-bc08-e7c43f723e8c'}, {'abstract': 'For Delhi’s fashionista crowd, high heels are a must in Khan market, despite the precarious pavement.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/delhi-donts-high-heels-in-khan-market/', 'snippet': 'For Delhi’s fashionista crowd, high heels are a must in Khan market, despite the precarious pavement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Khan Market looks like many other outdoor markets in Delhi – a crowded inner lane, uneven pavement, spontaneous potholes and an occasional pile of garbage or stray dog. Like the others, this U-shaped market is not the easiest to navigate, but many of its patrons wouldn’t dream of shopping there without the “right” footwear – high, high heels.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Delhi Don’ts: High Heels in Khan Market', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shoes and Boots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hermes International SA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Louboutin, Christian, LLC', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Delhi (India)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T07:03:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sujata Assomull Sippy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sujata', 'middlename': 'Assomull', 'lastname': 'Sippy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ebb6450-bb64-5e85-a972-36e2ede297b5', 'word_count': 676, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ebb6450-bb64-5e85-a972-36e2ede297b5'}, {'abstract': 'Verghese Kurien, who died this week at age 90, was one of India’s most important social revolutionaries. His enterprising leadership in the national dairy industry helped India to become the world’s largest milk producer.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/a-farewell-to-indias-milkman/', 'snippet': 'Verghese Kurien, who died this week at age 90, was one of India’s most important social revolutionaries. His enterprising leadership in the national dairy industry helped India to become the world’s largest milk producer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My latest column is an inadequate eulogy to one of the most useful Indian men ever, Verghese Kurien, who died this week. Mr. Kurien, who helped make India into the world’s leading milk producer, was among a generation of extraordinary social revolutionaries who are the proof that sometimes some Indian politicians do fully back good people and give them complete freedom.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Farewell to India’s Milkman', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T07:41:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manu Joseph', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manu', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Joseph', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/38c189c1-0a13-5e30-af