ject of a forthcoming glossy photo book, a smartphone application for personal data analysis and comparison, and an interactive version of the book for the iPad. The project is the brainchild of Rick Smolan, creator of the “Day in the Life” series of books.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/big-data-gets-its-own-photo-album/', 'snippet': 'Big Data is the subject of a forthcoming glossy photo book, a smartphone application for personal data analysis and comparison, and an interactive version of the book for the iPad. The project is the brainchild of Rick Smolan, creator of the “Day ...', 'lead_paragraph': ' Rick Smolan, the photographer and impresario of media projects, has tackled all sorts of big subjects over the years, from countries (“A Day in the Life of Australia” in 1981) to drinking water (“Blue Planet Run” in 2007). He typically recruits about 100 photographers for each, and their work is crafted into classy coffee-table books of striking photographs and short essays.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/technology/13bits-data-3/13bits-data-3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/technology/13bits-data-3/13bits-data-3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Big Data Gets Its Own Photo Album', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Putting a Face On the World Of Big Data', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smolan, Rick', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'EMC Corporation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T10:00:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Lohr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lohr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/650e5660-340e-58d5-9fbc-47c5a5b9b424', 'word_count': 1134, 'uri': 'nyt://article/650e5660-340e-58d5-9fbc-47c5a5b9b424'}, {'abstract': 'Political news from today’s Times and around the Web, plus a look at what’s happening in Washington.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/the-early-word-fallout/', 'snippet': 'Political news from today’s Times and around the Web, plus a look at what’s happening in Washington.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Today’s Times:The deadly attack on an American consulate in Libya on Tuesday pushed foreign policy to the front of the presidential campaign, with Mitt Romney quickly attacking President Obama for his response to the situation, Peter Baker and Ashley Parker write. But Mr. Romney’s attempt to use the event to draw a contrast with Mr. Obama on foreign policy started a confrontation that landed him on the defensive and drew attention away from questions about Mr. Obama’s handling of uprisings in the Arab world.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Early Word: Fallout', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T10:00:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Southall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Southall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0fbf1f62-9ca9-50bd-960f-0f19b52fb1f6', 'word_count': 572, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0fbf1f62-9ca9-50bd-960f-0f19b52fb1f6'}, {'abstract': 'Sush Krishnamoorthy, a student at Sardar Patel Vidyalaya, in New Delhi, is one of eight high school seniors around the world blogging about their college searches for The Choice.', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/envelope-please-sush-krishnamoorthy-1/', 'snippet': 'Sush Krishnamoorthy, a student at Sardar Patel Vidyalaya, in New Delhi, is one of eight high school seniors around the world blogging about their college searches for The Choice.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In fifth grade, I knew I wanted to study computer science when I grew up. My school did not offer much in that subject, so I spent my time building Web sites and silly apps on Visual Basic, and exploring random software. In high school, when I could finally take programming classes, I fell in love with programming. It was the perfect mix between art and science. I knew just what I wanted to do.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/03/education/envpls13-Sush-Krishnamoorthy/envpls13-Sush-Krishnamoorthy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 819, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/03/education/envpls13-Sush-Krishnamoorthy/envpls13-Sush-Krishnamoorthy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1343, 'width': 1074, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': Non