l': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/thai-billionaire-in-7-3-billion-bid-for-fraser-neave/', 'snippet': 'The bid is the latest effort in a battle to gain control of Asia Pacific Breweries, the beer business jointly owned by Heineken and Fraser & Neave.', 'lead_paragraph': '8:38 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thai Billionaire Tries to Edge Out Heineken for Singaporean Brewery', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T10:46:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/21d1d644-0ec0-598a-b0fd-dd45f0cb10c0', 'word_count': 547, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21d1d644-0ec0-598a-b0fd-dd45f0cb10c0'}, {'abstract': 'In lieu of a lesson, we are live streaming a Times education conference we think will be of great interest to our audience. Its theme? “Building a Better Teacher.”', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/live-stream-the-schools-for-tomorrow-conference/', 'snippet': 'In lieu of a lesson, we are live streaming a Times education conference we think will be of great interest to our audience. Its theme? “Building a Better Teacher.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Update | Sept. 25: You can now find this conference archived, below, in several separate videos.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Live Stream: The Schools for Tomorrow Conference', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T10:46:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5205e50-8991-5e4a-85a6-0f5f378af54b', 'word_count': 234, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5205e50-8991-5e4a-85a6-0f5f378af54b'}, {'abstract': 'Closing the deal on a perfect breast of lamb.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/16/magazine/always-be-crisping.html', 'snippet': 'Closing the deal on a perfect breast of lamb.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cooking is sales, as any child or restaurant chef will tell you. “The single word ‘crispy’ sells more food than a barrage of adjectives describing the ingredients or cooking techniques on a menu,” Mario Batali writes in “Babbo,” the best restaurant cookbook of the modern age, dedicated to the menu at his flagship restaurant in Greenwich Village. “There is something innately appealing about crispy food.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '72', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/magazine/16eat1/16eat1-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 488, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/16/magazine/16eat1/16eat1-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 488}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/magazine/16eat1/16eat1-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 652, 'width': 802, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/magazine/16eat1/16eat1-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 652, 'width': 802, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumb