oncentrate on keeping their customers happy and having enough cash in the bank to pay their bills, at least at first. They don’t think about their long-term goals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Business owners start businesses for a variety of reasons. A few do it to make a lot of money, but a vast majority do it for other reasons.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Introducing: Creating Value', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Family Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T11:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Josh Patrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Josh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Patrick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed259d75-77a5-507b-a6ae-484f09453d78', 'word_count': 661, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed259d75-77a5-507b-a6ae-484f09453d78'}, {'abstract': 'Riggall is the founder of London’s Future Cinema and Secret Cinema, two series in which films are rescreened with an interactive bent.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/styled-to-a-t-fabien-riggall/', 'snippet': 'Riggall is the founder of London’s Future Cinema and Secret Cinema, two series in which films are rescreened with an interactive bent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Guy', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Styled to a T | Fabien Riggall', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Styled to A T', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': '