None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Earth', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emotions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forests and Forestry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trees and Shrubs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALASKA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T14:10:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lauren E. Oakes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lauren', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Oakes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/92192556-9c53-5ed5-bb8d-6c0ce8b17f86', 'word_count': 1468, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92192556-9c53-5ed5-bb8d-6c0ce8b17f86'}, {'abstract': 'New York City Ballet is opening its fall season with two weeks of ballets choreographed to the music of Igor Stravinsky.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/16/arts/dance/new-york-city-ballet-offers-two-weeks-of-stravinsky.html', 'snippet': 'New York City Ballet is opening its fall season with two weeks of ballets choreographed to the music of Igor Stravinsky.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOR over a hundred years now the music of Igor Stravinsky has been central to ballet. In 1909, while still a virtual unknown, he orchestrated a Chopin number for the ballet “Les Sylphides” as part of the opening season of Diaghilev’s Ballets Russes. The next year Diaghilev presented the premiere of “The Firebird” with Stravinsky’s new score. The 20th century certainly spawned modernist composers, but none of them matched his profound instinct for dance rhythm; and none kept on so restlessly unlocking aspects of the new.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', '