e professing to be above the unethical muck dragging down lesser mortals in the sport.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/14/sports/14leading1/14leading1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 816, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/14/sports/14leading1/14leading1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1632, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/14/sports/14leading1/14leading1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/14/sports/14leading1/14leading1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/14/sports/14leading1/14leading1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At UConn, It’s Time to Go', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Calhoun, Jim', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Connecticut', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ollie, Kevin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pedroia, Dustin', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miles, Nate', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baltimore Orioles', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T15:09:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ebf27a4-340b-5d1b-a432-2eee0ceed645', 'word_count': 674, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ebf27a4-340b-5d1b-a432-2eee0ceed645'}, {'abstract': 'Lovers of the classic “Helplessly Hoping” can find dreamy harmonies in the music of Local Natives.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/booming/13match.html', 'snippet': 'Lovers of the classic “Helplessly Hoping” can find dreamy harmonies in the music of Local Natives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Five years ago, Val Haller, a suburban Chicago mom, started valslist, a Web site aimed at exposing her generation — she’s 55 — to the music of the generation of her sons, ages 20 to 27. Unlike Pandora, a digital music recommendation service governed by an algorithm, Ms. Haller is governed by her ear, long hours of listening and serendipity. At Lollapalooza Chicago 2012, she was 25 years older than the average music reporter. “My goal every single day is to find that one new track that speaks to me and won’t let me go,” she says.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/24/timestopics/michael-winerip/michael-winerip-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/08/24/timestopics/michael-winerip/michael-winerip-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/08/24/timestopics