g to defend Mitt Romney’s brisk critique of the Obama administration’s response to a controversial Web video and the protests it seemed to help spawn. However, by Thursday, the right’s \xa0establishment was starting to circle the wagons around Mr. Romney, the Republican presidential candidate.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Right Begins to Rally Around Romney’s Response to Attacks', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Erickson, Erick', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fleischer, Ari', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Noonan, Peggy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wall Street Journal', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cairo (Egypt)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T15:13:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Wheaton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wheaton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, '