ay inside the CBS corporate family, and give Showtime another way to compete with its bigger rival, HBO, on sports coverage.', 'lead_paragraph': '“60 Minutes” is extending itself to another network, Showtime, for a monthly newsmagazine called “60 Minutes of Sports.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '’60 Minutes’ to Produce a Monthly Sports Show for Showtime', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fager, Jeff', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS News', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Showtime', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T16:11:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3188e8af-fb77-580e-8fb9-a501fa54a48b', 'word_count': 288, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3188e8af-fb77-580e-8fb9-a501fa54a48b'}, {'abstract': 'The new executive, Sandra E. Peterson of Bayer, will be responsible for the company’s consumer units, which have been hit by a series of recalls.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/14/business/johnson-johnson-names-sandra-peterson-to-consumer-health-post.html', 'snippet': 'The new executive, Sandra E. Peterson of Bayer, will be responsible for the company’s consumer units, which have been hit by a series of recalls.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Johnson & Johnson named an outsider on Thursday to fill a top leadership role overseeing its troubled consumer health unit, a break from the company’s longstanding tradition of promoting executives from within. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'J.&J. Names Outsider to Run Its Troubled Consumer Unit', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'J.&J. Names Outsider to Run Its Troubled Consumer Unit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Johnson & Johnson', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Peterson, Sandra E', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T16:14:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katie Thomas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thomas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e08e54d5-91c5-5d20-8ad0-c41733257e53', 'word_count': 461, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e08e54d5-91c5-5d20-8ad0-c41733257e53'}, {'abstract': 'The book will include prison letters from the three members of Pussy Riot who have been jailed.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/e-book-planned-on-embattled-russian-punk-group/', 'snippet': 'The book will include prison letters from the three members of Pussy Riot who have been jailed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The women of Pussy Riot, the Russian punk group protesting President Vladimir V. Putin, will have their message out in a new medium: an e-book. “Pussy Riot! A Punk Prayer for Freedom,” to be released in about two weeks by The Feminist Press, part of the City University of New York, will include previously unavailable material, including prison letters from the three Pussy Riot members who have been jailed for “hooliganism inciting religious hatred” after a brief performance in an Orthodox cathedral in Moscow. The book will also include statements by their defense attorneys, poems and tributes from performers and artists, including Yoko Ono, Karen Finley and the poet Eileen Myles. Proceeds will go to the legal defense fund for the group.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'E-Book Planned on Embattled Russian Punk Group', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Finley, Karen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Medvedev, Dmitri A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ono, Yoko', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'City University of New York', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Feminist Press', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pussy Riot', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Moscow (Russia)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T16:30:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee071caf-4531-57c7-9a09-9a28864044c9', 'word_count': 251, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee071caf-4531-57c7-9a09-9a28864044c9'}, {'abstract': 'Protesters angered by an anti-Islam film attacked the American Embassy in Sana, the Yemeni capital, on Thursday, two days after the American ambassador to Libya was killed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/09/13/world/middleeast/20120914-YEMEN.html', 'snippet': 'Protesters angered by an anti-Islam film attacked the American Embassy in Sana, the Yemeni ca