tes International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Innocence of Muslims (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T16:39:55+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'World', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/7e52d219-a2a5-5e20-91fb-19e9d21ab748', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/7e52d219-a2a5-5e20-91fb-19e9d21ab748'}, {'abstract': 'The Federal Reserve opened a new chapter in its efforts to stimulate the American economy, saying that it intends to buy large quantities of mortgage bonds until the job market improves substantially.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/14/business/economy/fed-announces-new-round-of-bond-buying-to-spur-growth.html', 'snippet': 'The Federal Reserve opened a new chapter in its efforts to stimulate the American economy, saying that it intends to buy large quantities of mortgage bonds until the job market improves substantially.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Federal Reserve opened a new chapter Thursday in its efforts to stimulate the economy, saying that it intends to buy large quantities of mortgage bonds, and potentially other assets, until the job market improves substantially.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/14/business/Fed/Fed-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 996, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/14/business/Fed/Fed-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 1405, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/14/business/Fed/Fed-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/14/business/Fed/Fed-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/14/business/Fed/Fed-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fed Ties New Aid to Jobs Recovery in Forceful Move', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fed Links New Aid To Jobs Recovery In Forceful Move', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bernanke, Ben S', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgage-Backed Securities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quantitative Easing', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T16:41:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Binyamin Appelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Binyamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Appelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea97da76-eab5-5c8b-9fa3-5e237675c2e9', 'word_count': 1346, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea97da76-eab5-5c8b-9fa3-5e237675c2e9'}, {'abstract': 'Lydia Ko, a 15-year-old from New Zealand, shot an even-par 72 and was two strokes off the clubhouse lead at Royal Liverpool Golf Club.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/14/sports/golf/womens-british-open-first-round.html', 'snippet': 'Lydia Ko, a 15-year-old from New Zealand, shot an even-par 72 and was two strokes off the clubhouse lead at Royal Liverpool Golf Club.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HOYLAKE, England — Lydia Ko was climbing the first-round leader board Thursday at the Women’s British Open when her group was put on the clock for slow play. The move was probably funnier to her than any punch line delivered by her coach and caddie, Guy Wilson, who told her jokes between shots at Royal Liverpool Golf Club to relax her.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '15-Year-Old Trails by Two at Women’s British Open', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '15-Year-Old Trails by Two At Women’s British Open', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "United States Women's Open (Golf)", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ko, Lydia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kang, Haeji', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryu, So Yeon', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T16:41:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c8ffc9a-0a04-5f51-81a7-2a47970907e1', 'word_count': 935, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c8ffc9a-0a04-5f51-81a7-2a47970907e1'}, {'abstract': 'Hemingway has always been a big influence on Ralph Lauren, so you could imagine those bullfighting stories come to life on the runway, with models wearing gaucho pants, boleros and toreador jackets.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/hey-senorita/', 'snippet': 'Hemingway has always been a big influence on Ralph Lauren, so you could imagine those bullfighting stories come to life on the runway, with models wearing gaucho pants, boleros and toreador jackets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Olympic swimmers Conor Dwyer and Ryan Lochte attended the Ralph Lauren show this morning, suggesting all is forgiven over the designer’s production in China of ceremonial uniforms for the athletes this year. But if you thought Mr. Lauren might make a big pro-America statement on the runway, you would have thought wrong.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hey, Señorita!', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Models (Professional)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lauren, Ralph', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T16:50:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6fa1b91a-2bdf-5ed4-a43d-82d601587253', 'word_count': 153, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6fa1b91a-2bdf-5ed4-a43d-82d601587253'}, {'abstract': 'The actor and director will produce an illustrated adventure series that will first be released in book format and later as films.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/kevin-costner-plans-book-project/', 'snippet': 'The actor and director will produce an illustrated adventure series that will first be released in book format and later as films.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The director and actor Kevin Costner has signed a deal with Atria Books for a book project — an illustrated adventure series titled “The Explorers Guild” that will be released in 2014.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kevin Costner Plans Book Project', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Costner, Kevin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T16:53:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/281780a5-6b01-5d02-874c-9b246767c8a9', 'word_count': 99, 'uri': 'nyt://article/281780a5-6b01-5d02-874c-9b246767c8a9'}, {'abstract': 'Algal bloom is responsible for many of these events, an oceanographer says, but he warns against assuming that 2012 is setting a record.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/a-red-tide-epidemic/', 'snippet': 'Algal bloom is responsible for many of these events, an oceanographer says, but he warns against assuming that 2012 is setting a record.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As we mentioned here in an On Our Radar item this week, the Yangtze River in China changed from a warm brown to a deep, rusty orange a few days ago. Striking photographs showed a \xa0\xa0crimson current advancing alongside a stretch of untainted water. One Green reader wrote in to describe what she saw as \xa0a spate of red tide events around the world and inquired about the cause.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Red Tide Epidemic?', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALGAE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oceans and Seas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lamont-Doherty Earth Observatory', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T16:58:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emma Bryce', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emma', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bryce', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/176120c1-e011-526e-8da2-fa8163224ccc', 'word_count': 620, 'uri': 'nyt://article/176120c1-e011-526e-8da2-fa8163224ccc'}, {'abstract': 'A video shot with Google Glass offers a preview of what filmmaking may look like a few years from now.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/watch-list-how-film-might-look-after-googles-glass-goggles/', 'snippet': 'A video shot with Google Glass offers a preview of what filmmaking may look like a few years from now.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a preview of how we all may be making movies in a few years, take a look at “DVF Through Glass,” a short video made for, and partly shot by, the fashion designer Diane von Furstenberg. Other camera operators included employees of Ms. von Furstenberg’s label, DVF, and models who walked in her recent Fashion Week show. All were wearing Google’s futuristic “Glass” glasses, which come equipped with tiny cameras (as well as tiny computer monitors) and are poised to take us a big step closer to the cyborg age, once they become available to the public.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Watch List: How Film Might Look After Google’s Glasses', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Fashion Week', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wearable Computing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brin, Sergey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'von Furstenberg, Diane', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T17:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Hale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d85c7d9-40ee-5bc9-8ca7-2373f2994032', 'word_count': 331, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d85c7d9-40ee-5bc9-8ca7-2373f2994032'}, {'abstract': 'Boeing’s 787 Dreamliner, the lighter, more-fuel efficient aircraft recently made its American debut with the Chilean carrier LAN Airlines.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/dreamliner-makes-its-debut-in-chile/', 'snippet': 'Boeing’s 787 Dreamliner, the lighter, more-fuel efficient aircraft recently made its American debut with the Chilean carrier LAN Airlines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Boeing’s 787 Dreamliner, the lighter, more-fuel efficient and purportedly more comfortable aircraft that has forged fans of hopeful fliers, recently made its American debut with the Chilean carrier LAN Airlines.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dreamliner Makes Its Debut in Chile', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dreamliner Makes Its Debut in Chile', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T17:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elaine Glusac', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elaine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glusac', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5b5769c-d20a-5f62-abcd-90d7b92a4157', 'word_count': 150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5b5769c-d20a-5f62-abcd-90d7b92a4157'}, {'abstract': 'And on the seventh day, there was Kanye West and Kim Kardashian.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/fashion-week-stargazing-day-7/', 'snippet': 'And on the seventh day, there was Kanye West and Kim Kardashian.', 'lead_paragraph': 'And on the seventh day, there was Kanye West and Kim Kardashian. From the mayhem caused by the couple, first at Marchesa and later at Louise Goldin, you would have thought Richard Burton and Elizabeth Taylor had been reincarnated.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fashion Week Stargazing: Day 7', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kardashian, Kim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kors, Michael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'West, Kanye', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Marchesa', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T17:02:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bee-Shyuan Chang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bee-shyuan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/827b603d-fee8-50c4-962a-a6afc059eac2', 'word_count': 677, 'uri': 'nyt://article/827b603d-fee8-50c4-962a-a6afc059eac2'}, {'abstract': 'A round-up of new books with exotic settings around the world.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/bookshelf-24/', 'snippet': 'A round-up of new books with exotic settings around the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Han Han, China’s smart-aleck blogger (who’s also a pro racecar driver), uses satire to skewer philandering pols and media censors. His posts are now translated in ‘‘This Generation’’ (Simon & Schuster, $24). Set in New York, London and Maine, Christine Schutt’s novel ‘‘Prosperous Friends’’ (Grove, $24) tracks a young couple lost in a game of psychosexual brinkmanship. ‘‘The Grand Tour’’ (Harper, $28) collects Agatha Christie’s unpublished letters from an epic 1922 journey from South Africa to Hawaii. Neil Steinberg’s ‘‘You Were Never in Chicago’’ (University of Chicago, $25) is both a rollicking newspaperman’s memoir (he’s a Chicago Sun-Times columnist) and a strong case for Second City exceptionalism — belied, a bit, by the city’s inferiority complex: Chicago, Steinberg notes, ‘‘once conducted a study to prove its pedestrians walk faster than those in New York.’’', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '40', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bookshelf', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bookshelf', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Byrne, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Calle, So