il', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/14/business/media/14paper/14paper-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/14/business/media/14paper/14paper-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Taking Pointers From Web Sites, USA Today Modernizes Its Look', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Taking Pointers From Web Sites, USA Today Modernizes Its Look', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kramer, Lawrence S', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'USA Today', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gannett Company Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T17:23:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Haughney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haughney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d25b0a86-e55f-5e0d-898a-55895f727faf', 'word_count': 917, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d25b0a86-e55f-5e0d-898a-55895f727faf'}, {'abstract': 'There are many trials associated with enrolling in a cancer trial. Patients can fail to qualify, or later they can be thrown out or end up in a group that doesn’t get the drug. There are also challenges of geography and timing. But for some of us, a clinical trial is our best hope for living a little bit longer.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/the-trials-of-cancer-trials/', 'snippet': 'There are many trials associated with enrolling in a cancer trial. Patients can fail to qualify, or later they can be thrown out or end up in a group that doesn’t get the drug. There are also challenges of geography and timing. But for some of us,...', 'lead_paragraph': 'I spent last week trying to hope for the recurrence of a malignancy, a tumor of at least 1.5 centimeters (a bit more than half an inch) that would be visible on a CT scan. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Living With Cancer: The Trials of Cancer Trials', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cancer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Clinical Trials', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ovarian Cancer', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T17:24:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Gubar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gubar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d608465-691f-5d2b-93f6-5d269a191cf3', 'word_count': 1023, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d608465-691f-5d2b-93f6-5d269a191cf3'}, {'abstract': 'Advice on tracking down the genuine article.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/how-to-find-or-make-real-buttermilk/', 'snippet': 'Advice on tracking down the genuine article.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many thirsty readers wrote in to Dining on Wednesday after reading about the pleasures of buttermilk, asking how to get their hands on the good stuff. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Find (or Make) Real Buttermilk', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dairy Products', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mendelson, Anne', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T17:35:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Moskin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moskin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7d3c08e-004f-5226-9402-092b4f3ca25a', 'word_count': 704, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7d3c08e-004f-5226-9402-092b4f3ca25a'}, {'abstract': 'David Pogue tries out a pair of Google glasses (Google calls it Google Glass) and is impressed by the early prototype.', 'web_url': 'https://pogue.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/google-glass-and-the-future-of-technology/', 'snippet': 'David Pogue tries out a pair of Google glasses (Google calls it Google Glass) and is impressed by the early prototype.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New gadgets — I mean whole new gadget categories — don’t come along very often. The iPhone was one recent example. You could argue that the iPad was another. But if there’s anything at all as different and bold on the horizon, surely it’s Google Glass.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Google Glass and the Future of Technology', 'kicker': 'Pogue&#039;s Posts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Virtual Reality (Computers)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wearable Computing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'or