 of how hard it is to translate stage comedies and musicals to the screen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Maybe it sounds a little perverse, but I usually try to avoid seeing any movies made from stage plays or musicals I have particularly enjoyed. A natural curiosity about how the material has been translated into a new medium tends to be outweighed by a general foreboding born of past experience. Too often the particular delights of a stage production evaporate considerably — if not entirely — in the translation.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Theater Talkback: Flattened', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stage to Screen: Give It Up For the Audience', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Rock of Ages (Play)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baldwin, Alec', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brand, Russell', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dunst, Kirsten', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Headland, Leslye', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shankman, Adam', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T18:40:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Isherwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isherwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/60f68604-2157-5b67-be7f-c4e0ae32f7f9', 'word_count': 1170, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60f68604-2157-5b67-be7f-c4e0ae32f7f9'}, {'abstract': 'Fox’s alternate singing entry, “The X-Factor,” was hurt by going up against “The Voice” on NBC for an hour. Meanwhile, Fox’s “American Idol” is pursuing high-profile judges for its next season.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/fiercest-competition-this-season-may-be-among-singing-competitions/', 'snippet': 'Fox’s alternate singing entry, “The X-Factor,” was hurt by going up against “The Voice” on NBC for an hour. Meanwhile, Fox’s “American Idol” is pursuing high-profile judges for its next season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wednesday night brought further evidence that network television may be saturated with singing competitions, even as news reports circulated about which celebrated recording artists the Fox network would be adding as judges to revive the flagging flagship of singing shows, “American Idol.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fiercest Competition This Season May Be Among Singing Competitions', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T18:41:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/787bcd3f-eae6-553b-9523-71c5242e142c', 'word_count': 427, 'uri': 'nyt://article/787bcd3f-eae6-553b-9523-71c5242e142c'}, {'abstract': 'Scenes from the New York fashion week photo diary of Alfredo Piola.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/photos-of-the-moment-proenza-schouler-5/', 'snippet': 'Scenes from the New York fashion week photo diary of Alfredo Piola.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog48