athers', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kors, Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wang, Alexander', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Proenza Schouler', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T18:53:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ruth La Ferla', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ruth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'La Ferla', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/21e4cb47-cebe-55ca-87ae-8c078901dc77', 'word_count': 143, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21e4cb47-cebe-55ca-87ae-8c078901dc77'}, {'abstract': 'Izhar Patkin, once a major player in the New York art scene but hardly seen in years, has a new overtly political exhibition at the Jewish Museum in Manhattan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/16/arts/design/izhar-patkin-back-in-the-new-york-art-scene-at-jewish-museum.html', 'snippet': 'Izhar Patkin, once a major player in the New York art scene but hardly seen in years, has a new overtly political exhibition at the Jewish Museum in Manhattan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN the 1980s the Israeli-born painter and sculptor Izhar Patkin often seemed to be everywhere in the New York art world. He was a star in the stable of the flamboyant dealer Holly Solomon, for whom he made not only art but occasional apartment décor (painted dining-room curtains); an adventurous free floater among the worlds of art, fashion and design; and a standout in the 1987 Whitney Biennial, which featured his “Black Paintings,” an ominously beautiful series of images on pleated, hanging neoprene that is now in the collection of the Museum of Modern Art.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/arts/16PATKIN2_SPAN/16PATKIN2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/16/arts/16PATKIN2_SPAN/16PATKIN2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/arts/16PATKIN2_SPAN/16PATKIN2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/arts/16PATKIN2_SPAN/16PATKIN2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/arts/16PATKIN2_SPAN/16PATKIN2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/16/arts/16PATKIN2_SPAN/16PATKIN2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In His Narrative, Time to Get Back ‘Into the Game’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In His Narrative, Time to Get Back ‘Into the Game’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Patkin, Izhar', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jewish Museum (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T18:56:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name'