or so, it may be hard to discern what polling effects reflect momentum from the conventions and what are a response to the fallout from Libya.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Earlier on Thursday, I suggested that we have now gotten some pretty good guidance on the size of President Obama’s convention bounce. For the next week or two, most of our attention will be focused on how much of that bounce he maintains — and how it translates into swing states — and not on trying to gauge its magnitude.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reaction to Libya Attack Could Color Poll Analysis, and Vice Versa', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T19:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea8d9fcb-9778-5ef3-a315-ecfc2e15b380', 'word_count': 514, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea8d9fcb-9778-5ef3-a315-ecfc2e15b380'}, {'abstract': 'An ambassador’s death most likely will only increase efforts to protect American diplomatic personnel from the chaos of the countries where they are posted.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/14/world/middleeast/diplomats-pulled-2-ways-between-protection-and-accessibility.html', 'snippet': 'An ambassador’s death most likely will only increase efforts to protect American diplomatic personnel from the chaos of the countries where they are posted.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Security breaches at American diplomatic compounds in the Middle East this week highlight the two competing challenges that United States diplomats confront: keeping safe in a world full of anti-American extremism and 