he Toronto International Film Festival includes Joss Whedon’s “Much Ado About Nothing” and “Imogene,” starring Kristen Wiig.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/in-toronto-a-number-of-films-find-homes/', 'snippet': 'A roundup of film sales at the Toronto International Film Festival includes Joss Whedon’s “Much Ado About Nothing” and “Imogene,” starring Kristen Wiig.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Toronto International Film Festival is wrapping up with a spate of sales. Lionsgate and Roadside Attractions bought Joss Whedon’s adaptation of “Much Ado About Nothing,” which played well with “Buffy” fans at the festival. Shot in black-and-white in just 12 days, it has a modern tone (and a cast full of Whedon favorites, from “Angel,” “Dollhouse” and “Firefly”). ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Toronto a Number of Films Find Homes', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Film Festival', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Toronto International Film Festival', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burns, Edward', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cianfrance, Derek', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cooper, Bradley', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gosling, Ryan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jordan, Neil', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marclay, Christian', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mendes, Eva', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Whedon, Joss', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wiig, Kristen', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'First Run Features', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Focus Features', 'rank': 1