e': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sablich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sablich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/77a137e1-37cd-5c1c-810c-5969d6d3a942', 'word_count': 2020, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77a137e1-37cd-5c1c-810c-5969d6d3a942'}, {'abstract': 'Mark Wetjen, a Democratic member of the Commodity Futures Trading Commission, told an industry group that the agency was debating how to crack down on foreign derivatives trading.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/4-years-after-lehmans-demise-regulators-debate-overhaul/', 'snippet': 'Mark Wetjen, a Democratic member of the Commodity Futures Trading Commission, told an industry group that the agency was debating how to crack down on foreign derivatives trading.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Four years after Wall Street teetered on the brink of collapse, regulators are struggling to rein in foreign risk-taking that imperils American banks. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '4 Years After Lehman’s Demise, Regulators Debate Overhaul', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gensler, Gary S', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wetjen, Mark P', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Commodity Futures Trading Commission', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Swaps and Derivatives Assn', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lehman Brothers Holdings Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T20:01:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a6dee48-af2d-54f3-903a-da89c093ba60', 'word_count': 559, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a6dee48-af2d-54f3-903a-da89c093ba60'}, {'abstract': 'Russia’s president admits that some of his photographed wildlife encounters were not as spontaneous as they seemed.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/on-our-radar-putins-wildlife-exploits/', 'snippet': 'Russia’s president admits that some of his photographed wildlife encounters were not as spontaneous as they seemed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Russia’s president, Vladimir V. Putin, acknowledges that many of his outdoor adventures with wildlife have been carefully staged. For example, a tiger he was shown shooting in the wild with a tranquilizer gun was apparently a captive one that had been transported to the scene. [Reuters]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Our Radar: Putin’s Wildlife Exploits', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T20:05:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df864fc2-95c7-5038-876c-8c1d8b8749bf', 'word_count': 155, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df864fc2-95c7-5038-876c-8c1d8b8749bf'}, {'abstract': 'In her many pursuits, this Swedish-born, Netherlands-based tastemaker stays true to her roots.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/profile-in-style-ulrika-lundgren/', 'snippet': 'In her many pursuits, this Swedish-born, Netherlands-based tastemaker stays true to her roots.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Whether she’s designing her rock ’n’ roll-romantic fashion label, Rika, decorating the Amsterdam apartment she shares with her family or choosing art for the walls of Maison Rika, her tiny canal-side guesthouse, this Swedish-born, Netherlands-based tastemaker stays true to her roots — for the most part. “I’m super-Scandinavian in my style,” she says, “but because I haven’t lived there for so long, I’m influenced by other cultures and the places I go, like London, Paris, Mexico, Mallorca and Bali.” A common visual vein that runs through all of Lundgren’s work is her signature palette: black and cream punctuated by jolts of primary color in the form of art and accessories. “My interiors, like my clothes and bags, are quite urban,” she says. “But I don’t like coldness, so I soften the edges and add warmth.” More…', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '36', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Profile in Style | Ulrika Lundgren', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ulrika Lundgren', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T20:08:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sandra Ballentine', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ballentine', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b5c1dd4-aa00-5e06-8c47-be33f1bbdc2f', 'word_count': 136, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b5c1dd4-aa00-5e06-8c47-be33f1bbdc2f'}, {'abstract': '“Armor for the Joust of Peace” will be on display at the Great Hall at the Metropolitan Museum of Art to celebrate the arms and armor department’s centennial exhibition.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/14/arts/design/armor-for-the-joust-of-peace-at-the-met.html', 'snippet': '“Armor for the Joust of Peace” will be on display at the Great Hall at the Metropolitan Museum of Art to celebrate the arms and armor department’s centennial exhibition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Great Hall at the Metropolitan Museum of Art is such a busy place that it’s easy to miss the artworks periodically on view there. Two 1967-68 silk-screens of Warhol’s “Flowers” — a teaser to “Regarding Warhol: Sixty Artists, Fifty Years,” opening on Tuesday — were recently hung on the eastern side of the hall. A colossal statue of a pharaoh, weighing about nine tons, sits regally on the north side.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/14/arts/VOGEL2/VOGEL2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 671, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/14/arts/VOGEL2/VOGEL2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1342, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/14/arts/VOGEL2/VOGEL2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/14/arts/VOGEL2/VOGEL2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/14/arts/VOGEL2/VOGEL2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dusting Off a Horseman for New Battles', 'kicker': 'Inside Art', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARMOR', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Salle, David', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T20:11:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Vogel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vogel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/81bf6874-96f7-5469-888a-b5fb9ba0de98', 'word_count': 993, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81bf6874-96f7-5469-888a-b5fb9ba0de98'}, {'abstract': 'Two Republican senators introduced legislation that would forbid same-sex marriages on military bases.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/defending-conscience-restricting-rights/', 'snippet': 'Two Republican senators introduced legislation that would forbid same-sex marriages on military bases.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Having lost the fight over Don’t Ask, Don’t Tell—repealed a year ago this month— Senators James Inhofe of Oklahoma and Roger Wicker of Mississippi are trying to make it as hard as possible for gay men and lesbians to exercise their civil rights while serving their country in the armed forces.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Defending ‘Conscience,’ Restricting Rights', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense of Marriage Act (1996)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Inhofe, James M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wicker, Roger', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T20:12:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/081d10d3-0e72-54ec-95c3-8fc46410b6da', 'word_count': 362, 'uri': 'nyt://article/081d10d3-0e72-54ec-95c3-8fc46410b6da'}, {'abstract': 'The cost of adapters for iPhone chargers can add up fast.', 'web_url': 'https://pogue.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/the-cost-of-adapters-adds-up/', 'snippet': 'The cost of adapters for iPhone chargers can add up fast.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In my post about the new iPhone 5, I grumbled about the new power/sync connector, which doesn’t fit any of the millions of existing cords, docks, speakers and accessories. Unless, that is, you buy an insanely overpriced $30 plug adapter or a $40 cable adapter from Apple.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Cost of Adapters Adds Up', 'kicker': 'Pogue&#039;s Posts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T20:15:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Pogue', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogue', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9dff7e93-77ce-531c-83f3-01e2339b7582', 'word_count': 149, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9dff7e93-77ce-531c-83f3-01e2339b7582'}, {'abstract': 'Private equity’s use of carried interest to lower tax bills, though legal, has drawn criticism. But another lesser-known method might not withstand an I.R.S. challenge.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/14/business/a-private-equity-tax-tactic-may-not-be-legal-high-low-finance.html', 'snippet': 'Private equity’s use of carried interest to lower tax bills, though legal, has drawn criticism. But another lesser-known method might not withstand an I.R.S. challenge.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Anyone may arrange his affairs so that his taxes shall be as low as possible; he is not bound to choose that pattern which best pays the treasury. There is not even a patriotic duty to increase one’s taxes.”', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/19/business/norris-75-standardinline/norris-75-standardinline-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/04/19/business/norris-75-standardinline/norris-75-standardinline-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Tax Tactic That’s Open to Question', 'kicker': 'High & Low Finance', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Tax Tactic That’s Open To Question', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Gains Tax', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T20:22:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Floyd Norris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Norris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f77ff31-4d9c-5197-a47e-0c092ad912a4', 'word_count': 1296, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f77ff31-4d9c-5197-a47e-0c092ad912a4'}, {'abstract': 'Calvin Klein’s Francisco Costa brought the New York collections to a close this afternoon with a new take on the geometric black-and-white graphics that have been seen all over the runways in the form of stripes, grids and checks.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/the-new-york-finale-at-calvin-klein/', 'snippet': 'Calvin Klein’s Francisco Costa brought the New York collections to a close this afternoon with a new take on the geometric black-and-white graphics that have been seen all over the runways in the form of stripes, grids and checks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Francisco Costa brought the New York collections to a close this afternoon with a Calvin Klein collection that showed a new take on the geometric black-and-white graphics that have been all over the runways in the form of stripes, grids and checks. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The New York Finale at Calvin Klein', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Costa, Francisco', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Calvin Klein Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T20:26:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None,