 where the police fired tear gas to disperse crowds.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/protests-spread-across-middle-east-as-anger-over-video-mounts/', 'snippet': 'Two days after assailants killed four Americans in Libya, protests were reported at American missions in Morocco, Sudan and Tunisia, where the police fired tear gas to disperse crowds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Protests spread across the Middle East and North Africa on Thursday, most of them directed at American Embassies and offices linked to United States diplomatic activities, as anger mounted over a video denigrating the Prophet Muhammad.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Protests Spread as Anger Over Anti-Islam Film Mounts', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cairo (Egypt)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Middle East', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Morocco', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tahrir Square (Cairo)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tunisia', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '