: 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/13/fashion/20120913OFFTHERUNWAYEIGHT-slide-NNP7/20120913OFFTHERUNWAYEIGHT-slide-NNP7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/13/fashion/20120913OFFTHERUNWAYEIGHT-slide-NNP7/20120913OFFTHERUNWAYEIGHT-slide-NNP7-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Off the Runway: Day 8', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Fashion Week', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lauren, Ralph', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klein, Calvin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T21:49:57+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Fashion & Style', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/6465fd9c-9700-503a-b38b-a6d0cc1d6498', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/6465fd9c-9700-503a-b38b-a6d0cc1d6498'}, {'abstract': 'The sports radio talk show host on WFAN-AM appeared to nod off during an interview on Monday, but he says no. “I was dragging during the show,” is the most he will concede.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/my-eyes-were-heavy-but-i-didnt-doze-off-during-the-show-mike-francesa-says/', 'snippet': 'The sports radio talk show host on WFAN-AM appeared to nod off during an interview on Monday, but he says no. “I was dragging during the show,” is the most he will concede.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The sports radio talk show host Mike Francesa — who appeared to take a brief nap while conducting an interview on Monday on WFAN-AM in New York — said on Thursday that while he had been tired from getting no sleep the night before, he had not actually fallen asleep while talking to Sweeny Murti, who covers the Yankees for the station.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'My Eyes Were Heavy, but I Didn’t Doze Off During the Show, Mike Francesa Says', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sleep', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Francesa, Mike', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WFAN-AM', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'YES Network', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T21:50:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/58206591-ea82-557a-8d9a-f47d4a4f8353', 'word_count': 329, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58206591-ea82-557a-8d9a-f47d4a4f8353'}, {'abstract': 'The Met has arranged with Le Poisson Rouge, the high-art cabaret space in Greenwich Village, to present two concerts.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/met-opera-concerts-set-for-le-poisson-rouge/', 'snippet': 'The Met has arranged with Le Poisson Rouge, the high-art cabaret space in Greenwich Village, to present two concerts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Metropolitan Opera is going downtown. The Met has arranged with Le Poisson Rouge, the high-art cabaret space in Greenwich Village, to present two concerts based on Met productions of two contemporary operas: “The Tempest” by Thomas Adès and Nico Muhly’s “Two Boys.” The collaboration gives the Met some visibility in the slightly hipper, younger and more contemporary music scene, and adds big-institution luster to Le Poisson Rouge, which has become firmly established as a New York concert site. The Met often collaborates with major institutions like Juilliard, the Metropolitan Museum of Art and the Museum of Modern Art but rarely with such a small fish. “It seemed like a good idea, as a way of educating the audience and reaching out to a new audience, to have performances down there,” Peter Gelb, the Met’s general manager, said. Mr. Gelb said the first performance, on Oct. 26, would involve a few cast members of “The Tempest” and Mr. Adès as pianist performing scaled-down numbers from the opera. The concert will include works by Ives, Purcell, Stravinsky and Tippett, with other instrumentalists joining in, a spokesman later added. Mr. Muhly will play and program the second concert in May. Mr. Gelb said the Met was paying for the performances and would split the ticket take with Le Poisson Rouge.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Met Opera Concerts Set For Le Poisson Rouge', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Met Opera Concerts Set For Le Poisson Rouge', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Le Poisson Rouge', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Museum of Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T21:51:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf15d131-40bb-5838-8866-5a5dab992b2f', 'word_count': 218, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf15d131-40bb-5838-8866-5a5dab992b2f'}, {'abstract': 'Bruce Springsteen’s song “We Take Care of Our Own” was played immediately after President Obama’s speech at the Democratic National Convention on Sept. 6. By the end of the week, the song’s sales had surged 409 percent, according to Billboard, with 2,000 downloads.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/a-convention-bounce-for-the-boss/', 'snippet': 'Bruce Springsteen’s song “We Take Care of Our Own” was played immediately after President Obama’s speech at the Democratic National Convention on Sept. 6. By the end of the week, the song’s sales had surged 409 percent, according to Billboard, wit...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bruce Springsteen did not perform at the Democratic National Convention, but he is still enjoying a convention “bounce.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Convention ‘Bounce’ for the Boss', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Convention Lift For Springsteen, Too', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Democratic National Convention', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Springsteen, Bruce', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T21:55:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Corasaniti', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Corasaniti', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/789cc169-73f3-515e-89e0-82d93d866dd3', 'word_count': 334, 'uri': 'nyt://article/789cc169-73f3-515e-89e0-82d93d866dd3'}, {'abstract': 'The singer-songwriter-playwright Jason Robert Brown performed a set of his songs that are just short of being cabaret staples at 54 Below.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/14/arts/music/jason-robert-brown-at-54-below.html', 'snippet': 'The singer-songwriter-playwright Jason Robert Brown performed a set of his songs that are just short of being cabaret staples at 54 Below.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you pay little attention to the insular world of musical theater, you might not know that the 42-year-old singer, composer and playwright Jason Robert Brown is the Billy Joel of his generation. The heartfelt outpourings of this brainy, driven, hypersensitive, self-conscious introvert deserve to be standards, but still aren’t. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/14/arts/14BROWN_SPAN/14BROWN_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 715, 'width': 680, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/14/arts/14BROWN_SPAN/14BROWN_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 715, 'width': 680, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/14/arts/14BROWN_SPAN/14BROWN_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/14/arts/14BROWN_SPAN/14BROWN_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/14/arts/14BROWN_SPAN/14BROWN_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Striving for New Standards, Just the Way They Are', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Striving for New Standards, Just the Way They Are', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Jason Robert', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T21:56:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/451a1126-cd75-554e-aa6f-ccdd7213b000', 'word_count': 392, 'uri': 'nyt://article/451a1126-cd75-554e-aa6f-ccdd7213b000'}, {'abstract': 'A bankruptcy filing typically remains on a credit report for seven years, but that doesn’t mean borrowers have to wait that long to apply for a mortgage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/16/realestate/mortgages-life-after-bankruptcy.html', 'snippet': 'A bankruptcy filing typically remains on a credit report for seven years, but that doesn’t mean borrowers have to wait that long to apply for a mortgage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EVERY month tens of thousands of people file for federal bankruptcy protection, mostly to wipe out debts and start anew.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/realestate/16mort-graphic/16mort-graphic-articleLarge.png', 'height': 303, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/16/realestate/16mort-graphic/16mort-graphic-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xla