le/08aa6856-e089-5098-bc87-7e1b6fc80308'}, {'abstract': 'James Silvia, who in the 1950s served Alexander H. Rice as fourth footman, has a unique perspective on servant life on the American continent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/16/realestate/streetscapes-whatever-happened-to-the-fourth-footman.html', 'snippet': 'James Silvia, who in the 1950s served Alexander H. Rice as fourth footman, has a unique perspective on servant life on the American continent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAN’T wait until the new season of “Downton Abbey” starts in January? Well, then, how about the New York version, starring James Silvia, who in the 1950s served Alexander H. Rice as fourth footman in his Newport, R.I., mansion and New York town house at Fifth Avenue and at 71st Street. Now retired from a career of teaching in Manhattan, Mr. Silvia, the son of a Portuguese gardener who worked on the estates of Newport, has a unique perspective on servant life on the American continent.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/realestate/16STREETS1_SPAN/16STREETS1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/16/realestate/16STREETS1_SPAN/16STREETS1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/realestate/16STREETS1_SPAN/streets-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 772, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/realestate/16STREETS1_SPAN/streets-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1543, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtyp