 on a double-play ball in Boston, but he insists he can keep playing, and his manager believes him.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/jeter-says-he-feels-great-but-does-he/', 'snippet': 'The Yankees’ shortstop came up limping on a double-play ball in Boston, but he insists he can keep playing, and his manager believes him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON — Derek Jeter is, in the eyes of his manager, difficult to read. So when he arrived at Fenway Park on Thursday and told Joe Girardi than his left ankle felt great, Girardi had to interpret what this actually meant.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jeter Says He Feels Great, but Does He?', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANKLES (BODY PART)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garcia, Freddy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Girardi, Joe', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jeter, Derek', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nova, Ivan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pettitte, Andy', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T23:26:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a0c868bb-bde9-57b2-ba77-1048df02c90c', 'word_count': 791, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a0c868bb-bde9-57b2-ba77-1048df02c90c'}, {'abstract': 'Cassie Jaye’s “Right to Love: An American Family” chronicles the family of Jay Foxworthy and Bryan Leffew to make a case for same-sex marriage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/14/movies/the-documentary-the-right-to-love-an-american-family.html', 'snippet': 'Cassie Jaye’s “Right to Love: An American Family” chronicles the family of Jay Foxworthy and Bryan Leffew to make a case for same-sex marriage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The kids are adorable, their two dads effortlessly likable and the love that binds them all inarguable. Yet Cassie Jaye’s squishy documentary, “The Right to Love: An American Family,” tries the patience, and not just because of its regrettably saccharine soundtrack. Any film this committed to arguing in favor of same-sex marriage needs at least as much spine as heart.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/14/arts/14RDP_RIGHT_SPAN/14RDP_RIGHT_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/14/arts/14RDP_RIGHT_SPAN/14RDP_RIGHT_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/14/arts/14RDP_RIGHT_SPAN/14RDP_RIGHT_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/14/arts/14RDP_RIGHT_SPAN/14RDP_RIGHT_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 937, 'width': 1667, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image',