computers, fresh from Chinese factory floors, that carried a particularly pernicious computer virus — one capable of invading bank accounts, starting computer attacks and creating back doors to let criminals have their way with infected machines.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/microsoft-finds-pcs-that-ship-pre-infected/', 'snippet': 'Microsoft said it had discovered several new computers, fresh from Chinese factory floors, that carried a particularly pernicious computer virus — one capable of invading bank accounts, starting computer attacks and creating back doors to let crim...', 'lead_paragraph': ' One more thing to worry about: Your brand-spanking-new computer could be infected with a virus that will raid your online bank account.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Microsoft Finds PCs That Ship Pre-Infected', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T23:43:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicole Perlroth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicole', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perlroth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7dedf878-b04e-57f3-9ad9-cb4f429be376', 'word_count': 404, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7dedf878-b04e-57f3-9ad9-cb4f429be376'}, {'abstract': 'The $400 million face-lift at the flagship department store on 34th Street is compromising the Art Deco look of the ground-floor pillars, Theodore Grunewald says.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/13/macys-is-losing-its-marble-annoying-a-preservationist/', 'snippet': 'The $400 million face-lift at the flagship department store on 34th Street is compromising the Art Deco look of the ground-floor pillars, Theodore Grunewald says.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Macy’s is giving itself a $400 million makeover that it says will maintain the store’s “architectural integrity,” but one preservationist, Theodore Grunewald, is not happy.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/14/nyregion/13cityroom-macys-new/13cityroom-macys-new-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/14/nyregion/13cityroom-macys-new/13cityroom-macys-new-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1353, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/14/nyregion/13cityroom-macys-new/13cityroom-macys-new-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/14/nyregion/13cityroom-macys-new/13cityroom-macys-new-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/14/nyregion/13cityroom-macys-new/13cityroom-macys-new-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Makeover on 34th St., but Not All Believe in It', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Makeover On 34th St., But Not All Believe in It', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Building (Construction)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Macy's Inc", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-13T23:47:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Barron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1fb6487c-815b-5ee1-9aa9-67e8e977511f', 'word_count': 745, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1fb6487c-815b-5ee1-9aa9-67e8e977511f'}, {'abstract': '“The Manzanar Fishing Club” is a subdued documentary about the World War II internment of Japanese-Americans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/14/movies/the-manzanar-fishing-club.html', 'snippet': '“The Manzanar Fishing Club” is a subdued documentary about the World War II internment of Japanese-Americans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I don’t detect an overload of films documenting the World War II-era internment of Japanese-Americans, even though the political, social and cultural history clearly is significant enough to warrant more interest. An artifact in the new documentary “The Manzanar Fishing Club” makes that case: a badge reading, “Jap Hunting License — Open Season.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/14/arts/14RDP_MANZANAR_SPAN/14RDP_MANZANAR_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 806, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/14/ar