y-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Slain Contractor, a Life of Risks Overseas', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Slain Contractor, A Life of Risks Overseas', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Doherty, Glen A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Navy Seals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stevens, J Christopher', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T00:24:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jess Bidgood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jess', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bidgood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0bf118d4-35d2-544f-955c-3fbf860361e3', 'word_count': 411, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0bf118d4-35d2-544f-955c-3fbf860361e3'}, {'abstract': 'I was going to meet with Ambassador Stevens on a project that was the kind of partnership that he believed could help Libya move beyond decades of stagnation and despotism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/14/opinion/what-libya-lost-when-ambassador-stevens-died.html', 'snippet': 'I was going to meet with Ambassador Stevens on a project that was the kind of partnership that he believed could help Libya move beyond decades of stagnation and despotism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ON Wednesday morning, my colleagues and I were to meet in Benghazi with J. Christopher Stevens, the American ambassador to Libya, to discuss a plan for a new division of emergency medicine at Benghazi Medical Center, the largest and most modern hospital in eastern Libya. The meeting never took place. The night before, militants laid siege to the American Consulate in Benghazi, killing the ambassador and three other Americans. The ambassador was taken, without a pulse, to the hospital we hoped to upgrade. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Libya Lost', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What Libya Lost', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stevens, J Christopher', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T00:30:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ethan Chorin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ethan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chorin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa2864c0-af97-5b01-9ba3-2a5c74f8e25c', 'word_count': 1175, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa2864c0-af97-5b01-9ba3-2a5c74f8e25c'}, {'abstract': 'Diplomacy is a dangerous profession, and we must make its work safer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/14/opinion/in-libya-and-elsewhere-our-diplomats-deserve-better.html', 'snippet': 'Diplomacy is a dangerous profession, and we must make its work safer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Falls Church, Va.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': '