_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T08:32:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5bfcdbc-e922-5b31-8362-92d81866c977', 'word_count': 52, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5bfcdbc-e922-5b31-8362-92d81866c977'}, {'abstract': 'What company will begin posting calorie counts on all its menus next week?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/14/fast-food-calorie-counting/', 'snippet': 'What company will begin posting calorie counts on all its menus next week?', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHAT company will begin posting calorie counts on all its menus next week?WHAT healthy foods will this chain be adding?WHAT are the signs that other major restaurant chains are working to make their menus more healthful?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fast-Food Calorie Counting', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T08:44:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ariha Setalvad', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ariha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Setalvad', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2ada64e-a415-5a73-b549-2a54a663124c', 'word_count': 123, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2ada64e-a415-5a73-b549-2a54a663124c'}, {'abstract': 'The Associated Press’s “Today in History” videos should resonate with boomers. On Sept. 14, contraception and Princess Grace.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/14/booming/14history.html', 'snippet': 'The Associated Press’s “Today in History” videos should resonate with boomers. On Sept. 14, contraception and Princess Grace.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By the time you reach your 50s and 60s, you’ve lived through a good deal of history, although a lot of the time, as it was happening, you may not have realized it would turn into history. For many of my generation, that first memory is of Nov. 22, 1963, when President John F. Kennedy was assassinated. But during the recent memorial tributes to the astronaut Neil Armstrong, I was reminded of an earlier moment. When I was in third grade, in 1961, several classes at our school were led into the one room that had a TV, to watch America’s first manned spaceflight. Alan Shepard’s entire trip lasted 15 minutes — we watched the whole thing, broadcast live, in black and white. I remember the clapping when we knew he was safe and in particular how excited our usually reserved teachers were. I’d forgotten this until I saw the old news clip.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'History in the Making', 'kicker': 'Remember This', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Boomers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T09:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Booming', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Winerip', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Winerip', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c974464e-b992-5c98-afb4-00c91bc35e38', 'word_count': 314, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c974464e-b992-5c98-afb4-00c91bc35e38'}, {'abstract': 'Wanted: Your opinions on the more serious matters, along with some questions of absolutely no consequence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/14/booming/14friday.html', 'snippet': 'Wanted: Your opinions on the more serious matters, along with some questions of absolutely no consequence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Each Friday we’re going to ask you to give us your opinion about something or other that has to do with the boomer era. This is definitely not a test. Nor a scientific poll. In some cases it will be a more serious matter, like, “What has been the biggest societal change in your lifetime?” Other questions will be of absolutely no consequence, like, “Name the worst clothing fad not including bell bottoms.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/14/booming/14question/14question-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/14/booming/14question/14question-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/14/booming/14question/14question-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/14/booming/14question/14question-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/14/booming/14question/14question-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/14/booming/14question/14question-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/14/booming/14question/14question-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s Your Favorite ’60s or ’70s Song?', 'kicker': 'The Friday Question', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Boomers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T09:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Booming', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Winerip', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Winerip', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5fcd1288-5598-5263-b7f2-11c2d442c797', 'word_count': 140, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5fcd1288-5598-5263-b7f2-11c2d442c797'}, {'abstract': 'A daughter recalls, at age 12, her baby boomer father moving out and suddenly having “two home phone numbers — that’s 14 digits.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/14/booming/14children.html', 'snippet': 'A daughter recalls, at age 12, her baby boomer father moving out and suddenly having “two home phone numbers — that’s 14 digits.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'I will miss my family, but especially my dad.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/12/booming/12goldberg/12goldberg-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/12/booming/12goldberg/12goldberg-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/12/booming/12goldberg/12goldberg-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 670, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', '