 sixth and seventh installments of the continuing series “Smoke-Filled Rooms,” the Times staff photographer Stephen Crowley examines the recent presidential nominating conventions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The summer presidential nominating conventions in Tampa, Fla., and Charlotte, N.C., came and went — promises were made, stances were taken, confetti and balloons tumbled from the ceiling. The Republican spectacle was beset by bad weather, and the Democrats made every effort to demonstrate confidence. But the prevailing opinion of the pundits was that the conventions hardly mattered. Did they? Only 53 days remain until voting, and polls continue to show a neck-and-neck race, suggesting an electorate unmoved by all the fanfare. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Looking Back on the Party Conventions', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T09:00:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/82fcf7a5-2042-5a27-8b44-905f6f769fcb', 'word_count': 158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82fcf7a5-2042-5a27-8b44-905f6f769fcb'}, {'abstract': 'Anti-American rage that began over a video insult to Islam spread to nearly 20 countries in the Middle East and beyond.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/15/world/middleeast/anti-american-protests-over-film-enter-4th-day.html', 'snippet': 'Anti-American rage that began over a video insult to Islam spread to nearly 20 countries in the Middle East and beyond.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Anti-American rage that began this week over a video insult to Islam spread to nearly 20 countries across the Middle East and beyond on Friday, with violent and sometimes deadly protests that convulsed the birthplaces of the Arab 