ab School for Collaborative Studies, is one of eight high school seniors around the world blogging about their college searches.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The bus came to an abrupt stop and we were there. I was among a group of 45, high school freshmen at the time, who stepped onto the recently mowed grass in front of the admissions office. We were about to begin our first college tour.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Advocate for Students With Disabilities Imagines His Ideal College', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADMISSIONS STANDARDS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cerebral Palsy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Special Education', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Common Application, The', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T10:00:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bryan Stromer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bryan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stromer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/180005e5-6449-51f8-b6a2-46235c4e2132', 'word_count': 594, 'uri': 'nyt://article/180005e5-6449-51f8-b6a2-46235c4e2132'}, {'abstract': 'Political news from today’s Times, plus a look at what’s happening in Washington.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/14/the-early-word-in-it-for-the-duration/', 'snippet': 'Political news from today’s Times, plus a look at what’s happening in Washi