unce, Holding Obama’s Polls to a Higher Standard', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T11:55:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/82f9c8ce-980d-5737-9e20-21d46d5c885c', 'word_count': 774, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82f9c8ce-980d-5737-9e20-21d46d5c885c'}, {'abstract': 'Many retro apps try to recreate past technologies pretty closely, but there are of course other apps that take a retro idea and modernize it.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/14/app-smart-extra/', 'snippet': 'Many retro apps try to recreate past technologies pretty closely, but there are of course other apps that take a retro idea and modernize it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week’s App Smart column took you into the wonderful world of retro apps — apps that give you a bit of a blast from your past by emulating things from yesteryear.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'App Smart Extra: More Nostalgia', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Historypin.com', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Path.com', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T11:59:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kit Eaton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kit', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eaton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d77efcb8-4059-59ea-80e1-c446e96d56d4', 'word_count': 302, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d77efcb8-4059-59ea-80e1-c446e96d56d4'}, {'abstract': 'Answers to questions about consolidating loans, paying late fees, loan forgiveness for public service, and declaring bankruptcy.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/14/answers-to-your-questions-about-student-loans-part-three/', 'snippet': 'Answers to questions about consolidating loans, paying late fees, loan forgiveness for public service, and declaring bankruptcy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week, two New York Times reporters and Geoffry Walsh, an expert on student debt and bankruptcy at the National Consumer Law Center, are answering questions about ways to avoid default, pay off student loans or try to expunge student loans through bankruptcy court. Along with questions, some readers proposed their own answers. The first set of answers is here, the second is here, and the third set is below.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Answers to Your Questions About Student Loans, Part 3', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Student Loans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T12:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '