with its base, and some are wondering if the Greens’ alliance with the Socialist Party can survive.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/15/world/europe/energy-policy-divides-governing-coalition-in-france.html', 'snippet': 'Compromises on nuclear power have placed the Green Party’s leadership at odds with its base, and some are wondering if the Greens’ alliance with the Socialist Party can survive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — After just four months in power, the governing coalition of the Socialist Party and the Greens is already marred by deep ideological divisions over energy policy, in particular how quickly and sharply France should move to reduce its heavy dependence on nuclear energy.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Energy Policy in France Divides Governing Coalition of Socialists and Greens', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Energy Policy in France Divides Governing Coalition of Socialists and Greens', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hollande, Francois', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Energy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T13:22:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicola Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicola', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8914d724-0ec2-551b-8fd8-9b039effae0c', 'word_count': 1129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8914d724-0ec2