 about the royals’ privacy and fed the inexhaustible interest they generate at home and abroad. Do they deserve the celebrity treatment — and do we care?', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The European media were all aflutter on Friday as a French magazine published topless photos of Kate Middleton, the Duchess of Cambridge, wife of Britain’s Prince William and the future Queen of England.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/14/blogs/rdv-kate-middleton-in-asia/rdv-kate-middleton-in-asia-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 698, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/14/blogs/rdv-kate-middleton-in-asia/rdv-kate-middleton-in-asia-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1395, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/14/blogs/rdv-kate-middleton-in-asia/rdv-kate-middleton-in-asia-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/14/blogs/rdv-kate-middleton-in-asia/rdv-kate-middleton-in-asia-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/14/blogs/rdv-kate-middleton-in-asia/rdv-kate-middleton-in-asia-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Topless Royal Photos Expose Public’s Bottomless Fascination', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Royal Family', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Catherine, Duchess of Cambridge', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T13:56:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Morris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84605a86-f7be-5e4a-9bff-687b70bcaad6', 'word_count': 518, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84605a86-f7be-5e4a-9bff-687b70bcaad6'}, {'abstract': 'USA Today hits newsstands with a redesigned look, and YouTube’s decision to block an anti-Muslim video in Libya and Egypt highlights the role of its parent, Google.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/14/the-breakfast-meeting-usa-tomorrow-and-an-anti-muslim-video-vexes-youtube/', 'snippet': 'USA Today hits newsstands with a redesigned look, and YouTube’s decision to block an anti-Muslim video in Libya and Egypt highlights the role of its parent, Google.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A redesigned USA Today was on newsstands on Friday, and the redesign owes a big debt to the aesthetics and customs of the Internet, Christine Haughney reports. The USA Today Web site, which will be unveiled this weekend, has been redesigned to resemble an e-reader, with a smoother scroll from page to page. The twist, however, is that the abundance of information on the Internet has largely taken away what made the national newspaper special 30 years ago. The moves are part of a broader rethinking by USA Today’s parent company, Gannett, to consolidate the news gathering of its TV and newspaper assets.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: USA Tomorrow? And an Anti-Muslim Video Vexes YouTube', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'k