York Stock Exchange agreed to adopt new internal controls and pay a $5 million penalty to settle accusations that its trading data gave select clients a split-second advantage.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/09/14/n-y-s-e-settles-regulatory-action-on-trading-data/', 'snippet': 'The New York Stock Exchange agreed to adopt new internal controls and pay a $5 million penalty to settle accusations that its trading data gave select clients a split-second advantage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the latest federal action against a major exchange, the New York Stock Exchange settled accusations on Friday that its trading data gave select clients a split-second advantage over retail investors.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Stock Exchange Settles Case Over Early Data Access', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Big Board Settles Case Over Early Data Access', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'High-Frequency and Flash Trading', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Securities and Commodities Violations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Stock Exchange', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NYSE Euronext', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T15:18:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6388885f-e143-584f-b171-a50adff19e6c', 'word_count': 701, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6388885f-e143-584f-b171-a50adff19e6c'}, {'abstract': 'Rich Cohen describes the rise of Samuel Zemurray, the fruit peddler who came to control much of Central America.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/16/books/review/the-fish-that-ate-the-whale-by-rich-cohen.html', 'snippet': 'Rich Cohen describes the rise of Samuel Zemurray, the fruit peddler who came to control much of Central America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Amid the vast outpouring of literature about America’s banana empire in the Caribbean, no one seems to have written a full-fledged biography of the remarkable Samuel Zemurray, who guided the United Fruit Company through perilous times. Rich Cohen has rectified that oversight. Cohen, the author of “Tough Jews: Fathers, Sons, and Gangster Dreams” and “Sweet and Low: A Family Story,” now gives us the fascinating tale of “Sam the Banana Man,” a poor Russian Jew who emigrated to Alabama as a teenager and ended up controlling much of Central America.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Banana Republican', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Banana Republican', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cohen, Rich', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zemurray, Samuel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T15:19:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Lewis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lewis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1df546f-c1a3-5243-b333-b3880612395b', 'word_count': 629, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1df546f-c1a3-5243-b333-b3880612395b'}, {'abstract': 'Breast milk is full of chemicals; breasts are full of silicone.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/16/books/review/breasts-by-florence-williams.html', 'snippet': 'Breast milk is full of chemicals; breasts are full of silicone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The breast milk of the writer Florence Williams contains a striking level of perchlorate, a key component of rocket fuel. This does not, however, invest her with superpowers, as it might if she were a comic-book hero, or even make her special. Rather, as she explains in “Breasts: A Natural and Unnatural History,” her mammary glands are no different from those of most American women. In the year 2012, breast-feeding still passes many good things from mother to baby: vitamins, minerals and “a solid hedge of extras to help ward off a lifetime of diseases.” But the practice also typically transfers “paint thinners, dry-cleaning fluids, wood preservatives, toilet deodorizers, cosmetic additives, gasoline by-products, rocket fuel, termite poisons, fungicides” and varieties of flame retardants, one of which, Penta-BDE, was banned by the European Union because of its chronic toxicity to humans.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/books/review/16SUBLORD/16SUBLORD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 972, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/books/review/16SUBLORD/16SUBLORD-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1944, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/books/review/16SUBLORD/16SUBLORD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/16/books/review/16SUBLORD/16SUBLORD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/books/review/16SUBLORD/16SUBLORD-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Unnatural Women', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Unnatural Women', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Breasts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Florence', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T15:20:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By M. G. Lord', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/258c8948-8c1f-51fd-a446-19ea4c67deee', 'word_count': 1289, 'uri': 'nyt://article/258c8948-8c1f-51fd-a446-19ea4c67deee'}, {'abstract': 'In Clare Clark’s novel, the wife of a radical politician leads a double life in Victorian London.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/16/books/review/beautiful-lies-by-clare-clark.html', 'snippet': 'In Clare Clark’s novel, the wife of a radical politician leads a double life in Victorian London.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Clare Clark’s fiction manages to maintain historical accuracy even as it indulges in great storytelling and lush prose. In her first novel, “The Great Stink,” a thriller that takes place in the sewers of Victorian London, Clark wrote with such rich detail that you could almost smell the fetid air as you turned the pages. In “Savage Lands,” she transported readers to the young colony of Louisiana in the early 1700s, setting a complex love story against a fecund yet relentlessly cruel landscape that became as important to the plot as the characters themselves.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/books/review/16WULF/16WULF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 814, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/books/review/16WULF/16WULF-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1986, 'width': 1579, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/books/review/16WULF/16WULF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/16/books/review/16WULF/16WULF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/books/review/16WULF/16WULF-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Truth in Masquerade', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Truth in Masquerade', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clark, Clare (1967- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clark, Clare', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T15:21:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {