demands of the Common Core Standards with the content of that week’s New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/14/introducing-an-experiment-weekly-common-core-practice-prompts/', 'snippet': 'We’re collaborating with two New Jersey teachers and their freshman classes to bring you three quick, engaging tasks each week that match the demands of the Common Core Standards with the content of that week’s New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last year we took some baby steps in thinking about how the new Common Core State Standards will affect the work we do on this blog.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Introducing an Experiment: Weekly Common Core Practice Prompts', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T15:22:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff63acde-03be-50d5-acc2-001d049247e4', 'word_count': 1158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff63acde-03be-50d5-acc2-001d049247e4'}, {'abstract': 'In a pair of picture books, imagination triumphs over boredom and electronic gadgets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/16/books/review/im-bored-and-hello-hello.html', 'snippet': 'In a pair of picture books, imagination triumphs over boredom and electronic gadgets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Our brave new quickly expanding technological world has in it less human contact than ever before and less connection with — hence, less caring for — the natural world. Two new picture books explore this (oh, let’s call it a) situation. Both contain an important message for young readers, but neither is burdened by it, as so many “message-y” books have been.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/books/review/0916-bks-kids-1346788584141/0916-bks-kids-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 901, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/books/review/0916-bks-kids-1346788584141/0916-bks-kids-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1802, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/books/review/0916-bks-kids-1346788584141/0916-bks-kids-1346788584141-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/16/books/review/0916-bks-kids-1346788584141/0916-bks-kids-1346788584141-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/books/review/0916-bks-kids-1346788584141/0916-bks-kids-1346788584141-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Unplugged', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Unplugged', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Black, Michael Ian', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cordell, Matthew', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T15:23:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Small', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Small', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f8d2812-3349-543e-b3f9-44d558a17edb', 'word_count': 993, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f8d2812-3349-543e-b3f9-44d558a17edb'}, {'abstract': 'Two shivery books for middle schoolers are set in Victorian England.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/16/books/review/the-peculiar-and-splendors-and-glooms.html', 'snippet': 'Two shivery books for middle schoolers are set in Victorian England.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What a literary legacy those Victorians left us! Not only are Charles Dickens, H. G. Wells and Charlotte Brontë still widely read, but they and their compatriots continue to inspire writers today: steampunk aficionados with their marvelous mechanisms; those who go for Gothic shivers; and the many others who set their narratives in 19th-century England. Among them are writers for young people who, in addition to creating great stories, engage an audience with little knowledge or interest in Victoriana. Two who rise to the challenge this fall are the debut author Stefan Bachmann, a teenager who is studying music at the Zurich Conservatory, and the Newbery Award winner (for “Good Masters! Sweet Ladies!”) Laura Amy Schlitz. ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Night and Fog', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Night and Fog', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schlitz, Laura Amy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T15:23:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Boo