', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wal-Mart Stores Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T15:27:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Heather Timmons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Heather', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Timmons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/51f65404-613a-57f5-9f1c-4664fad63951', 'word_count': 366, 'uri': 'nyt://article/51f65404-613a-57f5-9f1c-4664fad63951'}, {'abstract': 'How pets can help us through the most difficult times.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/16/books/review/almost-home-by-joan-bauer-and-more.html', 'snippet': 'How pets can help us through the most difficult times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As any reader of middle-grade novels knows, it’s a cruel, viciously uncertain world out there, and all too often the adults in a child’s life are more a source of harm than help. Sometimes a child can trust no one but the loyal dog at his side. Together, they will survive and conquer.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rescue Dogs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rescue Dogs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Herlong, M H', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pyron, Bobbie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bauer, Joan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T15:29:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': '