 team of meteorologists casts serious doubt on a world temperature record of 136.4 degrees recorded on Sept. 13, 1922 in El Azizia, Libya. They cite the antiquated instrument used, the likelihood that the observer was inexperienced and the wide disparity with subsequent temperatures recorded at the site. That means that officially, the “new” record surface temperature is 134 degrees, recorded on July 10, 1913 at Greenland Ranch in Death Valley, Calif. [Arizona State University]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Our Radar: Temperature Record Is Cast Out', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T15:40:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25c2a2ee-5816-51c7-a101-51ee7019666d', 'word_count': 174, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25c2a2ee-5816-51c7-a101-51ee7019666d'}, {'abstract': 'Circle May 16, 2014, on your calendar if you’re a fan.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/14/date-set-for-unleashing-of-godzilla/', 'snippet': 'Circle May 16, 2014, on your calendar if you’re a fan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Godzilla last lumbered into American movie theaters in 1998 and gobbled up a respectable pile of money – $136 million in domestic ticket sales – while swatting away swarms of nasty reviews with his big scaly C.G.I. paws.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Date Set for Unleashing of ‘Godzilla’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Release Date Set for New u2018Godzillau2019', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': '