lls-1500-gallardos-for-fire-hazard/', 'snippet': 'The affected supercars, Coupe and Spyder models, are from the 2004-6 model years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lamborghini is recalling almost 1,500 of its 2004-6 Gallardo Coupe and Spyder models. In a report (PDF) posted recently on the Web site of the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration, Lamborghini outlined a kind of thermochemical conga line of misfortune that could potentially lead to a fire.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lamborghini Recalls 1,500 Gallardos for Fire Hazard', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Automobili Lamborghini SpA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Honda Motor Co Ltd', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Highway Traffic Safety Administration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T15:44:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d13306b0-441a-5fe5-b218-727a56cc6cb4', 'word_count': 199, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d13306b0-441a-5fe5-b218-727a56cc6cb4'}, {'abstract': 'The writer Daniel Alarcón shares some favorite spots from his native city, including a place where writers “wrestle.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/16/travel/in-lima-literary-slams-and-music.html', 'snippet': 'The writer Daniel Alarcón shares some favorite spots from his native city, including a place where writers “wrestle.”', 'lead_paragraph': '“IT’S a city with terrible traffic, alarming crime rates and a sky that’s gray for eight months a year,” said Daniel Alarcón, the 35-year-old author of the novel “Lost Radio City,” of his birthplace, Lima, Peru.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/travel/16QNA_SPAN/16QNA_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/16/travel/16QNA_SPAN/16QNA_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/travel/16QNA_SPAN/16QNA_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/travel/16QNA_SPAN/16QNA_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2040, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/travel/16QNA_SPAN/16QNA_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/16/travel/16QNA_SPAN/16QNA_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/travel/16QNA_SPAN/16QNA_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Lima, Literary Slams and Music', 'kicker': 'Q&A', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Lima, Literary Slams And Music', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lima (Peru)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alarcon, Daniel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T15:44:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily Brennan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brennan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/ffb6cbe3-ef3f-58ce-a1e6-9c80dcdd333a', 'word_count': 620, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ffb6cbe3-ef3f-58ce-a1e6-9c80dcdd333a'}, {'abstract': 'Tamales wrapped in a roll? Taco filling carved from a spit? The New York restaurateur Roberto Santibañez returns to his native city to reveal variations on these well-known foods.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/16/travel/mexico-city-for-tamales-tortas-and-tacos.html', 'snippet': 'Tamales wrapped in a roll? Taco filling carved from a spit? The New York restaurateur Roberto Santibañez returns to his native city to reveal variations on these well-known foods.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROBERTO SANTIBAÑEZ drove with me to a bakery in Mexico City called La Espiga expecting to be disappointed. Before leaving the city many years ago, he loved the tamales that a man sold on the sidewalk in front of the bakery, and he was hoping that maybe, just maybe, he could get those same tamales at that spot now.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012