ehgal discuss several new books about women’s issues; Julie Bosman has notes from the field; Tom Reiss talks about “The Black Count”; and Gregory Cowles has best-seller news. Sam Tanenhaus is the host.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Book Review Podcast', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Podcasts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T16:10:10+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/5dd2f3e7-0e8f-5d4f-9627-ab2ec2e7dc95', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/5dd2f3e7-0e8f-5d4f-9627-ab2ec2e7dc95'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney and Barack Obama in the foreign policy briar patch.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/14/in-search-of-a-middle-eastern-strategy/', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney and Barack Obama in the foreign policy briar patch.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here are four thoughts on the sudden intrusion of foreign policy into our all-about-the-economy political year:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Search of a Middle Eastern Strategy', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T16:11:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0bb5b766-dc4f-5951-90f9-a3e5957ccc73', 'word_count': 876, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0bb5b766-dc4f-5951-90f9-a3e5957ccc73'}, {'abstract': 'The University of Texas at Austin and North Dakota State University in Fargo, N.D., had ordered campus evacuations on Friday morning.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/15/us/university-of-texas-bomb-threat.html', 'snippet': 'The University of Texas at Austin and North Dakota State University in Fargo, N.D., had ordered campus evacuations on Friday morning.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DALLAS — The authorities in Texas and North Dakota said on Friday that they had found no explosives after two large public universities were evacuated over bomb threats — false alarms that forced tens of thousands of students and staff members to flee in the middle of classes at the University of Texas at Austin and at North Dakota State University in Fargo.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Explosives Found After Bomb Threats at Colleges', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Austin (Tex)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fargo (ND)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T16:12:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manny Fernandez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fernandez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6fbab7a5-be97-50e4-a2d9-4dfdd539038b', 'word_count': 568, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6fbab7a5-be97-50e4-a2d9-4dfdd539038b'}, {'abstract': 'Jacques Steinberg discussed the student-led series, “The Envelope, Please,” on the “Today” show.', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/14/the-choice-on-the-today-show-2/', 'snippet': 'Jacques Steinberg discussed the student-led series, “The Envelope, Please,” on the “Today” show.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jacques Steinberg of The Choice, a senior editor at The New York Times, appeared on NBC’s “Today” show on Friday morning to talk about college admissions and our student-led series, “The Envelope, Please.” Watch the full interview below. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Choice on the ‘Today’ Show', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADMISSIONS STANDARDS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Steinberg, Jacques', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T16:13:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2fe51081-e833-5d7c-80c8-7f3e13876b61', 'word_count': 50, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2fe51081-e833-5d7c-80c8-7f3e13876b61'}, {'abstract': 'Taking Questions: The second set of answers from Capt. Frank A. Bolz Jr., a retired New York Police Department hostage negotiator.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/14/answers-about-hostage-negotiation-part-2/', 'snippet': 'Taking Questions: The second set of answers from Capt. Frank A. Bolz Jr., a retired New York Police Department hostage negotiator.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is the second set of responses from Frank A. Bolz Jr., one of the founders of the New York Police Department’s hostage-negotiating unit, answering reader questions. Read the first and third set of responses and the introductory post about Mr. Bolz. We are no longer accepting questions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/14/nyregion/cityroom-takingquestions2/cityroom-takingquestions2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 672, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/14/nyregion/cityroom-takingquestions2/cityroom-takingquestions2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1343, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/14/nyregion/cityroom-takingquestions2/cityroom-takingquestions2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/14/nyregion/cityroom-takingquestions2/cityroom-takingquestions2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/14/nyregion/cityroom-takingquestions2/cityroom-takingquestions2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Answers About Hostage Negotiation, Part 2', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hostages', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T16:15:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organizati