ytimes.com/2012/09/16/books/review/editors-choice.html', 'snippet': 'Recently reviewed books of particular interest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TELEGRAPH AVENUE, by Michael Chabon. (Harper/HarperCollins, $27.99.) Chabon’s rich comic novel about fathers and sons in Berkeley and Oakland, Calif., juggles multiple plots and mounds of pop culture references in astonishing prose.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Editors’ Choice', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Editors’ Choice | Recent Books of Particular Interest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T16:19:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/1fa9fe97-9b45-51a6-b70e-f5121c9be2c1', 'word_count': 269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1fa9fe97-9b45-51a6-b70e-f5121c9be2c1'}, {'abstract': 'Vibrant hues, playful art and zesty food are all part of this online-only collection of photos from our Latin America issue.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/09/16/travel/16LATAM.html', 'snippet': 'Vibrant hues, playful art and zesty food are all part of this online-only collection of photos from our Latin America issue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Vibrant hues, playful art and zesty food are all part of this online-only collection of photos from our Latin America issue.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/travel/16-latinamerss-combo/16-latinamerss-combo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 395, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/travel/16-latinamerss-combo/16-latinamerss-combo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 395, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/travel/16-latinamerss-combo/16-latinamerss-combo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/16/travel/16-latinamerss-combo/16-latinamerss-combo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/travel/16-latinamerss-combo/16-latinamerss-combo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 92, 'width': 92, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Latin America Through a Lens', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Latin America', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T16:24:11+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/23f974ea-595e-5f4e-b8ea-1c7fc366f0c2', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/23f974ea-595e-5f4e-b8ea-1c7fc366f0c2'}, {'abstract': 'Because the annuity payment is based on how much is in the annuity, policyholders who had planned to add to their accounts will now see much smaller payments than they had expected.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/15/your-money/annuities/limits-on-annuity-contributions-annoy-investors.html', 'snippet': 'Because the annuity payment is based on how much is in the annuity, policyholders who had planned to add to their accounts will now see much smaller payments than they had expected.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ANNUITIES are sold with the word “guaranteed” sprinkled through the marketing material. A set payment for life seems mighty attractive when many people are worried about having enough income in retirement and interest rates on savings and Treasury bonds are almost nonexistent. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/15/your-money/15wealth/15wealth-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/15/your-money/15wealth/15wealth-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Guaranteed Return on an Annuity Has Limits After All', 'kicker': 'Wealth Matters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Guaranteed Return On an Annuity Has Limits After All', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANNUITIES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Retirement', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'High Net Worth Individuals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T16:28:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'subsection_name': 'Annuities', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4d37173-a9ff-5598-946e-c543efd5138f', 'word_count': 1368, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4d37173-a9ff-5598-946e-c543efd5138f'}, {'abstract': 'The waves of Northerners who signed up for short Army stints in 1862 had no idea what awaited them.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/14/nine-months-of-hell/', 'snippet': 'The waves of Northerners who signed up for short Army stints in 1862 had no idea what awaited them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was mid-September 1862, and the 900 soldiers of the 130th Pennsylvania Infantry were marching through western Maryland. Pvt. Edward Spangler — all 16 years and 92 pounds of him — struggled to stay with his regiment. The heat was “intense,” Spangler later wrote, “and the suffocating dust more than ankle deep.” Hundreds of raw recruits, ill-prepared and exhausted, were collapsing by the roadside. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nine Months of Hell', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Draft and Recruitment (Military)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lincoln, Abraham', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Army of the Potomac', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T16:30:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Will Hickox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Will', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hickox', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1877126e-180b-5cb1-9653-546cda71431a', 'word_count': 2207, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1877126e-180b-5cb1-9653-546cda71431a'}, {'abstract': 'In time for the anniversary of the occupation of Zuccotti Park on Sept. 17, Occupy Wall Street’s Alternative Banking group is offering for sale a set of anti-capitalist playing cards.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/14/in-a-deck-of-cards-finding-52-shades-of-greed/', 'snippet': 'In time for the anniversary of the occupation of Zuccotti Park on Sept. 17, Occupy Wall Street’s Alternative Banking group is offering for sale a set of anti-capitalist playing cards.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just in time for the one-year anniversary of the occupation of Zuccotti Park on Sept. 17, Occupy Wall Street’s Alternative Banking group is offering for sale an acerbically educational set of anti-capitalist playing cards.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In a Deck of Cards, Finding ‘52 Shades of Greed’', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cards and Card Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T16:41:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Feuer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Feuer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/026adb4e-ff93-5505-8dde-c83b76b1b6d8', 'word_count': 315, 'uri': 'nyt://article/026adb4e-ff93-5505-8dde-c83b76b1b6d8'}, {'abstract': 'Food-related events around New York.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/14/weekend-fare-109/', 'snippet': 'Food-related events around New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The annual Feast of San Gennaro is in full swing this weekend as local restaurants offer special menus during this street festival full of live music, parades and family-friendly activities. Bolstered in recent years by the presence of restaurants like Torrisi Italian Specialties, guests will find better food than what’s offered at typical New York street festivals. The 11-day event ends on Sept. 23.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Weekend Fare', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T16:44:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bao Ong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bao', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bac510d9-dd2f-596b-9959-3c5514c78081', 'word_count': 755, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bac510d9-dd2f-596b-9959-3c5514c78081'}, {'abstract': 'The new National Opera Center in Midtown Manhattan will provide spaces that are many steps up from the basements where opera auditions and rehearsals have often been held.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/15/arts/music/national-opera-center-is-to-open-in-manhattan.html', 'snippet': 'The new National Opera Center in Midtown Manhattan will provide spaces that are many steps up from the basements where opera auditions and rehearsals have often been held.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No more arpeggios in the bathroom. Goodbye, church basements. Hello, soundproofing.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/15/arts/15opera-2/15opera-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/15/arts/15opera-2/15opera-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None,