com/2012/09/14/what-new-polls-say-about-the-campaign/', 'snippet': 'Voters are more likely to blame George W. Bush than Barack Obama for the sluggish state of the economy. And they think the economy will improve.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New presidential election polls out today, including a New York Times/CBS News poll, don’t resolve the uncertainty of this race, which remains too close to call. But they do provide insight into how some of the big issues in the campaign have been playing – the economy, women’s rights, and Medicare.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What New Polls Say About the Campaign', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's Rights", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T16:54:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dde4b1b9-bcc8-59b2-a679-5ead036bcaf0', 'word_count': 403, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dde4b1b9-bcc8-59b2-a679-5ead036bcaf0'}, {'abstract': 'Three designers have shared their spring 2013 mood boards with T. The challenge: To identify the images on each.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/14/new-york-fashion-week-board-game/', 'snippet': 'Three designers have shared their spring 2013 mood boards with T. The challenge: To identify the images on each.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Three designers have shared their spring 2013 mood boards with T. The challenge: To identify the images on each. See all the mood boards here >>', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Fashion Week | Board Game', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T16:56:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25390d5c-142d-5975-b551-925025150f61', 'word_count': 26, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25390d5c-142d-5975-b551-925025150f61'}, {'abstract': 'David Carr and A. O. Scott discuss the dilemma that filmmakers are presented with when adapting movies from books.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/14/the-sweet-spot-september-14-2012/', 'snippet': 'David Carr and A. O. Scott discuss the dilemma that filmmakers are presented with when adapting movies from books.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David Carr and A. O. Scott talk about the dilemma that filmmakers are presented with when adapting movies from books.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Sweet Spot | Sept. 14, 2012', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carr, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scott, A O', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T17:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/068f9590-b741-55d8-bafa-6edc80d58559', 'word_count': 20, 'uri': 'nyt://article/068f9590-b741-55d8-bafa-6edc80d58559'}, {'abstract': 'If the Small Business Administration makes progress, that’s great — but the problems are bigger than the S.B.A.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/14/putting-the-s-b-a-into-perspective/', 'snippet': 'If the Small Business Administration makes progress, that’s great — but the problems are bigger than the S.B.A.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this political season, there will be a lot of dialogue about the Small Business Administration as a possible solution to the small-business lending crisis in America. As two examples, the S.B.A.’s administrator, Karen Mills, spoke recently at the Democratic National Convention and Robb Mandelbaum wrote a post for this blog about the effect a Romney administration might have on the S.B.A. budget.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Putting the S.B.A. Into Perspective', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Deposit Insurance Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Small Business Administration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T17:00:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ami Kassar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ami', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kassar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/998139ed-9f9d-5039-94c8-787d3da9dc3b', 'word_count': 419, 'uri': 'nyt://article/998139ed-9f9d-5039-94c8-787d3da9dc3b'}, {'abstract': 'Did Bernanke really take a stand?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/14/more-fedding/', 'snippet': 'Did Bernanke really take a stand?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Now that I’ve coughed my way through the morning, I thought I would offer a bit of clarification on my Bernanke post from last night.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Fedding', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T17:02:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/58b40938-f9a6-590f-a725-8ee713a73bcd', 'word_count': 214, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58b40938-f9a6-590f-a725-8ee713a73bcd'}, {'abstract': 'The choice of words becomes a spat between a fashion critic and a well-known fashion designer.', 'web_url': 'https://publiceditor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/14/hot-dogs-and-hamburgers-during-fashion-week-how-declasse/', 'snippet': 'The choice of words becomes a spat between a fashion critic and a well-known fashion designer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When The Times’s fashion critic Cathy Horyn called the noted fashion designer Oscar de la Renta a “hot dog,” in her review of his Tuesday runway show at Fashion Week, the octogenarian decided to add to the menu. He took out a full-page ad in Women’s Wear Daily on Friday, in the form of an open letter objecting to what he saw as personal criticism. “If you have the right to call me a hot dog, why do I not have the right to call you stale 3-day old hamburger?” he asked.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hot Dogs and Hamburgers? During Fashion Week? How Déclassé!', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T17:05:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5ba998d-050c-5e1b-baca-728a7dabb4c2', 'word_count': 423, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5ba998d-050c-5e1b-baca-728a7dabb4c2'}, {'abstract': 'Romney turns to the people who failed in Iraq.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/14/the-emerald-city-gang/', 'snippet': 'Romney turns to the people who failed in Iraq.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I have to admit that I haven’t been paying much attention to Mitt Romney’s foreign policy; the domestic side already offers a target-rich environment. But my eyebrows shot up when Dan Senor popped up speaking for Romney in the Libya/Egypt flap. Dan Senor?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Emerald City Gang', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T17:07:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2bcee70a-30de-5800-afc2-50bc25546956', 'word_count': 311, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2bcee70a-30de-5800-afc2-50bc25546956'}, {'abstract': 'Vito J. Lopez, the Democratic assemblyman who stands accused of sexual harassment, saw his favored candidate for a district leader leading an incumbent, partly because of Hasidic politics.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/14/loyalty-to-embattled-assemblyman-is-seen-in-a-brooklyn-election/', 'snippet': 'Vito J. Lopez, the Democratic assemblyman who stands accused of sexual harassment, saw his favored candidate for a district leader leading an incumbent, partly because of Hasidic politics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'He may be down, but he’s not out.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Loyalty to Embattled Assemblyman Is Seen in a Brooklyn Election', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lopez, Vito J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T17:10:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph Berger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Berger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/53b6748b-5108-52b8-a273-c3dc037914e2', 'word_count': 609, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53b6748b-5108-52b8-a273-c3dc037914e2'}, {'abstract': 'Matt Bissonnette, the ex-Navy SEAL who took part in the raid that killed Osama bin Laden, visited a Taco Bell drive-through as soon as he got back from the mission.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/23/books/review/inside-the-list.html', 'snippet': 'Matt Bissonnette, the ex-Navy SEAL who took part in the raid that killed Osama bin Laden, visited a Taco Bell drive-through as soon as he got back from the mission.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HEAD FOR THE BORDER: The new king of the hardcover nonfiction list is, no surprise, Mark Owen — or, as he’s known to his friends (and the rest of America by now), Matt Bissonnette. A former member of the Navy SEALs, Bissonnette is the author of “No Easy Day,” which enters the list at No. 1 and describes, among other things, his role in the raid that killed Osama bin Laden. The book (written with Kevin Maurer) has received admiring reviews — in the daily New York Times, Janet Maslin called it “an exciting, suspenseful account” — but it has also stirred anger among special operations forces, who adhere proudly to a code of silence. Breaking it means Bissonnette is unlikely to be included in future SEAL reunions, one retired Navy officer told The Washington Times: “The guys who run their mouths are typically not invited back.” But Bissonnette hasn’t let the critics keep him down. He sat for a recent “60 Minutes” interview (heavily disguised, inset) and told Scott Pelley the first thing he did upon returning from the mission was visit a Taco Bell drive-through.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/books/review/16list-img/16list-img-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 146, 'width': 143, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/books/review/16list-img/16list-img-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 146, 'width': 143, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/books/review/16list-img/16list-img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/16/books/review/16list-img/16list-img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwi