tname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eda87206-f165-5bd8-91bf-d62c9b35636a', 'word_count': 1067, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eda87206-f165-5bd8-91bf-d62c9b35636a'}, {'abstract': 'What should a parent say to a child after standardized test results are effectively broadcast to the entire class with the presentation of “medals” for achievement?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/14/when-children-get-medals-for-standardized-test-results/', 'snippet': 'What should a parent say to a child after standardized test results are effectively broadcast to the entire class with the presentation of “medals” for achievement?', 'lead_paragraph': 'A parent in California wrote me last week about the state’s STAR testing, and, more important, the practice, in some schools, of awarding medals for achievement on the tests to students. Her child’s school presented “gold” medals for advanced achievement in language arts and/or math, and “silver” to children whose score was “proficient.” (Yes, a medal for “proficiency.”) The medals were given to the children in an assembly. Children who weren’t given a medal were given a certificate.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/14/style/motherlode-medal/motherlode-medal-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 154, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/14/style/motherlode-medal/motherlode-medal-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 154, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/14/style/motherlode-medal/motherlode-medal-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/14/style/motherlode-medal/motherlode-medal-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/14/style/motherlode-medal/motherlode-medal-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 123, 'width': 123, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When Children Get Medals for Standardized Test Results', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests and Examinations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T17:45:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2984fa15-ac46-55b8-bcf8-de6ab4bf7624', 'word_count': 249, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2984fa15-ac46-55b8-bcf8-de6ab4bf7624'}, {'abstract': 'Bucks readers talk about their retirement financial planning in the wake of a decision by Prudential Securities to suspend contributions by some annuity policyholders.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/14/a-reminder-of-the-perils-of-retirement-planning/', 'snippet': 'Bucks readers talk about their retirement financial planning in the wake of a decision by Prudential Securities to suspend contributions by some annuity policyholders.', 'lead_paragraph': 'People without a pension who want to set up something that will pay them set amounts of money when they’re in retirement often turn to annuities. But Paul Sullivan writes this week in his Wealth Matters column about a decision by Prudential Annuities to suspend the ability of some policyholders to make further contributions. And annuity experts told Paul that they expect other insurers to take similar steps because they made promises before the financial crisis that they are now unable to keep.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Reminder of the Perils of Retirement Planning', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANNUITIES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Security (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T17:52:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bucks Editors', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bucks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Editors', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bab191c5-9c08-5261-bf2a-f492dd66ffa5', 'word_count': 230, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bab191c5-9c08-5261-bf2a-f492dd66ffa5'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of antivenin is stored at the Bronx Zoo because it is just a few miles from Jacobi Medical Center, which has one of the nation’s leading snakebite-treatment centers.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/14/near-the-zoos-snakes-a-hospitals-collection-of-medicine/', 'snippet': 'A collection of antivenin is stored at the Bronx Zoo because it is just a few miles from Jacobi Medical Center, which has one of the nation’s leading snakebite-treatment centers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Bronx Zoo has an impressive collection of venomous snakes on display in its Reptile House. But out of sight it also has an impressive collection of antivenin to treat snakebites — though none of the zoo’s snakes have ever bitten an employee or a visitor. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Near the Zoo’s Snakes, a Hospital’s Collection of Medicine', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Zoo Keeps Invaluable Antidotes for Doctors Who Treat Snakebites', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snakes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bronx Zoo Wildlife Conservation Park', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jacobi Medical Center', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T17:52:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Delafuente', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Delafuente', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1fe0cfb-0167-5c94-ac8a-78bd767d9a25', 'word_count': 1004, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1fe0cfb-0167-5c94-ac8a-78bd767d9a25'}, {'abstract': 'An Emmy nominee for directing a variety show discusses the “intense butterflies” he gets before every “Saturday Night Live.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/14/emmys-watch-don-roy-king-on-directing-saturday-night-live/', 'snippet': 'An Emmy nominee for directing a variety show discusses the “intense butterflies” he gets before every “Saturday Night Live.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'We will be talking to Emmy nominees leading up to the awards show on Sept. 23. First up is Don Roy King, nominated for best director for