y to open the country’s retail sector to global behemoths like Wal-Mart and Ikea, pushing for a profound shift in India’s economic and political direction.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/15/business/global/15rupee/15rupee-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/15/business/global/15rupee/15rupee-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/15/business/global/15rupee/15rupee-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 689, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/15/business/global/15rupee/15rupee-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1378, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/15/business/global/15rupee/15rupee-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/15/business/global/15rupee/15rupee-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/15/business/global/15rupee/15rupee-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'India Backs Foreign Investment in Retailing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'India Backs Foreign Investment in Retailing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Investments', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wal-Mart Stores Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T18:12:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gardiner Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gardiner', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/47ebf9d5-a4ad-5229-b012-2025b6bbf259', 'word_count': 938, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47ebf9d5-a4ad-5229-b012-2025b6bbf259'}, {'abstract': 'A production designer’s shop in Downtown Los Angeles is host to a rotating roster of eclectic antiques, home goods and other vintage finds.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/14/a-set-designer-sets-up-shop/', 'snippet': 'A production designer’s shop in Downtown Los Angeles is host to a rotating roster of eclectic antiques, home goods and other vintage finds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last month, the production designer Coryander Friend (“Beginners“) opened Storefront, a vintage shop in Downtown Los Angeles’s arts district. Housed adjacent to the popular eatery Wurstküche and around the corner from Apolis: Common Gallery and Poketo, Storefront showcases Friend’s rotating roster of eclectic antiques, home goods and other vintage finds. On my visit, I spotted everything from a brown Borge Mogensen leather sofa ($6,500) to a green dummy bomb ($650) to a 1960s jet-propelled aluminum surfboard ($1,800). Not to be missed are the store’s collection of Navajo rugs and prison keys. As the store’s head curator, Friend plans to switch up Storefront’s aesthetic on a quarterly basis by featuring new collectors and artists. Currently Storefront is selling pottery by Victoria Morris and surf photography by Will Adler, whose uncle Tom Adler is well known for his own surf-themed work. For her next installation, Friend will feature the work of her friend and mentor, the Window’s Greg Wooten. As for the theme? “The next one has to do with music, geometry and something I haven’t figured out yet,” Friend wrote in an e-mail. “I come from set decoration and production design. We are always telling stories with our environments. I want to work that way in my store. Who knows where it will go?”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Set Designer Sets Up Shop', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T18:19:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Azadeh Ensha', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Azadeh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ensha', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2a2e6fe-947b-5521-b29d-38ff8e8c75ef', 'word_count': 213, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2a2e6fe-947b-5521-b29d-38ff8e8c75ef'}, {'abstract': 'If you want a front-row seat at a fashion show, be prepared to tie your legs into a tight knot.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/16/fashion/front-row-at-new-york-fashion-week-requires-limber-legs.html', 'snippet': 'If you want a front-row seat at a fashion show, be prepared to tie your legs into a tight knot.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN you pack many famously thin and fashionable people into a confined space, strange things happen. Consider the pretzel twist seen on the crossed legs of front-row fashionistas like Anna Wintour; Carine Roitfeld, editor of CR Fashion Book; and the dedicated fashion follower Sarah Jessica Parker, among others. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/fashion/16PRETZEL1/16PRETZEL1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 848, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/fashion/16PRETZEL1/16PRETZEL1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1998, 'width': 1655, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/fashion/16PRETZEL1/16PRETZEL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/16/fashion/16PRETZEL1/16PRETZEL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/fashion/16PRETZEL1/16PRETZEL1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fashion Week’s Version of the Rockettes', 'kicker': 'New York Fashion Week', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fashion Week’s Version of the Rockettes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Fashion Week', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T18:20:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maria Ricapito', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maria', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ricapito', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0bd3175-f45a-5420-a1b2-03a5afb530e4', 'word_count': 802, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0bd3175-f45a-5420-a1b2-03a5afb530e4'}, {'abstract': 'Republicans, that’s who.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/14/who-could-oppose-a-jobs-bill-for-veterans/', 'snippet': 'Republicans, that’s who.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Congressional Republicans, resolute in their commitment to deny the Democrats anything that looks like an accomplishment in an election year, have spent the week obstructing passage of the Veterans Job Corps Act of 2012. It’s a perfectly inoffensive bill from Senator Patty Murray, the Washington Democrat, meant to increase hiring and job training for veterans, especially those who served in Iraq and Afghanistan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Could Oppose a Jobs Bill for Veterans?', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coburn, Tom', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murray, Patty', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Rand', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T18:23:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lawrence Downes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lawrence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Downes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fd7b9f0-bf81-5f93-834b-b95951903567', 'word_count': 450, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fd7b9f0-bf81-5f93-834b-b95951903567'}, {'abstract': 'Ferraris rally through the coastal fog of California, a vintage Bonneville racer visits Ohio and burnouts precede a drive on Sebring International Raceway this weekend.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/14/wheels-calendar-for-sept-14-16/', 'snippet': 'Ferraris rally through the coastal fog of California, a vintage Bonneville racer visits Ohio and burnouts precede a drive on Sebring International Raceway this weekend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A bite-size sampling of concours, cruise nights, auctions and other upwellings of car culture happening across America this weekend.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wheels Calendar for Sept. 14-16', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collectors and Collections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T18:28:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d580a6ed-4d01-58b1-8166-1fdc3dc7bd4a', 'word_count': 246, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d580a6ed-4d01-58b1-8166-1fdc3dc7bd4a'}, {'abstract': 'Officials said 63,000 applicants had already been scheduled for fingerprints and photographs, the second step in the process.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/15/us/us-cites-fast-pace-on-reprieves-for-young-illegal-immigrants.html', 'snippet': 'Officials said 63,000 applicants had already been scheduled for fingerprints and photographs, the second step in the process.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than 82,000 illegal immigrants have applied for a two-year reprieve from deportation in the first 30 working days of an Obama administration program, and 29 have been approved, officials from the Department of Homeland Security said on Friday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Says Fast Pace Conti