 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/f364d3af-8a7d-559d-a394-0bad88a24f99', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/f364d3af-8a7d-559d-a394-0bad88a24f99'}, {'abstract': 'After more than 20 years at 1070 Madison Avenue, at 81st Street, Eliot Rabin sent a letter to his customers this month telling them that the men’s shop, Peter Elliot, is closing at the end of October.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/14/mr-madison-moves-on/', 'snippet': 'After more than 20 years at 1070 Madison Avenue, at 81st Street, Eliot Rabin sent a letter to his customers this month telling them that the men’s shop, Peter Elliot, is closing at the end of October.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ELIOT RABIN, the founder of the Upper East Side temple of navy blazers and sherbet-colored sweaters that is Peter Elliot, is a retailer of a bygone era of gentility. He loves to amuse a customer with a good cliché, like his store motto: “The whimsical mood of timeless elegance.”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mr. Madison Moves On', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mr. Madison Moves On', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Madison Avenue (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T18:39:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3aface4a-71f0-529c-b707-230a149381a9', 'word_count': 483, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3aface4a-71f0-529c-b707-230a149381a9'}, {'abstract': 'The woman said that when she saw a man masturbating in Central Park two weeks ago, she told a park ranger.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/15/nyregion/central-park-rape-suspect-was-sought-in-a-2002-murder.html', 'snippet': 'The woman said that when she saw a man masturbating in Central Park two weeks ago, she told a park ranger.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 73-year-old woman who was raped in Central Park said Friday that when she encountered a man masturbating in the wooded Ramble area two weeks ago, she not only took his photograph, but also reported what she saw to a park ranger.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rape Victim, 73, Says She Reported Earlier Confrontation With Suspect', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rape Victim, 73, Says She Reported Earlier Confrontation With the Suspect', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mitchell, David Albert', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'CENTRAL PARK (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T18:46:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Wendy Ruderman and Nate Schweber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Wendy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ruderman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/249f75bf-3866-57d6-b461-10182cbb5959', 'word_count': 853, 'uri': 'nyt://article/249f75bf-3866-57d6-b461-10182cbb5959'}, {'abstract': 'Line by line, an account of the results if Washington fails to act to head off about $100 billion spending cuts scheduled to begin Jan. 2, 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/15/us/politics/white-house-report-details-effects-of-automatic-budget-cuts.html', 'snippet': 'Line by line, an account of the results if Washington fails to act to head off about $100 billion spending cuts scheduled to begin Jan. 2, 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Army operations and maintenance would lose nearly $7 billion next year, and the Navy more than $4 billion under a looming series of automatic cuts in federal spending. Educational achievement and special-education programs would be shaved by $2.3 billion. Medicare payments to hospitals would fall by $5.6 billion. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'White House Details Potential Effects If Automatic Budget Cuts Go Through', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'White House Details Potential Effects If Automatic Budget Cuts Go Through', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T18:49:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Weisman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weisman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b79068c7-a04c-5173-88bd-14d7b0a1cbf4', 'word_count': 985, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b79068c7-a04c-5173-88bd-14d7b0a1cbf4'}, {'abstract': 'Michelle Obama is a close second in the latest New York Times/CBS News poll.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/14/poll-bill-clinton-is-more-popular-than-ever/', 'snippet': 'Michelle Obama is a close second in the latest New York Times/CBS News poll.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Former President Bill Clinton is more popular now than at any time during the 20 years since his emergence as a presidential candidate, with two-thirds of registered voters viewing him favorably, according to the latest New York Times/CBS News poll. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bill Clinton Is More Popular Than Ever, Poll Finds', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Bill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Michelle', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Ann', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T18:59:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marjorie Connelly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marjorie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Connelly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/50fcbf2a-efba-5371-be58-ac3055c0d63b', 'word_count': 484, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50fcbf2a-efba-5371-be58-ac3055c0d63b'}, {'abstract': 'We examined contrarian bets on European bonds that are looking pretty smart right now. And with Treasury set to reduce its A.I.G. bet