': 'Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-14T19:56:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Castle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55e06efd-6bb5-54ba-958c-937d8d3c01a1', 'word_count': 1426, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55e06efd-6bb5-54ba-958c-937d8d3c01a1'}, {'abstract': 'In an opening statement, prosecutors in London portrayed Kweku Adoboli, a former USB trader facing fraud and false accounting charges, as a free-wheeling trader who doctored documents, invented profits and fabricated clients to cover up trading that led to a $2.3 billion loss at the Swiss bank.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/09/14/as-his-fraud-trial-opens-ex-ubs-trader-is-accused-of-brazen-gambling/', 'snippet': 'In an opening statement, prosecutors in London portrayed Kweku Adoboli, a former USB trader facing fraud and false accounting charges, as a free-wheeling trader who doctored documents, invented profits and fabricated clients to cover up trading th...', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Fictitious trading and brazen gambling by a single individual could have brought down the Swiss financial giant UBS, a British prosecutor said on Friday at the trial of a former bank employee accused of causing a multibillion-dollar trading loss.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ex-UBS Trader Is Accused of Gambling in a Big Loss', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ex-UBS Trader Is Accused Of Gambling in a Big Loss', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'B