ance to attack President Obama, while Mitt Romney and his wife chat it up with TV hosts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/15/us/politics/for-romney-and-ryan-its-hardball-and-softball.html', 'snippet': 'Paul D. Ryan, the Republican vice presidential candidate, uses an appearance to attack President Obama, while Mitt Romney and his wife chat it up with TV hosts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PAINESVILLE, Ohio — One of the advantages of the partnership between Mitt Romney and Paul D. Ryan is their ability to offer varied messages on the campaign trail — unusually varied, as shown on Friday. The running mates punched a list of campaign goals — rallying the conservative base, turning up the heat on President Obama and reaching out to women watching morning television — when each day counting down to Nov. 6 matters.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/15/us/CAMPAIGN/CAMPAIGN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 764, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/15/us/CAMPAIGN/CAMPAIGN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1527, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/15/us/CAMPAIGN/CAMPAIGN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/15/us/CAMPAIGN/CAMPAIGN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/15/us/CAMPAIGN/CAMPAIGN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'While Ryan Throws Hardballs, Romney Makes Friends on Morning TV', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'While Ryan Throws Hardballs, Romney Makes Friends on Morning TV', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-15T01:33:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Parker and Trip Gabriel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Trip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d8f5c83-ee4c-5f42-aea2-1a45c81255dd', 'word_count': 730, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d8f5c83-ee4c-5f42-aea2-1a45c81255dd'}, {'abstract': 'A prop master and a cinematographer reconnected at Do or Dine restaurant in Bedford-Stuyvesant, Brooklyn, to discuss the film industry and far-flung travels.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/16/nyregion/in-bed-stuy-reconnecting-at-a-destination-restaurant.html', 'snippet': 'A prop master and a cinematographer reconnected at Do or Dine restaurant in Bedford-Stuyvesant, Brooklyn, to discuss the film industry and far-flung travels.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The garish yellow awning out front still says, “B’s West Indian,” but the restaurant Do or Dine, which opened in June 2011 in Bedford-Stuyvesant, Brooklyn, has outgrown its original winking misdirection. In July, one of the chef-owners, Justin Warner, won Season 8 of the cable reality show “Food Network Star.” And by now the high-concept, lowish-budget restaurant has become a destination for Manhattanites, as well as a standby for locals, with or without oversize baseball caps. How do you tell the difference? “Manhattan customers are very used to being catered to in their whims,” said Luke Jackson, 33, another owner, whereas locals are more concerned with essential pleasures: the food and the atmosphere. All choose from a menu whose puckish inventiveness (foie gras doughnuts, banana split-pea soup) has drawn sighs of delight and exasperation. Last Tuesday, the disco mirror ball spun and the sound system played ghosts of hip-hop past.\xa0', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/nyregion/16TABLE_SPAN/16TABLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/16/nyregion/16TABLE_SPAN/16TABLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/nyregion/16TABLE_SPAN/16TABLE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/nyregion/16TABLE_SPAN/16TABLE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/nyregion/16TABLE_SPAN/16TABLE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/16/nyregion/16TABLE_SPAN/16TABLE-