oil and gas and a pioneer in the development of oil sands.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Peter Lougheed, the Alberta premier who harnessed his province’s vast oil and gas resources to transform its economy, died Thursday in Calgary, Alberta. He was 84.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/15/nyregion/LOUGHEED-obit/LOUGHEED-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 709, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/15/nyregion/LOUGHEED-obit/LOUGHEED-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1418, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/15/nyregion/LOUGHEED-obit/LOUGHEED-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/15/nyregion/LOUGHEED-obit/LOUGHEED-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/15/nyregion/LOUGHEED-obit/LOUGHEED-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Peter Lougheed, Ex-Premier of Alberta, Dies at 84', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Peter Lougheed, 84, Ex-Premier of Alberta', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lougheed, Peter', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALBERTA (CANADA)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil Sands', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-15T03:19:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/edf46598-08c0-5d96-a0b7-610e83ce2e82', 'word_count': 437, 'uri': 'nyt://article/edf46598-08c0-5d96-a0b7-610e83ce2e82'}, {'abstract': 'To help prevent the dumping of raw sewage into New York’s waterways during a storm, the city has installed inflatable dams in two locations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2012/09/16/nyregion/inflatable-dams.html', 'snippet': 'To help prevent the dumping of raw sewage into New York’s waterways during a storm, the city has installed inflatable dams in two locations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To help prevent the dumping of raw sewage into New York’s waterways during a storm, the city has installed inflatable dams in two locations.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Inflatable Dams', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sewers and Sewage', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Waste Materials and Disposal', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-15T03:22:08+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'New York', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/ebd94148-57ff-5032-96e3-1d6ba81864ad', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/ebd94148-57ff-5032-96e3-1d6ba81864ad'}, {'abstract': 'Adnan Latif, who died in his cell at the Guantánamo Bay prison camp on Sept. 8, was the ninth detainee to die. He was cleared three times for release, but there was no way to get out.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/14/opinion/life-and-death-at-guantanamo-bay.html', 'snippet': 'Adnan Latif, who died in his cell at the Guantánamo Bay prison camp on Sept. 8, was the ninth detainee to die. He was cleared three times for release, but there was no way to get out.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEFORE he died on Sept. 8, Adnan Farhan Abdul Latif had spent close to 4,000 days and nights in the American prison at Guantánamo Bay, Cuba. He was found unconscious, alone in his cell, thousands of miles from home and family in Yemen.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Face of Indefinite Detention', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Face of Indefinite Detention', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Latif, Adnan Farhan Abdul', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guantanamo Bay Naval Base (Cuba)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Habeas Corpus', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-15T03:25:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Baher Azmy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Baher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Azmy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/624119bb-84db-5536-a72b-9918c1b311bb', 'word_count': 945, 'uri': 'nyt://article/624119bb-84db-5536-a72b-9918c1b311bb'}, {'abstract': 'Xi Jinping, who is expected to take over the Communist Party, was last seen in public on Sept. 1, raising questions about his health.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/15/world/asia/a-leader-in-china-reappears-in-public.html', 'snippet': 'Xi Jinping, who is expected to take over the Communist Party, was last seen in public on Sept. 1, raising questions about his health.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — China’s next designated leader, Xi Jinping, reappeared in public on Saturday, two weeks after mysteriously disappearing from view. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/15/world/XI/XI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 708, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/15/world/XI/XI-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1086, 'width': 751, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/15/world/XI/XI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/15/world/XI/XI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/15/world/XI/XI-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Leader in China Reappears in Public', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Leader In China Reappears In Public', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xi Jinping', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-15T03:38:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca555347-79ea-5604-abfc-1e24a3fc5b32', 'word_count': 429, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca555347-79ea-5604-abfc-1e24a3fc5b32'}, {'abstract': 'The bodies of nine men, one of them hanging from a bridge and all shot in the head, were found Friday in Nuevo Laredo, across from Laredo, Tex., the authorities said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/15/world/americas/mexico-bodies-found-on-bridge.html', 'snippet': 'The bodies of nine men, one of them hanging from a bridge and all shot in the head, were found Friday in Nuevo Laredo, across from Laredo, Tex., the authorities said.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The bodies of nine men, one of them hanging from a bridge and all shot in the head, were found Friday in Nuevo Laredo, across from Laredo, Tex., the authorities said. Ruben Darío, a spokesman for the Tamaulipas State prosecutor’s office, said the bodies were all found near the bridge, with a message left near them, though he would not disclose what it said. In May, five men and four women were found hanging from another bridge in the city. This latest crime occurred a day after the top leader of the Gulf Cartel, one of Mexico’s largest, was captured by the Mexican Navy in Tamaulipas, leading security analysts to warn of possible violence resulting from the power vacuum. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], '