 consecutive day on Friday according to the FiveThirtyEight forecast. His chances of winning the Electoral College are now listed at 76.2 percent, down from 78.6 percent in Thursday’s forecast.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sept. 14: Obama Forecast Declines on Poor Manufacturing Report', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-15T10:59:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed553ada-c39d-52c9-be06-db4c833b6a1e', 'word_count': 607, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed553ada-c39d-52c9-be06-db4c833b6a1e'}, {'abstract': 'In the face of the latest upsurge of anti-American feeling in the Middle East, the U.S. is short of reliable local allies. As Washington continues to wrestle with the consequences of the Arab Spring, Morocco has emerged as an island of stability in a sea of troubles.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/15/morocco-emerges-as-key-u-s-ally-in-troubled-region/', 'snippet': 'In the face of the latest upsurge of anti-American feeling in the Middle East, the U.S. is short of reliable local allies. As Washington continues to wrestle with the consequences of the Arab Spring, Morocco has emerged as an island of stability i...', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Anti-American protests that have spread across the Arab world are overshadowing Washington’s latest steps to cement its ties with one of its closest allies in the region, Morocco.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morocco Emerges as Key U.S. Ally in Troubled Region', 'kicker': 'IH