Afghan lawmakers approved all three of President Hamid Karzai’s nominees for the government’s top security jobs on Saturday, avoiding a prolonged power vacuum.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — Afghan lawmakers approved all three of the president’s nominees for the government’s top security jobs on Saturday, avoiding a prolonged power vacuum as the country confronted multiple reminders of the fragility of its security. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Afghans Act to Fill Top Security Posts', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Afghans Act to Fill Top Security Posts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karzai, Hamid', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-15T19:10:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alissa J. Rubin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alissa', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Rubin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/056ba1e9-5190-5dbb-a1e5-d5d49e920832', 'word_count': 871, 'uri': 'nyt://article/056ba1e9-5190-5dbb-a1e5-d5d49e920832'}, {'abstract': 'Economic gains in many sectors have yet to solve the problem of feeding the world. In Africa alone, government policies and fertilizer costs are inhibiting agricultural progress.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/16/business/world-hunger-the-problem-left-behind-economic-view.html', 'snippet': 'Economic gains in many sectors have yet to solve the problem of feeding the world. In Africa alone, government policies and fertilizer costs are inhibiting agricultural progress.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE drought-induced run-up in corn prices is a reminder that we’re nowhere near solving the problem of feeding the world. The price surge, the third major international food price spike in the last five years, casts more doubt on the assumption that widespread economic development leads to corresponding gains in agriculture.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/business/16-VIEW/16-VIEW-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 831, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/business/16-VIEW/16-VIEW-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1663, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/business/16-VIEW/16-VIEW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/16/business/16-VIEW/16-VIEW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/business/16-VIEW/16-VIEW-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'World Hunger: The Problem Left Behind', 'kicker': 'Economic View', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'World Hunger: The Problem Left Behind', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 