ing catastrophe. The economic downturn and its consequences — including losses in jobs, income, investments and home equity — have made that bad situation much worse. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Road to Retirement', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Road to Retirement', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Retirement', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Security (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harkin, Tom', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': '401(k), 403(b) and 457 Plans', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-15T19:21:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/064bdc6c-a2fb-5451-85d1-f0ea8085c78f', 'word_count': 737, 'uri': 'nyt://article/064bdc6c-a2fb-5451-85d1-f0ea8085c78f'}, {'abstract': 'The economy could benefit from two very different events last week: the announcement of the Federal Reserve’s latest bond-buying plan and Apple’s introduction of the iPhone 5.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/16/your-money/from-the-fed-and-apple-a-possible-economic-lift.html', 'snippet': 'The economy could benefit from two very different events last week: the announcement of the Federal Reserve’s latest bond-buying plan and Apple’s introduction of the iPhone 5.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HELP for the beleaguered economy came last week from two powerhouses: the Federal Reserve and ... Apple.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/20/multimedia/author-jeff-sommer/author-jeff-sommer-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/20/multimedia/author-jeff-sommer/author-jeff-sommer-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/20/multimedia/author-jeff-sommer/author-jeff-sommer-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/20/multimedia/author-jeff-sommer/author-jeff-sommer-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/20/multimedia/author-jeff-sommer/author-jeff-sommer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/02/20/multimedia/author-jeff-sommer/author-jeff-sommer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/20/multimedia/author-jeff-sommer/author-jeff-sommer-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Kick-Starts From a Phone and the Fed', 'kicker': 'Strategies', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Kick-Starts From a Phone and the Fed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bernanke, Ben S', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jobs, Steven P', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quantitative Easing', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-15T19:24:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Sommer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sommer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf895a3d-af4d-5c84-b4dd-1ba30e49810b', 'word_count': 1149, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf895a3d-af4d-5c84-b4dd-1ba30e49810b'}, {'abstract': 'My life was full of trauma and abuse, but pulling the hair from my body made me feel calm and safe.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/15/surviving-the-pain-at-the-roots/', 'snippet': 'My life was full of trauma and abuse, but pulling the hair from my body made me feel calm and safe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I came out of the womb scratching. Mitts had to be put on my hands so I would stop clawing my skin. When I was seven and got mad I would bite myself, raising welts on my arms. This was already well into the time when I would have to touch certain spots on the cabinets, on the sidewalk, with my fingers and toes. At 12, after a seriously traumatic event, I began to pull out my hair. Every day since then, for the past 18 years, the hairs on my body have gone one by one, in the thousands, as I have tried to cope with overwhelming anxiety from a chaotic series of experiences that from birth have made me feel inside as if my very life is at stake if I do not pick and pull and bite and scratch.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Surviving the Pain at the Roots', 'kicker': 'Anxiety', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Anxiety: Surviving the Pain at the Roots', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Anxiety and Stress', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hair', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Obsessive-Compulsive Disorder', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-15T19:30:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexandra Heather Foss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexandra', 'middlename': 'Heather', 'lastname': 'Foss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/19b25780-1b14-54e1-b945-be6710713892', 'word_count': 1514, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19b25780-1b14-54e1-b945-be6710713892'}, {'abstract': 'Jiyai Shin of South Korea held a five-stroke lead after 36 holes of the Women’s British Open in Hoylake, England.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/16/sports/golf/shin-shoots-brilliant-64-at-womens-british-open.html', 'snippet': 'Jiyai Shin of South Korea held a five-stroke lead after 36 holes of the Women’s British Open in Hoylake, England.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HOYLAKE, England — Fairways as narrow as tongue depressors did not much bother Jiyai Shin, who hit all but one Saturday during the delayed second round of the Women’s British Open. Royal Liverpool Golf Club’s humpback greens were no worry, either; Shin did not miss any en route to a masterly eight-under-par 64, which left her at minus nine at the tournament’s halfway point. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/sports/LINKS/LINKS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 676, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/sports/LINKS/LINKS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1351, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/sports/LINKS/LINKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/16/sports/LINKS/LINKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/sports/LINKS/LINKS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Britain, One Player Blows Away the Field', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Britain, One Player Blows Away The Field', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's British Open (Golf)", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shin, Jiyai', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ko, Lydia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Creamer, Paula', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-15T19:31:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff043f5b-d513-5176-a103-4daa4f4f8cd0', 'word_count': 798, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff043f5b-d513-5176-a103-4daa4f4f8cd0'}, {'abstract': 'Readers comment on my column about Romney’s lapses on foreign policy.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/15/mitt-romney-and-foreign-policy/', 'snippet': 'Readers comment on my column about Romney’s lapses on foreign policy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My Sunday column argues that Mitt Romney’s foreign policy lapses last week are indicative of a larger problem: This is a world he doesn’t get, or gets wrong. Romney has clearly thought a good deal about domestic issues in the six years he’s been studying to be president, but there’s not much indication of interest or expertise in foreign affairs. And that’s putting it mildly.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mitt Romney and Foreign Policy', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-15T19:33:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/49a30d22-849b-51b0-8b8b-ff87202cc0bb', 'word_count': 148, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49a30d22-849b-51b0-8b8b-ff87202cc0bb'}, {'abstract': 'What happened to the tacit social prohibition against talking about money?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/16/opinion/sunday/money-money-money-can-we-talk-about-something-else.html', 'snippet': 'What happened to the tacit social prohibition against talking about money?', 'lead_paragraph': 'THESPIAN friends perform “The Seagull” in their garden. Only minutes into the first act, a lovely young woman named Masha, sick of hearing the lovesick schoolteacher Medvedenko whine about his penury, blurts out, “All you ever do is talk and talk about money.” That’s when it dawns on me: I’m sick of the subject, too. For the rest of Act I, I find myself ruminating about the glut of financial data that daily clogs the news: Libor and MF Global Holdings; HSBC’s money-laundering of Mexican drug-cartel money; “the London Whale” whose huge trades cost J.P. Morgan Chase billions; leveraged buyouts and mortgage-backed securities and derivatives and stimulus packages, Bain Capital and the tottering euro and the Greek bailout. Saul Bellow referred to this quotidian fretting about world affairs as “crisis chatter.” Today’s crises are all about what is euphemistically called “the financial services industry” — that is to say, they’re all about money.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/sunday-review/16COVER/16COVER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 465, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/16/sunday-review/16COVER/16COVER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 465}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/sunday-review/16COVER/16COVER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/sunday-review/16COVER/16COVER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1537, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy':