nfronts head on one of the most potentially damaging questions lingering over his re-election hopes: Are you better off than you were four years ago?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Ad Tries to Answer: Are You Better Off Than Four Years Ago?', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nevada', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-15T21:37:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy W. Peters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/73d57a86-127b-5472-bad3-0fd4220a29dd', 'word_count': 335, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73d57a86-127b-5472-bad3-0fd4220a29dd'}, {'abstract': 'On the anniversary of Occupy Wall Street’s encampment at Zuccotti Park, excerpts of letters to bank executives.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/16/opinion/sunday/letters-to-wall-street.html', 'snippet': 'On the anniversary of Occupy Wall Street’s encampment at Zuccotti Park, excerpts of letters to bank executives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOMORROW is the first anniversary of the Occupy Wall Street movement’s encampment at Zuccotti Park. Some of the protesters there created a Web site for Americans who couldn’t join them in Lower Manhattan. Called Occupy the Boardroom, the site invited people across the country to write detailed letters to the executives and directors of banks. The site’s developers promised to deliver them as e-mail and in person. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dear Bankers: Thanks for Wrecking Our Lives ...', 'kicker': 'Dispatch', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dear Bankers: Thanks for Wrecking Our Lives...', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Trouble Is the Banks: Letters to Wall Street (Book)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-15T21:44:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Greif', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greif', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/df7a891c-e436-5c1c-981c-8321ecbe6286', 'word_count': 153, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df7a891c-e436-5c1c-981c-8321ecbe6286'}, {'abstract': 'The locked-out N.F.L. referee Ed Hochuli on football rules, science fiction and “Sons of Anarchy.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/16/opinion/sunday/catching-up-with-ed-hochuli-a-locked-out-nfl-referee.html', 'snippet': 'The locked-out N.F.L. referee Ed Hochuli on football rules, science fiction and “Sons of Anarchy.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ed Hochuli is a trial lawyer and one of the 121 referees the N.F.L. has locked out of work because of disputes over pay and pensions. Known for his bodybuilder biceps, he was the model for the official in the Madden N.F.L. video games. After some  replacement referees’ blunders in season-opener games, fans are calling for his and his colleagues’ swift return.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/sunday-review/16DOWNLOAD/16DOWNLOAD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 646, 'width': 308, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/sunday-review/16DOWNLOAD/16DOWNLOAD-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 646, 'width': 308, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/sunday-review/16DOWNLOAD/16DOWNLOAD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/16/sunday-review/16DOWNLOAD/16DOWNLOAD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/sunday-review/16DOWNLOAD/16DOWNLOAD-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 97, 'width': 97, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ed Hochuli', 'kicker': 'Download', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ed Hochuli', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Officiating (Sports)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hochuli, Ed', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lockouts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-15T21:54:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/49de278a-9311-5bdf-bd86-eb7280ca9216', 'word_count': 309, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49de278a-9311-5bdf-bd86-eb7280ca9216'}, {'abstract': 'As the first anniversary of the repeal of “don’t ask, don’t tell” approaches, it is clear that there have been no disastrous consequences.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/16/opinion/sunday/a-military-success-story.html', 'snippet': 'As the first anniversary of the repeal of “don’t ask, don’t tell” approaches, it is clear that there have been no disastrous consequences.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the country approaches the first anniversary of the repeal of “don’t ask, don’t tell” on Sept. 20, politicians and others who warned of disastrous consequences if gay people were allowed to serve openly in the military are looking pretty foolish.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Military Success Story', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Military Success Story', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of California, Los Angeles', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, '