oldman was a real estate visionary who saw himself as a long-term investor in the revitalization of historic neighborhoods.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/16/nyregion/tony-goldman-real-estate-visionary-dies-at-68.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Goldman was a real estate visionary who saw himself as a long-term investor in the revitalization of historic neighborhoods.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tony Goldman, whose investor’s eye for spotting battered neighborhoods prime for rejuvenation led him to help revive SoHo in Manhattan in the 1970s and South Beach in Florida in the ’80s, died on Tuesday in Manhattan. He was 68.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/nyregion/dog-GOLDMAN-obit/dog-GOLDMAN-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 316, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/16/nyregion/dog-GOLDMAN-obit/dog-GOLDMAN-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 316}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/nyregion/dog-GOLDMAN-obit/dog-GOLDMAN-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 539, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/nyregion/dog-GOLDMAN-obit/dog-GOLDMAN-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1078, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/nyregion/dog-GOLDMAN-obit/dog-GOLDMAN-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/16/nyregion/dog-GOLDMAN-obit/dog-GOLDMAN-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/nyregion/dog-GOLDMAN-obit/dog-GOLDMAN-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tony Goldman, SoHo Pioneer, Dies at 68', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tony Goldman, SoHo Pioneer, Dies at 68', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'SoHo (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Beach (Miami Beach, Fla)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goldman, Tony', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-16T01:07:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Leslie Kaufman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Leslie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaufman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/85107ecc-e241-59eb-9491-41e8564c4f28', 'word_count': 911, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85107ecc-e241-59eb-9491-41e8564c4f28'}, {'abstract': 'When Armenia’s team returned home from the Chess Olympiad, its members were greeted by the president and treated to a parade in the capital.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/16/crosswords/chess/chess-armenia-wins-gold-at-olympiad.html', 'snippet': 'When Armenia’s team returned home from the Chess Olympiad, its members were greeted by the president and treated to a parade in the capital.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Eastern Europeans have dominated chess for decades, and one reason may be that they come from countries where the average citizen is simply more passionate about the game. \xa0', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'World’s No. 2 Player Leads Armenia to a Gold Medal', 'kicker': 'Chess', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'World’s No. 2 Player Leads Armenia to a Gold Medal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Aronian, Levon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARMENIA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chess', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-16T01:22:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'subsection_name': 'Chess', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dylan Loeb McClain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dylan', 'middlename': 'Loeb', 'lastname': 'McClain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9454e62-b57b-526e-b201-f52444b5be28', 'word_count': 443, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9454e62-b57b-526e-b201-f52444b5be28'}, {'abstract': 'The many sacrifices of Algernon Squier, a towering Civil War hospital steward.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/15/a-gentle-giant-stays-behind/', 'snippet': 'The many sacrifices of Algernon Squier, a towering Civil War hospital steward.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Sept. 15, 1862, Gen. Thomas J. “Stonewall” Jackson and his Confederates trapped the 12,700-man federal garrison in Harpers Ferry, Va. “We were as helpless as rats in a cage,” moaned one Union soldier. The federal commander, Col. Dixon S. Miles, had little choice but to surrender. Moments after the decision, the explosion of a stray artillery shell resulted in his mortal wounding. A subordinate made the final arrangements.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Gentle Giant Stays Behind', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisoners of War', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jackson, Stonewall', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-16T01:30:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ronald S. Coddington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ronald', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Coddington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eff7e9fb-70bb-58ed-9134-f2982c5418b5', 'word_count': 1249, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eff7e9fb-70bb-58ed-9134-f2982c5418b5'}, {'abstract': 'The winning lottery numbers for New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/16/nyregion/lottery-numbers-for-new-york-new-jersey-and-connecticut.html', 'snippet': 'The winning lottery numbers for New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sept. 15, 2012', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lottery Numbers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lottery Numbers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lotteries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-16T01:34:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news