. The two will work together to strengthen the offense of the Knicks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/16/sports/basketball/how-hakeem-olajuwon-became-invested-in-the-knicks.html', 'snippet': 'Hakeem Olajuwon and the Knicks Coach Mike Woodson formed a bond when they played together for the Rockets. The two will work together to strengthen the offense of the Knicks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mike Woodson made a request early. Even before he knew he would be coaching the Knicks again, Woodson looked into the future. He needed help. He called Hakeem Olajuwon, his longtime friend and a Hall of Famer known for teaching fundamentals. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Olajuwon Became Invested in the Knicks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How Olajuwon Became Invested in Knicks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Olajuwon, Hakeem', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woodson, Mike', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "Stoudemire, Amar'e", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANTHONY, CARMELO', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-16T02:43:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce1c7751-4d64-51ef-b7be-136ba0d97c12', 'word_count': 694, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce1c7751-4d64-51ef-b7be-136ba0d97c12'}, {'abstract': 'A look back at the week in politics, including reactions to an attack on the United States Consulate in Libya.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/09/15/us/politics/0915wip.html', 'snippet': 'A look back at the week in politics, including reactions to an attack on the United States Consulate in Libya.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A look back at the week in politics, including reactions to an attack on the United States Consulate in Libya.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/15/us/politics/0915wip-slide-C3JP/0915wip-slide-C3JP-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 329, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/15/us/politics/0915wip-slide-C3JP/0915wip-slide-C3JP-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 658, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/15/us/politics/0915wip-slide-C3JP/0915wip-slide-C3JP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/15/us/politics/0915wip-slide-C3JP/0915wip-slide-C3JP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/15/us/politics/0915wip-slide-C3JP/0915wip-slide-C3JP-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Week in Political Pictures: Sept. 9-15', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-16T03:24:17+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/e80e15b5-934b-5edc-8e81-8c5122123803', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/e80e15b5-934b-5edc-8e81-8c5122123803'}, {'abstract': 'The Swedish Elitserien has been the only top European league to say that it will not sign N.H.L. players to short-term contracts. But Sweden’s general counsel for competition plans to challenge the ban.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/15/in-event-of-lockout-a-swedish-league-faces-challenge-in-attempt-to-bar-n-h-l-players/', 'snippet': 'The Swedish Elitserien has been the only top European league to say that it will not sign N.H.L. players to short-term contracts. But Sweden’s general counsel for competition plans to challenge the ban.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Swedish Elitserien has been the only top European league to say that it will not sign N.H.L. players to short-term contracts if the N.H.L. locks them out, as is expected to happen when the current labor deal expires at midnight Saturday. But many believe the Elitserien would have to join other leagues in welcoming N.H.L. players under contracts of any length, since the Elitserien’s contract with its players union does not include bans on short-term deals.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Event of Lockout, Swedish League Faces Challenge in Attempt to Bar N.H.L. Players', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lockouts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Elitserien (Swedish Elite League)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-16T03:27:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa6fda64-c2b1-534c-b756-cbe3fd1e3540', 'word_count': 204, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa6fda64-c2b1-534c-b756-cbe3fd1e3540'}, {'abstract': 'The Mets wanted to see how well Jenrry Mejia would pitch now that he was back in the majors. The answer on Saturday was pretty badly.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/16/sports/baseball/mejia-falls-flat-in-mets-loss-to-brewers.html', 'snippet': 'The Mets wanted to see how well Jenrry Mejia would pitch now that he was back in the majors. The answer on Saturday was pretty badly.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MILWAUKEE — The suicide squeeze bunt that Mets pitcher Jenrry Mejia dropped down in the fourth inning Saturday night not only gave him a lead against the Milwaukee Brewers, but also gave him an odd distinction. Thirty-five games into his major league career, Mejia picked up his first major league run batted in before his first major league win.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mejia Bunts Well and Pitches Poorly in Mets’ Loss', 'kicker': 'Brewers 9, Mets 6', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Young Mets Starter Bunts Well but Pitches Poorly', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Milwaukee Brewers',