otball/notre-dame-snaps-michigan-states-home-game-win-streak.html', 'snippet': 'In his third career start, Everett Golson withstood Michigan State’s defense, completed 14 of his 32 passes for 178 yards and scored two touchdowns for Notre Dame.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST LANSING, Mich. — Two years ago here, a smirking Mark Dantonio shook Brian Kelly’s hand. In Kelly’s third game as Notre Dame’s coach, Dantonio had called a fake field goal in overtime to win, beginning a two-year run that redefined Michigan State as calm, cool and clutch. After that, the Spartans won 10 of their next 11 games decided by 10 points or fewer, while Kelly’s Fighting Irish went 8-5 in each of his first two seasons as Notre Dame faltered in its seemingly endless quest to regain a place atop the college football mountain.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/sports/spartans/spartans-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/sports/spartans/spartans-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1312, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/sports/spartans/spartans-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/16/sports/spartans/spartans-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/sports/spartans/spartans-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Notre Dame Makes a Statement by Stuffing Michigan State', 'kicker': 'Notre Dame 20, Michigan State 3', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Notre Dame Makes a Statement by Stuffing Michigan State', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dantonio, Mark', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Notre Dame', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Michigan State University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelly, Brian', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-16T04:52:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Rohan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/96d32575-8eb9-5880-bc64-e0befd6f582c', 'word_count': 844, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96d32575-8eb9-5880-bc64-e0befd6f582c'}, {'abstract': 'The good, the bad and the strange from the world of college football.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/16/college-football-around-the-country/', 'snippet': 'The good, the bad and the strange from the world of college football.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHRIS THOMPSON The Florida State running back scored on runs of 74 and 80 yards on successive carries to lead the No. 5 Seminoles to a 52-0 victory over Wake Forest.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'College Football Around the Country', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Around The Country: The Day’s Best', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [