nippet': 'London', 'lead_paragraph': 'London', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/fashion/runway-womens/mariosschwab_spring13app-slide-1R95/mariosschwab_spring13app-slide-1R95-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/16/fashion/runway-womens/mariosschwab_spring13app-slide-1R95/mariosschwab_spring13app-slide-1R95-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/fashion/runway-womens/mariosschwab_spring13app-slide-1R95/mariosschwab_spring13app-slide-1R95-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/16/fashion/runway-womens/mariosschwab_spring13app-slide-1R95/mariosschwab_spring13app-slide-1R95-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1365, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Marios Schwab: Spring 2013 RTW', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-16T14:37:57+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Fashion & Style', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': "Women's Runway", 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/6f0b2f18-63f5-5069-8ddc-3b1ddbac7d4d', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/6f0b2f18-63f5-5069-8ddc-3b1ddbac7d4d'}, {'abstract': 'The two will join Mariah Carey and Randy Jackson for a level of musical firepower that reflects both the show’s continuing importance to the music business and the need to freshen its appeal with viewers.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/16/american-idol-confirms-addition-of-nicki-minaj-and-keith-urban/', 'snippet': 'The two will join Mariah Carey and Randy Jackson for a level of musical firepower that reflects both the show’s continuing importance to the music business and the need to freshen its appeal with viewers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Fox network on Sunday morning made official the long-reported final additions to the judging lineup for “American Idol,” television’s dominant show of the past decade, and the new names were, as expected, the rap star Nicki Minaj and Keith Urban, one of the most popular singers in country music.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘American Idol’ Confirms Addition of Nicki Minaj and Keith Urban', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nicki Minaj and Keith Urban Join ‘American Idol’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carey, Mariah', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Minaj, Nicki', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Urban, Keith', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-16T14:39:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7275dda0-d5bd-531e-9721-72c6b2d75653', 'word_count': 271, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7275dda0-d5bd-531e-9721-72c6b2d75653'}, {'abstract': 'What lies beneath New York’s waterways has not been documented with precision, but it provides grist for a new exhibition and talks at the South Street Seaport Museum.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/16/underwater-a-train-a-dinette-and-dont-forget-the-chevy/', 'snippet': 'What lies beneath New York’s waterways has not been documented with precision, but it provides grist for a new exhibition and talks at the South Street Seaport Museum.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nicki Pombier Berger, who is listed as one of the speakers at an event called Underwater New York, is unequivocal: She is “terrified” of diving. She has never wanted an up-close-and-personal look at what she will be talking about at the South Street Seaport Museum, namely, the stuff that has piled up over time at the bottom of the Hudson River or the East River or New York Harbor — the jetsam of New York. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Underwater, a Train, a Dinette and Don’t Forget the Chevy', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Underwater Riches Include a Piano, a Train, and Don’t Forget the Chevy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN FOLK ART MUSEUM', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'South Street Seaport Museum', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chesapeake Bay', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East River (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hudson River', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-16T15:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Barron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5bd87749-b6e4-51b8-a125-7d922977235b', 'word_count': 588, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5bd87749-b6e4-51b8-a125-7d922977235b'}, {'abstract': 'The events in the Middle East have forced both campaigns to improvise and abandon the economic playbook they had imagined using.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/17/us/politics/for-romney-and-obama-a-need-to-control-the-message.html', 'snippet': 'The events in the Middle East have forced both campaigns to improvise and abandon the economic playbook they had imagined using.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is almost nothing more valuable to a presidential campaign than controlling the message.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/17/us/CAUCUS-1/CAUCUS-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 983, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/17/us/CAUCUS-1/CAUCUS-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1772, 'width': 1701, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/17/us/CAUCUS-1/CAUCUS-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Both Campaigns, a Need to Control the Message', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Unpredictability Ahead, Seeking to Deliver a Disciplined Message', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-16T15:06:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/56345a35-d98a-5a75-82a5-1e6d532fdfcf', 'word_count': 686, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56345a35-d98a-5a75-82a5-1e6d532fdfcf'}, {'abstract': 'Silicon Valley would like the world to think it doesn’t care about money. But these start-ups aren’t nonprofit organizations.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/16/disruptions-let-silicon-valley-eat-ramen-noodles/', 'snippet': 'Silicon Valley would like the world to think it doesn’t care about money. But these start-ups aren’t nonprofit organizations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You don’t have to spend much time in Silicon Valley to start hearing that the people don’t care about money. People here are just trying to make the world a better place. Entrepreneurs and venture capitalists eat ramen noodles for dinner and drive old, clunky Hondas to work. If they do make money, that’s just a tiny cherry on top of their altruistic Tofutti soy whip sundae.That’s what people here would like the world to think. Let’s be realistic, these start-ups aren’t nonprofit organizations.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit':