 'nyt://article/90e95d1d-6b7a-52bc-ac60-359973e1db36'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama is almost certain to win the state’s 7 electoral votes, but by a significantly smaller margin than he did in 2008.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/16/in-connecticut-wall-street-community-may-limit-obama-victory/', 'snippet': 'President Obama is almost certain to win the state’s 7 electoral votes, but by a significantly smaller margin than he did in 2008.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We continue our Presidential Geography series, a one-by-one examination of the peculiarities that drive the politics in all 50 states and the District of Columbia. Here is a look at Connecticut, the Constitution State. FiveThirtyEight spoke with Paul Bass, the editor of The New Haven Independent; Gary Rose, an associate professor of political science at Sacred Heart University; Ronald Schurin, an associate professor of political science at the University of Connecticut; and Kevin F. Rennie, a columnist for The Hartford Courant and a former Republican state senator and representative.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Connecticut, Wall Street Community May Limit Obama Victory', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Senate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McMahon, Linda E', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murphy, Christopher Scott', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value':