 Eli Manning finished with 510 passing yards to offset a miserable first half in which he threw three interceptions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST RUTHERFORD, N.J. — Giants Coach Tom Coughlin’s sideline histrionics are legendary moments of football cinema. The death stares, the icy glares and the occasional (but impressive) hurling of perfectly creased play charts all dovetail nicely with Coughlin’s perpetually ruddy complexion, making for an entertaining spectacle as he upbraids his charges.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/17/sports/football/17giants-pic/17giants-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/17/sports/football/17giants-pic/17giants-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/17/sports/football/17giants-pic/17giants-pic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 641, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/17/sports/football/17giants-pic/17giants-pic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1283, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/17/sports/football/17giants-pic/17giants-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/17/sports/football/17giants-pic/17giants-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/17/sports/football/17giants-pic/17giants-pic-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'With Frantic Fourth, Manning and Giants Slip Past Bucs', 'kicker': 'Giants 41, Buccaneers 34', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Giants Turn Frustration Into 25-Point Final Quarter', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manning, Eli', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nicks, Hakeem', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coughlin, Tom', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tampa Bay Buccaneers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bradshaw, Ahmad', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cruz, Victor', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-16T21:20:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Borden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ed21b3c-5c36-5cbc-aede-9d888d909ca0', 'word_count': 956, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ed21b3c-5c36-5cbc-aede-9d888d909ca0'}, {'abstract': 'The outbreak of violence in Karachi came after days of peaceful demonstrations against the release of a video, made in America, that mocked the Prophet Muhammad.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/17/world/asia/crowds-storm-us-consulate-in-pakistan-and-one-dies.html', 'snippet': 'The outbreak of violence in Karachi came after days of peaceful demonstrations against the release of a video, made in America, that mocked the Prophet Muhammad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISLAMABAD, Pakistan — One person was killed and dozens of people were injured when anti-American protesters tried to storm the American Consulate in the southern port city of Karachi and clashed for several hours with the police and paramilitary troops on Sunday evening, rescue workers and police officials said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pakistanis Try to Storm U.S. Outpost; One Is Killed', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pakistanis Try to Storm U.S. Outpost; One Is Killed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-16T21:29:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Salman Masood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Salman', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Masood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d90b7936-049a-53c0-9aa0-040739d8204e', 'word_count': 602, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d90b7936-049a-53c0-9aa0-040739d8204e'}, {'abstract': 'Does Joseph Smith’s theology suggest that one of our presidential candidates could be a deity?', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/16/why-i-love-mormonism/', 'snippet': 'Does Joseph Smith’s theology suggest that one of our presidential candidates could be a deity?', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve spent what is rapidly becoming nine years in New York City. It’s been a total blast. But as a transplanted Englishman one thing to which I’ve become rather sensitive in that time is which prejudices New Yorkers are permitted to express in public. Among \xa0my horribly overeducated and hugely liberal friends, expressions of racism are completely out of the question, Islamophobia is greeted with a slow shaking of the head and anti-Semitism is a memory associated with distant places that one sometimes visits — like France.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why I Love Mormonism', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christians and Christianity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mormons (Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-Day Saints)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Joseph (1805-44)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-16T21:30:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simon Critchley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Critchley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55050271-fe58-5057-9e21-134a6fba5f68', 'word_count': 3074, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55050271-fe58-5057-9e21-134a6fba5f68'}, {'abstract': 'Clarinda Mac Low stages improvisations in the spirit of the 1960s New York institution the Judson Dance Theater.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/17/arts/dance/clarinda-mac-low-and-simone-forti-recall-judson-dance-era.html', 'snippet': 'Clarinda Mac Low stages improvisations in the spirit of the 1960s New York institution the Judson Dance Theater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s fitting that “40 Dancers do 40 Dances for the Dancers,” a project conceived and directed by Clarinda Mac Low, was ruled by children — at least on opening night. Part of Ms. Mac Low’s intention for the event, as she states in program notes, is to recreate “a child’s-eye view of the 1970s New York ‘avant-garde’ arts world.” As the daughter of the poet, composer and performance artist  Jackson Mac Low, who died in 2004, she writes from experience. The children performing on Thursday evening at Danspace Project at St. Mark’s Church — notably, the adorable Ignacio Achugar-Granoff — offered some of the evening’s most genuine encounters.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/17/arts/maclow/maclow-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 712, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/17/arts/maclow/maclow-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1425, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/17/arts/maclow/maclow-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/17/arts/maclow/maclow-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/17/arts/maclow/maclow-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A ’60s Landmark in the Eyes of Children', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A ’60s Landmark In the Eyes of Children', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Danspace Project', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Judson Dance Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mac Low, Clarinda', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-16T21:39:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/450a129d-4a5b-5fba-bf96-91342bc00028', 'word_count': 534, 'uri': 'nyt://article/450a129d-4a5b-5fba-bf96-91342bc00028'}, {'abstract': 'Eleh, as he is called, played a show of electronic compositions in Brooklyn Heights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/17/arts/music/eleh-at-our-lady-of-lebanon-cathedral-in-brooklyn-heights.html', 'snippet': 'Eleh, as he is called, played a show of electronic compositions in Brooklyn Heights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Eleh, as he is called, walked down the aisle of Our Lady of Lebanon Cathedral in Brooklyn Heights after all the lights had been shut off and sat cross-legged before his equipment: an old Sequential Circuits analog keyboard synthesizer; a modular synthesizer about the shape of a large cash register, with red, yellow, orange, purple and black patch cables; and a hand-held digital multimeter to measure sound frequencies. You could see his outline only in the tiny readout lights of his gear. He is compact, of middling height and has short hair. Healthy. Maybe mid-30s.',