d0', 'word_count': 1180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72bb2dc2-f112-52cf-9b9b-f23aeb732cd0'}, {'abstract': 'Adam G. Perl bakes us a pie.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/16/itsy-bitsy-bit/', 'snippet': 'Adam G. Perl bakes us a pie.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MONDAY’S PUZZLE — Welcome back to another week of puzzling! I always enjoy Mondays. Well, not the concept (getting up for work or school after a relaxing weekend), but the puzzles. It feels like a fresh start after wrestling with the increasingly difficult week, tackling the Friday and Saturday grids, investing time in the Sunday … and then, poof! All that is gone, and we have a nice, simple Monday puzzle to sail through. It restores my faith in humanity, I tell you.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Itsy Bitsy Bit', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-16T22:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fdbed5d-0f5e-5155-b8bc-b55fa4275ffc', 'word_count': 256, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fdbed5d-0f5e-5155-b8bc-b55fa4275ffc'}, {'abstract': 'Data to be released includes the current account deficit for the second quarter, housing starts and existing home sales for August and the weekly jobless claims.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/17/business/economy/economic-reports-for-the-week-of-sept-16.html', 'snippet': 'Data to be released includes the current account deficit for the second quarter, housing starts and existing home sales for August and the weekly joble