raph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — For Google last week, the decision was clear. An anti-Islamic video that provoked violence worldwide was not hate speech under its rules because it did not specifically incite violence against Muslims, even if it mocked their faith.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/17/business/google/google-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/17/business/google/google-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'On Web, a Fine Line on Free Speech Across the Globe', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On Web, a Fine Line on Free Speech Across the Globe', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Innocence of Muslims (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'YouTube.com', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-17T00:15:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Somini Sengupta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Somini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sengupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba2d2de3-dede-5151-9a12-3223db1f35ed', 'word_count': 1111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba2d2de3-dede-5151-9a12-3223db1f35ed'}, {'abstract': 'Aereo hopes to offer an alternative for viewers who prefer to grab their favorite shows piecemeal from a number of online sources.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/17/technology/aereo-distributes-local-tv-channels-via-the-internet.html', 'snippet': 'Aereo hopes to offer an alternative for viewers who prefer to grab their favorite shows piecemeal from a number of online sources.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the ninth floor of an old tire factory in Downtown Brooklyn, Joe Lipowski, chief technology officer of a company called Aereo, proudly showed off a steel sheet covered with TV antennas. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/17/business/17aereojp1/17aereojp1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/17/business/17aereojp1/17aereojp1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For a Fee, Streaming Local TV', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For a Fee, Streaming Local TV', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Aereo Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-17T00:19:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenna Wortham', 'person': [{'firstname':