iven his campaign an air of anxiety — not what it wants to exude fewer than 50 days before the election.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/17/for-romney-campaign-an-unpleasant-week/', 'snippet': 'It may be fleeting, but for the moment Mitt Romney’s string of bad luck has given his campaign an air of anxiety — not what it wants to exude fewer than 50 days before the election.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — In presidential campaigns, as in life, there are unlucky and unpleasant weeks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Romney Campaign, an Unpleasant Week', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-17T09:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Barbaro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barbaro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/59524dd2-486a-5cdc-8295-bdc58a466e94', 'word_count': 341, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59524dd2-486a-5cdc-8295-bdc58a466e94'}, {'abstract': 'Remembering President Jimmy Carter at the Camp David peace accords, and 10 months later.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/17/booming/17history.html', 'snippet': 'Remembering President Jimmy Carter at the Camp David peace accords, and 10 months later.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By the time you’ve reached your 50s, you’ve lived through a good deal of history, although when it’s happening, it often seems to be just another edition of the nightly news. Of all the video clips linked here, the ones that struck me most were of former President Jimmy Carter, in September 1978, looking so vital at the Camp David peace accords, and then, just 10 months later, so deflated during his “crisis of confidence” speech. It’s a dramatic example of history taking its toll on a president.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jimmy Carter’s Brief Shining Moment', 'kicker': 'Remember This', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Boomers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-17T09:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Booming', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Winerip', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Winerip', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/334a00d8-4506-5185-96a6-7556a148869e', 'word_count': 224, 'uri': 'nyt://article/334a00d8-4506-5185-96a6-7556a148869e'}, {'abstract': 'A father’s sending of questionnaires to ballplayers started a life of newspaper writing that has been passed from generation to generation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/18/booming/18winerip.html', 'snippet': 'A father’s sending of questionnaires to ballplayers started a life of newspaper writing that has been passed from generation to generation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was recently rooting around in the crawl space under the house and came across two old letters that moved me greatly.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/15/fashion/18winerip-letter/18winerip-letter-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 307, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/15/fashio