tars of the American food scene. At 50, the author of the Web site “Wild Fermentation” and the how-to guide “The Art of Fermentation” has emerged as an evangelist for the pleasures and health benefits of sauerkraut, kimchi, kefir, kvass, umeboshi plums and hundreds of other fermented delights.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sandor Katz Is Answering Your Fermentation Questions', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bacteria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-17T17:35:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd7bc3da-3c20-59d8-9edd-09bc829fce2b', 'word_count': 142, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd7bc3da-3c20-59d8-9edd-09bc829fce2b'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama, under renewed fire from Mitt Romney for not standing up to China on behalf of American workers, used a rally in this battleground state to announce a new trade case against Beijing.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/17/filing-trade-suit-obama-raps-romney-on-china/', 'snippet': 'President Obama, under renewed fire from Mitt Romney for not standing up to China on behalf of American workers, used a rally in this battleground state to announce a new trade case against Beijing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CINCINNATI – President Obama, under renewed fire from Mitt Romney for not standing up to China on behalf of American workers, used a rally in this battleground state on Monday to announce a new trade case against Beijing. He said it was Mr. Romney who had sent jobs to China through his zealous practice of outsourcing at Bain Capital.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Filing Trade Suit, Obama Raps Romney on China', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Trade Organization', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-17T17:35:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/21b882c0-e4db-59e3-ac2c-7bcdf1943534', 'word_count': 1015, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21b882c0-e4db-59e3-ac2c-7bcdf1943534'}, {'abstract': 'It remains unclear if she wrote the music and lyrics to “Skyfall” or is simply performing the vocals, but the song is expected to be released after the movie is released in November.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/17/adele-records-the-theme-for-the-new-james-bond-film/', 'snippet': 'It remains unclear if she wrote the music and lyrics to “Skyfall” or is simply performing the vocals, but the song is expected to be released after the movie is released in November.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Forget Adele’s Grammy Awards and the fact that every teenage woman in the world knows the lyrics to most of her blockbuster album, “21.” You know the singer has finally arrived because she has recorded the theme for the new James Bond film, “Skyfall,” according to the Total Film Web site.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Adele Records the Theme for the New James Bond Film', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From ‘21’ to 007: A New Adele Number', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bond, James (Fictional Character)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adele (Singer)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crow, Sheryl', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Tom', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keys, Alicia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Madonna', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCartney, Paul', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Simon, Carly', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'White, Jack', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Duran Duran', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-17T17:44:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6da29558-0f2f-5cdc-9767-fc33ec94c17f', 'word_count': 180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6da29558-0f2f-5cdc-9767-fc33ec94c17f'}, {'abstract': 'A weekly capsule of travel news curated by our writers and editors.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/17/walkabout-917-travelers-to-the-middle-east-ponder-plans-and-students-go-abroad/', 'snippet': 'A weekly capsule of travel news curated by our writers and editors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wait and See While protests against an American-made online video mocking the Prophet Muhammad continue in the Middle East, North Africa and South Asia, experts are not encouraging Americans to abandon their travel plans to those countries (except for Libya, which the\xa0 State Department recommends avoiding). Rather, they suggest that travelers be patient while events unfold. (The Washington Post)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Walkabout – 9/17: Travelers to the Middle East Ponder Plans, and Students Go Abroad', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-17T17:44:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6287c4d-78e1-567b-ada9-a1ac0f9c85ac', 'word_count': 181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6287c4d-78e1-567b-ada9-a1ac0f9c85ac'}, {'abstract': 'The government said it had released 514 prisoners, many of whom were reported to have been political prisoners.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/18/world/asia/myanmar-frees-prisoners-as-thein-sein-prepares-for-general-assembly.html', 'snippet': 'The government said it had released 514 prisoners, many of whom were reported to have been political prisoners.', 'lead_paragraph': 'YANGON, Myanmar — Myanmar’s government said Monday that it was releasing more than 500 prisoners, the latest in a series of amnesties by President Thein Sein’s administration.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Myanmar Releases Hundreds of Prisoners', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Myanmar Releases Hundreds Of Prisoners', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'n