ocuments the recent party conventions for this age of instantaneous and continuous news.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Politicians today live in the era of the sound bite, which may give way to the Twitter message (and then something else altogether) — either way, instantaneous news seems to be the only way our news is consumed now, and this ravenous cycle guarantees that stories sometimes fly by unnoticed, undigested. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Examining Pre-Packaged Conventions', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barbaro, Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crowley, Stephen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Heisler, Todd', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stolarik, Robert', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winter, Damon', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-17T18:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt McCann', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McCann', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6a450ca-d4ae-5ec7-b1b2-0b1f259a5f12', 'word_count': 255, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6a450ca-d4ae-5ec7-b1b2-0b1f259a5f12'}, {'abstract': 'Parking Panda is offering a smartphone app to make it easier to find parking in markets like San Francisco.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/17/an-app-to-help-you-find-parking-on-the-spot/', 'snippet': 'Parking Panda is offering a smartphone app to make it easier to find parking in markets like San Francisco.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Parking Panda, an online service that helps you find and reserve parking spaces, has added the San Francisco market to its inventory and introduced a mobile app to help you find parking on the spot.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An App to Help You Find Parking On the Spot', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-17T18:00:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2775b0a7-94eb-5e52-bed4-293f34aa8634', 'word_count': 384, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2775b0a7-94eb-5e52-bed4-293f34aa8634'}, {'abstract': 'When Little Bear asked his mother to tell him a story about “the things I once did,” the sudden reference to the speedy passage of time cut me to the heart.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/17/why-little-bear-made-me-burst-into-tears/', 'snippet': 'When Little Bear asked his mother to tell him a story about “the things I once did,” the sudden reference to the speedy passage of time cut me to the heart.', 'lead_paragraph': '“What kind of story would you like to hear?” said Mother Bear.“Tell me about me,” said Little Bear. “Tell me about things I once did.”–Else Holmelund Minarik, “Little Bear”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/17/style/motherlode-little-bear/motherlode-little-bear-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 749, 'width': 481, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/17/style/motherlode-little-bear/motherlode-little-bear-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 749, 'width': 481, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/17/style/motherlode-little-bear/motherlode-little-bear-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/17/style/motherlode-little-bear/motherlode-little-bear-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/17/style/motherlode-little-bear/motherlode-little-bear-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why ‘Little Bear’ Made Me Burst Into Tears', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Minarik, Else Holmelund', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-17T18:00:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gretchen Rubin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gretchen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rubin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/722359af-113b-5bcb-9bc0-117aa9e51a30', 'word_count': 416, 'uri': 'nyt://article/722359af-113b-5bcb-9bc0-117aa9e51a30'}, {'abstract': 'Follow Garrett Oliver of Brooklyn Brewery as he starts making a batch of White House Honey Ale.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/17/brewing-obamas-ale-step-by-step/', 'snippet': 'Follow Garrett Oliver of Brooklyn Brewery as he starts making a batch of White House Honey Ale.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This month, after word got out that the White House was brewing its own beer, President Obama’s staff released its recipe for White House Honey Ale. Diner’s Journal asked Garrett Oliver, the brewmaster at Brooklyn Brewery, to make a batch that we could sample and assess. And on Friday, Mr. Oliver started the brewing – a monthlong process that we’ll occasionally drop in on, offering a glimpse of brewing both for those who know the art and for those who don’t.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Brewing Obama’s Ale, Step by Step', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Oliver, Garrett', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Brewery', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-17T18:01:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Garrett Oliver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Garrett', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Oliver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fad758b4-bad9-5965-863e-03b4b8325001', 'word_count': 1000, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fad758b4-bad9-5965-863e-03b4b8325001'}, {'abstract': 'Katie Couric’s talk show is the latest attempt to become a dominant force in daytime television, as Oprah Winfrey once was. Brian Stelter and Bill Carter discuss the high rewards and high hurdles she faces.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/17/stelter-and-carter-on-this-falls-search-for-the-next-oprah/', 'snippet': 'Katie Couric’s talk show is the latest attempt to become a dominant force in daytime television, as Oprah Winfrey once was. Brian Stelter and Bill Carter discuss the high rewards and high hurdles she faces.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Katie Couric has begun a daytime talk show, joining a crowded field that is becoming more crowded with newcomers like Steve Harvey and Jeff Probst and a returning host like Ricki Lake. In this video clip, Brian Stelter and Bill Carter discuss the high rewards, and the high hurdles, to becoming a dominant figure in daytime television, as Oprah Winfrey once was.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stelter and Carter on This Fall’s Search for the Next Oprah', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Couric, Katie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-17T18:02:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editors', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editors'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/952bee64-ac88-5fdd-974d-435699a5f892', 'word_count': 62, 'uri': 'nyt://article/952bee64-ac88-5fdd-974d-435699a5f892'}, {'abstract': 'Popular toys called Water Balz expand greatly in size when exposed to liquid, posing a hazard to pets and small children who may swallow them when they are the size of marbles, pediatricians warn.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/17/expanding-ball-toy-poses-hazard-to-children-and-pets/', 'snippet': 'Popular toys called Water Balz expand greatly in size when exposed to liquid, posing a hazard to pets and small children who may swallow them when they are the size of marbles, pediatricians warn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'They are known as Water Balz, and at first glance they look like marbles: small and spherical, brightly colored. But these balls are made of superabsorbent polymer, and they are capable of rapidly expanding to the size of a racquetball when doused in water.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/17/health/Water-Balz/Water-Balz-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 640, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/17/health/Water-Balz/Water-Balz-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 640, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/17/health/Water-Balz/Water-Balz-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/17/health/Water-Balz/Water-Balz-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/17/health/Water-Balz/Water-Balz-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Expanding Ball Toy Poses Hazard to Children and Pets', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Digestive Tract', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emergency Medical Treatment', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pets', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Toys', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-17T18:04:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': "By Anahad O'Connor", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anahad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Connor", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/269f1ab2-0a54-5ee3-a21e-e1ff7f5d685e', 'word_count': 855, 'uri': 'nyt://article/269f1ab2-0a54-5ee3-a21e-e1ff7f5d685e'}, {'abstract': 'Beth Hillel Congregation of Wilmette, Ill., takes a modest approach in its campaign to solicit new members.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/17/business/media/were-not-perfect-an-illinois-synagogues-ads-proclaim-campaign-spotlight.html', 'snippet': 'Beth Hillel Congregation of Wilmette, Ill., takes a modest approach in its campaign to solicit new members.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Madison Avenue loves to extol the perfection of products, from a whipped icing that is “the perfect blend of fudge and vanilla” to a luxury car that is devoted to “the relentless pursuit of perfection.” A new campaign, however, takes a much more modest tack by declaring, “We’re not perfect.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/17/business/media/17adnewsletter1/17adnewsletter1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 839, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/17/business/media/1