l': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/c08e7d69-e60a-5f0c-9d54-456fe569215d', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/c08e7d69-e60a-5f0c-9d54-456fe569215d'}, {'abstract': 'Stephen Burt, the Harvard professor and poet, has many brilliant peers in his generation of poetry critics, and if one doesn’t inspire you to read poetry, another might.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/17/whom-and-what-to-read-to-make-you-like-poetry-and-also-sci-fi/', 'snippet': 'Stephen Burt, the Harvard professor and poet, has many brilliant peers in his generation of poetry critics, and if one doesn’t inspire you to read poetry, another might.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stephen Burt, the Harvard professor and poet whom I wrote about in Sunday’s Education Issue, is a fanboy and an evangelist of poetry. As I wrote in the magazine, Burt defends his positivity by saying, “There’s so little airtime available for any poetry these days that when I get space and time in which I can do whatever I want, I don’t want to say, ‘X sucks.’ I almost always prefer to say, ‘Please check out Y,’ or ‘Z isn’t what you think,’ or ‘Look at what A, B and C have in common.’ ” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/17/magazine/17-ts-eliot/17-ts-eliot-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 734, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/17/magazine/17-ts-eliot/17-ts-eliot-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1468, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/17/magazine/17-ts-eliot/17-ts-eliot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/17/magazine/17-ts-eliot/17-ts-eliot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/17/magazine/17-ts-eliot/17-ts-eliot-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Whom and What to Read to Make You Like Poetry (and Also Sci-Fi)', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-17T19:52:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Oppenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Oppenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6d68455-c87b-5d93-af40-039b539614c1', 'word_count': 590, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6d68455-c87b-5d93-af40-039b539614c1'}, {'abstract': 'Lydia Ko, the leading amateur at the Women’s British Open, said she would like to play amateur golf for a couple of years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/18/sports/golf/15-year-old-golfer-lydia-ko-is-in-no-rush-to-turn-pro.html', 'snippet': 'Lydia Ko, the leading amateur at the Women’s British Open, said she would like to play amateur golf for a couple of years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HOYLAKE, England ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/18/sports/golf/18golf-pic/18golf-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/18/sports/golf/18golf-pi