ew standard for how the Justice Department deals with criminal conduct by corporations. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Deferred Prosecution Agreements and Cookie-Cutter Justice', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deferred Prosecution Agreements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Libor (London Interbank Offered Rate)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Breuer, Lanny A', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-17T20:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter J. Henning', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Henning', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8225dd8d-a913-54f7-a40d-eafb4e6af62c', 'word_count': 985, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8225dd8d-a913-54f7-a40d-eafb4e6af62c'}, {'abstract': 'A debate builds over the notion that humans have become a geological force powerful enough to leave a permanent record.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/17/the-anthropocene-as-environmental-meme-andor-geological-epoch/', 'snippet': 'A debate builds over the notion that humans have become a geological force powerful enough to leave a permanent record.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Paul Voosen, who’s one of my favorite science journalists these days, has written a fine piece examining the scientific and societal debate over the Anthropocene, the proposed term for this era in which human decisions (or indecision) will leave a durable mark in planetary systems and even in the planet’s stratified rock.* (The video above explores the Anthropocene as environmental meme.) ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The ‘Anthropocene’ as Environmental Meme and/or Geological Epoch', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Earth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Geology', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-17T20:02:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/80b41632-1ca2-5e17-9584-30eb508aec88', 'word_count': 352, 'uri': 'nyt://article/80b41632-1ca2-5e17-9584-30eb508aec88'}, {'abstract': 'The musical biography of the silent-film star took in $460,925 at the box office in its first full week.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/17/chaplin-off-to-quiet-start-at-broadway-box-office/', 'snippet': 'The musical biography of the silent-film star took in $460,925 at the box office in its first full week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The new Broadway musical “Chaplin” grossed a modest $460,925 in ticket sales in its first full week of performances since opening to largely negative reviews on Sept. 10, according to box office data released on Monday by the Broadway League, a trade association of theater owners and producers. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Chaplin’ Off to Quiet Start at Broadway Box Office', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Modest Debut For Musical ‘Chaplin’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McClure, Rob', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rudd, Paul', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shannon, Michael', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wright, Craig', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-17T20:02:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed35f0b8-730e-5477-acec-3f059b13bb8e', 'word_count': 351, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed35f0b8-730e-5477-acec-3f059b13bb8e'}, {'abstract': 'American Ballet Theater has recruited Ivan Vasiliev as a principal dancer, and will cast him during next year’s season at the Metropolitan Opera and on tours.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/17/vasiliev-joins-american-ballet-theater-as-principal-dancer/', 'snippet': 'American Ballet Theater has recruited Ivan Vasiliev as a principal dancer, and will cast him during next year’s season at the Metropolitan Opera and on tours.', 'lead_paragraph': 'American Ballet Theater has recruited Ivan Vasiliev as a principal dancer, and will cast him during next year’s season at the Metropolitan Opera and on tours, the company said on Monday. Mr. Vasiliev and the ballerina Natalia Osipova created a stir nearly a year ago when they announced they were leaving Moscow’s Bolshoi Ballet for the Mikhailovsky Theater in St. Petersburg. Mr. Vasiliev, who was born in 1989 in Vladivostok, Russia, made his debut at the Bolshoi in 2006 as Basilio in “Don Quixote” and made guest appearances at Ballet Theater last year. His roles with the company included Solor in “La Bayadère,” Franz in “Coppélia” and Ali in “Le Corsaire.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/17/arts/17artsbeat-vasiliev/17artsbeat-vasiliev-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 794, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/17/arts/17artsbeat-vasiliev/17artsbeat-vasiliev-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1402, 'width': 1087, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/17/arts/17artsbeat-vasiliev/17artsbeat-vasiliev-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/17/arts/17artsbeat-vasiliev/17artsbeat-vasiliev-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/17/arts/17artsbeat-vasiliev/17artsbeat-vasiliev-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Vasiliev Joins American Ballet Theater as Principal Dancer', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Vasiliev Signs as Principal With Ballet Theater', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vasiliev, Ivan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN BALLET THEATER', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-17T20:02:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 