rter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6776a04-e421-5929-8385-f7685de6738e', 'word_count': 880, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6776a04-e421-5929-8385-f7685de6738e'}, {'abstract': 'The clothes at Christpher Kane looked put together with the care of a beautifully wrapped package, and, of course, they played with the notion of women as pretty objects, tied with bows.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/17/christopher-kane-has-a-gift-for-you/', 'snippet': 'The clothes at Christpher Kane looked put together with the care of a beautifully wrapped package, and, of course, they played with the notion of women as pretty objects, tied with bows.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Shortly before the Christopher Kane show, in a high-rise near Oxford Street, the casting director Russell Marsh was playing Burt Lancaster to a bunch of blank-faced girls. He was giving them orders, drill-sergeant style, about not mussing up their clothes. Mr. Marsh probably gives such instructions routinely, but the spring collection of Mr. Kane was visibly delicate — in tissue paper-like silks and crepes, and in pale sugary pinks, yellow and dead white.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Christopher Kane Has a Gift for You', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'London Fashion Week', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kane, Christopher', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-17T22:39:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7ad46fd-9f85-5e1d-91cc-3fa108baba58', 'word_count': 250, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7ad46fd-9f85-5e1d-91cc-3fa108baba58'}, {'abstract': 'An Iranian religious foundation reportedly raised the price on the novelist Salman Rushdie’s head to $3.3 million, claiming that his murder would stop others from disrespecting Islam’s founding prophet.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/17/iranian-cleric-says-rushdies-murder-could-stop-insults-to-islams-prophet/', 'snippet': 'An Iranian religious foundation reportedly raised the price on the novelist Salman Rushdie’s head to $3.3 million, claiming that his murder would stop others from disrespecting Islam’s founding prophet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As my colleague Michiko Kakutani explains in her review of the novelist Salman Rushdie’s new memoir, an Iranian religious foundation reportedly raised the price on his head over the weekend to $3.3 million. The cleric who leads the foundation claimed that Mr. Rushdie’s murder would stop others from disrespecting Islam’s founder, The Associated Press reported from Tehran.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iranian Cleric Says Rushdie’s Murder Could Stop Insults to Islam’s Prophet', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khamenei, Ali', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khomeini, Ruhollah', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rushdie, Salman', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}],