istory lessons that need to be preserved.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KETRZYN, Poland — For nearly three years, Hitler commanded the Third Reich from a vast network of bunkers and buildings hidden in the forest here, guiding his genocidal war effort from an encampment called the Wolf’s Lair.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/18/world/POLAND-2/POLAND-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 689, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/18/world/POLAND-2/POLAND-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1379, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/18/world/POLAND-2/POLAND-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/18/world/POLAND-2/POLAND-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/18/world/POLAND-2/POLAND-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Restoring the Walls, and the History, at Hitler’s Wolf’s Lair', 'kicker': 'Ketrzyn Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Restoring the Walls, And the History, At Hitler’s Wolf’s Lair', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Poland', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hitler, Adolf', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-18T01:32:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanna Berendt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Berendt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/516d67e6-ce46-5f3e-a211-eea8b03fef8f', 'word_count': 947, 'uri': 'nyt://article/516d67e6-ce46-5f3e-a211-eea8b03fef8f'}, {'abstract': 'Until now, Mitt Romney’s campaign had been focused almost entirely on criticizing President Obama.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/18/us/politics/after-a-rocky-few-weeks-romney-shifts-strategy-to-policy-specifics.html', 'snippet': 'Until now, Mitt Romney’s campaign had been focused almost entirely on criticizing President Obama.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An effort by Mitt Romney to give his campaign new direction — built around new ads intended to highlight how a Romney presidency would take the nation on a better course than President Obama — was quickly overshadowed on Monday by the video of Mr. Romney’s unscripted remarks at a fund-raiser several months ago.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/18/us/politics/sub18ROMNEY/sub18ROMNEY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/18/us/politics/sub18ROMNEY/sub18ROMNEY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/18/us/politics/sub18ROMNEY/sub