6acc61b6234'}, {'abstract': 'Proving which initiatives work could turn the state into a model for others on how to cut Medicaid without harming the beneficiaries.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/18/opinion/new-yorks-medicaid-reforms.html', 'snippet': 'Proving which initiatives work could turn the state into a model for others on how to cut Medicaid without harming the beneficiaries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York State has substantially changed its Medicaid program in the past year and a half in ways likely to improve the health of its poorest residents and rein in the program’s enormous costs. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York’s Medicaid Reforms', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New York’s Medicaid Reforms', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicaid', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-18T01:35:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1c957e8-5478-5c35-8063-3c3a751d0f8e', 'word_count': 506, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1c957e8-5478-5c35-8063-3c3a751d0f8e'}, {'abstract': 'The chairman of the Metropolitan Transportation Authority is unfettered compared with most public officials on Twitter, who usually have a team operating their account.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/18/nyregion/joseph-lhota-mta-chief-tweets-to-his-delight.html', 'snippet': 'The chairman of the Metropolitan Transportation Authority is unfettered compared with most public officials on Twitter, who usually have a team operating their account.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It began inconspicuously enough — a Ronald Reagan quote here, a whiff of harmless promotion there — the mark of a seasoned city official wading cautiously into social media.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/18/nyregion/LHOTA/LHOTA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/18/nyregion/LHOTA/LHOTA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/18/nyregion/LHOTA/LHOTA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/18/nyregion/LHOTA/LHOTA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/18/nyregion/LHOTA/LHOTA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'M.T.A. Chief’s Latest Bold Move: Using Twitter by Himself', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'M.T.A. Chief’s Latest Bold Move: Using Twitter by Himself', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Transportation Authority', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lhota, Joseph J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-18T01:39:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Flegenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flegenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f3792a10-7dcf-5c88-848c-080f7183a021', 'word_count': 953, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f3792a10-7dcf-5c88-848c-080f7183a021'}, {'abstract': 'The Jets’ defense, expected to carry the team while it installs a new offense, struggled in Sunday’s loss to the Steelers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/18/sports/football/jets-turn-backs-on-game-that-slipped-right-through-their-hands.html', 'snippet': 'The Jets’ defense, expected to carry the team while it installs a new offense, struggled in Sunday’s loss to the Steelers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FLORHAM PARK, N.J. — On the ninth play of a 14-play drive that ate up more than 10 minutes of the fourth quarter, Pittsburgh running back Isaac Redman took a handoff and proceeded to shrug off what seemed like half the Jets’ defense. His right knee appeared to scuff the grass at Heinz Field while he was trapped in the backfield, and safety Yeremiah Bell wrestled the ball from Redman as he made the tackle. After an officials’ review, the Steelers kept the ball, and Redman got 6 yards.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/18/sports/JETS/JETS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 708, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/18/sports/JETS/JETS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1417, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jets Turn Backs on a Game That Slipped Right Through Their Hands', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jets Turn Backs on a Game That Slipped Right Through Their Hands', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Revis, Darrelle', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pittsburgh Steelers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maybin, Aaron', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-18T01:42:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Caldwell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caldwell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fed07d6b-4fed-5e52-80a6-535b55e534b9', 'word_count': 868, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fed07d6b-4fed-5e52-80a6-535b55e534b9'}, {'abstract': 'Political polarization in America is at its highest level since the late 19th century. Can we do anything about it?', 'web_url': 'https://campaignstops.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/17/look-how-far-weve-come-apart/', 'snippet': 'Political polarization in America is at its highest level since the late 19th century. Can we do anything about it?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the witches’ brew of fearmongering, unkeepable promises and poll-tested metaphors that both parties serve up to the electorate every four years, you can always find this predictable dash of inspiration: the image of Americans uniting and working together for the sake of the country. President Obama said in Charlotte, N.C. that America is “about what can be done by us, together.” In Tampa, Paul Ryan said, “Whatever your political party, let’s come together for the sake of our country.” And Mitt Romney closed his convention speech with three invocations of “That America, that united America.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Look How Far We’ve Come Apart', 'kicker': 'Campaign Stops', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-18T01:48:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Haidt and Marc J. Hetherington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haidt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Hetherington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2dfb835c-1034-5699-b64a-fb5c87a0a92c', 'word_count': 1755, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2dfb835c-1034-5699-b64a-fb5c87a0a92c'}, {'abstract': 'Did you hear about Mitt Romney’s comments from a fund-raiser earlier this year? They seemed to suggest that Romney doesn’t understand America.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/18/opinion/brooks-thurston-howell-romney.html', 'snippet': 'Did you hear about Mitt Romney’s comments from a fund-raiser earlier this year? They seemed to suggest that Romney doesn’t understand America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1980, about 30 percent of Americans received some form of government benefits. Today, as Nicholas Eberstadt of the American Enterprise Institute has pointed out, about 49 percent do.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-thumbLarge-v2.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Thurston Howell Romney', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Thurston Howell Romney', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Welfare (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-18T01:53:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Brooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/15b57682-53a3-5f64-8c72-b3335644e1c5', 'word_count': 801, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15b57682-53a3-5f64-8c72-b3335644e1c5'}, {'abstract': 'In Chicago, they’re fighting over the wrong things. Just look at what the top-performing education systems do.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/18/opinion/nocera-how-to-fix-the-schools.html', 'snippet': 'In Chicago, they’re fighting over the wrong things. Just look at what the top-performing education systems do.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No matter how quickly the Chicago teachers’ strike ends, whether it is this afternoon or two months from now, it’s not going to end well for the city’s public school students. Yes, I know; that’s the hoariest of clichés. But that doesn’t mean it’s not true.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}