: [{'firstname': 'Lizette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alvarez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b628579-b082-56d3-92b7-5b82eeb41e11', 'word_count': 894, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b628579-b082-56d3-92b7-5b82eeb41e11'}, {'abstract': 'Andrew Reynolds climbs to his debut.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/17/stop-fretting/', 'snippet': 'Andrew Reynolds climbs to his debut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TUESDAY’S PUZZLE — If you grew up when I did (I’m not going to be specific, but I will say that I am old enough to have been a devoted fan), you weren’t a fan of the rock and roll music unless you owned, played, memorized the liner notes of, and basically worshipped the album “Led Zeppelin IV.” This was the iconic album that contained the song “STAIRWAY TO HEAVEN,” which became the song of a generation and is celebrating the 40th (now 41st) anniversary of its release in November of 1971.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stop Fretting', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-18T02:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e43da568-9718-55ad-905d-fbc52aaca069', 'word_count': 649, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e43da568-9718-55ad-905d-fbc52aaca069'}, {'abstract': '“We need to have the French point of view,” said Xavier Romatet, president of Condé Nast France. “We need to be much more close to the French culture.”', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/17/cond-nast-plans-french-vanity-fair/', 'snippet': '“We need to have the French point of view,” said Xavier Romatet, president of Condé Nast France. “We need to be much more close to the French culture.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Vanity Fair magazine, which has been battling declining newsstand sales in the United States, is looking for more readers in Europe. Next year, Condé Nast is starting a monthly edition of Vanity Fair in France. The magazine will share the name of the American publication, but nearly 90 percent of the content will be original.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Condé Nast Plans French Vanity Fair', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Condé Nast Plans French Vanity Fair', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Conde Nast Publications Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vanity Fair', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-18T02:01:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Haughney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haughney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/583376ad-aee5-5ae1-bf0b-da7529072664', 'word_count': 458, 'uri': 'nyt://article/583376ad-aee5-5ae1-bf0b-da7529072664'}, {'abstract': 'A Hamas military court on Monday convicted four Palestinians of taking part in the 2011 kidnapping and killing of a pro-Palestinian Italian activist in the Gaza Strip.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/18/world/middleeast/gaza-hamas-court-convicts-4-in-murder-of-activist.html', 'snippet': 'A Hamas military court on Monday convicted four Palestinians of taking part in the 2011 kidnapping and killing of a pro-Palestinian Italian activist in the Gaza Strip.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Hamas military court on Monday convicted four Palestinians of taking part in the 2011 kidnapping and killing of a pro-Palestinian Italian activist in the Gaza Strip. Two of the defendants received life sentences for kidnapping and killing the activist, Vittorio Arrigoni, in April 2011. A third man was sentenced to 10 years for taking part in the kidnapping, and a fourth defendant was sentenced to a year for sheltering the kidnappers, said Khalil Shahin of the Palestinian Center for Human Rights. At the time, an extremist Salafist group claimed responsibility for kidnapping Mr. Arrigoni, 36, and demanded that Hamas release all Salafists from its prisons. Mr. Arrigoni was found dead before the kidnappers’ deadline had expired. The suspects were later captured by Hamas’s security force. Mr. Arrigoni was a member of the International Solidarity Movement, a pro-Palestinian activist organization with foreign volunteers in the West Bank and Gaza.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/18/world/BRIEFS/BRIEFS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 725, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/18/world/BRIEFS/BRIEFS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1451, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Gaza: Hamas Court Convicts 4 in Murder of Activist', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gaza: Hamas Court Convicts 4 in Murder of Activist', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hamas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kidnapping', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gaza Strip', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Arrigoni, Vittorio', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-18T02:15:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fares Akram', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fares', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Akram', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb3cce17-ebf4-5b54-80ba-be182b8b0472', 'word_count': 151, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb3cce17-ebf4-5b54-80ba-be182b8b0472'}, {'abstract': 'After falling to the Philadelphia Phillies, the Mets have now lost seven straight games at Citi Field and have not scored more than three runs at home since Aug. 12.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/18/sports/baseball/dickey-fails-in-bid-for-19-wins-as-mets-lose-to-phillies.html', 'snippet': 'After falling to the Philadelphia Phillies, the Mets have now lost seven straight games at Citi Field and have not scored more than three runs at home since Aug. 12.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Mets have returned to Citi Field, where they will have roughly a week and a half to leave some sort of lasting positive impression upon their fans before the off-season.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/18/sports/YMETS/YMETS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop