}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36bb3be5-af6f-5bc4-b102-9d703e90bfca', 'word_count': 22, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36bb3be5-af6f-5bc4-b102-9d703e90bfca'}, {'abstract': 'Haryana’s chief minister, now in his second term, on investment, pro-farmer policies and crime in his state.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/18/a-conversation-with-haryana-chief-minister-bhupinder-singh-hooda/', 'snippet': 'Haryana’s chief minister, now in his second term, on investment, pro-farmer policies and crime in his state.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI– Bhupinder Singh Hooda has been chief minister of Haryana since 2005, and is currently serving his second term. The state, which hugs India’s capital, is said to be the site of the epic battle described in the Mahabharata; it is now home to just over 2 percent of India’s people, some 25 million. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Conversation With: Haryana Chief Minister Bhupinder Singh Hooda', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Maruti Suzuki India Ltd', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gurgaon (India)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Haryana (India)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-18T06:27:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pamposh Raina and Heather Timmons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pamposh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Raina', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Heather', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Timmons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/da8aaa8d-f7dd-535e-99e2-8f67c4d10d5a', 'word_count': 2061, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da8aaa8d-f7dd-535e-99e2-8f67c4d10d5a'}, {'abstract': 'Despite success at home, Borussia Dortmund and its young stars seemed out of their element in last year’s Champions League. That may not be the case this time.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/18/champions-league-a-seasoned-dortmund-starts-fresh/', 'snippet': 'Despite success at home, Borussia Dortmund and its young stars seemed out of their element in last year’s Champions League. That may not be the case this time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sixteen years is a long time in soccer. Between one decade and the next, players, coaches or even entire teams and leagues that came to dominate and influence the very sport have to eventually accept the simple facts of fate and step aside as time picks its next champion. On Tuesday, Borussia Dortmund hosts Ajax in their first Champions League encounter since a fateful quarterfinal in 1996, during a forgotten time when both clubs were considered big players in Europe’s premier competition. Today, both sides will be hopeful of three points, and another shot at European success.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Champions League: A Seasoned Dortmund Starts Fresh', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'UEFA Champions League (Soccer)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Borussia Dortmund', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-18T06:44:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stefan Bienkowski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stefan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bienkow