 debt sold out at slightly lower rates, but uncertainty persisted over whether Spain would ask for aid from its European partners.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Spain took advantage of improved bond-market sentiment in the euro zone to sell government debt on Tuesday, but questions still lingered about whether, or when, it would seek European help to lower its borrowing costs.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Uncertainty About Bailout Lingers, Spain Sells $6 Billion in Short-Term Debt', 'kicker': 'Euro Watch', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Uncertainty About Bailout Lingers, Spain Sells $6 Billion in Short-Term Debt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Monetary Union', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Central Bank', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Bonds', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-18T10:58:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Castle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6f72a4d-762c-5dea-949f-4eba46cf8bfb', 'word_count': 662, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6f72a4d-762c-5dea-949f-4eba46cf8bfb'}, {'abstract': 'The Falcons-Broncos game on Monday night was a fiasco for the replacement officials. The N.F.L. has put them in an almost impossible position.', 'w