l and expenses wondering, ‘What are my customers thinking?'”", 'lead_paragraph': 'The Supreme Court decision upholding most of the Affordable Care Act came as a blow to Kurt Summers, a small-business owner in Austin, Tex. Soon after the decision was announced, he warned his fellow citizens, through the auspices of The Washington Post, that unless “we elect officials to both Congress and the White House who understand the importance of small business and who will return some sanity to Washington” — and repeal the health law — he will most likely have to postpone his considerable ambitions for his company.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Business Owner Expects the Worst From Health Insurance Overhaul', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Federation of Independent Business', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-18T12:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robb Mandelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mandelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/20a7879b-6f01-5978-ab94-594f70bba4c6', 'word_count': 1389, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20a7879b-6f01-5978-ab94-594f70bba4c6'}, {'abstract': 'Here’s another roundup of setbacks and slips in our continuing struggle to make verbs agree with their subjects and pronouns with their antecedents.', 'web