ght forecast showed that President Obama was more likely to lose the Electoral College while winning the popular vote than the other way around.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The FiveThirtyEight presidential forecast for Monday was essentially unchanged, with President Obama having a 74.8 percent chance of winning another term. Taken on the whole, Monday’s data was consistent with the current “story” the forecast model is telling about the race, which is that Mr. Obama’s polls have declined slightly from their post-convention highs, but are also still slightly better than his preconvention polls. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sept. 17: Electoral College May Not Help Obama', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-18T12:12:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09d263a3-7610-5ca3-9441-c2b024151ce9', 'word_count': 1733, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09d263a3-7610-5ca3-9441-c2b024151ce9'}, {'abstract': 'Metropolitan Diary: A car owner was almost resigned to replacing his dented plastic bumper, until a chance encounter at a red light showed him an alternative.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/18/the-bumper-man/', 'snippet': 'Metropolitan Diary: A car owner was almost resigne