Romney said that nearly of half of Americans were dependent on government assistance and felt entitled, were released by the liberal magazine Mother Jones on Monday and threatened to derail the Romney campaign as it tried to redefine its message 50 days before the election, Jim Rutenberg and Ashley Parker wrote. Speaking to wealthy donors at a Florida fund-raiser in May, Mr. Romney said “47 percent of the people” will vote for Mr. Obama “no matter what,” adding that they are “dependent upon government, who believe that they are victims, who believe the government has a responsibility to care for them.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: Romney Caught on Tape, and Detecting ‘Photoshopped’ Images', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-18T13:58:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noam Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/076bf821-90f3-57c3-8b57-71ffe0265828', 'word_count': 547, 'uri': 'nyt://article/076bf821-90f3-57c3-8b57-71ffe0265828'}, {'abstract': 'Just like a snowflake, every 0-2 N.F.L. team is unique, if not necessarily pretty. No doubt the most surprising of the winless teams is the New Orleans Saints.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/18/n-f-l-blueprints-for-getting-out-of-0-2-holes/', 'snippet': 'Just like a snowflake, every 0-2 N.F.L. team is unique, if not necessarily pretty. No doubt the most surprising of the winless teams is the New Orleans Saints.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chase Stuart writes about the historical and statistical side of football at his site,