 and Cee Lo Green next spring. It is evidence, along with the news of new big-name judges for “American Idol,” that stars are eager to hitch themselves to TV talent shows.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The judging wheel on television’s glut of singing-competition shows continues to spin, with two new superstar-singers, Usher and Shakira, signing on for NBC’s next edition of “The Voice” in the spring.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Usher and Shakira to Join ‘The Voice’ Next Season', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Usher and Shakira To Join ‘The Voice’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shakira', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Usher', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-18T15:10:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/be6ee0c8-93f4-5436-8227-8988c796370f', 'word_count': 334, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be6ee0c8-93f4-5436-8227-8988c796370f'}, {'abstract': 'A group of public interest organizations say they will soon file complaints against AT&T, alleging that the carrier is violating government rules by restricting the way customers use FaceTime, Apple’s video-conferencing tool that is built into iPhones and iPads.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/18/fcc-facetime-att/', 'snippet': 'A group of public interest organizations say they will soon file complaints against AT&T, alleging that the carrier is violating government rules by restricting the way customers use FaceTime, Apple’s video-conferencing tool that is built into iPh...', 'lead_paragraph': ' A group of public interest organizations said Tuesday that they would soon file complaints against AT&T, alleging that the carrier was violating government rules by restricting the way customers can use FaceTime, Apple’s video-conferencing tool, which is built into iPhones and iPads.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Groups Prepare to Fight AT&T Over FaceTime Restrictions', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPad', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Net Neutrality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telephones and Telecommunications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AT&T Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Communications Commission', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-18T15:18:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian X. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/12289628-7f97-544c-a71f-ef7dee27bcab', 'word_count': 363, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12289628-7f97-544c-a71f-ef7dee27bcab'}, {'abstract': 'Carl Hagelin of the Rangers is exploring playing for his hometown club in Sweden, SK Sodertalje, but he has not made a decision, his agent said Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/18/rangers-wing-considers-playing-in-sweden/', 'snippet': 'Carl Hagelin of the Rangers is exploring playing for his hometown club in Sweden, SK Sodertalje, but he has not made a decision, his agent said Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carl Hagelin of the Rangers is considering playing for his hometown club in Sweden, SK Sodertalje, but he still has not made a decision, his agent said Tuesday morning.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rangers Wing Considers Playing in Sweden', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hagelin, Carl', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-18T15:18:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ed4a8f9-fb1c-5346-a38e-0abdad3ec4fb', 'word_count': 395, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ed4a8f9-fb1c-5346-a38e-0abdad3ec4fb'}, {'abstract': 'The sumptuous hotels sprouting up near Unesco World Heritage sites.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/18/heritage-foundations/', 'snippet': 'The sumptuous hotels sprouting up near Unesco World Heritage sites.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hangaroa Eco Village & SpaEaster Island, a World Heritage site known for its ancient stone monoliths, has long been home to land disputes. In 2010, members of the Hito native clan staged a six-month occupation of Hangaroa, claiming the property had been taken from their ancestors illegally. Chilean police ended the protest, and now the hotel is open for business, with 75 rooms built of volcanic rock and a lobby that resembles a Polynesian canoe. The owners plan to donate funds to local charities. Doubles from $550; hangaroa.cl.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Heritage Foundations', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Heritage Foundations', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-18T15:19:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fred A. Bernstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fred', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Bernstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/08ca36fd-a0c1-5f8a-9f1e-f05a183f5260', 'word_count': 260, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08ca36fd-a0c1-5f8a-9f1e-f05a183f5260'}, {'abstract': 'Cruciferous vegetables make few appearances in North African tagines, but this dish is an appealing vehicle for nutritious cauliflower.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/20/health/nutrition/couscous-with-tomatoes-cauliflower-red-peppers-and-olives-recipes-for-health.html', 'snippet': 'Cruciferous vegetables make few appearances in North African tagines, but this dish is an appealing vehicle for nutritious cauliflower.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cauliflower is one of the few cruciferous vegetables you find in North African tagines. The spicy tagines make a good vehicle for this nutrient-rich food and are one of the few types of dishes in which cauliflower can be cooked until quite soft and not lose its appeal.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/health/nutrition/20recipehealth-pic/20recipehealth-pic-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 483, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/19/health/nutrition/20recipehealth-pic/20r