tackles what he sees as a deep strain of racism in the electorate.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/18/randy-newman-weighs-in-on-race-and-presidency-in-new-song/', 'snippet': 'In a new satirical song, Randy Newman tackles what he sees as a deep strain of racism in the electorate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You can always trust Randy Newman to talk about the elephant in the room. The award-winning songwriter, who supports President Obama, has weighed in on the role of race in the presidential election, releasing a satirical song on Tuesday poking fun at voters who long for the days when a white man was in the White House. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Randy Newman Weighs In on Race and Presidency in New Song', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Newman, Randy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Negro College Fund', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-18T17:50:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/80f94b8c-0769-5638-9157-55ef7469be39', 'word_count': 467, 'uri': 'nyt://article/80f94b8c-0769-5638-9157-55ef7469be39'}, {'abstract': 'Democrats now hold about a 70 percent chance of retaining control of the Senate, according to the new FiveThirtyEight forecast.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/18/fivethirtyeight-forecast-g-o-p-senate-hopes-slipping/', 'snippet': 'Democrats now hold about a 70 percent chance of retaining control of the Senate, according to the new FiveThirtyEight forecast.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Democrats are now favored to retain control of the Senate when the new Congress convenes in January, according to the FiveThirtyEight forecast, breaking a summer stalemate during which control of the chamber appeared about equally likely to go either way.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'FiveThirtyEight Forecast: G.O.P. Senate Hopes Slipping', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-18T17:50:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ceccc16-80bc-5aa6-ba0f-4cd97a88cc0b', 'word_count': 3208, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ceccc16-80bc-5aa6-ba0f-4cd97a88cc0b'}, {'abstract': 'The foreign ministers, led by Germany’s Guido Westerwelle, have called for a big increase in economic, political, diplomatic and even military integration within the European Union.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/19/world/europe/11-foreign-ministers-call-for-greater-european-union-integration.html', 'snippet': 'The foreign ministers, led by Germany’s Guido Westerwelle, have called for a big increase in economic, political, diplomatic and even military integration within the European Union.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Testing the theory that it often takes a crisis to bring Europeans together, 11 foreign ministers, led by Guido Westerwelle of Germany, have called for a big increase in economic, political, diplomatic and even military integration within the European Union.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Foreign Ministers Call for Stronger Ties Within Europe', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Foreign Ministers Call for Stronger Ties Within Europe', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Parliament', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Westerwelle, Guido', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Commission', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-18T17:59:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Castle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1700bada-c112-5927-a1d2-14fbb71a7183', 'word_count': 478, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1700bada-c112-5927-a1d2-14fbb71a7183'}, {'abstract': 'It’s an interesting market segment, a clear investment structure and the entrepreneur inspired confidence. I want to know more.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/18/pitching-an-employee-owned-assisted-living-facility/', 'snippet': 'It’s an interesting market segment, a clear investment structure and the entrepreneur inspired confidence. I want to know more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For our last pitch, I reviewed a bridal brokerage company focused on finding brides and grooms to take over abandoned weddings. This week, I review a pitch for an employee-owned assisted-living facility.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pitching an Employee-Owned Assisted Living Facility', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nursing Homes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Retirement Communities and Assisted Living', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-18T18:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Roth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6c01f08-2e7b-5969-aad8-c21bd7d24817', 'word_count': 476, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6c01f08-2e7b-5969-aad8-c21bd7d24817'}, {'abstract': 'Surveyors’ records from 1752 to 1889 give researchers a sense of what tree species dominated in a West Virginia forest before logging and farming got under way.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/18/the-witness-trees/', 'snippet': 'Surveyors’ records from 1752 to 1889 give researchers a sense of what tree species dominated in a West Virginia forest before logging and farming got under way.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Reaching into the past, Melissa Thomas-Van Gundy paints a vivid picture of a highlands forest dense with white oak, flaming sugar maple and American beeches, with a scattering of yellow poplar, wild cherry and spruce pine and, here and there, a singular crab apple, elm or soaring sycamore tree.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Witness Trees', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forests and Forestry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Logging Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trees and Shrubs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wilderness Areas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Monongahela River', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Virginia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-18T18:02:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emma Bryce', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emma', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bryce', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4501747e-f516-573d-93f5-14e7b4f40165', 'word_count': 610, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4501747e-f516-573d-93f5-14e7b4f40165'}, {'abstract': 'A 110-year-old brick building in the Brooklyn Navy Yard is home to Kings County Distillery, known for its minimalist flasks of bourbon and unaged moonshine.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/18/edible-selby-rise-and-shine/', 'snippet': 'A 110-year-old brick building in the Brooklyn Navy Yard is home to Kings County Distillery, known for its minimalist flasks of bourbon and unaged moonshine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When you grow up in a dry town in Kentucky, you develop a particular appreciation for moonshine. Or at least that was true for Colin Spoelman, the master distiller behind Kings County Distillery, which brews corn whiskeys in a 110-year-old brick building in the Brooklyn Navy Yard. “There were no liquor stores or bars,” Spoelman says of his hometown of Harlan. “People actually went to the bootlegger to buy alcohol.” Spoelman and his business partner, David Haskell, both 33, began making high-quality moonshine out of Spoelman’s apartment five years ago. Now their minimalist flasks of bourbon and unaged moonshine are poured at Roberta’s, Marlow & Sons and Il Buco, and sold at liquor stores all over New York City and beyond. “I think people appreciate our product in part because there isn’t marketing behind it,” Spoelman says. “Our strategy is not to have a strategy.” More…', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Edible Selby | Rise and Shine', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rise and Shine', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-18T18:05:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Todd Selby and Abby Aguirre', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Todd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Selby', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Abby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Aguirre', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f013de8f-4a39-56f3-8f89-c4c1f6cc3c1c', 'word_count': 146, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f013de8f-4a39-56f3-8f89-c4c1f6cc3c1c'}, {'abstract': 'Alan R. Mulally, chief executive of Ford, was joined in Times Square on Tuesday by Ryan Seacrest to mark the Ford Fusion Hybrid’s receiving a combined fuel-economy rating of 47 m.p.g.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/18/whats-in-a-number-for-the-ford-fusion-marketing-gold/', 'snippet': 'Alan R. Mulally, chief executive of Ford, was joined in Times Square on Tuesday by Ryan Seacrest to mark the Ford Fusion Hybrid’s receiving a combined fuel-economy rating of 47 m.p.g.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the rest of the country fixated on another 47 — or 46.4, if we’re splitting hairs — Ford created a blockwide buffer in Times Square on Tuesday where the number represented but one thing: a marketing opportunity.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s in a Number? For the Ford Fusion, Marketing Gold', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fuel Efficiency', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mulally, Alan R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Seacrest, Ryan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ford Motor Company', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Times Square and 42nd Street (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-18T18:08:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Schultz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schultz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9ab4995-5512-54d7-a568-d7e9dc97cff8', 'word_count': 571, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9ab4995-5512-54d7-a568-d7e9dc97cff8'}, {'abstract': 'In these activities, teachers and students can explore both the basic sequence of events unfolding in the Middle East and the far-reaching consequences, from the American presidential campaign to the decision-making of Internet companies like Google.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/18/how-an-internet-video-roiled-the-muslim-world/', 'snippet': 'In these activities, teachers and students can explore both the basic sequence of events unfolding in the Middle East and the far-reaching consequences, from the American presidential campaign to the decision-making of Internet companies like Goog...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Anti-American protests spread like wildfire last week throughout the Muslim world, raising profound questions about free speech, technology and the limits of diplomacy. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Uploading Trouble: Teaching About the Video that Roiled the Muslim World', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-18T18:17:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Marshall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Marshall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e6cee6f-7864-51b5-96b2-8c3747770ada', 'word_count': 1141, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e6cee6f-7864-51b5-96b2-8c3747770ada'}, {'abstract': 'Daniel Delaney, who served smoked brisket under the name Brisketlab at a series of pop-ups, is opening a counter-service restaurant.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/18/briskettown-to-open-in-williamsburg/', 'snippet': 'Daniel Delaney, who served smoked brisket under the name Brisketlab at a series of pop-ups, is opening a counter-service restaurant.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Daniel Delaney went from being the filmmaker to becoming the subject. A few years ago, he started doing videos of food trucks for a Web-based series called VendrTV, and became so hooked on barbecue, most notably Texas-style smoked brisket, that he is now part of the story. His camera is gathering dust while he hauls slabs of meat into an 18-foot smoker he acquired in Texas.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'BrisketTown to Open in Williamsburg', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Meat', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Delaney, Daniel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BrisketTown (Brooklyn, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Williamsburg (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-18T18:19:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97a28b23-691e-5c0b-b398-0a4003ec41b3', 'word_count': 252, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97a28b23-691e-5c0b-b398-0a4003ec41b3'}, {'abstract': 'Will those paying no federal income tax “vote for the president no matter what”? Probably not. A lot don’t vote, and of those who do, many vote Republican.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/18/how-do-the-47-vote/', 'snippet': 'Will those paying no federal income tax “vote for the president no matter what”? Probably not. A lot don’t vote, and of those who do, many vote Republican.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mitt Romney asserted that the 47 percent of Americans who had no federal income tax liability would “vote for the president no matter what.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Do the 47% Vote?', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-18T18:28:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/abc41352-c702-55c5-b42f-ea253b8c0c3c', 'word_count': 657, 'uri': 'nyt://article/abc41352-c702-55c5-b42f-ea253b8c0c3c'}, {'abstract': 'NBC got good news in the ratings for its new science-fiction show, aided by the lead-in of “The Voice,” but there is a history of such shows starting strong and then fading. “The Mob Doctor” on Fox had a rocky start.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/18/nbcs-revolution-is-fast-out-of-the-gate-but-will-its-audience-stay/', 'snippet': 'NBC got good news in the ratings for its new science-fiction show, aided by the lead-in of “The Voice,” but there is a history of such shows starting strong and then fading. “The Mob Doctor” on Fox had a rocky start.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Riding the lead-in from “The Voice,” the new NBC drama “Revolution” posted strong ratings for its debut on Monday night, scoring the best numbers for a drama premiere in three years.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'NBC’s ‘Revolution’ Is Fast Out of the Gate, but Will Its Audience Stay?', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ratings (Audience Measurement)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-18T18:43:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d772c547-40c1-5fd4-b1ec-70b6f3af2492', 'word_count': 247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d772c547-40c1-5fd4-b1ec-70b6f3af2492'}, {'abstract': 'Scenes from the London fashion week photo diary of Victor Frankowski.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/18/photos-of-the-moment-roksanda-ilincic-2/', 'snippet': 'Scenes from the London fashion week photo diary of Victor Frankowski.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Photos of The Moment | Roksanda Ilincic', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'London Fashion Week', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-18T18:45:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Victor Frankowski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Victor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Frankowski'