ltural plain near this tiny village, a two-hour drive south of Athens.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/business/global/19greeks/19greeks-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/19/business/global/19greeks/19greeks-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/business/global/19greeks/19greeks-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/business/global/19greeks/19greeks-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/business/global/19greeks/19greeks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/19/business/global/19greeks/19greeks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/business/global/19greeks/19greeks-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Euro or No, Economics of Everyday Greek Life Is Eroding', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Economics of Everyday Life Erode, Some Greeks See Little Hope', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-18T19:07:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Alderman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alderman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1928a942-8e23-5faa-bf9a-13563db8dec7', 'word_count': 1395, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1928a942-8e23-5faa-bf9a-13563db8dec7'}, {'abstract': 'A new column about gay and straight etiquette addresses a gay couple’s questions about the walk down the aisle and the first dance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/18/booming/18civilbehavior.html', 'snippet': 'A new column about gay and straight etiquette addresses a gay couple’s questions about the walk down the aisle and the first dance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Our new Civil Behavior advice column will be written by Steven Petrow, the author of “Steven Petrow’s Complete Gay & Lesbian Manners” (Workman, 2011) and the “The Essential Book of Gay Manners & Etiquette” (HarperCollins; 1995). Mr. Petrow will answer questions about issues of particular interest to lesbian, gay, bisexual and transgender people, as well their straight friends, co-workers and family members. The situations will be geared to a boomer-aged audience. This first column involves a wedding of gay men, the role of their parents and the question of who should have the first dance — the Moms and sons or Dads and sons. Mr. Petrow has written or edited more than a dozen books and covered the H.I.V./AIDS epidemic for more than 25 years. He started his career at The Wall Street Journal and has since held editorial positions at Life magazine, HotWired, Time Inc., Everyday Health and The Times’ Same Sex Marriage Topic page. He lives in Chapel Hill, N.C. —MICHAEL WINERIP', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/18/booming/18civilbehavior/18civilbehavior-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 250, 'width': 252, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/18/booming/18civilbehavior/18civilbehavior-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 250, 'width': 252, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/18/booming/18civilbehavior/18civilbehavior-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/18/booming/18civilbehavior/18civilbehavior-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/18/booming/18civilbehavior/18civilbehavior-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Making Parents Part of the Gay Wedding Day', 'kicker': 'Civil Behavior', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Wave of Staggering Loss, in a Country Unprepared', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Boomers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-18T19:11:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Booming', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Petrow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Petrow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a657aa8-6c93-5773-92ff-99152e59a1b0', 'word_count': 881, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a657aa8-6c93-5773-92ff-99152e59a1b0'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney said privately in May that “there’s just no way” for an independent Palestinian state to be established on the West Bank territory Israel has occupied since 1967.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/18/mitt-romneys-no-state-solution/', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney said privately in May that “there’s just no way” for an independent Palestinian state to be established on the West Bank territory Israel has occupied since 1967.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 5:50 p.m. As my colleague Sarah Wheaton reports, Mitt Romney said privately in May that “there’s just no way” for an independent Palestinian state to be established on the West Bank territory Israel has occupied since 1967. The Republican presidential candidate’s comments, during a discussion with donors in Florida, were secretly recorded by someone at the private event, and published on Tuesday by Mother Jones, a liberal magazine. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mitt Romney’s No-State Solution', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Said, Edward W', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'van Creveld, Martin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Bank', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-18T19:11:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f95c9ea2-4ca6-57d7-926d-c4fa1c77c880', 'word_count': 1679, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f95c9ea2-4ca6-57d7-926d-c4fa1c77c880'}, {'abstract': 'The Kremlin views American financial support for a wide range of civil society programs as thinly veiled meddling in the country’s internal affairs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/19/world/europe/russia-demands-us-end-pro-democracy-work.html', 'snippet': 'The Kremlin views American financial support for a wide range of civil society programs as thinly veiled meddling in the country’s internal affairs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — Russia has ordered the United States to end its financial support for a wide range of pro-democracy, public health and other civil society programs here, in an aggressive step by the Kremlin to halt what it views as American meddling in its internal affairs. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/world/JP-RUSSIA/JP-RUSSIA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/19/world/JP-RUSSIA/JP-RUSSIA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/world/JP-RUSSIA/JP-RUSSIA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images