': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Olsen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/dc276136-31de-5d69-901d-687cb4ed6c02', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/dc276136-31de-5d69-901d-687cb4ed6c02'}, {'abstract': 'A newly released survey of Americans’ attitudes toward Hispanics says prejudice against the country’s fastest-growing minority is perpetuated by negative media portrayals.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/18/media-feed-bias-against-latinos/', 'snippet': 'A newly released survey of Americans’ attitudes toward Hispanics says prejudice against the country’s fastest-growing minority is perpetuated by negative media portrayals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW YORK — As I write in my latest Female Factor column, Barack Obama and Mitt Romney are making big moves in the final stretch of the presidential campaign to recruit and win over Hispanics. At the same time, a new national study shows that a large number of Americans, influenced by negative images in the media, take a dim view of Hispanics.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Media Feed Bias Against Latinos', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-18T19:28:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Luisita Lopez Torregrosa', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Luisita', 'middlename': 'Lopez', 'lastname': 'Torregrosa', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72fcac06-1c0c-5e21-a3db-dde78e3b0827', 'word_count': 846, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72fcac06-1c0c-5e21-a3db-dde78e3b0827'}, {'abstract': 'Jean-Georges Vongerichten’s recipe for fried cakes of sushi-style rice topped with chipotle mayonnaise and raw scallop may just be a contender for “best of the year.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/19/dining/excellence-on-the-plate-even-without-a-chefs-edge.html', 'snippet': 'Jean-Georges Vongerichten’s recipe for fried cakes of sushi-style rice topped with chipotle mayonnaise and raw scallop may just be a contender for “best of the year.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'IF you’re a chef — a great one — you will go to almost any length to gain marginal improvement in a recipe. You’ll find the best provider for every given ingredient, and if you can gain an edge by fussing with those ingredients, you will. (Chances are you’re not the one doing the work anyway.) These kinds of differences define the food of the most talented chefs, at least those successful enough to indulge their talents.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/dining/19BITTMAN_SPAN/19BITTMAN_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/19/dining/19BITTMAN_SPAN/19BITTMAN_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/dining/19BITTMAN_SPAN/19BITTMAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/dining/19BITTMAN_SPAN/19BITTMAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type':