r relationship on the series with Josh Charles and turning 60 as a working performer.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/18/emmys-watch-christine-baranski-on-the-good-wife-and-competing-with-maggie-smith/', 'snippet': 'Christine Baranski, nominated for an Emmy for best supporting actress in a drama for “The Good Wife,” talks about the role, her relationship on the series with Josh Charles and turning 60 as a working performer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We will be talking to Emmy nominees leading up to the awards show on Sunday night. Previous entries in this series include Don Roy King, the director of “Saturday Night Live,” and Abi Morgan, nominated for writing “The Hour.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Emmys Watch: Christine Baranski on ‘The Good Wife’ and Competing With Maggie Smith', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Charles, Josh (1971- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chenoweth, Kristin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cumming, Alan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Michelle (Screenwriter)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Robert (Screenwriter)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lane, Nathan', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McNally, Terrence', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morgan, Abi', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Patinkin, Mandy', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shattuck, Kathryn', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Maggie', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sondheim, Stephen', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corporation', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-18T20:28:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b53b1e88-6035-515b-9152-8113b0bef849', 'word_count': 1061, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b53b1e88-6035-515b-9152-8113b0bef849'}, {'abstract': 'September’s back-to-school time — and for many adults, it’s also back-to-the-bar time. What’s your favorite end-of-summer drink?', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/18/feeling-rummy-in-a-good-way/', 'snippet': 'September’s back-to-school time — and for many adults, it’s also back-to-the-bar time. What’s your favorite end-of-summer drink?', 'lead_paragraph': 'September is back-to-school time — and for many adults, it’s also back-to-the-bar time. The last two weeks of August felt a little sleepy at the small bar where I work. But a few days ago, I had a busy, cheerful shift and felt happily back to business. Local teachers who’d been out of the neighborhood all summer were back in force, regulars who’d been lucky enough to take long vacations had returned, old friends who hadn’t stopped by for months came in to catch up over a few pints. And I sensed a subtle summer’s-over — effectively, if not calendrically — shift in my customers’ drink orders. Just a few weeks ago, I was shaking up margaritas and pouring crisp, bright cider over ice. Last week, even though it was sunny and warm, there was a greater call for darker beers and brown liquor.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/18/magazine/18-dark-rum/18-dark-rum-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/18/magazine/18-dark-rum/18-dark-rum-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1638, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/18/magazine/18-dark-rum/18-dark-rum-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/18/magazine/18-dark-rum/18-dark-rum-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/18/magazine/18-dark-rum/18-dark-rum-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Feeling Rummy (in a Good Way)', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALCOHOLIC BEVERAGES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rum', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-18T20:29:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rosie Schaap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rosie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schaap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/13f1e399-9141-5a5b-b5c1-e8d68f4c99e2', 'word_count': 368, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13f1e399-9141-5a5b-b5c1-e8d68f4c99e2'}, {'abstract': 'Whether you’re a casual user or you like to stay constantly connected, here are tips for using a smartphone overseas without going broke.', 'web_url': 'https://frugaltraveler.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/18/how-to-avoid-a-smartphones-bite/', 'snippet': 'Whether you’re a casual user or you like to stay constantly connected, here are tips for using a smartphone overseas without going broke.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Travel and smartphones go together — and these days, texting, updating Facebook and good old tweeting-while-eating are the least of it. Instant access to Yelp, TripAdvisor and endless other apps helps with everything from choosing an entree, tracking down discounts, posting a photo and checking the traffic ahead. Add a healthy dose of old-fashioned phone calls from poolside or mountain trail, and you might say staying connected has become something close to a constitutional right.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/travel/23FRUGAL/23FRUGAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 559, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/23/travel/23FRUGAL/23FRUGAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 559}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/travel/23FRUGAL/23FRUGAL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 947, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/travel/23FRUGAL/23FRUGAL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1894, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/travel/23FRUGAL/23FRUGAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/23/trav