e': 'London Fashion Week', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-18T22:01:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roberta Ridolfi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roberta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ridolfi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b54dc9f6-f69e-5ae2-904a-0788fe20d6ef', 'word_count': 36, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b54dc9f6-f69e-5ae2-904a-0788fe20d6ef'}, {'abstract': 'The Lyon Dance Biennial unfolds under the new leadership of the choreographer Dominique Hervieu.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/19/arts/dance/dominique-hervieu-leads-her-first-lyon-dance-biennial.html', 'snippet': 'The Lyon Dance Biennial unfolds under the new leadership of the choreographer Dominique Hervieu.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LYON, France — Every two years for the last 28 years the Lyon Dance Biennial has arrived in mid-September in this busy, bustling city with a certain amount of fanfare. It begins with the Défilé, a carnival-like procession that regularly draws more than 300,000 revelers to the streets, and continues for around three weeks with a dense pileup of performances, public balls, meetings with artists, films and talks, which seem to use every one of Lyon’s 30-odd theaters.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/arts/19biennial1/19biennial1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/19/arts/19biennial1/19biennial1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/arts/19biennial1/19biennial1-jum