p Over Ad in Kentucky House Race Featuring Executive Dressed as Miner', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Role-Playing TV Ad Stirs Up a Kentucky Race', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mines and Mining', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kentucky', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-18T22:58:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Eligon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eligon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/76a53dd2-65f6-5dae-b10b-7e90088beeb1', 'word_count': 626, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76a53dd2-65f6-5dae-b10b-7e90088beeb1'}, {'abstract': 'Goldman Sachs has made an effort to heal self-inflicted wounds and maintain its dominance in investment banking.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/09/18/behind-goldman-sachss-success-is-a-focus-on-survival/', 'snippet': 'Goldman Sachs has made an effort to heal self-inflicted wounds and maintain its dominance in investment banking.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It wasn’t long ago that Goldman Sachs was painted as an outsize villain of the financial crisis, and its future seemed hazy. Today, however, Goldman Sachs has retained its clients and its dominance. And recent missteps by its competitors are putting the investment bank in pole position to profit when a recovery comes.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Behind Goldman Sachs’s Success Is a Focus on Survival', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_head