19/opinion/romney-takes-on-47-of-america.html', 'snippet': 'Readers respond to news and opinion articles about the Mitt Romney video.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney Takes On 47% of America', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Romney Takes On 47% of America', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T00:43:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/11b62f32-0558-50cb-ac27-ac747d871f78', 'word_count': 752, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11b62f32-0558-50cb-ac27-ac747d871f78'}, {'abstract': 'The singer Tony Bennett, his wife, Susan Benedetto, and the Milton S. Eisenhower Foundation respond to a column by Joe Nocera.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/19/opinion/helping-disadvantaged-children-build-character.html', 'snippet': 'The singer Tony Bennett, his wife, Susan Benedetto, and the Milton S. Eisenhower Foundation respond to a column by Joe Nocera.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Helping Disadvantaged Children Build Character', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Helping Disadvantaged Children Build Character', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T00:43:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/40697294-71f2-5736-bac5-c0f0b3c13f90', 'word_count': 422, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40697294-71f2-5736-bac5-c0f0b3c13f90'}, {'abstract': 'Congress has decided politicking and vacationing is more important than getting the people’s work done.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/19/opinion/congress-chooses-recess-over-work.html', 'snippet': 'Congress has decided politicking and vacationing is more important than getting the people’s work done.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After a five-week recess and the hard labor of political conventioneering, members of the House managed to stop briefly at the Capitol last week to enact a temporary budget to avoid a government shutdown. But, after Friday, they will be back home politicking nonstop until Election Day, and the Senate is also expected to cancel its scheduled October duties in Washington. Lawmakers call their latest hiatus from the job of legislating “an extended district work period,” but it will be spent mostly bragging to voters about imaginary accomplishments. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hello, We Must Be Going', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hello, We Must Be Going', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T00:43:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/45bf020b-fda6-5cfc-9176-ec650496fab5', 'word_count': 412, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45bf020b-fda6-5cfc-9176-ec650496fab5'}, {'abstract': 'A letter printed in a Church of St. Catherine of Siena bulletin endorsed Mitt Romney for president, prompting a complaint with the I.R.S. and a petition with more than 20,000 signatures.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/19/nyregion/romney-endorsement-in-church-bulletin-raises-outcry.html', 'snippet': 'A letter printed in a Church of St. Catherine of Siena bulletin endorsed Mitt Romney for president, prompting a complaint with the I.R.S. and a petition with more than 20,000 signatures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two weeks ago, the weekly bulletin at the Church of St. Catherine of Siena on the Upper East Side of Manhattan carried a blunt political message from a priest on the parish staff.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Priest’s Dip Into Politics Raises Outcry', 'kicker': 'About New York', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Priest’s Dip Into Politics Raises Outcry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion-State Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endorsements', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Upper East Side (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T00:57:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Dwyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename