mbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/business/JP-ADCO-1/JP-ADCO-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 628, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/business/JP-ADCO-1/JP-ADCO-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1257, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/business/JP-ADCO-1/JP-ADCO-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/19/business/JP-ADCO-1/JP-ADCO-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/business/JP-ADCO-1/JP-ADCO-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Samsung-Apple Fight Moves to Marketing', 'kicker': 'Advertising', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Samsung-Apple Fight Moves to Marketing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Samsung Group', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T01:01:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tanzina Vega and Brian X. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tanzina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vega', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3939676-a38a-5418-a52d-73a819a7e77e', 'word_count': 1106, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3939676-a38a-5418-a52d-73a819a7e77e'}, {'abstract': 'A tribunal in London ruled that letters written by Prince Charles lobbying government ministers on a range of contentious political issues must be made public within a month.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/19/world/europe/britain-prince-charles-loses-ruling-on-letters.html', 'snippet': 'A tribunal in London ruled that letters written by Prince Charles lobbying government ministers on a range of contentious political issues must be made public within a month.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A freedom-of-information tribunal in London ruled Tuesday that letters written by Prince Charles lobbying government ministers on a range of contentious political issues must be made public within a month. The ruling was a victory for The Guardian, the newspaper that led a seven-year campaign for the release of letters that the prince, who is heir to the throne, had written to seven government departments. The letters, known as “black spider memos” among the ministers who received them because of the prince’s handwriting, have prompted widespread criticism from politicians and constitutional experts, who have accused Prince Charles, 63, of breaching the longstanding convention that members of the royal family should not intervene on matters of government policy. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Britain: Prince Loses Ruling on Letters', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Britain: Prince Loses Ruling on Letters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value':