', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/15730949-5e41-518a-9e24-08b4eebd02b9', 'word_count': 825, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15730949-5e41-518a-9e24-08b4eebd02b9'}, {'abstract': 'Andy Pettitte, who sustained a broken ankle in June, will pitch the first game of a doubleheader for the Yankees on Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/19/sports/baseball/yankees-rainout-delays-pettittes-return.html', 'snippet': 'Andy Pettitte, who sustained a broken ankle in June, will pitch the first game of a doubleheader for the Yankees on Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The postponement of the Yankees’ game Tuesday against Toronto at Yankee Stadium forced Andy Pettitte to wait one more day in his comeback from a broken bone in his left ankle, but it also afforded Derek Jeter another day to rest the bone bruise in his left ankle.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Postponement Forces Pettitte to Wait a Day', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Postponement Forces Pettitte To Wait a Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toronto Blue Jays', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pettitte, Andy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T01:29:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ecb4154d-a8bf-5589-aff9-35b02e4ea6d4', 'word_count': 185, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ecb4154d-a8bf-5589-aff9-35b02e4ea6d4'}, {'abstract': 'The 112th Congress, soon to depart for its election recess, is set to enter the record books as the least productive body in a generation, passing a mere 173 public laws as of last month.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/19/us/politics/congress-nears-end-of-least-productive-session.html', 'snippet': 'The 112th Congress, soon to depart for its election recess, is set to enter the record books as the least productive body in a generation, passing a mere 173 public laws as of last month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Members of Congress feel mighty proud of themselves this week, mainly because they appear to be avoiding a government shutdown — an outcome taken as an actual accomplishment in this turbulent and acrimonious legislature. But by the end of this week, lawmakers plan to leave town and not return until after the election, leaving behind a staggering pile of bills, many of pressing importance to voters across the nation. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/us/CONGRESS-1/CONGRESS-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 901, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/us/CONGRESS-1/CONGRESS-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1701, 'width': 1933, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/0