: 'nyt://article/860fd477-d4fb-5447-a9b8-927158173db5'}, {'abstract': 'The Mets are on pace to set a record for the lowest home-field winning percentage after the All-Star break. The old mark? It was set by the ’79 Mets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/19/sports/baseball/in-race-to-bottom-its-mets-vs-mets.html', 'snippet': 'The Mets are on pace to set a record for the lowest home-field winning percentage after the All-Star break. The old mark? It was set by the ’79 Mets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rain postponed the Mets’ game Tuesday night at Citi Field, providing a break in a mind-boggling stretch of home-field ineptitude that could, by season’s end, earn them an embarrassing entry in the record books. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/sports/METS/METS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 830, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/sports/METS/METS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1660, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Race to Bottom, It’s Mets vs. Mets', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Race to Bottom, It’s Mets vs. Mets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T02:13:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Keh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/43250d79-9091-567e-bd84-d8dfe817ea20', 'word_count': 622, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43250d79-9091-567e-bd84-d8dfe817ea20'}, {'abstract': 'JAL’s offering caps two years of intense reorganization that eliminated 21,000 jobs, or about a third of the airline’s work force, and cut pilots’ salaries by 30 percent.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/09/18/big-stock-offering-by-japan-airlines-is-overshadowed-by-chinas-anti-japanese-protests/', 'snippet': 'JAL’s offering caps two years of intense reorganization that eliminated 21,000 jobs, or about a third of the airline’s work force, and cut pilots’ salaries by 30 percent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — Japan Airlines made a lackluster return to the stock market Wednesday after the biggest initial public offering this year since Facebook, its share price weighed down by investor jitters over the airline’s prospects in a cutthroat industry, as well as anti-Japanese protests in China that threaten travel between the two countries.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China’s Anti-Japanese Protests Overshadow Japan Airlines I.P.O.', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Big Stock Offering by Japan Airlines Is Overshadowed by China’s Anti-Japanese Protests', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Japan Airlines', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T02:19:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hiroko Tabuchi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hiroko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tabuchi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f6a3de6-abde-5ff2-94d7-9bd6b7263e25', 'word_count': 1139, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f6a3de6-abde-5ff2-94d7-9bd6b7263e25'}, {'abstract': 'What does it say about our culture that the people funding presidential campaigns seem to regard their downscale fellow countrymen as a kind of alien race?', 'web_url': 'https://campaignstops.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/18/douthat-our-revolting-elites/', 'snippet': 'What does it say about our culture that the people funding presidential campaigns seem to regard their downscale fellow countrymen as a kind of alien race?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Were Mitt Romney’s now-famous comments at a fundraising dinner in May — in which he appeared to write off 47 percent of Americans as self-pitying freeloaders with no self-respect — a window into the elusive “real Romney” and proof that his moderate-seeming façade has always been a sham?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Our Revolting Elites', 'kicker': 'Campaign Stops', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T02:20:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/958c2252-271e-5177-8d1f-ebe5a2d88e1a', 'word_count': 827, 'uri': 'nyt://article/958c2252-271e-5177-8d1f-ebe5a2d88e1a'}, {'abstract': 'Which starting pitcher would get the call if the Yankees faced a wild-card game and survival?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/19/sports/baseball/early-polls-point-to-andy-pettitte-as-yankees-go-to-pitcher.html', 'snippet': 'Which starting pitcher would get the call if the Yankees faced a wild-card game and survival?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In an election season of interminable polling, it would be interesting to pose a multiple-choice question exclusively to increasingly edgy Yankees fans: for one wild-card game of suspense and survival, which starter would be most comforting, if only under these presumed conditions?', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/sports/19araton/19araton-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 699, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/sports/19araton/19araton-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1398, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/sports/19araton/19araton-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/19/sports/19araton/19araton-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/sports/19araton/19araton-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Early Polls Point to Pettitte as Yankees’ Go-To Pitcher', 'kicker': 'On Baseball', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Early Polls Point to Pettitte As Yankees’ Go-To Pitcher', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pettitte, Andy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sabathia, C C', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T02:23:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Araton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Araton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9863fd22-189c-512c-9f9a-6c60c07cbb23', 'word_count': 964, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9863fd22-189c-512c-9f9a-6c60c07cbb23'}, {'abstract': 'The money helped carry Mitt Romney through the Republican convention, when he was formally nominated and could tap into tens of millions of dollars in general election funds.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/18/romney-campaign-borrowed-20-million-to-get-through-convention/', 'snippet': 'The money helped carry Mitt Romney through the Republican convention, when he was formally nominated and could tap into tens of millions of dollars in general election funds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mitt Romney borrowed $20 million for his presidential campaign in August, a campaign official said on Tuesday, money that helped carry Mr. Romney through the Republican convention until he could tap into tens of millions of dollars in general election money his campaign raised.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney Campaign Borrowed $20 Million to Get Through Convention', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican National Committee', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T02:23:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Confessore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Confessore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3cbb4058-ac20-5896-a297-2723e0f23d4d', 'word_count': 353, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3cbb4058-ac20-5896-a297-2723e0f23d4d'}, {'abstract': 'Prison officials are under suspicion after the inmates escaped through a tunnel in Piedras Negras.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/19/world/americas/131-prisoners-tunnel-out-of-mexico-jail.html', 'snippet': 'Prison officials are under suspicion after the inmates escaped through a tunnel in Piedras Negras.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MEXICO CITY — The inmates were massed in the prison carpentry workshop when somebody gave the signal. Wedging themselves into a tunnel almost 10 feet below ground, 131 prisoners slid one by one along 23 feet to emerge at the base of the north watchtower. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/global-home/19mexico-image/19mexico-image-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/global-home/19mexi