 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Tax Comments, Romney Wades Into a Conservative Rift', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Much of Romney’s View on Taxes Conflicts With Longtime G.O.P. Stand', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brooks, Arthur C', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservatism (US Politics)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T02:34:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annie Lowrey and Michael Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lowrey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e085992-5945-54a4-909a-febe8fd059e1', 'word_count': 1173, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e085992-5945-54a4-909a-febe8fd059e1'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney’s views on the Middle East and Iran may have already been well known, but comments of his that were captured on video at a fund-raiser could bring difficulties if he wins the presidency.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/19/us/politics/mideast-comments-could-vex-a-romney-administration.html', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney’s views on the Middle East and Iran may have already been well known, but comments of his that were captured on video at a fund-raiser could bring difficulties if he wins the presidency.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON — No one has ever had any illusions about where Mitt Romney stands on the two hottest disputes in the Middle East: the argument over the creation of a Palestinian state, and the debate over what can be done to assure that Iran does not get a nuclear weapon. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Middle East Comments Could Vex a Romney Administration', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Comments Could Vex a Romney Administration', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T02:35:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By David E. Sanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Sanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5af3c768-70a3-5688-89ad-a4daa2928c3d', 'word_count': 867, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5af3c768-70a3-5688-89ad-a4daa2928c3d'}, {'abstract': 'The attack in Benghazi has set off a new debate in Washington and across the Middle East about whether Al Qaeda has been reinvigorated or lives on as a useful boogeyman.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/19/world/africa/questions-about-al-qaedas-potency-follow-libya-attack.html', 'snippet': 'The attack in Benghazi has set off a new debate in Washington and across the Middle East about whether Al Qaeda has been reinvigorated or lives on as a useful boogeyman.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The attack on the United States mission in Benghazi, Libya, that killed Ambassador J. Christopher Stevens has set off a new debate here and across the Middle East about whether Al Qaeda has been reinvigorated amid the chaos of the Arab Spring or instead merely lives on as a kind of useful boogeyman, scapegoat or foil.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Libya, Renewed Questions About the Potency of Al Qaeda', 'kicker': 'Memo From Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Libya, Renewed Questions About the Potency of Al Qaeda', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stevens, J Christopher', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T02:49:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Schmitt and David D. Kirkpatrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmitt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d97560c5-e014-5c30-9e05-0ebbd69e7fb1', 'word_count': 1064, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d97560c5-e014-5c30-9e05-0ebbd69e7fb1'}, {'abstract': 'Instead of projecting calm, the schools reflected what had happened in the rest of the country during the summer: the fighting had grown worse and the routines of daily life more dangerous.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/19/world/middleeast/syria-orders-schools-to-open-but-classes-give-way-to-war.html', 'snippet': 'Instead of projecting calm, the schools reflected what had happened in the rest of the country during the summer: the fighting had grown worse and the routines of daily life more dangerous.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DAMASCUS, Syria — At one Syrian school, in the Damascus suburbs, students were so scarce this week that teachers spent most of the last few days sitting around and drinking tea.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/world/SYRIA-1/SYRIA-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/19/world/SYRIA-1/SYRIA-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/world/SYRIA-1/SYRIA-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/world/SYRIA-1/SYRIA-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/world/SYRIA-1/SYRIA-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/19