imes', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/booming/19history/19history-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 326, 'width': 335, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/booming/19history/19history-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 326, 'width': 335, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/booming/19history/19history-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/19/booming/19history/19history-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/booming/19history/19history-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Can Turn the World On With Her Smile?', 'kicker': 'Remember This', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Boomers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T09:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Booming', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Winerip', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Winerip', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/52e342e8-0d11-5563-9845-a77a5338d982', 'word_count': 128, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52e342e8-0d11-5563-9845-a77a5338d982'}, {'abstract': 'A sexual drought that is far from the bounty of youth has many reasons. Desire isn’t one of them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/19/booming/19wadler.html', 'snippet': 'A sexual drought that is far from the bounty of youth has many reasons. Desire isn’t one of them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I am single, and therefore I spend a lot of time thinking about sex, which is very different than it was 40 years ago when I was in my 20s and spent a lot of time having sex. You have no doubt heard this before, but in the ‘70s there was a tremendous amount of sex to be had in New York; it was the way it was when they talk about the oysters in the harbor, all you had to do was put out a hand and scoop it up: Hello there, lady, I just saw you walking down the street, would you like to have sex? No thank you, Gallant Gent, I have to organize my sock drawer, which will certainly take an hour, and by that time you will have given three women herpes, the worst sexually transmitted disease Greenwich Village has ever known, may science soon find a cure.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/booming/19wadler/19wadler-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/19/booming/19wadler/19wadler-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/booming/19wadler/19wadler-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 601, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/booming/19wadler/19wadler-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1203, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/booming/19wadler/19wadler-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/19/booming/19wadler/19wadler-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/booming/19wadler/19wadler-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sex in the 60s', 'kicker': 'I Was Misinformed', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Boomers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T09:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Booming', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joyce Wadler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joyce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wadler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/707d41cf-1622-530d-864f-eedd623cea9c', 'word_count': 1014, 'uri': 'nyt://article/707d41cf-1622-530d-864f-eedd623cea9c'}, {'abstract': 'Malcolm X was keenly aware of the power of images to transform the 20th century.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/19/malcolm-x-as-visual-strategist/', 'snippet': 'Malcolm X was keenly aware of the power of images to transform the 20th century.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Robert L. Flora’s black-and-white portrait of Malcolm X, the national spokesman for the Nation of Islam, stands as one of the great meta-images about photography — an astute commentary on our insatiable hunger for pictures. Taken in Los Angeles in May 1963, the photo depicts the civil rights leader and his associates as they await the verdict of an all-white jury deliberating the fate of 14 Black Muslims accused of assaulting police officers. The pictorial magazines and tabloid newspapers they voraciously read to pass the time nearly crowd out the image.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Malcolm X as Visual Strategist', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Malcolm X', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T09:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maurice Berger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maurice', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Berger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/256fb58c-76da-57ae-9b2d-93ddf30bff14', 'word_count': 1170, 'uri': 'nyt://article/256fb58c-76da-57ae-9b2d-93ddf30bff14'}, {'abstract': 'Should student evaluations should be used by administrators, along with other data, to make decisions about teacher salary and job tenure?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/19/should-students-be-able-to-grade-their-teachers/', 'snippet': 'Should student evaluations should be used by administrators, along with other data, to make decisions about teacher salary and job tenure?', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Wednesday students in Chicago public schools returned to classes after missing more than a week of school because their teachers were on strike. One of the questions at the heart of the strike: How should teachers be evaluated? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Should Students Be Able to Grade Their Teachers?', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T09:09:09+0000', '