onator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/19/a-digital-tool-to-unlock-learning/', 'snippet': 'PowerMyLearning, a program that any student, parent or teacher can use for free, helps students take ownership of their learning.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When we think about education reform, we usually focus on teacher quality. The big battleground in education revolves around holding teachers accountable for their performance. With all the focus on teachers, however, one group that is often forgotten as a key learning resource are the students themselves.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Digital Tool to Unlock Learning', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Learning', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'WASHINGTON HEIGHTS (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T12:00:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Bornstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bornstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0bcb1130-401a-50bb-bc14-28cccdec8bf7', 'word_count': 1885, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0bcb1130-401a-50bb-bc14-28cccdec8bf7'}, {'abstract': 'Metropolitan Diary: The rehearsal by a group of 8-year-olds for a musical goes well, but a mother is surprised at the man filling in at the keyboard.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/19/a-sub-at-the-piano/', 'snippet': 'Metropolitan Diary: The rehearsal by a group of 8-year-olds for a musical goes well, but a mother is surprised at the man filling in at the keyboard.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dear Diary:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'mul