e reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Amateur Gourmet: Communal tables: not really as cool as they’re supposed to be. — Jeff Gordinier ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T13:38:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e58400c5-f058-508d-8dc8-dfd05ed35250', 'word_count': 500, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e58400c5-f058-508d-8dc8-dfd05ed35250'}, {'abstract': 'Goldman Sachs may be readying the next generation of leaders. | Apple closed above $700 a share for the first time. | The new 1,004-foot tower known as One57, in Midtown Manhattan, may be the new haven for billionaires.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/09/19/the-next-generation-at-goldman/', 'snippet': 'Goldman Sachs may be readying the next generation of leaders. | Apple closed above $700 a share for the first time. | The new 1,004-foot tower known as One57, in Midtown Manhattan, may be the new haven for billionaires.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Next Generation at Goldman \xa0|\xa0 Goldman Sachs is passing the torch to the next generation, as the investment bank announced that the longtime chief financial officer, David A. Viniar, would retire in January and Harvey M. Schwartz would take over.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Next Generation at Goldman', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T13:43:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/79e8803e-80f3-53aa-8623-75ab88cf2ac9', 'word_count': 2040, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79e8803e-80f3-53aa-8623-75ab88cf2ac9'}, {'abstract': 'Also, a French magazine is ordered to stop publishing Kate Middleton photos; and after losing to Apple in court Samsung goes after it in print.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/19/the-breakfast-meeting-more-47-percent-fallout-and-a-diller-rudin-e-book-venture/', 'snippet': 'Also, a French magazine is ordered to stop publishing Kate Middleton photos; and after losing to Apple in court Samsung goes after it in print.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The now-infamous 47 percent video – secretly taped at a Mitt Romney donor event in May – is still reverberating in media circles as well as political ones.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: More 47 Percent Fallout and a Diller-Rudin E-Book Venture', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Online Advertising', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'AGUILERA, CHRISTINA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carter, Jimmy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Diller, Barry', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Green, Cee Lo', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rudin, Scott', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sabol, Steve', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shakira', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Atavist Inc', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Charlie Hebdo', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'FunnyOrDie.com', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gizmodo', 'rank': 18, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mother Jones', 'rank': 19, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NFL Films', 'rank': 20, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Samsung Group', 'rank': 21, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T13:51:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editors', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editors'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7c7590b-90b9-5efb-90cb-b3d0a624d7d1', 'word_count': 472, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7c7590b-90b9-5efb-90cb-b3d0a624d7d1'}, {'abstract': 'From Maine to North Carolina, ocean temperatures off the East Coast in the first six months of this year were the hottest ever recorded.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/19/on-our-radar-warm-eastern-waters/', 'snippet': 'From Maine to North Carolina, ocean temperatures off the East Coast in the first six months of this year were the hottest ever recorded.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sea surface temperatures off the East Coast from North Carolina to the Gulf of Maine in the first six months of 2012 were the hottest ever recorded, NOAA reports. Above-average temperatures were found from the sea surface to the ocean bottom and out beyond the Gulf Stream, the agency says. [Mother Jones]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Our Radar: Warm Eastern Waters', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T13:54:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ef740bb-ca7b-5516-a679-f7299aa669fb', 'word_count': 222, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ef740bb-ca7b-5516-a679-f7299aa669fb'}, {'abstract': 'The first thing you notice about Rae Morris is her voice, something the 20-year-old singer from Blackpool, England, is just getting used to.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/19/timely-melody-maker/', 'snippet': 'The first thing you notice about Rae Morris is her voice, something the 20-year-old singer from Blackpool, England, is just getting used to.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first thing you notice about Rae Morris is her voice, something the 20-year-old singer from Blackpool, England, is just getting used to. “I only started singing two years ago,” she says from Los Angeles, where she is interviewing producers for her first album. “I was always the girl at school with the not-cool croaky voice.” Once she started writing songs, singing (while playing the piano) came easily, and she racked up some 200 live shows in a year. (Her parents drove her to almost every one.) And after signing to Atlantic Records and gaining Christopher Bailey’s endorsement as one of the Burberry Acoustic musicians, she now finds herself a long way from home, in a studio in the Hollywood Hills. “Can’t believe I’m here, to be honest. I keep having to pinch myself,” she says. “You don’t get this weather in Blackpool, that’s for sure.” ', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '122', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Timely | Melody Maker', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Melody Maker', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T14:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jacob Brown', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jacob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brown', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3991a136-c239-53f2-bf3b-8e17b4ce56cf', 'word_count': 165, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3991a136-c239-53f2-bf3b-8e17b4ce56cf'}, {'abstract': 'Opposition and allies in the governing coalition react to Ms. Banerjee’s decision to withdraw support.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/19/what-they-said-mamata-banerjee-pulling-out-of-the-upa/', 'snippet': 'Opposition and allies in the governing coalition react to Ms. Banerjee’s decision to withdraw support.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The regional party of Mamata Banerjee, the maverick leader of West Bengal who has threatened to pull out of the governing coalition, raised even more pressure on the national government by demanding the resignation of Prime Minister Manmohan Singh on Wednesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What They Said: Mamata Banerjee Pulling Out of the UPA', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Banerjee, Mamata', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'All India Trinamool Congress', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indian National Congress', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T14:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sruthi Gottipati', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sruthi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gottipati', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/547e68ad-b019-52cd-ba22-f2defe75d9b5', 'word_count': 338, 'uri': 'nyt://article/547e68ad-b019-52cd-ba22-f2defe75d9b5'}, {'abstract': 'The requirement is in jeopardy–and that’s a good thing.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/19/pennsylvanias-voter-id-law/', 'snippet': 'The requirement is in jeopardy–and that’s a good thing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In August, a Pennsylvania Commonwealth Court judge upheld the state’s new voter ID law—despite the fact that state officials presented no evidence of in-person voter fraud, and didn’t even try to claim that voter fraud would likely occur this November in the absence of an ID requirement.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pennsylvania’s Voter ID Law', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Turzai, Mike', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T14:06:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fcaa3e4f-4eaa-5f53-afc0-1473c0776461', 'word_count': 316, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fcaa3e4f-4eaa-5f53-afc0-1473c0776461'}, {'abstract': 'New consumer devices can monitor everything from kilocalories to REM sleep. Have you tried any gadgetry to measure your sleep, and did it help?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/19/gadgets-to-help-new-parents-sleep/', 'snippet': 'New consumer devices can monitor everything from kilocalories to REM sleep. Have you tried any gadgetry to measure your sleep, and did it help?', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you’re a new or young parent, you probably already know that your sleep is disrupted. But when\xa0Emily Waltz, a new mother,\xa0 realized her sleep was still poor even after her young son learned to sleep through the night, she wired herself up to a series of new consumer devices designed to measure everything from her REM sleep to the number of kilocalories she was burning daily, and wrote about it for the Web site of the Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers\xa0 (IEEE), a professional association for the advancement of technology.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/style/motherlode-sleep/motherlode-sleep-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/style/motherlode-sleep/motherlode-sleep-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/style/motherlode-sleep/motherlode-sleep-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/19/style/motherlode-sleep/motherlode-sleep-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/style/motherlode-sleep/motherlode-sleep-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Gadgets to Help New Parents Sleep', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sleep', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T14:20:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/02fa0950-9e64-5891-8e36-ed083977494a', 'word_count': 282, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02fa0950-9e64-5891-8e36-ed083977494a'}, {'abstract': 'Driving Around with Neil Young', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/19/well-hello-mr-soul/', 'snippet': 'Driving Around with Neil Young', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like a lot of people, I often read something in the magazine that involved a writer going to see this or that music/film/theater icon and think about how lucky that writer was. This week it was my turn.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/magazine/19young-car/19young-car-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/magazine/19young-car/19young-car-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'le