went ahead on Wednesday with a decision to publish cartoons featuring the Prophet Muhammad.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/blogs/rdv-charlie/rdv-charlie-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/blogs/rdv-charlie/rdv-charlie-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1369, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cartoons Spark Press Freedom Debate in France', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of the Press', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Charlie Hebdo', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T16:08:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Morris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8276bf32-a7a1-5d6a-8c37-566710eea83d', 'word_count': 645, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8276bf32-a7a1-5d6a-8c37-566710eea83d'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Leonard will receive the medal for Distinguished Contribution to American Letters.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/19/elmore-leonard-to-be-honored-by-national-book-foundation/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Leonard will receive the medal for Distinguished Contribution to American Letters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fall is awards season in the publishing industry, and on Wednesday the National Book Foundation announced the recipients of its annual lifetime achievement awards. The medal for Distinguished Contribution to American Letters will be presented to the novelist and screenwriter Elmore Leonard for his work in fiction. “For over five decades, Leonard’s westerns, crime novels, serialized novels and stories have enthralled generations of readers,” the foundation said in a statement. Harold Augenbraum, the executive director of the foundation, said Mr. Leonard has produced “vibrant literary work with an inimitable writing style.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Elmore Leonard to Be Honored by National Book Foundation', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'National Book Foundation Names Two Honorees', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leonard, Elmore', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sulzberger, Arthur Jr', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Book Foundation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T16:25:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8dd9d129-b198-5224-8427-16b7a4943d05', 'word_count': 215, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8dd9d129-b198-5224-8427-16b7a4943d05'}, {'abstract': 'The new Apple iOS 6, available Wednesday, substitutes its own maps for Google Maps, which may disappoint some people, but David Pogue says the other features make it worth downloading.', 'web_url': 'https://pogue.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/19/new-ios-6-loses-google-maps-but-adds-other-features/', 'snippet': 'The new Apple iOS 6, available Wednesday, substitutes its own maps for Google Maps, which may disappoint some people, but David Pogue says the other features make it worth downloading.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The arrival of the iPhone 5 isn’t the only big news for phone fans this week. Wednesday, Apple is also making iOS 6 available to anyone with a recent iPhone (3GS, 4, or 4S), iPod Touch (fourth generation) or iPad (2 or 3). It comes installed on the iPhone 5 and the new fifth-generation iPod Touch. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/18/technology/18pogue-ios6/18pogue-ios6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 847, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/18/technology/18pogue-ios6/18pogue-ios6-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1695, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/18/technology/18pogue-ios6/18pogue-ios6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/18/technology/18pogue-ios6/18pogue-ios6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New iOS 6 Loses Google Maps, but Adds Other Features', 'kicker': 'Pogue&#039;s Posts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPad', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maps', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Software', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T16:26:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Pogue', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogue', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aee65414-2997-532b-a54a-a6845505d5e0', 'word_count': 1391, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aee65414-2997-532b-a54a-a6845505d5e0'}, {'abstract': 'Over the next year, the Library plans to merge THOMAS, the online home for most of the its 151 million holdings, with the Legislative Information System, its private page for members of Congress and their staffs, to bring its online presence into the 21st Century.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/19/library-of-congress-overhauls-online-offerings/', 'snippet': 'Over the next year, the Library plans to merge THOMAS, the online home for most of the its 151 million holdings, with the Legislative Information System, its private page for members of Congress and their staffs, to bring its online presence into ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Library of Congress released a beta Web site on Wednesday that it says will replace its existing online catalogs in about a year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Library of Congress Overhauls Online Offerings', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T16:29:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Southall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'mid