 also demonstrated its high cost.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/19/emancipations-price/', 'snippet': 'The Battle of Antietam made freedom central to the Civil War, but also demonstrated its high cost.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Historians would later render their own judgments, but in the aftermath of the Battle of Antietam, each side took fast solace in the outcome. For men like John Dooley, a private in the First Virginia Infantry, it was the wondrous achievement of 15,000 or so “ragged, barefoot, hungry” Confederate soldiers who had “repulsed, prostrated, and demoralized” Gen. George B. McClellan’s “immense army,” more than triple the size of the Confederate corps. For Abraham Lincoln, the stalemated outcome was an imperfect opportunity to release his Emancipation Proclamation, a statement he had impatiently waited weeks to make. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Emancipation’s Price', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emancipation Proclamation (1863)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Slavery', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lincoln, Abraham', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McClellan, George B', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Army of Northern Virginia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maryland', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T16:31:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Emmett Curran', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': 'Emmett', 'lastname': 'Curran', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'typ