oduced the secret recordings of Mitt Romney in May alerted the Romney campaign in late August, as well as members of the media and prominent Democrats, about parts of the video.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An anonymous Twitter user who claims to have produced the secret recordings in May of Mitt Romney speaking at a private meeting of wealthy donors in Florida alerted the Romney campaign on Twitter last month, as well as members of the news media and prominent Democrats, about parts of the video.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Online Life of the Secret Romney Recordings', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mother Jones', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T20:28:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/73601c84-87cf-5643-a714-aa5ed2ef0299', 'word_count': 1053, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73601c84-87cf-5643-a714-aa5ed2ef0299'}, {'abstract': 'Companies sharpen their focus on content creators. Paperless Post pushes the envelope, literally. Digital etiquette dos and don’ts.f', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/19/timescast-tech-companies-make-new-content-deals/', 'snippet': 'Companies sharpen their focus on content creators. Paperless Post pushes the envelope, literally. Digital etiquette dos and don’ts.f', 'lead_paragraph': 'Companies sharpen their focus on content creators. Paperless Post pushes the envelope, literally. Digital etiquette dos and don’ts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'TimesCast Tech: Companies Make New Content Deals', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T20:31:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7a5f542-081b-542b-abe7-773fe09454e7', 'word_count': 18, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7a5f542-081b-542b-abe7-773fe09454e7'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama’s advocacy of long-accepted government policy is not Marxist.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/19/the-redistribution-of-wealth/', 'snippet': 'President Obama’s advocacy of long-accepted government policy is not Marxist.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Guided by pollsters like Frank Luntz, the Republican party upgraded all rich people into “job creators,” and tarnished the estate tax by calling it the “death tax.” Its candidates prefer “energy exploration” to oil drilling, and insist on the “religious freedom” of church groups to deny freedom of reproductive choice to their employees. Carefully choosing words to disguise or express contempt is so vital to the party’s strategy that Republicans won’t even properly use the name of the Democratic Party, cutting off the final “ic.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The ‘Redistribution’ of Wealth', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Luntz, Frank I', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T20:31:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Firestone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Firestone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f381de54-bbbd-5c96-92cc-4fe38bae9c39', 'word_count': 547, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f381de54-bbbd-5c96-92cc-4fe38bae9c39'}, {'abstract': 'Scenes from the Milan fashion week photo diary of Sonny Vandevelde.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/19/photos-of-the-moment-alberta-ferretti-5/', 'snippet': 'Scenes from the Milan fashion week photo diary of Sonny Vandevelde.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Photos of The Moment | Alberta Ferretti', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Milan Fashion Week', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T20:31:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sonny Vandevelde', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sonny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vandevelde', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe7df933-bf54-5573-8160-8ae646a33c77', 'word_count': 40, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe7df933-bf54-5573-8160-8ae646