 of starting their own businesses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — If and when the euro crisis ends, Europe will still face an existential economic question: Who will provide the jobs of the future?', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/21/business/global/21advert-2/21advert-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 250, 'width': 337, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/21/business/global/21advert-2/21advert-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 250, 'width': 337, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/21/business/global/21advert-2/21advert-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/21/business/global/21advert-2/21advert-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/21/business/global/21advert-2/21advert-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Europe Aims to Encourage Young to Be Entrepreneurs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Europe Aims to Encourage Young to Be Entrepreneurs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T20:55:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Pfanner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pfanner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/05bced33-91f9-5878-a9df-3923b1930216', 'word_count': 966, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05bced33-91f9-5878-a9df-3923b1930216'}, {'abstract': '“Life After Death,” by Damien Echols of the West Memphis Three murder case in Arkansas, is a dual memoir, partly about his prison life and partly about his tumultuous upbringing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/20/books/life-after-death-by-damien-echols.html', 'snippet': '“Life After Death,” by Damien Echols of the West Memphis Three murder case in Arkansas, is a dual memoir, partly about his prison life and partly about his tumultuous upbringing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Eighteen and a half years after he was sentenced to death for participating in the murders of three 8-year-old boys in Arkansas, Damien Echols finds himself in Faireyland. Mr. Echols’s new book, “Life After Death,” has a Shepard Fairey-inspired cover design that’s as coolly lionizing as Mr. Fairey’s “Hope” poster for President Obama. The book has a champion in Johnny Depp, who has compared Mr. Echols’s writing to Dostoyevsky’s. And his story is the subject of a forthcoming documentary, “West of Memphis,” even though that story has been exhaustively told in the three “Paradise Lost” films that paved the path to Mr. Echols’s release from death row. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/20/arts/jpbook/jpbook-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 737, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/20/arts/jpbook/jpbook-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1475, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/20/arts/jpbook/jpbook-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/20/arts/jpbook/jpbook-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/20/arts/jpbook/jpbook-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Freedom After Fire Ants and Tumult', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Freedom After Fire Ants and Tumult', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Echols, Damien', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Life After Death (Book)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T21:01:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Janet Maslin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Janet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Maslin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/580e3e99-1729-51b7-ab25-6a8becef2991', 'word_count': 1016, 'uri': 'nyt://article/580e3e99-1729-51b7-ab25-6a8becef2991'}, {'abstract': 'When the university professor Adrienne Pine nursed her sick baby on the first day of class, she stirred up a controversy, but public breast-feeding is far from the most important issue she raises.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/19/the-breast-feeding-professor-is-a-red-herring/', 'snippet': 'When the university professor Adrienne Pine nursed her sick baby on the first day of class, she stirred up a controversy, but public breast-feeding is far from the most important issue she raises.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many parents of infants have decided that “breast is best.” What\xa0 they haven’t agreed on is where and when breast-feeding is appropriate, or even acceptable. In past months, women have been chastised for nursing at a water park, a library, and a Georgia church. The feeding practice that’s encouraged (some would say pushed) by hospitals, pediatricians and fellow parents doesn’t always meet with approval when it goes public.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breast-Feeding Professor Is a Red Herring', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Breast-Feeding on the Job', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T21:06:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1474ba9d-2618-581a-bdf9-8d2986ed0b2a', 'word_count': 776, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1474ba9d-2618-581a-bdf9-8d2986ed0b2a'}, {'abstract': 'Clinical trials indicate that BG-12, developed by Biogen Idec, may be safer and more effective than existing treatments for patients in the early stages of the disease.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/20/health/research/bg-12-pill-shows-promise-in-suppressing-multiple-sclerosis-relapses.html', 'snippet': 'Clinical trials indicate that BG-12, developed by Biogen Idec, may be safer and more effective than existing treatments for patients in the early stages of the disease.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new oral medication to treat patients in the early stages of multiple sclerosis has shown considerable promise in two clinical trials, researchers announced on Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pill Found Promising in Treatment of M.S.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pill Found Promising In Treatment Of M.S.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Journal of Medicine', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Multiple Sclerosis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T21:07:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Research', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laurie Tarkan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laurie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tarkan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8e174d4-e127-5f9b-be7c-d6136f32ec33', 'word_count': 651, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8e174d4-e127-5f9b-be7c-d6136f32ec33'}, {'abstract': 'Rory McIlroy spent last week training informally alongside the Knicks at the invitation of his fitness trainer, Steve McGregor, who works with the team.', 'web_url': 'https://onpar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/19/training-with-knicks-mcilroy-works-on-jump-shot/', 'snippet': 'Rory McIlroy spent last week training informally alongside the Knicks at the invitation of his fitness trainer, Steve McGregor, who works with the team.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATLANTA — Rory McIlroy remains more likely to sink a 10-foot putt than a 10-foot jump shot, but the gap is closing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Training With Knicks, McIlroy Works on Jump Shot', 'kicker': 'On Par', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McIlroy, Rory', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T21:16:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Tierney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tierney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce4a2090-e7d0-5c7d-95c1-a10bffb37296', 'word_count': 74, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce4a2090-e7d0-5c7d-95c1-a10bffb37296'}, {'abstract': 'C. Wonder and Costume National have new stores, and Shop the Night Away will offer widespread discounts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/20/fashion/new-stores-sales-and-fashion-advice.html', 'snippet': 'C. Wonder and Costume National have new stores, and Shop the Night Away will offer widespread discounts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OPENINGS', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/20/fashion/20SCOUT1/20SCOUT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 394, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/20/fashion/20SCOUT1/20SCOUT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 3