/1e1f633d-c646-5145-8dcf-68b6e22a9a10', 'word_count': 405, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e1f633d-c646-5145-8dcf-68b6e22a9a10'}, {'abstract': 'New York City Ballet began its fall run at the Koch Theater with a three Greek ballets by Balanchine and an explosive performance by Robert Fairchild.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/20/arts/dance/apollo-orpheus-and-agon-at-city-ballet.html', 'snippet': 'New York City Ballet began its fall run at the Koch Theater with a three Greek ballets by Balanchine and an explosive performance by Robert Fairchild.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the start of Tuesday night’s New York City Ballet performance the curtain rose on Robert Fairchild in the title role of George Balanchine’s oldest surviving ballet, “Apollo.” In this seminal work you see the young god discovering art; and Mr. Fairchild plays the ballet, coolly but keenly, as an adventure. His performance made an auspicious start for City Ballet’s four-week fall season at the David H. Koch Theater.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/20/arts/20apollo/20apollo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/20/arts/20apollo/20apollo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/20/arts/20apollo/20apollo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/20/arts/20apollo/20apollo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit'