and double it.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/19/nation-of-takers/', 'snippet': 'Take that 47, and double it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Do today’s Republicans really believe that 47 percent of Americans are “takers”, living off money confiscated from the “makers”?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nation of Takers', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T22:04:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/39baf68b-c7b7-5699-8939-e1fbf82d62be', 'word_count': 213, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39baf68b-c7b7-5699-8939-e1fbf82d62be'}, {'abstract': 'Video of Chinese protesters in Beijing surrounding the American ambassador’s car on Tuesday was uploaded to YouTube by Ai Weiwei, a Chinese artist and dissident.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/19/ai-reporter/', 'snippet': 'Video of Chinese protesters in Beijing surrounding the American ambassador’s car on Tuesday was uploaded to YouTube by Ai Weiwei, a Chinese artist and dissident.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last Updated, Thursday 3:06 p.m. On Tuesday in Beijing, amid protests over the sovereignty of several tiny islands also claimed by Japan, a small group of protesters briefly surrounded the American ambassador’s car outside the United States Embassy, pelting it with objects. As our colleagues Thom Shanker and Ian Johnson reported, Ambassador Gary Locke said later, “I never felt in any danger.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ai, Reporter', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print