lue': 'Burton, Tim', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T22:41:26+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Movies', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/8d98e0c6-d461-5084-a0a3-8a8d59111e25', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/8d98e0c6-d461-5084-a0a3-8a8d59111e25'}, {'abstract': 'Fox Sports is close to a deal with Major League Baseball that would let it add more regular season and playoff games.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/20/sports/baseball/fox-closes-in-on-new-baseball-deal.html', 'snippet': 'Fox Sports is close to a deal with Major League Baseball that would let it add more regular season and playoff games.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fox Sports is close to a deal with Major League Baseball that will let it add more playoff and regular-season games, justifying its plan to create a new cable sports network, said three people with knowledge of the negotiations. By contrast, TBS will get fewer games in its pending deal.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fox and TBS Close In on New Baseball Deals', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fox Sports Nears Deal to Add More Games', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox Sports', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cable Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TBS Network', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Baseball', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T22:41:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f1b33c0-2319-5069-9580-d2b89f4c2669', 'word_count': 431, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f1b33c0-2319-5069-9580-d2b89f4c2669'}, {'abstract': 'I look for ways to talk and even laugh about my husband with our children, and I take my cues from them in dealing with our grief.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/19/as-daddy-mark-madoff-lives-on/', 'snippet': 'I look for ways to talk and even laugh about my husband with our children, and I take my cues from them in dealing with our grief.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Dec. 11, 2010, my husband, Mark Madoff, hung himself from an exposed beam in the living room of our downtown apartment. Even now I still wake up every morning with a jolt, as if I am hearing the news for the first time that my husband has killed himself. I’m rattled for a good five seconds as my brain acknowledges and accepts that Mark is gone. Oddly enough, the painful jarring of my heart is what gives me the strength to get up and start my day. I get up and push forward not only for myself but also for my children, Audrey and Nicholas.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As ‘Daddy,’ Mark Madoff Lives On', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grief (Emotion)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suicides and Suicide Attempts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Madoff, Mark', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T22:54:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Madoff Mack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': 'Madoff', 'lastname': 'Mack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b61c808-2a51-5fc7-8b01-1ca1c9b7fc38', 'word_count': 802, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b61c808-2a51-5fc7-8b01-1ca1c9b7fc38'}, {'abstract': 'The mayor’s personal wealth increased 28 percent in a year and is 10th among the richest Americans, according to the magazine’s calculations.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/19/bloombergs-fortune-jumped-to-25-billion-forbes-estimates/', 'snippet': 'The mayor’s personal wealth increased 28 percent in a year and is 10th among the richest Americans, according to the magazine’s calculations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Are you better off than you were a year ago? For Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg, the answer is almost certainly yes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bloomberg’s Fortune Jumped to $25 Billion, Forbes Estimates', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bloomberg LP', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Forbes Magazine', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T22:54:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael M. Grynbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4faca591-063c-5ca4-9e19-525e6cf03326', 'word_count': 322, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4faca591-063c-5ca4-9e19-525e6cf03326'}, {'abstract': 'Davy Rothbart, a founder of Found magazine, brings his voyeurism to New Haven in his 75-city tour with his brother Peter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/20/books/davy-rothbart-on-tour-for-book-peter-rothbart-for-album.html', 'snippet': 'Davy Rothbart, a founder of Found magazine, brings his voyeurism to New Haven in his 75-city tour with his brother Peter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW HAVEN — Davy Rothbart had misplaced his usual hype music, so Rage Against the Machine would have to do. Mr. Rothbart, a writer and a creator of Found magazine,  the repository for forgotten notes and photos, normally listened to Metallica’s “One” to get himself pumped for a show. But on Monday evening he popped a CD with “Bombtrack” into the player in his rented Dodge minivan and began fist-pumping along.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/20/arts/20jp-rothbart1/20jp-rothbart1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 375, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/20/arts/20jp-rothbart1/20jp-rothbart1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 375}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/20/arts/20jp-rothbart1/20jp-rothbart1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 665, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/20/arts/20jp-rothbart1/20jp-rothbart1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1330, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, '