deshow/2bfc0644-24a3-50dc-b508-6600ab7d3e28', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/2bfc0644-24a3-50dc-b508-6600ab7d3e28'}, {'abstract': 'The transfer of political power in China, which could begin in a matter of weeks, is arguably the most important political leadership change in the world this year — in a year of turnovers and elections. But what do the mysteries surrounding it mean? What will it presage for China and for the world?', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/19/q-and-a-chinas-leadership-transition-and-xi-jinping/', 'snippet': 'The transfer of political power in China, which could begin in a matter of weeks, is arguably the most important political leadership change in the world this year — in a year of turnovers and elections. But what do the mysteries surrounding it me...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sometime soon — perhaps next month in October — the most populous nation in the world will begin its biggest leadership transition in a decade. Dozens of the most senior positions in China’s Communist Party, government and army will change hands in a process that will last months (in the case of the army, perhaps even years.) Here are some questions and answers about this important event. Join the conversation with your own answers and questions in the Comments below. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/20/blogs/rdv-xi-large-plan/rdv-xi-large-plan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/20/blogs/rdv-xi-large-plan/rdv-xi-large-plan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/20/blogs/rdv-xi-large-plan/rdv-xi-large-plan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 689, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy