hile being honored by a sightseeing bus company. He also spoke about the Knicks and their coming season.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/19/after-lending-his-style-to-a-bus-frazier-offers-his-opinion-on-the-knicks/', 'snippet': 'Walt Frazier was greeted by a dozen or so fans while being honored by a sightseeing bus company. He also spoke about the Knicks and their coming season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A two-time N.B.A. champion and one of the most famous Knicks, Walt Frazier was greeted by a dozen or so fans while being honored Wednesday by the sightseeing bus company Gray Line New York. He also spoke about the Knicks and their coming season, with the team set to begin training camp in less than two weeks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Lending His Style to a Bus, Frazier Offers His Opinion on the Knicks', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Frazier, Walt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T23:31:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea52048d-7568-5dd1-aba3-f7d94c6adcd2', 'word_count': 461, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea52048d-7568-5dd1-aba3-f7d94c6adcd2'}, {'abstract': 'For many Berliners, the closing and impending demolition of a famed artists’ center marks the end of an era.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/20/opinion/creative-destruction-of-an-artists-center-in-berlin.html', 'snippet': 'For many Berliners, the closing and impending demolition of a famed artists’ center marks the end of an era.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Berlin', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Creative Destruction', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Creative Destruction', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Berlin (Germany)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Area Planning and Renewal', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gentrification', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T23:32:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jens Balzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jens', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Balzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/a538427c-15a0-52be-ac83-f8cc2acd185a', 'word_count': 1042, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a538427c-15a0-52be-ac83-f8cc2acd185a'}, {'abstract': 'Guest blogger Han-yi Shaw argues that Japan in effect stole the Diaoyu/Senkaku islands from China in 1895 as booty of war.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/19/the-inconvenient-truth-behind-the-diaoyusenkaku-islands/', 'snippet': 'Guest blogger Han-yi Shaw argues that Japan in effect stole the Diaoyu/Senkaku islands from China in 1895 as booty of war.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve had a longstanding interest in the Diaoyu/Senkaku islands, the subject of a dangerous territorial dispute\xa0 between Japan and China. The United States claims to be neutral but in effect is siding with Japan, and we could be drawn in if a war ever arose. Let me clear that I deplore the violence in the recent anti-Japan protests in China: \xa0the violence is reprehensible and makes China look like an irrational bully. China’s government should rein in this volatile nationalism rather than feed it. This is a dispute that both sides should refer to the International Court of Justice, rather than allow to boil over in the streets. That said, when I look at the underlying question of who has the best claim, I’m sympathetic to China’s position. I don’t think it is 100 percent clear, partly because China seemed to acquiesce to Japanese sovereignty between 1945 and 1970, but on balance I find the evidence for Chinese sovereignty quite compelling. The most interesting evidence is emerging from old Japanese government documents and suggests that Japan in effect stole the islands from China in 1895 as booty of war. This article by Han-Yi Shaw, a scholar from Taiwan, explores those documents. I invite any Japanese scholars to make the contrary legal case. – Nicholas Kristof', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Inconvenient Truth Behind the Diaoyu/Senkaku Islands', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-19T23:38:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Han-yi Shaw', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Han-yi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shaw', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e107e86f-b605-5fa0-9ebf-cc2c9bf836db', 'word_count': 1146, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e107e86f-b605-5fa0-9ebf-cc2c9bf836db'}, {'abstract': 'Jack McCollough and Lazaro Hernandez bring their PS1 bags and other creations to the East Side.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/20/fashion/proenza-schouler-on-madison-avenue-critical-shopper.html', 'snippet': 'Jack McCollough and Lazaro Hernandez bring their PS1 bags and other creations to the East Side.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN a world of fashion design densely populated by difficult, messy individuals, one can well understand the temptation to team up and clean up, à la Dolce & Gabbana or Viktor & Rolf. You and your partner may not agree on every inch of rickrack, but he’ll probably stop you from alcohol-fueled anti-Semitic rants and affairs with a tanned pornographic-film star half your age.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/20/fashion/20CRITIC3/20CRITIC3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 671, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/20/fashion/20CRITIC3/20CRITIC3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1343, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/20/fashion/20CRITIC3/20CRITIC3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/20/fashion/20CRITIC3/20CRITIC3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/20/fashion/20CRITIC3/20CRITIC3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'On Planet Proenza', 'kicker': 'Critical Shopper', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On Planet Proenza', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N