0/opinion/mr-and-mrs-jesus-christ.html', 'snippet': 'Does a new discovery of an ancient papyrus mean that Jesus was married? Probably not.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AT an academic conference in Rome on Tuesday, Karen L. King, a church historian at Harvard Divinity School, presented a finding that, according to some reports, threatened to overturn what we know about Jesus, as well as the tradition of priestly celibacy. She identified a small fragment of fourth-century papyrus that includes the words, “Jesus said to them, ‘My wife...’\xa0” Another clause appears to say, “she will be able to be my disciple.” Some experts have concluded that the manuscript, written in Coptic, is authentic.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mr. and Mrs. Jesus Christ?', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mr. and Mrs. Jesus Christ?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jesus Christ', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Manuscripts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Karen Leigh', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mary Magdalene', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christians and Christianity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Harvard Divinity School', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-20T00:14:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/245f6d0b-9a62-5481-af05-9b09aa15cceb', 'word_count': 841, 'uri': 'nyt://article/245f6d0b-9a62-5481-af05-9b09aa15cceb'}, {'abstract': 'The flawed incentives that guide businesses’ employment practices hurt women at both ends of the labor market.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/20/opinion/low-paid-women-want-predictable-hours-and-steady-pay.html', 'snippet': 'The flawed incentives that guide businesses’ employment practices hurt women at both ends of the labor market.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chicago', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/20/opinion/0920OPEDheuer/0920OPEDheuer-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1237, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/20/opinion/0920OPEDheuer/0920OPEDheuer-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1237}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/20/opinion/0920OPEDheuer/0920OPEDheuer-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/20/opinion/0920OPEDheuer/0920OPEDheuer-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 994, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/20/opinion/0920OPEDheuer/0920OPEDheuer-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/20/opinion/0920OPEDheuer/0920OPEDheuer-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/20/opinion/0920OPEDheuer/0920OPEDheuer-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'le