22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/20/nyregion/JP-NYELECTION2/JP-NYELECTION2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 737, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/20/nyregion/JP-NYELECTION2/JP-NYELECTION2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1919, 'width': 1382, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/20/nyregion/JP-NYELECTION2/JP-NYELECTION2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/20/nyregion/JP-NYELECTION2/JP-NYELECTION2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/20/nyregion/JP-NYELECTION2/JP-NYELECTION2-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Governor and Mayor Are Upset That 2 Backers of Gay Marriage May Fall', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Governor and Mayor Are Upset That 2 Backers of Gay Marriage May Fall', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McDonald, Roy J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saland, Stephen M', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-20T00:26:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Kaplan and Michael M. Grynbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5992f7b-a412-52ba-ab2f-7888ab7464f5', 'word_count': 870, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5992f7b-a412-52ba-ab2f-7888ab7464f5'}, {'abstract': 'On Friday morning,William Bouvay Jr., 42, called the 911 dispatcher and said that multiple bombs around Louisiana State University would detonate within two hours, the authorities said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/20/us/louisiana-arrest-in-bomb-threat.html', 'snippet': 'On Friday morning,William Bouvay Jr., 42, called the 911 dispatcher and said that multiple bombs around Louisiana State University would detonate within two hours, the authorities said.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The police arrested a man suspected of phoning in a bomb threat to Louisiana State University on Monday, prompting a campuswide evacuation. The man, William Bouvay Jr., 42, of Baton Rouge, La., was taken into custody shortly before midnight on Tuesday, the campus police department said in a statement. On Friday morning, Mr. Bouvay had called the 911 dispatcher and said that multiple bombs around the campus would detonate within two hours, the authorities said. Law enforcement agencies determined that the call had been made from a deactivated cellphone that could make only emergency calls; they were able to pinpoint the area from which the call was made through GPS technology. Mr. Bouvay, who was in the area, agreed to go in for questioning, but ultimately confessed and told the police where the phone could be found, the police said. They declined to discuss possible motives for the calls, but said Mr. Bouvay had been arrested in 2004 for making harassing phone calls to a former girlfriend who worked at the university. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Louisiana: Arrest in Bomb Threat', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Louisiana: Arrest In Bomb Threat', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Threats and Threatening Messages', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Louisiana State University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-20T00:27:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Campbell Robertson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Campbell', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robertson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/a80ddcad-2b16-53de-9e11-ac242ba03394', 'word_count': 174, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a80ddcad-2b16-53de-9e11-ac242ba03394'}, {'abstract': 'New York’s new traffic safety awareness campaign will feature a warning stenciled along curbsides at more than 100 of the city’s most dangerous intersections.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/20/nyregion/in-new-york-city-curbside-signs-to-look-both-ways.html', 'snippet': 'New York’s new traffic safety awareness campaign will feature a warning stenciled along curbsides at more than 100 of the city’s most dangerous intersections.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The British have a history of being unlucky on American shores, and in the winter of 1931, Winston S. Churchill was no exception. Alighting from a cab on Fifth Avenue on the Upper East Side, Churchill, accustomed to his home country’s driving conventions, looked right on the then-two way avenue when he should have looked left.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/20/nyregion/STREETS1/STREETS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/20/nyregion/STREETS1/STREETS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/20/nyregion/STREETS1/STREETS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 687, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/20/nyregion/STREETS1/STREETS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1374, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/20/nyregion/STREETS1/STREETS1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/20/nyregion/STREETS1/STREETS1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/20/nyregion/STREETS1/STREETS1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType