playing with an ankle injury, sat out the first game of a day-night doubleheader before returning to shortstop for the first time since Sept. 12.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Wednesday afternoon, for the first game of a day-night doubleheader at Yankee Stadium, Derek Jeter rested. He wore a blue hooded sweatshirt and the expression of a child forced to miss a class field trip because of the flu. He had his spikes on, but for the first time since June 27, Jeter did not need to use them.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jeter, After Resting in Game 1, Returns to Shortstop', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jeter, After Resting in Game 1, Returns to Shortstop', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jeter, Derek', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-20T01:30:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zach Schonbrun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zach', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schonbrun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/32b2bff9-73b0-510b-8659-f4d9e3e9271d', 'word_count': 642, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32b2bff9-73b0-510b-8659-f4d9e3e9271d'}, {'abstract': 'It remains unclear precisely how Mitt Romney’s views on redistribution differ from those of Barack Obama.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/19/a-closer-look-at-redistribution/', 'snippet': 'It remains unclear precisely how Mitt Romney’s views on redistribution differ from those of Barack Obama.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Amid the fallout over Mitt Romney’s comments that 47 percent of Americans believed they were “victims” and are dependent upon government, the Republican Party is stepping up attacks that President Obama favors redistributing wealth, citing a 1998 audio clip of him saying, “I actually believe in redistribution.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Closer Look at ‘Redistribution’', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Seeking to Turn Topic To Evils of Redistribution', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-20T01:30:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard A. Oppel Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Oppel', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3251bbb-b867-5f38-bbfe-913cd15861f8', 'word_count': 580, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3251bbb-b867-5f38-bbfe-913cd15861f8'}, {'abstract': 'Despite attacks against American embassies and violent protests, Washington must remain engaged with struggling Arab democracies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/20/opinion/the-united-states-and-the-muslim-world.html', 'snippet': 'Despite attacks against American embassies and violent protests, Washington must remain engaged with struggling Arab democracies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The anti-Islam video that set off attacks against American embassies and violent protests in the Muslim world was a convenient fuse for rage. Deeper forces are at work in those societies, riven by pent-up anger over a lack of jobs, economic stagnation and decades of repression by previous Arab governments. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The United States and the Muslim World', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The United States and the Muslim World', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stevens, J Christopher', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nasrallah, Hassan', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Innocence of Muslims (Movie)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-20T01:31:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/e771c383-9027-5004-93b1-bc3458a683c6', 'word_count': 572, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e771c383-9027-5004-93b1-bc3458a683c6'}, {'abstract': 'A study that linked genetically engineered corn to cancer in rats was criticized by some scientists but was seized on by backers of a California ballot measure to require labeling for genetically modified crops.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/20/business/energy-environment/disputed-study-links-modified-corn-to-greater-health-risks.html', 'snippet': 'A study that linked genetically engineered corn to cancer in rats was criticized by some scientists but was seized on by backers of a California ballot measure to require labeling for genetically modified crops.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rats fed either genetically engineered corn or the herbicide Roundup had an increased risk of developing tumors, suffering organ damage and dying prematurely, according to a new study that was immediately swept up into the furor surrounding crop biotechnology when it was released Wednesday. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Foes of Modified Corn Find Support in a Study', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Foes of Modified Corn Find Support in a Study', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corn', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Seralini, Gilles-Eric', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetic Engineering', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Monsanto Company', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defoliants and Herbicides', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-20T01:33:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Energy & Environment ', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Pollack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pollack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/59271457-3ad4-5e9e-b38c-612558b535ae', 'word_count': 713, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59271457-3ad4-5e9e-b38c-612558b535ae'}, {'abstract': 'It has been a year since “don’t ask, don’t tell” was repealed and by most measures the change has been a success, military officials and gay service members say.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/20/us/dont-ask-dont-tell-anniversary-passes-with-little-note.html', 'snippet': 'It has been a year since “don’t ask, don’t tell” was repealed and by most measures the change has been a success, military officials and gay service members say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Every Tuesday and Friday morning in a dining area tucked behind Dunkin’ Donuts in the Pentagon’s main food court, a gay coffee group meets to talk, do a little business and tell a few jokes.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/20/us/MILITARY-1/MILITARY-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/20/us/MILITARY-1/MILITARY-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/20/us/MILITARY-1/MILITARY-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 707, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/20/us/MILITARY-1/MILITARY-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1413, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/20/us/MILITARY-1/MILITARY-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/20/us/MILITARY-1/MILITARY-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit