20T01:43:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f3279fde-0dd2-588f-93ed-4ee293bfb79f', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f3279fde-0dd2-588f-93ed-4ee293bfb79f'}, {'abstract': 'Voters should not have to struggle to read the candidates’ names on the ballot because of the tiny print.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/20/opinion/squinting-at-the-polls-in-new-york-city.html', 'snippet': 'Voters should not have to struggle to read the candidates’ names on the ballot because of the tiny print.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many New Yorkers who went to the polls last Thursday were a little surprised to find a large magnifying sheet inside their voting booths. One glance at the ballot explained why. The names of the candidates were tiny, like the lower lines in the optometrist’s eye chart or the small print on a credit card notice. Even voters with excellent vision found themselves squinting in search of their preferred candidates.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Squinting at the Polls in New York City', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Squinting at the Polls in New York City', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Board of Elections (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Typography', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-20T01:43:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d661c0b-bc72-5020-956e-20501c2808ab', 'word_count': 339, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d661c0b-bc72-5020-956e-20501c2808ab'}, {'abstract': 'The consensus among the Jets is that it will be much easier for Santonio Holmes and Mark Sanchez if the tight end Dustin Keller, who has a hamstring injury, is able to play.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/20/sports/football/jets-hoping-dustin-keller-will-play-against-dolphins.html', 'snippet': 'The consensus among the Jets is that it will be much easier for Santonio Holmes and Mark Sanchez if the tight end Dustin Keller, who has a hamstring injury, is able to play.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FLORHAM PARK, N.J. — Jets tight end Dustin Keller showed up Wednesday for practice in full gear, high-stepping over a row of barriers before running 30-yard sprints with elegant, exaggerated strides. That part of the day seemed to go smoothly.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/20/sports/JETS/JETS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/20/sports/JETS/JETS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1600, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'To Help Sanchez and Holmes, Healthy Keller May Be the Key', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Help Sanchez and Holmes, Healthy Keller May Be the Key', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Rex', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keller, Dustin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Yor