ildren living in households where another member had been a victim of a nonfatal violent crime decreased by 68 percent, according to a government report.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Exposure to violence has a profound effect on children, making them more prone to emotional problems like depression and anxiety and increasing the chances that they will either become victims of violence themselves or commit crimes in later life. But a new government report suggests that the number of children in the United States who are exposed to violent crime has dropped precipitously in the last two decades, a decline that one expert termed “breathtaking.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fewer Children Are Found Exposed to Violent Crime', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fewer Children Are Found Exposed to Violent Crime', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime Rates', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Domestic Violence', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bureau of Justice Statistics', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-20T01:52:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erica Goode', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goode', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/69a5432d-9cb9-5946-b347-4e1d076c75f1', 'word_count': 637, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69a5432d-9cb9-5946-b347-4e1d076c75f1'}, {'abstract': 'Experts say bureaucracy and inefficiencies result in a system of medical rationing for organ donati