ctive.html', 'snippet': 'Iran’s top negotiator in talks with the big powers over his country’s disputed uranium enrichment program called negotiations with his counterpart, “constructive and helpful.”', 'lead_paragraph': ' Saeed Jalili, Iran’s top negotiator in talks with the big powers over his country’s disputed uranium enrichment program, called negotiations with Catherine Ashton, his counterpart, “constructive and helpful,” the official Islamic Republic News Agency reported on Wednesday. The talks on Tuesday in Istanbul, their first face-to-face meeting in three months, produced no breakthroughs, and it remained unclear when they would meet again. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iran: Top Nuclear Negotiator Calls Talks With Big Powers ‘Constructive’', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iran: Top Nuclear Negotiator Calls Talks With Big Powers ‘Constructive’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jalili, Saeed', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ashton, Catherine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-20T04:08:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/0595c4ed-0031-5c6f-ab85-1c35535a9975', 'word_count': 160, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0595c4ed-0031-5c6f-ab85-1c35535a9975'}, {'abstract':