eakfast-meeting-mother-jones-drives-the-debate-and-bskyb-found-fit-and-proper/', 'snippet': 'Also, Fox closes in on a deal with Major League Baseball; and Ai Weiwei, the dissident Chinese artist, becomes a reporter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With its release of a secretly recorded tape of Mitt Romney’s description of the 47 percent who are “dependent” on government, the magazine Mother Jones this week has been driving the political debate. That’s particularly good thing, Christine Haughney writes, for the 36-year-old left-leaning magazine, which has a circulation of just over 200,000 and a business model that is partly dependent on its readers’ contributions. One reader visited the magazine’s Washington bureau and dropped off a check.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: Mother Jones Drives the Debate, and BSkyB Found ‘Fit and Proper’', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-20T13:17:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noam Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c80a199a-44df-50ec-952f-96f4d005c4b4', 'word_count': 528, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c80a199a-44df-50ec-952f-96f4d005c4b4'}, {'abstract': 'Success can be misunderstood.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/20/the-trouble-with-fedspeak/', 'snippet': 'Success can be misunderstood.', 'lead_paragraph': 'So Fed hawks are all upset that expected inflation has risen since Bernanke announced QE3 — as indeed it has. Here’s the TIPS spread, the difference between the interest rate on ordinary 10-year bonds and inflation-protected securit