 County (Pa)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-20T14:30:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/52d3e973-4d77-59cc-96ee-8207aceb7971', 'word_count': 413, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52d3e973-4d77-59cc-96ee-8207aceb7971'}, {'abstract': 'The Italian spring shows have started and already there’s magical connectivity to London’s sports-chic.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/20/rumble-in-milan/', 'snippet': 'The Italian spring shows have started and already there’s magical connectivity to London’s sports-chic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Italian spring shows have started and already there’s magical connectivity to London’s sports-chic, at least from Tom Ford and Thomas Tait. It flared this morning at MaxMara, where silky blouson jackets came with detachable hoods, and striped knitted T-tops looked sporty with slim wrap skirts in brown suede or a crisp silk version that combined an animal print, a floral and a check. The collection’s safari-themed jackets and jumpsuits, its stenciled calf-hair clogs with ankle ties, were a loose interpretation of that style. Looking at those silk-backed knit tops and slim skirts you mainly saw cool ways to smarten up your look.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rumble in Milan', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mara, Max', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Emporio Armani', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-20T14:34:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9482842-5109-59dd-ab7a-b881fe30acaf', 'word_count': 142, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9482842-5109-59dd-ab7a-b881fe30acaf'}, {'abstract': 'Trulia, the real estate information site, rose 30 percent in its debut to open at roughly $22, defying the recent lackluster performance of newly public stocks.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/09/20/trulia-jumps-30-in-debut/', 'snippet': 'Trulia, the real estate information site, rose 30 percent in its debut to open at roughly $22, defying the recent lackluster performance of newly public stocks.', 'lead_paragraph': '4:24 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trulia Jumps 40% in Debut', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citigroup Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deutsche Bank AG', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Trulia.com', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Zillow.com', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wall Street (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-20T14:34:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Evelyn M. Rusli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Evelyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/438d5e3b-3df7-5c0e-8573-aa54ab7acf99', 'word_count': 257, 'uri': 'nyt://article/438d5e3b-3df7-5c0e-8573-aa54ab7acf99'}, {'abstract': 'The Republican candidate steps up his campaigning, focusing on a state that many believe could be decisive.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/20/romney-to-do-bus-tour-in-critical-state-of-ohio/', 'snippet': 'The Republican candidate steps up his campaigning, focusing on a state that many believe could be decisive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mitt Romney’s campaign — which in recent weeks has come under criticism for having a schedule light on public events and heavy on closed-door fund-raisers — has announced that the candidate will start to ramp up his campaign schedule in coming days.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney to Do Bus Tour in Critical State of Ohio', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cincinnati (Ohio)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cleveland (Ohio)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Columbus (Ohio)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dayton (Ohio)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Toledo (Ohio)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-20T14:37:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f3aef2f-d056-573d-a9d6-239bab05839f', 'word_count': 163, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f3aef2f-d056-573d-a9d6-239bab05839f'}, {'abstract': 'We asked readers of the International Herald Tribune for pictures and memories of their experiences with the paper to help celebrate the IHT’s 125th anniversary. One response made us realize that at times our readers have come dangerously close to the worst kind of news. Have you had such an experience?', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/20/iht-readers-close-encounter-with-the-news/', 'snippet': 'We asked readers of the International Herald Tribune for pictures and memories of their experiences with the paper to help celebrate the IHT’s 125th anniversary. One response made us realize that at times our readers have come dangerously close to...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week Rendezvous called on readers of the International Herald Tribune to share their favorite memories or photos about the paper to help us celebrate our 125th anniversary on Oct. 4. We’ve had some great responses so far, and we hope that many of you are still searching for the ideal backdrop for your own IHT portrait to rival the George Clooney photo we posted.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/blogs/IHTRDV-Lahore-clipping/IHTRDV-Lahore-clipping-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 505, 'width': 762, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/blogs/IHTRDV-Lahore-clipping/IHTRDV-Lahore-clipping-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 505, 'width': 762, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'IHT Readers’ Close Encounter With the News', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Herald Tribune', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lahore (Pakistan)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-20T14:43:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By The International Herald Tribune', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The International Herald Tribune'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df078db3-f8a0-56e0-b7f0-af5022f4b58b', 'word_count': 372, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df078db3-f8a0-56e0-b7f0-af5022f4b58b'}, {'abstract': 'Two-thirds of Americans admit to making “really bad” financial decisions.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/20/your-worst-financial-mistake/', 'snippet': 'Two-thirds of Americans admit to making “really bad” financial decisions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My husband and I have managed, so far, to avoid making a truly devastating financial mistake. I wish I could say this is because we’re super savvy about money. But the truth is that, while we are diligent about saving, cautious with debt and try to do our homework on investments, there’s a strong element of luck involved.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Your Worst Financial Mistake', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lamenting Money Moves', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mutual Funds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nocera, Joseph', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Federation of America', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-20T14:45:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fcec6f0b-b5a0-52b7-868b-cbbd8bfed5eb', 'word_count': 386, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fcec6f0b-b5a0-52b7-868b-cbbd8bfed5eb'}, {'abstract': 'The revival of Tennessee Williams’s 1955 drama will open on Jan. 17, 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/20/cat-revival-with-scarlett-johansson-is-set-with-benjamin-walker-as-brick/', 'snippet': 'The revival of Tennessee Williams’s 1955 drama will open on Jan. 17, 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Scarlett Johansson will play Maggie the Cat on Broadway this winter in Tennessee Williams’s “Cat on a Hot Tin Roof,” starring opposite Benjamin Walker (“Bloody Bloody Andrew Jackson”) as her alcoholic husband, Brick, the show’s lead producer, Stuart Thompson, announced on Thursday. The theater and television actor Ciaran Hinds will play Brick’s irascible father, Big Daddy Pollitt, and the Tony Award winner Debra Monk (“Curtains,” “Redwood Curtain”) will play Big Mama.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Cat’ Revival With Scarlett Johansson Is Set, With Benjamin Walker as Brick', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'u2018Catu2019 Revival Is Set With Scarlett Johansson', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hinds, Ciaran', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johansson, Scarlett', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Monk, Debra', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walker, Benjamin (1982- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Tennessee', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-20T14:46:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f5f5369-64e7-5131-953f-0793ce05703d', 'word_count': 244, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f5f5369-64e7-5131-953f-0793ce05703d'}, {'abstract': 'RIM announced a bunch of innovative features for its next smartphone last May. The only problem is, the iPhone has them now and the BlackBerry won’t arrive until sometime next year.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/20/rim-innovates-and-then-waits-as-iphone-moves/', 'snippet': 'RIM announced a bunch of innovative features for its next smartphone last May. The only problem is, the iPhone has them now and the BlackBerry won’t arrive until sometime next year.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Among the features of the new Apple iPhone 5 are a more movie-friendly display format, two tiny grills on the bottom that shield noise-canceling microphones, a more powerful processor and a slim, all-black case.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/blogs/Blackberry-10-copy/Blackberry-10-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 618, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'