r': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Page, Patrick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-20T15:31:02+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Theater', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/fed16425-ab9f-5739-ab55-7e68dc43831c', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/fed16425-ab9f-5739-ab55-7e68dc43831c'}, {'abstract': 'Carol Burnett and her co-stars Vicki Lawrence and Tim Conway will take part in a town hall event for SiriusXM radio hosted by Amy Schumer.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/20/stars-of-the-carol-burnett-show-reuniting-on-siriusxm/', 'snippet': 'Carol Burnett and her co-stars Vicki Lawrence and Tim Conway will take part in a town hall event for SiriusXM radio hosted by Amy Schumer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Keep your earlobes – and maybe a couple of tissues – within reach for a sentimental reunion of the stars of “The Carol Burnett Show” that SiriusXM radio is planning for next week. The satellite broadcaster said on Thursday that it would host a town hall event with Ms. Burnett, the five-time Emmy Award-winner, and Vicki Lawrence and Tim Conway, her co-stars from that long-running CBS variety series. (Not coincidentally, the event is timed to a new TimeLife DVD release for the show, including a 22-disc boxed set.) The town hall, which will incorporate questions from an audience of SiriusXM listeners, will be hosted by Amy Schumer, the standup comic, Comedy Central roast-ess and author of numerous jokes that would surely turn the head of genteel Starlet O’Hara. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stars of ‘The Carol Burnett Show’ Reuniting on SiriusXM', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burnett, Carol', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Conway, Tim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lawrence, Vicki', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schumer, Amy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-20T15:33:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70828b31-3698-5d17-9c19-4e99c5c8e532', 'word_count': 163, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70828b31-3698-5d17-9c19-4e99c5c8e532'}, {'abstract': 'Experienced with Shakespeare’s antagonists, Patrick Page also brings to his current bad guy, in “Cyrano de Bergerac,” personal insight into unhappiness and depression.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/23/theater/patrick-page-onetime-green-goblin-on-playing-in-cyrano.html', 'snippet': 'Experienced with Shakespeare’s antagonists, Patrick Page also brings to his current bad guy, in “Cyrano de Bergerac,” personal insight into unhappiness and depression.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PATRICK PAGE has dreamed of performing the title role in “Cyrano de Bergerac” on Broadway for as long as he can remember. It is his favorite play, “the greatest part ever written,” he said, and he has been in three productions of it over the past 25 years, including twice as Cyrano. But when he learned that a new Broadway revival was already committed to star a Tony Award winner, Mr. Page chose not to sulk. Instead, he sought to join the production as one of Cyrano’s antagonists, the aristocrat de Guiche. And soon the job was his, the latest in a career of villains from Richard III and Iago to, most recently, the spandex-and-foam-suited Green Goblin for 21 months in the Broadway musical “Spider-Man: Turn Off the Dark.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/arts/23PAGE2_SPAN/23PAGE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/23/arts/23PAGE2_SPAN/23PAGE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/arts/23PAGE2_SPAN/23PAGE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 671, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/arts/23PAGE2_SPAN/23PAGE2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1342, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/arts/23PAGE2_SPAN/23PAGE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/23/arts/23PAGE2_SPAN/23PAGE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Smile and Be a Villain; Despair and Be One, Too', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Smile and Be a Villain; Despair and Be One, Too', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Page, Patrick', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-20T15:33:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 