.”', 'lead_paragraph': '4:17 p.m. | Updated  CORAL GABLES, Fla. – President Obama took aim at Mitt Romney for his closed-door observation that 47 percent of Americans are dependent on government handouts, do not pay income taxes, and will inevitably vote for Mr. Obama.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Hits Romney Over 47 Percent Remark', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dream Act (Development, Relief and Education for Minors Act)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carney, Jay', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Univision', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Middle East', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Salinas (Calif)', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-20T19:21:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/410e5a99-84c9-5bba-af87-f6e38fb19002', 'word_count': 636, 'uri': 'nyt://article/410e5a99-84c9-5bba-af87-f6e38fb19002'}, {'abstract': '“Switch,” a documentary by Harry Lynch, is a guided global tour of where the planet’s future wattage will be coming from.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/20/movies/switch-explores-a-world-of-fuel-options.html', 'snippet': '“Switch,” a documentary by Harry Lynch, is a guided global tour of where the planet’s future wattage will be coming from.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Exhaustive and exhausting, the new energy documentary “Switch” is so monotonous it makes “An Inconvenient Truth” look like “Armageddon.” Forgetting that the movie theater is not a college classroom, the director and co-writer, Harry Lynch, bombards us with droning interviews and a guide (the geologist Scott Tinker) whose nodding affability verges on somnolent. He’s like a tranquilizer that works by knocking you out with numbers.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/20/movies/switch-span/switch-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/20/movies/switch-span/switch-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/20/movies/switch-span/switch-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/20/movies/switch-span/switch-span-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1080, 'width': 1920, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'supe