om Old Master painters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'T gave the set designer and art director Mary Howard carte blanche on the travel issue’s T. What she made of the magazine’s signature initial? A rich and most elaborate installation modeled after the works of Old Master painters like Jan Weenix, Jan van Eyck and Johannes Vermeer. Howard, whose work has appeared in magazines like Vogue, Vanity Fair and GQ — her sets are the backdrops for some of fashion’s most compelling pictures — has worked with many of the industry’s most illustrious photographers (Annie Leibovitz, Bruce Weber and Steven Klein), stylists (Edward Enninful, Camilla Nickerson and Tonne Goodman), models and celebrities. Here, she talks about the way she works and how she travels (light, spontaneously and without her iPad).', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '97', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trad and True', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trad And True', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Howard, Mary', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Orleans (La)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-20T19:32:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane Herman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Herman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ddaec73-42ae-5039-9f9b-6ad70e45c22d', 'word_count': 1238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ddaec73-42ae-5039-9f9b-6ad70e45c22d'}, {'abstract': 'A new restaurant is moving into the space that housed Manganaro’s Grosseria Italiana.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/20/tavola-italian-food-without-the-feud/', 'snippet': 'A new restaurant is moving into the space that housed Manganaro’s Grosseria Italiana.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There will no longer be any confusion over which Manganaro’s store is which. The one that opened 119 years ago on the West Side of Manhattan and became known as Manganaro Grosseria Italiana, or Manganaro Foods, is no more.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tavola, Italian Food Without the Feud', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Manganaro Foods', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-20T19:39:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/752ab632-4c30-5ed9-a224-64f209f1221f', 'word_count': 223, 'uri': 'nyt://article/752ab632-4c30-5ed9-a224-64f209f1221f'}, {'abstract': 'Starting on Friday night and through Sunday are free or dirt-cheap events featuring Jeffrey Eugenides, Denis Johnson and Kay Larson, as well as an art book swap and a Scrabble tournament.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/21/nyregion/brooklyn-book-festival-marks-seventh-year.html', 'snippet': 'Starting on Friday night and through Sunday are free or dirt-cheap events featuring Jeffrey Eugenides, Denis Johnson and Kay Larson, as well as an art book swap and a Scrabble tournament.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Brooklyn’s rise from shunned underdog to contemporary cultural Mecca happened so swiftly that the Miser has a hard time remembering the days when a Brooklyn literary event consisted mainly of spotting P