 and disliked practice.', 'web_url': 'https://publiceditor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/20/in-new-policy-the-times-forbids-after-the-fact-quote-approval/', 'snippet': 'The Times is one of the first major news organizations to take a firm stand against a growing and disliked practice.', 'lead_paragraph': '4:32 p.m. | Updated Full memo included at the end of this post.The New York Times is drawing “a clear line” against the practice of news sources being allowed to approve quotations in stories after the fact.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In New Policy, The Times Forbids After-the-Fact ‘Quote Approval’', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-20T19:53:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7fee2304-539d-5cf1-9529-ac7c7ddba3ea', 'word_count': 1234, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7fee2304-539d-5cf1-9529-ac7c7ddba3ea'}, {'abstract': 'This summer’s remarkable ice retreat around the North Pole has come to an end, as the journey toward an open polar sea (in summers) continues.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/20/arctic-ice-melt-and-the-path-toward-an-open-polar-sea/', 'snippet': 'This summer’s remarkable ice retreat around the North Pole has come to an end, as the journey toward an open polar sea (in summers) continues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the mid 1800s, some scientists and explorers — having not yet found a way through the forbidding sea ice sheathing much of the Arctic Ocean — posited that there was an “open polar sea” beyond those barricades, nourished by warm waters sweeping north past Scandinavian coasts. (I have the marvelous 1867 book “The Open Polar Sea” on my book shelf; you can read it online here.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pondering the Path To an Open Polar Sea', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Summer (Season)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARCTIC OCEAN', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Pole', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-20T19:57:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f55d2fa7-109a-5a89-9db6-551baa25e994', 'word_count': 1195, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f55d2fa7-109a-5a89-9db6-551baa25e994'}, {'abstract': 'In its crush of pink and red satin, in its papery flower appliqués, the spring Prada show on Thursday night seemed literally a Valentine to women.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/20/pradas-new-flower-power/', 'snippet': 'In its crush of pink and red satin, in its papery flower appliqués, the spring Prada show on Thursday night seemed literally a Valentine to women.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In its crush of pink and red satin, in its papery flower appliqués, the spring Prada show on Thursday night seemed literally a Valentine to women. But it was also a dazzling example of how to breathe modernity into cultural references — in this case, traditional Japanese style and architecture. European designers have had a long affair with the kimono, the obi and platform sandal, and the chrysanthemum pinks. There was a Dior couture show, maybe eight years ago, when John Galliano created an operatic Japanese story. But Miuccia Prada’s collection is a rare instance when you know you are looking at new fashion.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Prada’s New Flower Power', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Milan Fashion Week', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Prada, Miuccia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Prada SpA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-20T19:58:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a52bff47-a828-51db-907a-1844c7d0b6d0', 'word_count': 340, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a52bff47-a828-51db-907a-1844c7d0b6d0'}, {'abstract': "The European Central Bank's new headquarters reflect stability for the common currency but lack the austerity the bank preaches to countries like Greece and Spain.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/21/business/global/for-the-euro-a-costly-shelter-from-the-storm.html', 'snippet': "The European Central Bank's new headquarters reflect stability for the common currency but lack the austerity the bank preaches to countries like Greece and Spain.", 'lead_paragraph': 'FRANKFURT — In a bricks-and-mortar declaration that the euro is here to stay and that the European Central Bank is its headquarters, the bank marked a milestone Thursday with a ceremony for its imposing new office towers. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/21/business/ECB-2/ECB-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/21/business/ECB-2/ECB-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/21/business/ECB-2/ECB-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 736, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/21/business/ECB-2/ECB-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1472, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/21/business/ECB-2/ECB-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/21/business/ECB-2/ECB-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/21/business/ECB-2/ECB-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For the Euro, a Costly Shelter From the Storm', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For the ‘Irreversible’ Euro, an Enormously Costly Shelter From the Storm', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': '