ure for the planet. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Has Plant Life Reached Its Limits?', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flowers and Plants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Science (Journal)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-20T19:59:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sophia Li', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sophia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Li', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e15c006e-b5d5-5b1b-aef0-585553ba61ca', 'word_count': 582, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e15c006e-b5d5-5b1b-aef0-585553ba61ca'}, {'abstract': 'Research shows that some foods really are addictive.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/20/craving-an-ice-cream-fix/', 'snippet': 'Research shows that some foods really are addictive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The notion that food can be addictive has been debated for some time and largely rejected by both nutrition and addiction researchers. But this spring, the secretary of health, Kathleen Sebelius, said that for some, obesity is “an addiction like smoking.” One month earlier, Dr. Nora Volkow, director of the National Institute on Drug Abuse, gave a lecture at Rockefeller University, making the case that food and drug addictions have much in common, particularly in the way that both disrupt the parts of the brain involved in pleasure and self-control.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/magazine/23well/23well-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/23/magazine/23well/23well-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 429}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/magazine/23well/mag-23well-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 816, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/magazine/23well/mag-23well-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1195, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/magazine/23well/23well-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/23/magazine/23well/23well-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/magazine/23well/23well-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Craving an Ice-Cream Fix', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Addiction (Psychology)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Eating Disorders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-20T20:00:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Parker-Pope', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker-Pope', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/33314ee7-9b4d-5ee6-a1b9-f973b927191c', 'word_count': 483, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33314ee7-9b4d-5ee6-a1b9-f973b927191c'}, {'abstract': 'Find out if you are prone to food addiction. Take the Well quiz.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/20/quiz-are-you-addicted-to-food/', 'snippet': 'Find out if you are prone to food addiction. Take the Well quiz.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Are you a food addict? Several studies now suggest that food and drug addictions have much in common, particularly in the way that both disrupt the parts of the brain involved in pleasure and self-control. While the scientific community continues to debate whether food addiction is real, researchers at Yale have devised a Food Addiction Scale to determine if a person shows signs of addictive behavior toward food. Take this short version to see if your cupcake cravings and ice cream binges might qualify as an addiction. And to learn more, read “Craving an Ice-Cream Fix.”Take the Quiz', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quiz: Are You Addicted to Food?', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Addiction (Psychology)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-20T20:02:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Parker-Pope', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker-Pope', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8693b82-558f-562a-ae9d-9df3242d947f', 'word_count': 109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8693b82-558f-562a-ae9d-9df3242d947f'}, {'abstract': 'The photographer for our cover article on Cuba answers questions about capturing the country’s vibrant culture within an ossified system.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/20/how-we-got-those-cuba-pictures/', 'snippet': 'The photographer for our cover article on Cuba answers questions about capturing the country’s vibrant culture within an ossified system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Andrew Moore’s photographs of Cuba are the perfect visual companion to this week’s cover story by John Jeremiah Sullivan, who takes the pulse of the country today and considers what it might be like tomorrow. We wish we could take credit for generating the pictures, but in\xa0fact we stumbled upon them. Originally, we hoped to send a photographer to Cuba and applied for a journalist visa. But in early August, following a months-long wait, the Cuban government turned us down: our request was “too general.” We had asked permission to take portraits of Cubans from all walks of life.\xa0(Sullivan was able to visit the country with his wife, who is Cuban-American.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/magazine/19moore2/19moore2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 826, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/magazine/19moore2/19moore2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1652, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/19/magazine/19moore2/19moor