 of the statistics from the 252-page Mayor’s Management Report, which also serves as a reminder that the first four letters of “numbers” spell “numb.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The number of firefighters burned in firehouses is down by 60 percent. Street cave-ins are plummeting. The adoption rate for children in foster care is climbing even as the Adopt-a-Highway rate is in decline. The average city worker has 12 more square feet of office space than last year.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/21/nyregion/cityroom-stats-2/cityroom-stats-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/21/nyregion/cityroom-stats-2/cityroom-stats-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/21/nyregion/cityroom-stats-2/cityroom-stats-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/21/nyregion/cityroom-stats-2/cityroom-stats-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/21/nyregion/cityroom-stats-2/cityroom-stats-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Your City Government by the Numbers, and More Numbers', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Government by the Numbers (At Least Ones Rarely Noted)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Statistics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-20T21:27:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3526a30-3c45-54f4-8e9f-8252b80c3f97', 'word_count': 728, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3526a30-3c45-54f4-8e9f-8252b80c3f97'}, {'abstract': '“Light and Landscape,” a new exhibition at Storm King Art Center by 14 artists, including Peter Coffin, Anish Kapoor and Roni Horn, is inspired by natural light in its many forms.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/21/arts/design/light-and-landscape-at-storm-king-art-center.html', 'snippet': '“Light and Landscape,” a new exhibition at Storm King Art Center by 14 artists, including Peter Coffin, Anish Kapoor and Roni Horn, is inspired by natural light in its many forms.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOUNTAINVILLE, N.Y. — Storm King Art Center, the bucolic 500-acre sculpture preserve near West Point, makes me think of Steven Spielberg’s “Jurassic Park.” With giant dinosaurs of Modernist abstraction by Alexander Calder, Alexander Liberman and Mark di Suvero looming over the gently rolling landscape, it takes visitors back to a nearly forgotten era — the 1960s — when sheer bigness and industrial materials and processes were compelling signs of sophisticated sculptural ambition. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/21/arts/21LIGHT1_SPAN/LIGHT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy'