ted', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/62c72210-7ac8-5368-999c-4dafdbce587c', 'word_count': 912, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62c72210-7ac8-5368-999c-4dafdbce587c'}, {'abstract': 'An American surfer hanging out in Peru finds himself jailed on trumped-up charges in “186 Dollars to Freedom,” and refuses to play along with corrupt officials to get out.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/21/movies/186-dollars-to-freedom-directed-by-camilo-vila.html', 'snippet': 'An American surfer hanging out in Peru finds himself jailed on trumped-up charges in “186 Dollars to Freedom,” and refuses to play along with corrupt officials to get out.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Almost from the moment we meet Wayne (John Robinson), a towheaded California surfer, we want to shake him. Languishing on a beach in Lima, Peru, in early 1980, catching waves and chasing women on a long-expired visa, he’s oblivious to the growing political turmoil around him. So when he’s arrested by corrupt police on a trumped-up drug charge and thrown into prison, of course he’s too pigheaded to call his parents and obtain the bribes necessary for his release. Why should he? He’s an American!', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/21/arts/21RDP_ONEEIGHTYSIX_SPAN/21RDP_ONEEIGHTYSIX_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/21/arts/21RDP_ONEEIGHTYSIX_SPAN/21RDP_ONEEIGHTYSIX_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/21/arts/21RDP_ONEEIGHTYSIX_SPAN/21RDP_ONEEIGHTYSIX_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 593, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, 