ongs about the fears and desires of minority veterans who have returned from Iraq and Afghanistan.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Holding It Down: The Veterans’ Dreams Project,” the third long-form collaboration between the jazz pianist and composer Vijay Iyer and the poet Mike Ladd, is a multimedia work about minority veterans of the Iraq and Afghanistan wars. It’s from the inside: about divided selves and awful dreams, the opioids the ex-soldiers take to sleep, and their desire to return to who they were before they reported for duty. It’s dense, intense, provocative and honorable.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/21/arts/21VJAY1_SPAN/21VJAY1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/21/arts/21VJAY1_SPAN/21VJAY1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/21/arts/21VJAY1_SPAN/VJAY1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/21/arts/21VJAY1_SPAN/VJAY1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1355, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/21/arts/21VJAY1_SPAN/21VJAY1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/21/arts/21VJAY1_SPAN/21VJAY1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/21/arts/21VJAY1_SPAN/21VJAY1_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sleepless in Kandahar or Mosul, in Raw Verse', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sleepless in Kandahar Or Mosul, in Raw Verse', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Iyer, Vijay', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Harlem Stage', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-20T22:03:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Ratliff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ratliff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/25f2fed5-83be-5c71-ab04-e5fb007ecc55', 'word_count': 670, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25f2fed5-83be-5c71-ab04-e5fb007ecc55'}, {'abstract': 'PBS will find out on Sunday night if it won in categories like best drama for the series “Downton Abbey.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/21/arts/television/emmy-anticipation-runs-high-for-pbs.html', 'snippet': 'PBS will find out on Sunday night if it won in categories like best drama for the series “Downton Abbey.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'EVERY year PBS earns dozens of Emmy nominations and comes away with an armful of golden statuettes. But Paula Kerger, the PBS president, has never gone to the “Primetime Emmy Awards” — until now. “This is such an exciting year, I want to be in the room,” she said. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/21/arts/