 Graduate Center for Studies in Decorative Arts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-20T22:12:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Glenn Collins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Glenn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eecb28d3-64c6-529a-ae5c-777c7ba15431', 'word_count': 1353, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eecb28d3-64c6-529a-ae5c-777c7ba15431'}, {'abstract': 'After the authorities in Cairo painted over a graffiti mural dedicated to the martyrs of the Egyptian revolution this week, the city’s street artists struck back, beginning a new mural on the same wall.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/20/cairos-graffiti-revolutionaries-reclaim-wall/', 'snippet': 'After the authorities in Cairo painted over a graffiti mural dedicated to the martyrs of the Egyptian revolution this week, the city’s street artists struck back, beginning a new mural on the same wall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the Cairene journalist and blogger Soraya Morayef reported on Thursday, many Egyptians who took part in the 2011 street protests, and the battles with the military rulers that followed, were outraged this week when the authorities suddenly painted over an elaborate graffiti mural dedicated to the martyrs of the revolution at the edge of Tahrir Square.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cairo’s Graffiti Revolutionaries Reclaim Wall', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Graffiti', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cairo (Egypt)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-20T22:14:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/22ef139a-dbc1-523d-8211-c41eef4d19ff', 'word_count': 403, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22ef139a-dbc1-523d-8211-c41eef4d19ff'}, {'abstract': 'Junot Díaz’s new collection of stories features a familiar character, Yunior, and themes of family history, cultural mores and romantic infidelity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/23/books/review/this-is-how-you-lose-her-by-junot-diaz.html', 'snippet': 'Junot Díaz’s new collection of stories features a familiar character, Yunior, and themes of family history, cultural mores and romantic infidelity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Junot Díaz writes in an idiom so electrifying and distinct it’s practically an act of aggression, at once alarming and enthralling, even erotic in its assertion of sudden intimacy: “Dude was figureando hard. Had always been a papi chulo, so of course he dove right back into the grip of his old sucias, snuck them down into the basement whether my mother was home or not.” Breaking easily and often out of first-person narration to address his readers directly, Díaz flatters us with his confidences. Yet his prose also throws up walls, equally abruptly and equally seductively. Refusing to condescend or even pause for edification, the narrative moves along at speed, exciting us with its demands. This, then, is the Díaz rhythm: a syncopated stagger-step between opacity and transparency, exclusion and inclusion, defiance and desire.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/books/review/23COHEN/23COHEN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 658, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/books/review/23COHEN/23COHEN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1315, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/books/review/23COHEN/23COHEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/23/books/review/23COHEN/23COHEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/books/review/23COHEN/23COHEN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Love Stories', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Love Stories', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'This Is How You Lose Her (Book)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Diaz, Junot', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-20T22:16:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Leah Hager Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Leah', 'middlename': 'Hager', 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ffc4771-cafa-5be4-a189-c851355710ee', 'word_count': 1217, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ffc4771-cafa-5be4-a189-c851355710ee'}, {'abstract': 'Comedy Central suspended its usual practice of bleeping swear words during a ‘Daily Show’ segment about Fox News.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/20/jon-stewart-unbleeped-the-daily-show-leaves-some-choice-words-intact/', 'snippet': 'Comedy Central suspended its usual practice of bleeping swear words during a ‘Daily Show’ segment about Fox News.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The Daily Show” is not changing its standards concerning which words it will bleep and which it won’t, though it might have seemed that way Wednesday night.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jon Stewart Unbleeped: ‘The Daily Show’ Leaves Some Choice Words Intact', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Language and Languages', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stewart, Jon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Comedy Central', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox News Channel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-20T22:23:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ede85a78-badf-52f9-b5fe-4d25b168ea72', 'word_count': 333, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ede85a78-badf-52f9-b5fe-4d25b168ea72'}, {'abstract': 'Scenes from the Milan fashion week photo diary of Sonny Vandevelde.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/20/photos-of-the-moment-emporio-armani-4/', 'snippet': 'Scenes from the Milan fashion week photo diary of Sonny Vandevelde.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Photos of The Moment | Emporio Armani', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-20T22:25:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sonny Vandevelde', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sonny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vandevelde', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf01b639-9bbf-5fbf-b5f8-0fcdb44dcaf3', 'word_count': 36, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf01b639-9bbf-5fbf-b5f8-0fcdb44dcaf3'}, {'abstract': 'In the area of regulatory law, the United States Court of Appeals for the District of Columbia is controlled by judicial activists who seem willing to negate regulations they do not like.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/21/business/circuit-court-needs-to-let-the-sec-do-its-job.html', 'snippet': 'In the area of regulatory law, the United States Court of Appeals for the District of Columbia is controlled by judicial activists who seem willing to negate regulations they do not like.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The second-most important court in the United States has three vacancies, one of which was created in 2005. It may yet be the institution that dooms many or even most of the Dodd-Frank financial reforms that Congress passed in 2010 and that regulatory agencies have been struggling to put in place since then.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/19/business/norris-75-standardinline/norris-75-standardinline-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/04/19/business/norris-75-standardinline/norris-75-standardinline-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Circuit Court Needs to Let the S.E.C. Do Its Job', 'kicker': 'High & Low Finance', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Circuit Court Needs to Let The S.E.C. Do Its Job', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appeals Courts (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-20T22:42:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Floyd Norris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Norris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9cf9684-9e56-5018-8b99-79c88e3bef49', 'word_count': 1480, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9cf9684-9e56-5018-8b99-79c88e3bef49'}, {'abstract': 'Fereydoon Abbasi, the head of Iran’s Atomic Energy Organization, did not reveal the nature of the information or say when it was presented or to whom.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/21/world/middleeast/iran-atomic-official-says-it-gave-false-nuclear-information-to-fool-spies.html', 'snippet': 'Fereydoon Abbasi, the head of Iran’s Atomic Energy Organization, did not reveal the nature of the information or say when it was presented or to whom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Iran’s top atomic energy official said in an article published Thursday that because of foreign espionage, his government had sometimes provided false information to protect its nuclear program, which Western powers and Israel have called a cloak to develop a nuclear weapons capacity.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iran’s Top Atomic Official Says Nation Issued False Nuclear Data to Fool Spies', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iran’s Top Atomic Official Says Nation Issued False Nuclear Data to Fool Spies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL HAYAT', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abbasi, Fereydoon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Uranium', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'British Secret Intelligence Service', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Atomic Energy Agency', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-20T22:44:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone and Christine Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname'