e shift of American focus from the battlefields of Iraq and Afghanistan to the Pacific Rim.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama’s complex relationship with China began with hope and accommodation but fell into disillusionment after Beijing started flexing its muscles on trade and military questions and proved to be a truculent partner on a variety of global issues.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/21/blogs/rdv-china-military/rdv-china-military-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 655, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/21/blogs/rdv-china-military/rdv-china-military-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1309, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'China Becomes an Issue in the U.S. Campaign', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-20T22:51:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fff182fc-2a02-5949-841d-b089370969a5', 'word_count': 288, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fff182fc-2a02-5949-841d-b089370969a5'}, {'abstract': 'Vahik Pirhamzei plays the son of an old-country Armenian, and that son’s father, in the comedy “My Uncle Rafael.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/21/movies/my-uncle-rafael-with-a-reality-show-armenian.html', 'snippet': 'Vahik Pirhamzei plays the son of an old-country Armenian, and that son’s father, in the comedy “My Uncle Rafael.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'At first glance, the kindly, bearish oldster who headlines “My Uncle Rafael” suggests broad comedy straight ahead: age makeup, cardigan, hat with feather, jokes about an adult E.S.L. class. But Vahik Pirhamzei’s Armenian title character, adapted from his stage routines, turns out to be a sweet and often funny creation: a well-meaning, lumbering family man from the old country who dispenses advice and proudly dons a uniform to serve coffee at his daughter’s shop.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/21/arts/21RDP_MYUNCLE_SPAN/21RDP_MYUNCLE_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/21/arts/21RDP_MYUNCLE_SPAN/21RDP_MYUNCLE_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/21/arts/21RDP_MYUNCLE_SPAN/21RDP_MYUNCLE_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 814, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/21/arts/21RDP_MYUNCLE_SPAN/21RDP_MYUNCLE_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 814, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/21/arts/21RDP_MYUNCLE_SPAN/21RDP_MYUNCLE_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 't