nization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d2dcd83-fb35-5962-ad29-cd5974c0524c', 'word_count': 923, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d2dcd83-fb35-5962-ad29-cd5974c0524c'}, {'abstract': '“Fred Won’t Move Out” looks at the uncomfortable moment when adult children have to switch roles with their parents.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/21/movies/fred-wont-move-out-directed-by-richard-ledes.html', 'snippet': '“Fred Won’t Move Out” looks at the uncomfortable moment when adult children have to switch roles with their parents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Elliott Gould’s septuagenarian character in “Fred Won’t Move Out” is as blunt as the movie’s title. When he barks, “I’m not going,” he means it. Having lived in the same suburban house for more than 50 years with his wife, Susan (Judith Roberts), who has Alzheimer’s, Fred, who has difficulty walking, refuses to accept the reality that their days of living independently are over. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/21/arts/21FRED_SPAN/21FRED_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/21/arts/21FRED_SPAN/21FRED_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/21/arts/21FRED_SPAN/FRED-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/21/arts/21FRED_SPAN/FRED-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, '