ual “incumbency advantage”?', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When the White House Speaks on the Campaign Trail', 'kicker': 'Room for Debate', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-21T00:34:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/33ec2585-420a-59b7-8ca6-e14929e257b8', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33ec2585-420a-59b7-8ca6-e14929e257b8'}, {'abstract': 'Yankees first baseman Mark Teixeira said he plans to travel to Tampa, Fla., to ramp up the rehabilitation efforts on his strained left calf, but he remains unsure when he might return to the lineup.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/20/teixeira-unsure-of-return-is-heading-to-tampa/', 'snippet': 'Yankees first baseman Mark Teixeira said he plans to travel to Tampa, Fla., to ramp up the rehabilitation efforts on his strained left calf, but he remains unsure when he might return to the lineup.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yankees first baseman Mark Teixeira said he plans to travel to Tampa, Fla., on Monday to ramp up the rehabilitation efforts on his strained left calf, but he remains unsure when he might return to the lineup.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Teixeira, Unsure of Return, Is Heading to Tampa', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Teixeira, Mark', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tampa (Fla)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-21T00:36:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zach Schonbrun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zach', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schonbrun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d9d417a-9858-526a-ae00-aeb8ce7b8a73', 'word_count': 242, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d9d417a-9858-526a-ae00-aeb8ce7b8a73'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo’s administration now says its decision on whether to allow hydrofracking in New York State will have to wait until it conducts a review of the potential public health effects.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/21/nyregion/new-york-states-decision-on-hydrofracking-will-await-health-review.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo’s administration now says its decision on whether to allow hydrofracking in New York State will have to wait until it conducts a review of the potential public health effects.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After four years of study by the state, the Cuomo administration now says its decision on whether to allow high-volume hydraulic fracturing in New York will have to wait until it conducts a review of the potential public health effects of the controversial natural gas drilling process.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York State Plans Health Review as It Weighs Gas Drilling', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'State Plans Health Review as It Weighs Gas Drilling', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Natural Gas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Marcellus Shale', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hydraulic Fracturing', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-21T00:41:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mireya Navarro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mireya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Navarro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b9ef934-ed07-5e26-bb87-c79ff9510a12', 'word_count': 611, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b9ef934-ed07-5e26-bb87-c79ff9510a12'}, {'abstract': 'The action film “Dredd 3D,” based on the comic-book character, depicts a judgmental hero in a futuristic western dystopia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/21/movies/dredd-3d-with-karl-urban.html', 'snippet': 'The action film “Dredd 3D,” based on the comic-book character, depicts a judgmental hero in a futuristic western dystopia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s bang, bang, splat, splat for the 98 unmodulated minutes that are “Dredd 3D,” an action movie written by Alex Garland and directed by Pete Travis. Grim, gory and devoid of pleasure, kinetic or otherwise, this is the second big-screen take on the British comics series Judge Dredd, after a 1995 Sylvester Stallone vehicle best remembered for Sly’s shiny, oversize codpiece. Like that movie, this one takes place in ye olde dystopia, a neo-wild West in which the gizmos look futuristic, but everything else — the drooling cretins, generic innocents, slathering villainy and fascistic overtones — is B-movie familiar, although with 100 percent more digitally enhanced carnage.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/21/arts/21DREDD_SPAN/21DREDD_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarg