 mountain of debt and unpaid salaries. Arik halted its flights as workers, including employees at Nigeria’s aviation agencies, the airport authority and the meteorological office, went on strike over what an Aviation Ministry spokesman said were the company’s unpaid bills to the government, amounting to more than $25 million. \xa0 ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nigeria: Airline Suspends Flights', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Africa', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nigeria: Airline Suspends Flights', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Strikes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nigeria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-21T03:18:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Nossiter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nossiter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4a17d48-8f4e-5e27-b7b6-29719d83626c', 'word_count': 108, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4a17d48-8f4e-5e27-b7b6-29719d83626c'}, {'abstract': 'Cricket’s appeal is strong and growing, sports network said.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/20/espn-targets-american-cricket-fans/', 'snippet': 'Cricket’s appeal is strong and growing, sports network said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cricket fans in the United States have a reason to rejoice: the sports network ESPN is now focusing on the game.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'hea