oup immediately claimed responsibility, but suspicions fell on the Shabab, the militant Islamic group that has carried out a wave of bombings since it was driven from the capital last year. The group has threatened more mayhem since the selection of a new president, and it tried to assassinate him before his inauguration last week. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Somalia: Blasts Kill at Least 14', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Africa', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Somalia: Blasts Kill at Least 14', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mogadishu (Somalia)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shabab', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Committee to Protect Journalists', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Somalia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-21T03:22:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/512a7385-adee-574a-a728-38b6e440a942', 'word_count': 131, 'uri': 'nyt://article/512a7385-adee-574a-a728-38b6e440a942'}, {'abstract': 'The life expectancy of whites without a high school degree has fallen in recent years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2012/09/21/health/a-troubling-trend-in-life-expectancy.html', 'snippet': 'The life expectancy of whites without a high school degree has fallen in recent years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The life expectancy of whites without a high school degree has fallen in recent years.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Troubling Trend in Life Expectancy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Longevity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Population', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-21T03:24:33+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Health', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/3f1fb3bd-a66a-5f19-a7e3-b9407ea658e7', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/3f1fb3bd-a66a-5f19-a7e3-b9407ea658e7'}, {'abstract': 'Campaign filings, and disclosures by major “super PACs” supporting both candidates, challenge the appearance of financial strength that Mitt Romney enjoyed over the summer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/21/us/politics/cash-low-romney-striving-to-find-new-large-donors.html', 'snippet': 'Campaign filings, and disclosures by major “super PACs” supporting both candidates, challenge the appearance of financial strength that Mitt Romney enjoyed over the summer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mitt Romney entered the final months of the presidential campaign with a cash balance of just $35 million, racing to find new large donors and rally low-dollar contributors in August even while he raised tens of millions of dollars for the Republican Party.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Low on Cash, Romney Tries to Rally Donors for Final Phase', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cash Low, Romney Striving To Find New Large Donors', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'k