n on the apple front, rebel sympathies die hard.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/21/still-fighting-the-war-in-an-orchard/', 'snippet': 'Metropolitan Diary: A transplanted New Yorker’s encounter at a Virginia orchard indicates that even on the apple front, rebel sympathies die hard.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dear Diary:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Still Fighting the War, in an Orchard', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'APPLES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-21T12:30:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carole Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carole', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/83f7f6de-77b8-57d2-8159-c92e26b34401', 'word_count': 176, 'uri': 'nyt://article/83f7f6de-77b8-57d2-8159-c92e26b34401'}, {'abstract': 'The public editor takes up readers’ questions that have showed up in her e-mail this week.', 'web_url': 'https://publiceditor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/21/on-identifying-a-rape-victim-naming-a-prophet-and-nate-silvers-role-the-public-editor/', 'snippet': 'The public editor takes up readers’ questions that have showed up in her e-mail this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Readers have written to me about a number of issues in the past week. Here’s a roundup of some of their questions and complaints (paraphrased here for clarity), and my answers and comments.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Identifying a Rape Victim, Naming a Prophet, and Nate Silver’s Role', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Silver, Nate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-21T13:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5ea309a-6ca1-5f62-acd0-955dcaaf4602', 'word_count': 703, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5ea309a-6ca1-5f62-acd0-955dcaaf4602'}, {'abstract': 'T offers up a black book for the White City.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/21/essentials-tel-aviv/', 'snippet': 'T offers up a black book for the White City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tel Aviv, Israel’s intoxicating cultural capital, is only 103 years old — or, if you count Jaffa, it’s only 7,603 years old. By turns exultant and exhausting, the city is open around the clock, and seems always to be changing, especially lately, as Tel Aviv’s hotels and restaurants are finally living up to its fabled beaches and nightlife. To go along with our fall travel cover story, T offers up a black book for the White City.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Essentials | Tel Aviv', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tel Aviv (Israel)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-21T13:00:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Grant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9206284c-4f21-558e-8bab-8279384bc2a8', 'word_count': 1082, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9206284c-4f21-558e-8bab-8279384bc2a8'}, {'abstract': 'Internet and cellphone service suspended by state authorities in Kashmir for several hours on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/21/telecom-services-blocked-to-curb-protests-in-kashmir/', 'snippet': 'Internet and cellphone service suspended by state authorities in Kashmir for several hours on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New Delhi– The state government of Jammu and Kashmir ordered telecom companies to block access to YouTube and Facebook in the Kashmir Valley, effective midnight Thursday, to curb potential protests over an amateur video that has angered Muslims.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Telecom Services Blocked to Curb Protests in Kashmir', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'YouTube.com', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kashmir and Jammu (India)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-21T13:01:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pamposh Raina and Betwa Sharma', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pamposh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Raina', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role':