h': 'POINTING FINGERS: Campaign season wouldn’t feel like campaign season without a best seller from Bob Woodward, and — right on cue — his latest, “The Price of Politics,” lands at No. 2 on this week’s hardcover nonfiction list.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/books/review/30woodward/30woodward-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 289, 'width': 278, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/books/review/30woodward/30woodward-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 289, 'width': 278, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/books/review/30woodward/30woodward-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/30/books/review/30woodward/30woodward-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/books/review/30woodward/30woodward-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside the List', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'TBR: Inside the List', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-21T15:51:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gregory Cowles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gregory', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/be088207-7f23-5034-9d00-39432ffb1dff', 'word_count': 616, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be088207-7f23-5034-9d00-39432ffb1dff'}, {'abstract': 'Richard Plepler, the new chief executive of HBO, occupies a role that goes well beyond television and extends into New York’s political, media and entertainment cliques.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/23/fashion/richard-plepler-of-hbo-stands-tall-in-new-yorks-cultural-elite.html', 'snippet': 'Richard Plepler, the new chief executive of HBO, occupies a role that goes well beyond television and extends into New York’s political, media and entertainment cliques.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ON Sept. 5, Cipriani 42nd Street was decked out as if for a 1920s New Year’s Eve soiree: black candelabras with hydrangeas arranged like Art Deco sentinels, a model of a vintage airplane hanging overhead. A woman sang Cole Porter tunes while guests slurped freshly shucked oysters and sipped gin. Some partygoers reclined on metallic gold couches, their shadows cast by illuminated votives. All was designed to invoke the Prohibition-era setting of “Boardwalk Empire,” the HBO show about to enter its third season.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/fashion/23PLEPLER1_SPAN/23PLEPLER1_SPAN-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 361, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/23/fashion/23PLEPLER1_SPAN/23PLEPLER1_SPAN-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 361}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/fashion/23PLEPLER1_SPAN/23PLEPLER1_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 735, 'width': 1024, '