l': 'By Christopher F. Schuetze', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Schuetze', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8f65305-80cb-55af-ac46-154eeeb1e9be', 'word_count': 314, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8f65305-80cb-55af-ac46-154eeeb1e9be'}, {'abstract': 'Many people are experiencing a problem when trying to start Passbook, the new iOS 6 rewards card and ticket management program. Here is how to fix it.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/21/fixing-the-passbook-connection-in-ios-6/', 'snippet': 'Many people are experiencing a problem when trying to start Passbook, the new iOS 6 rewards card and ticket management program. Here is how to fix it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The new Apple software upgrades have resulted in some strange glitches – in my case many of my mail settings spontaneously changed so I couldn’t get or send e-mail.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fixing the Passbook Connection in iOS 6', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Software', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-21T16:05:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roy Furchgott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Furchgott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/385c64ee-7b04-5479-8648-b0f8b30db0a8', 'word_count': 299, 'uri': 'nyt://article/385c64ee-7b04-5479-8648-b0f8b30db0a8'}, {'abstract': 'Scenes from the Milan fashion week photo diary of Carlotta Manaigo.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/21/photos-of-the-moment-moschino-3/', 'snippet': 'Scenes from the Milan fashion week photo diary of Carlotta Manaigo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Photos of The Moment | Moschino', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-21T16:05:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carlotta Manaigo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carlotta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Manaigo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a25bae60-9791-5eb4-ab76-1106327dad8c', 'word_count': 36, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a25bae60-9791-5eb4-ab76-1106327dad8c'}, {'abstract': 'Things can seem black and white when you’re outside a situation, and yet so difficult when you’re entangled in it. How do we address ethical issues in our everyday lives?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/22/your-money/doing-the-right-thing-whatever-that-is-shortcuts.html', 'snippet': 'Things can seem black and white when you’re outside a situation, and yet so difficult when you’re entangled in it. How do we address ethical issues in our everyday lives?', 'lead_paragraph': 'I RECENTLY found myself in a position where I had some moral qualms about a writing assignment. No, it wasn’t for this publication, and no, I wasn’t being asked to make up quotes or leave out pertinent facts. But I was being asked to phrase things in a way I didn’t feel totally comfortable with.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/22/business/SUB-SHORTCUTS/SUB-SHORTCUTS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/22/business/SUB-SHORTCUTS/SUB-SHORTCUTS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/22/business/SUB-SHORTCUTS/SUB-SHORTCUTS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 713, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/22/business/SUB-SHORTCUTS/SUB-SHORTCUTS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1426, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Doing the Right Thing, Whatever That Is', 'kicker': 'Shortcuts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Doing the Right Thing, Whatever That Is', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Institutional)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Personal)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-21T16:06:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alina Tugend', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tugend', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1468d911-9c37-51a6-8752-64f7922c7a9b', 'word_count': 1282, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1468d911-9c37-51a6-8752-64f7922c7a9b'}, {'abstract': 'As replacement referees officiate the first few weeks of the National Football League season, bettors are trying to figure out how the league’s labor dispute might help their wallets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/22/sports/football/factoring-replacement-officials-into-betting-lines.html', 'snippet': 'As replacement referees officiate the first few weeks of the National Football League season, bettors are trying to figure out how the league’s labor dispute might help their wallets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sports gamblers everywhere unite in the perpetual quest to find an edge, and never more so than when they bet on the N.F.L. This search knows no bounds; several years ago, when the league cracked down on helmet-to-helmet hits, handicappers ignored the typical hand-wringing from fans upset about losing their usual fill of brutality and instead just wanted to know how the rule change would affect their bets.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/22/sports/gamblers/gamblers-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 788, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/22/sports/gamblers/gamblers-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1984, 'width': 1527, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/22/sports/gamblers/gamblers-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/22/sports/gamblers/gamblers-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/22/sports/gamblers/gamblers-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Gamblers Watch for Trends as They Study New Officials', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gamblers Watch for Trends As They Study New Officials', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Officiating (Sports)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gambling', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-21T16:07:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Borden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6e7fa3e-189a-5d28-a18f-a082519a4093', 'word_count': 829, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6e7fa3e-189a-5d28-a18f-a082519a4093'}, {'abstract': 'Lawyers and government officials caution would-be whistle-blowers to first understand what they are getting into.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/22/your-money/for-whistle-blowers-consider-the-risks-wealth-matters.html', 'snippet': 'Lawyers and government officials caution would-be whistle-blowers to first understand what they are getting into.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A $104 million award for a whistle-blower is probably enough of an incentive to make most people divulge secrets about their employer, or even their friends, for that matter. The award, the largest ever paid by the Internal Revenue Service, went to Bradley C. Birkenfeld last week for revealing secrets about the Swiss banking system. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': N