 political edition of “Saturday Night Live” drew a huge audience to see Tina Fey’s impersonation of Sarah Palin. On Thursday night, the audience was much smaller, and the comedies that followed didn’t do much better.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/21/without-palin-to-mock-prime-time-s-n-l-has-modest-ratings/', 'snippet': 'In 2008, a special political edition of “Saturday Night Live” drew a huge audience to see Tina Fey’s impersonation of Sarah Palin. On Thursday night, the audience was much smaller, and the comedies that followed didn’t do much better.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Political news did not help NBC Thursday night as the first edition of “Saturday Night Live” in prime time for the election year failed to ignite NBC’s comedy lineup.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Without Palin to Mock, Prime-Time ‘S.N.L.’ Has Modest Ratings', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ratings (Audience Measurement)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-21T16:47:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c883e315-ee10-5187-9c1d-884f45bb74cd', 'word_count': 320, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c883e315-ee10-5187-9c1d-884f45bb74cd'}, {'abstract': 'Dr. Joseph Dutkowsky, an orthopedic surgeon specializing in the care of children, occupies contested territory, both intellectually and theologically, at the top of his profession.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/22/nyregion/a-doctors-ministry-bridging-science-and-spirit.html', 'snippet': 'Dr. Joseph Dutkowsky, an orthopedic surgeon specializing in the care of children, occupies contested territory, both intellectually and theologically, at the top of his profession.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Forty years ago, long before the recent afternoon when Dr. Joseph Dutkowsky knelt at the warped feet of his 4-year-old patient, he was a small-town teenager approaching his Catholic confirmation and needing to select a patron saint. He made an unlikely choice, a newly canonized figure, St. Martin de Porres, the illegitimate child of a former black slave in 16th-century Peru. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/22/nyregion/22religion-cnd/22religion-cnd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/22/nyregion/22religion-cnd/22religion-cnd-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/22/nyregion/22religion-cnd/22religion-cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/22/nyregion/22religion-cnd/22religion-cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/22/nyregion/22religion-cnd/22religion-cnd-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}]