 paying attention to recent trends in footwear.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/21/fancy-footwear-in-milan/', 'snippet': 'There was the distinct impression that the designers at Tod’s, the luxury footwear label, have been paying attention to recent trends in footwear.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was the distinct impression that the designers at Tod’s, the luxury footwear label, have been paying attention to recent trends in footwear. At the company’s spring presentation, which was held at an opulent 1930s mansion that is now a museum, a display of loafers came with surprisingly colorful soles, including versions in yellow, burnt orange and green, reflecting a recent trend in men’s shoes. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fancy Footwear in Milan', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shoes and Boots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Tod's Group", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-21T17:10:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7342fb8-33be-507b-ae60-b87970da117c', 'word_count': 227, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7342fb8-33be-507b-ae60-b87970da117c'}, {'abstract': 'The new video game FarmVille 2 is a slicker, more attractive — and more money-hungry — version of the original.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/22/arts/video-games/the-farmville-2-video-game-is-released.html', 'snippet': 'The new video game FarmVille 2 is a slicker, more attractive — and more money-hungry — version of the original.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From afar, the first FarmVille game on Facebook seemed to be a manipulative horror, a collection of psychological tricks that preyed on our desire to find something predictable in life. It was a simple test that doled out predictable rewards: Plant some seeds with a mouse click, and they would sprout minutes, hours or days later — faster if you paid for them to hurry or if you bugged friends for help.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/21/arts/farm/farm-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/21/arts/farm/farm-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/21/arts/farm/farm-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/21/arts/farm/farm-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1200, 'width': 1920, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/21/arts/farm/farm-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/21/arts/farm/farm-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/21/arts/farm/farm-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cash Crops, Emphasis on the Cash', 'kicker': 'Video Game Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cash Crops, Emphasis On the Cash', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Zynga Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'FarmVille (Video Game)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-21T17:11:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Video Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Totilo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Totilo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0c6f7e8-b29d-57f5-9973-2f4ed9e8ba23', 'word_count': 983, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0c6f7e8-b29d-57f5-9973-2f4ed9e8ba23'}, {'abstract': 'Groups aligned with the Tea Party and other conservative causes are using Jim Crow-era tactics at the ballot box.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/22/opinion/voter-harassment-circa-2012.html', 'snippet': 'Groups aligned with the Tea Party and other conservative causes are using Jim Crow-era tactics at the ballot box.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is how voter intimidation worked in 1966: White teenagers in Americus, Ga., harassed black citizens in line to vote, and the police refused to intervene. Black plantation workers in Mississippi had to vote in plantation stores, overseen by their bosses. Black voters in Choctaw County, Ala., had to hand their ballots directly to white election officials for inspection.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Voter Harassment, Circa 2012', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Voter Harassment, Circa 2012', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'True the Vote', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tea Party Movement', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-21T17:12:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/2bb566bf-f7ca-5229-a470-e02f13c1b209', 'word_count': 588, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2bb566bf-f7ca-5229-a470-e02f13c1b209'}, {'abstract': 'On a spartan journey to the breakaway Caucasus region of Nagorno-Karabakh, the author finds ghost cities, mountain tableaus and strands of personal connection to the area.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/23/travel/off-the-map-in-nagorno-karabakh-a-region-in-the-southern-caucasus.html', 'snippet': 'On a spartan journey to the breakaway Caucasus region of Nagorno-Karabakh, the author finds ghost cities, mountain tableaus and strands of personal connection to the area.', 'lead_paragraph': 'STANDING on a limestone ridge in the foothills of the Lesser Caucasus Mountains, I surveyed the landscape that lay before me. To the west, illuminated by a late-day sun and with ever more craggy peaks as a backdrop, was Vankasar Mountain, capped by a solitary, ancient church. To the east, yellow grassland and scrub stretched to the horizon. And then there was the ghost city of Agdam, its thousands of ruined buildings representing the last exchanges of a late 20th-century conflict that many people have never heard of.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/travel/23EXPLORER_SPAN/23EXPLORER_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/23/travel/23EXPLORER_SPAN/23EXPLORER_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 390}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/travel/23EXPLORER_SPAN/23EXPLORER_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/travel/23EXPLORER_SPAN/23EXPLORER_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2046, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/travel/23EXPLORER_SPAN/23EXPLORER_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/23/travel/23EXPLORER_SPAN/23EXPLORER_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Off the Map in the Black Garden', 'kicker': 'Explorer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Off the Map in the Black Garden', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Armenians', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nagorno-Karabakh', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-21T17:12:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Russ Juskalian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Russ', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Juskalian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7bee5821-0c0c-5ca1-9231-b26315a5c45f', 'word_count': 2010, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7bee5821-0c0c-5ca1-9231-b26315a5c45f'}, {'abstract': 'This spring, La Barrique added a full kitchen to complement its well-chosen wine list. Now, diners can choose from dishes like mint and prawns and rabbit confit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/23/travel/restaurant-report-la-barrique-in-rome.html', 'snippet': 'This spring, La Barrique added a full kitchen to complement its well-chosen wine list. Now, diners can choose from dishes like mint and prawns and rabbit confit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'La Barrique, a wine bar in Rome’s Monti district, has improved with age. It opened in 2001 with a fairly basic wine list, but grew more and more sophisticated, ultimately offering one of the city’s most impressive selections of Champagnes, and Italian and German wines. After adding a full kitchen in the spring, La Barrique now offers hot meals, too.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/travel/23BITES/23BITES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/travel/23BITES/23BITES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1814, 'width': 1814, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/travel/23BITES/23BITES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail