ank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2570577-d57c-5fc2-bbe5-afb5346c7332', 'word_count': 710, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2570577-d57c-5fc2-bbe5-afb5346c7332'}, {'abstract': 'Growing up, I always looked forward to the Jewish holidays, even though my family was not religious. Those were pretty much the only times we had real food in our house, since my father was always dieting. Here are a few of my holiday favorites.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/21/fat-dad-joy-in-holiday-recipes/', 'snippet': 'Growing up, I always looked forward to the Jewish holidays, even though my family was not religious. Those were pretty much the only times we had real food in our house, since my father was always dieting. Here are a few of my holiday favorites.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Growing up, I always looked forward to the Jewish holidays, even though my family was not religious. Those were pretty much the only times we had real food in our house, since my father was always dieting.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fat Dad: Joy in Holiday Recipes', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Yom Kippur', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-21T17:15:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dawn Lerman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dawn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lerman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/772342e2-e10f-518d-9bf6-12d841d7f66f', 'word_count': 2071, 'uri': 'nyt://article/772342e2-e10f-518d-9bf6-12d841d7f66f'}, {'abstract': 'Readers respond to articles about seeing fall leaves and shoes for travel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/23/travel/letters-to-the-editor.html', 'snippet': 'Readers respond to articles about seeing fall leaves and shoes for travel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor: Regarding “Where Fall Deals Grow on Trees” (Sept. 9), I would add Topnotch Resort\xa0in Stowe, Vt., to the list of leaf-peeping trips. Perhaps not the least expensive place, but the heated pool facing Mount Mansfield is worth it, especially at sunset! Lake Winnipesaukee, in New Hampshire, is also stunning in early October. In upstate New York, we’re checking out Tahoe Resort\xa0in the Adirondacks in a few weeks to leaf-peep and hopefully grab one last swim.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Letters to the Editor', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Leaf-Pepping In New England', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-21T17:15:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/241275d1-93ff-54be-9615-adfb6592af1f', 'word_count': 90, 'uri': 'nyt://article/241275d1-93ff-54be-9615-adfb6592af1f'}, {'abstract': 'Have you found your travel bills peppered with extra fees? The Getaway columnist Stephanie Rosenbloom looks at some reasons behind these charges, and offers tips on how to get around them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/travel/100000001796736/the-getaway-fee-for-all.html', 'snippet': 'Have you found your travel bills peppered with extra fees? The Getaway columnist Stephanie Rosenbloom looks at some reasons behind these c