no financial help from their families get more credit for their accomplishments than people who did?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this weekend’s Your Money column, I take a look at a group of haves and have-nots we don’t focus on very often: adults who get financial help from their parents and those who do not.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Measuring the Achievements of Adults Who Don’t Get Family Financial Help', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private and Sectarian Schools', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-21T17:57:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Lieber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lieber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/732b6d00-6520-562d-82fa-68f76019c8c6', 'word_count': 175, 'uri': 'nyt://article/732b6d00-6520-562d-82fa-68f76019c8c6'}, {'abstract': 'A six-story, six-bedroom Modernist brick house is on a prime historic block steps from Central Park.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/21/big-ticket-sold-for-16-million/', 'snippet': 'A six-story, six-bedroom Modernist brick house is on a prime historic block steps from Central Park.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A six-story Modernist brick town house that has weathered the burden of an ugly duckling reputation in its relatively short history at 7 East 69th Street sold for $16 million, in the most expensive sale of the week, according to city records.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Big Ticket | Sold for $16 Million', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Big Ticket: $16,000,000', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Upper East Side (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-21T17:58:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Finn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Finn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ea998b4-e3cb-5728-82e3-abd40737414b', 'word_count': 518, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ea998b4-e3cb-5728-82e3-abd40737414b'}, {'abstract': 'Ben Hatke talks about “Legends of Zita the Spacegirl.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/21/graphic-books-best-sellers-to-the-rescue/', 'snippet': 'Ben Hatke talks about “Legends of Zita the Spacegirl.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'New to the paperback graphic books best-seller list this week is “Legends of Zita the Spacegirl,” by Ben Hatke, at No. 6. It is the second adventure of Zita, an Earth girl, who gets involved in some deep-space adventures. In the first, she had to rescue her best friend. In this one, she must deal with a robot imposter and a “star heart,” a galactic menace that strips down planets to bedrock. Spoiler alert: she comes through with a save, but there are enough loose ends to warrant another installment, which is already in the works. In a recent e-mail interview, Mr. Hatke talked about his work. (As always, the complete best-seller lists can be found here, along with an explanation of how they are assembled.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type':