: 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Oppel', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8051038-8297-566f-91c0-95632fed69cb', 'word_count': 909, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8051038-8297-566f-91c0-95632fed69cb'}, {'abstract': 'A Navy SEAL says goodbye to his best friend, Glen Doherty, who was killed during the attack on the American mission in Benghazi, Libya.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/21/a-letter-to-my-friend-glen-doherty/', 'snippet': 'A Navy SEAL says goodbye to his best friend, Glen Doherty, who was killed during the attack on the American mission in Benghazi, Libya.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Glen A. Doherty, a security contractor and former member of the Navy SEALs, was killed in Libya on Sept. 12, 2012, while defending the American Mission in Benghazi, Libya. During a memorial service for Mr. Doherty and the three other Americans killed in the attack — the Ambassador\xa0J. Christopher Stevens,\xa0Tyrone S. Woods\xa0and\xa0Sean Smith — President\xa0 Obama said of Mr. Doherty: “He believed that his life he could make a difference, a calling that he fulfilled as a Navy SEAL…in Benghazi, as he tended to others, he laid down his life, loyal as always, protecting his friends.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/21/world/africa/atwar-webb-1/atwar-webb-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/21/world/africa/atwar-webb-1/atwar-webb-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'su