3:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Sciaretta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sciaretta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/add6009c-8c1c-5a76-ad79-6355889d8ae6', 'word_count': 966, 'uri': 'nyt://article/add6009c-8c1c-5a76-ad79-6355889d8ae6'}, {'abstract': 'Telling tales across Georgia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/23/t-magazine/telling-tales-with-the-moth.html', 'snippet': 'Telling tales across Georgia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There were scorch marks on the landing outside the guest room at cousin Alvin’s, but I slept well on the first night in Savannah, Ga. A young woman named Elna Baker was in the bedroom across the landing. The next afternoon someone let on that my room was where “that young man set himself on fire, though he died across the hall in the kitchen” and added that Elna’s room was where “that poor heartbroken girl killed herself.” I didn’t tell Elna, but nor did I sleep at all on the second night. I’d wanted to go deep into the heart of storytelling, and now, clearly, I was there.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '66', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/t-magazine/23talk-moth-slide-H3BT/23talk-moth-slide-H3BT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/t-magazine/23talk-moth-slide-H3BT/23talk-moth-slide-H3BT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/t-magazine/23talk-moth-slide-H3BT/23talk-moth-slide-H3BT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/23/t-magazine/23talk-moth-slide-H3BT/23talk-moth-slide-H3BT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/t-magazine/23talk-moth-slide-H3BT/23talk-moth-slide-H3BT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Bus Called Wanda', 'kicker': 'Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Bus Called Wanda', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Moth, The', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buses', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Green, George Dawes', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-21T19:03:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joan Juliet Buck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joan', 'middlename': 'Juliet', 'lastname': 'Buck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0b33a9d-9d89-5f32-90a6-a7152d9356ca', 'word_count': 2847, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0b33a9d-9d89-5f32-90a6-a7152d9356ca'}, {'abstract': 'What do 30,000 Australian wool growers have in common with Jackie Kennedy’s favorite pajama maker?', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/21/evolving-species/', 'snippet': 'What do 30,000 Australian wool growers have in common with Jackie Kennedy’s favorite pajama maker?', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHAT do 30,000 Australian wool growers have in common with Jackie Kennedy’s favorite pajama maker? Now there’s a stretch. But, along with the dinners and parties (on Friday, a performance by Beth Ditto at the Versace house), there is a second tier of events, mainly to promote new collaborations, start-up labels or, in the case of a Woolmark event, merino wool and its long connection to Italian fashion.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Evolving Species', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Evolving Species', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pajamas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-21T19:05:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37ec0b14-9543-5ca6-af8f-7e1915a6192b', 'word_count': 418, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37ec0b14-9543-5ca6-af8f-7e1915a6192b'}, {'abstract': 'There are 20,000 real estate agents in New York City. Three new sales agents tell why they are getting into the business.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/23/realestate/debriefing-so-you-want-to-be-a-broker.html', 'snippet': 'There are 20,000 real estate agents in New York City. Three new sales agents tell why they are getting into the business.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROBIN GOLDBERG, a sales associate at Sotheby’s International Realty, became a licensed agent after making a midlife career change in December 2010: she is, she says, in her 50s and previously worked in finance and fashion. A native New Yorker who grew up in the Bronx, she has lived in a loft in Little Italy for 35 years; her husband, Richard Goldberg, is a wine consultant, and they have two children, 18 and 21.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/realestate/23DEBRIEF1/23DEBRIEF1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1013, 'width': 334, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/realestate/23DEBRIEF1/23DEBRIEF1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1013, 'width': 334, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/realestate/23DEBRIEF1/23DEBRIEF1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/23/realestate/23DEBRIEF1/23DEBRIEF1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/realestate/23DEBRIEF1/23DEBRIEF1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'So You Want to Be a Broker', 'kicker': 'Debriefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'So You Want to Be a Broker', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate Brokers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-21T19:09:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Finn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Finn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c46bb48-8951-57d7-b468-1cd4240542b7', 'word_count': 1492, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c46bb48-8951-57d7-b468-1cd4240542b7'}, {'abstract': 'Linebacker Bart Scott told a reporter in the Jets’ locker room on Friday that he would smack him.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/21/jets-scott-threatens-reporter/', 'snippet': 'Linebacker Bart Scott told a reporter in the Jets’ locker room on Friday that he would smack him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FLORHAM PARK, N.J. – Jets linebacker Bart Scott had to be restrained by a team media-relations official Friday after threatening to punch a reporter in the locker room. The altercation began when the reporter, Dan Leberfeld of Jets Confidential, tried taking a photograph of Scott, who has staged a boycott of the news media for the last three weeks, while he casually chatted with a reporter.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jets’ Scott Threatens Reporter', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scott, Bart', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-21T19:09:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization'