original': 'By THE STAFF', 'person': [], 'organization': 'THE STAFF'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c21f8b9b-2c5f-5cd3-b474-486b86c18a65', 'word_count': 24, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c21f8b9b-2c5f-5cd3-b474-486b86c18a65'}, {'abstract': 'The fall issue of travel provides a different lens on some familiar places and experiences.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/21/now-online-t-fall-travel-2012/', 'snippet': 'The fall issue of travel provides a different lens on some familiar places and experiences.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The fall travel issue of T begins in Tel Aviv, where we visit Claire Danes on the set of the hit spy series, “Homeland.” Next it’s off to Cape Bjare, Sweden, for a look at how the peninsula’s prized potatoes are giving root to a new culinary scene. Such specialization is an art in Tokyo, our third stop, where restaurants and bars with a fascinatingly specific focus — one establishment is dedicated entirely to Tom Waits — break down the city’s vastness. Along the way, we check into Panama City’s hottest hotels, meet the young winemakers who are putting California’s Central Coast on the map and take the pulse in Montreal’s hippest neighborhood. Finally, we set sail at a French boating academy in Ireland with Verlyn Klinkenborg, and Joan Juliet Buck goes on tour with The Moth. See more from the issue >>', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Now Online | T Fall Travel 2012', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-21T19:26:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/32fd50f1-4848-580f-bb66-ca31aaa2b81f', 'word_count': 143, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32fd50f1-4848-580f-bb66-ca31aaa2b81f'}, {'abstract': 'The need to constantly adapt is the new reality for anyone whose job is touched by computing — not just to change careers, but simply to stay competitive on one’s chosen path.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/22/business/to-stay-relevant-in-a-career-workers-train-nonstop.html', 'snippet': 'The need to constantly adapt is the new reality for anyone whose job is touched by computing — not just to change careers, but simply to stay competitive on one’s chosen path.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the last decade, Ty Hallock has steered his business from Web site creation to social media to mobile apps. In three more years, he expects to be back at the drawing board again.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/22/business/MASTERY/MASTERY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/22/business/MASTERY/MASTERY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/22/business/MASTERY/MASTERY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 641, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/22/business/MASTERY/MASTERY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1282, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/22/business/MASTERY/MASTERY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'he