 'nyt://article/bba16492-e987-5605-9766-eb0f1e1ae225', 'word_count': 319, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bba16492-e987-5605-9766-eb0f1e1ae225'}, {'abstract': 'Representative Paul D. Ryan faced a tough and at some points hostile audience, drawing applause when he introduced his mother but eliciting boos and shouts of “No!” when he called for the repeal of Obamacare.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/21/mixed-reaction-for-ryan-at-aarp-convention/', 'snippet': 'Representative Paul D. Ryan faced a tough and at some points hostile audience, drawing applause when he introduced his mother but eliciting boos and shouts of “No!” when he called for the repeal of Obamacare.', 'lead_paragraph': '5:43 p.m. | Updated NEW ORLEANS – Representative Paul D. Ryan faced a tough and at some points hostile audience on Friday at the AARP convention here, drawing applause when he introduced his mother but eliciting wide boos and shouts of “No!” when he called for the repeal of Obamacare, as well as scattered shouts of “47 percent” and “liar” as he attacked other aspects of President Obama’s policies.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mixed Reaction for Ryan at AARP Convention', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AARP', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Orleans (La)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-21T20:29:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard A. Oppel Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Oppel', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1dd9cc46-53a8-5e53-a6c7-45c78f22577b', 'word_count': 800, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1dd9cc46-53a8-5e53-a6c7-45c78f22577b'}, {'abstract': 'Or, actually, bankers.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/21/friday-night-music-the-ladies-who-lunch/', 'snippet': 'Or, actually, bankers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was reading David Glasner’s takedown of James Bullard — the economy will eventually recover, so let’s not do anything to help! — along with Gillian Tett’s critique of quantitative easing based on, well, some whines about how the effects are uncertain. And I found these lyrics running through my head:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Friday Night Music: The Ladies Who Lunch', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-21T20:32:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fbffb80e-254d-5ec4-9bb6-b7ed9302d34b', 'word_count': 69, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fbffb80e-254d-5ec4-9bb6-b7ed9302d34b'}, {'abstract': 'New York City’s ban on large sweetened beverages has been hotly disputed, but these clinical trials show that replacing sugary drinks can slow weight gain in children.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/22/health/avoiding-sugary-drinks-improves-childrens-weight-in-2-studies.html', 'snippet': 'New York City’s ban on large sweetened beverages has been hotly disputed, but these clinical trials show that replacing sugary drinks can slow weight gain in children.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Amid fervid criticism that New York City risks becoming a nanny state, city health officials this month banned the sale of supersize sugar-laden drinks in restaurants and movie theaters. Now scientists have handed the ban’s advocates a potent weapon: strong evidence that replacing sugared drinks with sugar-free substitutes or water really can slow weight gain in children. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/22/us/SODA/SODA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/22/us/SODA/SODA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Avoiding Sugared Drinks Limits Weight Gain in Two Studies', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Avoiding Sugared Drinks Limits Weight Gain in Two Studies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Obesity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Journal of Medicine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soft Drinks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Boston Children's Hospital", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beverages', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'VU University Amsterdam', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sugar', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-21T20:33:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roni Caryn Rabin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roni', 'middlename': 'Caryn', 'lastname': 'Rabin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1fb7fcd2-cd28-5be5-bd30-56fe81156cb9', 'word_count': 895, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1fb7fcd2-cd28-5be5-bd30-56fe81156cb9'}, {'abstract': 'A look at the ratings for NBC’s new slate of shows offers mixed news for the also-ran network.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/21/nbc-gets-early-but-mixed-results-for-new-shows/', 'snippet': 'A look at the ratings for NBC’s new slate of shows offers mixed news for the also-ran network.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the other broadcast television networks opting to roll out most of their fall programming later in the season, NBC has taken the opposite tack by unveiling most of its new shows right out of the gate. The results so far? Mixed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'NBC Gets Early but Mixed Results for New Shows', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murphy, Ryan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Matthew', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-21T20:33:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6ce21c1-bd40-53c7-8dad-89752924df6e', 'word_count': 298, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6ce21c1-bd40-53c7-8dad-89752924df6e'}, {'abstract': 'The husband of one of the jailed members of the Russian punk group accepts the LennonOno Grant for Peace on the group’s behalf.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/21/an-award-and-more-support-for-pussy-riot/', 'snippet': 'The husband of one of the jailed members of the Russian punk group accepts the LennonOno Grant for Peace on the group’s behalf.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The husband of a jailed member of Pussy Riot, the Russian feminist punk-rock group, received an award from Yoko Ono and Amnesty International in New York on Friday. Pyotr Verzilov, the husband of Nadezhda Tolokonnikova, accepted the LennonOno Grant for Peace from Ms. Ono at Liberty Hall in the Ace Hotel. Actually, Mr. Verzilov’s and Ms. Tolokonnikova’s daughter, 4-year-old Gara, accepted the glass sculpture, twirling with it in her pink velveteen dress.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Award and More Support for Pussy Riot', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hitchens, Christopher', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ono, Yoko', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tolokonnikova, Nadezhda', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMNESTY INTERNATIONAL', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name