m the monorail suffered “a severe bite to the leg” and cuts to his back and was in critical condition, the police said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 10:30 p.m. | The monorail glided through the hilly and leafy Bronx Zoo as riders settled in Friday afternoon to enjoy a close-up view of 43 wooded acres, hoping to glimpse antelopes, rhinoceroses, elephants and other exotic Asian animals.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Man Mauled After Leaping Into Tiger Area at Bronx Zoo', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Man Mauled After Leaping Into Tiger Habitat at Bronx Zoo', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bronx Zoo Wildlife Conservation Park', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-21T20:40:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Wendy Ruderman and Patrick McGeehan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Wendy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ruderman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGeehan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f1f63cc-d326-598a-b18f-448bbc44ec0c', 'word_count': 449, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f1f63cc-d326-598a-b18f-448bbc44ec0c'}, {'abstract': 'Jonny Lee Miller joins a long line of actors interpreting the role of Sherlock Holmes, in CBS’s new modern-day series “Elementary.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/23/arts/television/jonny-lee-miller-as-sherlock-holmes-in-elementary.html', 'snippet': 'Jonny Lee Miller joins a long line of actors interpreting the role of Sherlock Holmes, in CBS’s new modern-day series “Elementary.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'SHERLOCK HOLMES, popular culture’s most famous private detective, may not be an actor-proof role, but almost anybody can play it once — anybody, that is, with a passable English accent; a long, narrow face; a penetrating gaze; and the ability to rattle off complicated sentences at head-splitting speed. In the movies the great sleuth has been portrayed by, among others, Michael Caine, Christopher Plummer, Nicol Williamson, Robert Stephens, John Neville, Jonathan Pryce, Peter Cushing, Ian Richardson, and, most recently, Robert Downey Jr., all of whom sensibly took the part in just one or two films. (Mr. Downey has bravely signed on for a third.) The true test of a Holmes, though, is whether an actor’s interpretation can bear the weight of repetition, because Holmes was, after all, a series character, who appeared in 56 short stories and 4 novels between 1887 and 1927. The author Arthur Conan Doyle sometimes wearied of the character, and once even tried to kill him off, but the public wouldn’t allow Doyle to leave his hero forever at the bottom of the Reichenbach Falls. Holmes came back, and has been coming back ever since, again and again and again.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/arts/23SHERLOCK2_SPAN/23SHERLOCK2_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/23/arts/23SHERLOCK2_SPAN/23SHERLOCK2_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/arts/23SHERLOCK2_SPAN/23SHERLOCK2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/arts/23SHERLOCK2_SPAN/23SHERLOCK2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 998, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/arts/23SHERLOCK2_SPAN/23SHERLOCK2_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/23/arts/23SHERLOCK2_SPAN/23SHERLOCK2_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/arts/23SHERLOCK2_SPAN/23SHERLOCK2_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'So Which Borough Is Baker Street In?', 'kicker': 'Television', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'So Which Borough Is Baker Street In?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corporation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holmes, Sherlock (Fictional Character)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miller, Johnny Lee', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cumberbatch, Benedict', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-21T20:41:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Terrence Rafferty', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Terrence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rafferty', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/960ec9ef-4e47-54b3-9cf0-721029a9b177', 'word_count': 1189, 'uri': 'nyt://article/960ec9ef-4e47-54b3-9cf0-721029a9b177'}, {'abstract': 'Photos from Pakist