dered off to chat or buy something in the convenience store, so that every hose is in use.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Etiquette of Electric Car Ownership', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric and Hybrid Vehicles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nissan Motor Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sacramento (Calif)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-21T21:30:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicity Barringer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicity', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barringer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea401a6b-09bf-5b24-9fef-1542789084c5', 'word_count': 834, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea401a6b-09bf-5b24-9fef-1542789084c5'}, {'abstract': 'Scenes from the Milan fashion week photo diary of Sonny Vandevelde.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/21/photos-of-the-moment-sportmax-3/', 'snippet': 'Scenes from the Milan fashion week photo diary of Sonny Vandevelde.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Photos of The Moment | Sportmax', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-21T21:40:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sonny Vandevelde', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sonny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vandevelde', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ed787f9-5707-59cb-82d4-019fc8980c16', 'word_count': 36, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ed787f9-5707-59cb-82d4-019fc8980c16'}, {'abstract': 'Apparently, Mitt Romney really doesn’t see much difference between giving to charity and giving to the government.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/21/taxes-are-not-a-charitable-donation/', 'snippet': 'Apparently, Mitt Romney really doesn’t see much difference between giving to charity and giving to the government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Almost all federal taxpayers who itemize their charitable deductions on their returns deduct the full amount, in order to keep their tax burden as low as possible. Mitt Romney didn’t do that in 2011, according to tax returns released today, leaving $1.8 million un-deducted so he could tell voters he paid a federal tax rate of at least 13 percent. That’s a luxury reserved only for wealthy politicians who can afford to pay an extra few hundred thousand for image purposes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Taxes Are Not a Charitable Donation', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-21T21:46:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Firestone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Firestone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1