cent Medicare tax levied on wage income will be the same in 2013 as it was in 2011. But starting that year, high-income taxpayers will pay more – and in the Romneys’ case – much more.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/21/obamas-health-care-law-would-drive-romneys-tax-bill-up/', 'snippet': 'For most taxpayers, the 2.9 percent Medicare tax levied on wage income will be the same in 2013 as it was in 2011. But starting that year, high-income taxpayers will pay more – and in the Romneys’ case – much more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most Americans pay more in payroll taxes – which finance Social Security and Medicare – than they do in income taxes. The rich are different.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama’s Health Care Law Would Drive Romney’s Tax Bill Up', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-22T00:25:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Floyd Norris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Norris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d328d076-c0e3-5400-9355-f636f317e7cb', 'word_count': 179, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d328d076-c0e3-5400-9355-f636f317e7cb'}, {'abstract': 'For the Obamas and the Romneys, saying they like “Modern Family,” ABC’s hit sitcom, is an easy way to signal that they identify with white middle-class suburbia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/22/us/politics/using-modern-family-to-woo-undecided-voters.html', 'snippet': 'For the Obamas and the Romneys, saying they like “Modern Family,” ABC’s hit sitcom, is an easy way to signal that they identify with white middle-class suburbia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s not so surprising that Michelle Obama said “Modern Family” was one of her family’s favorite shows. And it’s only a little surprising that Ann Romney claimed that she and her husband, Mitt, were also devoted fans. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/22/us/22family/22family-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/22/us/22family/22family-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/22/us/22family/22family-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 780, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/22/us/22family/22family-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1560, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Watching a Hit Sitcom, and Seeing Undecided Voters', 'kicker': 'The TV Watch', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Watching a Hit Sitcom, and Seeing Undecided Voters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Ann', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Modern Family (TV Program)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Michelle', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-22T00:28:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alessandra Stanley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alessandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stanley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71bb52a7-2353-5787-98ad-f10a0a531a39', 'word_count': 772, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71bb52a7-2353-5787-98ad-f10a0a531a39'}, {'abstract': '“Beach Life,” an exhibition of works by Eric Fischl at the Guild Hall Museum in East Hampton, dovetails not only with the local landscape but with a sociology of beachgoing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/23/nyregion/a-review-of-eric-fischl-beach-life-in-east-hampton.html', 'snippet': '“Beach Life,” an exhibition of works by Eric Fischl at the Guild Hall Museum in East Hampton, dovetails not only with the local landscape but with a sociology of beachgoing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If being a starving or unsuccessful artist sounds harrowing, being a successful one comes with its own pitfalls. Take Eric Fischl, for instance. One of the most successful figurative painters of his generation, Mr. Fischl, who was born in 1948, attended the California Institute of Arts when it was a hotbed of post-1960s Conceptualism, but followed a less popular path and remained a painter. In the course of his career, he has been denounced by feminists, who saw his nudes as throwbacks to earlier eras in which women were objectified by male painters, and by postmodernists, who considered his large canvases luxury objects that exemplified rather than opposed the excesses of the 1980s art market.', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/nyregion/23ARTSLI2/0923ARTSLI2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 540, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/nyregion/23ARTSLI2/0923ARTSLI2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1079, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/nyregion/23ARTSLI2/23ARTSLI2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/23/nyregion/23ARTSLI2/23ARTSLI2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/nyregion/23ARTSLI2/23ARTSLI2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bodies, Sand and Changing Times', 'kicker': 'Arts | Long Island', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bodies, Sand and Changing Times', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Hampton (NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fischl, Eric', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Guild Hall Museum', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-22T00:31:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Schwendener', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwendener', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/08125791-2724-524f-9736-4bec6ed70392', 'word_count': 969, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08125791-2724-524f-9736-4bec6ed70392'}, {'abstract': 'Standout performances by Andre Brown, Ramses Barden and others who were once low on the Giants’ depth chart showed that the Giants are more than just their stars.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/22/sports/football/capitalizing-on-chances-giants-reserves-contribute.html', 'snippet': 'Standout performances by Andre Brown, Ramses Barden and others who were once low on the Giants’ depth chart showed that the Giants are more than just their stars.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST RUTHERFORD, N.J. — The Giants knew when they entered the season that they had star power. Two returning 1,000-yard receivers, Hakeem Nicks and Victor Cruz, served as targets for Eli Manning, and the defense relied on three premier pass-rushing ends, Jason Pierre-Paul, Justin Tuck and Osi Umenyiora.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Giants Believe Their Depth Can Carry Them to Great Heights', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Giants Believe Their Depth Can Carry Them to Great Heights', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Andre', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barden, Ramses', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nicks, Hakeem', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bradshaw, Ahmad', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-22T00:36:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Pedulla', 'person':