a9d0-3a01fead5a63'}, {'abstract': 'Why we should celebrate the Emancipation Proclamation.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/21/lincolns-great-gamble/', 'snippet': 'Why we should celebrate the Emancipation Proclamation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Countless school children have been taught that Abraham Lincoln was the Great Emancipator. Others have been taught — and many have concluded — that the Emancipation Proclamation, which Abraham Lincoln announced on Sept. 22, 1862, has been overemphasized, that it was inefficacious, a sham, that Lincoln’s motivations were somehow unworthy, that slavery was ended by other ways and means, and that slavery was on the way out in any case.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lincoln’s Great Gamble', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emancipation Proclamation (1863)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Slavery', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Douglass, Frederick', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greeley, Horace', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lincoln, Abraham', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-22T01:30:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Striner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Striner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2cff9b3a-f702-5e5e-838b-c71ef0e0297c', 'word_count': 1824, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2cff9b3a-f702-5e5e-838b-c71ef0e0297c'}, {'abstract': 'The state attorney general’s office is suing O. Aldon James Jr., the eccentric former leader of the National Arts Club, to recover club money it says Mr. James misused.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/22/nyregion/state-sues-ousted-national-arts-club-leader-o-aldon-james-jr.html', 'snippet': 'The state attorney general’s office is suing O. Aldon James Jr., the eccentric former leader of the National Arts Club, to recover club money it says Mr. James misused.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The long and colorful battle between the National Arts Club and its eccentric former president, O. Aldon James Jr., reached a new phase on Friday, as the state attorney general sued Mr. James for more than $2 million, charging that he misused the club’s money and real estate for his own benefit. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/22/nyregion/JAMES/JAMES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 737, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/22/nyregion/JAMES/JAMES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1415, 'width': 1019, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/22/nyregion/JAMES/JAMES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/22/nyregion/JAMES/JAMES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/22/nyregion/JAMES/JAMES-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Attorney General Sues Club’s Ex-Leader for $2 Million, Citing Misuse of Its Money', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Attorney General Sues Club’s Ex-Leader for $2 Million, Citing Misuse of Its Money', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, O Aldon Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organizations, Societies and Clubs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gramercy Park (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Arts Club', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schneiderman, Eric T', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-22T01:31:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Leland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/45cbbecb-31c2-576c-91cf-667ee3b36a97', 'word_count': 849, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45cbbecb-31c2-576c-91cf-667ee3b36a97'}, {'abstract': 'Since 2006, inflation-adjusted Medicare payments for emergency-room services have increased more quickly than hospital costs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2012/09/22/business/a-sharp-rise-in-medicare-payments.html', 'snippet': 'Since 2006, inflation-adjusted Medicare payments for emergency-room services have increased more quickly than hospital costs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since 2006, inflation-adjusted Medicare payments for emergency-room services have increased more quickly than hospital costs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Sharp Rise in Medicare Payments', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-22T01: