key, Qatar and Saudi Arabia for supporting his government’s opponents, saying they were pursuing the “Libyan model” for Syria. Mr. Assad asserted that he was open to dialogue with his opponents and that the government had already pursued substantial political reforms. Also on Friday, an opposition group, the National Coordination Committee for Democratic Change, reported that three of its members had been arrested in Damascus, the capital. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Syria: Assad Assails Help for Rebels', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Syria: Assad Assails Help for Rebels', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-22T02:01:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kareem Fahim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kareem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fahim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e6948bd-0f45-5087-8b50-78d74b19af3d', 'word_count': 95, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e6948bd-0f45-5087-8b50-78d74b19af3d'}, {'abstract': 'The college football season is young, but Big Ten teams have already put themselves in a 4-8 rut against teams from Bowl Championship Series conferences or Notre Dame.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/22/sports/ncaafootball/big-ten-teams-struggle-against-bcs-foes.html', 'snippet': 'The college football season is young, but Big Ten teams have already put themselves in a 4-8 rut against teams from Bowl Championship Series conferences or Notre Dame.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The season is young, but already the Big Ten has made an impression as a middling conference. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/22/sports/big-ten-1/big-ten-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 702, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/22/sports/big-ten-1/big-ten-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1404, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/22/sports/big-ten-1/big-ten-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'As Losses Stack Up, Big Ten Sees Relevance Head South', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Losses Stack Up, Big Ten Sees Relevance Head South', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Big Ten Conference', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-22T02:03:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Rohan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/034363f1-09a6-5a0b-a624-5f568d8ef6cb', 'word_count': 761, 'uri': 'nyt://article/034363f1-09a6-5a0b-a624-5f568d8ef6cb'}, {'abstract': 'The humanitarian and security situation in northern Mali has eroded under Al Qaeda and the other extremist groups controlling the region, the United Nations Security Council said Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/22/world/africa/security-council-urges-west-africa-to-develop-a-plan-to-assist-mali.html', 'snippet': 'The humanitarian and security situation in northern Mali has eroded under Al Qaeda and the other extremist groups controlling the region, the United Nations Security Council said Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The humanitarian and security situation in northern Mali has eroded under Al Qaeda and the other extremist groups controlling the region, the United Nations Security Council said Friday as it expressed its “grave concern.” It urged West African states to develop a “feasible” collective plan to confront the situation. The initial West African proposal stressed the need to begin any joint military effort from Bamako, the capital, which Mali rejects. World leaders attending the United Nations General Assembly meeting will discuss the problems facing the sub-Saharan region on Wednesday, but no new initiatives on Mali are expected. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Security Council Urges West Africa to Develop a Plan to Assist Mali', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | United Nations', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Security Council Urges West Africa To Develop a Plan to Assist Mali', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bamako (Mali)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Security Council (UN)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mali', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-22T02:09:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil MacFarquhar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacFarquhar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/edfe3ac9-3afb-5be1-9fd5-1873055599b3', 'word_count': 98, 'uri': 'nyt://article/edfe3ac9-3afb-5be1-9fd5-1873055599b3'}, {'abstract': 'David Garza, who runs the Henry Street Settlement, a social service agency, starts and ends his Sundays by walking his Tibetan mastiff and golden retriever.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/23/nyregion/for-david-garza-sundays-a-day-for-dog-walking-and-diners.html', 'snippet': 'David Garza, who runs the Henry Street Settlement, a social service agency, starts and ends his Sundays by walking his Tibetan mastiff and golden retriever.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David Garza, 48, runs the Henry Street Settlement, a social service agency on the Lower East Side, but his Sundays belong to Park Slope, Brooklyn, where he grew up. He still lives on the same block, with his wife, Gina Meggo-Garza, 46, a L’Oreal executive; daughter, Alexandra Garza, 20, a student at Smith College; and two dogs, Beck, a Tibetan mastiff, and Phoebee, a golden retriever. After working in retail and in television production, Mr. Garza joined Henry Street in 2001 and became its executive director in 2010. Though he spends the occasional weekend in the Catskills, he devotes most Sundays to revisiting old neighborhood haunts and exploring new ones.\xa0 ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/nyregion/23ROUTINE1_SPAN/23ROUTINE1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/23/nyregion/23ROUTINE1_SPAN/23ROUTINE1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/nyregion/23ROUTINE1_SPAN/0923ROUTINE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/nyregion/23ROUTINE1_SPAN/0923ROUTINE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/nyregion/23ROUTINE1_SPAN/23ROUTINE1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/23/nyregion/23ROUTINE1_SPAN/23ROUTINE1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/nyregion/23ROUTINE1_SPAN/23ROUTINE1_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Day for Dogs and Diners', 'kicker': 'Sunday Routine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Day for Dogs and Diners', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Henry Street Settl