The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hoopla in the Atlantic Yards in Brooklyn', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hoopla in the Atlantic Yards in Brooklyn', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Atlantic Yards (Brooklyn)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mixed-Use Developments', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Forest City Ratner Companies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Barclays Center (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ratner, Bruce', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Nets', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-22T02:22:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d0539a9-167d-515a-bf81-8ae376ebed3c', 'word_count': 282, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d0539a9-167d-515a-bf81-8ae376ebed3c'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney and Representative Paul D. Ryan are healthy and fit, according to medical summaries released on Friday by the Romney campaign.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/22/us/politics/gop-ticket-is-picture-of-health-doctors-say.html', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney and Representative Paul D. Ryan are healthy and fit, according to medical summaries released on Friday by the Romney campaign.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Medical summaries by doctors who have regularly examined Mitt Romney and Representative Paul D. Ryan were released Friday by the Romney campaign and show both men to be conspicuously healthy and fit. Both men, however, have significant family histories of heart disease and have been closely monitored for it.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'G.O.P. Ticket Is Picture of Health, Doctors Say', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'G.O.P. Ticket Is Picture Of Health, Doctors Say', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-22T02:23:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lawrence K. Altman and Denise Grady', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lawrence', 'middlename': 'K.', 'lastname': 'Altman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Denise', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grady', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2be02e11-d975-5673-a7a7-e1f915f5d025', 'word_count': 787, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2be02e11-d975-5673-a7a7-e1f915f5d025'}, {'abstract': 'With big-money politics presenting an ever greater ethical threat, the House must keep open the Office of Congressional Ethics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/22/opinion/congresss-unpopular-watchdog.html', 'snippet': 'With big-money politics presenting an ever greater ethical threat, the House must keep open the Office of Congressional Ethics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Office of Congressional Ethics, a proven force for good on Capitol Hill, is in need of a fresh lease from House leaders if it is to continue conducting discreet preliminary investigations of corruption allegations against lawmakers. The quasi-independent office has tallied an impressive 101 ethics inquiries in its four years of existence. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Congress’s Unpopular Watchdog', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Congress’s Unpopular Watchdog', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Office of Congressional Ethics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House Committee on Ethics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Institutional)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-22T02:24:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a4fde62-cbe2-5d6e-8dab-c3f322a8068a', 'word_count': 335, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a4fde62-cbe2-5d6e-8dab-c3f322a8068a'}, {'abstract': 'Along with the United States government, businesses will have important roles to play to encourage reform.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/22/opinion/myanmars-fragile-democracy.html', 'snippet': 'Along with the United States government, businesses will have important roles to play to encourage reform.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Now that Daw Aung San Suu Kyi, Myanmar’s revered opposition leader, has given the go-ahead, the United States should further ease sanctions against that country, which is beginning to embrace democracy. Sanctions are intended to encourage positive change and will have value only if affected governments trust that the penalties will be lifted as they make progress. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Myanmar’s Fragile Democracy', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Myanmar’s Fragile Democracy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Aung San Suu Kyi', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Myanmar', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thein Sein', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-22T02:27:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9f7d259-47fd-5682-9f1a-50e2eabd4b1e', 'word_count': 441, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9f7d259-47fd-5682-9f1a-50e2eabd4b1e'}, {'abstract': 'To a lifelong Mets fan, September baseball at Citi Field means a surreal excursion into a cavernous shell abandoned by optimism long ago.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/22/sports/baseball/mets-ending-season-that-has-questioned-fan-loyalty.html', 'snippet': 'To a lifelong Mets fan, September baseball at Citi Field means a surreal excursion into a cavernous shell abandoned by optimism long ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is with no traditional autumnal sense of baseball anticipation that my son Nick and I ride the rumbling 7 train to Citi Field for a couple of games with the hated Phillies. We are father-and-son rubber-neckers drawn to the spectacular car wreck that is our team.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Turn Out the Lights on the Mets', 'kicker': 'An Appraisal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Turn Out The Lights', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citi Field (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-22T02:31:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Powell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Powell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'An Appraisal', '_id': 'nyt://article/6477b0ec-ce8b-5579-9549-01e39b566ca0', 'word_count': 2447, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6477b0ec-ce8b-5579-9549-01e39b566ca0'}, {'abstract': 'The Moscow police are searching for a band of vigilante “dog hunters” who have set traps with poisoned meat to kill stray dogs. But the poison has killed pets instead.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/22/world/europe/russia-dogs-poisoned-in-moscow.html', 'snippet': 'The Moscow police are searching for a band of vigilante “dog hunters” who have set traps with poisoned meat to kill stray dogs. But the poison has killed pets instead.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The Moscow police are searching for a band of vigilante “dog hunters” who have set traps with poisoned meat to kill stray dogs. But the poison has killed pets instead, and on Friday the police opened a criminal investigation. Last week, residents of a Moscow neighborhood complained that several pets had mysteriously died just as warnings to pet owners began to appear in a local park. “If you don’t follow the rules of walking your dog — it will die,” said one of the fliers, a Russian news agency reported. Packs of stray dogs are a common sight in Russia; the government estimates that tens of thousands roam Moscow’s streets. The police say that several dogs have been killed recently, but Moscow residents say that the number is actually in the dozens. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia: Dogs Poisoned in Moscow', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia: Dogs Poisoned in Moscow', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dogs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Moscow (Russia)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poisoning and Poisons', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-22T02:32:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Roth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/31878459-6de3-553b-9854-0af7986d9e56', 'word_count': 134, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31878459-6de3-553b-9854-0af7986d9e56'}, {'abstract': 'Emblematic of Mr. Obama’s good-but-not-great polling day were a set of polls, which had him ahead in four of the five swing states: Ohio, Virginia, Colorado and North Carolina.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/21/sept-21-presidential-race-changes-but-swing-states-stay-the-same/', 'snippet': 'Emblematic of Mr. Obama’s good-but-not-great polling day were a set of polls, which had him ahead in four of the five swing states: Ohio, Virginia, Colorado and North 