Outsiders, get together over e-mail to discuss the biggest games and story lines around the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Each week, two of college football’s seasoned observers, Pre-Snap Read’s Paul Myerberg and Robert Weintraub of Football Outsiders, get together over e-mail to discuss the biggest games and story lines around the country.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Matchups: Night Starts and B.C.S. Implications', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'College Letter Men', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-22T04:18:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Myerberg and Robert Weintraub', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Myerberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weintraub', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a1983a2-2ccc-599b-a523-af29edac7eb0', 'word_count': 691, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a1983a2-2ccc-599b-a523-af29edac7eb0'}, {'abstract': 'Linebacker Khaseem Greene says his long layoff after a broken leg helped him improve his game and rediscover his love of football.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/22/sports/ncaafootball/healed-from-injury-khaseem-greene-leads-rutgers-in-tackles.html', 'snippet': 'Linebacker Khaseem Greene says his long layoff after a broken leg helped him improve his game and rediscover his love of football.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PISCATAWAY, N.J. — Less than five minutes remained in the 2011 season when Rutgers linebacker Khaseem Greene charged through the Iowa State offensive line and forced an incomplete pass. Then he was flat on his back, surrounded by trainers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Healed From Injury, Greene Leads Rutgers in Tackles', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rutgers’s Greene, Healed From Injury, Leads Team in Tackles', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greene, Khaseem', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-22T04:26:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Caldwell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caldwell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cdc1e41c-cb13-5b08-885d-365b01652ab5', 'word_count': 796, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cdc1e41c-cb13-5b08-885d-365b01652ab5'}, {'abstract': 'The income disparity in New York has hardly diminished, but pop culture’s recent portrayals of the class wars haven’t been indicative of the boiling debate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/23/nyregion/rich-as-the-devil.html', 'snippet': 'The income disparity in New York has hardly diminished, but pop culture’s recent portrayals of the class wars haven’t been indicative of the boiling debate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The television series “666 Park Avenue,” whose title invites little thematic speculation, arrives next week on ABC and will be, to the best of my knowledge, the second time an architecturally significant apartment building in Manhattan has been deployed as a fictional vessel for Satanism. The reason would seem fairly clear; you just can’t situate allegories of demonic venality or depraved ambition as persuasively in places like Philadelphia, White Plains or San Diego. Had New York City as we now know it existed in 1600, civilization would have been forever left to reckon with the Macbeths of East 78th Street.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/nyregion/23BIGCITY2_SPAN/23BIGCITY2_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/23/nyregion/23BIGCITY2_SPAN/23BIGCITY2_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/nyregion/23BIGCITY2_SPAN/23JPBIGCITY2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/nyregion/23BIGCITY2_SPAN/23JPBIGCITY2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/nyregion/23BIGCITY2_SPAN/23BIGCITY2_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/23/nyregion/23BIGCITY2_SPAN/23BIGCITY2_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rich as the Devil, but No Gordon Gekko', 'kicker': 'Big City', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_hea