: 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/22/fashion/runway-womens/bottegaveneta_spring13app-slide-VZUV/bottegaveneta_spring13app-slide-VZUV-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 902, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/22/fashion/runway-womens/bottegaveneta_spring13app-slide-VZUV/bottegaveneta_spring13app-slide-VZUV-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 902}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/22/fashion/runway-womens/bottegaveneta_spring13app-slide-VZUV/bottegaveneta_spring13app-slide-VZUV-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 681, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/22/fashion/runway-womens/bottegaveneta_spring13app-slide-VZUV/bottegaveneta_spring13app-slide-VZUV-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1363, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bottega Veneta: Spring 2013 RTW', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-22T14:22:36+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Fashion & Style', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': "Women's Runway", 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/ec6a2f9a-f11f-5072-a925-5a4b94021e1f', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/ec6a2f9a-f11f-5072-a925-5a4b94021e1f'}, {'abstract': 'Scenes from the Milan fashion week photo diary of Sonny Vandevelde.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/22/photos-of-the-moment-bottega-veneta-7/', 'snippet': 'Scenes from the Milan fashion week photo diary of Sonny Vandevelde.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Photos of The Moment | Bottega Veneta', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-22T14:58:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sonny Vandevelde', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sonny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vandevelde', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0549e6a6-b2ae-58a8-b9ce-0a7a71be515b', 'word_count': 36, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0549e6a6-b2ae-58a8-b9ce-0a7a71be515b'}, {'abstract': 'The Mets badly want R.A. Dickey to reach 20 victories. But three of the last six Cy Young Awards were given to pitchers with no more than 16 victories.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/22/mets-knuckleballer-has-an-honor-at-his-fingertips/', 'snippet': 'The Mets badly want R.A. Dickey to reach 20 victories. But three of the last six Cy Young Awards were given to pitchers with no more than 16 victories.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Terry Collins, the Mets’ manager, sat gloomily at a news conference after his team lost to Philadelphia on Monday. His staff ace, R. A. Dickey, had lost despite allowing only two earned runs in seven innings. The Mets badly want Dickey to reach 20 victories, the magic threshold for a starting pitcher.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mets’ Knuckleballer Has an Honor at His Fingertips', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Extra Bases: Knuckleballer Has an Honor At His Fingertips', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cy Young Award', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dickey, R A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-22T15:05:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf60559a-5ca2-5fe2-affd-eab0413b3418', 'word_count': 929, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf60559a-5ca2-5fe2-affd-eab0413b3418'}, {'abstract': 'And you can see it in the numbers.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/22/inequality-kills/', 'snippet': 'And you can see it in the numbers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kathleen Geier makes a point I should have noticed. She points to the shocking story in yesterday’s Times about sharply declining life expectancies for less-educated whites, and points out that these declines took place at a time of rapidly rising income inequality. And we have lots of evidence that low socioeconomic status leads to higher mortality — even if you correct for things like availability of health insurance.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Inequality Kills', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-22T15:06:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd3cce4b-92ce-5296-9d16-9e97a02990ba', 'word_count': 126, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd3cce4b-92ce-5296-9d16-9e97a02990ba'}, {'abstract': 'A campaign to end demand for prostitution will harm trafficking victims and sex workers more than it helps them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/23/opinion/sunday/ending-demand-wont-stop-prostitution.html', 'snippet': 'A campaign to end demand for prostitution will harm trafficking victims and sex workers more than it helps them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEATEN. Burned. Branded with a bar code or with a pimp’s name carved into her thigh. Thrown into the trunk of a car for punishment. Forced to provide sexual services for countless callous and violent men. This is the dominant image of young people in the sex trade, and it is fueling deeply flawed campaigns against prostitution. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/sunday-review/23PROSTITUTION1/23PROSTITUTION1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 446, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/23/sunday-review/23PROSTITUTION1/23PROSTITUTION1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 446}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/sunday-review/23PROSTITUTION1/23PROSTITUTION1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/sunday-review/23PROSTITUTION1/23PROSTITUTION1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'c