 tax credit is due to expire, officials in Oregon will cut the ribbon on what some say is the largest onshore wind farm in the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The wind industry’s main trade association is predicting that new installations will fall to zero without a renewal of the production tax credit, which applies only to projects finished by New Year’s Eve. Since renewal is iffy, some wind machine factories are already shutting down, as my colleague Diane Cardwell reported on Friday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wind Sprints to the Cliff', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Aid (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wind Power', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wyden, Ron', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Wind Energy Assn', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Energy Department', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Electric Company', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sumitomo Corporation', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oregon', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-22T17:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://