owd', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c6a93b2-e20c-527f-92d6-67be761b1dac', 'word_count': 838, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c6a93b2-e20c-527f-92d6-67be761b1dac'}, {'abstract': 'The government needs to do a better job of getting out the word about federal programs that help students in debt.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/23/opinion/sunday/avoiding-student-loan-default.html', 'snippet': 'The government needs to do a better job of getting out the word about federal programs that help students in debt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The federal student loan program offers flexible payment plans that are supposed to keep borrowers out of default even when they have lost their jobs and can afford almost nothing in monthly payments. But these programs will never serve their intended purpose until the government does a better job of getting out the word about them and makes them easier to use. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Avoiding Student Loan Default', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Avoiding Student Loan Default', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Student Loans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Department (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-22T17:21:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f880d02-f8f2-5031-b90d-19e109559a74', 'word_count': 604, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f880d02-f8f2-5031-b90d-19e109559a74'}, {'abstract': 'A damaging court ruling would obliterate privacy rights and the Fourth Amendment’s warrant requirement.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/23/opinion/sunday/when-gps-tracking-violates-privacy-rights.html', 'snippet': 'A damaging court ruling would obliterate privacy rights and the Fourth Amendment’s warrant requirement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the right to personal privacy to survive in America in this digital age, courts must be meticulous in applying longstanding privacy protections to new technology. This did not happen in an unfortunate ruling last month by a three-judge panel of the United States Court of Appeals for the Sixth Circuit. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When GPS Tracking Violates Privacy Rights', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When GPS Tracking Violates Privacy Rights', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Positioning System', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cellular Telephones', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fourth Amendment (US Constitution)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-22T17:24:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/9bdcd983-5236-5557-b441-9f7484c110b9', 'word_count': 469, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9bdcd983-5236-5557-b441-9f7484c110b9'}, {'abstract': 'Whenev