', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'America the Anxious', 'kicker': 'Anxiety', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Anxiety and Stress', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Happiness', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-22T18:26:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ruth Whippman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ruth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Whippman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7dc8d8d-acf7-5f2a-b116-8627644df2e6', 'word_count': 1294, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7dc8d8d-acf7-5f2a-b116-8627644df2e6'}, {'abstract': 'Venezuela’s national drug police took part in an operation directed from Washington to capture one of South America’s most wanted kingpins.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/23/world/americas/unlikely-cooperation-led-to-drug-lords-arrest-in-venezuela.html', 'snippet': 'Venezuela’s national drug police took part in an operation directed from Washington to capture one of South America’s most wanted kingpins.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CARACAS, Venezuela — To President Hugo Chávez, the United States has long been The Enemy, the imperialist power that seeks to undermine his Socialist-inspired revolution, that plots to oust him from office — and that he loves to taunt. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/world/23venez-span/23venez-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 357, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name