 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3909ef45-c4b6-5ffc-a443-ac7ffd1e5e9a', 'word_count': 247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3909ef45-c4b6-5ffc-a443-ac7ffd1e5e9a'}, {'abstract': 'Secret recordings made by President Kennedy, which include Oval Office discussions about Cuba and space exploration, will now be made accessible to the general public.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/23/us/in-kennedy-secret-recordings-historys-raw-materials.html', 'snippet': 'Secret recordings made by President Kennedy, which include Oval Office discussions about Cuba and space exploration, will now be made accessible to the general public.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON — President John F. Kennedy opened the newspaper one day in 1963 and learned to his horror that military aides had built a hospital bedroom for his pregnant wife at an air base on Cape Cod in case she went into labor. He thought the $5,000 spent on the furniture was wasteful and would be a public-relations disaster that would prompt Congress to cut his military budget. The angry president picked up the phone.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/us/JFK/JFK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/23/us/JFK/JFK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 345}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/us/JFK/JFK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 807, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/us/JFK/JFK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1614, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, '