pot in the Eastern Conference semifinals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/23/sports/basketball/with-playoff-berth-secured-liberty-unload-on-shock.html', 'snippet': 'The Liberty ended their regular season with a win against the Tulsa Shock, a contract extension for Cappie Pondexter and a spot in the Eastern Conference semifinals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEWARK — Citing recent champions who capitalized on the momentum of late-season surges, Liberty Coach John Whisenant says his team is in the right spot to challenge for the W.N.B.A. title.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Playoff Berth Secured, Liberty Unload on Shock', 'kicker': 'Liberty 91, Shock 74', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pierson Leads Liberty', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Liberty', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tulsa Shock', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pondexter, Cappie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-23T00:01:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Seth Berkman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Berkman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/baf2a20f-f07b-55bb-92a5-919d6d5aeb04', 'word_count': 589, 'uri': 'nyt://article/baf2a20f-f07b-55bb-92a5-919d6d5aeb04'}, {'abstract': 'Of the 20 acts scheduled for the coming 38th season of “Austin City Limits,” only five have been on the show before. In advance of this season’s Oct. 6 premiere, a look at this year’s freshman class.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/23/us/giving-viewers-some-new-music-to-treasure.html', 'snippet': 'Of the 20 acts scheduled for the coming 38th season of “Austin City Limits,” only five have been on the show before. In advance of this season’s Oct. 6 premiere, a look at this year’s freshman class.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last month, just as Tim McGraw was about to sit down for his post-set interview in the “Austin City Limits” studio, his eyes wandered toward a framed photograph of George Strait’s first appearance on the PBS concert showcase. Mr. McGraw immediately ran back to his dressing room, grabbed his wife, Faith Hill, and showed her Mr. Strait’s baby face, beaming from beneath a tall white cowboy hat.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '31B', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/us/sub23TTLanger/sub23TTLanger-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 718, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/us/sub23TTLanger/sub23TTLanger-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1437, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Giving Viewers Some New Music to Treasure', 'kicker': 'Texas Monthly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Giving Viewers Some New Music to Treasure', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Austin (Tex)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Alabama Shakes (Music Group)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Radiohead', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGraw, Tim', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Edmonson, Kat', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Staples, Mavis', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-23T00:07:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Langer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Langer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/265f3f68-1732-5431-9648-e189966fe859', 'word_count': 908, 'uri': 'nyt://article/265f3f68-1732-5431-9648-e189966fe859'}, {'abstract': 'In Wisconsin on Saturday, President Obama said Mitt Romney’s vision for the country had no room for the middle class, the elderly, students or veterans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/23/us/politics/in-ryans-wisconsin-obama-again-attacks-47-percent-remarks.html', 'snippet': 'In Wisconsin on Saturday, President Obama said Mitt Romney’s vision for the country had no room for the middle class, the elderly, students or veterans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MILWAUKEE — President Obama traveled to the home turf of his opponent’s running mate, Representative Paul D. Ryan, on Saturday, reprising his attack on Mitt Romney for remarks he made behind closed doors characterizing Obama voters as the 47 percent of the population who depend on government handouts and do not pay federal income taxes.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/us/obama/obama-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/23/us/obama/obama-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 345}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/us/obama/obama-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 746, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy':