adline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-23T07:45:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c5270da-e381-54e5-83fb-adc4c4efb08e', 'word_count': 20, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c5270da-e381-54e5-83fb-adc4c4efb08e'}, {'abstract': 'Embassies used to be essential places for journalists and diplomats to trade real information. All that changed even before the Chris Stevens tragedy.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/23/in-praise-of-what-has-been-lost-at-u-s-embassies/', 'snippet': 'Embassies used to be essential places for journalists and diplomats to trade real information. All that changed even before the Chris Stevens tragedy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rendezvous regular Mark McDonald asked for fresh U.S. embassy stories. Here is an old one from back when America waded into Vietnam, China was a forbidding foe, and Cold War rivals could have easily blown each other off the map.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Praise of What Has Been Lost at U.S. Embassies', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-23T10:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mort Rosenblum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mort', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenblum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0aa50e78-06a2-58c8-a66e-839874b33d6b', 'word_count': 632, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0aa50e78-06a2-58c8-a66e-839874b33d6b'}, {'abstract': 'Home teams have beaten the point spread in 61.3 percent of their games this season, and the replacement officials may have something to do with it.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/23/a-new-home-advantage-in-the-n-f-l/', 'snippet': 'Home teams have beaten the point spread in 61.3 percent of their games this season, and the replacement officials may have something to do with it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the N.F.L.’s replacement officials try their luck again today, here’s a trend to monitor:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Home Advantage in the N.F.L.?', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Officiating (Sports)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-23T11:14:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/625a3031-8188-5382-9d04-e22ac127100d', 'word_count': 324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/625a3031-8188-5382-9d04-e22ac127100d'}, {'abstract': 'Spoiled children like me aren’t the problem. It’s spoiled children who think they’re entitled to their privilege who are trouble.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/23/im-spoiled-but-im-not-a-brat/', 'snippet': 'Spoiled children like me aren’t the problem. It’s spoiled children who think they’re entitled to their privilege who are trouble.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While growing up, I would routinely choose to play Pokémon over doing the dishes. The fact that I had a choice never struck me as strange. While I certainly had chores — cleaning my room when it became unlivable, walking the dog I had begged for, attending the piano lessons my parents had paid for — I had very few household responsibilities. You could say I was spoiled. And thanks to the recent discourse surrounding my generation’s upbringing, I’ve just discovered that I’m one of millions of 21st-century American kids who have been shielded from hardship by overprotective parents.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘I’m Spoiled, but I’m Not a Brat’', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (Secondary)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-23T12:00:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maria Yagoda', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maria', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yagoda', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aefee538-7f9b-5dd1-94d1-b394a037cd4e', 'word_count': 803, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aefee538-7f9b-5dd1-94d1-b394a037cd4e'}, {'abstract': 'After President Obama carried Nebraska’s Second District in 2008, Republicans redrew the district lines to make it even more Republican-leaning in 2012.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/23/nebraska-g-o-p-draws-a-tougher-map-for-obama/', 'snippet': 'After President Obama carried Nebraska’s Second District in 2008, Republicans redrew the district lines to make it even more Republican-leaning in 2012.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We continue our Presidential Geography series, a one-by-one examination of the peculiarities that drive the politics in all 50 states and the District of Columbia. Here is a look at Nebraska, the Cornhusker State. FiveThirtyEight spoke with John R. Hibbing, a professor of political science at the University of Nebraska-Lincoln, and Paul Landow, a professor of political science at the University of Nebraska at Omaha.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nebraska G.O.P. Draws a Tougher Map for Obama', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2008', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Redistricting and Reapportionment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nebraska', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-23T12:06:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Micah Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Micah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1f979d5-4ca3-5e7a-be73-92dfc3787737', 'word_count': 932, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1f979d5-4ca3-5e7a-be73-92dfc3787737'}, {'abstract': 'Everyone in Milan seems taken with minimalism this season.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/23/getting-some-air-in-milan/', 'snippet': 'Everyone in Milan seems taken with minimalism this season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Everyone in Milan seems taken with minimalism this season. “Firmness… sparseness as elegance,” the Marni show notes began. Scraping away most of the Marni trinkets and funky layers, Consuelo Castiglioni presented a very spare collection indeed. The newsy portions included sleeveless dresses that floated over the body, with their shape enhanced by crisp fabrics and flattering pleats and folds. Nothing seemed too much in this appealing show. The checked outfits that opened the show had a slight 3-D effect, and Ms. Castiglioni included a few more eye tricks later with dresses in a green half-circle print cut and assembled on a diagonal. But she was right to concentrate on her sculptural A-line pieces in solid neutral tones, some as simple as a loose cotton top over flared matching shorts and others with a kind of crazily deconstructed peplum.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Getting Some Air in Milan', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-23T12:17:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1683bc68-5efb-5c70-8086-dac87bc25537', 'word_count': 201, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1683bc68-5efb-5c70-8086-dac87bc25537'}, {'abstract': 'One could find all kinds of meaning in Jil Sander’s show and her return to the label after an eight-year absence.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/23/jil-sander-minimalism-with-a-kick/', 'snippet': 'One could find all kinds of meaning in Jil Sander’s show and her return to the label after an eight-year absence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One could find all kinds of meaning in Jil Sander’s show and her return to the label after an eight-year absence. There was the white set with a concave, spherical ceiling that resembled an architect’s idea of a modern, corporate conference room. One woman — Ms. Sander herself — was going to speak that day and the audience, seated around the square platform, was going to listen.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jil Sander: Minimalism With a Kick', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sander, Jil', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-23T13:09:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/56db7f3d-89ea-56be-9e4e-41cc8e36fb7d', 'word_count': 392, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56db7f3d-89ea-56be-9e4e-41cc8e36fb7d'}, {'abstract': 'Myanmar’s opposition leader, Aung San Suu Kyi, visited the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/21/opinion/heng-cartoon-aung-san-suu-kyi-visits-us.html', 'snippet': 'Myanmar’s opposition leader, Aung San Suu Kyi, visited the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Myanmar’s opposition leader, Aung San Suu Kyi, visited the United States.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/21/opinion/21iht-edheng-image/21iht-edheng-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 423, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/21/opinion/21iht-edheng-image/21iht-edheng-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'x