l': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/09/23/fashion/runway-womens/marni-spring-2013-rtw.html', 'snippet': 'Milan', 'lead_paragraph': 'Milan', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/fashion/runway-womens/marni_spring13app-slide-4UMZ/marni_spring13app-slide-4UMZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/23/fashion/runway-womens/marni_spring13app-slide-4UMZ/marni_spring13app-slide-4UMZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/fashion/runway-womens/marni_spring13app-slide-4UMZ/marni_spring13app-slide-4UMZ-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/fashion/runway-womens/marni_spring13app-slide-4UMZ/marni_spring13app-slide-4UMZ-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1365, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Marni: Spring 2013 RTW', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-23T14:46:22+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Fashion & Style', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': "Women's Runway", 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/d8f8a801-a1a1-5a60-a603-b2efff2d2baa', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/d8f8a801-a1a1-5a60-a603-b2efff2d2baa'}, {'abstract': 'Not the same.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/23/expectations-and-the-confidence-fairy/', 'snippet': 'Not the same.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some readers have asked whether there isn’t an inconsistency between my view that the Fed can promote economic recovery by changing expectations about future policy, and my ridicule of austerity proponents who invoke “confidence” as a reason to believe that austerity will actually be expansionary. But there isn’t really any inconsistency; it’s an orders of magnitude thing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Expectations and the Confidence Fairy', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-23T14:50:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc771004-ce79-59c3-a3cb-629df8c4ec62', 'word_count': 280, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc771004-ce79-59c3-a3cb-629df8c4ec62'}, {'abstract': 'Why does Romney love Phil Gramm?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/23/mr-mental-recession/', 'snippet': 'Why does Romney love Phil Gramm?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Brad DeLong is upset by the illogic of John Taylor and Phil Gramm’s attack on the Fed. Indeed: it boggles the mind that they believe that a downside of expansionary policy now is that it will require contractionary policy once the economy has recovered. Um, isn’t that exactly what you want monetary policy to do — boost the economy when it’s weak, take away the punchbowl when the party gets going?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mr. Mental Recession', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-23T14:58:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c1f36db-227f-5152-b8e2-b971eaf28341', 'word_count': 147, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c1f36db-227f-5152-b8e2-b971eaf28341'}, {'abstract': 'Joe Wiegand, who looks like Theodore Roosevelt, was the inspiration for a sculpture of the former president that will soon be housed at the American Museum of Natural History.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/23/teddy-by-kilgannon/', 'snippet': 'Joe Wiegand, who looks like Theodore Roosevelt, was the inspiration for a sculpture of the former president that will soon be housed at the American Museum of Natural History.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROCK TAVERN, N.Y. — Double bully!', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Roosevelt Mimic Plays Him for Posterity', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Roosevelt Mimic Plays Him for Posterity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-23T15:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Corey Kilgannon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Corey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kilgannon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/30a61c9d-5eec-5de4-91b5-06c9fab04cef', 'word_count': 706, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30a61c9d-5eec-5de4-91b5-06c9fab04cef'}, {'abstract': 'If Apple continues on its current trajectory, it might break a barrier on April 9, 2015, that no company has ever touched.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.