c-5aa7-b1eb-e73a70160446'}, {'abstract': 'A week after the giant panda cub was born to great fanfare, it was found dead of causes that were not yet clear.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/24/us/newborn-panda-cub-dies-at-national-zoo.html', 'snippet': 'A week after the giant panda cub was born to great fanfare, it was found dead of causes that were not yet clear.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — A giant panda’s distress call sent keepers at the National Zoo rushing to the aid of her tiny, lifeless cub on Sunday, and the elation over the cub’s birth just a week earlier turned to despair over its death.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Joy Turns to Despair at National Zoo as Newborn Panda Is Found Dead', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Joy Turns to Despair at National Zoo As Newborn Panda Is Found Dead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pandas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Smithsonian National Zoological Park', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-23T18:48:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emmarie Huetteman and Michael Schwirtz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emmarie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Huetteman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwirtz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e5dff0d-8864-5c7d-9d10-2bb43ef2484d', 'word_count': 889, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e5dff0d-8864-5c7d-9d10-2bb43ef2484d'}, {'abstract': 'In “Mary Broome,” a comedy by Allan Monkhouse, known for his acerbic take on the English bourgeoisie, a man leading a life of privilege is suddenly thrust into poverty.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/24/theater/reviews/mary-broome-by-allan-monkhouse-at-mint-theater.html', 'snippet': 'In “Mary Broome,” a comedy by Allan Monkhouse, known for his acerbic take on the English bourgeoisie, a man leading a life of privilege is suddenly thrust into poverty.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Class conflict gets a workout in the Mint Theater  Company’s lively, penetrating revival of “Mary Broome,” the troupe’s latest invigoration of a largely forgotten work. The play’s author, Allan Monkhouse (1858-1936), also a novelist and critic, was known for his acerbic dissections of the English bourgeoisie. “Mary Broome” — a comedy that first appeared in Manchester in 1911 and was last staged in Manhattan in 1919, at the Neighborhood Playhouse on Grand Street — cuts right to its heart.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/24/theater/24broome/24broome-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/24/theater/24broome/24broome-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1365, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/24/theater/24broome/24broome-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/24/theater/24broome/24broome-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'th