ent George W. Bush and top officials in his administration assured Americans that Saddam Hussein had weapons of mass destruction and that an American invasion of that country was justified and wouldn’t be that difficult.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iraq, Afghanistan … Iran? We’ve Been Here Before.', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003-11)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-23T21:34:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Albert R. Hunt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Albert', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Hunt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ea47307-9be6-5d17-9672-9a579e4a0df0', 'word_count': 349, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ea47307-9be6-5d17-9672-9a579e4a0df0'}, {'abstract': 'The Yankees had yet another opportunity to pull out a late-inning victory, but the Athletics held on to end New York’s seven-game winning streak.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/24/sports/baseball/this-time-athletics-ensure-theres-no-late-magic-by-yankees.html', 'snippet': 'The Yankees had yet another opportunity to pull out a late-inning victory, but the Athletics held on to end New York’s seven-game winning streak.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There would be no dramatic comeback or postgame delirium at Yankee Stadium, in contrast to the previous two days. The Yankees, for the third time this series, had an opportunity to win with a hit. But the Oakland Athletics held on for a 5-4 win Sunday.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The N