ean Union.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/24/world/europe/little-suspense-as-belarus-votes.html', 'snippet': 'The question was not whether President Aleksandr G. Lukashenko’s supporters would continue to dominate Parliament, but whether electoral changes would pass muster with the European Union.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MINSK, Belarus — Belarus held parliamentary elections on Sunday, though the outcome was hardly in doubt: supporters of President Aleksandr G. Lukashenko have traditionally won, and now hold, all 110 seats in the chamber.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/24/world/SUB-BELARUS/SUB-BELARUS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/24/world/SUB-BELARUS/SUB-BELARUS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/24/world/SUB-BELARUS/SUB-BELARUS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/24/world/SUB-BELARUS/SUB-BELARUS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/24/world/SUB-BELARUS/SUB-BELARUS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/24/world/SUB-BELARUS/SUB-BELARUS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/24/world/SUB-BELARUS/SUB-BELARUS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Belarus Votes as Europe Keeps a Watch for Signs That Sanctions Can End', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Belarus Votes as Europe Keeps a Watch for Signs That Sanctions Can End', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Belarus', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lukashenko, Aleksandr G', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-23T22:01:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew E. Kramer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Kramer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1e4f94a-ec4b-50e6-9405-cb21e281034c', 'word_count': 734, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1e4f94a-ec4b-50e6-9405-cb21e281034c'}, {'abstract': 'Thecreators of the series announced that HBO had ordered a fourth and final season one day before the Season 3 premiere, The Times-Picayune of New Orleans reported.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/24/arts/television/more-treme-is-on-the-way.html', 'snippet': 'Thecreators of the series announced that HBO had ordered a fourth and final season one day before the Season 3 premiere, The Times-Picayune of New Orleans reported.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fans of the HBO drama “Treme” were given multiple reasons to celebrate over the weekend as David Simon and Eric Overmyer, the creators of the series, announced that HBO had ordered a fourth and final season one day before the Season 3 premiere, The Times-Picayune of New Orleans reported. In a speech before a show screening at the Joy Theater in New Orleans on Saturday Mr. Simon told the audience that the fourth season would be shortened, with a total episode count to be determined. “We are going to be back for a season 3.5,” Mr. Simon said. He also announced that all of the actors who portray the varied characters that populate the show’s post-Katrina New Orleans, will return, “To a person they all came back,” he said. “We’re happy for a chance to finish the story on our own terms.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More ‘Treme’ Is on the Way', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'More ‘Treme’ Is on the Way', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Treme (TV Program)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Home Box Office', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-23T22:10:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ade81a8-738b-598a-bc5f-a195892cc5ba', 'word_count': 144, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ade81a8-738b-598a-bc5f-a195892cc5ba'}, {'abstract': 'The idea of a fall season of TV premieres, originally tied to the model year for cars, has survived changing viewer habits and the constant flow of new cable programs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/24/business/media/television-changes-but-the-fall-season-endures.html', 'snippet': 'The idea of a fall season of TV premieres, originally tied to the model year for cars, has survived changing viewer habits and the constant flow of new cable programs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For years, Alan Wurtzel, the head of research for NBC, has questioned the enduring validity of a television season — the ritual competition of network series, which begins again Monday night.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/24/business/sub-networks-1348441910127/sub-networks-1348441910127-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/24/business/sub-networks-1348441910127/sub-networks-1348441910127-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/24/business/sub-networks-1348441910127/sub-networks-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/24/business/sub-networks-1348441910127/sub-networks-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1438, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/24/business/sub-networks-1348441910127/sub-networks-1348441910127-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/24/business/sub-networks-1348441910127/sub-networks-1348441910127-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/24/business/sub-networks-1348441910127/sub-networks-1348441910127-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Television’s Fall Season Endures', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Television’s Fall Season Endures', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC INC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMC (TV Network)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'FX (TV Network)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corporation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-23T22:19:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a91a6a8-837c-520f-ae43-b4f507bf8b6b', 'word_count': 1131, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a91a6a8-837c-520f-ae43-b4f507bf8b6b'}, {'abstract': 'Designs for a new building by the architecture firm Sanaa, to be used as a spiritual and community center, are to be submitted for approval on Monday by Grace Farms Foundation in New Canaan, Conn.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/24/arts/design/a-connecticut-building-for-sanaa.html', 'snippet': 'Designs for a new building by the architecture firm Sanaa, to be used as a spiritual and community center, are to be submitted for approval on Monday by Grace Farms Foundation in New Canaan, Conn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Designs for a new building by the architecture firm Sanaa, to be used as a spiritual and community center, are to be submitted for approval on Monday by Grace Farms Foundation in New Canaan, Conn. The plans for the building, called the River, which must be approved by the town’s Planning and Zoning Commission, call for construction on a sliver of the 75-acre Grace Farms property that the foundation is preserving as permanent open space. The building is to have landscaping by the Philadelphia firm Olin. Sanaa, founded in Tokyo in 1995, is the architecture firm of Kazuyo Sejima and Ryue Nishizawa, who received the Pritzker Architecture Prize in 2010.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Connecticut Building for Sanaa', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Connecticut Building for Sanaa', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Canaan (Conn)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Grace Farms Foundation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sanaa', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-23T22:20:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Pogrebin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogrebin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ae1896d-8cc0-5bd2-9ec8-30776a2656fc', 'word_count': 112, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ae1896d-8cc0-5bd2-9ec8-30776a2656fc'}, {'abstract': 'Sebastian Vettel won the race in Singapore, but Fernando Alonso, by finishing third, proved once again how important consistency is in the race for the 2012 drivers’ title.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/23/another-lesson-in-consistency-as-vettel-wins-in-singapore/', 'snippet': 'Sebastian Vettel won the race in Singapore, but Fernando Alonso, by finishing third, proved once again how important consistency is in the race for the 2012 drivers’ title.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SINGAPORE — It has been the leitmotif of the season: The key to who will win the drivers’ title will likely come down to consistency, not necessarily victories. Sebastian Vettel took only his second victory of the season in his Red Bull car at the Singapore Grand Prix on Sunday, but he moved back into second place in the series. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/blogs/rdv-vettel-singapore/rdv-vettel-singapore-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 613, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/blogs/rdv-vettel-singapore/rdv-vettel-singapore-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1227, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Lesson in Consistency, as Vettel Wins in Singapore', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Formula One', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-23T22:28:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brad Spurgeon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spurgeon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0d90407-757f-53