_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34bf7236-4082-54aa-99f5-ffdf3fd41d25', 'word_count': 650, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34bf7236-4082-54aa-99f5-ffdf3fd41d25'}, {'abstract': 'Politicians have always pressed the flesh, but few relish doing so as heartily as Vice President Joseph R. Biden Jr.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/24/us/politics/on-the-trail-biden-gets-closer-than-most-to-voters.html', 'snippet': 'Politicians have always pressed the flesh, but few relish doing so as heartily as Vice President Joseph R. Biden Jr.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MANCHESTER, N.H. — Yes, Joseph R. Biden Jr. gives a lot of stump speeches.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/24/us/BIDEN/BIDEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/24/us/BIDEN/BIDEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/24/us/BIDEN/BIDEN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/24/us/BIDEN/BIDEN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1348, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/24/us/BIDEN/BIDEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/24/us/BIDEN/BIDEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/24/us/BIDEN/BIDEN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Vice President, a Heartbeat Away From the Public Isn’t Close Enough', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Vice President, a Heartbeat Away From the Public Isn’t Close Enough', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vice Presidents and Vice Presidency (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-23T23:32:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Trip Gabriel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Trip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/02169bc7-a7d2-5dc8-90dc-fd1d8ef87a6f', 'word_count': 799, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02169bc7-a7d2-5dc8-90dc-fd1d8ef87a6f'}, {'abstract': 'A new Nebraska poll is not very important, as fun as it might be to speculate about cases where Omaha could make the difference.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/23/sept-23-does-omaha-matter/', 'snippet': 'A new Nebraska poll is not very important, as fun as it might be to speculate about cases where Omaha could make the difference.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s something of a tradition for newspapers to release polls on Sundays late in a presidential campaign. This Sunday, there were polls out in Ohio, Florida and Pennsylvania — but as it’s Nebraska day at FiveThirtyEight, let’s start with one from the Cornhusker State.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sept. 23: Does Omaha Matter?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Omaha World-Herald', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nebraska', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-23T23:35:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b61aa98a-a7e5-5e9d-8903-10a7fdf76f6c', 'word_count': 1850, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b61aa98a-a7e5-5e9d-8903-10a7fdf76f6c'}, {'abstract': 'The Ten Commandments and the Golden Rule are no longer adequate. We need fresh approaches to right and wrong.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/23/reinventing-ethics/', 'snippet': 'The Ten Commandments and the Golden Rule are no longer adequate. We need fresh approaches to right and wrong.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What’s good and what’s bad? There are plenty of reasons to believe that human nature changes slowly, if at all — all’s still fair in love and war. For millennia, religious believers have attributed our nature to God’s image, as well as to God’s plan. \xa0In recent years, evolutionary psychologists peered directly at our forerunners on the savannahs of East Africa; if human beings change, we do so gradually over thousands of years. \xa0Given little or nothing new in the human firmament, traditional morality — the “goods” and “bads” as outlined in the Ten Commandments or the Golden Rule — should suffice.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reinventing Ethics', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Personal)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-23T23:40:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Howard Gardner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Howard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gardner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6659d17a-ae21-58d0-a867-2772f4228131', 'word_count': 1790, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6659d17a-ae21-58d0-a867-2772f4228131'}, {'abstract': 'A little-noticed result of Verizon’s $3.9 billion airwave purchase is that cable companies can now use the carrier’s retail presence to sell cable packaged with phone and wireless service.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/24/business/media/verizon-airwave-purchase-unites-mobile-and-cable-companies.html', 'snippet': 'A little-noticed result of Verizon’s $3.9 billion airwave purchase is that cable companies can now use the carrier’s retail presence to sell cable packaged with phone and wireless service.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BASKING RIDGE, N.J. — Tucked amid rows of office cubicles at the sprawling Verizon Wireless headquarters here and hidden behind a locked door sit the company’s best kept retail secrets. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'cre