baseball/yankees-not-the-best-in-tight-races.html', 'snippet': 'Over the decades, the Yankees have been baseball’s top team, though not because of a dominance in close pennant and division races.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For all the American League and division titles in their glorious history, the Yankees were for decades seldom involved in a day-to-day, night-to-night pennant race that boiled down to the season’s final weekend, if not the final game.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yankees Not the Best in Tight Races', 'kicker': 'Sports of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Yankees Not the Best In Tight Races', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tampa Bay Rays', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baltimore Orioles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-24T00:32:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Anderson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Anderson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/afa2ccc2-f455-5c04-849e-610aa6d8b769', 'word_count': 900, 'uri': 'nyt://article/afa2ccc2-f455-5c04-849e-610aa6d8b769'}, {'abstract': 'Internet radio services like Pandora hope legislation recently introduced in Congress will lower the rates they pay copyright holders to the levels paid by satellite radio.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/24/business/media/proposed-bill-could-change-royalty-rates-for-internet-radio.html', 'snippet': 'Internet radio services like Pandora hope legislation recently introduced in Congress will lower the rates they pay copyright holders to the levels paid by satellite radio.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Willing buyer, willing seller. Those four words would seem innocuous, but in the world of Internet radio nothing is more contentious.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/24/business/stream/stream-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 671, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/24/business/stream/stream-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1342, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Proposed Bill Could Change Royalty Rates for Internet Radio', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Proposed Internet Radio Royalty Bill Would Change Rate-Setting Standard', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Royalties', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radio', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pandora Media Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-24T00:35:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/10753f67-3cc4-5e3b-a54c-21b971991b60', 'word_count': 465, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10753f67-3cc4-5e3b-a54c-21b971991b60'}, {'abstract': 'Asked why he was behind in some polls, Mitt Romney accused the Obama campaign of distorting his record. He also attributed his light campaign schedule to the president’s decision to opt out of the federal campaign finance system.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/23/romney-blames-obama-for-his-campaign-challenges/', 'snippet': 'Asked why he was behind in some polls, Mitt Romney accused the Obama campaign of distorting his record. He also attributed his light campaign schedule to the president’s decision to opt out of the federal campaign finance system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DENVER — Mitt Romney, who has been criticized by members of his party in recent weeks for not campaigning aggressively enough and who trails President Obama in polls in most swing states, placed the blame for his campaign’s struggles squarely on the president himself Sunday afternoon.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney Blames Obama for His Campaign Challenges', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-24T00:37:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/67f3f014-b6dd-565e-bb22-974ec46764da', 'word_count': 945, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67f3f014-b6dd-565e-bb22-974ec46764da'}, {'abstract': 'Needing to win the Tour Championship to beat out Rory McIlroy for the FedEx Cup, Brandt Snedeker came up with three big birdies on the back nine at East Lake Golf Club.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/24/sports/golf/brandt-snedeker-wins-tour-championship-and-fedex-cup-title.html', 'snippet': 'Needing to win the Tour Championship to beat out Rory McIlroy for the FedEx Cup, Brandt Snedeker came up with three big birdies on the back nine at East Lake Golf Club.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATLANTA — Before the most critical round of his professional career, Brandt Snedeker stopped by the Shepherd Center, a rehabilitation hospital for patients with spinal cord or brain injuries, and spent 30 minutes with his longtime instructor’s son, Tucker Anderson. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/24/sports/golf/24golf-1/24golf-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/24/sports/golf/24golf-1/24golf-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/24/sports/golf/24golf-1/24golf-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 715, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/24/sports/golf/24golf-1/24golf-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1430, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/24/sports/golf/24golf-1/24go