ebound when it has been stripped of its most fertile members as the cod has been.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The ideal fish for human consumption would mature quickly and reproduce in staggering numbers. This does not describe the Atlantic cod. Cod mature late — at 4 to 6 years old — and they can live as long as 25 years. Female cod do, in fact, produce astonishing numbers of eggs. But older cod lay two or three times as many eggs as younger cod. This means that a healthy cod population must include relatively large numbers of older fish.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Shocking News About Cod', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Shocking News About Cod', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cod (Fish)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fishing, Commercial', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-24T01:15:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a744ca7-9887-5030-a2e5-0a8be8a2b385', 'word_count': 372, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a744ca7-9887-5030-a2e5-0a8be8a2b385'}, {'abstract': 'Among personnel pulled from Benghazi after the assault on the American mission were intelligence operatives and contractors who were crucial to surveillance on militants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/24/world/africa/attack-in-libya-was-major-blow-to-cia-efforts.html', 'snippet': 'Among personnel pulled from Benghazi after the assault on the American mission were intelligence operatives and contractors who were crucial to surveillance on militants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The attack in Benghazi, Libya, that killed Ambassador J. Christopher St