nt': 701, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22f3a082-c141-5410-9336-3e696c8692dc'}, {'abstract': 'The time is long past for the F.C.C. to give state prisoners access to reasonably priced interstate telephone service.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/24/opinion/costly-phone-calls-for-state-inmates.html', 'snippet': 'The time is long past for the F.C.C. to give state prisoners access to reasonably priced interstate telephone service.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Members of Congress and civil rights groups are pushing the Federal Communications Commission to rein in telephone companies that, in many states, charge inmates spectacularly high rates that can force their families to choose between keeping in touch with a relative behind bars and, in some cases, putting food on the table. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Costly Phone Calls for Inmates', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Costly Phone Calls for Inmates', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telephones and Telecommunications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Communications Commission', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-24T02:04:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/830e4ab0-3371-57a5-a123-0330b68f8e68', 'word_count': 351, 'uri': 'nyt://article/830e4ab0-3371-57a5-a123-0330b68f8e68'}, {'abstract': 'An obscure militant group based in the Sinai region claimed responsibility for a cross-border attack Friday that killed an Israeli soldier.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/24/world/mid