ent years, providing seed money to inventors who make the toilet more sustainable.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/24/sustainable-innovation-the-gates-foundation-reinvents-the-toilet/', 'snippet': 'Known for tackling some of the most difficult global challenges, the Gates Foundation turned to human waste in recent years, providing seed money to inventors who make the toilet more sustainable.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With 2.5 billion people in the world not having access to proper sanitation, sustainable development experts are thinking a lot about toilets.\xa0 That’s because our modern toilet, whose technology has been around for centuries, requires a lot of running\xa0(and fairly clean) water.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/24/blogs/rdv-sustainable-toilet-gates/rdv-sustainable-toilet-gates-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 710, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/24/blogs/rdv-sustainable-toilet-gates/rdv-sustainable-toilet-gates-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1419, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sustainable Innovation: Gates Foundation Reinvents the Toilet', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bathrooms and Toilets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gates, Bill and Melinda, Foundation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-24T11:36:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher F. Schuetze', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Schuetze', 'qualifier': None,