ndslides and claimed at least 27 lives in recent days.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Floods and Landslides Kill Dozens in North East India', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Landslides and Mudslides', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monsoons', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rescues', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hazarika, Sanjoy', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brahmaputra River (India)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sikkim (India)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-24T12:29:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neha Thirani and Hari Kumar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thirani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Hari', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kumar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/834e5a84-242e-53eb-98c0-5adac2a347fc', 'word_count': 720, 'uri': 'nyt://article/834e5a84-242e-53eb-98c0-5adac2a347fc'}, {'abstract': 'Patriots Coach Bill Belichick’s bump with one of the officials after a game figures to further stoke controversy over the performance of the replacement officials.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/24/rough-day-for-replacements-as-belichick-boils-over/', 'snippet': 'Patriots Coach Bill Belichick’s bump with one of the officials after a game figures to further stoke controversy over the performance of the replacement officials.', 'lead_paragraph': '“It simply comes down to this: The replacement officials don’t know the N.F.L. rules, they don’t know how to enforce what they don’t know and they don’t know how to manage the games.” Mike Pereira, former N.F.L. supervisor of officials, writing for FoxSports.com.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rough Day for Replacements as Belichick Boils Over', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Officiating (Sports)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Belichick, Bill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-24T12:46:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/120575a4-907a-58b2-8fe4-d8adb90e61ae', 'word_count': 361, 'uri': 'nyt://article/120575a4-907a-58b2-8fe4-d8adb90e61ae'}, {'abstract': '18. BRUCE LEE. W1N W1N. BATMAN. In Hong Kong, these and other vanity plates — including copious combinations of double and triple initials — have raised millions at transportation department auctions.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/24/what-would-you-pay-for-a-vanity-license-plate-90000/', 'snippet': '18. BRUCE LEE. W1N W1N. BATMAN. In Hong Kong, these and other vanity plates — including copious combinations of double and triple initials — have raised millions at transportation department auctions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — They are quirky or funny. Boastful or decorative. Hyper-expensive or a bargain, at a mere 5,000 Hong Kong dollars a pop, about $650. And for those walking the streets of Hong Kong, they are addictive: Once you know they are out there, you can’t stop looking for more.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/24/blogs/rdv-license-plates-hk/rdv-license-plates-hk-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 432, 'width': 576, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/24/blogs/rdv-license-plates-hk/rdv-license-plates-hk-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 432, 'width': 576, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Would You Pay for a Vanity License Plate? $90,000?', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hong Kong', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-24T12:52:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bettina Wassener', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bettina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wassener', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b528a11-2917-55d7-9d94-72ace1e601b2', 'word_count': 357, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b528a11-2917-55d7-9d94-72ace1e601b2'}, {'abstract': 'Scenes from the Milan fashion week photo diary of Carlotta Manaigo.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/24/photos-of-the-moment-marni-6/', 'snippet': 'Scenes from the Milan fashion week photo diary of Carlotta Manaigo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Photos of The Moment | Marni', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-24T13:00:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carlotta Manaigo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carlotta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Manaigo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5dfa035-a0f1-5e92-8481-28bd520d0c91', 'word_count': 36, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5dfa035-a0f1-5e92-8481-28bd520d0c91'}, {'abstract': 'A statement on the band’s Web site said Mr. Armstrong was being treated for substance abuse after he halted the band’s performance on Friday at the iHeartRadio Music Festival to deliver an angry tirade.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/24/green-days-billie-joe-armstrong-seeks-treatment-after-rant/', 'snippet': 'A statement on the band’s Web site said Mr. Armstrong was being treated for substance abuse after he halted the band’s performance on Friday at the iHeartRadio Music Festival to deliver an angry tirade.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While the occasional onstage outburst or round of instrument destruction would seem to be well within the purview of a modern-day rock star, this behavior has led the Green Day front man Billie Joe Armstrong to seek rehabilitation after a profanity-laden rant at a performance over the weekend, the band announced on its Web site. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Green Day’s Billie Joe Armstrong Seeks Treatment After Rant', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Green Day Singer’s Tirade Leads Him to Seek Rehab', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ARMSTRONG, BILLIE JOE', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Green Day', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-24T13:03:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9d4b0a7-fa0f-54a9-84eb-f89cbbb126bd', 'word_count': 269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9d4b0a7-fa0f-54a9-84eb-f89cbbb126bd'}, {'abstract': 'The Day: Daw Aung San Suu Kyi, who has emerged from house arrest in Myanmar to become the opposition leader in Parliament, embodies the never-ending struggle for human dignity and decency, everywhere.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/24/a-voice-from-myanmar-worthy-of-a-heros-welcome/', 'snippet': 'The Day: Daw Aung San Suu Kyi, who has emerged from house arrest in Myanmar to become the opposition leader in Parliament, embodies the never-ending struggle for human dignity and decency, everywhere.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Long ago, Daw Aung San Suu Kyi lived for a few years in New York. On her arrival in the late 1960s, she was surprised to find a city that was exactly as she had pictured it, skyscrapers and all. “I thought, ‘Oh, it looks just like a postcard,’” Ms. Aung San Suu Kyi said on Saturday. “Somehow, I never really believed it would be quite like that.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Voice From Myanmar, Worthy of a Hero’s Welcome', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Aung San Suu Kyi', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Queens College, City University of New York', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-24T13:15:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clyde Haberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clyde', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/886022e5-76a7-53d0-b809-47816315c284', 'word_count': 891, 'uri': 'nyt://article/886022e5-76a7-53d0-b809-47816315c284'}, {'abstract': 'Ehud Olmert, a former prime minister of Israel, was sentenced by a Jerusalem court on Monday to a one-year suspended jail term and a maximum fine of about $19,000 for breach of trust.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/25/world/middleeast/former-israeli-premier-gets-suspended-sentence.html', 'snippet': 'Ehud Olmert, a former prime minister of Israel, was sentenced by a Jerusalem court on Monday to a one-year suspended jail term and a maximum fine of about $19,000 for breach of trust.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — Ehud Olmert, a former prime minister of Israel, was sentenced by a Jerusalem court on Monday to a one-year suspended prison term and a maximum fine of about $19,000 for breach of trust. The relatively light sentence ended a long-running prosecution that forced Mr. Olmert from office. It also opened the way for a possible political comeback. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/25/world/ISRAEL/ISRAEL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/25/world/ISRAEL/ISRAEL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Former Israeli Premier Gets Suspended Sentence', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Former Israeli Premier Gets Suspended Sentence', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Olmert, Ehud', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bribery and Kickbacks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-24T13:22:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Kershner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7967afd6-59ab-544e-adc1-7c54d044574e', 'word_count': 642, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7967afd6-59ab-544e-adc1-7c54d044574e'}, {'abstract': 'Milan', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/09/24/fashion/runway-womens/dsquared2-spring-2013-rtw.html', 'snippet': 'Milan', 'lead_paragraph': 'Milan', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/24/fashion/runway-womens/dsquared_spring13app-slide-6KKR/dsquared_spring13app-slide-6KKR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'le