8-2adda49cfca9'}, {'abstract': 'The gift is from Allen R. Adler and his wife, Frances Beatty Adler.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/24/a-4-5-million-gift-for-princeton-art-museum/', 'snippet': 'The gift is from Allen R. Adler and his wife, Frances Beatty Adler.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Princeton University Art Museum has received a $4.5 million gift from Allen R. Adler, a longtime member of the museum’s advisory council and his wife, Frances Beatty Adler, vice president of Richard L. Feigen & Company, a New York art gallery, and chairwoman of the Drawing Center in SoHo. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A $4.5 Million Gift for Princeton Art Museum', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '$4.5 Million Gift For Princeton Museum', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Princeton University Art Museum', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Princeton (NJ)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-24T15:10:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Vogel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vogel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d02741e-b88e-528b-a558-01154b97af39', 'word_count': 130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d02741e-b88e-528b-a558-01154b97af39'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Gore’s Climate Reality Project plans another live streaming event to call attention to weather extremes and link them to human-caused emissions.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/24/al-gore-sees-dirty-weather-ahead/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Gore’s Climate Reality Project plans another live streaming event to call attention to weather extremes and link them to human-caused emissions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Sunday, Al Gore was in New York — well, he appeared in a video screened there — to promote the second iteration of “24 Hours of Reality,” an event streamed online to help people connect the dots between climate change and its diverse impacts around the globe. This year’s version, scheduled for Nov. 14-15, is titled “24 Hours of Reality: The Dirty Weather Report.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Al Gore Sees ‘Dirty Weather’ Ahead', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drought', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gore, Al', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-24T15:11:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emma Bryce', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emma', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bryce', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/770f76bb-f480-5c9b-a1be-fd71cc2c87e2', 'word_count': 445, 'uri': 'nyt://article/770f76bb-f480-5c9b-a1be-fd71cc2c87e2'}, {'abstract': 'Nicholas Kristof will be holding an “AMA” (Ask Me Anything) on Reddit on Monday, September 24 at 2:30 pm.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/24/my-reddit-ama/', 'snippet': 'Nicholas Kristof will be holding an “AMA” (Ask Me Anything) on Reddit on Monday, September 24 at 2:30 pm.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Today at 2:30 pm I will be holding an “AMA” (Ask Me Anything) on Reddit. I invite all my readers, including my critics, to submit questions regarding my coverage as a columnist on the editorial page, the PBS documentary based on the book I co-wrote with my wife, Sheryl WuDunn, “Half the Sky,” or my extracurricular activities (hiking the Pacific Crest Trail, sampling mouse shish kebabs, etc). I look forward to a stimulating conversation!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'My Reddit “AMA”', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-24T15:26:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/abff9c5f-f30c-5277-a202-73ba2fb98491', 'word_count': 74, 'uri': 'nyt://article/abff9c5f-f30c-5277-a202-73ba2fb98491'}, {'abstract': 'Apple on Monday said it had sold 5 million new iPhones just three days after the phone’s release, beating first-weekend sales of its predecessor, the iPhone 4S, by about one million, but still missing some analysts’ forecasts. Still, the number sold over the weekend is about as many smartphones as some competitors, like Nokia, can say they’ve sold over all.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/24/apple-sells-5-million-new-iphones/', 'snippet': 'Apple on Monday said it had sold 5 million new iPhones just three days after the phone’s release, beating first-weekend sales of its predecessor, the iPhone 4S, by about one million, but still missing some analysts’ forecasts. Still, the number so...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Apple on Monday said it had sold five million new iPhones just three days after the phone’s release, beating first-weekend sales of its predecessor, the iPhone 4S, by about one million, but still missing some analysts’ forecasts. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/24/blogs/iphone-5-sales/iphone-5-sales-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 731, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/24/blogs/iphone-5-sales/iphone-5-sales-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1462, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/24/blogs/iphone-5-sales/iphone-5-sales-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/24/blogs/iphone-5-sales/iphone-5-sales-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/24/blogs/iphone-5-sales/iphone-5-sales-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Apple Sells Five Million New iPhones', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nokia Oyj', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Samsung Group', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-24T15:30:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name