ng-back-to-war-trading-a-gun-for-a-pen/', 'snippet': 'Civilians have been writing about military affairs for generations, and many have done a superb job. Do veterans have an edge over nonveterans when it comes to covering war?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The documentary filmmakers Sebastian Junger and Tim Hetherington embedded in Afghanistan with one mission: to document war. The result was the gripping documentary “Restrepo.” For nearly one year, they lived in peril alongside the United States Army. Their project won the Grand Jury Prize at the Sundance Film Festival in 2010 and was nominated for an Academy Award in 2011. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Going Back to War, Trading a Gun for a Pen', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003-11)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hetherington, Tim', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Junger, Sebastian', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pyle, Ernie', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Silva, Joao', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Marine Corps', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'USA Today', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Marine Corps Base Camp Lejeune (SC)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-24T18:21:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas James Brennan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': 