nizations', 'value': 'Xstrata', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-24T19:02:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6374023e-927d-5e13-9128-a811cc6f5e08', 'word_count': 877, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6374023e-927d-5e13-9128-a811cc6f5e08'}, {'abstract': 'The paintings — previously thought to be fakes or not fully by the hand of the master and hidden in storage for decades by the National Museum Wales — have now been reclassified as the real things.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/24/three-fake-j-m-w-turner-paintings-authenticated/', 'snippet': 'The paintings — previously thought to be fakes or not fully by the hand of the master and hidden in storage for decades by the National Museum Wales — have now been reclassified as the real things.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Three J.M.W. Turner paintings previously thought to be fakes or not fully by the hand of the master and hidden in storage for decades have now been reclassified as the real things. And unlike most painting authentication cases, which proceed in scholarly seclusion for years, this one played out on television.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Three “Fake” J.M.W. Turner Paintings Authenticated', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On a Second Look, Turners Are Real', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collectors and Collections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Turner, Joseph Mallord William', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'British Broadcasting Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cardiff (Wales)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wales', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-24T19:02:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randy Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kennedy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f78ea0c-1e45-52ba-bcc2-a6b3592d84f7', 'word_count': 200, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f78ea0c-1e45-52ba-bcc2-a6b3592d84f7'}, {'abstract': 'The fourth-annual Brooklyn Invitational, featuring builders from around the United States and an atmosphere that was emphatically of its place, was the anti-Sturgis.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/24/at-brooklyn-invitational-disrupting-notions-of-motorcycle-culture/', 'snippet': 'The fourth-annual Brooklyn Invitational, featuring builders from around the United States and an atmosphere that was emphatically of its place, was the anti-Sturgis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A send-off to a long, hot summer was orchestrated on Sept. 22, as thousands of motorcyclists descended on the waterfront of North Williamsburg for the Brooklyn Invitational Custom Motorcycle Show. The attendance and variety of motorcycle culture on view further cemented the position of the show, in its fourth year, as among the most important in North America.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Brooklyn Invitational, Disrupting Notions of Motorcycle Culture', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-24T19:09:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By AUSTIN CONSIDINE', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Austin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'CONSIDINE', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d83aa66c-f180-5151-84d7-a710b36e60bd', 'word_count': 739, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d83aa66c-f180-5151-84d7-a710b36e60bd'}, {'abstract': 'A study of a large multiethnic population found an increased risk of cardiovascular disease and stroke among women who reached menopause before age 47.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/24/early-menopause-is-linked-to-heart-risk/', 'snippet': 'A study of a large multiethnic population found an increased risk of cardiovascular disease and stroke among women who reached menopause before age 47.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a new analysis of a multiethnic population, early menopause has been shown to be associated with an increased risk of cardiovascular disease and stroke.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/04/health/well_aging/well_aging-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 215, 'width': 211, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/04/health/well_aging/well_aging-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 215, 'width': 211, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/04/health/well_aging/well_aging-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/04/health/well_aging/well_aging-thumbStandard