 {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b9fb2ca-b0ac-599f-9882-fe9194f3be2f', 'word_count': 384, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b9fb2ca-b0ac-599f-9882-fe9194f3be2f'}, {'abstract': 'Michael Mina brings back an early model of digital content: a free e-mail that contains a video and hands-on cooking instruction, and is part of a larger plan.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/24/blueprint-of-a-meal-from-in-box-to-table/', 'snippet': 'Michael Mina brings back an early model of digital content: a free e-mail that contains a video and hands-on cooking instruction, and is part of a larger plan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As cooking on the Web moves beyond recipe sites, Cook Taste Eat, a new enterprise from the San Francisco chef Michael Mina that opened Monday, brings back an early model of digital content: a free e-mail that lands in your in-box each morning. That e-mail contains a video and hands-on cooking instruction, like the one above, and is part of a larger plan. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Blueprint of a Meal, From In-Box to Table', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-24T19:14:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Moskin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moskin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9134c058-b89f-5f8a-9b1d-71fc2006bd56', 'word_count': 222, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9134c058-b89f-5f8a-9b1d-71fc2006bd56'}, {'abstract': '“Ruth & Erica,” a YouTube drama, is the latest in a series of movies, TV shows and books that focus on aging.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/24/the-drama-of-aging-and-caregiving-on-youtube/', 'snippet': '“Ruth & Erica,” a YouTube drama, is the latest in a series of movies, TV shows and books that focus on aging.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I don’t want to take care of them,” Erica confesses in Episode 12 to the man she’s just slept with, speaking about her elderly parents.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Drama of Aging and Caregiving, on YouTube', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lippman, Amy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'YouTube.com', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-24T19:26:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paula Span', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paula', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Span', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a508cf1f-be45-5d3a-8cb3-bbf4cc1bf423', 'word_count': 526, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a508cf1f-be45-5d3a-8cb3-bbf4cc1bf423'}, {'abstract': 'Researchers have been studying the Tsimane, the largest indigenous group in the Amazon still living in traditional ways, to tease out insights into diseases ailing modernized societies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/25/health/in-the-bolivian-amazon-a-yardstick-for-modern-health.html', 'snippet': 'Researchers have been studying the Tsimane, the largest indigenous group in the Amazon still living in traditional ways, to tease out insights into diseases ailing modernized societies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SANTA MARÍA, Bolivia — There seems to be little that distinguishes the indigenous Tsimane of northern Bolivia from dozens of other native Amazonian peoples. They still live in small communities, fishing daily, hunting and relying on subsistence farming. They remain relatively isolated from the outside world. They still have large families and fall victim to parasites, worms and infectious diseases. And until a decade ago, few had contact with doctors.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/25/science/25BOLI_SPAN/25BOLI-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/25/science/25BOLI_SPAN/25BOLI-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/25/science/25BOLI_SPAN/25BOLI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/25/science/25BOLI_SPAN/25BOLI-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/25/science/25BOLI_SPAN/25BOLI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/25/science/25BOLI_SPAN/25BOLI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None,