rstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crowley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/983c1053-6fbf-5615-a71c-7ce68d51fa2a', 'word_count': 1, 'uri': 'nyt://article/983c1053-6fbf-5615-a71c-7ce68d51fa2a'}, {'abstract': 'The company’s campaign, created by the DiMassimo Goldstein ad agency in New York, is aimed at busy consumers who care enough about the quality and provenance of the food they buy to pay FreshDirect’s prices.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/24/in-2-million-ad-campaign-freshdirect-to-emphasize-food-quality/', 'snippet': 'The company’s campaign, created by the DiMassimo Goldstein ad agency in New York, is aimed at busy consumers who care enough about the quality and provenance of the food they buy to pay FreshDirect’s prices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FreshDirect, the online home-delivery grocer, is preparing a new advertising approach as it seeks to, er, um, freshen its brand image.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In $2 Million Ad Campaign, FreshDirect to Emphasize Food Quality', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'DiMassimo Goldstein', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'FreshDirect', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-24T19:45:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/76e0a3ed-64cf-510e-90e8-a87932cb9bfd', 'word_count': 818, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76e0a3ed-64cf-510e-90e8-a87932cb9bfd'}, {'abstract': 'As Groupon continues its quest to become a big platform for merchants, it appears that the online coupon purveyor is moving into restaurant reservations — and a little into OpenTable’s domain.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/09/24/groupon-moves-into-restaurant-reservations-with-savored-deal/', 'snippet': 'As Groupon continues its quest to become a big platform for merchants, it appears that the online coupon purveyor is moving into restaurant reservations — and a little into OpenTable’s domain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over recent months, Groupon has sought to expand its core business of daily deals with a number of new business propositions, including with ventures like a mobile payment system.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Groupon Moves Into Restaurant Reservations With Savored Deal', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Groupon Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-24T19:52:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d4b0d6e-1589-50a3-95e0-8905d2336018', 'word_count': 322, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d4b0d6e-1589-50a3-95e0-8905d2336018'}, {'abstract': 'Often, these kinds of activities are led by those who have been through M.B.A. programs — but M.B.A.’s don’t always understand how smaller companies work.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/24/small-business-lessons-from-harley-davidsons-turnaround/', 'snippet': 'Often, these kinds of activities are led by those who have been through M.B.A. programs — but M.B.A.’s don’t always understand how smaller companies work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This weekend, I read an article in the Wall Street Journal about how Harley-Davidson turned itself around using “lean” manufacturing strategies. Lean, or just-in-time, manufacturing is the Toyota production system, which started with W. Edwards Deming and his work with statistical quality control. Whenever I see this kind of article about a large company, I think about how the thoughts and principles can be applied to the smaller companies I work with.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Small-Business Lessons From Harley-Davidson’s Turnaround', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Business Schools', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Harley-Davidson Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-24T20:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Josh Patrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Josh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Patrick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3dd201d6-98de-5767-a93d-e110bb12d064', 'word_count': 484, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3dd201d6-98de-5767-a93d-e110bb12d064'}, {'abstract': 'Pavel Datsyuk, locked out like the rest of N.H.L. players eight days ago, scored a goal off a soccer-style header that was waved off Monday in his debut with CSKA Moscow.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/24/pavel-datsyuk-makes-his-debut-with-cska-moscow/', 'snippet': 'Pavel Datsyuk, locked out like the rest of N.H.L. players eight days ago, scored a goal off a soccer-style header that was waved off Monday in his debut with CSKA Moscow.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pavel Datsyuk scored a goal off a soccer-style header that was waved off Monday in his debut with CSKA Moscow, but emerged victorious anyway as Datsyuk’s army club beat Avangard Omsk, 1-0. Igor Radulov’s second-period goal, set up by his more famous brother, Alexander, was the difference.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pavel Datsyuk Makes His Debut With CSKA Moscow', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christensen, Erik', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Datsyuk, Pavel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kostitsyn, Andrei', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Malkin, Evgeni', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Radulov, Alexander', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yakupov, Nail', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CSKA Moscow', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-24T20:01:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization':