: 'The four wins for “Homeland” at the Emmys have created a coming-of-age moment for Showtime, a network long in the shadow of HBO.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Here’s what happens when you win an Emmy Award for best actress, as Claire Danes did on Sunday night. You give dozens of backstage interviews, answering the same questions again and again. Then your limo driver takes you to lavish parties, where you say “thank you” again and again and take photos with well-wishers. But all you really want to do is see your mom and dad, who watched your acceptance speech from a hotel suite miles away. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/arts/television/20120923-EMMYS-slide-35BC/20120923-EMMYS-slide-35BC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 727, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/arts/television/20120923-EMMYS-slide-35BC/20120923-EMMYS-slide-35BC-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1453, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/arts/television/20120923-EMMYS-slide-35BC/20120923-EMMYS-slide-35BC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/23/arts/television/20120923-EMMYS-slide-35BC/20120923-EMMYS-slide-35BC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/23/arts/television/20120923-EMMYS-slide-35BC/20120923-EMMYS-slide-35BC-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Showtime Jumps to Capitalize on Emmy Glory for ‘Homeland’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Showtime Jumps to Capitalize on Emmy Glory for ‘Homeland’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Danes, Claire', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lewis, Damian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Showtime', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emmy Awards', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-24T21:57:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/98d40bd6-5ba5-5c65-8aea-a33db71f7e3f', 'word_count': 932, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98d40bd6-5ba5-5c65-8aea-a33db71f7e3f'}, {'abstract': 'Joan Juliet Buck and members of a storytelling group embark on a tour across Georgia.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/24/stories-from-the-unchained-tour/', 'snippet': 'Joan Juliet Buck and members of a storytelling group embark on a tour across Georgia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a film by Matthew T. Perry, Joan Juliet Buck — who wrote about her time on tour across Georgia with the Unchained Tour for our fall travel issue — expounds on the experience as wandering bard.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stories From the Unchained Tour', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Buck, Joan Juliet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Moth, The', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-24T22:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rebecca Ruiz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rebecca', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ruiz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97922012-480d-58b8-8b10-fbe05003171d', 'word_count': 117, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97922012-480d-58b8-8b10-fbe05003171d'}, {'abstract': 'What is the measure of a great jazz drummer? The answer was worth mulling over at the Thelonious Monk International Jazz Competition, won by Jamison Ross.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/25/arts/music/jamison-ross-wins-thelonious-monk-contest.html', 'snippet': 'What is the measure of a great jazz drummer? The answer was worth mulling over at the Thelonious Monk International Jazz Competition, won by Jamison Ross.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Jamison Ross sauntered onstage at the National Museum of Natural History here on Saturday with the solicitous gleam of a casino floor manager, his bulky frame encased in a suit and his face bearing a wide-open smile. Graciously, he initiated a round of applause for his fellow hopefuls in the 25th-annual Thelonious Monk International Jazz Competition, and another for the event’s unflappable house band. Then he sat down, picked up a pair of brushes and counted off “Bye Bye Blues,” an uncomplicated song recorded by dozens of American entertainers from the 1930s on. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/25/arts/monk1/monk1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 727, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/25/arts/monk1/monk1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1246, 'width': 1754, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/25/arts/monk1/monk1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/25/arts/monk1/monk1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/25/arts/monk1/monk1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In a Monk Showcase, the Best Is Saved for Last', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In a Monk Showcase, the Best Is Saved for Last', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Monk, Thelonious', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ross, Jamison', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-24T22:05:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a382190-f331-5ab3-ba08-a16673fd9951', 'word_count': 1126, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a382190-f331-5ab3-b