ives in recent days.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/25/world/asia/india-deluge-strikes-northeast.html', 'snippet': 'While parts of India struggle with crop failures and water shortages, the northeastern states of Sikkim and Assam have been hit by heavy rains and flash floods that have caused landslides and claimed at least 27 lives in recent days.', 'lead_paragraph': ' While parts of India struggle with crop failures and water shortages, the northeastern states of Sikkim and Assam have been hit by heavy rains and flash floods that have caused landslides and claimed at least 27 lives in recent days. Heavy rainfall last week has caused “enormous” damage in Sikkim, an official said. The region is now largely cut off from the rest of India because of the flooding and landslides, which have closed roads. In Assam, floods have affected nearly 1.3 million people, spread across 1,972 villages, said a state disaster official. The state has set up 166 relief camps, which now shelter more than 200,000 people. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'India: Deluge Strikes Northeast', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'India: Deluge Strikes Northeast', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Landslides and Mudslides', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-25T00:46:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neha Thirani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thirani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/f59f9102-b8ba-57dc-ae04-a666a3df43bc', 'word_count': 108, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f59f9102-b8ba-57dc-ae04-a666a3df43bc'}, {'abstract': 'The last Agricultural Census in 2007 showed a 4 percent increase in the number of farms, the first increase since 1920, and some college graduates are joining in the return to the land.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/25/nyregion/the-farm-life-draws-some-students-for-post-graduate-work.html', 'snippet': 'The last Agricultural Census in 2007 showed a 4 percent increase in the number of farms, the first increase since 1920, and some college graduates are joining in the return to the land.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RED HOOK, N.Y. — It was harvest time, and several farm hands were hunched over a bed of sweet potatoes under the midday sun, elbow deep in soil for $10 an hour. But they were not typical laborers.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/25/nyregion/FARM-1/FARM-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/25/nyregion/FARM-1/FARM-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/25/nyregion/FARM-1/FARM-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/25/nyregion/FARM-1/FARM-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/25/nyregion/FARM-1/FARM-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thu