 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mayor’s Tale of Recovery Hasn’t Been Reality for Some', 'kicker': 'Gotham', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mayor’s Tale of Recovery Hasn’t Been Reality for Some', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'City Council (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ratner, Bruce C', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-25T00:50:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Powell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Powell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/da8419f6-88f5-5906-a049-fbb31fff8f1d', 'word_count': 794, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da8419f6-88f5-5906-a049-fbb31fff8f1d'}, {'abstract': 'It was clear on Monday that the Romney-Ryan campaign believes that with six weeks to go before the election it can still score points off Mr. Obama’s handling of turmoil across the Middle East.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/24/on-stump-in-ohio-ryan-criticizes-obamas-military-and-foreign-policies/', 'snippet': 'It was clear on Monday that the Romney-Ryan campaign believes that with six weeks to go before the election it can still score points off Mr. Obama’s handling of turmoil across the Middle East.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LIMA, Ohio – Representative Paul D. Ryan took aim at President Obama’s military policies on Monday, likening the differing national security philosophies of Mitt Romney and Mr. Obama to those of Ronald Reagan and Jimmy Carter, while lambasting a United States Army plan to halt Pentagon funding for several years for the nation’s only main battle tank, which employs 800 people at a plant in this northwest Ohio town.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Stump in Ohio, Ryan Criticizes Obama’s Military and Foreign Policies', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-25T00:50:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard A. Oppel Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Oppel', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1edce724-aa70-59a3-ba1a-f52edd1561af', 'word_count': 651, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1edce724-aa70-59a3-ba1a-f52edd1561af'}, {'abstract': 'Trying to wipe out Al Qaeda with drone strikes alone is a losing strategy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/25/opinion/dont-kill-every-terrorist.html', 'snippet': 'Trying to wipe out Al Qaeda with drone strikes alone is a losing strategy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cambridge, Mass.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dead Men Share No Secrets', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dead Men Share No Secrets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drones (Pilotless Planes)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Targeted Killings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-25T00:51:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marisa L. Porges', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marisa', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Porges', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ec59b85-7b82-5d22-a2a6-be8765e5cb90', 'word_count': 831, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ec59b85-7b82-5d22-a2a6-be8765e5cb90'}, {'abstract': 'Democrat or Republican, we are all both makers and takers.', 'web_url': 'https://campaignstops.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/24/we-are-the-96-percent/', 'snippet': 'Democrat or Republican, we are all both makers and takers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHENMitt Romney told the guests at a fund-raiser in Florida in May that America is divided between people who pay no income taxes and depend on government and pretty much everyone else, he missed the deeper truth. It is not just that most of the 47 percent Mr. Romney talked about do pay payroll taxes and that many of them have paid income taxes in the past. The reality he glossed over is that nearly all Americans have used government social policies at some point in their lives. The beneficiaries include the rich and the poor, Democrats and Republicans. Almost everyone is both a maker and a taker.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'We Are the 96 Percent', 'kicker': 'Campaign Stops', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment Insurance', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-25T00:51:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Suzanne Mettler and John Sides', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Suzanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mettler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sides', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/91207b43-e753-5cb8-80b8-e52f780bc3c1', 'word_count': 951, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91207b43-e753-5cb8-80b8-e52f780bc3c1'}, {'abstract': 'Counts of absentee ballots in tight New York races showed that one incumbent challenged by a social conservative, Stephen M. Saland, won, but another, Roy J. McDonald, seemingly lost.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/25/nyregion/gop-state-senator-who-backed-same-sex-marriage-is-apparently-defeated.html', 'snippet': 'Counts of absentee ballots in tight New York races showed that one incumbent challenged by a social conservative, Stephen M. Saland, won, but another, Roy J. McDonald, seemingly lost.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALBANY — One of the four Republican state senators who voted for same-sex marriage claimed victory Monday in a close primary against an opponent critical of his vote, while another of the four appeared increasingly certain to lose his party’s nomination over the issue.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/25/nyregion/NYELECT-1/NYELECT-1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/25/nyregion/NYELECT-1/NYELECT-1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1353, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/25/nyregion/NYELECT-1/NYELECT-1-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/25/nyregion/NYELECT-1/NYELECT-1-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/25/nyregion/NYELECT-1/NYELECT-1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Results for G.O.P. Backers of Gay Marriage: Two Victories and, It Appears, a Loss', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Results for G.O.P. Backers of Gay Marriage: Two Victories and, It Appears, a Loss', 'name': None, 'seo':