/09/25/us/mayor-of-struggling-gary-ind-turns-to-chicagos-richard-daley-for-advice.html', 'snippet': 'Mayor Karen Freeman-Wilson, struggling to revive Gary, Ind., has sought advice from many quarters, including from former Mayor Richard M. Daley of Chicago and his graduate students.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — When Karen Freeman-Wilson was elected the mayor of Gary, Ind., last year, she found herself confronting some grim truths about her hometown. Revenues in an already emaciated city budget were shrinking by millions of dollars. About a quarter of the buildings, she said, were empty. All the while, people were moving away.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mayor of an Ailing Indiana Mill Town Turns to a Chicago Veteran for Advice', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mayor of an Ailing Indiana Mill Town Turns to a Chicago Veteran for Advice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Daley, Richard M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gary (Ind)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Freeman-Wilson, Karen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Chicago', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-25T01:32:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Monica Davey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Monica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0fd395dc-3d18-5fb0-966a-80179077b6a2', 'word_count': 617, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0fd395dc-3d18-5fb0-966a-80179077b6a2'}, {'abstract': 'About 1,000 times a year, a plane or a vehicle moves onto an active runway by mistake, and regulators have been slow to address the problem.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/25/business/runway-safety-remains-a-concern-for-airports.html', 'snippet': 'About 1,000 times a year, a plane or a vehicle moves onto an active runway by mistake, and regulators have been slow to address the problem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Southwest Airways Flight 844 from Minneapolis had just landed at Chicago’s Midway International Airport last December and was about to cross a runway on its way to the terminal when the co-pilot noticed a business jet barreling toward him. He shouted for the captain to stop. The plane, carrying 74 passengers, screeched to a halt just short of the runway as the smaller jet crossed before their eyes.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/25/business/Nearmiss1/Nearmiss1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 313, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/25/business/Nearmiss1/Nearmiss1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 313}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/25/business/Nearmiss1/Nearmiss1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 533, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/25/business/Nearmiss1/Nearmiss1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1067, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/25/business/Nearmiss1/Nearmiss1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/25/business/Nearmiss1/Nearmiss1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/25/business/Nearmiss1/Nearmiss1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Safer Flights, but Risk Lurks on the Runway', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Safer Flights, but Close Calls Lurk on the Runway', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Aviation Administration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aviation Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRPORTS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Transportation Safety Board', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-25T01:32:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jad Mouawad', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mouawad', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e9ebdf9-9e31-5138-8917-ed4ade3d6a74', 'word_count': 1203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e9ebdf9-9e31-5138-8917-ed4ade3d6a74'}, {'abstract': 'The Republican presidential candidate and the country’s richest of the rich share a fondness for capital gains.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/25/opinion/nocera-romney-and-the-forbes-400.html', 'snippet': 'The Republican presidential candidate and the country’s richest of the rich share a fondness for capital gains.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week, sandwiched between Monday’s leak of the video in which Mitt Romney dismissed “the 47 percent” and Friday’s release of the Romneys’ 2011 tax returns — showing that they had paid an effective tax rate of 14 percent — Forbes magazine published its annual list of the 400 wealthiest Americans. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbLarge-v4.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney and the Forbes 400', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Romney And the Forbes 400', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'High Net Worth Individuals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Gains Tax', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Forbes Magazine', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-25T01:35:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Nocera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nocera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/afc58769-82fc-5544-9708-2b4629685a71', 'word_count': 801, 'uri': 'nyt://article/afc58769-82fc-5544-9708-2b4629685a71'}, {'abstract': 'How predictive are late September polls to the actual outcome of a presidential race? A close look at poll numbers going back to 1936 reveals some strong themes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/25/us/politics/as-election-nears-polls-are-better-predictors.html', 'snippet': 'How predictive are late September polls to the actual outcome of a presidential race? A close look at poll numbers going back to 1936 reveals some strong themes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With fewer than 45 days left in the presidential campaign, it is no longer a cliché to say that every week counts. This is probably the last week, for instance, in which Mitt Romney can reasonably hope that President Obama’s poll numbers will deteriorate because of a deflating convention bounce.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Election Nears, Polls Are Better Predictors', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Solid Record for Polls As Elections Near', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Elections (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-25T01:38:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f4f03c4-7f3b-5275-97b0-2408b2f26de5', 'word_count': 919, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f4f03c4-7f3b-5275-97b0-2408b2f26de5'}, {'abstract': 'At Ecuador’s Middle of the World park, tourists stand on a yellow line that is said to be precisely at Earth’s midpoint. Except that it is not. The Equator is hundreds of feet north.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/25/world/americas/in-ecuador-center-of-the-earth-is-a-little-off-kilter.html', 'snippet': 'At Ecuador’s Middle of the World park, tourists stand on a yellow line that is said to be precisely at Earth’s midpoint. Except that it is not. The Equator is hundreds of feet north.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN ANTONIO DE PICHINCHA, Ecuador — Those who visit the Middle of the World, a government-owned park that pays tribute to the Equator, are not drawn by the trinket shops or cafes offering roasted guinea pig. They want to stand on a yellow line painted on the ground here that is said to be precisely at Earth’s midpoint — 0 degrees latitude, 0 minutes, 0 seconds. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/25/world/ECUADOR/ECUADOR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/25/world/ECUADOR/ECUADOR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/25/world/ECUADOR/ECUADOR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/25/world/ECUADOR/ECUADOR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1362, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/25/world/ECUADOR/ECUADOR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/25/world/ECUADOR/ECUADOR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/25/world/ECUADOR/ECUADOR-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How the Center of the Earth Got a Little Off Kilter', 'kicker': 'San Antonio De Pichincha Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How Center Of the Earth Got a Little Off Kilter', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Antonio de Pichincha (Ecuador)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monuments and Memorials (Structures)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ecuador', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Geography', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-25T01:38:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Neuman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Neuman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce2502c7-6052-593d-b4ef-cf8cda210e31', 'word_count': 959, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce2502c7-6052-593d-b4ef-cf8cda210e31'}, {'abstract': 'Lawyers for the men, imprisoned by the United States military in Afghanistan for years, are filing documents they say undermine a ruling against their clients.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/25/world/asia/us-hearings-again-sought-for-3-detainees.html', 'snippet': 'Lawyers for the men, imprisoned by the United States military in Afghanistan for years, are filing documents they say undermine a ruling against their clients.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Lawyers for three men who have been imprisoned by the United States military in Afghanistan without trial for nearly a decade are renewing their quest for hearings in American courts. They say new information has emerged that undermines an appeals court ruling against them two years ago.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Hearings Again Sought for 3 Detainees', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Hearings Again Sought for 3 Detainees', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Habeas Corpus', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bagram Air Base (Afghanistan)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-25T01:42:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/49b328f6-3b56-595f-831b-811044d52c14', 'word_count': 650, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49b328f6-3b56-595f-831b-811044d52c14'}, {'abstract': 'Richard J. Lipsky, a lobbyist convicted of bribing former State Senator Carl Kruger, is asking a judge for leniency when he is sentenced.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/25/nyregion/richard-lipsky-cooperates-with-authorities-before-his-sentencing.html', 'snippet': 'Richard J. Lipsky, a lobbyist convicted of bribing former State Senator Carl Kruger, is asking a judge for leniency when he is sentenced.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A prominent New York lobbyist convicted of bribing former State Senator Carl Kruger has been secretly cooperating with the federal authorities and is asking a judge for leniency when he is sentenced on Friday, newly filed court documents show.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Convicted Lobbyist Aids U.S. in Inquiry', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Convicted Lobbyist Aids U.S. in Inquiry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bribery and Kickbacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bharara, Preet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lipsky, Richard J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kruger, Carl', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-25T01:43:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Weiser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weiser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3669154-313d-5d99-bf74-8f60a2113a35', 'word_count': 460, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3669154-313d-5d99-bf74-8f60a2113a35'}, {'abstract': 'Ichiro Suzuki treats his bats like fine instruments, delicately caring for them in a moisture-free, shock-proof case for every Yankees game.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/25/sports/baseball/for-ichiro-suzuki-respect-for-bats-is-key-to-hitting.html', 'snippet': 'Ichiro Suzuki treats his bats like fine instruments, delicately caring for them in a moisture-free, shock-proof case for every Yankees game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MINNEAPOLIS — During a game for the Orix Blue Wave in Japan in 1999, Ichiro Suzuki struck out and returned to the dugout unusually frustrated. In a fit of anger, he destroyed his black Mizuno bat. Embarrassed, Suzuki wrote a letter of apology to the craftsman who had made his bats by hand from Tamo wood, grown on the Japanese island of Hokkaido. Such was the respect that Suzuki felt for the process that created the bats, which he wielded with such skill.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/25/sports/ICHIRO/ICHIRO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/25/sports/ICHIRO/ICHIRO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/25/sports/ICHIRO/ICHIRO-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/201