 'kicker': 'Room for Debate', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-25T01:51:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a55fb689-0fb7-5280-8749-4d0d392e812d', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a55fb689-0fb7-5280-8749-4d0d392e812d'}, {'abstract': 'After a weekend of negotiations between the N.F.L. and its locked-out officials, significant differences remain between the two sides, according to a memo from the league’s general counsel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/25/sports/football/packers-seahwaks-monday-night-football-roundup.html', 'snippet': 'After a weekend of negotiations between the N.F.L. and its locked-out officials, significant differences remain between the two sides, according to a memo from the league’s general counsel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After a weekend of negotiations between the N.F.L. — including Commissioner Roger Goodell — and its locked-out game officials, significant economic and noneconomic differences remain between the sides, according to a memo sent to the teams by Jeff Pash, the league’s general counsel and lead negotiator. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/25/sports/YNFL/YNFL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/25/sports/YNFL/YNFL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Officials and League Remain Divided', 'kicker': 'N.F.L. Roundup', 'content_kicker': None,