ct': 'UEFA has finally started to show there is more to their drive for financial sustainability in European soccer than words, but holes remain in its Financial Fair Play rules.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/24/are-financial-fair-play-rules-destined-to-be-broken/', 'snippet': 'UEFA has finally started to show there is more to their drive for financial sustainability in European soccer than words, but holes remain in its Financial Fair Play rules.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the UEFA president Michel Platini preached prudence and wisdom to Europe’s soccer elite last month, the setting seemed rather incongruous, almost undermining the words he spoke.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Are Financial Fair Play Rules Destined to Be Broken?', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Union of European Football Assns (UEFA)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-25T03:45:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Graham Ruthven', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Graham', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ruthven', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4199130a-c45e-59cf-bda4-c36006c1158c', 'word_count': 819, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4199130a-c45e-59cf-bda4-c36006c1158c'}, {'abstract': 'This word has appeared in 200 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/25/word-of-the-day-translucent/', 'snippet': 'This word has appeared in 200 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'translucent •\\tranz-ˈlü-sənt\\• adjective', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Word of the Day | translucent', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-25T04:02:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/987b2739-9990-5189-9908-d8f79368e9b4', 'word_count': 250, 'uri': 'nyt://article/987b2739-9990-5189-9908-d8f79368e9b4'}, {'abstract': 'A major investor for the $12 million musical “Rebecca,” a mystery man named Paul Abrams, seems to have died before raising $4.5 million for the show, leading to questions about whether he existed at all.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/25/theater/rebecca-the-musical-and-the-vanishing-act-of-its-investor.html', 'snippet': 'A major investor for the $12 million musical “Rebecca,” a mystery man named Paul Abrams, seems to have died before raising $4.5 million for the show, leading to questions about whether he existed at all.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The business of Broadway has always been cloaked in mystery. Most of its 40 theaters are run by three private organizations that operate out of public view. Producers keep deal-making under wraps. The biggest mystery of all is why so many sophisticated investors go along with business-as-usual on Broadway when few shows turn a profit.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/25/arts/subrebecca/subrebecca-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/25/arts/subrebecca/subrebecca-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/25/arts/subrebecca/subrebecca-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 668, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/25/arts/subrebecca/subrebecca-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1335, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/25/arts/subrebecca/subrebecca-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/25/arts/subrebecca/subrebecca-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/25/arts/subrebecca/subrebecca-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Rebecca’ Sees Investor Fade, as if Dreamt', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Rebecca’ Sees Investor Fade, As if Dreamt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shubert Organization', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abrams, Paul', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Rebecca (Play)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sprecher, Ben', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-25T04:16:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank':