zor.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/25/man-charged-with-hate-crime-after-antigay-attack/', 'snippet': 'Keith Patron, 44, got into an argument with a man inside a McDonald’s in the West Village, the police said, made antigay statements and cut him with a razor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A 44-year-old man has been arrested on charges of hate-crime assault for the antigay slashing last week of a 22-year-old man in a McDonald’s in the West Village, the police said on Tuesday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Man Charged With Hate Crime After Antigay Attack', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hate Crimes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Village (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-25T15:42:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/860af433-d62a-5ec7-947b-dd9aecc184ec', 'word_count': 133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/860af433-d62a-5ec7-947b-dd9aecc184ec'}, {'abstract': 'An exhibition at the Aperture Gallery explores how the petrochemical industry has reshaped the Mississippi River corridor in Louisiana.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/25/a-landscape-reconfigured/', 'snippet': 'An exhibition at the Aperture Gallery explores how the petrochemical industry has reshaped the Mississippi River corridor in Louisiana.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the stark white space of the Aperture Gallery in Chelsea, billboard-size photographs present an array of haunting scenes. A chemical plant with a cemetery in the foreground. An empty basketball court alongside a turreted oil refinery. A lush swamp filled with trees, one of which has a Shell Oil sign nailed to it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Oil and Nature: A Landscape Reconfigured', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chemicals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hazardous and Toxic Substances', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pipelines', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refineries', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Misrach, Richard', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'APERTURE FOUNDATION', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Louisiana', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mississippi River', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-25T15:50:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emma Bryce', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emma', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bryce', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d1aee79-ca72-5b10-a565-ff91ae510831', 'word_count': 638, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d1aee79-ca72-5b10-a565-ff91ae510831'}, {'abstract': 'Stephen C. Byrd, a Broadway producer, says he has seen the film at least 25 times and is developing a stage musical based on it.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/25/producer-hopes-to-bring-black-orpheus-to-broadway/', 'snippet': 'Stephen C. Byrd, a Broadway producer, says he has seen the film at least 25 times and is developing a stage musical based on it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Broadway producer Stephen C. Byrd, who mounted a multiracial “Streetcar Named Desire” last season and an all-black “Cat on a Hot Tin Roof” in 2008, is developing a new stage musical based on the 1959 film “Black Orpheus,” which won the Academy Award for best foreign-language picture in 1960.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Producer Hopes to Bring ‘Black Orpheus’ to Broadway', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Broadway Plans For ‘Black Orpheus’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ashford, Rob', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Byrd, Stephen C', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jobim, Antonio Carlos', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Bill T', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taymor, Julie', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rio de Janeiro (Brazil)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-25T15:57:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/38d4813c-6782-5427-8828-18ece581ba60', 'word_count': 296, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38d4813c-6782-5427-8828-18ece581ba60'}, {'abstract': 'Conventions of 1912 were described as having “psychopathic” conditions. In 1966, a columnist wrote that George Romney was “almost too good to be true.” And in 1974, Richard Nixon got the editorial cartoon treatment. Take a peek into our archive to see how has the IHT covered U.S. politics in the past.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/25/iht125-presidential-coverage/', 'snippet': 'Conventions of 1912 were described as having “psychopathic” conditions. In 1966, a columnist wrote that George Romney was “almost too good to be true.” And in 1974, Richard Nixon got the editorial cartoon treatment. Take a peek into our archive to...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The International Herald Tribune celebrates its 125th birthday in October, and over the coming weeks we’ll be sharing highlights from our archives.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/24/opinion/25iht-rdv-elections-ss-slide-R59O/25iht-rdv-elections-ss-slide-R59O-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 467, 'width': 1021, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/24/opinion/25iht-rdv-elections-ss-slide-R59O/25iht-rdv-elections-ss-slide-R59O-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 467, 'width': 1021, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Some Things Never Change', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-25T16:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eleanor Miller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eleanor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://ar