urn the controversial call of a game-winning touchdown for the Seahawks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'N.F.L. Supports Decision Not to Overturn Winning Touchdown', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Officiating (Sports)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Green Bay Packers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Seattle Seahawks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-25T16:57:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f144c1f2-0efe-5aaf-97d9-a57e00133fba', 'word_count': 529, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f144c1f2-0efe-5aaf-97d9-a57e00133fba'}, {'abstract': 'Even many health care professionals remain unfamiliar with Lewy body dementia, though it affects about 1.3 million people in this country.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/25/a-form-of-dementia-that-is-often-misdiagnosed/', 'snippet': 'Even many health care professionals remain unfamiliar with Lewy body dementia, though it affects about 1.3 million people in this country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lori Roberts’s father, who used to deliver the mail in Mitchell, S.D., has undergone startling personality changes. “He used to be very easygoing,” Ms. Roberts said. “Now he’s gotten kind of physical with my mom and my brother, pushing and shoving.” The other day, when her exhausted mother visited him in the nursing home he had recently entered — by sad coincidence, it was their 53rd wedding anniversary – he loudly insisted that she take him to Mexico, immediately.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Form of Dementia That Is Often Misdiagnosed', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dementia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Paul', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York University Langone Medical Center', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-25T16:58:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paula Span', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paula', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Span', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4629317-5639-5657-bf43-14c6b66c138e', 'word_count': 873, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4629317-5639-5657-bf43-14c6b66c138e'}, {'abstract': 'Andrew Bird, a talented multi-instrumentalist from Chicago, has been described as having one of the most vivid imaginations in modern indie rock.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/25/booming/25match-booming.html', 'snippet': 'Andrew Bird, a talented multi-instrumentalist from Chicago, has been described as having one of the most vivid imaginations in modern indie rock.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Each week, Val Haller, the founder of the music Web site Valslist.com, matches music from her baby boom generation to music of her 20-something sons’ generation. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/25/booming/25match-booming/25match-booming-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 323, 'width': 28