under a new visa agreement that the two countries reached this month.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia Eases Limits on Visas for Americans', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Visas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-25T17:00:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathleen Calkins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathleen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Calkins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac0377cf-c25b-5fd8-8b6b-1e1b49babac0', 'word_count': 167, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac0377cf-c25b-5fd8-8b6b-1e1b49babac0'}, {'abstract': 'CBS showed some weakness for the premiere of “Partners” and “Hawaii Five-O,” and ratings took a nosedive for ABC’s “Dancing With the Stars.”', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/25/first-night-of-the-new-season-has-nbc-and-cbs-swapping-places/', 'snippet': 'CBS showed some weakness for the premiere of “Partners” and “Hawaii Five-O,” and ratings took a nosedive for ABC’s “Dancing With the Stars.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first night of the official network television season turned the competition almost on its head as NBC dominated in the advertiser-preferred ratings, ABC dominated with older viewers, CBS saw its Monday lineup take a dive and Fox took a general battering.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'First Night of the New Season Has NBC and CBS Swapping Places', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ratings (Audience Measurement)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sheen, Charlie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC INC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-25T17:05:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d59bbd2-9b0e-545d-92f3-874c59ea5af5', 'word_count': 470, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d59bbd2-9b0e-545d-92f3-874c59ea5af5'}, {'abstract': 'The accessories designer Kristine Johannes brings something new to the landscape of luxury handbags.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/25/one-word-plastics-2/', 'snippet': 'The accessories designer Kristine Johannes brings something new to the landscape of luxury handbags.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In an effort to bring something new to the landscape of luxury handbags, the accessories designer Kristine Johannes deliberately avoided the one material that most obviously defines it: leather. “I just got sick of skins,” says Johannes, whose previous stints at J. Crew and Devi Kroell required a good amount of working with hides and exotics. “There are so many amazing man-made materials, I thought, ‘Why does the standard evening bag have to look like X?’ “ Which is how Rauwolf, Johannes’s line of angular plexiglass evening clutches, came to be so Y. Produced in an Italian factory that specializes in accessory parts like belt buckles and shoe heels, the seven bags in the fall collection take their cues from cut gemstones, with sharp lines, reflective surfaces and facets as dizzying as diamonds. “In a way, plexi is like stone,” Johannes says. “It comes in all of these thicknesses and gets carved down and filed down and heat treated to do what you want it to do.” The glassy-blue Shalimar clutch above has a magnetic closure, a sharp hourglass shape and — bonus points — doubles as a mirror for the quick makeup check. $2,300; rauwolfnyc.com.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'One Word: Plastics', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'One Word: Plastics', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-25T17:05:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane Herman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Herman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/79012601-3f98-5f12-a3b9-d6aebb63b957', 'word_count': 196, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79012601-3f98-5f12-a3b9-d6aebb63b957'}, {'abstract': 'The British Bankers’ Association is expected to give up its responsibility for the global interest rate at the center of a recent manipulation scandal, according to a person with direct knowledge of the matter.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/09/25/british-bankers-group-seen-losing-control-over-libor/', 'snippet': 'The British Bankers’ Association is expected to give up its responsibility for the global interest rate at the center of a recent manipulation scandal, according to a person with direct knowledge of the matter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — A British banking group is preparing to give up its control over the interest rate at the center of a recent manipulation scandal, according to a person with direct knowledge of the matter.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'British Bankers Group May Give Up Control Over Libor', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trade Group Seen as Near Conceding Libor Power', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Libor (London Interbank Offered Rate)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wheatley, Martin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "British Bankers' Association", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-25T17:11:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b87cbb5b-8bf7-5643-84da-80bbb6300dbe', 'word_count': 764, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b87cbb5b-8bf7-5643-84da-80bbb6300dbe'}, {'abstract': 'The candidate has fine ideas on foreign aid. But they’re not exactly new.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/25/romney-at-the-clinton-global-initiative/', 'snippet': 'The candidate has fine ideas on foreign aid. But they’re not exactly new.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Republican nominee’s speech at the Clinton Global Initiative was surprisingly reasonable. Granted, Mr. Romney got in a few digs at President Obama, but they were subtle and almost funny. And he was a bit light on details, but the occasion didn’t really call for granularity.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney at the Clinton Global Initiative', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Aid', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Clinton Global Initiative', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-25T17:15:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae30ca16-8a71-541f-ba07-81e133138705', 'word_count': 513, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae30ca16-8a71-541f-ba07-81e133138705'}, {'abstract': 'In the course of an investigation into Representative Maxine Waters, the special committee determined that the House rules were not sufficient to prevent certain conflicts of interest.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/25/after-waters-inquiry-house-panel-recommends-new-ethics-rules/', 'snippet': 'In the course of an investigation into Representative Maxine Waters, the special committee determined that the House rules were not sufficient to prevent certain conflicts of interest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Saying that public trust is at stake, a special House ethics panel on Tuesday called for new rules to prevent lawmakers and their staffs from violating conflict of interest standards and proposed other new measures designed to keep partisan squabbles from undermining future investigations of such wrongdoing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Waters Inquiry, House Panel Recommends New Ethics Rules', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conflicts of Interest', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Institutional)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Waters, Maxine', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'OneUnited Bank', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-25T17:21:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Lipton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lipton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1fa898f8-e608-5cee-9a3f-edd94caeed7d', 'word_count': 882, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1fa898f8-e608-5cee-9a3f-edd94caeed7d'}, {'abstract': 'Ads that incite hatred against Muslims may be legal, but they are wrong and repugnant.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/25/opinion/the-sin-of-sowing-hatred-of-islam.html', 'snippet': 'Ads that incite hatred against Muslims may be legal, but they are wrong and repugnant.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two weeks ago, on the morning of Sept. 11, I noticed a woman wearing a traditional Muslim head covering on the packed platform of the train station in Scarsdale, N.Y. Her attention was focused on a billboard ad that announced “19,250 deadly Islamic attacks since 9/11/01” and pre-empted those who might dispute that claim with the refrain: “It’s not Islamophobia, it’s Islamorealism.” I could only imagine what she was feeling. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Sin of Sowing Hatred of Islam', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Sin of Sowing Hatred of Islam', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Freedom Defense Initiative', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslim-Americans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transit Systems', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Transportation Authority', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-25T17:23:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Jacobs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jacobs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/64c45715-bf26-5edf-92d9-45c987802165', 'word_count': 720, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64c45715-bf26-5edf-92d9-45c987802165'}, {'abstract': 'Authors of a study claimed that fewer particulate emissions were produced by running commercial diesel engines than by charbroiling hamburgers.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/25/charbroiling-burgers-an-air-quality-scourge-that-may-be-worse-than-diesel-trucks/', 'snippet': 'Authors of a study claimed that fewer particulate emissions were produced by running commercial diesel engines than by charbroiling hamburgers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Freakonomics-like fashion, researchers at the University of California, Riverside, have concluded that producing a charbroiled hamburger emits