ironment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanna M. Foster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ce1e836-1af4-5231-bd29-b7f6c1a2fcee', 'word_count': 384, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ce1e836-1af4-5231-bd29-b7f6c1a2fcee'}, {'abstract': 'Tuesday is the last day that Representative Todd Akin, a Republican, can drop out of the Senate race against Senator Claire McCaskill in Missouri.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/us/politics/100000001805866/a-deadline-in-the-missouri-senate-race.html', 'snippet': 'Tuesday is the last day that Representative Todd Akin, a Republican, can drop out of the Senate race against Senator Claire McCaskill in Missouri.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tuesday is the last day that Representative Todd Akin, a Republican, can drop out of the Senate race against Senator Claire McCaskill in Missouri.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/25/us/politics/video-pol-120925-missouri/video-pol-120925-missouri-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/25/us/politics/video-pol-120925-missouri/video-pol-120925-missouri-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/25/us/politics/video-pol-120925-missouri/video-pol-120925-missouri-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/25/us/politics/video-pol-120925-missouri/video-pol-120925-missouri-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Deadline in the Missouri Senate Race', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Missouri', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Akin, Todd', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCaskill, Claire', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-25T19:02:10+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'John Eligon, Dan Gill and Vijai Singh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eligon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gill', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Vijai', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Singh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/a1616aa4-f76e-5dc1-8522-676f88f328e8', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/a1616aa4-f76e-5dc1-8522-676f88f328e8'}, {'abstract': 'Kit Kemp, hotel owner and interior designer, details her approach to distinctive decorating in a new book.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/25/one-of-a-kind/', 'snippet': 'Kit Kemp, hotel owner and interior designer, details her approach to distinctive decorating in a new book.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the eight hotels that Kit Kemp owns with her husband, Tim — among them the Crosby Street Hotel in Manhattan and the Dorset Square Hotel in London — no two rooms are alike. This is because Kemp, who designed the spaces, eschews the common practice of selecting a single scheme to be repeated throughout, instead embarking on a painstaking process of decorating every room to be utterly distinct from the next. She selects each, say, 1960s Lucite lamp, piece of boiled-wool upholstery and Filipino totem sculpture, then pulls them all together in a highly individualized, homey whole that is greater than the sum of its parts. In a new book, “Kit Kemp: A Living Space” (Hardie Grant, $50), Kemp details her approach to design (for residential as well as hotel projects), and sums it up as, “Keep it personal.” Her secret? Finding “little touches — like using a kerosene can, instead of classically cut crystal, as a lamp base in a romantic bedroom.”', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'One of a Kind', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'One of a Kind', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-25T19:02:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abby Aguirre', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Aguirre', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb63164b-0067-5837-b142-25587590ddef', 'word_count': 164, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb63164b-0067-5837-b142-25587590ddef'}, {'abstract': 'A new show at the Musée du Quai Branly in Paris celebrates the importance of hair in art, fashion, style, ritual, sexuality, religion and culture, from antiquity to today.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/25/in-paris-an-exhibition-dedicated-to-hair/', 'snippet': 'A new show at the Musée du Quai Branly in Paris celebrates the importance of hair in art, fashion, style, ritual, sexuality, religion and culture, from antiquity to today.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Hair, as the song from the musical goes, can be “long, straight, curly, fuzzy, snaggy, shaggy, ratty, matty, oily, greasy, fleecy.” ', 'print_se