'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f929fa03-8b16-5cf0-88a7-b921e534b61f', 'word_count': 374, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f929fa03-8b16-5cf0-88a7-b921e534b61f'}, {'abstract': 'The ceremony will be held on Oct. 15 at the Apollo Theater and hosted by Elizabeth Streb.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/25/paul-taylor-to-receive-bessie-lifetime-achievement-award/', 'snippet': 'The ceremony will be held on Oct. 15 at the Apollo Theater and hosted by Elizabeth Streb.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The choreographer Paul Taylor will receive a lifetime achievement Bessie, the nickname for the New York Dance and Performance Awards, Dance/NYC, which helps produce the award ceremony, said on Tuesday. Alice Teirstein, the founding director of the Young Dancemakers Company and a longtime faculty member at the Fieldston School, will be honored for service to the dance field. The ceremony will be held on Oct. 15 at the Apollo Theater, hosted by Elizabeth Streb and featuring performances by the Trisha Brown Company and Souleymane Badolo. Presenters include Marina Abramovic, Ron Brown, Brenda Bufalino, Archie Burnett, Bebe Neuwirth, Charles Reinhart, David Thomson, and Wendy Whelan.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paul Taylor to Receive Bessie Lifetime Achievement Award', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Bessie Award For Paul Taylor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Dance and Performance Awards (Bessies)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taylor, Paul', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'APOLLO THEATER', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dancemakers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-25T19:30:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c965cd52-95cc-56fb-a8ff-21bc7db68378', 'word_count': 105, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c965cd52-95cc-56fb-a8ff-21bc7db68378'}, {'abstract': 'The G.A.O. concluded that the credit was too small to sway business owners. Moreover, it said, claiming the credit is a task so complicated as to discourage many companies from trying.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/25/why-the-health-care-tax-credit-eludes-many-small-businesses/', 'snippet': 'The G.A.O. concluded that the credit was too small to sway business owners. Moreover, it said, claiming the credit is a task so complicated as to discourage many companies from trying.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Agenda has now profiled three small businesses that are struggling in different ways with providing health insurance to employees. The companies are very different — they trade in very different parts of the economy, and couldn’t be located much further apart\xa0geographically — but they do have one thing in common: Though all three have fewer than 25 employees, not one has qualified for the tax credit in the Affordable Care Act that was intended to help small businesses pay for health insurance. Indeed, the credit is one element of the controversial health law that has already fallen short of expectations.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why the Health Care Tax Credit Eludes Many Small Businesses', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and