09/25/past-forward-the-fight-over-fracking/', 'snippet': 'A look at Western Pennsylvania and what fracking may actually mean for people’s lives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With a skeptical eye fixed on industry in an era of rapid technological development two generations ago, Rachel Carson “made a powerful case for the idea that if humankind poisoned nature, nature would in turn poison humankind,” as Eliza Griswold put it in last weekend’s magazine, marking the 50th anniversary of the publication of Carson’s\xa0seminal book, “Silent Spring.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/24/magazine/24-fracking-spread/24-fracking-spread-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 491, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/24/magazine/24-fracking-spread/24-fracking-spread-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 491, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/24/magazine/24-fracking-spread/24-fracking-spread-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/24/magazine/24-fracking-spread/24-fracking-spread-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/24/magazine/24-fracking-spread/24-fracking-spread-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Past Forward: The Fight Over Fracking', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'n