: 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/12236a24-93fa-50cb-a672-8c172a59fd7e', 'word_count': 596, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12236a24-93fa-50cb-a672-8c172a59fd7e'}, {'abstract': 'David Flynn and Nicolas Clerc of the hot new cafe Télescope share their favorite spots.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/25/in-paris-restos-for-fashions-restless/', 'snippet': 'David Flynn and Nicolas Clerc of the hot new cafe Télescope share their favorite spots.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Coffee is having something of a fashionable moment in Paris, a city long derided for its substandard roasts. And at the vanguard of the bean revolution are David Flynn and Nicolas Clerc of the hot new cafe Télescope, which proved an instant hit when it opened behind the Palais Royal’s illustrious arcades in April. Clerc, a Parisian photographer, and Flynn, the American co-founder of the monthly barista throwdown Frog Fight, also happen to be very attuned to the city’s evolving culinary scene. They’re as discerning about the food they eat as the coffee they brew and drink.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Paris, Restos for Fashion’s Restless', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-25T21:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lindsey Tramuta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lindsey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tramuta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/034cb9fd-c3ea-548b-b6fe-22e845e3f60d', 'word_count': 564, 'uri': 'nyt://article/034cb9fd-c3ea-548b-b6fe-22e845e3f60d'}, {'abstract': 'The strike, by a United States drone in Pakistan’s North Waziristan region, killed five people, including the two militants, a Pakistani official said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/26/world/asia/qaeda-operatives-killed-in-drone-strike-official-says.html', 'snippet': 'The strike, by a United States drone in Pakistan’s North Waziristan region, killed five people, including the two militants, a Pakistani official said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PESHAWAR, Pakistan — An Al Qaeda operative of Turkish origin and an Iraqi reported to be a liaison between Al Qaeda and the Taliban were among five people killed on Monday in a United States drone strike in Pakistan’s lawless North Waziristan region, a Pakistani security official confirmed Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Qaeda Operatives Killed in Drone Strike, Official Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pakistan: U.S. Drone Strike Kills Two Linked to Al Qaeda, Official Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civilian Casualties', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drones (Pilotless Planes)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Waziristan (Pakistan)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-25T21:01:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_nam