” about what it’s like to experience the New York City subway.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/26/arts/dance/a-single-ride-by-ephrat-asherie-at-dixon-place.html', 'snippet': 'The talented Ephrat Asherie, known in the dance world as Bounce, has choreographed “Single Ride,” about what it’s like to experience the New York City subway.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What is it about a subway ride that ignites a choreographer’s imagination? In recent years the subway-inspired dance has become as frequent as the L train at rush hour. Remember Camille A. Brown’s energetic yet contrived “Groove to Nobody’s Business” for Alvin Ailey American Dance Theater? Just about every retelling of what it’s like to experience the New York City subway proves that while there’s a lot to see — stations bustle with constant activity — there really isn’t much to say. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/26/arts/BOUNCE/BOUNCE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/26/arts/BOUNCE/BOUNCE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1474, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/26/arts/BOUNCE/BOUNCE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/26/arts/BOUNCE/BOUNCE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/26/arts/BOUNCE/BOUNCE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Grooving to the Beat and Bang of the Subway', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Grooving to the Beat And Bang of the Subway', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-25T21:33:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/01c587aa-bf71-5cc4-95ba-2c6880380377', 'word_count': 396, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01c587aa-bf71-5cc4-95ba-2c6880380377'}, {'abstract': 'Google said it hasn’t made a move to restore its maps to the iPhone, but it declined to say whether the company had submitted a new maps app to Apple’s App Store. And why would Google show its cards? Here is an opportunity for the company to show that phones using Android have a more robust maps product. Some of Apple’s other competitors are already playing this game.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/25/rivals-pile-on-apple-maps/', 'snippet': 'Google said it hasn’t made a move to restore its maps to the iPhone, but it declined to say whether the company had submitted a new maps app to Apple’s App Store. And why would Google show its cards? Here is an opportunity for the company to show ...', 'lead_paragraph': ' Eric E. Schmidt, Google’s chairman, told reporters in Tokyo on Tuesday that the company had done nothing to get its maps back onto the iPhone since Apple removed them in its new iOS 6 operating system\xa0for mobile devices.\xa0He said Apple should have stuck with Google’s maps, but, according to Bloomberg, he declined to say whether the company had submitted a new maps app to Apple’s App Store.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Apple’s Competitors Pile On With Map Critiques', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maps', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schmidt, Eric E', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-25T21:34:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian X. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5fcc7430-ebf5-547e-98ac-8db2b0d64f89', 'word_count': 501, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5fcc7430-ebf5-547e-98ac-8db2b0d64f89'}, {'abstract': 'Marcus Samuelsson teams with Restaurant Associates at Lincoln Center and the M. Wells team is back, at MoMA P.S. 1.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/26/dining/a-marcus-samuelsson-collaboration-at-lincoln-center-the-m-wells-team-at-moma-ps-1.html', 'snippet': 'Marcus Samuelsson teams with Restaurant Associates at Lincoln Center and the M. Wells team is back, at MoMA P.S. 1.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Opening', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/26/dining/27OFF/27OFF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 731, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/26/dining