cy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/26/arts/26schneemann/26schneemann-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1456, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/26/arts/26schneemann/26schneemann-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/26/arts/26schneemann/26schneemann-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/26/arts/26schneemann/26schneemann-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Veteran of Judson Dance Recalls Its Wild 1960s Heyday', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Veteran of Judson Dance Recalls Its Wild 1960s Heyday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Danspace Project', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schneemann, Carolee', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-25T21:54:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Seibert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seibert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f2b438b5-4e8e-5e7f-832e-34c2cff10a32', 'word_count': 550, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f2b438b5-4e8e-5e7f-832e-34c2cff10a32'}, {'abstract': 'Blacksocks, a Swiss company, attaches a radio ID tag to its socks so that by using an RFID reader, you can always put the correct pair together.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/25/radio-tagged-socks-for-the-obsessive/', 'snippet': 'Blacksocks, a Swiss company, attaches a radio ID tag to its socks so that by using an RFID reader, you can always put the correct pair together.', 'lead_paragraph': 'How do you know when you have slipped from detail-oriented, past anal-retentive, all the way to obsessive-compulsive?', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Radio-Tagged Socks for the Obsessive', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An App Too Far? Using an iPhone to Sort Your Socks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-25T21:57:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roy Furchgott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Furchgott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0726eaa-e399-5676-9644-c1a59bb310e7', 'word_count': 377, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0726eaa-e399-5676-9644-c1a59bb310e7'}, {'abstract': 'And why you should go see them.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/25/efterklang-tonight-at-the-apple-store-in-soho/', 'snippet': 'And why you should go see them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I had the great fortune this weekend of seeing the Danish band Efterklang perform at the Metropolitan Museum of Art. The band (whose name means “reverberation” or something close to it in Danish) performed with an orchestra, backup singers and a horn section. To reach the theater where the concert was held, you had to meander through the Egyptian exhibit: past ornate sarcophaguses and hieroglyphic friezes. I’d never been to any kind of presentation in a museum, particularly on a Saturday night. I kind of half-expected some crank in the audience (all seated reverently) to rise and declaim his apocalyptic visions, as in ‘‘The DaVinci Code’’ or ‘‘12 Monkeys.’’ That didn’t happen, quite. But for an encore, the singer, Caspar Clausen, exhorted the crowd to stand and groove for at least a few minutes. The crowd obliged.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Efterklang, Tonight at the Apple Store in SoHo', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-25T22:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By WM. FERGUSON', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Wm', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/74f01944-a64f-52b9-81a0-7ac0bb17071d', 'word_count': 180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74f01944-a64f-52b9-81a0-7ac0bb17071d'}, {'abstract': 'Facebook does not offer a way to automatically merge two personal accounts, but you can do it manually.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/25/qa-combining-two-facebook-pages/', 'snippet': 'Facebook does not offer a way to automatically merge two personal accounts, but you can do it manually.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q&A: Combining Two Facebook Pages', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Combining Facebook Pages', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_da