firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lyall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55c486a2-d090-5f52-8059-0bfcc41e1e3e', 'word_count': 914, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55c486a2-d090-5f52-8059-0bfcc41e1e3e'}, {'abstract': 'Brett Gardner, who had inflamed tissue and a bone spur removed from his non-throwing elbow July 24, was activated by the Yankees Tuesday as a possible pinch runner.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/25/gardner-returns-for-pinch-running-duty/', 'snippet': 'Brett Gardner, who had inflamed tissue and a bone spur removed from his non-throwing elbow July 24, was activated by the Yankees Tuesday as a possible pinch runner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MINNEAPOLIS — Brett Gardner still has not taken batting practice on the field, and he might not be ready to hit in a game until next week. But the Yankees need Gardner’s legs more than his bat, and his legs are fine.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gardner Returns for Pinch-Running Duty', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gardner, Brett', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T00:06:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pat Borzi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pat', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borzi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ab54544-2de9-549c-8198-b3f2b6f9784a', 'word_count': 718, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ab54544-2de9-549c-8198-b3f2b6f9784a'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Keen was a scholar who re-examined the code used among knights and determined it was meant to protect the warrior class rather than to emphasize good deeds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/26/books/maurice-h-keen-dies-at-78-redefined-chivalry.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Keen was a scholar who re-examined the code used among knights and determined it was meant to protect the warrior class rather than to emphasize good deeds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Honorable men, as they were called in the golden age of chivalry, were rich enough to outfit a squadron of knights and brutal enough to lead them into battle, often culminating in the killing and plundering of civilian populations. The code of chivalry defined honor in ways that are familiar to people today — as honesty, loyalty, courage — and in ways that are not. It was honorable, for example, to show mercy to a defeated enemy, but only if the enemy was a social equal. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/26/world/keen-obit-1/keen-obit-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 708, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/26/world/keen-obit-1/keen-obit-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1416, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/26/world/keen-obit-1/keen-obit-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/26/world/keen-obit-1/keen-obit-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, '