: 'The attack on a hotel housing newly elected lawmakers came as an American team arrived in Tripoli to investigate the death of Ambassador J. Christopher Stevens.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BENGHAZI, Libya — Libyan militia fighters assaulted a hotel in Tripoli housing members of the newly elected General National Congress on Tuesday, dramatizing the challenge the government faces in enforcing its ultimatum that all unauthorized brigades must submit to its authority or disband by the start of the day. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Libya Presses Some Militias to Disband, Fighters Attack a Hotel in Tripoli', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Libya Presses Some Militias to Disband, Fighters Attack a Hotel in Tripoli', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qaddafi, Muammar el-', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stevens, J Christopher', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T00:48:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By David D. Kirkpatrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed1d8ad1-6068-5f9e-af92-87da674e8890', 'word_count': 805, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed1d8ad1-6068-5f9e-af92-87da674e8890'}, {'abstract': 'Studies of more than 50,000 people who watched the Games depict vast shifts in how people watch television, especially with second devices like tablets or smartphones.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/26/business/media/nbc-unpacks-trove-of-viewer-data-from-london-olympics.html', 'snippet': 'Studies of more than 50,000 people who watched the Games depict vast shifts in how people watch television, especially with second devices like tablets or smartphones.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ONE afternoon in early August, a 41-year-old working mother in Los Angeles didn’t get much work done.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/26/business/ADCO-1/ADCO-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 811, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/26/business/ADCO-1/ADCO-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1622, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'NBC Unpacks Trove of Data From Olympics', 'kicker': 'Advertising', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'NBC Unpacks Trove of Data From Olympics', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tablet Computers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NBC Universal', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T00:52:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'origi