_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c16e9f12-78ab-5cc2-acde-4487ac61cf94', 'word_count': 738, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c16e9f12-78ab-5cc2-acde-4487ac61cf94'}, {'abstract': 'Roger Goodell, commissioner of the National Football League, is caught between the fiasco of this season’s replacement officials and a lockout being enforced by deep-pocketed team owners.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/26/sports/football/nfl-commissioner-goodell-caught-between-bad-calls-and-owners.html', 'snippet': 'Roger Goodell, commissioner of the National Football League, is caught between the fiasco of this season’s replacement officials and a lockout being enforced by deep-pocketed team owners.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Roger Goodell became the commissioner of the National Football League in 2006, he made protecting certain aspects of the sport’s good name his consuming aim. He was concerned with the fan experience at stadiums as well as the behavior of players in bars. Goodell wanted a league populated by upstanding citizens who provided captivating entertainment while, not incidentally, generating great business, too.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/26/sports/football/26goodell-span/26goodell-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/26/sports/football/26goodell-span/26goodell-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/26/sports/football/26goodell-span/26goodell-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/26/sports/fo