aph': 'One of the iron laws of Middle East politics for the last half-century has been that extremists go all the way and moderates tend to just go away. That is what made the march in Benghazi, Libya, so unusual last Friday. This time, the moderates did not just go away. They got together and stormed the headquarters of the Islamist militia Ansar al-Sharia, whose members are suspected of carrying out the attack on the U.S. Consulate in Benghazi that resulted in the death of four Americans, including Ambassador Chris Stevens.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Backlash to the Backlash', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Backlash to the Backlash', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T01:03:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas L. Friedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Friedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/faa864f9-e0e3-592b-a866-aff6c50b634a', 'word_count': 865, 'uri': 'nyt://article/faa864f9-e0e3-592b-a866-aff6c50b634a'}, {'abstract': 'The city and state governments need to restore cuts and reinstate programs that helped destitute families get on back their feet.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/26/opinion/more-children-in-homeless-shelters.html', 'snippet': 'The city and state governments need to restore cuts and reinstate programs that helped destitute families get on back their feet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Almost 20,000 children now go to bed every night in New York City’s homeless shelters, up from 16,000 last year. If homelessness is hard on adults, for the young, it can be disastrous, starting a slide into a lifetime of problems. Mayor Michael Bloomberg and Gov. Andrew Cuomo could reduce these numbers by restarting programs that help homeless families move from shelters to permanent rental housing. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Children in Homeless Shelters', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'More Children in Homeless Shelters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homeless Persons', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T01:04:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ab5777e-d99e-5835-bee1-8d297752db43', 'word_count': 325, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ab5777e-d99e-5835-bee1-8d297752db43'}, {'abstract': 'With the high-stakes Senate race still very close, Senator Scott P. Brown is seeking to convert almost everything into a character attack on Elizabeth Warren.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/26/us/politics/in-massachusetts-brown-attacks-warrens-character.html', 'snippet': 'With the high-stakes Senate race still very close, Senator Scott P. Brown is seeking to convert almost everything into a character attack on Elizabeth Warren.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON — Video emerged on Tuesday showing supporters of Senator Scott P. Brown making tomahawk gestures with their arms and yelling Indian war whoops at supporters of Elizabeth Warren, his Democratic challenger, outside a pub on Saturday. The gestures were meant to mock Ms. Warren’s assertions, for which she has offered no documentation, that she has Native American ancestry.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/26/us/ALT-MASS-1/ALT-MASS-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 781, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/26/us/ALT-MASS-1/ALT-MASS-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1563, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/26/us/ALT-MASS-1/ALT-MASS-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/26/us/ALT-MASS-1/ALT-MASS-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/26/us/ALT-MASS-1/ALT-MASS-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Massachusetts, Brown Attacks Warren’s Character', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Close Massachusetts Senate Race, Brown Attacks Warren’s Character', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Warren, Elizabeth', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Scott P', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Senate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T01:05:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katharine Q. Seelye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katharine', 'middlename': 'Q.', 'lastname': 'Seelye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/afb78e5e-6ff0-5fad-8fb1-60f0763130b3', 'word_count': 966, 'uri': 'nyt://article/afb78e5e-6ff0-5fad-8fb1-60f0763130b3'}, {'abstract': 'Federal regulators need to make sure that easier billing doesn’t lead to Medicare fraud by billing for services never provided.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/26/opinion/abuse-of-electronic-medical-records.html', 'snippet': 'Federal regulators need to make sure that easier billing doesn’t lead to Medicare fraud by billing for services never provided.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Obama administration has issued a strong and much-needed warning to hospitals and doctors about the fraudulent use of electronic medical records to illegally inflate their billings to Medicare. Attorney General Eric Holder Jr. and the health and human services secretary, Kathleen Sebelius, cited “troubling indications” that some providers are billing for services never provided and vowed to prosecute. They sent a letter to five major hospital trade associations on Monday, two days after an article in The Times described in detail how greater use of electronic records might be making it easier for hospitals and doctors to submit erroneous payment claims.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Abuse of Electronic Health Records', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Abuse of Electronic Health Records', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electronic Health Records', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Center for Public Integrity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN HOSPITAL ASSN', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T01:05:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1801c46-d900-513c-857c-5f5506651e39', 'word_count': 422, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1801c46-d900-513c-857c-5f5506651e39'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama and Mitt Romney have very different approaches to deficit reduction. Figures below are drawn from similar base lines reflecting realistic fiscal situations, as generally agreed to by research organizations and the Congressional Budget Office.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2012/09/25/us/politics/comparing-the-candidates-deficit-proposals.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama and Mitt Romney have very different approaches to deficit reduction. Figures below are drawn from similar base lines reflecting realistic fiscal situations, as generally agreed to by research organizations and the Congressional Bud...', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama and Mitt Romney have very different approaches to deficit reduction. Figures below are drawn from similar base lines reflecting realistic fiscal situations, as generally agreed to by research organizations and the Congressional Budget Office.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Comparing the Deficit Proposals', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T01:11:34+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/01eacd0e-6129-5644-994f-ee722a0a219a', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/01eacd0e-6129-5644-994f-ee722a0a219a'}, {'abstract': 'The Bronx district attorney’s office has refused to prosecute some people who were arrested for trespassing at public housing projects after discovering that many were innocent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/26/nyregion/in-the-bronx-resistance-to-prosecuting-stop-and-frisk-arrests.html', 'snippet': 'The Bronx district attorney’s office has refused to prosecute some people who were arrested for trespassing at public housing projects after discovering that many were innocent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a significant blow to New York City’s use of stop-and-frisk tactics, the Bronx district attorney’s office is no longer prosecuting people who were stopped at public housing projects and arrested for trespassing, unless the arresting officer is interviewed to ensure that the arrest was warranted.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/26/nyregion/sub-jp-frisk/sub-jp-frisk-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/26/nyregion/sub-jp-frisk/sub-jp-frisk-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/26/nyregion/sub-jp-frisk/sub-jp-frisk-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 672, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_n