 a win Tuesday. That left St. Louis fighting off Milwaukee and the Dodgers for the second wild-card slot.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/26/sports/YBASE/YBASE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 715, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/26/sports/YBASE/YBASE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1429, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fight for Second Wild Card in the National League', 'kicker': 'Roundup', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Braves Clinch Wild-Card Berth One Year After Letting It Slip Away', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Atlanta Braves', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Marlins', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T02:37:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2930a7a-0fb7-57ea-b3aa-697def539347', 'word_count': 709, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2930a7a-0fb7-57ea-b3aa-697def539347'}, {'abstract': 'In what could be the ultimate in personalized medicine, animal models, referred to by researchers as avatars, are being used to help determine the best treatment for a patient.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/26/business/mice-as-stand-ins-in-the-fight-against-disease.html', 'snippet': 'In what could be the ultimate in personalized medicine, animal models, referred to by researchers as avatars, are being used to help determine the best treatment for a patient.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BALTIMORE — Megan Sykes, a medical researcher, has a mouse with a human immune system — her own. She calls it “Mini-Me.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/22/business/avatar-ss-slide-1A7T/avatar-ss-slide-1A7T-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/22/business/avatar-ss-slide-1A7T/avatar-ss-slide-1A7T-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/22/business/avatar-ss-slide-1A7T/avatar-ss-slide-1A7T-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 649, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/22/business/avatar-ss-slide-1A7T/avatar-ss-slide-1A7T-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1297, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/22/business/avatar-ss-slide-1A7T/avatar-ss-slide-1A7T-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/22/business/avatar-ss-slide-1A7T/avatar-ss-slide-1A7T-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/22/business/avatar-ss-slide-1A7T/avatar-ss-slide-1A7T-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbL