 of Prime Minister Mariano Rajoy mounted on several fronts on Tuesday as thousands of demonstrators besieged Parliament. Raphael Minder reports from Madrid. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'IHT Quick Read: Wednesday, Sept. 26', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T07:34:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By The International Herald Tribune', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The International Herald Tribune'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/76464408-3e88-5dba-87f3-4ca1b18d9e91', 'word_count': 241, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76464408-3e88-5dba-87f3-4ca1b18d9e91'}, {'abstract': 'Demonstrators took to the streets Wednesday in Greece to protest new cuts being discussed, and protesters in Spain surrounded Parliament for a second day over the prime minister’s austerity program.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/world/europe/greece-faces-national-strike-to-protest-austerity.html', 'snippet': 'Demonstrators took to the streets Wednesday in Greece to protest new cuts being discussed, and protesters in Spain surrounded Parliament for a second day over the prime minister’s austerity program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATHENS — After a period of relative calm, European markets shuddered once again on Wednesday as protests erupted across Greece and demonstrators surrounded the Spanish Parliament for a second day to protest the austerity program of Prime Minister Mariano Rajoy. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/world/europe/GREECE-REFER/GREECE-REFER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'image