a coveted guano, the reporter Simon Romero couldn’t stomach more than an afternoon. The Chilean photographer Tomás Munita, undaunted, stayed weeks.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/26/losing-fear-learning-to-see/', 'snippet': 'On a demanding assignment off Peru’s coast, in search of a coveted guano, the reporter Simon Romero couldn’t stomach more than an afternoon. The Chilean photographer Tomás Munita, undaunted, stayed weeks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SANTIAGO, Chile — The motor boat cut through choppy waters before reaching Isla de Asia, off Peru’s coast. We arrived half-drenched and shivering to a stunning scene: Quechua-speaking laborers with pickaxes trying to collect hardened guano, the bird dung so coveted in the 19th century as a fertilizer that nations waged wars over the islands where it is found.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Losing Fear and Learning to See', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Munita, Tomas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romero, Simon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chile', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Santiago (Chile)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T09:00:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simon Romero', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Romero', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab497f7a-d79b-5573-aaf9-dd4900b7d5c7', 'word_count': 1134, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab497f7a-d79b-5573-aaf9-dd4900b7d5c7'}, {'abstract': 'Tell us how well you sleep, when you sleep, how your waking life affects your sleeping life, and your reaction to the ideas in this article.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/26/what-are-your-sleep-habits/', 'snippet': 'Tell us how well you sleep, when you sleep, how your waking life affects your sleeping life, and your reaction to the ideas in this article.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A piece from the Sunday Review about “rethinking sleep” has been on the most e-mailed list all week. It states that getting eight consecutive hours of sleep every night may not be as essential as we think. Instead, the author proposes, taking short naps throughout the day may actually be more beneficial and improve cognitive function.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Are Your Sleep Habits?', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T09:01:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ariha Setalvad', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ariha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Setalvad', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef7d2594-8d9f-585a-b6ce-7ed810e34721', 'word_count': 479, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef7d2594-8d9f-585a-b6ce-7ed810e34721'}, {'abstract': 'More Ryan awesomeness.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/26/death-by-powerpoint-continued/', 'snippet': 'More Ryan awesomeness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Update: OK, the word is that this was really clumsy satire.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Death By PowerPoint, Continued', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, '