est long-range problem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Is football the next boxing? Michael Silver of Yahoo Sports makes that connection in recommended reading today:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'N.F.L. Has Bigger Problems Than Officials', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T11:23:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/265e0f6a-f990-5fd1-97f5-4fb293d793da', 'word_count': 633, 'uri': 'nyt://article/265e0f6a-f990-5fd1-97f5-4fb293d793da'}, {'abstract': 'In this week’s links: The Dutch passion for philosophy; the difference between good and bad novels of ideas; and Bourdieu’s map of “food-space,” updated.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/26/stone-links-thinking-dutch/', 'snippet': 'In this week’s links: The Dutch passion for philosophy; the difference between good and bad novels of ideas; and Bourdieu’s map of “food-space,” updated.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The Dutch, it seems, like their philosophy. In an essay for Filosofie Magazine, Frank Mulder discusses the public role of philosophy in the Netherlands. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stone Links: Thinking Dutch', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bourdieu, Pierre', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Lapham's Quarterly", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Netherlands', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T11:30:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark de Silva', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'de Silva', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df7c17e0-8c69-55ce-b44b-d2dc49d2696b', 'word_count': 420, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df7c17e0-8c69-55ce-b44b-d2dc49d2696b'}, {'abstract': 'On a large scale, the biggest impact of the shift may be the changes in the Arctic’s ability to function as a cooling system for the globe’s oceans.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/26/imagining-a-warmer-arctic/', 'snippet': 'On a large scale, the biggest impact of the shift may be the changes in the Arctic’s ability to function as a cooling system for the globe’s oceans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From more snowfall (which can act as an insulating blanket, keeping ice warm) to more storms and stronger winds and waves, a look at the implications of a potentially ice-free Arctic. [Scientific American]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Imagining a Warmer Arctic', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T11:32:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00854bef-15fe-5210-8131-ee9ddbec207f', 'word_count': 109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00854bef-15fe-5210-8131-ee9ddbec207f'}, {'abstract': 'Julius Malema, the former leader of the African National Congress youth wing, is charged in connection with state contracts with an engineering company linked to him.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/world/africa/julius-malema-charged-with-money-laundering.html', 'snippet': 'Julius Malema, the former leader of the African National Congress youth wing, is charged in connection with state contracts with an engineering company linked to him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JOHANNESBURG — Julius Malema, the firebrand former leader of the African National Congress youth wing, appeared in a court in his home province of Limpopo on Wednesday to face a charge of money laundering in connection with state contracts with an engineering company linked to him. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fallen South African Politician Charged With Laundering', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fallen South African Politician Charged With Laundering', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Malema, Julius S', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Africa', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T11:33:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lydia Polgreen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lydia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Polgreen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/75574e34-c12d-58f8-a41c-21700b3dbd39', 'word_count': 523, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75574e34-c12d-58f8-a41c-21700b3dbd39'}, {'abstract': 'Iran’s announcement, coming after it won an Oscar for best foreign-language film earlier this year, left some in Hollywood scratching their heads.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/26/iran-will-boycott-oscars-to-protest-anti-muslim-video/', 'snippet': 'Iran’s announcement, coming after it won an Oscar for best foreign-language film earlier this year, left some in Hollywood scratching their heads.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The boycott appears straightforward: Mohammad Hosseini, Iran’s culture minister, on Tuesday confirmed that his country would not submit a film for consideration at next year’s Oscars in protest of “Innocence of Muslims,” the anti-Islam YouTube video that has sparked deadly riots. He specifically cited the “failure” of Oscar organizers to take an official position on the incendiary “film.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iran Will Boycott Oscars to Protest Anti-Muslim Video', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boycotts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Farhadi, Asghar', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T11:36:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/77726e1a-65e9-544f-afd8-c50e22f331c3', 'word_count': 287, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77726e1a-65e9-544f-afd8-c50e22f331c3'}, {'abstract': 'A closer look at a play that might have saved the game against Miami, and that might have saved the Jets’ season.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/26/breaking-down-laron-landrys-pick-six-for-jets/', 'snippet': 'A closer look at a play that might have saved the game against Miami, and that might have saved the Jets’ season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jonathan Bales will pick a big play from each week and break it down. In Week 2, he analyzed Victor Cruz’s 80-yard catch-and-run for a score against Tampa Bay:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Breaking Down LaRon Landry’s Pick-Six for Jets', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Landry, LaRon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tannehill, Ryan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Dolphins', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T12:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Bales', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bales', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/681b5fc3-7a07-52ff-bb4e-4e8cb683e2b4', 'word_count': 666, 'uri': 'nyt://article/681b5fc3-7a07-52ff-bb4e-4e8cb683e2b4'}, {'abstract': 'For modernists and classicists alike, a guide to new cultural happenings, restaurants and watering holes in the city of lights.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/26/off-the-runway-more-on-where-to-go-between-the-shows-in-paris/', 'snippet': 'For modernists and classicists alike, a guide to new cultural happenings, restaurants and watering holes in the city of lights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fashion folk who simply never O.D. on their métier will want to high-heel it to the Cité de la Mode et du Design (34 Quai d’Austerlitz, 75013) to catch the last days of “Cristobal Balenciaga, Fashion Collector,” which features looks by the master alongside historical garments he collected. Next door, Rei Kawakubo designed the unusual scenography for “Comme des Garçons, White Drama,” which showcases her all-white S/S ’12 collection ensconced in large-scale bubble formations. Through Oct. 7.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Off the Runway | More on Where to Go Between the Shows in Paris', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T12:02:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Moroz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moroz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9701a20-af0f-5ef1-9176-26d7c3ed7076', 'word_count': 660, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9701a20-af0f-5ef1-9176-26d7c3ed7076'}, {'abstract': 'Shinzo Abe, a nationalist former prime minister, won the race to lead Japan’s Liberal Democractic Party, giving him a chance of regaining the nation’s top job.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/world/asia/japans-opposition-picks-shinzo-abe-as-leader.html', 'snippet': 'Shinzo Abe, a nationalist former prime minister, won the race to lead Japan’s Liberal Democractic Party, giving him a chance of regaining the nation’s top job.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — Shinzo Abe, a nationalist former prime minister, was elected to lead Japan’s main opposition party on Wednesday, giving him a chance of regaining the nation’s top job — a prospect that could worsen the country’s tense relations with China and its other Asian neighbors.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/world/japan/japan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 927, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/world/japan/japan-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1854, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/world/japan/japan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/27/world/japan/japan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/world/japan/japan-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Former Prime Minister in Japan Elected to Lead Opposition Party', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Former Prime Minister in Japan Elected to Lead Opposition Party', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABE, SHINZO', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}