ed food and a family home for all.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHNOM PENH — In a union office\xa0for garment workers on the outskirts of the capital on a recent afternoon, Tith Srey Mom and her sister Mach were pondering what to do next. After losing a 10-year legal battle to keep their 200-square-meter plot of land, they were being evicted. All legal avenues had been exhausted. All they could do was wait for the police to come and forcibly remove them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cambodia’s Landless Class', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Land Use Policies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cambodia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T12:18:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Luke Hunt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Luke', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hunt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0cfd193-161b-54f5-a3fe-64ce828a24f2', 'word_count': 683, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0cfd193-161b-54f5-a3fe-64ce828a24f2'}, {'abstract': 'As people are evaluated more by their social media ratings, companies have a responsibility to use the information to help customers, not simply judge them.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/26/using-a-social-media-rating-to-help-people-not-judge-them/', 'snippet': 'As people are evaluated more by their social media ratings, companies have a responsibility to use the information to help customers, not simply judge them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Today, we are expected to maintain a good credit rating. A few years from now, we might be judged by how much we post on Twitter or update Facebook.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia':