ally easier wins for Democrats.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/26/sept-25-romneys-narrow-path-without-ohio/', 'snippet': 'With President Obama leading in polls of Ohio, Mitt Romney would need to make gains in other Midwestern states, like Iowa and Wisconsin, that are traditionally easier wins for Democrats.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With President Obama consistently holding a lead in polls of Ohio, Mitt Romney may need to devise a strategy to win the Electoral College without it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sept. 25: Romney’s Narrow Path Without Ohio', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electoral College', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T12:35:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/349fb992-3ed9-5de1-b88b-a14b882b877b', 'word_count': 1148, 'uri': 'nyt://article/349fb992-3ed9-5de1-b88b-a14b882b877b'}, {'abstract': 'Also, a trial date is set for Rebekah Brooks and Andy Coulson and a royal slip-up by the BBC.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/26/the-breakfast-meeting-the-nook-as-ipad-lite-and-lessons-from-the-olympics/', 'snippet': 'Also, a trial date is set for Rebekah Brooks and Andy Coulson and a royal slip-up by the BBC.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Roughly 217 million people watched Olympic coverage on NBC networks during the London games and eight million people downloaded NBC’s mobile apps for the Olympics, according to new figures released by the network, part of a vast trove of consumer research based on viewing during the games. Watching video on tablet computers – no surprise – also surged and the most popular events on any device were women’s gymnastics and the women’s soccer final. The good news for the network: the popularity of the live feed during the day didn’t seem to cannibalize viewers from NBC’s primetime package. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: The Nook as ‘iPad Lite,’ and Lessons From the Olympics', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tablet Computers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bell, Kristen', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brooks, Rebekah', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coulson, Andy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lehrer, Jonah', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Barnes & Noble Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'British Broadcasting Corp', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Target Corporation', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Warner Brothers', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T12:35:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editors', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editors'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ec616d9-d18f-508c-9358-56afe7a954db', 'word_count': 439, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ec616d9-d18f-508c-9358-56afe7a954db'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney talks directly to the camera for nearly a minute to say that while both sides care about working families, only his plan will help. It directly contradicts an earlier Obama spot.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/26/romney-makes-direct-claim-of-compassion-as-47-percent-drives-ads/', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney talks directly to the camera for nearly a minute to say that while both sides care about working families, only his plan will help. It directly contradicts an earlier Obama spot.', 'lead_paragraph': '11:10 a.m. | Updated Mitt Romney’s “47 percent” remarks are continuing to drive ad messages on both sides in the presidential race.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney Makes Direct Claim of Compassion as ‘47 Percent’ Drives Ads', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T12:37:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Wheaton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wheaton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8d49c33-74c8-5d3f-beb1-8af2cebf99ee', 'word_count': 402, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8d49c33-74c8-5d3f-beb1-8af2cebf99ee'}, {'abstract': 'The British banking group that controls Libor is said to be preparing to give up that responsibility, Tesla Motors conceded it would be turning to investors and taxpayers for help, and the Mexican arm of Banco Santander staged one of the year’s biggest I.P.O.’s.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/09/26/libors-new-masters/', 'snippet': 'The British banking group that controls Libor is said to be preparing to give up that responsibility, Tesla Motors conceded it would be turning to investors and taxpayers for help, and the Mexican arm of Banco Santander staged one of the year’s bi...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Libor’s New Masters \xa0|\xa0 The British banking group that controls a crucial lending rate is preparing to give up that responsibility, a person with direct knowledge of the matter tells DealBook’s Mark Scott.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Libor’s New Masters', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T12:51:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/59347c3f-c21b-59d2-8ae2-e7b8affb4d43', 'word_count': 1942, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59347c3f-c21b-59d2-8ae2-e7b8affb4d43'}, {'abstract': 'The European Commission tried to calm some governments — notably Germany, Finland and the Netherlands — over recapitalizing ailing euro zone banks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/business/global/27iht-eubanks27.html', 'snippet': 'The European Commission tried to calm some governments — notably Germany, Finland and the Netherlands — over recapitalizing ailing euro zone banks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRUSSELS — The European Commission sought on Wednesday to ease concerns that some governments have about using the euro z