in an effort to match the expansive infrastructure of the Obama campaign.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every night, state-based field operatives hired by the Republican National Committee are collecting daily absentee ballot reports from elections officials in Colorado, Florida and North Carolina.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Republican Committee Seeks to Match Obama Ground Game', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Priebus, Reince R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican National Committee', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T13:31:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/10595621-6c3d-587f-8751-a7f1e1bad3a7', 'word_count': 1162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10595621-6c3d-587f-8751-a7f1e1bad3a7'}, {'abstract': 'A summary of what’s on today’s editorial page.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/26/opinion-report-homeless-children/', 'snippet': 'A summary of what’s on today’s editorial page.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From the editorial page', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Opinion Report: Homeless Children', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T13:45:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fac59603-2e2b-592d-831d-fdc479f72b5b', 'word_count': 106, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fac59603-2e2b-592d-831d-fdc479f72b5b'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/26/what-were-reading-530/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Vulture: Can you actually make moonshine from torpedo fuel, paint thinner or darkroom chemicals, as Joaquin Phoenix does in “The Master”? — Emily Weinstein', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T13:50:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/15910535-2a19-545b-be32-4306215652c1', 'word_count': 425, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15910535-2a19-545b-be32-4306215652c1'}, {'abstract': 'A new male-centric housewares collection offers limited-edition pieces within a reasonable price range.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/26/a-guy-thing/', 'snippet': 'A new male-centric housewares collection offers limited-edition pieces within a reasonable price range.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jonah Takagi’s mixed-media coffee tables and pendant lights can be found at edgy design stores like Matter and the Future Perfect. But the 33-year-old designer’s house is full of Ikea basics and estate-sale finds, not unlike most of his fashionable 30-something guy friends. So it’s with them — and himself — in mind that he started Field (field-online.com), a new male-centric housewares collection designed by, well, himself and his friends, which include Hallgeir Homstvedt, Jonathan Nesci and Oscar Diaz. “I saw an opportunity to make new vintage pieces, ones that will age well and hold their own alongside a cast-iron desk or shop lights,” says Takagi.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Guy Thing', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Guy Thing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T14:00:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Monica Khemsurov', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Monica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Khemsurov', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/143acdb2-f9e7-5aa6-9e1a-e79f6ec58e83', 'word_count': 200, 'uri': 'nyt://article/143acdb2-f9e7-5aa6-9e1a-e79f6ec58e83'}, {'abstract': 'After years of consistent decline, traffic fatalities from July 2011 through June 2012 increased to a total of 291, a rise of 23 percent from the previous year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/nyregion/in-reversal-new-york-city-traffic-fatalities-rise.html', 'snippet': 'After years of consistent decline, traffic fatalities from July 2011 through June 2012 increased to a total of 291, a rise of 23 percent from the previous year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For years, the New York City Transportation Department has held a trump card in the roiling debate over its many roadway interventions: When officials said the measures, like pedestrian plazas and bike lanes, had made streets safer, the numbers appeared to back them up.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/nyregion/27traffic/27traffic-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/27/nyregion/27traffic/27traffic-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/nyregion/27traffic/27traffic-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/nyregion/27traffic/27traffic-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/nyregion/27traffic/27traffic-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/27/nyregion/27traffic/27traffic-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/nyregion/27traffic/27traffic-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Deaths Rise for Drivers, Bikers and Walkers on City Streets', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Deaths Rise for Drivers, Bikers and Walkers on City Streets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transportation Department (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sadik-Khan, Janette', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bicycles and Bicycling', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T14:08:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Flegenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flegenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/48c1d04b-e0f8-5f94-b8f9-89d88b3bedeb', 'word_count': 838, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48c1d04b-e0f8-5f94-b8f9-89d88b3bedeb'}, {'abstract': 'In the battle for control of the United States Senate, the Democratic Party has little room for error and is particularly intent on protecting senators who are standing for re-election in presidential battleground states.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/26/new-polls-show-ohio-and-florida-senators-maintaining-lead-over-challengers/', 'snippet': 'In the battle for control of the United States Senate, the Democratic Party has little room for error and is particularly intent on protecting senators who are standing for re-election in presidential battleground states.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAMPA, Fla. — In the battle for control of the United States Senate, the Democratic Party has little room for error and is particularly intent on protecting senators who are standing for re-election in presidential battleground states.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Polls Show Ohio and Florida Senators Maintaining Lead Over Challengers', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Battle For the Senate: Holding On to Strong Leads', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Sherrod', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Casey, Robert P Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nelson, Bill', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T14:12:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Zeleny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zeleny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c990eda-2b0f-5ceb-a86e-8113b5d541c5', 'word_count': 250, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c990eda-2b0f-5ceb-a86e-8113b5d541c5'}, {'abstract': 'The Braves recovered from their epic collapse in 2011, and the lockout of N.F.L. referees has Commissioner Roger Goodell in everyone’s cross hairs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/sports/a-year-later-the-braves-celebrate-leading-off.html', 'snippet': 'The Braves recovered from their epic collapse in 2011, and the lockout of N.F.L. referees has Commissioner Roger Goodell in everyone’s cross hairs.', 'lead_paragraph': "Every once in a while the sports calendar reminds us that so much can change as we make only one trip around the sun. On Tuesday night it was the Atlanta Braves marking time and metaphorical distance, putting a mere 12 months between their mesmerizing twin swan dive (with the Red Sox) out of last year’s baseball playoffs and clinching a spot in this year’s. It is instructive to think back over that 12-month stretch, remembering when baseball had a wild-card format that allowed for such thrilling finishes. (Sigh.) And in the N.F.L., remember when fans were giddy to have their favorite game saved from the teeth of a greedy league lockout? The N.B.A.'s was just getting rolling back then and N.H.L. owners were still dreamily planning for their chance to mess up their sport.", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/sports/27leading1/27leading1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/27/sports/27leading1/27leading1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/sports/27leading1/27leading1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 647, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/sports/27leading1/27leading1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1294, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/sports/27leading1/27leading1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/27/sports/27leading1/27leading1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/sports/27leading1/27leading1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Year Later, the Braves Celebrate', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Atlanta Braves', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goodell, Roger', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Guillen, Ozzie', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Freeman, Freddie (1989- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T14:38:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/318e2d24-51e9-57b2-9e19-51780d315f62', 'word_count': 628, 'uri': 'nyt://article/318e2d24-51e9-57b2-9e19-51780d315f62'}, {'abstract': 'EvePearl, owned by an Emmy-winning makeup artist, considers pitching its skin-care and makeup products on ShopNBC.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/business/smallbusiness/evepearl-a-cosmetics-company-weighs-risks-of-appearing-on-shopnbc-case-study.html', 'snippet': 'EvePearl, owned by an Emmy-winning makeup artist, considers pitching its skin-care and makeup products on ShopNBC.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EvePearl is a Manhattan makeup studio, boutique and e-commerce business with 10 employees that sells cosmetics containing skin-care nutrients. The products are developed by the company’s namesake and founder, a 46-year-old Emmy-winning TV makeup artist. She created her first foundation and concealer products seven years ago while working for Barbara Walters, Meredith Vieira, and the rest of the hosts on “The View.” ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_