ation.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/26/n-ways-to-apply-algebra-with-the-new-york-times/', 'snippet': 'Is algebra necessary? An Op-Ed essay argues it isn’t. We list algebraic opportunities you can find in the pages of The Times, and invite you to join the conversation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This summer, the political scientist Andrew Hacker’s New York Times Op-Ed essay “Is Algebra Necessary?” set off a national debate on mathematics education. Here is how the essay begins:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'N Ways to Apply Algebra With The New York Times', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T15:02:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Honner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Honner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d5deba1-0477-5d43-8bcc-c9879bf2a845', 'word_count': 1923, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d5deba1-0477-5d43-8bcc-c9879bf2a845'}, {'abstract': 'Although still a darling of India’s liberal elite and those who read literary fiction, something of a chasm has opened between Salman Rushdie and contemporary India.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/26/beneath-rushdies-feet-the-shifting-ground-of-india/', 'snippet': 'Although still a darling of India’s liberal elite and those who read literary fiction, something of a chasm has opened between Salman Rushdie and contemporary India.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — Against the backdrop of the highly newsworthy publication of Salman Rushdie’s memoir, “Joseph Anton,” which was released this month, my latest column attempts to describe the complex relationship between Mr. Rus