ooper’', 'kicker': 'MOVIES', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Rian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Looper (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T16:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/3d5cd20a-f419-5ba0-ba5f-85ddf5e3a5d7', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/3d5cd20a-f419-5ba0-ba5f-85ddf5e3a5d7'}, {'abstract': 'The 25-year-old Israeli drew on her years of military service for her first novel.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/26/shani-boianjiu-on-her-new-novel-and-women-soldiers-in-israel/', 'snippet': 'The 25-year-old Israeli drew on her years of military service for her first novel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Shani Boianjiu’s first novel, “The People of Forever Are Not Afraid,” follows three young female friends before, during and after their mandatory service in the Israeli Defense Forces. Ms. Boianjiu, 25, spent two years in the military and later studied at Harvard. In a recent e-mail interview, she discussed the ways she’s reflected in her characters, her sense of humor, whether she feels obligated to speak out about politics and more. Below are edited excerpts from the conversation:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/26/arts/26artsbeat-book1/26artsbeat-book1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 782, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype