e energy to the grid.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/26/adapting-gas-fired-power-to-a-greener-grid/', 'snippet': 'General Electric introduces a new natural gas plant that can quickly adjust its output to compensate for the uneven flow of renewable energy to the grid.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Making electricity from natural gas is cleaner than making it from coal or oil, but as gas gains a bigger market share in the business in the United States and elsewhere, the idea of what constitutes a good generator is shifting. General Electric announced a line of new models on Wednesday, with two interesting environmental twists.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Adapting Gas-Fired Power to a Greener Grid', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Light and Power', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Natural Gas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Solar Energy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wind Power', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Energy Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Electric Company', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Xcel Energy Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T16:00:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c254e62-0282-508e-ad1b-dd31d815191b', 'word_count': 686, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c254e62-0282-508e-ad1b-dd31d815191b'}, {'abstract': 'The coming Broadway revival of “Annie” has found its leading orphan: the 11-year-old veteran actress Lilla Crawford.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/30/theater/lilla-crawford-the-star-of-the-annie-revival.html', 'snippet': 'The coming Broadway revival of “Annie” has found its leading orphan: the 11-year-old veteran actress Lilla Crawford.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The theater director James Lapine personally auditioned 150 little girls to be the star of the new Broadway revival of “Annie,” and finally chose his orphan after a half-dozen callbacks with the young actress Lilla Crawford.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/arts/30SNAPSHOT/30SILOSNAPSHOT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 562, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/arts/30SNAPSHOT/30SILOSNAPSHOT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1888, 'width': 1037, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/arts/30SNAPSHOT/30SILOSNAPSHOT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/30/arts/30SNAPSHOT/30SILOSNAPSHOT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/arts/30SNAPSHOT/30SILOSNAPSHOT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Broadway Baby? No Way! She’s 11 Already!', 'kicker': 'Snapshot | Lilla Crawford', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Broadway Baby? No Way! She’s 11 Already!', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crawford, Lilla', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'ANNIE (PLAY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lapine, James', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T16:07:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d3ab412-1756-57d6-b2da-2e91cdc2ce9f', 'word_count': 843, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d3ab412-1756-57d6-b2da-2e91cdc2ce9f'}, {'abstract': 'Military trainers in Afghanistan are still doing the work of transferring control to the Afghan forces, but they are now doing it with increasing distance and ever-present body armor.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/26/trainers-in-afghanistan-arm-themselves-against-both-sides/', 'snippet': 'Military trainers in Afghanistan are still doing the work of transferring control to the Afghan forces, but they are now doing it with increasing distance and ever-present body armor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In The Times today, Matthew Rosenberg (@mrosenbergNYT) reports from Bad Pakh, Afghanistan, on the new protective strategy used by military advisers to the Afghan Army: keep body armor on and weapons loaded, all the time. He writes of the advisers in a base in Bad Pakh: “Their guard was up even though they were there for a day of training Afghan soldiers without once leaving the confines of a fortified base — even when chatting with the Afghan officers over a lunch of goat meat and yogurt.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trainers in Afghanistan Arm Themselves Against Both Sides', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosenberg, Matthew', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T16:09:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/14b6ca8c-79fe-5b5d-b0ad-5a588f3f162e', 'word_count': 209, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14b6ca8c-79fe-5b5d-b0ad-5a588f3f162e'}, {'abstract': 'Senator Claire McCaskill of Missouri criticizes her opponent, Representative Todd Akin over comments he made in August, and Mr. Akin gets some support from Republicans for his candidacy.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/26/mccaskill-hits-akin-for-legitimate-rape-comments-in-new-ad/', 'snippet': 'Senator Claire McCaskill of Missouri criticizes her opponent, Representative Todd Akin over comments he made in August, and Mr. Akin gets some support from Republicans for his candidacy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Republicans started calling for Todd Akin to bow out of the United States Senate race in Missouri last month, Senator Claire McCaskill, his Democratic opponent, tried to avoid talking about his “legitimate rape” controversy on the campaign trail. But now that the final deadline for Mr. Akin to withdraw has passed, with Mr. Akin locked in as the Republican nominee, she is swinging as expected.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'McCaskill Hits Akin for ‘Legitimate Rape’ Comments in New Ad', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Incumbent Pounces In Missouri Senate Race', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Senate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Akin, Todd', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCaskill, Claire', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Missouri', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T16:13:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Yaccino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yaccino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/83e58fa5-7d32-57d4-aeb8-d758e4bf4a5e', 'word_count': 376, 'uri': 'nyt://article/83e58fa5-7d32-57d4-aeb8-d758e4bf4a5e'}, {'abstract': 'The investigation was prompted by an article in National Geographic that quotes Msgr. Cristóbal Garcia as telling an American reporter how to smuggle illegal figurines into the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/world/asia/priest-investigated-in-ivory-smuggling-inquiry-in-philippines.html', 'snippet': 'The investigation was prompted by an article in National Geographic that quotes Msgr. Cristóbal Garcia as telling an American reporter how to smuggle illegal figurines into the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MANILA — Philippine law enforcement officials said on Wednesday that they were investigating whether a senior priest in the Roman Catholic Church was involved in the smuggling of elephant ivory to feed the country’s passion for religious icons. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Priest Investigated in Ivory-Smuggling Inquiry in Philippines', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_hea