keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Modell, Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baltimore Ravens', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cleveland Browns', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T16:26:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Hoffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68a72ce0-4709-5d78-9b66-5aa39da13aa0', 'word_count': 215, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68a72ce0-4709-5d78-9b66-5aa39da13aa0'}, {'abstract': 'With a new eight-year deal in place, regular officials will work Thursday’s Ravens-Browns game, and the officials’ union will vote Friday to ratify the contract and work Sunday’s games.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/sports/football/nfl-and-referees-reach-labor-deal.html', 'snippet': 'With a new eight-year deal in place, regular officials will work Thursday’s Ravens-Browns game, and the officials’ union will vote Friday to ratify the contract and work Sunday’s games.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The National Football League reached agreement on an eight-year labor deal with its game officials late Wednesday night, effectively ending a lockout that forced unprepared replacement officials onto the field, creating three weeks of botched calls, acute criticism, furious coaches and players, and a blemish — however temporary — on the integrity of the country’s most popular sport. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/sports/Y-JP-REFS/Y-JP-REF