, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/26/arts/20120926WILLIAMS-slide-XR9D/20120926WILLIAMS-slide-XR9D-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Andy Williams Through the Years', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Andy (1927-2012)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T17:04:36+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Arts', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/010f2366-6136-5155-ade7-019c668ca175', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/010f2366-6136-5155-ade7-019c668ca175'}, {'abstract': 'Preparing for retirement has become considerably more complicated since the Great Recession.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/26/booming/26expert-booming.html', 'snippet': 'Preparing for retirement has become considerably more complicated since the Great Recession.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As boomers move toward retirement — the oldest of our generation are now 66 — the complexities of preparing multiply. Unfortunately, matters have become considerably more complicated since the Great Recession. Of all demographic groups, people ages 55 to 64 have suffered the most financially, losing 10 percent of household income. I’ve had several friends say that they’re never going to be able to retire, that they’ll have to work until they drop. Hopefully not. Today’s expert is Doug Wheat, a certified financial planner with Family Wealth Management, based in western Massachusetts. One of the things that drew him to this work was having to manage his mother’s finances after his father died. Among the questions he is prepared to discuss are:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/26/booming/26expert-booming/26expert-booming-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/26/booming/26expert-booming/26expert-booming-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1365, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/26/booming/26expert-booming/26expert-booming-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/26/booming/26expert-booming/26expert-booming-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/26/booming/26expert-booming/26expert-booming-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Prepare for Retirement', 'kicker': 'Ask an Expert', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Boomers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Retirement', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T17:05:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Booming', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Winerip', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Winerip', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fbbbad63-49b6-5324-8f41-67540e371357', 'word_count': 196, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fbbbad63-49b6-5324-8f41-67540e371357'}, {'abstract': 'Two new Middle Eastern leaders, despite being swept to power by popular uprisings, issued rebuttals to President Obama’s defense of Western values at the United Nations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/world/united-nations-general-assembly.html', 'snippet': 'Two new Middle Eastern leaders, despite being swept to power by popular uprisings, issued rebuttals to President Obama’s defense of Western values at the United Nations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'UNITED NATIONS — The new presidents of Egypt and Yemen — both of whom were swept to power by uprisings demanding democratic rights — issued clear rebuttals on Wednesday to President Obama’s ardent defense of Western values at the United Nations, arguing that cultural limits on rights like freedom of speech had to be respected. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/world/27nations_395-span/27nations_395-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/27/world/27nations_395-span/27nations_395-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/world/27nations_395-span/27nations_395-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image',