on Wednesday defended that decision and sought to define the cause of its recent ratings setbacks, including the end of its 16-year weekly winning streak.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Today’ Producer Says Ouster of Ann Curry Was His Choice', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Today’ Executive Defends A Shift in the Show’s Hosts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bell, Jim', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Curry, Ann', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lauer, Matt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC INC', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T17:30:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/79d45565-7bb9-51f0-be92-e74387b93e2f', 'word_count': 631, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79d45565-7bb9-51f0-be92-e74387b93e2f'}, {'abstract': 'A Times reporter would like more flexibility but finds the term accurate and useful.', 'web_url': 'https://publiceditor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/26/immigration-reporter-julia-prestons-views-on-illegal-immigrant/', 'snippet': 'A Times reporter would like more flexibility but finds the term accurate and useful.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Earlier this week, I opened up the question of whether the term “illegal immigrant” is disparaging or simply accurate. The response has been robust, and I’m paying attention to all of it – in e-mails, on Twitter, in comments on my blog posts and in conversations.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Immigration Reporter Julia Preston’s Views on ‘Illegal Immigrant’', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigrants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Language and Languages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T17:33:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5233b9c-f57c-5599-a735-9e07be43d051', 'word_count': 647, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5233b9c-f57c-5599-a735-9e07be43d051'}, {'abstract': 'Secretary of State Hillary Rodham Clinton suggested an affiliate of Al Qaeda in North Africa was behind the attack on the United States mission in Benghazi.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/world/africa/clinton-cites-clear-link-between-al-qaeda-and-attack-in-libya.html', 'snippet': 'Secretary of State Hillary Rodham Clinton suggested an affiliate of Al Qaeda in North Africa was behind the attack on the United States mission in Benghazi.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Secretary of State Hillary Rodham Clinton on Wednesday suggested there was a link between the Qaeda franchise in North Africa and the attack at the American diplomatic mission in Benghazi, Libya, that killed the American ambassador and three others. She was the highest-ranking Obama administration official to publicly make the connection, and her comments intensified what is becoming a fiercely partisan fight over whether the attack could