ek.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A simple line of malicious code embedded in a Web page can cause some Samsung Galaxy smartphones to lose all their data, security researchers revealed this week. But Samsung says a fix has been out for months.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Malicious Code Can Wipe Out Some Samsung Phones', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Samsung Group', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T18:23:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian X. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/466f4256-0228-5a50-92de-a7d153fa64e3', 'word_count': 365, 'uri': 'nyt://article/466f4256-0228-5a50-92de-a7d153fa64e3'}, {'abstract': 'Seeking explanations for D.C.’s influence-peddling arms race.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/26/the-wealth-of-washington/', 'snippet': 'Seeking explanations for D.C.’s influence-peddling arms race.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a post pivoting off my weekend column on Washington’s extraordinary recent growth, Dylan Matthews of Wonkblog marshals data showing that the soaring wage premium for Washingtonians doesn’t correlate directly with increases in the federal government’s share of G.D.P. The two have spiked together in the last few years, but the D.C. economy achieved separation from national trends in the Reagan and Clinton years and lift-off under George W. Bush, a long three decade period when government’s share of the national income was relatively flat. What does correlate, though, is the growth in Washingtonian wealth and the steady expansion of lobbying: As Matthews notes, “the growth in inflation-adjusted lobbying spending, as measured by\xa0OpenSecrets, tracks the D.C. wage premium’s rise since the 1990s quite well.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Wealth of Washington', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T18:33:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d2919ab-7d47-5c18-9b16-a3929f953ceb', 'word_count': 749, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d2919ab-7d47-5c18-9b16-a3929f953ceb'}, {'abstract': 'The Ninja Turtles have been updated to appeal to today’s audiences, but the legend remains the same, and the toys are flying off the shelves.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/30/arts/television/teenage-mutant-ninja-turtles-retooled-for-nickelodeon.html', 'snippet': 'The Ninja Turtles have been updated to appeal to today’s audiences, but the legend remains the same, and the toys are flying off the shelves.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/arts/30TURTLES1_SPAN/30TURTLES1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 335, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/30/arts/30TURTLES1_SPAN/30TURTLES1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 335}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'c