he best shoes right off the runway. Today’s pick: a microcheckerboard lace-up mule.', 'lead_paragraph': 'T plucks the best shoes right off the runway.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Daily Shoe | Dries Van Noten', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T18:42:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/58d2c4a9-14a8-59f7-9530-b1695c48c2bf', 'word_count': 96, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58d2c4a9-14a8-59f7-9530-b1695c48c2bf'}, {'abstract': 'Alex Rodriguez said he should be able to play for the Yankees on Thursday against the Blue Jays in Toronto.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/26/yankees-rodriguez-rests-sore-left-foot/', 'snippet': 'Alex Rodriguez said he should be able to play for the Yankees on Thursday against the Blue Jays in Toronto.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MINNEAPOLIS — Alex Rodriguez was not in the starting lineup for the Yankees on Wednesday afternoon because of a sore left foot. Rodriguez fouled a ball off the top of his foot in his final at-bat in Tuesday’s 5-4 loss to the Minnesota Twins, and it swelled. X-rays were not deemed necessary by the Yankees, and Rodriguez said he should be able to play Thursday against the Blue Jays in Toronto.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yankees’ Rodriguez Rests Sore Left Foot', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodriguez, Alex', 'rank': 2