, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/ef92a850-d389-5ac4-8c96-61b19bef2765'}, {'abstract': 'Senator Scott P. Brown of Massachusetts issued a warning to his campaign staff members who participated in the tomahawk chops and Indian war whoops — and to all of his staff — that such conduct would not be tolerated.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/26/cherokee-chief-demands-scott-brown-apologize-for-supporters-actions/', 'snippet': 'Senator Scott P. Brown of Massachusetts issued a warning to his campaign staff members who participated in the tomahawk chops and Indian war whoops — and to all of his staff — that such conduct would not be tolerated.', 'lead_paragraph': '8:43 p.m. | Updated BOSTON — Senator Scott P. Brown’s campaign issued a statement Wednesday evening saying he “regrets” what he called “unacceptable” behavior by some staff members who participated in the tomahawk chops and Indian war whoops at a campaign rally.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Scott Brown Says He ‘Regrets’ His Staff’s ‘Unacceptable’ Behavior', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Senate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Scott P', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Warren, Elizabeth', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T20:11:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katharine Q. Seelye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katharine', 'middlename': 'Q.', 'lastname': 'Seelye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/efb6f759-9756-52cb-aeec-79782c94208d', 'word_count': 728, 'uri': 'nyt://article/efb6f759-9756-52cb-aeec-79782c94208d'}, {'abstract': 'Rising metal concentrations in the Upper Snake River watershed seem to dovetail with the effects of a warming climate.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/26/climate-change-metal-and-waterways/', 'snippet': 'Rising metal concentrations in the Upper Snake River watershed seem to dovetail with the effects of a warming climate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'High in the Rocky Mountains, just west of the Continental Divide, metal concentrations in the Upper Snake River have been climbing over the last 30 years, in some cases increasing as much as fourfold. Strong evidence links this trend to climate change, according to a recent study led by the United States Geological Survey and University of Colorado at Boulder.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Climate Change, Metal and Waterways', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T20:17:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dylan Walsh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dylan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Walsh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/143ada6b-6764-560d-a6a5-cae76f903660', 'word_count': 454, 'uri': 'nyt://article/143ada6b-6764-560d-a6a5-cae76f903660'}, {'abstract': '“Reykjavik” will have a staged reading, followed by a panel discussion, at the Baruch Performing Arts Center on Thursday evening.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/26/richard-rhodes-writes-a-play-about-reagan-gorbachev-and-nuclear-weapons/', 'snippet': '“Reykjavik” will have a staged reading, followed by a panel discussion, at the Baruch Performing Arts Center on Thursday evening.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Richard Rhodes, the Pulitzer Prize-winning author of 24 books, has written his first play, and it spins off of his research into the history of nuclear weapons. Mr. Rhodes’s “Reykjavik,” about the historic 1986 meeting between Ronald Reagan and Mikhail Gorbachev in that city, will have a free staged reading on Thursday at 6:30 pm at the Baruch Performing Arts Center. Mr. Rhodes and several other experts in nuclear disarmament will appear at a panel discussion following the reading. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Richard Rhodes Writes a Play About Reagan, Gorbachev and Nuclear Weapons', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Re-enacting History', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Easton, Richard', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gorbachev, Mikhail S', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reagan, Ronald Wilson', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rhodes, Richard', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanders, Jay O', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baruch Performing Arts Center', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T20:23:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicia R. Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicia', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ace8e131-8ba0-5878-b14a-991a0a15efff', 'word_count': 288, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ace8e131-8ba0-5878-b14a-991a0a15efff'}, {'abstract': 'The Phildelphia site is given the highest rating by the United States Green Building Council.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/26/new-home-for-barnes-foundation-a-bright-shade-of-green/', 'snippet': 'The Phildelphia site is given the highest rating by the United States Green Building Council.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Critics have differed on the merits of the new home for the Barnes Foundation, the world-class art collection that was relocated from a Philadelphia suburb to a downtown museum quarter this year after a long-running court battle. But at least one arbiter has now given the museum an unqualified stamp of approval.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Home for Barnes Foundation a Bright Shade of Green', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Barnes Home: A Bright Shade of Green', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Energy Efficiency', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tsien, Billie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Tod', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Barnes Foundation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Green Building Council', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philadelphia (Pa)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T20:25:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randy Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kennedy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c43d359b-6212-57ce-a006-08dd5c6bb62c', 'word_count': 181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c43d359b-6212-57ce-a006-08dd5c6bb62c'}, {'abstract': 'Told he could not ride his bicycle in a certain area, the politician Andrew Mitchell told two officers they were “plebs,” according to a police report.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/world/europe/plebs-insult-by-british-official-andrew-mitchell-stirs-controversy.html', 'snippet': 'Told he could not ride his bicycle in a certain area, the politician Andrew Mitchell told two officers they were “plebs,” according to a police report.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — For an ambitious politician, it is rarely a good idea to lose your cool — and never with the police. But Andrew Mitchell apparently compounded the error further by deriding police officers as his social inferiors, and that has turned a small incident into a big political headache for Prime Minister David Cameron and his ruling Conservative Party. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/world/britain/britain-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 813, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/world/britain/britain-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1626, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Tory, His Bike and an Ill-Chosen Insult', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Tory, His Bike and an Ill-Chosen Insult', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mitchell, Andrew', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cameron, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Conservative Party (Great Britain)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T20:25:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Castle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0023d23f-5b5c-5bfe-a668-9c09823d767c', 'word_count': 801, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0023d23f-5b5c-5bfe-a668-9c09823d767c'}, {'abstract': 'The competition has been fierce because the observatory will be one of the highest and presumably most lucrative in the nation.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/26/3-bidders-left-to-run-world-trade-center-observatory/', 'snippet': 'The competition has been fierce because the observatory will be one of the highest and presumably most lucrative in the nation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'And then there were three.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '3 Bidders Left to Run World Trade Center Observatory', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '3 Finalists To Compete To Operate Observatory', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': '1 World Trade Center (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Port Authority of New York and New Jersey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-26T20:29:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles V. Bagli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': 'V.', 'lastname': 'Bagli', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f42e645-0a8a-5df3-90bb-c4d7fabff506', 'word_count': 498, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f42e645-0a8a-5df3-90bb-c4d7fabff506'}, {'abstract': 'C. C. Sabathia (14-6) struck out 10 in eight solid innings as the Yankees moved closer to clinching the American League East.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/sports/baseball/sabathia-gives-yankees-bullpen-a-break.html', 'snippet': 'C. C. Sabathia (14-6) struck out 10 in eight solid innings as the Yankees moved closer to clinching the American League East.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MINNEAPOLIS — Joe Mauer, a former most valuable player, came into Wednesday’s game with a .326 batting average — second only to Miguel Cabrera in the American League — and was hitting a staggering .418 in September. But by the time his fourth at-bat came around against C. C. Sabathia, he had struck out three times and did not look so dangerous. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/sports/baseball/27yankees-pic/27yankees-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/27/sports/baseball/27yankees-pic/27yankees-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/sports/baseball/27yankees-pic/27yankees-pic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 700, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/sports/baseball/27yankees-pic/27yankees-pic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1401, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/sports/baseball/27yankees-pic/27yankees-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'wid