d_paragraph': 'To be honest, I wasn’t a fan of Andy Williams. But I wasn’t a critic, either. Coming of age in the 1960s, I was pretty much rock ‘n’ roll, 24/7. Andy Williams, Perry Como, Bing Crosby, Tony Bennett — they blurred together for me. It seemed like they all owned the same cashmere sweater. I had the same problem with Dinah Shore and Doris Day. While it’s true they sang music you could slow dance to — meaning you got to lean against a girl — for me, it was bar mitzvah music, the slow, grown-up stuff you were forced to listen to until the real music came on. Slow dancing for me was John Lennon’s “Julia.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/26/booming/26williams-booming/26williams-booming-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/26/booming/26williams-booming/26williams-booming-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/26/booming/26williams-booming/26williams-booming-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1021, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/26/booming/26williams-booming/26williams-booming-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2041, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/26/booming/26williams-booming/26williams-booming-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/26/booming/26williams-booming/26williams-booming-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailh