fba14cd5d'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama needs to apply his own doctrine on foreign conflict spots where it would benefit the United States most: Syria.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/opinion/5-reasons-to-intervene-in-syria-now.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama needs to apply his own doctrine on foreign conflict spots where it would benefit the United States most: Syria.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHETHER you agree or disagree with President Obama, there is no doubt that he has formulated a coherent approach to the use of American power. The Obama Doctrine involves getting into a conflict zone and getting out fast without ground wars or extended military occupations. This approach proved its effectiveness in Libya last year.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '5 Reasons to Intervene in Syria Now', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributors', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '5 Reasons to Intervene in Syria Now', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Free Syrian Army', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'No-Fly Zones', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-27T00:13:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Doran and Ma