3be58d', 'word_count': 877, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69b2558c-c19e-5f3c-a4c3-78a2f23be58d'}, {'abstract': 'Bavaria’s traditional culture may be falling victim to its economic success, as the governing party’s philosophy is tested by newcomers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/world/europe/bavaria-political-shifts-could-have-wide-effects.html', 'snippet': 'Bavaria’s traditional culture may be falling victim to its economic success, as the governing party’s philosophy is tested by newcomers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MUNICH — With two mighty blows from a large wooden mallet, Christian Ude, the popular mayor of Bavaria’s capital here, tapped the first keg of Oktoberfest and officially opened this year’s festival. As tradition dictates, the first beer went to the man he hopes to unseat in next year’s election, state premier Horst Seehofer. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/world/germany1/germany1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/27/world/germany1/germany1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/world/germany1/germany1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 739, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/world/germany1/germany1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1478, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/world/germany1/germany1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop