g and mathematics. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Visas for Scientists, With a Catch', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Visas for Scientists, With a Catch', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Visas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Lamar S', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-27T01:24:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0d73a5d-852a-5463-a991-10d72d9c25b1', 'word_count': 321, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0d73a5d-852a-5463-a991-10d72d9c25b1'}, {'abstract': 'The Gullah and Geechee people could be forced out of an island off Georgia because of exorbitant real estate taxes from local government.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/opinion/surviving-where-slaves-held-fast.html', 'snippet': 'The Gullah and Geechee people could be forced out of an island off Georgia because of exorbitant real estate taxes from local government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Six years ago, Congress took note of one of the nation’s great sagas of endurance — descendants of slavery who survived for generations on the barrier chain of Sea Islands along the southeast coast. The government created a cultural heritage corridor from North Carolina to Florida to celebrate the Gullah and Geechee peoples, as they are known. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': 