y', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/4d6ab2f9-5d2d-5a60-8647-945e331d0047', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/4d6ab2f9-5d2d-5a60-8647-945e331d0047'}, {'abstract': 'As Georgia’s state archives prepares to reduce its staff and accessibility drastically next month, archivists worry about a long-term impact on public records nationwide.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/us/budget-cuts-to-limit-public-access-to-georgia-archives.html', 'snippet': 'As Georgia’s state archives prepares to reduce its staff and accessibility drastically next month, archivists worry about a long-term impact on public records nationwide.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MORROW, Ga. — The Georgia Archives, which holds both historical curiosities and virtually every important state government document ever created, is about to become nearly impossible to visit.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/us/ARCHIVES-4/ARCHIVES-4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/27/us/ARCHIVES-4/ARCHIVES-4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/us/ARCHIVES-4/ARCHIVES-4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 670, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/us/ARCHIVES-4/ARCHIVES-4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1340, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/2