t': 'The federal government’s announcement of a program to enlist contractors to develop technology is seen as a turning point in a long-secret program.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/us/us-officials-opening-up-on-cyberwarfare.html', 'snippet': 'The federal government’s announcement of a program to enlist contractors to develop technology is seen as a turning point in a long-secret program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — For years, even as the United States carried out sophisticated cyberattacks on Iran’s nuclear program and the Pentagon created a Cyber Command, officials have been hesitant to discuss American offensive cyberwarfare programs openly. Since June, in fact, F.B.I. agents have been investigating leaks to The New York Times about the computer attacks on Tehran.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cyberwarfare Emerges From Shadows for Public Discussion by U.S. Officials', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cyberwarfare Emerges From Shadows for Public Discussion by U.S. Officials', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberwarfare', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Security Agency', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-27T02:52:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Shane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a838994-a653-5308-8af5-ee8adae34179', 'word_count': 1105, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a838994-a653-5308-8af5-ee8adae34179'}, {'abstract': 'Luke Donald, an Englishman, went to Northwestern University and has a home near Medinah Country Club, the site of the Ryder Cup.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/sports/golf/at-ryder-cup-in-illinois-americans-are-playing-on-luke-donalds-home-turf.html', 'snippet': 'Luke Donald, an Englishman, went to Northwestern University and has a home near Medinah Country Club, the site of the Ryder Cup.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MEDINAH, Ill. — Their volunteer shift at Medinah Country Club was over and Bill Arbogast and John Mudrock, two retirees with gray mustaches, were camped out by the seventh green, putting together their lists of the two Ryder Cup teams and trying to match the Europeans with their nationalities.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/sports/DONALD/DONALD-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/27/sports/DONALD/DONALD-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/sports/DONALD/DONALD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/sports/DONALD/DONALD-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1338, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/sports/DONALD/DONALD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thum