}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0220d2a-f07e-547f-80d1-759f3aba4518', 'word_count': 135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0220d2a-f07e-547f-80d1-759f3aba4518'}, {'abstract': 'Los Angeles beat the San Diego Padres, 8-2, and Milwaukee beat the Cincinnati Reds, 8-1, to move to three and a half games behind St. Louis in the wild-card race.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/sports/baseball/mlb-baseball-roundup.html', 'snippet': 'Los Angeles beat the San Diego Padres, 8-2, and Milwaukee beat the Cincinnati Reds, 8-1, to move to three and a half games behind St. Louis in the wild-card race.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Only two weeks remain in the season, and the National League playoff race has come down to the second wild-card spot: Cincinnati and San Francisco have clinched their divisions, and Washington and Atlanta are assured of playoff berths. St. Louis has the upper hand for the wild-card berth, but the Dodgers and Milwaukee gained ground with victories Wednesday. Two others, Philadelphia and Arizona, have slim hopes of stealing that spot, but another fringe contender, Pittsburgh, was eliminated with a loss to the Mets.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dodgers and Brewers Prevail to Pick Up a Game on St. Louis', 'kicker': 'Roundup', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dodgers and Brewers Prevail To Pick Up a Game on St. Louis', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Dodgers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Milwaukee Brewers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'St Louis Cardinals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Diego Padres', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-27T03:21:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36d6c3ad-80dd-5305-a733-764d46c1ab8e', 'word_count': 625, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36d6c3ad-80dd-5305-a733-764d46c1ab8e'}, {'abstract': 'Five members of the Sun once played for UConn, while the Liberty have three former Rutgers players.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/sports/basketball/liberty-sun-playoff-has-a-big-east-feel.html', 'snippet': 'Five members of the Sun once played for UConn, while the Liberty have three former Rutgers players.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before the Connecticut Sun played their first game, Teresa Weatherspoon, the Liberty’s point guard at the time, anointed the two teams as rivals.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/sports/Liberty-1/Liberty-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/sports/Liberty-1/Liberty-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1536, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Liberty-Sun Playoff Has a Big East Feel', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Liberty-Sun Playoff Has a Big East Feel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weatherspoon, Teresa', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pondexter, Cappie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Connecticut Sun', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Liberty', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-27T03:26:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Seth Berkman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Berkman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f003fd0e-470e-516d-ae72-7d30b1b83a89', 'word_count': 816, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f003fd0e-470e-516d-ae72-7d30b1b83a89'}, {'abstract': 'Polio, which seems like it should be a disease from a bygone era, persists mainly now in just three countries — Pakistan, Afghanistan and Nigeria. The Taliban has been blocking vaccinations in Pakistan. India, meanwhile, has had no new cases of polio in more than a year.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/26/india-wins-while-pakistan-keeps-losing-in-fight-against-polio/', 'snippet': 'Polio, which seems like it should be a disease from a bygone era, persists mainly now in just three countries — Pakistan, Afghanistan and Nigeria. The Taliban has been blocking vaccinations in Pakistan. India, meanwhile, has had no new cases of po...', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — India and Pakistan compete — often angrily, and usually at full volume — in just about everything. Cricket. Nuclear weapons. They dispute a marshy creek that runs between their two countries. And they spend fortunes to bivouac military units on a glacier so high, cold and forbidding that it is sometimes called “the third pole.” That standoff at 22,000 feet has famously been likened to “a struggle of two bald men over a comb.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/blogs/polio-rdv/polio-rdv-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 731, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/blogs/polio-rdv/polio-rdv-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1463, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'India Wins (While Pakistan Keeps Losing) in Fight Against Polio', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poliomyelitis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Afridi, Shakil', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gates, Bill', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-27T03:33:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark McDonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McDonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/099aad14-c21c-50fd-b192-235695a17de0', 'word_count': 741, 'uri': 'nyt://article/099aad14-c21c-50fd-b192-235695a17de0'}, {'abstract': 'To achieve baseball’s triple crown, Miguel Cabrera will have to fend off four sluggers who could finish this season atop the home run leader board.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/sports/baseball/miguel-cabreras-triple-crown-hopes-threatened-by-josh-hamilton.html', 'snippet': 'To achieve baseball’s triple crown, Miguel Cabrera will have to fend off four sluggers who could finish this season atop the home run leader board.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Miguel Cabrera continues to pursue baseball’s first triple crown since 1967, most of the remaining uncertainty surrounds the home run title, as his leads in batting average and runs batted in appear fairly safe. Cabrera, the Tigers’ third baseman, is among a group of flawed yet powerful sluggers with a chance at finishing on top in homers.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Four Sluggers Pose Threat to Cabrera’s Triple Crown', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Four Sluggers Pose Threat To Cabrera’s Triple Crown', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Granderson, Curtis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dunn, Adam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hamilton, Josh', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Texas Rangers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toronto Blue Jays', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago White Sox', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mauer, Joe', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cabrera, Miguel', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Tigers', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-27T03:40:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Hoffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 