h Chrysler', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Autoworkers Reach Deal With Chrysler', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Canadian Auto Workers Union', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chrysler Group LLC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-27T04:29:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3cef858e-e2a5-5fa3-b52d-a513691fdd0a', 'word_count': 506, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3cef858e-e2a5-5fa3-b52d-a513691fdd0a'}, {'abstract': 'Once used by Mughal rulers to communicate, pigeons are now raised for competition.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/in-old-delhi-the-ancient-art-of-kabootarbaazi-pigeon-rearing-lives-on/', 'snippet': 'Once used by Mughal rulers to communicate, pigeons are now raised for competition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI–One of the winding alleys of the Chitli Qabar neighborhood in Old Delhi leads to a four-story, narrow white house, where several cats hungrily ply the stairs almost constantly.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Old Delhi, the Ancient Art of Kabootarbaazi (Pigeon Rearing) Lives On', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Perfumes and Fragrances', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pigeons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Delhi (India)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-27T05:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Raksha Kumar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Raksha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kumar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6a33a49-4adc-5d49-81b1-785b7749f580', 'word_count': 721, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6a33a49-4adc-5d49-81b1-785b7749f580'}, {'abstract': 'The bitter citizens of a small English town are the focus in “The Casual Vacancy,” J. K. Rowling’s new novel for adults.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/books/book-review-the-casual-vacancy-by-j-k-rowling.html', 'snippet': 'The bitter citizens of a small English town are the focus in “The Casual Vacancy,” J. K. Rowling’s new novel for adults.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With J. K. Rowling’s new novel, “The Casual Vacancy,” we are firmly in Muggle-land — about as far from the enchanted world of Harry Potter as we can get. There is no magic in this book — in terms of wizarding or in terms of narrative sorcery. Instead, this novel for adults is filled with a variety of people like Harry’s aunt and uncle, Petunia and Vernon Dursley: self-absorbed, small-minded, snobbish and judgmental folks, whose stories neither engage nor transport us. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/arts/27BOOK/27BOOK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 667, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': '