times.com/2012/09/27/sports/football/nfls-deal-with-referees-brings-relief-but-resentment-lingers.html', 'snippet': 'Despite the satisfaction of a deal between the N.F.L. and it’s officials, coaches and players still feel the sting of replacement officials’ bad calls.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the N.F.L. and its referees drew closer to a new labor agreement late Wednesday, reports flew across the Internet — each, it seemed, only slightly different from the last. The deal was done. Then it was not. Then it was close. Then it was really close. Then all it needed was a signature.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Relief and Resentment After N.F.L. Deal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Relief and Resentment After N.F.L. Deal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Officiating (Sports)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-27T05:14:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Greg Bishop', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Greg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bishop', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/408ab338-7bab-5f5b-ba38-ed5a103a5a24', 'word_count': 642, 'uri': 'nyt://article/408ab338-7bab-5f5b-ba38-ed5a103a5a24'}, {'abstract': 'Facing a foe with superior weapons and firepower, the Syrian rebels wage an impassioned and complex fight.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/world/middleeast/100000001809375/fighting-for-idlib.html', 'snippet': 'Facing a foe with superior weapons and firepower, the Syrian rebels wage an impassioned and complex fight.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Facing a foe with superior weapons and firepower, the Syrian rebels wage an impassioned and complex fight.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/26/world/video-idlib/video-idlib-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/26/world/video-idlib/video-idlib-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/26/world/video-idlib/video-idlib-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/26/world/video-idlib/video-idlib-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fighting for Idlib', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Middle East', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-27T05:40:04+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'Ben Solomon and Christopher Chivers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Solomon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chivers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/1c078c9d-e35c-5036-87bc-c4f3d790816e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/1c078c9d-e35c-5036-87bc-c4f3d790816e'}, {'abstract': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/news-quiz-september-27-2012/', 'snippet': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'See what you know about the news below. To prepare, you might scan the articles or summaries on today’s paper. Good luck!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Quiz | September 27, 2012', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-27T05:59:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anastasia Economides', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anastasia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Economides', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f696bc68-b27a-5c6d-bb18-eb4331cf6529', 'word_count': 22, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f696bc68-b27a-5c6d-bb18-eb4331cf6529'}, {'abstract': 'News, fashion, arts and sports in today’s International Herald Tribune.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/iht-quick-read-thursday-sept-27/', 'snippet': 'News, fashion, arts and sports in today’s International Herald Tribune.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEWS After a period of relative calm, European markets shuddered once again on Wednesday as protests erupted across Greece and demonstrators surrounded the Spanish Parliament for a second day to protest the austerity program of Prime Minister Mariano Rajoy. Liz Alderman and Niki Kitsantonis report from Athens. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'IHT Quick Read: Thursday, Sept. 27', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-27T07:42:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By The International Herald Tribune', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The International Herald Tribune'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a01e0de-24d6-5273-a3e0-e3438bda712c', 'word_count': 338, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a01e0de-24d6-5273-a3e0-e3438bda712c'}, {'abstract': 'Can you choose the word pair that best completes the sentence?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/test-yourself-english-sept-27-2012/', 'snippet': 'Can you choose the word pair that best completes the sentence?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The question was written by Shannon Doyne. It comes from the article “Discovery of Skeleton Puts Richard III in Battle Once Again.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Test Yourself | English, Sept. 27, 2012', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-27T08:11:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b5b13d5-8053-535c-9e9f-87cadd873ead', 'word_count': 50, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b5b13d5-8053-535c-9e9f-87cadd873ead'}, {'abstract': 'The popular children’s magazine recently published its 600th issue, and circulation is growing.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/a-conversation-with-tinkle-magazine-editor-rajani-thindiath/', 'snippet': 'The popular children’s magazine recently published its 600th issue, and circulation is growing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tinkle, India’s first English-language comic book for children, published its 600th issue last month. Anant Pai, a former news executive known fondly to readers as Uncle Pai, introduced the magazine in April 1980. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Conversation With: Tinkle Magazine Editor Rajani Thindiath', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comic Books and Strips', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pai, Anant', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Amar Chitra Katha', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cartoon Network', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-27T08:14:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Malavika Vyawahare', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Malavika', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vyawahare', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/665de564-bb1b-5414-a7f2-063c2005f7a1', 'word_count': 1255, 'uri': 'nyt://article/665de564-bb1b-5414-a7f2-063c2005f7a1'}, {'abstract': 'What is the viral hit “Gangnam Style” about, according to this short blog post?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/going-viral-with-gangnam-style/', 'snippet': 'What is the viral hit “Gangnam Style” about, according to this short blog post?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Go to related blog post »', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Going Viral With ‘Gangnam Style’', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-27T08:22:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/049cbfff-9fe9-5e5c-8786-37c3828e1db1', 'word_count': 134, 'uri': 'nyt://article/049cbfff-9fe9-5e5c-8786-37c3828e1db1'}, {'abstract': 'The idea of hair “going gray” is a bit of a misnomer, as the only thing going anywhere is a pigment called melanin.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/booming/27question-booming.html', 'snippet': 'The idea of hair “going gray” is a bit of a misnomer, as the only thing going anywhere is a pigment called melanin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the height of a presidential campaign, you have to take your nonpartisanship where you can get it, and so let’s cast our gaze not at the head of state but at the state of the head. There we will find that most democratic of processes, the graying of the hair, which recognizes neither party (see Clinton, Bill and Bush, Barbara) nor sex (see previous parentheses).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Am I Going Gray?', 'kicker': 'Question Mark', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Boomers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hair', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-27T09:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Booming', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Nagourney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nagourney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1571a0a-5076-5c8d-9a67-13c4395fe77e', 'word_count': 431, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1571a0a-5076-5c8d-9a67-13c4395fe77e'}, {'abstract': 'Joe Mantegna, Al Pacino, Liev Schreiber and Bobby Cannavale talk about tackling the iconic character in ‘Glengarry Glen Ross.’', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/30/magazine/glengarry-glen-ross.html', 'snippet': 'Joe Mantegna, Al Pacino, Liev Schreiber and Bobby Cannavale talk about tackling the iconic character in ‘Glengarry Glen Ross.’', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s no surprise that “Glengarry Glen Ross,” the 28-year-old Pulitzer winner by David Mamet, is returning to Broadway: what better time to remount a show about ruthless real estate agents off-loading bum property onto suckers as the nation claws its way out of a recession? At the play’s center is Ricky Roma — the salesman’s salesman, a shark in a sharkskin suit. There have been three legendary takes on the role: Joe Mantegna, who originated it on Broadway in 1984 (and won a Tony); Al Pacino in the 1992 film (Oscar nomination); and Liev Schreiber, in the 2005 revival (also won a Tony). Next up: Bobby Cannavale, who’ll play Roma opposite Pacino in a new Broadway production this fall. (No pressure.) In interviews conducted by phone or e-mail (and edited and condensed), Mickey Rapkin consulted each of them about inhabiting Roma — and walking in one another’s loafers.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '48', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/magazine/30glengarry/30glengarry-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 409, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/magazine/30glengarry/30glengarry-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1985, 'width': 792, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/magazine/30glengarry/30glengarry-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/30/magazine/30glengarry/30glengarry-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Mount Rushmore of Ricky Roma', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ricky Roma Rides Again', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mantegna, Joe', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mamet, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schreiber, Liev', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pacino, Al', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cannavale, Bobby', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-27T09:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'Interviews by Mickey Rapkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Interviews', 'middlename': 'Mickey', 'lastname': 'Rapkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/21c276c8-fb3e-5d1d-a09e-e7d97da1a633', 'word_count': 1225, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21c276c8-fb3e-5d1d-a09e-e7d97da1a633'}, {'abstract': 'How the “Girl on Fire” turned a tossed-off phrase into a song.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/30/magazine/alicia-keys-goes-from-spark-to-fire.html', 'snippet': 'How the “Girl on Fire” turned a tossed-off phrase into a song.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alicia Keys got the spark for the title track of her new album at a very meta-moment: while reading about herself. “It came from this interview that I did, and the woman wrote something like, ‘She’s like a girl on fire,’ ” Keys said recently at her studio. “And I was like: I love that. And I remember thinking, I’m writing a song called ‘Girl on Fire’ for sure.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/magazine/30Keys1/30Keys1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/30/magazine/30Keys1/30Keys1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/magazine/30Keys1/mag-30Keys-t_CA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/magazine/30Keys1/mag-30Keys-t_CA1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/magazine/30Keys1/30Keys1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/30/magazine/30Keys1/30Keys1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/magazine/30Keys1/30Keys1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Alicia Keys Goes From Spark to Fire', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Alicia Keys Goes From Spark to Fire', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keys, Alicia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-27T09:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zachary Woolfe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zachary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Woolfe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c4fc5feb-3276-5442-a603-05d09fa1e64e', 'word_count': 1257, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4fc5feb-3276-5442-a603-05d09fa1e64e'}, {'abstract': 'A decade-dormant punk band awakens.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/30/magazine/desaparecidos-makes-the-perfect-protest-music-again.html', 'snippet': 'A decade-dormant punk band awakens.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The perfect protest album for 2012 happens to have been released 10 years ago by Desaparecidos, a band named after the dissenters who “disappeared” under Pinochet and other Latin American dictators. Desaparecidos was formed by Conor Oberst (more recently of Bright Eyes) and four friends from the Omaha music scene, and their only record, “Read Music/Speak Spanish,” catalogs the ills of modern America, including the failure of exurban expansion (“Greater Omaha”) and the warping influence of consumerism (“Mall of America”). It also eerily presaged the specter of drone warfare (“The Happiest Place on Earth”).', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '52', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/magazine/30desaparecidos/30desaparecidos-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/30/magazine/30desaparecidos/30desaparecidos-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/magazine/30desaparecidos/30desaparecidos-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/magazine/30desaparecidos/30desaparecidos-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1098, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/magazine/30desaparecidos/30desaparecidos-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/30/magazine/30desaparecidos/30desaparecidos-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/magazine/30desaparecidos/30desaparecidos-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Desaparecidos Makes the Perfect Protest Music (Again)', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Desaparecidos Makes the Perfect Protest Music (Again)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Oberst, Conor', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Desaparecidos (Music Group)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-27T09:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin Lincoln', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lincoln', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6466fd8-4b7d-5da8-889d-5a01fee74879', 'word_count': 810, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6466fd8-4b7d-5da8-889d-5a01fee74879'}, {'abstract': 'The creation stories behind the best movies, books, TV shows, music and plays on the horizon, featuring Alicia Keys, Michael Chabon, Quentin Tarantino, Al Pacino, Junot Díaz, Carrie Brownstein, Carly Rae Jepsen, Debra Winger, Patti LuPone and (a lot) more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2012/09/30/magazine/inspiration-issue.html', 'snippet': 'The creation stories behind the best movies, books, TV shows, music and plays on the horizon, featuring Alicia Keys, Michael Chabon, Quentin Tarantino, Al Pacino, Junot Díaz, Carrie Brownstein, Carly Rae Jepsen, Debra Winger, Patti LuPone and (a l...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The creation stories behind the best movies, books, TV shows, music and plays on the horizon, featuring Alicia Keys, Michael Chabon, Quentin Tarantino, Al Pacino, Junot Díaz, Carrie Brownstein, Carly Rae Jepsen, Debra Winger, Patti LuPone and (a lot) more.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/magazine/homepage-slide-ATV0/homepage-slide-ATV0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/magazine/homepage-slide-ATV0/homepage-slide-ATV0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/magazine/homepage-slide-ATV0/homepage-slide-ATV0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/30/magazine/homepage-slide-ATV0/homepage-slide-ATV0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/magazine/homepage-slide-ATV0/homepage-slide-ATV0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 122, 'width': 122, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Inspiration Issue', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-27T09:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/2899a89e-244e-57e5-949e-71d1d76809fc', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/2899a89e-244e-57e5-949e-71d1d76809fc'}, {'abstract': 'Chinua Achebe, Ken Burns, Carrie Brownstein, Lupe Fiasco and more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/30/magazine/great-moments-in-inspiration.html', 'snippet': 'Chinua Achebe, Ken Burns, Carrie Brownstein, Lupe Fiasco and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Anthony Bourdain Chef/Author, “Kitchen Confidential: Adventures in the Culinary Underbelly”“It was as a young man entering my teenage years, picking up Rolling Stone magazine and reading the first Hunter Thompson article of what would later become ‘Fear and Loathing in Las Vegas.’ For me, that was an electrifying moment that changed how I looked at the world. When you’re an insecure, reasonably neurotic, postpubescent young man entering high school, the Thompson character was a comforting one. But I think in the end Thompson was also an important cautionary tale, because when I finally did have success with a book, I had only to look at my original hero to see the perils of playing the part. He was stuck playing the Raoul Duke character for the rest of his life.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Great Moments in Inspiration', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Great Moments in Inspiration', 'name': N