Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ca12bcf-b407-507a-9989-15053cb5dfb0', 'word_count': 154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ca12bcf-b407-507a-9989-15053cb5dfb0'}, {'abstract': 'The private equity firm will start selling its $2.5 billion stake in Japan’s struggling Aozora Bank this year in a much-anticipated exit for Cerberus more than a decade after its initial investment.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/cerberus-to-sell-2-5-billion-stake-in-japanese-bank/', 'snippet': 'The private equity firm will start selling its $2.5 billion stake in Japan’s struggling Aozora Bank this year in a much-anticipated exit for Cerberus more than a decade after its initial investment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — The private equity firm Cerberus Capital Management will start selling its $2.5 billion stake in Japan’s struggling Aozora Bank this year, the Asian lender said on Thursday, in a much-anticipated exit for the firm more than a decade after its initial investment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cerberus to Sell $2.5 Billion Stake in Japanese Bank', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cerberus Capital Management', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-27T10:43:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hiroko Tabuchi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hiroko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tabuchi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c3df587-0787-5eb0-b7e0-f2e2cc7f1f49', 'word_count': 315, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c3df587-0787-5eb0-b7e0-f2e2cc7f1f49'}, {'abstract': 'Brian Burke is back with the game probabilities for the N.F.L. season, and he offers a primer on his system of prediction.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/n-f-l-week-4-game-probabilities-are-back/', 'snippet': 'Brian Burke is back with the game probabilities for the N.F.L. season, and he offers a primer on his system of prediction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is the fourth season I’ve been invited to share my game probabilities with Fifth Down readers, so it might be time for a short refresher course.\xa0 The model I use to predict outcomes is based on team efficiency stats and home field advantage. The overall idea behind the model is to tune things to predict the future rather than explain the past. The distinction may seem subtle, but it’s the key to accuracy and understanding how the sport really works.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'N.F.L. Week 4: Game Probabilities Are Back', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-27T10:45:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Burke', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burke', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/415388ad-bfa3-5b8f-942a-a6dbea7f5a54', 'word_count': 563, 'uri': 'nyt://article/415388ad-bfa3-5b8f-942a-a6dbea7f5a54'}, {'abstract': 'Confidence among European businesses and consumers continued to decline in September, the European Commission reported.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes