.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/q-and-a-farming-for-an-uncertain-future/', 'snippet': 'Wes Jackson, a co-founder of the Land Institute, reflects on population growth, resource depletion and the accumulation of carbon — and what it means for contemporary agriculture.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nearly 40 years ago, while teaching environmental studies at California State University in Sacramento, Wes Jackson began reflecting that something about the country’s agricultural practices wasn’t quite right. Soon that instinct grew into a powerful itch.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q. and A.: Farming for an Uncertain Future', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetic Engineering', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seeds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jackson, Wes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-27T11:42:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d935bed4-a0b6-5b82-8f7d-e1c87bbee2ec', 'word_count': 1731, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d935bed4-a0b6-5b82-8f7d-e1c87bbee2ec'}, {'abstract': 'Wade Guyton, who creates art on computers, is the subject of a midcareer survey at the Whitney Museum.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/30/arts/design/wade-guytons-computer-made-works-at-the-whitney.html', 'snippet': 'Wade Guyton, who creates art on computers, is the subject of a midcareer survey at the Whitney Museum.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE artist Wade Guyton works on the edge of Chinatown in a commodious light-filled space with windows looking over the Bowery. One portion is dominated by desks with little on them but Macs. Nearby is the biggest printer Epson makes — a hulking Stylus Pro 11880 inkjet. There is no smell of turpentine, no haphazard array of easels, no cans of paint or stacks of used canvases. In fact, there are none of the things one would expect in a painter’s studio. Instead all the creating is executed on computer screens and printers. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/arts/30GUYTON_SPAN/30GUYTON-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 381, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/30/arts/30GUYTON_SPAN/30GUYTON-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 381}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/arts/30GUYTON_SPAN/30GUYTON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/arts/30GUYTON_SPAN/30GUYTON-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/arts/30GUYTON_SPAN/30GUYTON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/30/arts/30GUYTON_SPAN/30GUYTON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/arts/30GUYTON_SPAN/30GUYTON-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Painting, Rebooted', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Painting, Rebooted', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Whitney Museum of American Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Guyton, Wade', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-27T12:00:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Vogel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vogel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb34f49c-f206-5d4e-8cdb-a1e7812e2445', 'word_count': 1773, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb34f49c-f206-5d4e-8cdb-a1e7812e2445'}, {'abstract': 'Think your Web mail service might be down? Here’s how to check on it.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/tip-of-the-week-checking-the-mail-service/', 'snippet': 'Think your Web mail service might be down? Here’s how to check on it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Web-based mail services like Google’s Gmail or Microsoft Hotmail/Outlook.com can keep you up to date with e-mail and online calendar services wherever you can get an Internet connection. These sites may have occasional technical trouble that can prevent you from getting your messages. If your mailbox seems suspiciously quiet for a period of time, you may want to check the status of your mail service to make sure it is up and running.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tip of the We