27:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Southall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Southall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7208dc9-19ef-5d10-9015-ba6d2484c58d', 'word_count': 340, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7208dc9-19ef-5d10-9015-ba6d2484c58d'}, {'abstract': 'This week’s Poetry Pairing matches W.S. Merwin’s poem “To the Light of September” with “Was It Hard, Our Year in the Woods? Yes and No,”a Green blog post about a year living “off the grid” in Maine.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/poetry-pairing-to-the-light-of-september/', 'snippet': 'This week’s Poetry Pairing matches W.S. Merwin’s poem “To the Light of September” with “Was It Hard, Our Year in the Woods? Yes and No,”a Green blog post about a year living “off the grid” in Maine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'View from a cabin in the Maine woods where the author of “Was It Hard, Our Year in the Woods? Yes and No” installed a game camera on a tree last October. Go to related blog post »', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Poetry Pairing | ‘To the Light of September’', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-27T13:41:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shannon Doyne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shannon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Doyne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0336753b-fc4d-5538-8a70-a695242501c2', 'word_count': 830, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0336753b-fc4d-5538-8a70-a695242501c2'}, {'abstract': 'Mark Lilla considers Charles R. Kesler’s “I Am the Change: Barack Obama and the Crisis of Liberalism.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/30/books/review/up-front.html', 'snippet': 'Mark Lilla considers Charles R. Kesler’s “I Am the Change: Barack Obama and the Crisis of Liberalism.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this week’s Book Review, Mark Lilla considers Charles R. Kesler’s “I Am the Change: Barack Obama and the Crisis of Liberalism.” In a recent e-mail interview, he talked about America’s current political landscape and discussed why grappling with the “new nature of capitalism” is the most pressing intellectual and political task facing us:\xa0', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/books/review/0930-bks-upfront/0930-bks-upfront-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 590, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/books/review/0930-bks-upfront/0930-bks-upfront-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1180, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/books/review/0930-bks-upfront/0930-bks-upfront-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/30/books/review/0930-bks-upfront/0930-bks-upfront-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/books/review/0930-bks-upfront/0930-bks-upfront-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Up Front', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Up Front', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lilla, Mark', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-27T13:43:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editors', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editors'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c3ee036-6363-5fa3-8f70-10083f913b17', 'word_count': 553, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c3ee036-6363-5fa3-8f70-10083f913b17'}, {'abstract': 'Charles R. Kesler’s book so exaggerates the historical significance of Barack Obama that he becomes both Alien and Predator.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/30/books/review/the-great-disconnect.html', 'snippet': 'Charles R. Kesler’s book so exaggerates the historical significance of Barack Obama that he becomes both Alien and Predator.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Once upon a time there was a radical president who tried to remake American society through government action. In his first term he created a vast network of federal grants to state and local governments for social programs that cost billions. He set up an imposing agency to regulate air and water emissions, and another to regulate workers’ health and safety. Had Congress not stood in his way he would have gone much further. He tried to establish a guaranteed minimum income for all working families and, to top it off, proposed a national health plan that would have provided government insurance for low-income families, required employers to cover all their workers and set standards for private insurance. Thankfully for the country, his second term was cut short and his collectivist dreams were never realized.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/26/books/lilla/lilla-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/26/books/lilla/lilla-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/26/books/lilla/lilla-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 594, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/26/books/lilla/lilla-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1188, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/26/books/lilla/lilla-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/26/books/lilla/lilla-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Great Disconnect', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Great Disconnect', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kesler, Charles R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-27T13:43:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Lilla', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lilla', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0e44f81-302b-5ebe-9e05-c8224cd0ba51', 'word_count': 2799, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0e44f81-302b-5ebe-9e05-c8224cd0ba51'}, {'abstract': 'Stereo versions will be released on Nov. 13, with mono versions coming next year.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/shades-of-yesterday-new-vinyl-versions-of-beatles-albums-on-the-way/', 'snippet': 'Stereo versions will be released on Nov. 13, with mono versions coming next year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Though EMI put considerable effort into both the sound and packaging of the remastered Beatles catalog in 2009, and then staked out a new market with its iTunes downloads in 2010, many fans of the group have argued that such newfangled ways of hearing the band are inauthentic – that the experience just isn’t the same on anything but vinyl, the format on which the albums were originally released.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shades of Yesterday: New Vinyl Versions of Beatles’ Albums on the Way', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Getting Back to Yesterday: Beatles on Vinyl', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Audio Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Compact Discs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, George', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Beatles, The', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'EMI Group PLC', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'iTunes', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-27T13:51:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'p