iots', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-27T14:40:30+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'Mac William Bishop, Channon Hodge and Pedro Rosado', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mac', 'middlename': 'William', 'lastname': 'Bishop', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Channon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hodge', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Pedro', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosado', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/79c9c613-3b86-500f-9d43-b4069238dc8c', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/79c9c613-3b86-500f-9d43-b4069238dc8c'}, {'abstract': 'While women make up about half of all medical students and a third of academic faculty members, they are nearly absent in leadership roles.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/women-still-missing-from-medicines-top-ranks/', 'snippet': 'While women make up about half of all medical students and a third of academic faculty members, they are nearly absent in leadership roles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The newly renovated suite of offices for our medical department was beautiful — clean, sleek lines that nevertheless incorporated features of the century-old hospital. The chairman of the department had a new office there, as well as all the division chiefs and the main administrators of the department. It was a plum location.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/05/09/health/Danielle-Ofri/Danielle-Ofri-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 969, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None,