 run Florida, Nevada and Colorado.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/obama-unveils-new-ad-as-early-voting-begins/', 'snippet': 'Early voting begins Thursday in Iowa, the first of many battleground states that allow people to cast their ballots well before Election Day on Nov. 6. The Obama campaign said the new ad would also run Florida, Nevada and Colorado.', 'lead_paragraph': '4:31 p.m. | Updated At two minutes long, President Obama’s new ad, “Table,” is his longest direct pitch to voters in a television commercial this year. And the stakes could not be higher.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Unveils New Ad as Early Voting Begins', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colorado', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nevada', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-27T14:40:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy W. Peters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18841c96-cc4b-5761-991d-aeff030a603a', 'word_count': 288, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18841c96-cc4b-5761-991d-aeff030a603a'}, {'abstract': 'An additional 386,000 jobs were created between April 2011 and March 2012, representing a 20 percent increase over previous estimates, the government says.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/more-jobs-than-we-knew/', 'snippet': 'An additional 386,000 jobs were created between April 2011 and March 2012, representing a 20 percent increase over previous estimates, the government says.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The government’s estimates of job creation are not particularly accurate, a point that is often made and often ignored. On Thursday morning, the Bureau of Labor Statistics provided another reminder. The agency said it probably undercounted the extent of job creation between April 2011 and March 2012 by 20 percent.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Jobs Than We Knew', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-27T14:45:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Binyamin Appelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Binyamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Appelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c61ba74-8abb-542d-973f-70f6127d7186', 'word_count': 218, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c61ba74-8abb-542d-973f-70f6127d7186'}, {'abstract': 'In time, the outrage over the replacement referees will fade, but for now, people shouldn’t forget the N.F.L.’s failures.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/leading-off-n-f-l-undervalued-competence-paid-in-integrity/', 'snippet': 'In time, the outrage over the replacement referees will fade, but for now, people shouldn’t forget the N.F.L.’s failures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Now that the N.F.L. has been successfully tarred and feathered and forced to admit its referee lockout was an unmitigated disaster — well, O.K., the league will not admit that, but you can read it in the egg yolk dripping down the facade — there are a few things to take away from the entire debacle. Yes, the league is every bit as arrogant and heavy handed as any big corporation that feels it has no one to answer to, and it deserves all scorn shoveled its way. And yes, fans can congratulate themselves for mustering the outrage to howl the league to its senses.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/sports/football/27ed/27ed-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 602, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/sports/football/27ed/27ed-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1204, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/sports/football/27ed/27ed-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/27/sports/football/27ed/27ed-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/sports/football/27ed/27ed-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Leading Off: N.F.L. Undervalued Competence, Paid in Integrity', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hochuli, Ed', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Green Bay Packers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Seattle Seahawks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-27T14:45:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fb3be1a-a46d-505b-8267-243687d43ff2', 'word_count': 537, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fb3be1a-a46d-505b-8267-243687d43ff2'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Lom, a Czech-born actor, played roles including Peter Sellers’s boss in the Pink Panther franchise, Napoleon Bonaparte and a witch hunter in the horror film “Mark of the Devil.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/28/arts/herbert-lom-frustrated-boss-of-inspector-clouseau-dies-at-95.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Lom, a Czech-born actor, played roles including Peter Sellers’s boss in the Pink Panther franchise, Napoleon Bonaparte and a witch hunter in the horror film “Mark of the Devil.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Herbert Lom, the versatile Czech-born actor who could play Napoleon Bonaparte or a witch hunter with equal aplomb but who was perhaps best known as Peter Sellers’s frustrated boss in the Pink Panther franchise, died on Thursday at his home in London. He was 95.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/28/obituaries/28lom/28lom-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy'