fort of Noah Baumbach and Greta Gerwig.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s a lot of talk about the most significant relationship one could have in life in the new Noah Baumbach film “Frances Ha,” premiering this Sunday at the New York Film Festival. And one can’t help but wonder if this is in some reference to Baumbach’s relationship with his real-life paramour, Greta Gerwig, who stars as the titular character and who is increasingly becoming the go-to actress for offbeat, likeable female roles (“Damsels in Distress,” “Greenberg“).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Noah and Greta Make a Movie', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Frances Ha (Movie)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Film Festival', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baumbach, Noah', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gerwig, Greta', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Frances Ha (Movie)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-27T16:02:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joy Dietrich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dietrich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f17802d-3a00-5722-9782-ec8f4db3a6e8', 'word_count': 570, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f17802d-3a00-5722-9782-ec8f4db3a6e8'}, {'abstract': 'The British bank, which agreed last month to pay the New York State’s top banking regulator $340 million to settle money-laundering allegations, may be at risk of losing money on a $1 billion loan to an Indonesian mining company to make an investment th