t, a northern Indiana weekly paper, lashed out in indignation at the president’s capitulation to abolitionist pressure. The proclamation would prompt the South’s “servile population” of “savage negros” to rise up in “insurrection, rapine, murder, arson, and what not,” the paper predicted. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Emancipation in Indiana', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emancipation Proclamation (1863)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Slavery', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lincoln, Abraham', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indiana', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-27T16:30:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen E. Towne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Towne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a9e0556-5377-5141-abe2-5efb74bd710d', 'word_count': 1370, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a9e0556-5377-5141-abe2-5efb74bd710d'}, {'abstract': 'Camera+, an iPhone app that has been a top seller in the App Store for years, expanded to the iPad on Thursday. Not many people shoot photos with an iPad, but the core features of the app are its editing suite and integration of Apple’s iCloud online storage service. The company also released an update for the iPhone version of the camera app to include cloud synchronization, so photos taken on an iPhone will also appear in the iPad app.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/camera-plus-ipad-app/', 'snippet': 'Camera+, an iPhone app that has been a top seller in the App Store for years, expanded to the iPad on Thursday. Not many people shoot photos with an iPad, but the core features of the app are its editing suite and integration of Apple’s iCloud onl...', 'lead_paragraph': ' Camera+, an iPhone camera app that has been a top seller in the App Store for years, expanded to the iPad on Thursday. Not many people shoot photos with an iPad, but the core features of the app are its editing suite and integration of Apple’s iCloud online storage service. The company also released an update for the iPhone version of the camera app to include cloud synchronization, so that photos taken on an iPhone will also appear in the iPad app.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/26/technology/26bits-cameraplus/26bits-cameraplus-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/26/technology/26bits-cameraplus/26bits-cameraplus-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/26/technology/26bits-cameraplus/26bits-cameraplus-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/26/technology/26bits-cameraplus/26bits-cameraplus-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/26/technology/26bits-cameraplus/26bits-camer