 'pub_date': '2012-09-27T16:56:32+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/5822c63f-1113-57ad-b159-2b4ba573f3f5', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/5822c63f-1113-57ad-b159-2b4ba573f3f5'}, {'abstract': 'Mountain Travel Sobek is offering a 25-day journey along nine rivers with class III through V rapids.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/rapid-transit-indeed-rafting-six-continents/', 'snippet': 'Mountain Travel Sobek is offering a 25-day journey along nine rivers with class III through V rapids.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are white-water rafting trips and then there are white-water rafting voyages. Mountain Travel Sobek offers the latter: a 25-day, six-continent journey along nine rivers with class III through V rapids.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rapid Transit Indeed: Rafting Six Continents', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rafts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rivers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-27T17:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elaine Glusac', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elaine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glusac', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/45359d7e-4687-52e7-9375-667f06b9dc76', 'word_count': 169, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45359d7e-4687-52e7-9375-667f06b9dc76'}, {'abstract': 'Pamela Love applies her signature jewelry motifs to classic motorcycle boots.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/the-get-pamela-love-for-nine-west-boots/', 'snippet': 'Pamela Love applies her signature jewelry motifs to classic motorcycle boots.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the jewelry designer Pamela Love set out to design shoes for the first time, in a three-piece collection for Nine West, she took inspiration from the grungy clothes worn by Royal Trux rocker Jennifer Herrema; the classic motorcycle boots made by Harley Davidson and Yves Saint Laurent; and the raffish hippie look, as seen in movies like “Easy Rider” and “Midnight Cowboy.” “When I think of the Pamela Love girl, she’s probably not wearing six-inch heels or strappy sandals,” Love says. “She’s sort of tough, sort of fashion-forward, sort of practical. She wants a pair of shoes that she can wear to death and beat to the ground.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Get | Pamela Love for Nine West Boots', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-27T17:00:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1ca9f09-e883-52e4-9782-b8fb750f4f75', 'word_count': 219, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1ca9f09-e883-52e4-9782-b8fb750f4f75'}, {'abstract': 'The $100,000 award, recognizing a play or musical inspired by American history, is being established at Columbia University in honor of Senator Edward M. Kennedy.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/new-theater-award-at-columbia-to-honor-kennedy/', 'snippet': 'The $100,000 award, recognizing a play or musical inspired by American history, is being established at Columbia University in honor of Senator Edward M. Kennedy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A $100,000 theater award, recognizing a play or musical inspired by American history, is being established at Columbia University in honor of the Senator Edward M. Kennedy, the university and one of Mr. Kennedy’s sisters, Jean Kennedy Smith, announced on Thursday.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Theater Award at Columbia to Honor Kennedy', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '$100,000 Theater Prize Honors Singing Senator', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy, Edward M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Columbia University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-27T17:02:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e12aba4-c2d4-59d4-beee-2fe94af2b810', 'word_count': 557, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e12aba4-c2d4-59d4-beee-2fe94af2b810'}, {'abstract': 'I’m always being prescribed medicine, but I never thought I’d get a prescription for a puppy.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/a-cancer-patients-best-friend/', 'snippet': 'I’m always being prescribed medicine, but I never thought I’d get a prescription for a puppy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I was growing up, my dream was to one day become a veterinarian. In fourth and fifth grade, I volunteered every day after school at a veterinarian’s clinic. I didn’t view it as an “internship” — in my mind, I was apprenticing for a certain future in the field. When I was 10, I asked for an incubator for Christmas. By spring, I was carting around a dozen baby chicks in my purple doll stroller. In middle school I walked dogs at the local animal shelter. But as I got older, there was college, summer travel, then my first real job, at a law firm in France. I was entering the “real world,” as they say in commencement speeches. And there was no room in my adult life for a dog. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/health/27suleika_dog/27suleika_dog-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/health/27suleika_dog/27suleika_dog-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1358, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/health/27suleika_dog/27suleika_dog-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/27/health/27suleika_dog/27suleika_dog-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/27/health/27suleika_dog/27suleika_dog-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Cancer Patient’s Best Friend', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'na