ity forces raided a house in the country’s restive eastern region of Qatif.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/saudi-forces-kill-two-in-manhunt-in-eastern-province/', 'snippet': 'A man wanted by the government, and a youth with him, were shot and killed when security forces raided a house in the country’s restive eastern region of Qatif.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Saudi Arabia’s security forces killed a man who was wanted by the government in the country’s restive eastern region of Qatif on Wednesday, and also shot dead a youth who was with him.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Saudi Forces Kill Two in Manhunt in Eastern Province', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Assembly (UN)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'YouTube.com', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Saudi Arabia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-27T21:36:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8dd52091-88a7-5799-836d-90373a075dc1', 'word_count': 461, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8dd52091-88a7-5799-836d-90373a075dc1'}, {'abstract': 'Blue Sky Riders — a trio of the songwriters Kenny Loggins, Gary Burr and Georgia Middleman — are having their debut New York performances at Feinstein’s at Loews Regency.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/28/arts/music/kenny-loggins-and-blue-sky-riders-at-feinsteins.html', 'snippet': 'Blue Sky Riders — a trio of the songwriters Kenny Loggins, Gary Burr and Georgia Middleman — are having their debut New York performances at Feinstein’s at Loews Regency.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Blue Sky Riders, a sturdy pop-country trio consisting of Kenny Loggins, Gary Burr and Georgia Middleman, is the latest illustration of a continuing phenomenon in which Nashville is the late-career catch basin for singers and songwriters from both coasts. It makes sense. There never was much stylistic difference between introspective New York folkies and laid-back Southern California dudes whose close harmonies in guitar-based arrangements were marginally less rural in sound and attitude than modern country music. Homogenization was the thing. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/28/arts/28LOGGINS_SPAN/28LOGGINS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/28/arts/28LOGGINS_SPAN/28LOGGINS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/28/arts/28LOGGINS_SPAN/LOGGINS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/28/arts/28LOGGINS_SPAN/LOGGINS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/28/arts/28LOGGINS_SPAN/28LOGGINS_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/28/arts/28LOGGINS_SPAN/28LOGGINS_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/28/arts/28LOGGINS_SPAN/28LOGGINS_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Familiar Faces in Pop-Country Trio’s New York Debut', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Familiar Faces in Pop-Country Trio’s New York Debut', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Feinstein's at the Regency", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Loggins, Kenny', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-27T21:38:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/13aa3cb7-9447-50af-b707-46cf61bfbd9d', 'word_count': 316, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13aa3cb7-9447-50af-b707-46cf61bfbd9d'}, {'abstract': 'James Purefoy plays the title character in “Solomon Kane,” based on the Robert E. Howard novel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/28/movies/solomon-kane-based-on-robert-e-howards-novel.html', 'snippet': 'James Purefoy plays the title character in “Solomon Kane,” based on the Robert E. Howard novel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An Elizabethan English Puritan with mad sword skills named Solomon Kane sounds ludicrous, but his creator, the pulp writer Robert E. Howard (1906-36), excelled in outrageous fantasy. Best known for Conan the Barbarian, Howard described Solomon as “a strange blending of Puritan and Cavalier, with a touch of the ancient philosopher, and more than a touch of the pagan.” There isn’t much philosophizing in the 2009 British movie “Solomon Kane,” which, in between the smoting and smiting, introduces a character whose name — evoking at once King Solomon and Cain — telegraphs that this is one caped crusader who brings both piety and Old Testament-style wrath. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/28/arts/28SOLOMON_SPAN/28SOLOMON_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/28/arts/28SOLOMON_SPAN/28SOLOMON_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/28/arts/28SOLOMON_SPAN/SOLOMON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/28/arts/28SOLOMON_SPAN/SOLOMON-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1080, 'width': 1920, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/28/arts/28SOLOMON_SPAN/28SOLOMON_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/28/arts/28SOLOMON_SPAN/28SOLOMON_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/28/arts/28SOLOMON_SPAN/28SOLOMON_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], '