. Thursday’s selection includes visually mapping the “Star Wars” stories and characters, a do-it-yourself iPhone 5 accessory and a tale of how easy it is to forget that simple tech tasks can go wrong.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/todays-scuttlebot-cable-haiku-and-carbon-fiber-failures/', 'snippet': 'The technology reporters and editors of The New York Times scour the Web for important and peculiar items. Thursday’s selection includes visually mapping the “Star Wars” stories and characters, a do-it-yourself iPhone 5 accessory and a tale of how...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some interesting items that the tech reporters and editors of The New York Times found on the Web recently.\xa0See more here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Today’s Scuttlebot: Cable Haiku and Carbon Fiber Failures', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-27T21:44:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8fd3b9cd-1ca2-5275-bd5f-1d859d980c53', 'word_count': 114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8fd3b9cd-1ca2-5275-bd5f-1d859d980c53'}, {'abstract': 'In two varied exhibitions, Thomas Hirschhorn reappropriates the news and surveys his public art.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/28/arts/design/thomas-hirschhorn-exhibitions-at-gladstone-and-dia.html', 'snippet': 'In two varied exhibitions, Thomas Hirschhorn reappropriates the news and surveys his public art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In his installations the Swiss artist Thomas Hirschhorn waxes didactic on politics and philosophy, even as he bombards us with sensational imagery. But in Mr. Hirschhorn’s current double showing in Chelsea, at Gladstone Gallery and at the future Dia project space, those two approaches have been teased apart. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/28/arts/28HIRSCHHORN1_SPAN/HIRSCHHORN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 386, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/28/arts/28HIRSCHHORN1_SPAN/HIRSCHHORN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 386}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/28/arts/28HIRSCHHORN1_SPAN/HIRSCHHORN1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/28/arts/28HIRSCHHORN1_SPAN/HIRSCHHORN1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/28/arts/2