pected to open in 2015, will be 625 feet tall and displace the Singapore Flyer for the record.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg said on Thursday that the world’s tallest Ferris wheel would rise above the Staten Island waterfront. The 625-foot-tall ride will displace the Singapore Flyer, at 541 feet the record-holder of the moment. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'World’s Tallest Ferris Wheel Planned for Staten Island', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ferris Wheel Planned on Staten Island Would Be the World’s Tallest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ferris Wheels', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Staten Island (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-27T23:36:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Barron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a07b4b21-d93f-52da-926e-76d99249acf5', 'word_count': 315, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a07b4b21-d93f-52da-926e-76d99249acf5'}, {'abstract': 'During warm-ups before Baltimore’s 23-16 victory, Ravens Coach John Harbaugh hugged the referee Gene Steratore, who is entering his 10th season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/28/sports/football/nfl-football-roundup.html', 'snippet': 'During warm-ups before Baltimore’s 23-16 victory, Ravens Coach John Harbaugh hugged the referee Gene Steratore, who is entering his 10th season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BALTIMORE — About an hour before the Baltimore Ravens kicked off to the Cleveland Browns to begin their game Thursday night, a roar circulated through the lower bowl of M&T Bank Stadium. ', 'pri