, 'word_count': 177, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3b64169-f081-51d3-9b2c-45d1f7578bd4'}, {'abstract': 'Nope. Not by a long shot. The real question is why negativity is always with us.', 'web_url': 'https://campaignstops.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/is-this-the-nastiest-election-ever/', 'snippet': 'Nope. Not by a long shot. The real question is why negativity is always with us.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A month after pundits declared the current presidential contest the “meanest,” “nastiest,” “most poisonous,” and “dirtiest campaign in history,” those summer laments already seem like poignant reminders of a kinder, gentler time. Thanks to recent efforts to score political points on violence in Egypt and Libya, and charges of class warfare rising on both sides, this mean and nasty season has only gotten worse.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is This the Nastiest Election Ever?', 'kicker': 'Campaign Stops', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidents and Presidency (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adams, John (1735-1826)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ADAMS, JOHN QUINCY', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brookhiser, Richard', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cleveland, Grover', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hemings, Sally', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jackson, Andrew', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-28T02:09:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Manseau', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Manseau', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank':