ute of Technology saw gains on their funds for the fiscal year, while Harvard’s lost 0.05 percent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An uneven economic year yielded uneven results for the largest university endowments, with reports released through Thursday revealing a range of results, from a fractional loss on investments for Harvard to a healthy gain for M.I.T.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mixed Returns for Endowments', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mixed Returns for Endowments', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yale University', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endowments', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Harvard University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Massachusetts Institute of Technology', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-28T03:17:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Pérez-Peña', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pérez-Peña', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7bd80b0f-487c-51f4-8ca9-10535d838385', 'word_count': 384, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7bd80b0f-487c-51f4-8ca9-10535d838385'}, {'abstract': 'The second-season premiere of “Scandal” solved a few puzzles but raised at least one more.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/channel-surfing-scandal-in-an-election-year/', 'snippet': 'The second-season premiere of “Scandal” solved a few puzzles but raised at least one more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This season, the critics Neil Genzlinger and Mike Hale are checking out favorite shows and seeing how they hold up. Previous entries in this series include posts on “New Girl” and “NCIS.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Channel Surfing: ‘Scandal’ in an Election Year', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Scandal (TV Program)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goldwyn, Tony', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Washington, Kerry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC INC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-28T03:24:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/485f66aa-242f-51b7-93b2-fa83622c50c7', 'word_count': 636, 'uri': 'nyt://article/485f66aa-242f-51b7-93b2-fa83622c50c7'}, {'abstract': 'NASA’s Mars rover Curiosity has spotted pieces of an old streambed where water rushed by billions of years ago, scientists reported at a news conference on Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/28/science/space/rover-finds-signs-of-old-streambed.html', 'snippet': 'NASA’s Mars rover Curiosity has spotted pieces of an old streambed where water rushed by billions of years ago, scientists reported at a news conference on Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NASA’s Mars rover Curiosity has spotted pieces of an old streambed where water rushed by billions of years ago, scientists reported at a news conference on Thursday. “It just seemed like someone came along the surface of Mars with a jackhammer and lifted up a sidewalk that you might see in downtown L.A.,” said John Grotzinger, the mission’s project scientist. From the size of the rounded pebbles embedded in the slab, the scientists estimated that water was flowing about a yard a second and was between ankle and hip deep. NASA has found bountiful evidence of liquid water on early Mars when it might have been warmer, but this was the first observation of an ancient streambed. Curiosity is looking for carbon-based molecules which, together with liquid water, could have provided all of the necessary building blocks for life. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rover Finds Signs of Old Streambed', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Space', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rover Finds Signs of Old Streambed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mars (Planet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Aeronautics and Space Administration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Curiosity (Mars Rover)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-28T03:32:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Space & Cosmos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kenneth Chang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kenneth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/f26ae6cf-9c71-5964-bbff-741472f412d4', 'word_count': 139, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f26ae6cf-9c71-5964-bbff-741472f412d4'}, {'abstract': 'The number of missions in which Afghan security forces work in partnership with American and allied troops is growing again, Pentagon and military officials said Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/28/world/asia/afghanistan-joint-missions-rise-again.html', 'snippet': 'The number of missions in which Afghan security forces work in partnership with American and allied troops is growing again, Pentagon and military officials said Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The number of missions in which Afghan security forces work in partnership with American and allied troops is growing again, although restrictions ordered after a spate of “insider attacks” have not been lifted, Pentagon and military officials said Thursday. In a significant restriction on a core element of the Western exit strategy from Afghanistan, the American-led military coalition said last week that all joint operations with Afghan forces conducted below the battalion level had to first go through a formal approval process — an effort to stem attacks by members of the Afghan security forces that have killed 51 American or allied service members this year. Officials now say those approvals were being handled efficiently enough that the number of partnered operations was returning to normal. Before the order, about 90 percent of all missions were conducted jointly. The number is now climbing again, said officials, who declined to offer specifics. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Afghanistan: Joint Missions Rise Again', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Afghanistan: Joint Missions Rise Again', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-28T03:39:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thom Shanker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shanker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b9e6bda-db43-536a-9921-cf894db43daf', 'word_count': 151, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b9e6bda-db43-536a-9921-cf894db43daf'}, {'abstract': 'Even Texas legislators who ran as outsiders, proclaiming Tea Party approval, are now part of the legislative “structure” and will have to act accordingly.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/28/us/in-texas-newly-elected-legislator-must-now-face-reality.html', 'snippet': 'Even Texas legislators who ran as outsiders, proclaiming Tea Party approval, are now part of the legislative “structure” and will have to act accordingly.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ross Ramsey, the executive editor of The Texas Tribune, writes a regular column for the Tribune.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/28/us/28ttRamsey/28ttRamsey-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 726, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/28/us/28ttRamsey/28ttRamsey-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1040, 'width': 737, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/28/us/28ttRamsey/28ttRamsey-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Time to Confront Reality, Now That They’re Elected', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Time to Confront Reality, Now That They’re Elected', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tea Party Movement', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, House of Representatives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-28T03:42:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Ramsey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ramsey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/29896b0a-c058-505d-9b57-f15327f89714', 'word_count': 763, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29896b0a-c058-505d-9b57-f15327f89714'}, {'abstract': 'The Mexican Navy said Thursday that its marines had captured a top leader of the Zetas drug gang, Iván Velázquez Caballero.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/28/world/americas/mexico-suspected-drug-boss-captured.html', 'snippet': 'The Mexican Navy said Thursday that its marines had captured a top leader of the Zetas drug gang, Iván Velázquez Caballero.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The Mexican Navy said Thursday that its marines had captured a top leader of the Zetas drug gang, Iván Velázquez Caballero. Mr. Velázquez Caballero had been feuding with another Zeta leader, Miguel Ángel Treviño Morales, a Navy spokesman said. The feud had caused a surge in violence in parts of northern Mexico. Mr. Velázquez Caballero was caught on Wednesday night in San Luis Potosí, north of Mexico City. The Navy has made several high-profile arrests recently, but experts say that lieutenants quickly rise to take the place of captured crime bosses, bringing struggles that generate new violence. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mexico: Suspected Drug Boss Captured', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mexico: Suspected Drug Boss Captured', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico City (Mexico)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trevino Morales, Miguel Angel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Zetas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-28T03:45:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Malkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Malkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/7318dbcd-b844-5a09-9a65-be793d6e8305', 'word_count': 97, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7318dbcd-b844-5a09-9a65-be793d6e8305'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Adler, a former New York City teacher, became a prolific writer of books on math and science for young people after being forced from the classroom during the early 1950s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/27/books/irving-adler-author-of-science-and-math-books-for-the-young-dies-at-99.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Adler, a former New York City teacher, became a prolific writer of books on math and science for young people after being forced from the classroom during the early 1950s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Irving Adler, a former New York City teacher who became a prolific writer of books on math and science for young people after being forced from the classroom during t