Ai paid a bond of $1.3 million to contest the government order. Tax officials are expected to keep the bond, which means Mr. Ai will owe $1.1 million. It was unclear what would happen if he did not pay. The government still holds Mr. Ai’s passport, and he has been forced to cancel overseas appearances. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China: Dissident Artist Rejects Fines', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: Dissident Artist Rejects Fines', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ai Weiwei', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fines (Penalties)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-28T03:54:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ac8f182-c2a3-5c42-9b06-59b304babd5e', 'word_count': 135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ac8f182-c2a3-5c42-9b06-59b304babd5e'}, {'abstract': 'This word has appeared in 123 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/28/word-of-the-day-naivete/', 'snippet': 'This word has appeared in 123 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'naïveté •\\nä-ˌev-ˈta, -ˌe-və-; nä-ˈev-ˌta, -ˈe-və-; ni-\\• noun', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Word of the Day | naïveté', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-28T04:01:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa08b8e9-3330-5c97-aeaf-df7fd1892461', 'word_count': 168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa08b8e9-3330-5c97-aeaf-df7fd1892461'}, {'abstract': 'After surges in enrollment in 2008 and 2009, the number of students entering graduate schools declined last year for the second year in a row.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/28/business/new-enrollment-drops-again-in-us-graduate-schools.html', 'snippet': 'After surges in enrollment in 2008 and 2009, the number of students entering graduate schools declined last year for the second year in a row.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Enrollment in college is still climbing, but students are increasingly saying no to graduate school in the United States. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/28/business/Grad/Grad-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 675, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/28/business/Grad/Grad-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1350, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/28/business/Grad/Grad-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/28/business/Grad/Grad-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/28/business/Grad/Grad-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Enrollment Drops Again in Graduate Programs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Enrollment Drops Again In Graduate Programs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Students (in US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Graduate Schools and Students', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Council of Graduate Schools', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-28T04:01:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4015603f-f6ac-5979-9e00-f5e01dc2bf93', 'word_count': 651, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4015603f-f6ac-5979-9e00-f5e01dc2bf93'}, {'abstract': 'Australia’s A-League is about to kickoff season No. 8 with a couple of new faces — Alessandro Del Piero and Emile Heskey.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/28/australias-a-league-banks-to-del-piero/', 'snippet': 'Australia’s A-League is about to kickoff season No. 8 with a couple of new faces — Alessandro Del Piero and Emile Heskey.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — Perhaps it is ordained that Australia, blessed with sun, sea and surf, could not also have the beautiful game in all its glory. For years, soccer has struggled there. A national league folded in 2004 amid bankruptcy and bad feeling, and the shiny new A-League that started a year later has yet to establish a solid foundation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Australia’s A-League Banks on Del Piero', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Del Piero, Alessandro', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Soccer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Serie A', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Australia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-28T04:01:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Duerden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Duerden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9375fa78-2b51-5b69-aadb-a2ca07a9014d', 'word_count': 982, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9375fa78-2b51-5b69-aadb-a2ca07a9014d'}, {'abstract': 'A New York State report says a spike in horse fatalities at Aqueduct Racetrack in Queens might have been prevented had racing authorities more closely monitored the use of prescription drugs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/28/sports/aqueduct-racing-officials-faulted-in-horse-deaths.html', 'snippet': 'A New York State report says a spike in horse fatalities at Aqueduct Racetrack in Queens might have been prevented had racing authorities more closely monitored the use of prescription drugs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than half of the 21 racehorses who had fatal breakdowns at Aqueduct Racetrack earlier this year might have been saved had racing authorities more closely monitored their health and the liberal use of prescription drugs to keep them racing, according to an investigation ordered by Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo of New York.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/28/sports/28racing2_337/28racing2_337-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/28/sports/28racing2_337/28racing2_337-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/28/sports/28racing2_337/28racing2_337-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 654, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/28/sports/28racing2_337/28racing2_337-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1309, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/28/sports/28racing2_337/28racing2_337-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/28/sports/28racing2_337/28racing2_337-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/28/sports/28racing2_337/28racing2_337-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Inquiry Faults Racing Officials in Horse Fatalities at Aqueduct', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Inquiry Faults Racing Officials In Horse Fatalities at Aqueduct', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject'