ole': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b851f3bb-3c16-5244-8c2f-106fd337f336', 'word_count': 682, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b851f3bb-3c16-5244-8c2f-106fd337f336'}, {'abstract': 'On Oct. 9, PBS will air “The Choice,” a Frontline documentary exploring the formative experiences, decisive moments and worldviews of President Obama and Mr. Romney.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/28/frontline-documentary-explores-the-lives-of-romney-and-obama/', 'snippet': 'On Oct. 9, PBS will air “The Choice,” a Frontline documentary exploring the formative experiences, decisive moments and worldviews of President Obama and Mr. Romney.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What do the notes from Professor Barack Obama’s law school classes look like? How was Senator Ted Kennedy of Massachusetts able to fillet Mitt Romney, his challenger, in Mr. Romney’s first major debate? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Frontline Documentary Explores the Lives of Romney and Obama', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Public Broadcasting Service', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-28T13:17:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9311ba91-ed94-55de-979a-ae9805d6bf07', 'word_count': 154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9311ba91-ed94-55de-979a-ae9805d6bf07'}, {'abstract': 'Brazil’s truth commission must establish once and for all that there was a systematic effort to torture and kill opponents of the military regime that ruled from 1964 to 1985.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/28/brazils-truth-commission-gets-to-work/', 'snippet': 'Brazil’s truth commission must establish once and for all that there was a systematic effort to torture and kill opponents of the military regime that ruled from 1964 to 1985.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SÃO PAULO — It was more than two decades ago, but I still remember the shocked look my brother and I shared when our father first told us he had done time in prison for working against Brazil’s military government. In disbelief, we went straight to our mother. She was surprised: “I thought we were going to wait until they were older.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Uncomfortable Truths', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-28T13:21:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel Politi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Politi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c536d7b6-2780-5077-9f6c-051935ea7936', 'word_count': 785, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c536d7b6-2780-5077-9f6c-051935ea7936'}, {'abstract': 'Unable to safely investigate in Benghazi, the F.B.I. is trying to piece together a deadly attack from more than 400 miles away, and it’s facing “a cavalcade of obstacles,” one American official says.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/29/world/africa/security-fears-hobble-inquiry-of-libya-attack.html', 'snippet': 'Unable to safely investigate in Benghazi, the F.B.I. is trying to piece together a deadly attack from more than 400 miles away, and it’s facing “a cavalcade of obstacles,” one American official says.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BENGHAZI, Libya — Sixteen days after the death of four Americans\xa0in an attack on a United States diplomatic mission here, fears about the near-total lack of security have kept F.B.I. agents from visiting the scene of the killings and forced them to try to piece together the complicated crime from Tripoli, more than 400 miles away.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/28/world/africa/jp-libya/jp-libya-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/28/world/africa/jp-libya/jp-libya-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/28/world/africa/jp-libya/jp-libya-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 613, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/28/world/africa/jp-libya/jp-libya-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1227, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/28/world/africa/jp-libya/jp-libya-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/28/world/africa/jp-libya/jp-libya-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'th