 the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chop Chop: A recipe for a sandwich that might help persuade your kids to try sardines. — Jeff Gordinier ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-28T13:34:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3984c18b-a281-5b8f-8c5a-8298d9519de1', 'word_count': 560, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3984c18b-a281-5b8f-8c5a-8298d9519de1'}, {'abstract': 'In Lisa Zeidner’s satirical novel, a heavily armed woman disrupts a suburban marriage ceremony. Lisa Zeidner’s new novel about the middle class deploys sympathetic characters and edgy satire.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/30/books/review/shotgun-wedding-suburban-jungle.html', 'snippet': 'In Lisa Zeidner’s satirical novel, a heavily armed woman disrupts a suburban marriage ceremony. Lisa Zeidner’s new novel about the middle class deploys sympathetic characters and edgy satire.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Do the self-satisfactions of the middle class and its rituals somehow prove irresistible to a novelist? Is it just too tempting to consider how a big social gathering might go disastrously wrong? Consider Ayelet Waldman’s “Red Hook Road,” in which a young couple meet a tragic end hours after taking their vows, or, in a more playful register, Ali Smith’s “There but for the,” which sends a dinner party spinning out of control when a guest locks himself in a room and refuses to leave. Lisa Zeidner’s funny, chaotic new novel, “Love Bomb,” is pitched in tone somewhere between Waldman’s and Smith’s: realistic in its depiction of sympathetic characters facing a crisis, while edgy in its satire of a well-off New Jersey suburb and its sometimes hapless police force.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/books/review/0930-bks-brownrigg/0930-bks-brownrigg-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 788, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/books/review/0930-bks-brownrigg/0930-bks-brownrigg-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1575, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/books/review/0930-bks-brownrigg/0930-bks-brownrigg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/30/books/review/0930-bks-brownrigg/0930-bks-brownrigg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/books/review/0930-bks-brownrigg/0930-bks-brownrigg-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Shotgun Wedding Suburban Jungle', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Shotgun Wedding', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zeidner, Lisa', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-28T13:35:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sylvia Brownrigg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sylvia', 'midd