is City?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winthrop, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speeches and Statements', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-28T14:32:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ted Widmer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ted', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Widmer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/263f6f62-1e10-583c-9dfc-efd5983579af', 'word_count': 1244, 'uri': 'nyt://article/263f6f62-1e10-583c-9dfc-efd5983579af'}, {'abstract': 'On Friday, the chiefs of Fiat and Volkswagen resolved a dispute over leadership of an industry lobbying group.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/28/for-marchionne-and-winterkorn-a-parisian-showdown-is-averted/', 'snippet': 'On Friday, the chiefs of Fiat and Volkswagen resolved a dispute over leadership of an industry lobbying group.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A dispute at the highest levels of the principal lobbying group for Europe’s automotive industry was resolved with a handshake on Friday, as Sergio Marchionne, the chief executive of Fiat and Chrysler, met with Martin Winterkorn, chief executive of Volkswagen, on the convention floor at the Paris motor show.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Marchionne and Winterkorn, a Parisian Showdown Is Averted', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paris Motor Show', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marchionne, Sergio', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winterkorn, Martin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fiat SpA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Volkswagen AG', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-28T14:36:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Schultz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schultz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a5f5a12-c2ae-547d-9f2f-45854aacce02', 'word_count': 278, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a5f5a12-c2ae-547d-9f2f-45854aacce02'}, {'abstract': 'Recently reviewed books of particular interest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/30/books/review/editors-choice.html', 'snippet': 'Recently reviewed books of particular interest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THIS IS HOW YOU LOSE HER,  by Junot Díaz. (Riverhead, $26.95.) The stories in this collection are about love, but they’re also about the undertow of family history and cultural mores, presented in Díaz’s exciting, irresistible and entertaining prose.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Editors’ Choice', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': "Editors' Choice | Recent Books of Particular Interest", 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-28T14:39:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/279839c6-3d86-597b-ae54-28eb20def271', 'word_count': 262, 'uri': 'nyt://article/279839c6-3d86-597b-ae54-28eb20def271'}, {'abstract': 'Paperback books of particular interest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/30/books/review/paperback-row.html', 'snippet': 'Paperback books of particular interest.', 'lead_paragraph': ' ANATOMY OF A DISAPPEARANCE,  by Hisham Matar (Dial, $15.) Matar’s fiction revolves around his parents, and especially his father, a Libyan dissident who was kidnapped by Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi’s agents in Cairo in 1990. In his elegiac second novel, a boy struggles with the mysterious abduction of his father, exiled from an unnamed Arab country, and with his confused, preadolescent desire for his father’s much younger second wife. ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paperback Row', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Paperback Row', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-28T14:41:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ihsan Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ihsan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ee8033d-9dd7-549b-9db1-05fae3194f00', 'word_count': 480, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ee8033d-9dd7-549b-9db1-05fae3194f00'}, {'abstract': 'Offering ideas; denying gratitude.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/30/magazine/book-burdening.html', 'snippet': 'Offering ideas; denying gratitude.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I recently started reading a wonderful and compelling book about sports. Before I finished it, I bought a copy and gave it to my 14-year-old nephew. As I got further into the book, I came upon a homosexual relationship that I thought might not be appropriate for my nephew to be reading, as he was brought up in a very religious household. I’m now feeling irresponsible for not having finished the book before giving him a copy. I am inclined to tell his parents my feelings, but he may have already read the book and perhaps thought nothing of it. Do I confess all? KATHRYN KORS-JACOBSON, CROTON-ON-HUDSON, N.Y.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/magazine/30ethicist/30ethiscist-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 402, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/magazine/30ethicist/30ethiscist-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 402, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/magazine/30ethicist/30ethiscist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/30/magazine/30ethicist/30ethiscist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/magazine/30ethicist/30ethiscist-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Book Burdening', 'kicker': 'The Ethicist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Book Burdening', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': '