n': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5034e66-c569-5296-8d53-08ef2d0c6a9c', 'word_count': 636, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5034e66-c569-5296-8d53-08ef2d0c6a9c'}, {'abstract': 'Paris', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/09/28/fashion/runway-womens/chalayan-spring-2013-rtw.html', 'snippet': 'Paris', 'lead_paragraph': 'Paris', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/28/fashion/runway-womens/chalayan_spring13app-slide-BL87/chalayan_spring13app-slide-BL87-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/28/fashion/runway-womens/chalayan_spring13app-slide-BL87/chalayan_spring13app-slide-BL87-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/28/fashion/runway-womens/chalayan_spring13app-slide-BL87/chalayan_spring13app-slide-BL87-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/28/fashion/runway-womens/chalayan_spring13app-slide-BL87/chalayan_spring13app-slide-BL87-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1365, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chalayan: Spring 2013 RTW', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-28T14:41:53+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Fashion & Style', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': "Women's Runway", 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/9f0ea8ba-d516-5377-9192-a72e03a50598', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/9f0ea8ba-d516-5377-9192-a72e03a50598'}, {'abstract': 'Michael Chabon’s best-selling new novel, “Telegraph Avenue,” started out a dozen years ago as an unproduced television pilot.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/10/07/books/review/inside-the-list.html', 'snippet': 'Michael Chabon’s best-selling new novel, “Telegraph Avenue,” started out a dozen years ago as an unproduced television pilot.', 'lead_paragraph': ' PILOT EXPERIMENT: Michael Chabon’s new novel, “Telegraph Avenue” — it’s at No. 7 on the hardcover fiction list — tells the story of two families, one black and one white, in Oakland and Berkeley, Calif. Twelve years ago, when Chabon’s novel “The Amazing Adventures of Kavalier & Clay” was starting to make some noise (it went on to win a Pulitzer in 2001), newspaper profiles mentioned that the author was wrapping up another project: a television pilot called “Telegraph Avenue,” about a black family and a white family in Oakland and Berkeley, Calif. How did Chabon get from there to here? “When I first considered the possibility of transforming the script into a novel,” he said via e-mail, “I went through the usual process, apparently requisite to my beginning any novel, of lying to myself about how easy it was going to be. I told myself I would just be able to ‘novelize’ it. Two and a half years later, battered and discouraged and ready to quit, and ready to kill the optimistic idiot who got me into this mess, I belatedly realized my mistake. A pilot is there to set the table. To set it beautifully, and with a proper and adequate complement of utensils for the coming meal. But in terms of nourishment it only really sets out some canapés, maybe a dish of olives. A novel has to serve a full, seven-course meal with sherbet in the middle and maybe a last little passed tray of petits fours. I had to start all over again, and reconceive the entire thing.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/10/07/books/review/07LIST/07LIST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/10/07/books/review/07LIST/07LIST-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1876, 'width': 1876, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/10/07/books/review/07LIST/07LIST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/10/07/books/review/07LIST/07LIST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/10/07/books/review/07LIST/07LIST-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside the List', 'kicker': 'TBR', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Inside The List', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-28T14:42:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gregory Cowles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gregory', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc30f68b-c3f7-5caf-be65-5125f84c268a', 'word_count': 646, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc30f68b-c3f7-5caf-be65-5125f84c268a'}, {'abstract': 'A proposed desalination plant will make the region around San Diego less dependent on imported water from the Los Angeles-based Metropolitan Water District of Southern California.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/28/on-our-radar-a-desalination-giant/', 'snippet': 'A proposed desalination plant will make the region around San Diego less dependent on imported water from the Los Angeles-based Metropolitan Water District of Southern California.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The San Diego County Water Authority agrees to buy the entire output of what will be the Western Hemisphere’s largest seawater desalination plant, removing a hurdle to construction. [Associated Press]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Our Radar: A Desalination Giant', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-28T14:45:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e671ec0f-6287-58a4-af95-d0a8dc1a3340', 'word_count': 173, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e671ec0f-6287-58a4-af95-d0a8dc1a3340'}, {'abstract': "At Fender, rock 'n' roll tries to beat the economy. | Real estate listings languish over fracking fears in Catskills. | James B. Stewart on which Americans are better off now.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/business/100000001812991/manufacturing-music.html', 'snippet': "At Fender, rock 'n' roll tries to beat the economy. | Real estate listings languish over fracking fears in Catskills. | James B. Stewart on which Americans are better off now.", 'lead_paragraph': "At Fender, rock 'n' roll tries to beat the economy. | Real estate listings languish over fracking fears in Catskills. | James B. Stewart on which Americans are better off now.", 'source': 'The N