dac60'}, {'abstract': 'Handel’s harpsichord music has since been overshadowed by that of his contemporaries.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/30/arts/music/handel-keyboard-suites-by-lisa-smirnova.html', 'snippet': 'Handel’s harpsichord music has since been overshadowed by that of his contemporaries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HANDEL: KEYBOARD SUITES', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/arts/30HANDEL/30HANDEL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/arts/30HANDEL/30HANDEL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Moving Handel’s Harpischord to the Modern Piano', 'kicker': 'Classical Recordings', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Moving Handel’s Harpischord to the Modern Piano', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Handel, George Frederick', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smirnova, Lisa', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-28T17:29:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivien Schweitzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweitzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/2bd70362-b4ac-55cf-8005-abf8036ccd86', 'word_count': 320, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2bd70362-b4ac-55cf-8005-abf8036ccd86'}, {'abstract': 'Richard P. Feynman has come back to my reading list in the form of “The Manhattan Projects,” which enters our softcover list at No. 8.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/28/graphic-books-best-sellers-a-justice-league-of-scientists/', 'snippet': 'Richard P. Feynman has come back to my reading list in the form of “The Manhattan Projects,” which enters our softcover list at No. 8.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In all my years of reading comics, I never thought that one of my favorite characters would be the real-life physicist Richard P. Feynman. I learned quite a bit about him last year, when I read the biography “Feynman,” published by First Second. As I said then, “much of the science went over my head, but the story was always captivating as were the scenes from his everyday life.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Graphic Books Best Sellers: A Justice League of Scientists', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feynman, Richard P', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-28T17:30:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Gene Gustines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': 'Gene', 'lastname': 'Gustines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/edad02bc-387a-52bc-8b15-fa9ba08c2735', 'word_count': 204, 'uri': 'nyt://article/edad02bc-387a-52bc-8b15-fa9ba08c2735'}, {'abstract': 'Apparently unaware of the unwritten rules of both ethical journalism and satire, an Iranian news agency published an edited copy of a report from The Onion on Friday, without crediting the original.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/28/iranian-news-agency-plagiarizes-the-onion/', 'snippet': 'Apparently unaware of the unwritten rules of both ethical journalism and satire, an Iranian news agency published an edited copy of a report from The Onion on Friday, without crediting the original.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last Updated: Saturday, 6:13 p.m. Apparently unaware of the unwritten rules of both ethical journalism and satire, an Iranian news agency published an edited copy of a report from The Onion on Friday, without crediting the original or acknowledging that it was fiction.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iranian News Agency Plagiarizes The Onion', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Onion, The', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Press TV', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Reuters Group PLC', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-28T17:30:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/73558968-c67c-56bc-a128-b57c03e6ddbc', 'word_count': 1808, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73558968-c67c-56bc-a128-b57c03e6ddbc'}, {'abstract': 'The $2.43 billion that Bank of America will pay in the Merrill Lynch case ranks as one of the 10 largest settlements in in a securities class-action lawsuits, behind the settlement over the disastrous AOL-Time Warner merger.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/09/28/the-cost-of-putting-the-merrill-lynch-merger-behind-it/', 'snippet': 'The $2.43 billion that Bank of America will pay in the Merrill Lynch case ranks as one of the 10 largest settlements in in a securities class-action lawsuits, behind the settlement over the disastrous AOL-Time Warner merger.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bank of America has resolved one of the largest and most embarrassing pieces of litigation related to its merger with Merrill Lynch in 2008. But the settlement comes with a pretty hefty price tag, since the bank has agreed to pay $2.43 billion to end the lawsuit. That monetary award ranks it as one of the largest settlements in a securities class-action case, behind the settlement over the disastrous AOL–Time Warner merger.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Bank of America, More Trouble From Merrill Lynch Merger', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Compensation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lewis, Kenneth D', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bank of America Corporation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Countrywide Financial Corp', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Merrill Lynch & Co', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-28T17:31:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter J. Henning and Steven Davidoff Solomon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Henning', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': 'Davidoff', 'lastname': 'Solomon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9b97e43-6c75-508f-9725-aa160a4a62c1', 'word_count': 846, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9b97e43-6c75-508f-9725-aa160a4a62c1'}, {'abstract': 'The Federal Communications Commission approved a process to pay television broadcasters to give up airwaves that would then be auctioned to cellphone companies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/29/technology/fcc-approves-auction-process-for-spectrum.html', 'snippet': 'The Federal Communications Commission approved a process to pay television broadcasters to give up airwaves that would then be auctioned to cellphone companies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The government took a big step on Friday to aid the creation of new high-speed wireless Internet networks that could fuel the development of the next generation of smartphones and tablets, and devices that haven’t even been thought of yet.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'F.C.C. Backs Proposal to Realign Airwaves', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'F.C.C. Backs Proposal To Realign Airwaves', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Communications Commission', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radio Spectrum', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-28T17:31:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wyatt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wyatt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a206f97-65ea-58d2-b3f8-4922a00617a8', 'word_count': 906, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a206f97-65ea-58d2-b3f8-4922a00617a8'}, {'abstract': 'The sale, which was first struck last November, was completed on Friday. Even after Universal sells off a third of EMI’s assets, as required by regulators, it will have a market share of 36 percent.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/28/universal-closes-on-emi-deal-becoming-by-far-biggest-of-remaining-big-three/', 'snippet': 'The sale, which was first struck last November, was completed on Friday. Even after Universal sells off a third of EMI’s assets, as required by regulators, it will have a market share of 36 percent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Universal Music Group closed on its $1.9 billion acquisition of EMI Music on Friday, a week after receiving regulatory clearance in Europe and the United States and more than 10 months after it first made the deal with Citigroup.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Universal Closes on EMI Deal, Becoming, by Far, Biggest of Remaining Big Three', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'n