ed with French wines and liquors. A French flea market, live music, wine tastings, games and a French bulldog show are part of the schedule. On Saturday from 6:30 to 11 p.m., Le Soiree turns the event into a big dinner party where guests can meet chefs. Tickets for the day session are $30 in advance, available online or $40 at the door. The Sunday evening program is $149 a person.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Weekend Fare', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-28T17:47:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bao Ong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bao', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1504a188-2c51-593d-836e-3f876c29909d', 'word_count': 663, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1504a188-2c51-593d-836e-3f876c29909d'}, {'abstract': 'Although he was elected on a pro-growth platform, the first budget from President François Hollande instead emphasizes freezing government spending and raising taxes on corporations and the wealthy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/29/world/europe/hollandes-new-budget-focuses-on-cutting-frances-deficit.html', 'snippet': 'Although he was elected on a pro-growth platform, the first budget from President François Hollande instead emphasizes freezing government spending and raising taxes on corporations and the wealthy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — President François Hollande, a Socialist who was elected this year on a pro-growth platform, presented a budget on Friday that would produce the biggest cut in the public deficit in 30 years while raising the top rate for the wealthiest taxpayers to 75 percent from the current 41 percent. ', 'print_section': 'A',