ing-mexican-flavors-in-a-california-surf-town.html', 'snippet': 'A high school reunion lures a New Yorker back to Southern California, where she begins a Mexican food odyssey at a place called Beach Liquor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'YOU know what doesn’t change in 20 years? The smell of eucalyptus. To some people, that soft, sweet green scent is the smell of massages and yoga classes. To me, it’s teenage angst. To me, the smell of high school, the smell of nervousness, awkwardness, acne, hormones, the smell of being a teenager is all wrapped up in the smell of eucalyptus.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/travel/30JOURNEYS4/30JOURNEYS4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/30/travel/30JOURNEYS4/30JOURNEYS4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 402}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/travel/30JOURNEYS4/30JOURNEYS4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/travel/30JOURNEYS4/30JOURNEYS4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/travel/30JOURNEYS4/30JOURNEYS4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/30/travel/30JOURNEYS4/30JOURNEYS4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/travel/30JOURNEYS4/30JOURNEYS4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Revisiting Mexican Flavors in a California Surf Town', 'kicker': 'Personal Journeys', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In a Surf Town, Revisiting Mexican Flavors', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Santa Barbara (Calif)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mexican Food (Cuisine)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surfing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Montecito (Calif)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-28T18:17:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Danielle Pergament', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Danielle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pergament', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c37565c3-2d0d-5800-889a-a9264239b1e5', 'word_count': 1823, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c37565c3-2d0d-5800-889a-a9264239b1e5'}, {'abstract': 'On a peninsula in northwest Costa Rica, aspiring wave riders go to surf school alongside an exotic jungle habitat.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/30/travel/waves-and-wildlife-in-costa-rica.html', 'snippet': 'On a peninsula in northwest Costa Rica, aspiring wave riders go to surf school alongside an exotic jungle habitat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT’S not every day that you step out from a sunset surf session straight into a jungle habitat of howler monkeys dangling in leafy guarumo trees, cicadas conducting a symphony, and a pair of white-nosed coati — raccoon-like animals with striped tails and masks — strolling across a dirt road, sending geckos darting out of their path. It was so enchanting that I even forget to swat at the mosquitoes hovering about, getting ready to divebomb my legs.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/travel/30NEXT1_SPAN/30NEXT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 327, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/30/travel/30NEXT1_SPAN/30NEXT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 327}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/travel/30NEXT1_SPAN/30NEXT1_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/travel/30NEXT1_SPAN/30NEXT1_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/travel/30NEXT1_SPAN/30NEXT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/30/travel/30NEXT1_SPAN/30NEXT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/travel/30NEXT1_SPAN/30NEXT1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Waves and Wildlife in Costa Rica', 'kicker': 'Next Stop', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Costa Rica, All Kinds Of Waves', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'v