tion': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c5efbf75-a8a0-512a-ae53-96f1623c7192', 'word_count': 504, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c5efbf75-a8a0-512a-ae53-96f1623c7192'}, {'abstract': 'A reader responds to an article about a destination in Guatemala.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/30/travel/letters-to-the-editor.html', 'snippet': 'A reader responds to an article about a destination in Guatemala.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor: Regarding “Pools, Caves and Chocolate” (Sept. 16), I found this article to misrepresent the experience of visiting Semuc Champey, which is a standard stop on the tourist trail in Guatemala. It’s a pity that the author has to recycle tired travel-writing tropes of “discovery” to make her observations seem more exciting. I understand that one of the appeals of Semuc Champey is its remoteness, that it’s not completely overrun with other tourists, but the author seems to be indulging in some kind of fantasy in which she and her boyfriend discover an untouched Eden.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Letters to the Editor', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Guatemala Getaway', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Semuc Champey (Guatemala)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-28T18:20:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/cbca80d1-2da6-54c6-932b-d0680b38204d', 'word_count': 142, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cbca80d1-2da6-54c6-932b-d0680b38204d'}, {'abstract': 'The couple, who have extensive history in diplomatic work, are married in Georgia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/30/fashion/weddings/heather-thompson-and-edward-burke-vows.html', 'snippet': 'The couple, who have extensive history in diplomatic work, are married in Georgia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EDWARD BURKE was taking photographs of a group of young women from South Africa who were visiting the Smithsonian’s National Museum of African Art, where he is the public affairs specialist. As he framed a shot through the lens, his focus jumped to the chaperon: the tall, lithe Heather Joy Thompson.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/fashion/weddings/30VOWS1_SPAN/30VOWS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/30/fashion/weddings/30VOWS1_SPAN/30VOWS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/fashion/weddings/30VOWS1_SPAN/30VOWS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/fashion/weddings/30VOWS1_SPAN/30VOWS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/fashion/weddings/30VOWS1_SPAN/30VOWS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/30/fashion/weddings/30VOWS1_SPAN/30VOWS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/fashion/weddings/