29/world/middleeast/white-house-move-to-give-egypt-450-million-in-aid-meets-resistance.html', 'snippet': 'Lawmakers wary of foreign aid in general, and of Egypt’s new leadership in particular, protested the planned infusion of cash, which the Obama administration disclosed to Congress on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Obama administration notified Congress on Friday that it would provide Egypt’s new government an emergency cash infusion of $450 million, but the aid immediately encountered resistance from a prominent lawmaker wary of foreign aid and Egypt’s new course under the leadership of the Muslim Brotherhood.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Move to Give Egypt $450 Million in Aid Meets Resistance', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Emergency Aid to Egypt Encounters an Objection', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mubarak, Hosni', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Aid', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Granger, Kay', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Libya)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-28T19:33:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Lee Myers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': 'Lee', 'lastname': 'Myers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ef2f535-9cc7-5868-a033-a1d5f85d33a1', 'word_count': 956, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ef2f535-9cc7-5868-a033-a1d5f85d33a1'}, {'abstract': 'In Port Jefferson Station, L.I., homes range from apartments, to tiny cottages on small plots, to substantial properties on several acres.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/30/realestate/port-jefferson-station-living-in-versatile-housing-in-both-kind-and-cost.html', 'snippet': 'In Port Jefferson Station, L.I., homes range from apartments, to tiny cottages on small plots, to substantial properties on several acres.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AS it slices east to west through Port Jefferson Station, the thoroughfare called Nesconset Highway, or Route 347, is a dividing line in more than just a physical sense. According to the Census Bureau, the southern portion of town actually has a different name: Terryville. ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/realestate/30LIVINGIN_SPAN/30LIVINGIN_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/30/realestate/30LIVINGIN_SPAN/30LIVINGIN_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/realestate/30LIVINGIN_SPAN/living-in-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/