 New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Apple’s Plans for Internet Radio Run Up Against Big Music Publisher', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Apple Web Radio Plans Stall Over Music Rights From Sony/ATV', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SONY/ATV Music Publishing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-28T23:29:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf425e3e-38c9-5fed-a616-6b3fe88544b6', 'word_count': 321, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf425e3e-38c9-5fed-a616-6b3fe88544b6'}, {'abstract': 'The N.F.L. strike is a metaphor for the battle in American business.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/29/opinion/the-nfl-strike-and-modern-economy.html', 'snippet': 'The N.F.L. strike is a metaphor for the battle in American business.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT was a thoroughly modern economic game, this three-way tiff between N.F.L. owners, players and referees. The N.F.L.’s unionized officials asked for significant wage and pension changes from America’s leading sporting league. In response, the N.F.L. locked out the unionized refs and brought in replacements. The replacement refs struggled. In turn, players spoke out against the replacement refs — especially after an egregious error that ended a marquee game between Green Bay and Seattle. Players, fans and members of the media demanded that the N.F.L. capitulate and pay whatever it took to bring back the regular refs. Finally, a deal was done. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Talent Shows', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Talent Shows', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Officiating (Sports)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-28T23:31:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roger L. Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roger', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/17ea6f39-93b1-5b06-845e-4fddde7f95e5', 'word_count': 765, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17ea6f39-93b1-5b06-845e-4fddde7f95e5'}, {'abstract': 'City Limits, in White Plains, recently emerged from a four-month renovation without its traditional diner counter but retaining its expansive menu.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/30/nyregion/a-review-of-city-limits-restaurant-in-white-plains.html', 'snippet': 'City Limits, in White Plains, recently emerged from a four-month renovation without its traditional diner counter but retaining its expansive menu.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THESE days, calling City Limits a diner may be a misnomer. After a four-month renovation, it reopened in August, with the traditional diner counter removed and a new earth-tone c