f Teachers is spending $1 million for commercials in New York City as a new film called “Won’t Back Down,” which is about the education system, is released.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/29/education/new-york-teachers-union-announces-ad-campaign.html', 'snippet': 'The United Federation of Teachers is spending $1 million for commercials in New York City as a new film called “Won’t Back Down,” which is about the education system, is released.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Teachers’ unions have come under fire from politicians like Mayor Rahm Emanuel of Chicago and Mitt Romney in recent months. But rarely has opposition to teachers’ unions worn a face as sympathetic as that of Maggie Gyllenhaal, the Academy Award-nominated actress who plays a crusading parent confronting a bullying, bureaucratic union in a new movie, “Won’t Back Down.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Film and Union’s Ads, Dueling Views of Teachers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Film and Union’s Ads, Dueling Views of Teachers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Federation of Teachers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weingarten, Randi', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mulgrew, Michael', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "Won't Back Down (Movie)", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN FEDERATION OF TEACHERS', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}