e.html', 'snippet': 'Growth is weak and unemployment is high, but Mitt Romney is having a hard time convincing voters that President Obama is responsible.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Mitt Romney sees it, this week’s economic data ought to be bad news for President Obama. The economy slowed to a crawl in the second quarter and the current quarter looks like more of the same. A nascent housing recovery was offset by setbacks in manufacturing. A drop in military spending previewed the pain that is to come if lawmakers don’t find a way to avert even deeper automatic cuts that Republican lawmakers insisted on for 2013.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Economy and the Blame', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Economy and the Blame', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-29T01:08:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/db0ce460-514f-53b5-91ba-8cfa1c0f69cc', 'word_count': 472, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db0ce460-514f-53b5-91ba-8cfa1c0f69cc'}, {'abstract': 'Tall and underappreciated, Seattle’s secondary is proving that big defenders do not necessarily lack speed and agility, but have the ability to terrorize receivers with their size.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/29/sports/football/seahawks-towering-secondary-is-batting-away-conventional-wisdom.html', 'snippet': 'Tall and underappreciated, Seattle’s secondary is proving that big defenders do not necessarily lack speed and agility, but have the ability to terrorize receivers with their size.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RENTON, Wash. — The youngest, tallest, most underappreciated secondary in professional football consists of two players chosen in the draft’s fifth round, another plucked from the Canadian Football League and another whose diminutive stature almost led to the worst kind of group nickname: Three and a Half Men.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/29/sports/seahawks/seahawks-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/29/sports/seahawks/seahawks-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 345}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/29/sports/seahawks/seahawks-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 696, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/29/sports/seahawks/seahawks-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1392, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/29/sports/seahawks/seahawks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/29/sports/seahawks/seahawks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/29/sports/seahawks/seahawks-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Seattle’s Tall Secondary Is Batting Away Conventional Wisdom', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Seattle’s Tall Secondary Is Batting Away Conventional Wisdom', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sherman, Richard', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thomas, Earl (1989- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carroll, Pete', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Browner, Brandon', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Seattle Seahawks', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chancellor, Kam', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-29T01:09:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Greg Bishop', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Greg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bishop', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3658585-2028-5616-99b7-513683c0f3a4', 'word_count': 993, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3658585-2028-5616-99b7-513683c0f3a4'}, {'abstract': 'Eradicating the world of the virus should be a top priority of the United Nations and should lead to immunizing all children against infectious diseases.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/29/opinion/an-unfinished-campaign-against-polio.html', 'snippet': 'Eradicating the world of the virus should be a top priority of the United Nations and should lead to immunizing all children against infectious diseases.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Leaders of the global fight to eradicate polio vowed at the United Nations on Thursday to step up their efforts to eliminate the virus from the three countries where the disease still has a foothold — Afghanistan, Pakistan and Nigeria. The challenge is that those countries are troubled by political unrest, violence and social customs that can interfere with the delivery of vaccines to the children and adults who need protection.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Unfinished Campaign Against Polio', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Unfinished Campaign Against Polio', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poliomyelitis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nigeria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-29T01:11:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8406d3c-4553-55e1-ba34-a108306fed94', 'word_count': 299, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8406d3c-4553-55e1-ba34-a108306fed94'}, {'abstract': 'A report warns that far tighter controls for horse safety are needed to prevent further compromise of racing’s integrity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/29/opinion/thoroughbred-survival-at-the-racetrack.html', 'snippet': 'A report warns that far tighter controls for horse safety are needed to prevent further compromise of racing’s integrity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An alarming rise in thoroughbred fatalities last winter at Aqueduct Racetrack is prompting a much-needed overhaul of inept, pro-industry regulation of a sport that increasingly puts horses’ lives at risk in the pursuit of profit. A report by a panel of experts said the lives of 11 of 21 horses that died at the track might have been saved if the state had had proper safeguards against overmedicated and substandard horses’ running for purses inflated by profits from the new adjacent casino at Aqueduct.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thoroughbred Survival at the Racetrack', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Thoroughbred Survival at the Racetrack', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Racing Assn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-29T01:14:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc3a9dd0-56a9-5709-ba6e-56ca655846e1', 'word_count': 279, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc3a9dd0-56a9-5709-ba6e-56ca655846e1'}, {'abstract': 'Five friends gathered at Kutsher’s Tribeca on Franklin Street after Yom Kippur.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/30/nyregion/breaking-their-fast-with-a-downtown-twist.html', 'snippet': 'Five friends gathered at Kutsher’s Tribeca on Franklin Street after Yom Kippur.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kutsher’s Tribeca on Franklin Street was designed for a downtown crowd that still craves Jewish home cooking: it bills itself as a modern Jewish bistro, the hip offspring of the original Kutsher’s Country Club resort in the Catskills. For this year’s High Holy Days, it offered special meals, including a Yom Kippur break-fast menu of smoked fish and other favorites alongside nontraditional touches like duck schmaltz French fries. On Wednesday, families small and large and groups of friends filled the plush booths and tables set between blond-wood panels and glowing lights.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/nyregion/30TABLE_SPAN/30TABLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/30/nyregion/30TABLE_SPAN/30TABLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/nyregion/30TABLE_SPAN/30TABLE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 662, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/nyregion/30TABLE_SPAN/30TABLE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1325, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/nyregion/30TABLE_SPAN/30TABLE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/30/nyregion/30TABLE_SPAN/30TABLE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/nyregion/30TABLE_SPAN/30TABLE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumb