ustein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df16297e-f98a-59c0-b0be-a05c62766bc7', 'word_count': 497, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df16297e-f98a-59c0-b0be-a05c62766bc7'}, {'abstract': 'Cambodia’s request for American help in the repatriation of a Khmer warrior at the Norton Simon Museum came as Sotheby’s and federal prosecutors argued in court over the fate of a matching work.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/29/arts/design/cambodia-now-seeking-return-of-norton-simon-statue.html', 'snippet': 'Cambodia’s request for American help in the repatriation of a Khmer warrior at the Norton Simon Museum came as Sotheby’s and federal prosecutors argued in court over the fate of a matching work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Cambodian government has asked the United States to help it recover a 10th-century Khmer sandstone statue from the Norton Simon Museum in California. It says the work was looted from a Cambodian temple complex during the country’s political upheavals in the 1970s.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cambodia Is Seeking 2nd Statue', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cambodia Is Seeking 2nd Statue', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Norton Simon Museum', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHAEOLOGY', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reparations and Restitution', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Daniels, George B', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Looting', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cambodia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Sotheby's", 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-29T01:30:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ralph Blumenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ralph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Blumenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c1e1815-4154-5d7f-9244-d55878d59db9', 'word_count': 639, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c1e1815-4154-5d7f-9244-d55878d59db9'}, {'abstract': 'A childbirth is never far away in “Call the Midwife,” and some of the scenes are about as detailed as you can get, short of fitting the kid with a helmet-cam in utero.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/29/arts/television/call-the-midwife-a-bbc-series-comes-to-pbs.html', 'snippet': 'A childbirth is never far away in “Call the Midwife,” and some of the scenes are about as detailed as you can get, short of fitting the kid with a helmet-cam in utero.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s the fall TV season, which means that babies are thick in the air, since childbirth scenes are a sure way to draw “aws” and “ews” from jaded viewers. Babies arrived this week on the premiere of the Fox series “The Mindy Project,” about a young obstetrician, and on the wretched TLC reality show “Here Comes Honey Boo Boo.” Another birth is surely coming on the NBC series “The New Normal,” about a male couple and their mother-for-hire, and the first lady appears to be pregnant on ABC’s “Scandal.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/29/arts/29MIDWIFE/29MIDWIFE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 958, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/29/arts/29MIDWIFE/29MIDWIFE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1197, 'width': 1279, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/29/arts/29MIDWIFE/29MIDWIFE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/29/arts/29MIDWIFE/29MIDWIFE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/29/arts/29MIDWIFE/29MIDWIFE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Career in Obstetrics, With On-the-Job Training', 'kicker': 'Television Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Career in Obstetrics, With On-the-Job Training', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Call the Midwife (TV Program)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-29T01:32:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/08a77a8d-24a3-5c4f-9855-8f7294d4cdeb', 'word_count': 607, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08a77a8d-24a3-5c4f-9855-8f7294d4cdeb'}, {'abstract': 'The R&B singer Bettye LaVette speaks about her long career and struggle to become a star.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/29/arts/music/bettye-lavette-the-rampb-singer-reflects-on-her-career.html', 'snippet': 'The R&B singer Bettye LaVette speaks about her long career and struggle to become a star.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WEST ORANGE, N.J. — Bettye LaVette makes no apologies for her life. Sitting cross-legged on an Art Deco chair in her living room here, sipping wine, she was animated and gritty as she talked about the decades she spent singing in clubs and cursing her “buzzard luck,” while her contemporaries, like Aretha Franklin and Diana Ross, became superstars.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/29/arts/29LAVETTE/29LAVETTE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 921, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/29/arts/29LAVETTE/29LAVETTE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1267, 'width': 1408, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/29/arts/29LAVETTE/29LAVETTE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/29/arts/29LAVETTE/29LAVETTE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/29/arts/29LAVETTE/29LAVETTE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 149, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hard Times, With Regret But Without Apology', 'kicker': 'A Word With: Bettye Lavette', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hard Times, With Regret But Without Apology', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'LaVette, Bettye', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-29T01:33:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interview', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd6dd996-6a92-58fb-afe2-b1f9e4ba3d70', 'word_count': 979, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd6dd996-6a92-58fb-afe2-b1f9e4ba3d70'}, {'abstract': 'We often talk about the important role that the economy plays in the election. But Americans perceptions of the economy are also colored by their political views.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/28/sept-28-a-circular-relationship-between-political-and-economic-views/', 'snippet': 'We often talk about the important role that the economy plays in the election. But Americans perceptions of the economy are also colored by their political views.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama’s probability of winning the Electoral College fell slightly in Friday’s FiveThirtyEight forecast, from 83.9 percent to 82.7 percent on Thursday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sept. 28: A Circular Relationship Between Political and Economic Views', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Bill', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], '