ue': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Picard, Irving H', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-29T01:36:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97a1b33b-a0d3-582f-9bfe-7418b93f5cf5', 'word_count': 382, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97a1b33b-a0d3-582f-9bfe-7418b93f5cf5'}, {'abstract': '“666 Park Avenue,” which has its premiere on ABC on Sunday, features Vanessa Williams and Terry O’Quinn as owners of an apartment building where heating shouldn’t be a problem.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/29/arts/television/666-park-avenue-has-premiere-on-abc.html', 'snippet': '“666 Park Avenue,” which has its premiere on ABC on Sunday, features Vanessa Williams and Terry O’Quinn as owners of an apartment building where heating shouldn’t be a problem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'How powerful is the Devil? Powerful enough, apparently, to get a not particularly necessary series like “666 Park Avenue” onto network television.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/29/arts/29PARKAVE/29PARKAVE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 872, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/29/arts/29PARKAVE/29PARKAVE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1743, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image'