table; others, highly unlikely. A brief, intriguing recital presented on Thursday evening by Mikhail Rudy, a Russian pianist born in Uzbekistan and based in France since the 1970s, managed to be both at once.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/29/arts/29RUDY/29RUDY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 881, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/29/arts/29RUDY/29RUDY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1761, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/29/arts/29RUDY/29RUDY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/29/arts/29RUDY/29RUDY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/29/arts/29RUDY/29RUDY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Museum Gathers Piano, Paintings and Video in a Blended Work', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Museum Gathers Piano, Paintings and Video in a Blended Work', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Guggenheim, Solomon R, Museum', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-29T01:39:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/247f157a-cfd5-5dcf-86f6-cf5fff617534', 'word_count': 393, 'uri': 'nyt://article/247f157a-cfd5-5dcf-86f6-cf5fff617534'}, {'abstract': 'The Garth Fagan Dance company is performing the premiere of “Lighthouse/Lightning Rod” at the Brooklyn Academy of Music.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/29/arts/dance/garth-fagan-dance-at-brooklyn-academy-of-music.html', 'snippet': 'The Garth Fagan Dance company is performing the premiere of “Lighthouse/Lightning Rod” at the Brooklyn Academy of Music.', 'lead_paragraph': '\xa0A lighthouse guides a ship to safety. A lightning rod diverts a bolt from a structure by providing a direct path to the ground. Still, the opening images of “Lighthouse/Lightning Rod,” a new work by the choreographer Garth Fagan, with loose, exuberant music by the jazz composer and trumpeter Wynton Marsalis, hint at danger as much as at security.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/29/arts/SUB-29-FAGAN/SUB-29-FAGAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/29/arts/SUB-29-FAGAN/SUB-29-FAGAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1275, 'width': 1913, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/29/arts/SUB-29-FAGAN/SUB-29-FAGAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/29/arts/SUB-29-FAGAN/SUB