r Stravinsky gave ballet a new pulse. When the curtain rises on “Stravinsky Violin Concerto,” it’s as if the five stationary dancers — four men and one woman — were taking a moment to match their heartbeats to the music. The ballerina takes the first step, a bent-knee kick to the side, and in that instant the music and the dance become one. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/29/arts/29STRAVINSKY/29STRAVINSKY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 637, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/29/arts/29STRAVINSKY/29STRAVINSKY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1275, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/29/arts/29STRAVINSKY/29STRAVINSKY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/29/arts/29STRAVINSKY/29STRAVINSKY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/29/arts/29STRAVINSKY/29STRAVINSKY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Confirming the Beats Of a Throbbing Pulse', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Confirming the Beats Of a Throbbing Pulse', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Ballet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-29T01:41:27+0000', '