 has fallen sharply along with gas prices, and in the face of inevitable litigation. [Sept. 30, 11:13 p.m. | Updated | Danny Hakim describes the reaction of drilling supporters and foes to Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo’s latest move on fracking.]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York May Restart Review of Gas-Drilling Rules', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drilling and Boring', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Natural Gas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shale', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cornell University', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ENVIRONMENTAL CONSERVATION DEPARTMENT', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Marcellus Shale', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-29T03:54:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8376453-2d64-5ecd-839d-558d15200ea7', 'word_count': 458, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8376453-2d64-5ecd-839d-558d15200ea7'}, {'abstract': 'After having lost eight of nine, the Chicago White Sox, for one night at least, stopped its slide and Tampa Bay’s late-season surge.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/29/sports/baseball/with-victory-white-sox-stop-slide-and-rays-surge.html', 'snippet': 'After having lost eight of nine, the Chicago White Sox, for one night at least, stopped its slide and Tampa Bay’s late-season surge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — The September narratives for the White Sox and the Tampa Bay Rays seemed written Friday morning. The Rays were in the midst of a late-season charge for the second straight year, winners of eight straight to trim a six-game deficit on Sept. 18 to two in the American League wild-card race. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Rays and White Sox, One More Reversal in Upside-Down Year', 'kicker': 'White Sox 3, Rays 1', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Rays and White Sox, One More Reversal in Upside-Down Year', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago White Sox', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tampa Bay Rays', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-29T03:59:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Strauss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Strauss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cacba05a-f057-5c06-a244-5efe599d2738', 'word_count': 632, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cacba05a-f057-5c06-a244-5efe599d2738'}, {'abstract': 'President Abdu Rabbu Mansour Hadi’s support of drone attacks in Yemen cemented his status as a favored counterterrorism partner of the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/29/world/middleeast/yemens-leader-president-hadi-praises-us-drone-strikes.html', 'snippet': 'President Abdu Rabbu Mansour Hadi’s support of drone attacks in Yemen cemented his status as a favored counterterrorism partner of the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The president of Yemen gave an unqualified endorsement of American drone strikes in his country during a visit here on Friday, cementing his status as a favored counterterrorism partner of the United States.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/29/world/29hadi_337/29hadi_337-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 653, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/29/world/29hadi_337/29hadi_337-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1306, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/29/world/29hadi_337/29hadi_337-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/29/world/29hadi_337/29hadi_337-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/29/world/29hadi_337/29hadi_337-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Yemen’s Leader Praises U.S. Drone Strikes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Drone Strikes Draw Praise From Leader Of Yemen', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Al Qaeda in the Arabian Peninsula', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drones (Pilotless Planes)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saleh, Ali Abdullah', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hadi, Abdu Rabbu Mansour', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-29T04:12:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Shane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/22154ef4-4778-54db-adde-8ee5ad983ea9', 'word_count': 533, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22154ef4-4778-54db-adde-8ee5ad983ea9'}, {'abstract': 'Robinson Cano’s left hand was hit by a pitch in Friday’s victory over the Blue Jays, but he stayed in the game.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/29/x-rays-for-cano/', 'snippet': 'Robinson Cano’s left hand was hit by a pitch in Friday’s victory over the Blue Jays, but he stayed in the game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TORONTO — Robinson Cano was struck in the back of the left hand with a pitch in the sixth inning of Friday’s 11-4 victory over the Toronto Blue Jays. He remained in the game, which was a good sign, but he wasn’t able to get an X-ray until late on Friday, so there was no definitive word on the extent of the injury immediately after the game.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'X-Rays for Cano', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'X-Rays', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cano, Robinson', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Toronto (Ontario)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-29T04:18:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72aa3f6d-c267-55a5-8ac7-53c556aeecf8', 'word_count': 158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72aa3f6d-c267-55a5-8ac7-53c556aeecf8'}, {'abstract': 'In an interview, Prime Minister Antonis Samaras of Greece said there was “zero risk” that Greece will leave the euro, but warned of growing unrest in Europe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/29/world/europe/greek-leader-samaras-sees-hope-if-europe-helps.html', 'snippet': 'In an interview, Prime Minister Antonis Samaras of Greece said there was “zero risk” that Greece will leave the euro, but warned of growing unrest in Europe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATHENS — He waited his whole life for this moment, and many European leaders see him as Greece’s last best hope for stability. But for Antonis Samaras, leading his country is no fun at all. “Do you think anyone can be happy being prime minister of Greece?” he asked in a low voice in an interview here on Friday, placing his elbows on his knees. “This is the toughest job in the world. It’s just pain.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/29/world/greece/greece-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/29/world/greece/greece-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/29/world/greece/greece-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/29/world/greece/greece-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/29/world/greece/greece-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/29/world/greece/greece-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Greek Premier Sees Hope, but Only if Europe Helps', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Greek Premier Sees Hope, But Only if Europe Helps', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Samaras, Antonis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Golden Dawn (Greece)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-29T04:22:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Donadio and Liz Alderman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Donadio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alderman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f9d6bb6-a3f6-54b7-821b-8441350746f3', 'word_count': 1241, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f9d6bb6-a3f6-54b7-821b-8441350746f3'}, {'abstract': 'Secretary of State Hillary Rodham Clinton formally removed an Iranian opposition group from the State Department’s list of designated terrorist organizations on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/29/world/middleeast/iranian-group-now-off-terror-list.html', 'snippet': 'Secretary of State Hillary Rodham Clinton formally removed an Iranian opposition group from the State Department’s list of designated terrorist organizations on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Secretary of State Hillary Rodham Clinton formally removed an Iranian opposition group from the State Department’s list of designated terrorist organizations on Friday. The decision, first reported last week, is expected to make it easier to find new countries for more than 3,000 members of the group, the Mujahedeen Khalq, who are currently in Iraq. The department took into account the group’s public renunciation of violence and “the absence of confirmed acts of terrorism” by the group, known as the M.E.K., for more than a decade. But the department said it would not forget the M.E.K.’s past acts of terrorism, “including its involvement in the killing of U.S. citizens in Iran in the 1970s and an attack on U.S. soil in 1992.” It also expressed “serious concerns” about accusations that the group had committed abuses against some of its own members. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iranian Group Now Off Terror List', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iranian Group Now Off Terror List', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mujahedeen Khalq', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-29T04:26:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Shane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/9047ef98-016f-57bc-b389-ddc9ef6cd86d', 'word_count': 141, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9047ef98-016f-57bc-b389-ddc9ef6cd86d'}, {'abstract': 'A mob set fire to an encampment of 35 foreign Roma in a Marseille neighborhood on Thursday night, the French authorities said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/29/world/europe/france-roma-camp-burned.html', 'snippet': 'A mob set fire to an encampment of 35 foreign Roma in a Marseille neighborhood on Thursday night, the French authorities said.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A mob set fire to an encampment of 35 foreign Roma in a Marseille neighborhood on Thursday night, the French authorities said. Local officials and rights groups were outraged, but there were no arrests, a police spokesman said. Residents of a housing project forced the Roma, also known as Gypsies, out of an adjacent field, the spokesman said, before setting fire to their possessions. Residents told local news media that they were responding to several recent thefts that they attributed to the camp’s inhabitants. As many as 20,000 foreign Roma are said to live in France, most of them Romanians or Bulgarians. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France: Roma Camp Burned', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France: Roma Camp Burned', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Romani People', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Camps and Camping', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Marseille (France)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-29T04:30:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Sayare', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sayare', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/36060d3e-cf7d-5a8c-80ed-29f2a9de2282', 'word_count': 102, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36060d3e-cf7d-5a8c-80ed-29f2a9de2282'}, {'abstract': 'National assets can be sold, if revenue maximization is not the goal, court says.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/29/government-can-decide-how-to-allocate-natural-resources-supreme-court-rules/', 'snippet': 'National assets can be sold, if revenue maximization is not the goal, court says.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI–India’s Supreme Court upheld the government’s right to sell natural resources as it sees fit, saying it wasn’t necessary for the administration to use auctions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Government Can Decide How to Allocate Natural Resources, Supreme Court Rules', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', '