aint a Clearer M.V.P. Picture', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Extra Bases: Triple Crown Would Paint A Clearer M.V.P. Picture', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Braun, Ryan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cabrera, Miguel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-29T15:45:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ecd0daa6-9555-5aa0-b1c7-ae0d7e712973', 'word_count': 1175, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ecd0daa6-9555-5aa0-b1c7-ae0d7e712973'}, {'abstract': 'During the lockout, and beyond, fans and the N.H.L. Players’ Association should make no mistake: Commissioner Gary Bettman is definitely running the show.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/30/sports/hockey/on-hockey-bettman-is-the-undisputed-nhl-enforcer.html', 'snippet': 'During the lockout, and beyond, fans and the N.H.L. Players’ Association should make no mistake: Commissioner Gary Bettman is definitely running the show.', 'lead_paragraph': 'How much power does N.H.L. Commissioner Gary Bettman have? Is he merely the instrument of the owners, taking orders and doing what he is told, or is it the other way around?', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bettman Undisputed N.H.L. Enforcer', 'kicker': 'On Hockey', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bettman Undisputed N.H.L. Enforcer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bettman, Gary', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lockouts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-29T15:52:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d738536a-8265-5594-9ede-a265951467d7', 'word_count': 981, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d738536a-8265-5594-9ede-a265951467d7'}, {'abstract': 'Arthur Ochs Sulzberger transformed The New York Times and stood up to the government in the Pentagon Papers case. He was king, and we miss him.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/29/punch-sulzberger-rip/', 'snippet': 'Arthur Ochs Sulzberger transformed The New York Times and stood up to the government in the Pentagon Papers case. He was king, and we miss him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Arthur Ochs Sulzberger, better known as Punch, transformed this newspaper and had a vast impact on journalism. He oversaw the emergence of an array of feature sections that put this newspaper on a solid financial footing, and he risked everything when he defied the White House and published the top-secret Pentagon Papers from the Vietnam War. But on hearing just now that he passed away overnight at the age of 86, I kept thinking of Punch mostly as a really good and decent man who oozed likability as well as leadership. (Here’s his obituary)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Punch’ Sulzberger, R.I.P.', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-09-29T15:53:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f985f23-3382-5ed4-8f8e-a6430da84f4b', 'word_count': 604, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f985f23-3382-5ed4-8f8e-a6430da84f4b'}, {'abstract': 'A sketchy diagramless crossword puzzle by Fred Piscop.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/29/variety-an-artsy-diagramless/', 'snippet': 'A sketchy diagramless crossword puzzle by Fred Piscop.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SECOND SUNDAY PUZZLE — O.K., so I stretched things a bit. That’s not the first time that has happened here at Wordplay.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Variety: An Artsy Diagramless', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-29T16:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e5f541f-0aaf-5d81-9651-d4df4d58f3ef', 'word_count': 271, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e5f541f-0aaf-5d81-9651-d4df4d58f3ef'}, {'abstract': 'Scenes from the Paris fashion week photo diary of Adrian Crispin.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/29/photos-of-the-moment-jun