e': 'May', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e26e4841-9b29-5312-bc3d-e7a9eada4867', 'word_count': 826, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e26e4841-9b29-5312-bc3d-e7a9eada4867'}, {'abstract': 'American Airlines should no longer be flying across the Atlantic. It does not have the know-how or the equipment, and its employees have clearly lost interest in the endeavor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/30/opinion/sunday/a-trans-atlantic-trip-turns-kafkaesque.html', 'snippet': 'American Airlines should no longer be flying across the Atlantic. It does not have the know-how or the equipment, and its employees have clearly lost interest in the endeavor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You, American Airlines, should no longer be flying across the Atlantic. You do not have the know-how. You do not have the equipment. And your employees have clearly lost interest in the endeavor. Like the country whose name graces the hulls of your flying ships, you are exhausted and shorn of purpose. You need to stop.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Trans-Atlantic Trip Turns Kafkaesque', 'kicker': 'Loose Ends', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Trans-Atlantic Trip Turns Kafkaesque', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Delays (Transportation)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN AIRLINES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRPORTS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-29T17:04:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gary Shteyngart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': Non