 — The parades to celebrate the centenary of the signing of the Ulster Covenant — the 1912 petition against home rule that helped lead to the partition of Ireland — passed peacefully on Saturday amid the biggest police operation here in more than 20 years.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/world/30belfast_image1/30belfast_image1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/09/30/world/30belfast_image1/30belfast_image1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/world/30belfast_image1/30belfast_image1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 659, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/world/30belfast_image1/30belfast_image1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1318, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/world/30belfast_image1/30belfast_image1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/30/world/30belfast_image1/30belfast_image1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/world/30belfast_image1/30belfast_image1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tension, Though No Violence, as Protestants Parade in Belfast', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tension, Though No Violence, as Protestants Parade in Belfast', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Protestant Churches', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Belfast (Northern Ireland)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parades', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Northern Ireland', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-29T19:17:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Douglas Dalby', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Douglas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dalby', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2eb7f14c-64f1-5589-8a1b-04406f8cd01c', 'word_count': 484, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2eb7f14c-64f1-5589-8a1b-04406f8cd01c'}, {'abstract': 'Dr. Praeger was a co-chief of cardiothoracic surgery at Hackensack University Medical Center and chief executive of Dr. Praeger’s Sensible Foods, a maker of frozen natural foods.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/30/business/peter-praeger-a-surgeon-with-a-health-food-company-dies-at-65.html', 'snippet': 'Dr. Praeger was a co-chief of cardiothoracic surgery at Hackensack University Medical Center and chief executive of Dr. Praeger’s Sensible Foods, a maker of frozen natural foods.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dr. Peter Praeger, a heart surgeon who saved a man’s life and as a result wound up owning a gefilte fish company — and who as a result of that wound up starting a successful natural-foods company — died on Sept. 22 in Hackensack, N.J. He was 65.', 'print_section': 'A', 'prin