, California, Nevada, Delaware and New Jersey.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/29/things-i-saw-no-34/', 'snippet': 'The artist draws things he saw in Maryland, New York, California, Nevada, Delaware and New Jersey.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Suggestions for what you’d like Jason to see and draw may be sent to thingsisaw@nytimes.com.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Things I Saw — No. 34', 'kicker': 'Things I Saw', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Delaware', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maryland', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nevada', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-29T20:13:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Polan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Polan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2855aeb-577e-56ac-a552-0c5d55d63424', 'word_count': 20, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2855aeb-577e-56ac-a552-0c5d55d63424'}, {'abstract': 'How to avoid our tendency as writers to repeat sentence patterns and words.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/29/escaping-ones-own-shadow-in-writing/', 'snippet': 'How to avoid our tendency as writers to repeat sentence patterns and words.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before we get started, you should know this about me: I’ve written short stories, news articles, essays, reviews and a couple of nonfiction books. In pursuit of my ambitions, I’ve put in long hours of reading, writing and rewriting. But because life unfolds the way life does, I also have a day job as a think tank researcher, where I spend about half of my time writing or reading in genres and styles that are — how can I put this? — less juicy than the ones I practice and aspire to produce. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/sunday-review/30DRAFT-art/30DRAFT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 942, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/sunday-review/30DRAFT-art/30DRAFT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1347, 'width': 1465, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/sunday-review/30DRAFT-art/30DRAFT-art-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/30/sunday-review/30DRAFT-art/30DRAFT-art-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/sunday-review/30DRAFT-art/30DRAFT-art-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Escaping One’s Own Shadow', 'kicker': 'Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-29T20:14:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Erard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/90653612-9369-5c0c-85e1-9bd1c3a183f0', 'word_count': 1137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90653612-9369-5c0c-85e1-9bd1c3a183f0'}, {'abstract': 'Jean Paul Gaultier’s show paid tribute to pop stars of the 1980s.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/29/gaultier-pays-tribute-to-80s-pop-stars/', 'snippet': 'Jean Paul Gaultier’s show paid tribute to pop stars of the 1980s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jean Paul Gaultier’s show tonight was an absolute hoot. Paying tribute to pop stars of the 1980s, the designer dressed his models to look like Grace Jones, Madonna, Michael Jackson, David Bowie and Annie Lennox, with hilarious accuracy. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gaultier Pays Tribute to ’80s Pop Stars', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gaultier, Jean Paul', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-29T20:18:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ca247df-1dea-5102-8ebb-ea819c84d932', 'word_count': 173, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ca247df-1dea-5102-8ebb-ea819c84d932'}, {'abstract': 'The first incarnation of the Washington Senators, the team of the author’s childhood, left for Minnesota in 1960.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/30/sports/baseball/with-washington-senators-move-a-youth-torn-away.html', 'snippet': 'The first incarnation of the Washington Senators, the team of the author’s childhood, left for Minnesota in 1960.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1989, my 10-year-old son, Brendan, asked if I would take him and his younger brother Patrick to a trading card show. When I was Brendan’s age, in 1955, I boasted the largest card collection in my Washington neighborhood — hundreds filling two large boxes. The cards in those days were not for collecting. They were for bartering, trading and learning the career statistics of favorite players. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/sports/dowd3/dowd3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 778, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/sports/dowd3/dowd3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1556, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/sports/dowd3/dowd3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/09/30/sports/dowd3/dowd3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/sports/dowd3/dowd3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'End of the Line for the Senators, and a Childhood', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'End of the Line For the Senators, And a Childhood', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Senators (Defunct Team)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Nationals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Killebrew, Harmon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-29T20:26:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin Dowd', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dowd', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ed3d424-ffa0-5699-b046-adc3cb8f68b6', 'word_count': 1729, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ed3d424-ffa0-5699-b046-adc3cb8f68b6'}, {'abstract': 'The chief of Revolution Foods aims to provide healthy school meals. The company now creates a daily volume of 200,000 breakfasts, lunches, snacks and dinners.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/09/30/jobs/revolution-foods-chief-on-healthier-school-meals.html', 'snippet': 'The chief of Revolution Foods aims to provide healthy school meals. The company now creates a daily volume of 200,000 breakfasts, lunches, snacks and dinners.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I GREW up in San Antonio, and loved to spend time at my grandparents’ cattle ranch about 90 miles away in Hunt, Tex. ', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/business/30BOSS/30BOSS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 790, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/09/30/business/30BOSS/30BOSS-superJumbo.jpg', 'hei