}, {'abstract': 'The web-slinging superhero, who was born in Queens and usually works in Manhattan, moves to another borough to protect its good citizens from evil villains, such as bedbugs.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/30/spider-man-by-mallozzi/', 'snippet': 'The web-slinging superhero, who was born in Queens and usually works in Manhattan, moves to another borough to protect its good citizens from evil villains, such as bedbugs.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Stuart Moore and his hero, Spider-Man, were both born in 1962. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spider-Man Moves to Brooklyn to Fight Bedbugs and Eviction', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spider-Man Moves To Brooklyn to Fight Bedbugs and Eviction', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comic Books and Strips', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parker, Peter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'DC Comics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Marvel Entertainment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-30T15:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vincent M. Mallozzi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vincent', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a458c3ca-35e7-5fb9-ac26-fb8a4256eff4', 'word_count': 946, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a458c3ca-35e7-5fb9-ac26-fb8a4256eff4'}, {'abstract': 'Modern technology can do strange things to your brain. Just ask the man who tried to turn a magazine page with a finger swipe.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/30/your-brain-on-e-books-and-smartphone-apps/', 'snippet': 'Modern technology can do strange things to your brain. Just ask the man who tried to turn a magazine page with a finger swipe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week, my brain played a cruel trick on me. While waiting for my flight to take off, I was reading The New Yorker, the paper version, of course — I know the rules. I became engrossed in an article and swiped my finger down the glossy page to read more.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/10/01/technology/01bits-disrupt/01bits-disrupt-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/10/01/technology/01bits-disrupt/01bits-disrupt-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/10/01/technology/01bits-disrupt/01bits-disrupt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/10/01/technology/01bits-disrupt/01bits-disrupt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/10/01/technology/01bits-disrupt/01bits-disrupt-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Disruptions: Your Brain on E-Books and Smartphone Apps', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Your Brain on E-Books And Smartphone Apps', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Brain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPad', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nass, Clifford', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-30T15:00:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/87a87277-d5ef-5ebf-886a-981e97f39651', 'word_count': 664, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87a87277-d5ef-5ebf-886a-981e97f39651'}, {'abstract': '“Winners” and “Losers,” two plays by Brian Friel presented as “Lovers,” are being staged at the Beckett Theater.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/10/01/theater/reviews/lovers-by-brian-friel-at-the-beckett-theater.html', 'snippet': '“Winners” and “Losers,” two plays by Brian Friel presented as “Lovers,” are being staged at the Beckett Theater.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I can’t wait for the future, Joe.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/10/01/arts/lovers/lovers-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 696, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/10/01/arts/lovers/lovers-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1392, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/10/01/arts/lovers/lovers-thumbStandard.jpg', 'heigh