': 'Accounts', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News From the Advertising Industry', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'News From the Advertising Industry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-30T21:29:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6803805-65d3-578d-85cc-11f2b3c3f133', 'word_count': 819, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6803805-65d3-578d-85cc-11f2b3c3f133'}, {'abstract': 'The novelist Andrew Krivak, who wrote “The Sojourn,” and Adam Hochschild, the author of “To End All Wars,” have won the 2012 Dayton Literary Peace Prize for fiction and nonfiction.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/09/30/winners-named-for-dayton-literary-peace-prize/', 'snippet': 'The novelist Andrew Krivak, who wrote “The Sojourn,” and Adam Hochschild, the author of “To End All Wars,” have won the 2012 Dayton Literary Peace Prize for fiction and nonfiction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The novelist Andrew Krivak, who wrote “The Sojourn” (Bellevue Literary Press), and Adam Hochschild, the author of “To End All Wars” (Houghton Mifflin Harcourt), have won the 2012 Dayton Literary Peace Prize for fiction and nonfiction. The runners-up are Ha Jin, for “Nanjing Requiem” (Pantheon Books), and Annia Ciezadlo for “Day of Honey” (Free Press). ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Winners Named for Dayton Literary Peace Prize', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dayton Prize Winners', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hochschild, Adam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jin, Ha', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-09-30T21:30:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/643e2605-ffb9-5a5c-99d2-e3ab457a7ce6', 'word_count': 93, 'uri': 'nyt://article/643e2605-ffb9-5a5c-99d2-e3ab457a7ce6'}, {'abstract': 'The second of five programs in the Fall for Dance festival at City Center featured Pam Tanowitz’s “Fortune,” Twyla Tharp’s “Sinatra Suite,” Martha Graham’s “Chronicle” and Peter Quanz’s “Luminous.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/10/01/arts/dance/fall-for-dance-festival-at-city-center.html', 'snippet': 'The second of five programs in the Fall for Dance festival at City Center featured Pam Tanowitz’s “Fortune,” Twyla Tharp’s “Sinatra Suite,” Martha Graham’s “Chronicle” and Peter Quanz’s “Luminous.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The audience gave such lusty applause to all four offerings in Fall for Dance’s program on Saturday night at City Center that it sounded as if for each piece the theater was populated solely by the performers’ friends and family. Afterward, however, while leaving the theater, you could hear people discussing ardently which items had worked for them, which they’d tolerated and which they hadn’t cared for. I was relieved to find that I wasn’t the only person who hadn’t loved everything.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/10/01/arts/fallfordance/fallfordance-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 274, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/10/01/arts/fallfordance/fallfordance-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 274}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/10/01/arts/fallfordance/fallfordance-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 467, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/10/01/arts/fallfordance/fallfordance-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 935, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/10/01/arts/fallfordance/fallfordance-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/10/01/arts/fallfordance/fallfordance-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/10/01/arts/fallfordance/fallfordance-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cool and Complex: Many Moving Parts Running Smoothly Askew', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cool and Complex: Many Moving Parts Running Smoothly Askew', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fall for Dance Festival (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'nam